\par\par \uc2 Global development\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Blood on their hands\u8217\'20\'19: world\u8217\'20\'19s medics condemn US overturn of  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights\b0\par\par\uc2 Lizzy Davies \par \uc2 1,067 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 June 2022\par 19:19 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 13\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Statement signed by more than 100 global healthcare groups says US court decision \u8216\'20\'18will cost lives for years to come\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Doctors and pro-choice activists have condemned the overturning of Roe v Wade, describing it as an \u8220\'20\'1Cunconscionable attack\u8221\'20\'1D that will leave the supreme court justices with \u8220\'20\'1Cblood on their hands\u8221\'20\'1D and cause a global chilling effect on women\u8217\'20\'19s rights.\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.figo.org/us-supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-global-organisations-defend-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a statement}}}\uc2  signed by more than 100 global healthcare organisations, including the UK\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Royal College of Obstetricians and Gynaecologists\uc2  (\uc2 RCOG\uc2 ), medics said the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s move was \u8220\'20\'1Ca catastrophic blow\u8221\'20\'1D to millions. The statement, also signed by the \uc2 RCOG\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s faculty of sexual and reproductive healthcare, warned: \u8220\'20\'1CIt is a decision that will cost lives for years to come.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Dr Edward Morris, president of the \uc2 RCOG\uc2 , said: \u8220\'20\'1CThis decision is an unconscionable attack on the health and rights of women and girls in the United States \u8230\'20\'26 It is shocking to think that the future of so many women and girls has been dictated by politics rather than evidence-based opinion.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Dr Ranee Thakar, president-elect of the \uc2 RCOG\uc2 , urged governments to support healthcare workers to provide women with safe abortions, rather than impose greater legal restraints.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe chilling effect of the ruling will undoubtedly be felt around the world,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe call on governments to create and protect legal and regulatory environments that support healthcare professionals to provide access to safe and affordable \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Ever since it became clear in May that the supreme court was preparing to strike down the 1973 legislation that effectively legalised \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , pro-choice campaigners and medics have been warning that the ripple effect {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2022/may/18/us-supreme-court-abortion-reversal-would-be-global-catastrophe-for-women"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 would be felt internationally}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 particularly in countries where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights are fragile.\par \par \uc2 Concern is now mounting that the decision could embolden the anti-choice movement, increase pressure on healthcare workers performing abortions, and threaten hard-won gains in countries where stigma around terminations is still rampant.\par \par \uc2 Activists have said they are particularly worried about the impact in Central America, a region with a number of total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans, and sub-Saharan Africa. But the message the court\u8217\'20\'19s opinion sends \u8211\'20\'13 that legalising \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been \u8220\'20\'1Cegregiously wrong from the start\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 could find echoes almost everywhere, not least in the European anomalies Poland and Malta.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe fallout from this calculated decision will also reverberate worldwide, emboldening other anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , anti-woman and anti-gender movements and impacting other reproductive freedoms,\u8221\'20\'1D said Dr Alvaro Bermejo, director of the \uc2 International Planned Parenthood Federation\uc2  (\uc2 IPPF\uc2 ).\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe justices who put their personal beliefs ahead of American will, precedent and law will soon have blood on their hands, and we are devastated for the millions of people who will suffer from this cruel judgment.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Banchiamlack Dessalegn, MSI\u8217\'20\'19s Africa director, said the decision could undermine the pro-choice movement\u8217\'20\'19s efforts in countries across the continent. She said: \u8220\'20\'1CI am so proud of the steps the government in Ethiopia has taken to expand access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  over the last two decades; action that has saved countless lives and empowered women to take control of their futures.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBoth here and across Africa, US-linked groups have been trying for years to roll back this progress, with well-funded misinformation campaigns and by lobbying governments to restrict access. But we vow to protect choice. We are not going back.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.unfpa.org/press/unfpa-statement-global-implications-new-restrictions-access-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 In a statement}}}\uc2  that did not directly refer to the supreme court decision, \uc2 UNFPA\uc2 , the \uc2 UN\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s sexual and reproductive health agency, said it feared in general that if women faced greater barriers to getting terminations, more unsafe abortions would occur, particularly in low- and middle-income countries.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAlmost all unsafe abortions currently occur in developing countries, and \uc2 UNFPA\uc2  fears that more unsafe abortions will occur around the world if access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  becomes more restricted. Decisions reversing progress gained have a wider impact on the rights and choices of women and adolescents everywhere,\u8221\'20\'1D it said.\par \par \uc2 Dr Jeanne Conry, president of the \uc2 International Federation of Gynaecology and Obstetrics (FIGO)\uc2 , said the impact of the decision would be \u8220\'20\'1Cfelt on a global scale.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis decision undermines our commitment to advancing the rights of women and girls around the world, and is a threat to gender equality and the bodily autonomy of millions. The United States now is out of step with the rest of the world, and fails to take into account the overwhelming global medical evidence that supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as essential health care,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Sarah Shaw, the head of advocacy at MSI Reproductive Choices, said history had already shown that decisions made in Washington DC \u8211\'20\'13 such as the imposition of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2019/mar/26/trump-global-gag-rule-us-aid-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 global gag rule}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 could \u8220\'20\'1Chave an impact far beyond [US] borders\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Shaw added: \u8220\'20\'1CBut while this vote may embolden the anti-choice movement around the world, it has also motivated the global community to reassert the right to choose.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTo anyone who wants to deny someone\u8217\'20\'19s right to make decisions about what is right for their body and their future, our message is \u8230\'20\'26 We will never stop working towards a world where everyone, everywhere has the right to choose, and this attack only strengthens our resolve.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Echoing her defiant spirit, Sara Pantuliano, chief executive of the ODI global affairs thinktank, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SaraPantuliano/status/1540361732664721409?s=20&t=18Tq18FXi0nryclyUjSIvw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote on Twitter}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CMake no mistake, this ruling is a threat to everyone, everywhere. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Solidarity?src=hashtag_click"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Solidarity}}}\uc2  with those in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/US?src=hashtag_click"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US}}}\uc2  who will be faced with unimaginable decisions following this ruling, as they seek to protect their {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/bodilyautonomy?src=hashtag_click"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bodily autonomy}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLet this be the fire to ignite our collective determination to prevent further backsliding. We must fight to ensure this trend does not gain any further momentum. We must draw a line by dealing in deeds not words.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The decision sparked fury among many politicians in Britain, where \uc2 Diana Johnson\uc2 , Labour MP and chair of the all-party parliamentary group on sexual and reproductive health, urged \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s government \u8220\'20\'1Cto stand in support of women in the US and condemn this decision\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Stella Creasy\uc2 , Labour MP for Walthamstow, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/stellacreasy/status/1540338119660150784?s=20&t=18Tq18FXi0nryclyUjSIvw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tweeted}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CTo every one of our American sisters, we are with you. We will not rest until your rights are restored as your fight is our fight. They won\u8217\'20\'19t stop trying to control women and we won\u8217\'20\'19t stop fighting for their freedom everywhere. None of us should live under his eye.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220624ei6o002gz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
