\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Biden condemns \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18tragic error\u8217\'20\'19 of overturning Roe v Wade\b0\par\par\uc2 Joan E Greve in Washington \par \uc2 546 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 June 2022\par 18:34 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 President says conservative justices\u8217\'20\'19 ruling to eliminate the federal right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  mean \u8216\'20\'18the health and life of women in this nation are now at risk\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  condemned {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision}}}\uc2  to overturn Roe v Wade on Friday, saying the conservative justices\u8217\'20\'19 ruling to eliminate the federal right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access represented \u8220\'20\'1Ca realization of an extreme ideology and a tragic error\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWith Roe gone, let\u8217\'20\'19s be very clear: the health and life of women in this nation are now at risk,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is an extreme and dangerous path the court is now taking us on.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Democratic US president promised he will \u8220\'20\'1Cdo everything in my power\u8221\'20\'1D to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, as dozens of Republican-controlled states prepare to ban the procedure.\par \par \uc2 Biden said his administration would prevent states from restricting travel to access \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services, and the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2  will also protect the distribution of medication that can terminate a pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 But while outlining his plan to protect reproductive freedom in America, Biden acknowledged that only Congress has the ability to re-establish the federal right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Congressional Democrats have already attempted to codify Roe, but they currently do not have the votes in the Senate needed to pass such legislation. Echoing fellow members of his party, Biden stressed the urgent need to elect more Democrats in the midterm elections this November, giving them an opportunity to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access and other fundamental rights.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CVoters need to make their voices heard. This fall, we must elect more senators and representatives who will codify a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to choose into federal law once again,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 Biden referenced {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/clarence-thomas-roe-gay-marriage-contraception-lgbtq"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Justice Clarence Thomas\u8217\'20\'19s concurring opinion}}}\uc2  in Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization, which suggested the court may soon reconsider other major rulings. Thomas specifically cited cases that established the right to access contraception and legalized same-sex marriage.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis fall, Roe is on the ballot. Personal freedoms are on the ballot \u8211\'20\'13 the right to privacy, liberty, equality. They\u8217\'20\'19re all on the ballot,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CWith your vote, you can act. You can have the final word. This is not over.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden empathized with the millions of Americans who are outraged by the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision to overturn nearly 50 years of precedent to end Roe, and he pleaded with the country to not engage in violence over the ruling. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-decision-reaction-republicans-democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Crowds had already gathered outside of the supreme court}}}\uc2  on Friday morning, as Americans of all ideologies protested or celebrated the ruling.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI call on everyone, no matter how deeply they care about this decision, to keep all protests peaceful \u8211\'20\'13 peaceful, peaceful, peaceful,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CNo intimidation. Violence is never acceptable. Threats and intimidation are not speech. We must stand against violence in any form, regardless of your rationale.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden will leave Saturday for the \uc2 G7\uc2  summit in Germany and the Nato summit in Spain. While overseas, the US president will probably face questions from his foreign counterparts about why America is stripping away a right that is considered a guarantee in so many of its peer nations. He may not have any good answers to offer.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220624ei6o002s4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
