\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  deserts: America\u8217\'20\'19s new geography of access to care \u8211\'20\'13 mapped\b0\par\par\uc2 Alvin Chang, Andrew Witherspoon and Jessica Glenza \par \uc2 568 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 June 2022\par 18:01 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 With the supreme court ending the federal right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , women will face much longer journeys for treatment\par \par \uc2 The supreme court has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturned}}}\uc2  the landmark 1973 decision Roe v Wade, which guaranteed a federal right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In its absence, states hostile to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  are free to ban or severely restrict the procedure. That would leave entire regions of the country without an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic within a day\u8217\'20\'19s drive, reshaping the geography of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in America in a single, seismic shift.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  won\u8217\'20\'19t be accessible for huge swaths of the country\par \par \uc2 More than half of US states are almost certain or likely to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  now that the supreme court has overturned Roe v Wade. Several states already have \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans on the books that would no longer be blocked by Roe v Wade, while others have \u8220\'20\'1Ctrigger laws\u8221\'20\'1D, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/03/what-states-abortion-clinics-access-trigger-laws"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 which are now put in motion}}}\uc2  with the federal government no longer protecting reproductive rights.\par \par \uc2 When those states ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , about a quarter of the country\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics would close \u8211\'20\'13 overwhelmingly in states where clinics are already sparse.\par \par \uc2 In Cameron county, at the southern tip of Texas, a woman would need to travel to a clinic more than 680 miles away in New Mexico. On the meandering roads of rural America, that\u8217\'20\'19s more than 800 miles: a 12-hour drive.\par \par \uc2 Women in some states will have to travel more than 500 miles to the nearest \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thelancet.com/journals/lanpub/article/PIIS2468-2667(17)30158-5/fulltext"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2017 study}}}\uc2  found that half of US women live within 11 miles (17km) of an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic, but about 20% of them have to travel 43 miles (68km). \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans in half of US states would drastically increase those travel times, particularly in the south, where a large swath of contiguous states are likely to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But traveling to another state for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  may not even be an option. People who seek abortions are disproportionately likely to have low incomes, and most already have children. Experts also warn that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/03/us-abortions-travel-wave-of-restrictions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 states may pass laws}}}\uc2  to restrict women from traveling out of state to seek \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is legally protected in some states, but that won\u8217\'20\'19t stop further restrictions or bans\par \par \uc2 A handful of states do have legal protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , either in their constitution or as statutes. While existing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws may not immediately kick with Roe v Wade overturned, Republicans in some of those states are expected to make a push to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In Kansas, for example, the constitution protects a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to access \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cjonline.com/story/opinion/2021/10/15/kansas-could-find-itself-heart-national-abortion-battle-value-them-both/8461340002/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 referendum in August}}}\uc2  will determine whether that protection will be eliminated. A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fhsu.edu/docking/Kansas-Speaks/2021-kansas-speaks-report-final_1.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 poll}}}\uc2  earlier this year found that more than 60% of Kansans oppose making \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  completely illegal. But the referendum is part of the primary elections, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cjonline.com/story/news/politics/elections/2022/02/22/poll-shows-kansas-residents-skeptical-banning-abortion-all-cases/6878658001/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 primary voters tend to be more conservative}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  reports that Republican senators have discussed federal legislation to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/nation/2022/05/02/abortion-ban-roe-supreme-court-mississippi/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ban \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  after six weeks}}}\uc2 , called \u8220\'20\'1Cheartbeat\u8221\'20\'1D bills by proponents. Many women don\u8217\'20\'19t know they are pregnant until after six weeks, and a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC5269518/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2018 study}}}\uc2  found that younger women, women of color and women without college degrees are more likely to find out after the seven-week mark.\par \par \uc2 Together, these new restrictions could further endanger legal protections in states that support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220624ei6o002e9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
