\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18One of our darkest days\u8217\'20\'19: outrage after supreme court overturns Roe v Wade\b0\par\par\uc2 Gloria Oladipo \par \uc2 921 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 June 2022\par 18:04 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  condemns justices on \u8216\'20\'18the extremist Maga court\u8217\'20\'19 but conservative lawmakers move swiftly to trigger \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans\par \par \uc2 Outrage and disappointment swept the US after the supreme court decision overturning the constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , upending federal reproductive protections set nearly 50 years ago in the landmark {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  case.\par \par \uc2 Democrats decried the opinion as a painful blow to rights for millions.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  denounced today\u8217\'20\'19s opinion as \u8220\'20\'1Cso extreme\u8221\'20\'1D, emphasizing the wide-reaching effect it will have on reproductive health nationwide. \u8220\'20\'1CNow with Roe gone, let\u8217\'20\'19s be very clear: the health and life of women in this nation are now at risk,\u8221\'20\'1D said Biden.\par \par \uc2 Biden said his administration will work to protect other means of accessing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in restrictive states, including \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills by mail, the ability to obtain out-of-state abortions, and other ways. \u8220\'20\'1CIf any state or local official, high or low, tries to interfere with a woman\u8217\'20\'19s exercise of her basic right to travel, I will do everything in my power to fight that deeply un-American attack,\u8221\'20\'1D said Biden.\par \par \uc2 Barack Obama{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/barackobama/status/1540340642848690176?s=21&t=Q8CgODugeguOJO2c_woZiw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CToday, the supreme court not only reversed nearly 50 years of precedent, it relegated the most intensely personal decision someone can make to the whims of politicians and ideologues \u8211\'20\'13 attacking the essential freedoms of millions of Americans.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Senate majority leader, \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , called Friday \u8220\'20\'1Cone of the darkest days our country has ever seen\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAmerican women are having their rights taken by five unelected justices on the extremist Maga court,\u8221\'20\'1D Schumer continued. \u8220\'20\'1CThese justices \u8211\'20\'13 appointed by Republicans and presiding without accountability \u8211\'20\'13 have stolen the fundamental right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Massachusetts senator Elizabeth Warren criticized the opinion {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.warren.senate.gov/newsroom/press-releases/senator-warren-statement-on-dobbs-v-jackson-womens-health-organization"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 via a statement}}}\uc2 , writing: \u8220\'20\'1CSix radical supreme court justices have overturned nearly 50 years of precedent, stripping away the constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . They have decided that the government \u8211\'20\'13 not the person who is pregnant \u8211\'20\'13 should make a private health care decision and deny women the right to control their own bodies and futures.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She said Democrats must fight against the effects of the ruling.\par \par \uc2 Many legislators who previously had publicly shared their personal stories of receiving abortions have also condemned the opinion.\par \par \uc2 The Missouri congresswoman \uc2 Cori Bush\uc2 , who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/sep/30/congresswomen-personal-abortion-stories-cori-bush-barbara-lee-pramila-jayapal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  testified about her own \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  at the age of 17, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CoriBush/status/1540339687977525250"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care IS healthcare. It was so before this. And it will remain so after this. We don\u8217\'20\'19t care what a far-right extremist supreme court that is in a crisis of legitimacy says.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYour racist, sexist, classist ruling won\u8217\'20\'19t stop us from accessing the care we need.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights advocacy groups also vowed to protect reproductive rights despite the ruling.\par \par \uc2 The non-profit Planned Parenthood {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PPFA/status/1540340537114378241"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tweeted}}}\uc2  its disappointment and frustration: \u8220\'20\'1CWe know you may be feeling a lot of things right now \u8211\'20\'13 hurt, anger, confusion. Whatever you feel is OK. We\u8217\'20\'19re here with you \u8211\'20\'13 and we\u8217\'20\'19ll never stop fighting for you.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It used \uc2 Twitter\uc2  to share an aid hotline for those trying to access \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Naral Pro-Choice America, a reproductive rights non-profit, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NARAL/status/1540342656865296385"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shared its anger }}}\uc2  on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , writing: \u8220\'20\'1CThe supreme court just overturned Roe v Wade; ending the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  for millions across the country. We share your hurt, anger, and confusion. We are in this fight together.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Medical professionals have also denounced today\u8217\'20\'19s ruling as an attack on bodily autonomy and healthcare rights.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 American College of Obstetricians and Gynecologists\uc2  released a statement on the ruling, writing in part: \u8220\'20\'1CToday\u8217\'20\'19s decision is a direct blow to bodily autonomy, reproductive health, patient safety and health equity in the United States.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Advocates for Indigenous women also decried the decision as detrimental for Native communities and other marginalized groups.\par \par \uc2 Crystal Echo Hawk of IllumiNative, an Indigenous woman-led social justice organization, released a statement spotlighting the impact of today\u8217\'20\'19s opinion on Indigenous communities: \u8220\'20\'1CThe supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision is particularly devastating for the Native community, who will undoubtedly see an increase in violence towards Native women and girls as a result of today\u8217\'20\'19s decision.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAccess to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and reproductive care is foundational to safety and wellbeing \u8211\'20\'13this is a matter of life or death for many in Native communities.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Many Republicans celebrated the opinion, with some conservative lawmakers already taking steps to outlaw abortions in their states.\par \par \uc2 The Senate minority leader, \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/sahilkapur/status/1540342615245193218"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said of the ruling}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CThe supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s landmark ruling in Dobbs is courageous and correct. This is an historic victory for the constitution and for the most vulnerable in our society.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Republican House minority leader, Kevin McCarthy, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GOPLeader/status/1540340187649253381"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CEvery unborn child is precious, extraordinary, and worthy of protection. I applaud this historic ruling, which will save countless innocent lives. The court is right to return the power to protect the unborn to the people\u8217\'20\'19s elected representatives in Congress and the states.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In Missouri, shortly after the supreme court announcement, \uc2 Eric Schmitt\uc2 , the state\u8217\'20\'19s Republican attorney general, signed an opinion ending abortions throughout the state.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFollowing the \uc2 Scotus\uc2  [supreme court of the United States] ruling overturning Roe v Wade, Missouri has just become the first in the country to effectively end \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  with our AG opinion signed moments ago. This is a monumental day for the sanctity of life,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AGEricSchmitt/status/1540338042413944832"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tweeted Schmitt}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Other conservative states have signaled that they will follow suit, with at least {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/03/what-states-abortion-clinics-access-trigger-laws"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 26 states}}}\uc2  expected to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  immediately or as soon as practicable.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220624ei6o002bm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
