\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Jan 6 hearings: Raffensperger debunks Trump\u8217\'20\'19s baseless fraud claim: \u8216\'20\'18The numbers don\u8217\'20\'19t lie\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein in Washington \par \uc2 6,034 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 June 2022\par 11:56 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Capitol attack committee convenes for fourth hearingRusty Bowers recounts \u8216\'20\'18I will not break my oath\u8217\'20\'19 callNo supreme court decision on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  or gun rightsSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 The fourth hearing of the January 6 committee explored both the official effort to overturn the 2020 election and the impact of personal attacks by Trump and his lawyer \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  against a pair of Georgia poll workers. Meanwhile, Congress is in the midst of a flurry of legislating, with lawmakers days away from taking a two-week break.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else happened today:\par \par \uc2 * South Dakota state attorney general \uc2 Jason Ravnsborg\uc2  lied to investigators and abused the power of his office after he struck and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/sep/14/south-dakota-attorney-general-fatal-crash"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 killed a pedestrian}}}\uc2 , prosecutors argued earlier today {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/21/an-6-hearings-trump-capitol-attack-live-updates?page=with:block-62b1f0188f08a75f2786f7e2#block-62b1f0188f08a75f2786f7e2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 at the opening}}}\uc2  of an impeachment trial that could remove him from office.\par \par \uc2 * Documentary film maker Alex Holder is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/21/an-6-hearings-trump-capitol-attack-live-updates?page=with:block-62b1e7818f08ba6b54b3129a#block-62b1e7818f08ba6b54b3129a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cooperating}}}\uc2  with a subpoena by the House select committee investigating the attack on the US Capitol on January 6, 2021, and related events. He filmed interviews with Trump and family.\par \par \uc2 * Congress is inching towards votes on a bipartisan gun control {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/21/an-6-hearings-trump-capitol-attack-live-updates?page=with:block-62b1e0048f0883e7ca64b7c0#block-62b1e0048f0883e7ca64b7c0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 compromise}}}\uc2  reached between Republicans and Democrats, spurred on by the Uvalde school massacre as well as the racist killings at a grocery store in Buffalo.\par \par \uc2 * The \uc2 US Supreme Court\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/21/an-6-hearings-trump-capitol-attack-live-updates?page=with:block-62b1d7af8f0883e7ca64b760#block-62b1d7af8f0883e7ca64b760"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 struck down}}}\uc2  a state-funded program in Maine that covers the costs of some private schools \u8212\'20\'14 but only those that are nonsectarian.\par \par \uc2 The US politics blog will return tomorrow, but for all the developments in the Russian invasion of Ukraine {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/series/ukraine-live"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 as they happen}}}\uc2 , including news on the visit by US attorney general \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2 , the fate of American citizens fighting on Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s side, and what\u8217\'20\'19s happening on the ground, do follow our global live blog on the war, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/jun/21/russia-ukraine-war-moscow-to-summon-eu-ambassador-over-openly-hostile-kaliningrad-cargo-transit-ban-live-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 The testimony by Ruby Freeman and Wandrea \u8220\'20\'1CShaye\u8221\'20\'1D Moss was the emotional climax of the January 6 committee\u8217\'20\'19s fourth hearing, as they detailed how being personally attacked by Trump ruined their lives. Their experience is unfortunately not unique.\par \par \uc2 Alexander Vindman, a prominent witness in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first impeachment investigation, tweeted his support:\par \par \uc2 enltrLady Ruby and Shaye,\par \par \uc2 I know what it\u8217\'20\'19s like to have the President of the United States attack me. Stay strong. We are better than him and we will prevail. Much love!\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Alexander S. Vindman (@AVindman) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AVindman/status/1539330296109146113?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 21, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Former US attorney and Trump foe \uc2 Preet Bharara\uc2  weighed in:\par \par \uc2 enltrIf Shaye Moss can come testify, so can \uc2 Mike Pence\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Preet Bharara\uc2  (@PreetBharara) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PreetBharara/status/1539330966036140032?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 21, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 A spokesman for Ron Johnson has responded to evidence presented in today\u8217\'20\'19s January 6 hearing that appeared to show the Republican senator cooperated with Trump\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to disrupt the 2020 election results in crucial swing states.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe senator had no involvement in the creation of an alternate slate of electors and had no foreknowledge that it was going to be delivered to our office. This was a staff to staff exchange. His new Chief of Staff contacted the Vice President\u8217\'20\'19s office.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 alexa henning (@alexahenning) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/alexahenning/status/1539324091970248704?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 21, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrThe Vice President\u8217\'20\'19s office said not to give it to him and we did not. There was no further action taken. End of story.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 alexa henning (@alexahenning) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/alexahenning/status/1539324093157236738?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 21, 2022}}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/21/an-6-hearings-trump-capitol-attack-live-updates?page=with:block-62b2083a8f08d3fd9a77afc1#block-62b2083a8f08d3fd9a77afc1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 In its hearing}}}\uc2 , the committee detailed a plan by Trump supporters to create \u8220\'20\'1Cfake elector documents,\u8221\'20\'1D which would say that states crucial to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s victory such as Georgia and Arizona actually voted for Trump. The idea was to get these into the hands of \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , who was to certify Biden\u8217\'20\'19s victory on January 6, 2021. The committee showed an aide for Johnson contacted the vice-president\u8217\'20\'19s staff about getting the documents to Pence, but they ultimately rejected the request.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 The January 6 committee has finished its hearing for the day, and as is its practice, ended with a preview of its next presentation, set for Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Committee chair \uc2 Bennie Thompson\uc2  said the House lawmakers will explore Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cattempt to corrupt and the country\u8217\'20\'19s top law enforcement body, the justice department, to support his attempt to overturn the election.\u8221\'20\'1D He played a brief excerpt from the testimony of Richard Donoghue, the acting deputy attorney general at the end of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s term.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe president said suppose I do this, suppose I replace Jeff Rosen with him, Jeff Clark, what do you do? And I said, sir, I would resign immediately. There is no way I\u8217\'20\'19m serving one minute under this guy Jeff Clark,\u8221\'20\'1D Donoghue is heard saying.\par \par \uc2 Rosen was the acting attorney general for the final weeks of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s time in the White House. Clark was an assistant attorney general who is accused of plotting with Trump to overturn the election, and is now facing disbarment.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/oct/17/jeffrey-clark-scrutiny-trump-election-subversion-scheme"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pressure mounts on ex-DoJ official Jeff Clark over Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18election subversion scheme\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 The committee also showed Trump attacking Freeman as a \u8220\'20\'1Cvote scammer\u8221\'20\'1D in a call with the Georgia secretary of state. Moss and Freeman are ending their testimony with the latter describing how it feels to be personally attacked by the president.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere is nowhere I feel safe. Nowhere. Do you know how it feels to have the president of the United States to target you? The President of the United States is supposed to represent every American. Not to target one. But he targeted me,\u8221\'20\'1D Freeman said in recorded testimony played by the committee.\par \par \uc2 Earlier, Moss had described just how intense the attacks from Trump supporters against them became. People would repeatedly make large pizza orders to Freeman\u8217\'20\'19s home, sending delivery drivers to her door. In one instance, Moss said, strangers turned up at Freeman\u8217\'20\'19s home and tried to force their way in to attempt a \u8220\'20\'1Ccitizens arrest\u8221\'20\'1D of her. Around January 6, Freeman was advised by the \uc2 FBI\uc2  to leave her home for her safety.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 Moss and her mother Ruby Freeman are detailing how Trump and Giuliani\u8217\'20\'19s promotion of a conspiracy theory that they somehow rigged the vote has disrupted their lives.\par \par \uc2 Moss and her mother Ruby Freeman are passing around USB ports \u8220\'20\'1Cas if they are vials of heroin or cocaine,\u8221\'20\'1D Giuliani said in video testimony to the Georgia senate that the committee just played. In reality, Moss testified, what\u8217\'20\'19s shown being passed in that video was a ginger mint. But that allegation started the campaign of attacks by Trump supporters against the mother and daughter.\par \par \uc2 Moss, who is Black, said people found her \uc2 Facebook\uc2  profile and left her \u8220\'20\'1Chateful\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cracist\u8221\'20\'1D messages, including one saying \u8220\'20\'1CBe glad it\u8217\'20\'19s 2020 and 1920.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t go to the grocery store at all. I haven\u8217\'20\'19t been anywhere. I gained about 60 pounds,\u8221\'20\'1D Moss said of the the threats\u8217\'20\'19 effects on her. \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t want to go anywhere. I second-guessed everything that I do.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 The three Republican officials have now finished their testimony before the committee, and the lawmakers are now hearing from Wandrea \u8220\'20\'1CShaye\u8221\'20\'1D Moss, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/dec/24/ex-georgia-election-workers-sue-giuliani-oan-trump-conspiracy-theory"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Georgia poll worker who, along with her mother, was accused of rigging the vote in a number of conspiracies promoted by Trump supporters}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Her mother is seated behind her in the hearing room.\par \par \uc2 Moss has been a Fulton county election worker for 10 years, and began by confirming she never received threats before like she did during the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 Raffensperger debunks Trump fraud claim: 'The numbers don't lie'\par \par \uc2 Using Trump\u8217\'20\'19s words from a recorded phone call with Raffensperger, the committee is having the two Georgia officials debunk all of his claims of a stolen election in their state.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe numbers are the numbers and numbers don\u8217\'20\'19t lie,\u8221\'20\'1D Raffensperger said, defending his office\u8217\'20\'19s conduct. \u8220\'20\'1CEvery single allegation, we checked, we ran down the rabbit trail to make sure that our numbers were accurate.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FBI\uc2  and \uc2 Georgia Bureau of Investigation\uc2  also investigated the claims and found them to be baseless.\par \par \uc2 Adam Schiff, the California Democrat leading today\u8217\'20\'19s question, said that the committee has learned that around the time of the dispute over Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s vote, \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2 , Trump\u8217\'20\'19s chief of staff, wanted to send Georgia election investigators \u8220\'20\'1Ca shitload of Potus stuff,\u8221\'20\'1D in the words of one White House aide. These included coins and autographed Maga hats. \u8220\'20\'1CWhite House staff intervened to make sure that didn\u8217\'20\'19t happen,\u8221\'20\'1D Schiff said.\par \par \uc2 Brad Raffensperger\uc2 , the Georgia secretary of state. Photograph: Will Oliver/\uc2 EPA\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Sterling is detailing some of the conspiracy theories that followed Biden\u8217\'20\'19s election victory in Georgia, and debunking them. But despite the evidence he outlined that the theories weren\u8217\'20\'19t true, he said it was hard to get people to believe him.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt was kind of like a shovel trying to empty the ocean,\u8221\'20\'1D Sterling said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt was frustrating. I even have family members who I had to argue with about some of these things, and I would show them things, and the problem you have is you\u8217\'20\'19re getting to people\u8217\'20\'19s hearts.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COnce you get past the heart, the facts don\u8217\'20\'19t matter as much. And our job, from our point of view, is to get the facts out,\u8221\'20\'1D Sterling added.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 The January 6 committee has resumed its hearing, with the focus turning to \uc2 Brad Raffensperger\uc2 , Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s secretary of state. As with Bowers before him, Raffensperger begins by confirming his bonafides as a conservative Republican who wanted Trump to win.\par \par \uc2 Also answering questions is \uc2 Gabriel Sterling\uc2 , Raffensperger\u8217\'20\'19s deputy, who went viral for his speech following the election in which he strongly denounced Trump\u8217\'20\'19s baseless insistence that the 2020 election was stolen in Georgia.\par \par \uc2 Sterling is addressing that speech before the committee, saying it was prompted by direct threats to staff members in his office.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI lost my temper,\u8221\'20\'1D Sterling said. \u8220\'20\'1CBut it seemed necessary at the time, because it was just getting worse.\u8221\'20\'1D He also noted that he\u8217\'20\'19s not aware of any request from Trump to his supporters not to use violence.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 The committee is now taking a recess, but before they concluded, Bowers, a Republican who said he voted for Trump in the 2020 election, detailed the costs of his refusal to go along with the former president\u8217\'20\'19s plot to swing Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s electoral votes in his favor.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe received, my secretaries would say, in excess of 20,000 emails, tens of 1000s of voicemails and texts which saturated our offices and we are unable to work,\u8221\'20\'1D Bowers said.\par \par \uc2 Every Saturday, Bowers said organizations that he did not name would stage protests near his house.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have various groups combined. They have had video panel trucks with videos of me, proclaiming me to be a pedophile and a pervert and a corrupt politician and blaring loudspeakers in my neighborhood, and leaving literature, both on my property and arguing and threatening with neighbors, and with myself,\u8221\'20\'1D Bowers said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 The committee is now airing evidence that groups of Trump supporters from several states met after the 2020 election to create \u8220\'20\'1Cfake electors documents,\u8221\'20\'1D which they sent to Washington in an attempt to change their states\u8217\'20\'19 electoral votes from Trump to Biden.\par \par \uc2 The states included Arizona, Georgia, Michigan, Pennsylvania, New Mexico, Nevada and Wisconsin, and the meetings were done at the request of the Trump campaign. The intention was to submit the documents to vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , and the National Archives.\par \par \uc2 The committee then showed text messages that indicate Wisconsin Senator Ron Johnson attempted to get the fake elector documents to Pence. An aide to the vice-president ultimately prevented the documents from reaching him.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Per Bowers\u8217\'20\'19 retelling, the pressure campaign against him went on for some time, and included calls from those outside the White House.\par \par \uc2 Andy Biggs, a Republican House representative from Arizona, asked Bowers to support decertifying the Biden electors. \u8220\'20\'1CI wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t,\u8221\'20\'1D the Arizona speaker said he replied.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have no legal pathway, both in state law nor to my knowledge in federal law for us to execute such a request,\u8221\'20\'1D Bowers said of his opposition to the demands from Trump\u8217\'20\'19s team, which included reconvening Arizona lawmakers to either reject Biden\u8217\'20\'19s electors or send two lists of electors to Congress. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd I am not allowed to walk or act beyond my authority.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Rusty Bowers\uc2  shakes Adam Schiff\u8217\'20\'19s hand. Photograph: Chip Somodevilla/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Arizona House speaker: 'I will not break my oath'\par \par \uc2 Rusty Bowers\uc2 , the Republican speaker of the Arizona House of Representatives is now testifying. He\u8217\'20\'19s detailing a phone call from Trump and Giuliani following the 2020 election in which he was pressured to act to change the state\u8217\'20\'19s vote in the electoral college from Biden to Trump.\par \par \uc2 The two men claimed that the state\u8217\'20\'19s election was tainted by fraud, to which Bowers demanded evidence.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDid you ever receive from him that evidence, either during the call, after the call or to this day?\u8221\'20\'1D asked Adam Schiff, the Democratic House representative leading the questioning.\par \par \uc2 Rusty Bowers\uc2 , \uc2 Brad Raffensperger\uc2  and \uc2 Gabriel Sterling\uc2 . Photograph: Michael Reynolds/\uc2 EPA\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNever,\u8221\'20\'1D replied Bowers. Giuliani then came on the call to demand that Bowers \u8220\'20\'1Cwould allow an official committee at the capitol so that they can hear this evidence, and that we can take action thereafter.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI refused. I said up to that time that the circus, I called it circus, had been brewing with lots of demonstrations, both in the counting center (and) at the capitol,\u8221\'20\'1D Bowers said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd I didn\u8217\'20\'19t want to have that in the House.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLook, you are asking me to do something that is counter to my oath,\u8221\'20\'1D Bowers said to their demands that he act to change the state\u8217\'20\'19s vote. \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19re asking me to do something against my oath, and I will not break my oath.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 The committee is airing a video detailing a multi-pronged effort to convince, cajole and intimidate state officials into acting in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s favor in the aftermath of the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 There were phone calls from \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  and Jenna Ellis, both lawyers for Trump, to state lawmakers, pushing them to act to give Trump their state\u8217\'20\'19s electoral votes. Trump also publicly posted the contact details of lawmakers in crucial states.\par \par \uc2 The efforts had a tangible effect, the committee is showing. \u8220\'20\'1CAll of my personal information was doxed online. It was my personal email, my personal cell phone, my home phone number. In fact, we had to disconnect our home for about three days because it would rain all hours of the night would fill up with messages,\u8221\'20\'1D Bryan Cutler, the Republican speaker of Pennsylvania\u8217\'20\'19s House of Representatives told the committee.\par \par \uc2 The video ends with shots of protests by Trump supporters, some of which are armed or making threats of violence against lawmakers, or both.\par \par \uc2 The commitee is expected to hold at least six public hearings. Photograph: Shawn Thew/\uc2 EPA\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 The committee is now showing video of Trump supporters gathered outside Michigan Secretary of State \uc2 Jocelyn Benson\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s house at night.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CStop the steal!\u8221\'20\'1D the video shows them chanting, with one voicing calling Benson a \u8220\'20\'1Cthreat to democracy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy stomach sunk,\u8221\'20\'1D Benson told the committee. \u8220\'20\'1CAre they coming with guns? Are they going to attack my house?... That was the scariest moment just not knowing what was gonna happen.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDon\u8217\'20\'19t be distracted by politics. This is serious,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 , the January 6 committee\u8217\'20\'19s top Republican member, said in an appeal against partisan politics as the hearing began.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe cannot let America become a nation of conspiracy theories and thug violence,\u8221\'20\'1D she added.\par \par \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  on Tuesday. Photograph: Mandel Ngan/AFP/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 Yet Cheney herself may not be able to escape the partisan implications of her strident denunciation of Trump and his actions around January 6. She\u8217\'20\'19s been booted from her state\u8217\'20\'19s Republican party and is facing a vigorous primary challenge.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/20/liz-cheney-jan-6-hearings-republican-party"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Liz Cheney\u8217\'20\'19s condemnation of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lies wins over Democrats}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 January 6 committee begins fourth hearing\par \par \uc2 The House committee investigating the January 6 insurrection has begun its fourth hearing, focusing on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to convince state officials to swing the results of the 2020 election in his favor.\par \par \uc2 Among those testifying today will be:\par \par \uc2 * Georgia Secretary of State \uc2 Brad Raffensperger\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/24/raffensperger-defeats-hice-georgia-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 who last month fended off a Trump-backed attempt to oust him from office}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Gabriel Sterling\uc2 , Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s voting system implementation manager during the 2020 election who is now Raffensperger\u8217\'20\'19s top deputy and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Z94jxqOs3II"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 vocally condemned Trump\u8217\'20\'19s baseless claims about the integrity of his state\u8217\'20\'19s election.}}}\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Rusty Bowers\uc2 , the Republican speaker of the Arizona House.\par \par \uc2 * Wandrea \u8220\'20\'1CShaye\u8221\'20\'1D Moss, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/dec/24/ex-georgia-election-workers-sue-giuliani-oan-trump-conspiracy-theory"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Georgia poll worker who, along with her mother, was accused of rigging the vote in a number of conspiracies promoted by Trump supporters}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 Interim summary\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s been a busy day so far in US politics, building to this afternoon\u8217\'20\'19s latest hearing by the House January 6 committee investigating the insurrection in 2021 and events surrounding \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s efforts to overturn his election defeat (and potentially to corrupt future election results, as an alleged \u8220\'20\'1Cclear and present\u8221\'20\'1D danger to American democracy).\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll have live coverage of the hearing, beginning at the top of the hour.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where things stand:\par \par \uc2 * South Dakota state attorney general \uc2 Jason Ravnsborg\uc2  lied to investigators and abused the power of his office after he struck and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/sep/14/south-dakota-attorney-general-fatal-crash"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 killed a pedestrian}}}\uc2 , prosecutors argued earlier today {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/21/an-6-hearings-trump-capitol-attack-live-updates?page=with:block-62b1f0188f08a75f2786f7e2#block-62b1f0188f08a75f2786f7e2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 at the opening}}}\uc2  of an impeachment trial that could remove him from office.\par \par \uc2 * Documentary film maker Alex Holder is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/21/an-6-hearings-trump-capitol-attack-live-updates?page=with:block-62b1e7818f08ba6b54b3129a#block-62b1e7818f08ba6b54b3129a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cooperating}}}\uc2  with a subpoena by the House select committee investigating the attack on the US Capitol on January 6, 2021, and related events. He filmed interviews with Trump and family.\par \par \uc2 * Congress is inching towards votes on a bipartisan gun control {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/21/an-6-hearings-trump-capitol-attack-live-updates?page=with:block-62b1e0048f0883e7ca64b7c0#block-62b1e0048f0883e7ca64b7c0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 compromise}}}\uc2  reached between Republicans and Democrats, spurred on by the Uvalde school massacre as well as the racist killings at a grocery store in Buffalo.\par \par \uc2 * The \uc2 US Supreme Court\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/21/an-6-hearings-trump-capitol-attack-live-updates?page=with:block-62b1d7af8f0883e7ca64b760#block-62b1d7af8f0883e7ca64b760"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 struck down}}}\uc2  a state-funded program in Maine that covers the costs of some private schools \u8212\'20\'14 but only those that are nonsectarian.\par \par \uc2 For all the developments in the Russian invasion of Ukraine {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/series/ukraine-live"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 as they happen}}}\uc2 , including news on the visit by US attorney general \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2 , the fate of American citizens fighting on Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s side, and what\u8217\'20\'19s happening on the ground, do follow our global live blog on the war, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/jun/21/russia-ukraine-war-moscow-to-summon-eu-ambassador-over-openly-hostile-kaliningrad-cargo-transit-ban-live-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 South Dakota state attorney general \uc2 Jason Ravnsborg\uc2  lied to investigators and abused the power of his office after he struck and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/sep/14/south-dakota-attorney-general-fatal-crash"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 killed a pedestrian}}}\uc2 , prosecutors argued earlier today at the opening of an impeachment trial that could remove him from office, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 Ravnsborg\u8217\'20\'19s attorneys countered that such an action would improperly undo the will of voters for what he has maintained was an accident.\par \par \uc2 Ravnsborg, a Republican who only recently announced he wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t seek a second term, faces two charges in the state\u8217\'20\'19s first-ever impeachment trial over his actions in following a 2020 crash that led criminal investigators, some lawmakers and the victim\u8217\'20\'19s family to question his truthfulness.\par \par \uc2 Senators may also vote on whether Ravnsborg should be barred from holding future office.\par \par \uc2 Either way, the outcome of a proceeding expected to take two days will close a chapter that has roiled state politics, pitting Republican governor \uc2 Kristi Noem\uc2  against Ravnsborg and some in her own party who objected to her aggressive pursuit of his removal.\par \par \uc2 He absolutely saw the man that he struck in the moments after,\u8221\'20\'1D said Alexis Tracy, the Clay County state\u8217\'20\'19s attorney who is leading the prosecution.\par \par \uc2 Prosecutors also told senators that Ravnsborg had used his title \u8220\'20\'1Cto set the tone and gain influence\u8221\'20\'1D in the aftermath of the crash, even as he allegedly made \u8220\'20\'1Cmisstatements and outright lies\u8221\'20\'1D to the crash investigators.\par \par \uc2 The prosecution played a montage of audio clips of Ravnsborg referring to himself as the attorney general.\par \par \uc2 Ravnsborg has maintained that he did nothing wrong and cast the impeachment trial as a chance to clear himself.\par \par \uc2 He resolved the criminal case last year by pleading no contest to a pair of traffic misdemeanors, including making an illegal lane change and using a phone while driving, and was fined by a judge.\par \par \uc2 South Dakota Attorney General \uc2 Jason Ravnsborg\uc2  during opening remarks by the defense at his impeachment trial today in Pierre. Photograph: Erin Woodiel/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Alex Holder, a documentary film-maker {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/newsletters/playbook/2022/06/21/scoop-jan-6-panel-subpoenas-unseen-trump-tapes-00040911?cid=hptb_primary_0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 who Politico reported has been subpoenaed by the January 6 committee for his interviews with Trump and his inner circle}}}\uc2 , responded to the news:\par \par \uc2 enltrMy statement in response to being subpoenaed by Congress: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/LOY53rEynI"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/LOY53rEynI}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Alex Holder (@alexjholder) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/alexjholder/status/1539254430033387522?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 21, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Robert Costa of CBS News has some details of what Holder may have captured:\par \par \uc2 enltrSome reporting on the Alex Holder Trump doc, per convos with 3 people this morning who worked on Trump 2020...\par \par \uc2 1-They recall a film crew coming to HQ at least once. They also remember it being odd because campaign's legal team seemed surprised, as if it was an unvetted project.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Robert Costa (@costareports) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/costareports/status/1539260768486563842?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 21, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltr2-The campaign's lawyers were like, "Huh, what is this? What's going on today?" Saw it as another side project from the family/Trump confidants.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Robert Costa (@costareports) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/costareports/status/1539261398223560705?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 21, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltr3-"This was a family thing," one of the campaign staffers told {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CBSNews?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @CBSNews}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Robert Costa (@costareports) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/costareports/status/1539262383868284934?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 21, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrNEWS: Per a person familiar with the project, ALEX HOLDER has made a 3-part series on Trump. Spent Sept. 2020-Jan. 2021 with the Trump family and campaign, filming. Was on Cap grounds, not WH day of Jan. 6. He had full editorial control, was not paid. Paid for crew, hotels, etc.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Robert Costa (@costareports) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/costareports/status/1539264738810548224?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 21, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Stephen Colbert has spoken out following the Thursday evening arrests of several of his crew members near the US Capitol, as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/ramon-antonio-vargas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ramon Antonio Vargas}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 Talkshow host {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/stephen-colbert"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Stephen Colbert}}}\uc2  on Monday called the recent arrests of seven staffers near the US Capitol \u8220\'20\'1Cunpleasant\u8221\'20\'1D but said both his employees and the police officers who detained them \u8220\'20\'1Cwere just doing their job\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEveryone was very professional,\u8221\'20\'1D Colbert added during the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Hri8Tr3Om_g"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 monologue}}}\uc2  of his show Monday, four days after the arrests. \u8220\'20\'1CEveryone was very calm.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Late Show host also bristled at comparisons \u8211\'20\'13 even tongue-in-cheek ones \u8211\'20\'13 between the deadly January 6 attack at the Capitol and Thursday night\u8217\'20\'19s detentions, including that of the voice behind the puppet character Triumph the Insult Comic Dog.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis was first-degree puppetry,\u8221\'20\'1D Colbert joked, before striking a more serious tone and adding: \u8220\'20\'1CDrawing any equivalence between rioters storming our Capitol to prevent the counting of electoral ballots and a cigar-chomping toy dog is a shameful and grotesque insult to the memory of everyone who died and trivializes the service and the courage the \uc2 Capitol police\uc2  showed on that terrible day.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/21/colbert-show-staffers-arrested-capitol-hill-police"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Stephen Colbert says police who arrested his employees \u8216\'20\'18were just doing their job\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Spurred on by the Uvalde massacre as well as the killings at a grocery store in Buffalo, New York, Congress is inching towards votes on a bipartisan gun control compromise reached between Republicans and Democrats.\par \par \uc2 Senators {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/12/us-senators-bipartisan-gun-control-deal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced an agreement}}}\uc2  on the legislation last week, but they need to write the bill before it can be put up for a vote. \uc2 John Cornyn\uc2 , the Texas senator who is the lead Republican in the talks, says the bill\u8217\'20\'19s text should be released soon.\par \par \uc2 enltrCORNYN tells me there will be text \u8220\'20\'1Chopefully shortly.\u8221\'20\'1D Bill is hung up over \u8220\'20\'1Cdetails.\u8221\'20\'1D Asked about getting booed in TX over the weekend: he\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Call for people exercising their first amendment rights\u8221\'20\'1D but the reaction doesn\u8217\'20\'19t change how he\u8217\'20\'19s negotiating the gun reform bill. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/x0y0RDB4C1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/x0y0RDB4C1}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Allison Pecorin (@AllisonMPecorin) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AllisonMPecorin/status/1539257775460605953?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 21, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 While the measure lacks many of the provisions they believe are necessary to stop future mass shootings, Democrats are expected to back the compromise, viewing it as better than nothing. The proposal is also seen as likely to receive 10 votes from Republicans, who are typically hostile to gun control legislation. Their support is necessary to overcome a filibuster from others in their party, and Cornyn himself {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/17/biden-recession-jan-6-hearings-putin-russia-latest-updates?page=with:block-62acd7b28f08daac4266b4d2#block-62acd7b28f08daac4266b4d2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 faced the wrath of some of his fellow Texas Republicans last week for working on the compromise}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s been another alarming revelation about the botched police response to the Uvalde school shooting last month.\par \par \uc2 The director of Texas\u8217\'20\'19s Department of Public Safety told a state Senate committee that police officers could have stopped the shooting three minutes after it began, and called their response an \u8220\'20\'1Cabject failure,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/politics-shootings-texas-bad08b96b38793c80ab92575640f8438"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the Associated Press}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Police officers with rifles instead stood and waited in a school hallway for nearly an hour while the gunman carried out the May 24 attack that left 19 children and two teachers dead.\par \par \uc2 Col. \uc2 Steve McCraw\uc2 , director of the \uc2 Texas Department of Public Safety\uc2 , testified at a state Senate hearing on the police handling of the tragedy.\par \par \uc2 Delays in the law enforcement response have been the focus of federal, state and local investigations of the mass shooting.\par \par \uc2 McCraw told the Senate committee that Pete Arredondo, the Uvalde school district police chief, decided to put the lives of officers ahead of the lives of children.\par \par \uc2 The public safety chief began outlining for the committee a series of missed opportunities.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 Breaking along ideological lines, the supreme court has struck down a state-funded program in Maine that covers the costs of some private schools \u8212\'20\'14 but only those that are nonsectarian.\par \par \uc2 The decision will allow people in the state to use public money to pay for religious schooling, as Reuter\u8217\'20\'19s Lawrence Hurley explains:\par \par \uc2 enltrBREAKING: Supreme Court backs public money for religious schools in Maine case\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lawrence Hurley (@lawrencehurley) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/lawrencehurley/status/1539255087968698371?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 21, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrChief Justice Roberts: "... a neutral benefit program in which public funds flow to religious organizations\par \par \uc2 through the independent choices of private benefit recipients does not offend the Establishment Clause"\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lawrence Hurley (@lawrencehurley) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/lawrencehurley/status/1539255583068536833?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 21, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrCase is on whether people can use public money for religious schools from funding that Maine provides for people to pay for tuition at private high school in some parts of the state that lack public high schools. Court says "yes" on 6-3 vote\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lawrence Hurley (@lawrencehurley) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/lawrencehurley/status/1539256344359981057?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 21, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The court\u8217\'20\'19s conservative justices all supported the ruling, while its three liberals Elena Kagan, \uc2 Sonia Sotomayor\uc2  and \uc2 Stephen Breyer\uc2  dissented.\par \par \uc2 The supreme court has ended its release of decisions today with a ruling on a 233-year old statute regarding federal court orders:\par \par \uc2 enltrIn its final opinion of the day, \uc2 SCOTUS\uc2  rules on the scope of the All Writs Act, a 233-year-old statute that gives federal courts broad power to issue orders. The case involved an Ohio death-row prisoner trying to develop new evidence to challenge his conviction and sentence.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 SCOTUSblog (@SCOTUSblog) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SCOTUSblog/status/1539257507733983233?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 21, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 The supreme court has thus far announced three decisions, none of which deal with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , gun rights, environmental regulation or the other contentious topics they are expected to rule on before the current term ends.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a rundown of what they\u8217\'20\'19ve done so far, from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.scotusblog.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SCOTUSblog}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 enltrIn a technical dispute about health insurance reimbursements for kidney dialysis, the Supreme Court sides with a health insurer, rejecting a claim from \uc2 DaVita Inc\uc2 . (one of the nation's largest providers of dialysis) that the insurer's low reimbursement rates violated federal law.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 SCOTUSblog (@SCOTUSblog) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SCOTUSblog/status/1539247357816184839?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 21, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrIn the second (but not final) opinion of the day, the Supreme Court narrows the definition of "crime of violence" in a federal criminal statute. The court agrees with a criminal defendant that the definition excludes attempted robbery under the Hobbs Act.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 SCOTUSblog (@SCOTUSblog) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SCOTUSblog/status/1539249700586631169?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 21, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrThe Supreme Court strikes down a Washington law that made it easier for certain workers to get workers' comp from the federal government if they became sick while cleaning up a decommissioned nuclear site. \uc2 SCOTUS\uc2  says the law violates the doctrine of intergovernmental immunity.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 SCOTUSblog (@SCOTUSblog) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SCOTUSblog/status/1539252450980413441?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 21, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 Attorney General \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  has made a surprise visit to Ukraine, expressing support for the country\u8217\'20\'19s effort to prosecute the perpetrators of war crimes following Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion.\par \par \uc2 Here he is along with Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s prosecutor general Iryna Venediktova:\par \par \uc2 enltrIn unannounced trip, Attorney General \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  Visits Ukraine, Reaffirms U.S. Commitment to Help Identify, Apprehend, and Prosecute Individuals Involved in War Crimes and Atrocities {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/GzHPGqOUYV"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/GzHPGqOUYV}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Anthony Coley (@AnthonyColeyDOJ) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AnthonyColeyDOJ/status/1539239785058926592?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 21, 2022}}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/mar/23/russia-war-crimes-ukraine-us-blinken"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The United States has already formally accused Russia of committing war crimes in Ukraine}}}\uc2 , and the country has started trying Russian soldiers for alleged abuses.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/18/russian-soldier-pleads-guilty-first-ukraine-war-crimes-trial-since-invasion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Russian soldier pleads guilty in first Ukraine war crimes trial since invasion}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 When it begins announcing decisions in a few minutes, the supreme court could release an opinion that sharply curtails \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights nationwide, and Democratic leaders are trying to make the most of what they hope many of their voters would see as a bad situation.\par \par \uc2 As Politico reports, the party is making plans to focus voters\u8217\'20\'19 attention on the ruling\u8217\'20\'19s implications, and away from the issues that have swamped Biden\u8217\'20\'19s approval ratings in recent months, such as gas prices and inflation overall.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/06/21/democratic-strategy-sessions-post-roe-campaign-00040770"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 From their article}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 The Democratic Congressional Campaign Committee\u8217\'20\'19s preparations, previewed by a committee official, are a window into the Democratic Party\u8217\'20\'19s broader efforts to capitalize \u8212\'20\'14 in the middle of a brutal-looking midterm election climate \u8212\'20\'14 on the Supreme Court\u8217\'20\'19s likely reversal of Roe v. Wade, which would change a half-century of precedent and let states decide the legality of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Support for Roe is at an all-time high with voters, and the Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 strategy is aimed at firing up a flagging Democratic base, while also trying to compete for some of the college-educated, female, suburban swing voters who backed them during the Trump era. The question, though, is how to make \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  a top issue for voters in November while facing a range of challenges, especially gas prices averaging $5 a gallon and inflation ticking up.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re not going to be able to keep it in the national news, but we\u8217\'20\'19re going to put a lot of money on paid advertising \u8212\'20\'14 on TV, on digital ads, on mail, on radio \u8212\'20\'14 and in key places across the country, and that\u8217\'20\'19s how this issue will matter,\u8221\'20\'1D said Stephanie Schriock, former president of EMILY\u8217\'20\'19s List, a Democratic pro-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights group. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd in some states, it will be in the news every day, because state legislatures are going to push this issue further and further to the right with outright bans.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 What else can you expect from the January 6 committee? \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/hugo-lowell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hugo Lowell}}}\uc2  has taken a closer look at how the House lawmakers will present their witnesses and evidence at today\u8217\'20\'19s hearing:\par \par \uc2 The House select committee investigating the January 6 Capitol attack is expected to show at its fourth hearing on Tuesday that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  and top advisers coordinated the scheme to send fake slates of electors as part of an effort to return him to the White House.\par \par \uc2 The panel is expected to also examine Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign to pressure top officials in seven crucial battleground states to corruptly reverse his defeat to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in the weeks and months after the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 At the afternoon hearing, the select committee is expected to focus heavily on the fake electors scheme, which has played a large part in its nearly year-long investigation into Trump\u8217\'20\'19s effort to overturn the results of the election at the state level.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/21/donald-trump-plotted-fake-electors-scheme-january-6-panel-set-to-show"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump plotted fake electors scheme, January 6 panel set to show}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 In its hearings thus far, the January 6 committee has focused on the circumstances leading up to the attack in Washington, particularly Trump\u8217\'20\'19s baseless claims that the election was stolen.\par \par \uc2 Viewers will be taken farther afield in today\u8217\'20\'19s hearing, which will feature testimony from state officials about how Trump pushed them to interfere with their election results for his benefit.\par \par \uc2 Among its guests will be Georgia Secretary of State \uc2 Brad Raffensperger\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/24/raffensperger-defeats-hice-georgia-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 who last month fended off a Trump-backed attempt to oust him from office}}}\uc2 . He will be joined by Arizona House speaker \uc2 Rusty Bowers\uc2  and \uc2 Gabriel Sterling\uc2 , a top official in the Georgia secretary of state\u8217\'20\'19s office.\par \par \uc2 The hearing will also feature an appearance by Wandrea \u8220\'20\'1CShaye\u8221\'20\'1D Moss, a Georgia poll worker who, along with her mother, was accused of rigging the vote in a number of conspiracies promoted by Trump supporters. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/dec/24/ex-georgia-election-workers-sue-giuliani-oan-trump-conspiracy-theory"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 She is now suing Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyer Rudy Giuliani, rightwing One America News Network and several of its senior executives for defamation}}}\uc2 , saying the claims put them in physical danger.\par \par \uc2 Expect to hear more about just what she endured at the hearing today.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 January 6 committee to investigate pressure campaign on state officials as search for evidence continues\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics live blog readers. At 1pm eastern time, the January 6 committee will be holding its fourth hearing into last year\u8217\'20\'19s attack on the Capitol, with this session focusing on former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s pressure campaign on state officials to throw the 2020 election in his direction. The committee is meanwhile continuing its search for evidence. Politico reports that it has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/newsletters/playbook/2022/06/21/scoop-jan-6-panel-subpoenas-unseen-trump-tapes-00040911?cid=hptb_primary_0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 subpoenaed a documentary film-maker who had access}}}\uc2  to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s inner circle around the time of the insurrection.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else to expect today:\par \par \uc2 * Democrats and Republicans in Congress are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://punchbowl.news/archive/6-21-22-punchbowl-news-am/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 scrambling to find agreement on gun control legislation and an innovation bill}}}\uc2  as time runs out to pass the legislation before an upcoming two-week recess.\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The supreme court}}}\uc2  will release another batch of opinions at 10 am eastern time. Among these could be their opinions on closely watched cases dealing with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , gun rights, environmental regulation and other controversial issues.\par \par \uc2 * Voters will head to the polls (or cast mail-in ballots) in Virginia and Washington DC, while run-off elections are being held in Alabama and Georgia.\par \par \uc2 * President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  announced he will appoint Marilynn Malerba as treasurer of the United States. She is the chief of the Mohegan Tribe and would be the first Native American in the position that oversees the US Mint, among other responsibilities.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220621ei6l001jr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
