\par\par \uc2 Law\par \b \uc2 Sonia Sotomayor\uc2  says supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18mistakes\u8217\'20\'19 can be corrected over time\b0\par\par\uc2 Guardian staff and agencies \par \uc2 529 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 June 2022\par 10:05 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Liberal-leaning justice says \u8216\'20\'18there are days I get discouraged \u8230\'20\'26 sometimes I cry\u8217\'20\'19 but urges leftwing lawyers to persevere\par \par \uc2 The liberal-leaning supreme court justice \uc2 Sonia Sotomayor\uc2  said on Thursday that \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cmistakes\u8221\'20\'1D in high-profile cases can be corrected over time \u8211\'20\'13 as she adopted a positive tone ahead of a decision in which the court\u8217\'20\'19s conservative majority is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/03/biden-democrats-reaction-codifying-roe-v-wade-reform-scotus"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expected to reverse}}}\uc2  the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in America.\par \par \uc2 Sotomayor, speaking in Washington DC at the annual meeting of a liberal legal group, did not directly address last month\u8217\'20\'19s publication of a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/02/roe-v-wade-abortion-supreme-court-draft-opinion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 leaked draft opinion}}}\uc2  in an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  case out of Mississippi that includes a request to overturn the pivotal 1973 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade ruling}}}\uc2 , or any of the court\u8217\'20\'19s other current cases.\par \par \uc2 But {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/sonia-sotomayor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sotomayor}}}\uc2  said she believed the court can help people \u8220\'20\'1Cregain the public\u8217\'20\'19s confidence\u8221\'20\'1D in government institutions.\par \par \uc2 The leaked draft ruling, written by the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2022/may/06/samuel-alito-profile-abortion-supreme-court-justice"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 conservative associate justice Samuel Alito}}}\uc2 , indicated that the court\u8217\'20\'19s conservative majority is set to overturn the opinion that legalized \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide.\par \par \uc2 The court has a 6-3 conservative majority, with Sotomayor one of only three liberal-leaning justices after Donald Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2020/dec/22/abortion-gun-control-conservatives-pet-cases-supreme-court-barrett"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 got to nominate}}}\uc2  three conservative-leaning judges during his administration.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CInstitutions are made up by humans. Because we are human, by necessity we make mistakes. It is the nature of the human enterprise,\u8221\'20\'1D Sotomayor told the \uc2 American Constitution Society\uc2  meeting.\par \par \uc2 Asked why lawyers on the left should have hope, Sotomayor said they had no choice but to fight.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere are days I get discouraged, there are moments where I am deeply disappointed,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CEvery time I do that, I lick my wounds for a while, sometimes I cry, and then I say: \u8216\'20\'18Let\u8217\'20\'19s fight.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Sotomayor noted that it took almost a century for the court to undo the notorious 1857 Dred Scott decision that declared that the US constitution did not apply to Black people.\par \par \uc2 She noted that it also took until 1954 for the court to issue its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2017/sep/24/little-rock-arkansas-school-segregation-racism"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Brown v Board of Education ruling}}}\uc2  that struck down racial segregation in education, undoing an 1896 ruling in Plessy v Ferguson allowing \u8220\'20\'1Cseparate but equal\u8221\'20\'1D treatment of the races.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDred Scott lost his 11-year battle for freedom in the courts \u8230\'20\'26 Yet he won the war,\u8221\'20\'1D Sotomayor said. \u8220\'20\'1CSo that\u8217\'20\'19s why I think we have to have continuing faith in the court system, in our system of government, in our ability \u8230\'20\'26 I hope not through war \u8230\'20\'26 towards continuing the battle each day to regain the public\u8217\'20\'19s confidence.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The draft opinion on the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/nov/30/explainer-mississippi-abortion-rights-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mississippi \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  case}}}\uc2  set off a political firestorm, with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/may/14/abortion-protests-us-roe-v-wade-politics-live-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 staging rallies}}}\uc2  outside the courthouse and at locations around the US, as well as an internal crisis at the nation\u8217\'20\'19s top judicial body.\par \par \uc2 Chief Justice \uc2 John Roberts\uc2  ordered an investigation into the source of the unprecedented disclosure, which is still under way.\par \par \uc2 Sotomayor, who has served on the court since 2009, spoke of the importance of believing that when people do \u8220\'20\'1Cwrong things\u8221\'20\'1D it does not mean they are \u8220\'20\'1Cbad people\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220620ei6k002nn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
