\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Workers at US  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights groups seek unions to prepare for post-Roe care\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 995 \uc2 words\par \uc2 18 June 2022\par 09:01 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Clinic employees say more staffing and resources will be needed to manage an expected influx of out-of-state patients\par \par \uc2 As reproductive rights groups brace for an anticipated \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  decision to overturn Roe v Wade and strike down federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in America, workers at these groups are organizing to unionize ahead of the expected legal changes.\par \par \uc2 About 400 workers at 28 clinics in five states in the midwest \u8211\'20\'13 Minnesota, Iowa, Nebraska, North Dakota and South Dakota, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.seiuhealthcaremn.org/news/planned-parenthood-north-central-states-workers-file-for-union-election/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  in late May 2022 their intent to unionize with SEIU Healthcare Minnesota and Iowa. They have filed for a union election with the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2  after a majority of workers signed authorization cards and their request for voluntary recognition was turned down by management.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFiling before the Roe decision comes out and before the CEO of Planned Parenthood North Central States Sarah Stoelz {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.plannedparenthood.org/planned-parenthood-north-central-states/about-ppncs/media-relations/sarah-stoesz-announces-plans-to-step-aside-as-president-and-ceo-of-planned-parenthood-north-central-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 leaves}}}\uc2  was really important, just because of what\u8217\'20\'19s going on in the country right now. It is kind of an emergency and we want to be able to provide better care to our patients,\u8221\'20\'1D said April Clark, a registered nurse and senior training specialist in Iowa. \u8220\'20\'1CEverything is going to be changing really quickly once the Roe decision comes out, if it comes out the way we expect it after the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/03/first-edition-abortion-rights-leak-roe-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  leak}}}\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On 2 May, a draft opinion from the supreme court was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/02/roe-v-wade-abortion-supreme-court-draft-opinion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 leaked}}}\uc2  to the news website Politico, striking down the 1973 Roe v Wade ruling that affirmed the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with an anticipated final ruling that would allow states to decide whether to restrict or ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Reproductive rights workers have said they need a union to support their working conditions while taking on the challenges to come with the scaling back of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the US.\par \par \uc2 Clark explained that clinics in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.desmoinesregister.com/story/news/politics/2022/05/03/iowa-abortion-law-if-roe-v-wade-overturned-supreme-court-ruling/9627766002/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Iowa }}}\uc2  have already been seeing an uptick in patients from out of state and that problems such as high turnover rates at Planned Parenthood need to be addressed through a union.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe really can\u8217\'20\'19t even safely maintain clinics now with our staffing, much less once the need gets higher. They\u8217\'20\'19re constantly pushing to have less staff in the clinic and at the same time do more, and we want to make sure we can provide safe care to patients,\u8221\'20\'1D Clark said.\par \par \uc2 Workers also cited pay inequity, low pay and workers\u8217\'20\'19 concerns being ignored by management as a few of the issues they are seeking to address through a union.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s such a massive disconnect between the executive leadership team and folks on the ground who are running the day-to-day operations of Planned Parenthood,\u8221\'20\'1D said Ashley Schmidt, a training and development specialist at Planned Parenthood in Nebraska and western Iowa. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s really hard for us to give the excellent patient care that we want to be giving because we just don\u8217\'20\'19t have the resources or they\u8217\'20\'19ve taken the resources that we want to use away from us.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 An election date hasn\u8217\'20\'19t been set by the \uc2 NLRB\uc2 , but workers are expecting mail-in ballots to go out some time in the next few weeks.\par \par \uc2 In an email, Molly Gage, vice-president of human resources at Planned Parenthood North Central States, said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe support employees\u8217\'20\'19 decisions about whether to be represented by a union and want every union-eligible employee\u8217\'20\'19s voice to be heard.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 About 200 workers at Planned Parenthood in Massachusetts are also seeking to unionize with 1199 \uc2 SEIU\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMyself and my co-workers, especially folks in the health center, we are understaffed, underpaid and overworked,\u8221\'20\'1D said Andy Saltzberg, who works in a Planned Parenthood clinic in Worcester, Massachusetts. \u8220\'20\'1CWe need to make sure that workers on the ground that are providing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care have everything they need, we need to make sure that they are heard and valued.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In response to the unionization efforts, the CEO of Planned Parenthood League of Massachusetts sent an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PplmUnited/status/1532938289942077441"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 email }}}\uc2  to all workers encouraging them to vote against a union, citing the overturning of Roe v Wade and claiming the union is a third party.\par \par \uc2 In an emailed statement, Planned Parenthood League of Massachusetts did not address the email sent to workers, but their CEO, Dr Jennifer Childs-Roshak, stated, \u8220\'20\'1CPPLM respects its workers\u8217\'20\'19 right to organize in favor of a union, which is why we are actively working with the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  to facilitate an election later this month, giving every eligible employee the opportunity to fully understand the process and make their own choice. PPLM will honor the results of that election.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 At the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 , a reproductive health research and policy organization based in New York and Washington DC, 61 workers are seeking to unionize, with mail-in ballots due at the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  on 27 June. The non-profit {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/guttunion/status/1532017865381056512"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hired}}}\uc2  the union avoidance firm Jackson Lewis ahead of the election.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWith the upcoming Roe decision, we really need a more supportive and sustainable Guttmacher and I feel like the best way to go about that is giving staff a seat at the table and by unionizing,\u8221\'20\'1D said Ashley Little, a research assistant at Guttmacher. \u8220\'20\'1CBoth \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and workers\u8217\'20\'19 rights are about having control of the decisions that affect your life, and if we\u8217\'20\'19re going to continue on in a post-Roe America, workers need to have a say in their lives.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for Guttmacher said they offered voluntary recognition, but with restrictions, which the workers declined due to those stipulations.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur CEO has been very clear from the moment a group of employees expressed their intention to form a union that she fully respects staff\u8217\'20\'19s right to organize, and that management will not oppose or in any way interfere in that process,\u8221\'20\'1D said the spokesperson. \u8220\'20\'1CGuttmacher management has and will continue to encourage staff to participate in this election and exercise their right to vote.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220618ei6i0012x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
