\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Ex-Trump adviser \uc2 Peter Navarro\uc2  pleads not guilty to contempt charges in January 6 case \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein \par \uc2 6,173 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 June 2022\par 20:08 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Former trade adviser refuses to testify to House panelCapitol attack prosecutors press House panel for transcriptsSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 Thanks for joining the US politics blog for another day of news from Washington and across the United States. The ongoing January 6 hearings were a major story this week as were the Senate negotiations over gun control, both of which will continue next week.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a recap of what happened today:\par \par \uc2 * Ex-Trump advisor Peter Navarro{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/17/biden-recession-jan-6-hearings-putin-russia-latest-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-62ac91418f08f2b5ecc6a506#block-62ac91418f08f2b5ecc6a506"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pled not guilty}}}\uc2  to two charges of contempt of Congress in relation to the January 6 attack on the US Capitol by extremist supporters of the former president who were trying, in vain, to prevent the certification of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s election victory.\par \par \uc2 * Trump told his own version of his interactions with vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  in the run-up to January 6, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/17/biden-recession-jan-6-hearings-putin-russia-latest-updates?page=with:block-62acd26e8f08f2b5ecc6a8d0#block-62acd26e8f08f2b5ecc6a8d0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 denying that he\u8217\'20\'19d insulted his running mate or pressured him to overturn the 2020 election}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * Speaking of Pence, he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/17/biden-recession-jan-6-hearings-putin-russia-latest-updates?page=with:block-62acc9208f08d6171258c235#block-62acc9208f08d6171258c235"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gave an interview to The Wall Street Journal}}}\uc2  and hinted he was considering a run for president in 2024 \u8212\'20\'14 which Trump has said he\u8217\'20\'19s thinking of doing as well.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 John Cornyn\uc2 , the Republican senator trying to reach a gun control compromise with Democrats, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/17/biden-recession-jan-6-hearings-putin-russia-latest-updates?page=with:block-62acd7b28f08daac4266b4d2#block-62acd7b28f08daac4266b4d2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was booed when he went back home to Texas to speak at a state party convention}}}\uc2 . Many in the state are apparently not a fan of his negotiations on firearms legislation.\par \par \uc2 * The Food and Drug administration approved Covid-19 vaccines for the youngest Americans, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/17/biden-recession-jan-6-hearings-putin-russia-latest-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-62aca2f18f08d6171258bfe2#block-62aca2f18f08d6171258bfe2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a development Biden cheered}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Monday is the Juneteenth federal holiday and thus, the blog will return on Tuesday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/17/biden-recession-jan-6-hearings-putin-russia-latest-updates?page=with:block-62ac95a08f08daac4266b135#block-62ac95a08f08daac4266b135"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 with the supreme court set to release another batch of decisions}}}\uc2  at 10 am eastern time, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/17/biden-recession-jan-6-hearings-putin-russia-latest-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-62acbb8a8f08f2b5ecc6a7ef#block-62acbb8a8f08f2b5ecc6a7ef"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the January 6 committee meeting later in the day}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 Legendary journalists Bob Woodward and Carl Bernstein reunited today to mark the 50th anniversary of the Watergate break-in, the event that came to define their careers and resulted in President Richard Nixon\u8217\'20\'19s eventual resignation.\par \par \uc2 But much of today\u8217\'20\'19s discussion at the DC headquarters of \uc2 The Washington Post\uc2 , the newspaper that published Woodward and Bernstein\u8217\'20\'19s history-making scoops 50 years ago, focused on more recent events.\par \par \uc2 Bernstein drew a direct comparison between Nixon and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who he described as \u8220\'20\'1Ca seditious, criminal president\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Pointing to the January 6 insurrection, Bernstein said Trump \u8220\'20\'1Cstaged an attempted coup, such as you would see in a junta [or] in a banana republic\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut one of the things that\u8217\'20\'19s developing that\u8217\'20\'19s very different than in Watergate is that the wife of a supreme court justice is now part of the story,\u8221\'20\'1D Bernstein said, referring to Ginni Thomas, the conservative activist and wife of Justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The January 6 committee has obtained messages showing Thomas communicated with former White House chief of staff \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2  and conservative lawyer John Eastman about efforts to overturn the results of the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt looks very much like -- and certainly is the opinion of a number of people on that committee -- that she is caught up in the conspiracy and very likely is a co-conspirator,\u8221\'20\'1D Bernstein said.\par \par \uc2 Noting that Thomas has indicated she will cooperate with the committee\u8217\'20\'19s requests for information, Woodward said of the committee members, \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re treading very carefully, and I think wisely.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 Texas senator \uc2 John Cornyn\uc2  has the attention of Democrats in Washington for being willing to negotiate over a gun control compromise, but those efforts have apparently earned him the ire of some of his fellow Republicans back home.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a clip of how his speech went at the state party\u8217\'20\'19s convention:\par \par \uc2 enltrUS Sen \uc2 John Cornyn\uc2  gets viciously booed during much of his speech here at the Republican Party of Texas Convention. Here\u8217\'20\'19s his closing remarks and the cascade of boos. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/m2Hua9WdrV"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/m2Hua9WdrV}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jeremy Wallace (@JeremySWallace) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JeremySWallace/status/1537871974940168193?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 17, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Cornyn is the lead Republican negotiator on the gun control compromise, which Democrats have acknowledged is nowhere near as strong as they would like it to be, but better than nothing when it comes to responding to the mass shootings in Uvalde, Texas and Buffalo New York.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.houstonchronicle.com/politics/texas/article/With-no-gun-deal-yet-U-S-Sen-John-Cornyn-17249034.php"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Houston Chronicle has a look}}}\uc2  at the stakes for Cornyn back home, where his detractors accuse him of violating their \u8220\'20\'1CGod given rights.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.22pm BST\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/16/jan-6-committee-hearing-live-ginni-thomas-eastman-latest-updates?page=with:block-62ab7e2b8f08f2b5ecc69ad4#block-62ab7e2b8f08f2b5ecc69ad4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 In the telling of the January 6 committee\u8217\'20\'19s witnesses}}}\uc2 , Trump reasoned with, pressured and finally berated \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  in the lead-up to the certification of the 2020 election, all in a failed effort to stop \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  from taking the White House.\par \par \uc2 Speaking in Nashville, the former president has offered his take on what happened between him and Pence in the closing weeks of their term:\par \par \uc2 enltrTrump: "I never called \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  a wimp. I never called him a wimp. \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  had a chance to be great. He had a chance to be frankly historic... But Mike did not have the courage to act... Mike was afraid of whatever he was afraid of."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 David Smith (@SmithInAmerica) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SmithInAmerica/status/1537872321758875649?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 17, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrTrump: They said I told Pence to decide the election. "I never said that. It's not true. I wanted him to send it up to the legislatures, so it goes back to Pennsylvania, state legislatures."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 David Smith (@SmithInAmerica) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SmithInAmerica/status/1537873152377856001?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 17, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Trump has long insisted, with no evidence, that he won the electoral college in 2020, but here he is now claiming that he also won the popular vote. In reality, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cookpolitical.com/2020-national-popular-vote-tracker"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  he was defeated}}}\uc2  by an even bigger margin than in 2016.\par \par \uc2 enltrTrump: "We did much better in the second election than the first. Millions and millions more votes... They say we lost. Don't believe it."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 David Smith (@SmithInAmerica) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SmithInAmerica/status/1537873460336140288?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 17, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The committee aired testimony yesterday that on the morning of January 6, Trump called Pence and used harsh language \u8212\'20\'14 including what one witness said was the \u8220\'20\'1Cp word\u8221\'20\'1D \u8212\'20\'14 to get him to go along with his plot to prevent the certification of the 2020 vote. Trump has a different take:\par \par \uc2 enltrTrump: "I said to Mike, 'If you do this, you could be Thomas Jefferson'. And after all it went down I looked at him one day and said, 'Mike, you're not Thomas Jefferson'."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 David Smith (@SmithInAmerica) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SmithInAmerica/status/1537874110927224833?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 17, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 On stage now at the Faith and Freedom Coalition\u8217\'20\'19s event in Nashville, Trump has condemned the January 6 committee in language that\u8217\'20\'19s familiar to anyone who remembers his time in the White House.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/davidsmith"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 David Smith}}}\uc2  is there:\par \par \uc2 enltrTrump on investigations: "It's the same people with the same words. If you just insert the same words with 'January 6' instead of 'Russia, Russia, Russia'."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 David Smith (@SmithInAmerica) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SmithInAmerica/status/1537869501156425729?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 17, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrTrump on January 6 committee: "Every one of them is a radical left hater. Hates all of you. Hates me even more but I'm just trying to help you out."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 David Smith (@SmithInAmerica) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SmithInAmerica/status/1537869881080786944?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 17, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrTrump: "They're knowingly spinning a fake and phony narrative in a chilling attempt" to hurt opponents. "Video that's been deceptively edited."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 David Smith (@SmithInAmerica) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SmithInAmerica/status/1537870176070291456?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 17, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrTrump: "What you're seeing is a complete and total lie. It's a complete and total fraud."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 David Smith (@SmithInAmerica) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SmithInAmerica/status/1537870436205309952?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 17, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrTrump: "They have their narrative and they know we're leading in every single poll.. Crazy \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 David Smith (@SmithInAmerica) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SmithInAmerica/status/1537870680410177538?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 17, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Republican Cheney\u8217\'20\'19s opposition to Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/nov/15/liz-cheney-wyoming-republican-party-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has particularly high stakes for her continued career as the lone House representative for Wyoming}}}\uc2 . She faces a primary challenger endorsed by the former president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2022-election/cheneys-jan-6-committee-spotlight-burns-wyoming-primary-rcna32616"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 who appears to be beating her in opinion polls}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal has secured an interview with Trump\u8217\'20\'19s vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , the star of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/16/jan-6-hearings-mike-pence-analysis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s January 6 hearing}}}\uc2 , though he himself didn\u8217\'20\'19t attend.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/pence-plots-2024-bid-as-jan-6-hearings-remind-voters-of-his-break-from-trump-11655471256"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The interview}}}\uc2  contains a bit of news: Pence is thinking about running for the Republican nomination in 2024 \u8212\'20\'14 which would likely put him up against Trump, whom he hasn\u8217\'20\'19t spoken to in \u8220\'20\'1Cabout a year\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 Mr. Pence said his own decision on whether to mount another campaign, likely to come in early 2023, will be based on prayer with his wife and conversations with friends, not on whether Mr. Trump decides to run.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ll go where we\u8217\'20\'19re called,\u8221\'20\'1D Mr. Pence said. \u8220\'20\'1CBut I won\u8217\'20\'19t let anybody else make that decision for me.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The article shows Pence is otherwise returning to his mainstream Republican roots, stumping for candidates such as Ohio governor \uc2 Mike DeWine\uc2 , Georgia governor Brian Kemp and Arizona governor \uc2 Doug Ducey\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 all of whom clashed with Trump. On Monday, Pence will be in Chicago for a speech on economic policy, a potent attack line against president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , given how high inflation is in the United States.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 As we await Trump\u8217\'20\'19s speech at the Faith and Freedom Coalition\u8217\'20\'19s event in Nashville, take a look at this report from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/hugo-lowell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hugo Lowell}}}\uc2  on tension between the January 6 committee and federal prosecutors, who would like to take a look at what the congressional probe has found:\par \par \uc2 Tensions between the US justice department and the House of Representatives January 6 select committee have escalated after federal prosecutors complained that their inability to access witness transcripts was hampering criminal investigations into rioters who stormed the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 The complaint that came from the heads of the justice department\u8217\'20\'19s national security and criminal divisions and the US attorney for Washington Matthew Graves showed a likely collision course for the parallel congressional and criminal probes {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/16/trump-clear-present-danger-to-us-democracy-conservative-judge-warns"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 into the Capitol attack}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe interviews the select committee conducted are not just potentially relevant to our overall criminal investigations, but are likely relevant to specific prosecutions,\u8221\'20\'1D Graves wrote, alongside assistant attorneys general Kenneth Polite and \uc2 Matthew Olsen\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe select committee\u8217\'20\'19s failure to grant the department access to these transcripts complicates the department\u8217\'20\'19s ability to investigate and prosecute those who engaged in criminal conduct in relation to the January 6 attack on the Capitol.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/17/capitol-attack-prosecutors-press-january-6-committee-for-transcripts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Capitol attack prosecutors press January 6 committee for transcripts }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 It looks like the gun control negotiations aren\u8217\'20\'19t going as smoothly as expected in the Senate.\par \par \uc2 enltrGOP source familiar with gun talks says "it's going to be a "long time before bill text is released." Source blames D staff "for trying to relitigate and reopen issues in the bill text that have already been agreed to in principle at the member level."\par \par \uc2 Dem source disputes that\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Manu Raju (@mkraju) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1537845806388199425?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 17, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrDems believe they are still making progress, and the Dem source they are still going through the back-and-forth of translating principles they agreed upon into detailed legislative text. Talks between members and at the staff level are expected to continue over the weekend,\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Manu Raju (@mkraju) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1537846043391533056?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 17, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrBut even if negotiators reach an agreement on bill text over the weekend, the Senate has very little time to process a guns package by the end of the week. The chamber is not in session until Tuesday and the Senate is expected to begin a two-week recess at week's end.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Manu Raju (@mkraju) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1537846354919272454?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 17, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrSenators want a bill passed before the July 4th recess because they are worried that allowing it to hang over two weeks while members are back home will halt any momentum the talks have enjoyed.\par \par \uc2 Boyfriend loophole and funding for states on red flag laws need to be resolved\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Manu Raju (@mkraju) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1537846356739600385?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 17, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Recall that the week {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/12/us-senators-bipartisan-gun-control-deal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 began with news of a compromise reached between Democrats and Republicans}}}\uc2  to pass legislation in response to the mass shootings in Uvalde, Texas and Buffalo, New York.\par \par \uc2 It appeared to have momentum. The Senate\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic leader said he would put the legislation up for a vote as soon as it was written, while the chamber\u8217\'20\'19s top Republican \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/14/trump-republicans-primary-elections-jan-6-hearings-biden-us-politics-live-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-62a8d48a8f0892aa32e163f0#block-62a8d48a8f0892aa32e163f0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he would support it}}}\uc2 , boosting its chances of passage since it will need the support of at least 10 of his party\u8217\'20\'19s lawmakers to pass. But now it\u8217\'20\'19s Friday, and here we are.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 January 6 committee sets fourth hearing for next Tuesday\par \par \uc2 The January 6 committee has announced it will hold its fourth hearing next Tuesday at 1 pm eastern time.\par \par \uc2 enltrNew: Jan. 6 committee formally announces fourth hearing will take place on June 21 at 1p ET\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Hugo Lowell (@hugolowell) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hugolowell/status/1537839336221249539?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 17, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 At the third hearing held on Thursday, committee members detailed the efforts by Trump to pressure his vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  to overturn the 2020 election at the joint sitting of Congress set for January 6, 2021.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/16/jan-6-hearings-mike-pence-analysis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18System nearly failed\u8217\'20\'19: US democracy was left hanging by the thread of Pence\u8217\'20\'19s defiance}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 As communities across the state grapple with a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/16/yellowstone-floods-water-supply-billings-montana"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 historic bout of flooding that has imperiled the water supply of its largest city}}}\uc2 , many in Montana are wondering: where is the governor?\par \par \uc2 State officials have only said that \uc2 Greg Gianforte\uc2  was on a planned trip abroad, but wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t mention the location. The answer appears to be Italy\u8217\'20\'19s Tuscany region, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newsy.com/stories/montana-gov-gianforte-returning-from-tuscany-vacation-as-flood-disaster-grows/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to Newsy}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Newsy obtained a photo of Gianforte and the first lady at a restaurant in Casole d\u8217\'20\'19Elsa, which is a small village in the Tuscany region of Italy. The photo is time-stamped at 9:31 p.m. local time Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 A source that wishes to remain anonymous sent us a photo of the couple dining with multiple other people. The governor\u8217\'20\'19s office confirmed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://billingsgazette.com/news/state-and-regional/governor-out-of-the-country-declares-statewide-disaster-in-response-to-floods/article_784ac6c8-ebfb-11ec-9519-035afcbc28c5.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gianforte was out of the country}}}\uc2  when it was noticed his lieutenant governor signed a statewide emergency declaration as acting governor.\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson said he and the first lady left late last week on a long-planned personal trip, but details about the timeline and the destination were left out.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://montanafreepress.org/2022/06/15/montana-gov-greg-gianforte-overseas-amid-yellowstone-floods/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Montana Free Press}}}\uc2  reports on how cagey the state has been about the whereabouts of Gianforte, a Republican elected in 2020:\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for the governor\u8217\'20\'19s office has said only that Gianforte left the country last week, before the Yellowstone River rose to take out massive chunks of infrastructure and isolate entire communities in Park, Carbon and Stillwater counties, on a \u8220\'20\'1Clong-scheduled personal trip\u8221\'20\'1D with his wife, Susan Gianforte. But the office has declined to say what country Gianforte is visiting and specifically when the governor will be back in Montana.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe governor is returning early and as quickly as possible,\u8221\'20\'1D gubernatorial spokesperson Brooke Strokye said in a statement Wednesday afternoon in response to repeated questions from the media.\par \par \uc2 The governor\u8217\'20\'19s whereabouts have been an increasing topic of speculation on social media after Lt. Gov. Kristen Juras signed a declaration of disaster Tuesday in response to the flooding in southern Montana.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe fact that [the flooding] is so extreme and his office has just been pretty recalcitrant about where he is and what\u8217\'20\'19s going on is not great,\u8221\'20\'1D said Eric Austin, a public administration professor at \uc2 Montana State University\uc2  who teaches a class on government leadership and ethics.\par \par \uc2 There are legitimate reasons why a public official would not share their location during international travel, Austin said, but during a natural disaster, \u8220\'20\'1Cperceptually, that doesn\u8217\'20\'19t really help.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 According to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nbcmontana.com/news/local/gianforte-scheduled-to-return-to-montana"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBC Montana}}}\uc2 , Gianforte was supposed to return to the state on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Our {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/davidsmith"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 David Smith}}}\uc2  is at the Faith and Freedom Road to Majority conference in Nashville, Tennessee, a fascinating gathering of parts of the Republican party.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is speaking there a day after he was accused on Capitol Hill of endangering his own vice president\u8217\'20\'19s life, calling \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  the p-word (about which Stephen Colbert {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/colbertlateshow/status/1537642691135098880"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cogitates}}}\uc2  ) and \u8220\'20\'1Csetting the mob\u8221\'20\'1D on him, per the House select committee.\par \par \uc2 Senator \uc2 Rick Scott\uc2 , formerly Florida governor, is there and speaking. here\u8217\'20\'19s Smith on the spot reporting via \uc2 Twitter\uc2 . He\u8217\'20\'19ll have a dispatch later.\par \par \uc2 enltrScott: "The American people are going to give a complete butt kicking to the Democrats this November. But after we win, then what?"\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 David Smith (@SmithInAmerica) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SmithInAmerica/status/1537820004745347078?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 17, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s mild.\par \par \uc2 enltrScott: The Biden administration has done something new. "They've figured out how to merge radical leftwing policies with gross incompetence... We want our freedom back. It's time to rescue America... It's time to take this country back."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 David Smith (@SmithInAmerica) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SmithInAmerica/status/1537819929847676929?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 17, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrAt Faith & Freedom Road to Majority conference in Nashville. Senator \uc2 Rick Scott\uc2 : The woke left have an agenda to end the American experiment. "They want to replace freedom with control... They're the modern day version of book burners."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 David Smith (@SmithInAmerica) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SmithInAmerica/status/1537819515555352576?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 17, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Rick Scott\uc2  earlier this week.\par \par \uc2 From the pulpit of \uc2 Rick Scott\uc2 . Florida Senator Scott holds a news article on gas prices during a press conference in Washington earlier this week. Photograph: Bonnie Cash/UPI/REX/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 Smith on Pence:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/17/mike-pence-trump-plot-january-6-hearing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pence the \u8216\'20\'18hero\u8217\'20\'19 who foiled Trump\u8217\'20\'19s plot \u8211\'20\'13 could it lead to a 2024 run?}}}\par \par \uc2 And Colbert:\par \par \uc2 enltrIvanka\u8217\'20\'19s former chief of staff revealed that T**** called his VP \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cthe P word.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/6IZ1r0m4EG"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/6IZ1r0m4EG}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Late Show (@colbertlateshow) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/colbertlateshow/status/1537642691135098880?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 17, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Interim summary\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s been a busy morning in US political news, though not as frenzied as some. There\u8217\'20\'19s more to come and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is due to speak at the top of the hour at the extraordinarily-named Faith & Freedom Road to Majority conference in Nashville, Tennessee. A day after he was repeatedly accused of breaking the law from both right and left at the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/16/jan-6-hearings-mike-pence-analysis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 third January 6 hearing}}}\uc2  into the 2021 insurrection at the US Capitol.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where things stand:\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has cheered the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/17/biden-recession-jan-6-hearings-putin-russia-latest-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-62aca2f18f08d6171258bfe2#block-62aca2f18f08d6171258bfe2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decision today}}}\uc2  to authorize Covid-19 vaccines for children younger than five years old, the last group of Americans that didn\u8217\'20\'19t have access to the jabs.\par \par \uc2 * The Iowa supreme court{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/17/biden-recession-jan-6-hearings-putin-russia-latest-updates?page=with:block-62ac95a08f08daac4266b135#block-62ac95a08f08daac4266b135"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 issued a ruling}}}\uc2  that would make it easier for the state to curtail or ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  procedures outright, days before the \uc2 US Supreme Court\uc2  is set to rule in a pivotal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  case out of Mississippi that includes a request to overturn Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 * Ex-Trump advisor Peter Navarro{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/17/biden-recession-jan-6-hearings-putin-russia-latest-updates?page=with:block-62ac95a08f08daac4266b135#block-62ac95a08f08daac4266b135"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pleads not guilty}}}\uc2  to two charges of contempt of Congress in relation to the January 6, 2021 attack on the US Capitol by extremist supporters of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  trying, in vain, to prevent the certification of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s election victory.\par \par \uc2 * The US president gives a rare one-on-one interview, to the Associated Press and talks about the climate crisis, Americans\u8217\'20\'19 low morale in a sea of coronavirus and division, says a recession is not inevitable and, essentially, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/17/biden-recession-jan-6-hearings-putin-russia-latest-updates?page=with:block-62ac74fd8f08daac4266af32#block-62ac74fd8f08daac4266af32"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stakes his presidency}}}\uc2  on continued support for Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s against-the-odds resistance to the Russian invasion, warning: \u8220\'20\'1CIf we let Russia roll and Putin roll, he wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t stop.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden hails \uc2 FDA\uc2  authorization of Covid vaccines for young children\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has cheered the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s decision today to authorize Covid-19 vaccines for children younger than five years old, the last group of Americans that didn\u8217\'20\'19t have access to the jabs.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday is a day of huge relief for parents and families across America. Following a rigorous scientific review, the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2  has authorized the first COVID-19 vaccines for kids under the age of five. As early as next week, pending recommendations from the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  (CDC), parents will finally be able to get their youngest kids the protection of a safe and effective COVID-19 vaccine,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said in a statement released by the White House.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are the first country to protect our youngest children with COVID-19 vaccines, offering safe and highly effective mRNA doses to children as young as six months old. My Administration secured vaccine doses for America\u8217\'20\'19s youngest children and now with \uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s authorization, we will begin shipping millions of vaccine doses for kids to thousands of locations parents know and trust\u8212\'20\'14including pediatricians\u8217\'20\'19 offices, children\u8217\'20\'19s hospitals, and pharmacies. As doses are delivered, parents will be able to start scheduling vaccinations for their youngest kids as early as next week, with appointments ramping up over the coming days and weeks.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/17/us-fda-covid-vaccines-infants-preschoolers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US authorizes first Covid vaccines for infants and preschoolers}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 Those who have been following the inflation story closely know that car buyers often find themselves on the losing end of the nationwide price surge. For \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 , Allan Chernoff reports on the lengths one man went just to pay sticker price for a new \uc2 Toyota\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 After an auto dealer demanded $10,000 above sticker price for a new hybrid vehicle, car shopper Michael Rathjen of Kirkland, Washington, resolved to pay no more than the manufacturer\u8217\'20\'19s suggested retail price (MSRP) for the vehicle of his choice. He never dreamed his quest would take him eight months and 3,000 miles from home.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m calling across the entire country. I\u8217\'20\'19m thinking this is not going to be possible. I\u8217\'20\'19m not going to find a dealer selling at MSRP,\u8221\'20\'1D recalled Rathjen, a technical writer. \u8220\'20\'1CI kept calling further and further away until I hit Vermont.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In early May, Rathjen flew to Burlington, Vermont, to pick up his new \uc2 Toyota\uc2  RAV4 Prime, paid $51,000 for the fully equipped premium model, then immediately turned around and drove it cross-country to bring it home. The drive took eight days, with some stops to see sights and friends.\par \par \uc2 Near-record low inventory levels, supply chain backups and production delays do not fully capture the monumental challenge confronting consumers seeking to buy a popular new car, light truck or SUV without being gouged by profiteering dealers. Determined shoppers who want to pay sticker price in today\u8217\'20\'19s market must rely upon a reservoir of persistence and patience, and, in some cases, travel hundreds, even thousands of miles. Even so, shoppers like Rathjen are happy to do so. \u8220\'20\'1CI felt very lucky to get exactly what I wanted, and at MSRP,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/jun/17/car-prices-deals-across-us-pandemic-supply-latest"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Soaring US car prices compel buyers to travel thousands of miles for deals}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 No, redistricting is not over. Louisiana has filed a petition before the supreme court asking it to overturn a lower court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling that ordered it to draw a second majority Black congressional district to comply with the Voting Rights Act.\par \par \uc2 enltrNew: Louisiana officials ask Supreme Court to restore GOP-drawn congressional map that includes just one heavily Black district out of six. Federal district judge ordered creation of second one. \uc2 Scotus\uc2  previously reinstated Alabama map in similar circumstances.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Greg Stohr (@GregStohr) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GregStohr/status/1537814454326403079?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 17, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrAs the filing notes, the 5th Circuit refused to grant a stay but is scheduled to hear arguments July 8th. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/wDOW8gim2K"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/wDOW8gim2K}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Greg Stohr (@GregStohr) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GregStohr/status/1537816040197042177?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 17, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 zxxltr {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/A7tsTTUUzH"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/A7tsTTUUzH}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Greg Stohr (@GregStohr) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GregStohr/status/1537816082366488576?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 17, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Louisiana\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic governor and it\u8217\'20\'19s Republican-led legislature have been in a lengthy tussle over the state\u8217\'20\'19s congressional map, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/voting-rights-john-bel-edwards-louisiana-government-and-politics-congress-14760c94d7d4acb7ec3f66d7e6407322"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 as the Associated Press reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 The supreme court will issue batches of opinions next week on Tuesday and Thursday, and, as always, the justices could release decisions on any of the cases before them, including one that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/03/chief-justice-roberts-abortion-leak-investigation-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 could overturn \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The nation\u8217\'20\'19s highest court isn\u8217\'20\'19t alone in considering \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. Earlier today, the Iowa supreme court issued a ruling that would make it easier for the state to curtail or ban the procedure outright, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/abortion-health-iowa-supreme-court-government-and-politics-0074e14defa4a6699e65d921f0edbc58"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the Associated Press}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 The court, now composed almost entirely of Republican appointees, concluded that a less conservative court wrongly decided that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is among the fundamental privacy rights guaranteed by the Iowa Constitution and federal law.\par \par \uc2 Friday\u8217\'20\'19s ruling comes amid expectations that the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  will overturn {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/what-is-roe-v-wade-33c08858dc8b0aa5f0450858b51a648a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the landmark Roe v. Wade decision}}}\uc2  that legalized \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide. Then Iowa lawmakers could ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the state without completing the lengthy process of amending the state constitution.\par \par \uc2 The Iowa decision stemmed from a lawsuit filed by \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers who challenged a 2020 law that required a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/laws-iowa-us-news-state-courts-courts-e504280a3d02961cd71d1deb7e8ed944"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 24-hour waiting period}}}\uc2  before a woman could get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/iowa-courts-health-government-and-politics-b5af0c6b67b2549b899cca26cc342beb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 judge who struck down}}}\uc2  the law cited the state high court\u8217\'20\'19s 2018 ruling. The judge also concluded the law violated rules prohibiting passage of bills with more than one subject.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile in Kansas, voters will in August be asked to decide on a new amendment to the state constitution that would also allow lawmakers in the conservative state to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kansascity.com/news/politics-government/article262553552.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Kansas City Star has a good report}}}\uc2  on how groups supporting and opposing the amendment are crafting their campaigns to attract moderate voters:\par \par \uc2 One of the first two TV ads aimed at defeating an anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  amendment in Kansas doesn\u8217\'20\'19t use the word \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  once.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CKansans don\u8217\'20\'19t want another government mandate,\u8221\'20\'1D the ad, titled \u8220\'20\'1Cmandate\u8221\'20\'1D says while a photo of a church closure sign flashes across the screen.\par \par \uc2 The ad was released Wednesday morning by Kansans for Constitutional Freedom, a coalition of advocacy organizations and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers fighting the amendment, alongside an additional 30-second spot that mentions \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  once \u8212\'20\'14but only in the context of rape, incest and life of the mother.\par \par \uc2 Hours later Kansans for Life, one of the leading organizations fighting for passage of the amendment, distanced itself from its national affiliate after the organization published model legislation that would ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in nearly all instances.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn the event Roe v. Wade is overturned, states will have a significant opportunity to protect the unborn,\u8221\'20\'1D James Bopp, Jr., general counsel for the \uc2 National Right to Life Committee\uc2 , said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn doing so, it is important that such states not only prohibit illegal abortions, but also employ a robust enforcement regime, so that these laws are sure to be enforced.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 Peter Navarro\uc2  pleads not guilty to two charges of contempt of Congress Former Trump administration trade adviser \uc2 Peter Navarro\uc2  arrives for a court appearance at the US District Court in Washington, DC on 17 June 2022. Photograph: Shawn Thew/\uc2 EPA\par \par \uc2 Then there are those who refuse to cooperate with the January 6 committee, such as \uc2 Peter Navarro\uc2 , a former top adviser on trade to Trump. He\u8217\'20\'19s just pleaded not guilty to two charges of contempt of Congress over his refusal to provide documents or testify to the House panel, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/world/us/ex-trump-adviser-navarro-pleads-not-guilty-contempt-congress-charges-2022-06-17/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Reuters reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/03/peter-navarro-indicted-trump-adviser-capitol-attack-inquiry"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Navarro was indicted and taken into custody earlier this month}}}\uc2  on the charges, despite his insistence that executive privilege protected him {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/mar/28/capitol-attack-committee-contempt-prosecution-vote-trump-aides"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 from cooperating with the probe}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 As The Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/hugo-lowell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hugo Lowell}}}\uc2  has reported:\par \par \uc2 Navarro {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/06/house-navarro-scavino-trump-advisers-contempt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was referred to the justice department}}}\uc2  for criminal contempt of Congress by the full House of Representatives in April after he entirely ignored a subpoena issued to him in February demanding that he produce documents and appear for a deposition.\par \par \uc2 The top White House trade adviser to Trump was deeply involved in efforts to overturn the results of the 2020 election from the very start, the \uc2 Guardian\uc2  has previously reported, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/mar/16/trump-white-house-aide-secret-author-dominion-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 deputizing his aides}}}\uc2  to help produce reports on largely debunked claims of election fraud.\par \par \uc2 Navarro was also in touch with Trump\u8217\'20\'19s legal team led by \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  and operatives working from a Trump \u8220\'20\'1Cwar room\u8221\'20\'1D at the Willard hotel in Washington {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/nov/30/donald-trump-called-top-aides-capitol-riot-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to stop Biden\u8217\'20\'19s election certification}}}\uc2  from taking place on January 6 \u8211\'20\'13 a plan he christened the \u8220\'20\'1CGreen Bay Sweep\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/31/peter-navarro-january-6-subpoena-grand-jury"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump aide Peter Navarro ordered to testify before grand jury over January 6}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 Former US Court of Appeals judge for the Fourth Circuit, \uc2 J Michael Luttig\uc2 , testifies during a public hearing of the House Select Committee to Investigate the January 6th Attack on the US Capitol, on 16 June 2022. Photograph: Shawn Thew/\uc2 EPA\par \par \uc2 He spoke slowly and at times haltingly, but noted conservative jurist \uc2 J Michael Luttig\uc2  offered some of the harshest condemnations and direst warnings at yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s January 6 committee hearings.\par \par \uc2 In fact, most of his toughest words were actually {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/06/16/j-michael-luttig-opening-statement-jan-6-hearing-00040255"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 written down in the opening statement he sent to the committee before the hearing}}}\uc2 , which was not read during its televised session.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2022/06/17/ignoring-jan-6-hearings-michael-luttig-explains-why-you-shouldnt/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a good rundown of Luttig\u8217\'20\'19s arguments}}}\uc2 , both from that statement and from his testimony:\par \par \uc2 He spared few in public life. Though he is clear about Trump\u8217\'20\'19s role in starting the war over the 2020 election that erupted into violence, he sees the broader internal political divisions, the war that preceded the insurrection, as the end result of the conduct of virtually the entire class of elected officials and their allies. In his telling, this war was \u8220\'20\'1Cconceived and instigated from our nation\u8217\'20\'19s capital \u8230\'20\'26 [and] cynically prosecuted by them to fever pitch, now to the point that they have recklessly put America herself at stake.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Luttig described America as \u8220\'20\'1Cadrift\u8221\'20\'1D and said he prays that it is only for a fleeting moment in the long span of American history. But his diagnosis of what he called \u8220\'20\'1Can immoral war\u8221\'20\'1D is frightening in its implications. He wrote: \u8220\'20\'1CWe Americans no longer agree on what is right or wrong, what is to be valued and what is not, what is acceptable behavior and not, and what is and is not tolerable discourse in civilized society.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Americans cannot agree on how to be governed or by whom or on a set of shared values, beliefs and goals. The attack that Trump instigated, he argued, was a natural \u8220\'20\'1Cand foreseeable culmination\u8221\'20\'1D of the broader war for America. Trump was prepared to execute a plan to overturn the election to cling to power \u8220\'20\'1Cthat the American people had decided to confer upon his successor.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 The partner of \uc2 Capitol Police\uc2  officer Brian Sicknick, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/09/caroline-edwards-testimony-january-6-hearings-capitol-attack"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 who died in the aftermath of the January 6 insurrection}}}\uc2 , has a message for \uc2 Jared Kushner\uc2  and \uc2 Ivanka Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Speaking on CNN following Thursday\u8217\'20\'19s hearing of the House committee investigating the attack, Sandra Garza took the couple to task for not speaking up as Trump made clear his plans for that day.\par \par \uc2 Yes, it\u8217\'20\'19s hard to stand up to a family member, a father, a father in law, but you could have done something. You could have avoided the bloodshed that took place, including the suicides that took place after.\par \par \uc2 You can watch the interview {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/videos/politics/2022/06/16/garza-sicknick-partner-message-to-ivanka-trump-jared-kushner-sot-tapper-lead-vpx.cnn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s Biden\u8217\'20\'19s White House today, but yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s January 6 committee hearing made clear that things could have turned out very different that day in 2021 if Trump\u8217\'20\'19s vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  had decided to act differently, as my colleague {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/joan-greve"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joan E Greve}}}\uc2  reports.\par \par \uc2 The January 6 select committee showed on Thursday that \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  withstood an intense pressure campaign from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his allies to overturn the results of the 2020 presidential election.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s advisers repeatedly tried to convince Pence to disrupt the congressional certification of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s victory on January 6, even after they themselves acknowledged that there was no constitutional basis for the vice-president to do so.\par \par \uc2 Pence ultimately refused to interfere with the certification process, despite facing threats to his personal safety from Trump\u8217\'20\'19s supporters who stormed the Capitol. But if Pence had acquiesced to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s demands, the US could have faced an unprecedented constitutional crisis, the committee warned on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/16/jan-6-hearings-mike-pence-analysis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18System nearly failed\u8217\'20\'19: US democracy was left hanging by the thread of Pence\u8217\'20\'19s defiance}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 There was a lot in Biden\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/biden-ap-interview-transcript-fefb405f8383c6fdb4674eef9706fd65"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 interview with the Associated Press}}}\uc2 , which was in and of itself notable for happening at all, since the president doesn\u8217\'20\'19t sit down with reporters that often.\par \par \uc2 Biden retold the story of how the 2017 white supremacist rally in Charlottesville, Virginia, and then-president Trump\u8217\'20\'19s response to it, spurred him to jump into the 2020 race:\par \par \uc2 I made a commitment and I think I can say that I\u8217\'20\'19ve never broken, if I make a commitment. I wasn\u8217\'20\'19t going to run again, this time. I mean for real. I was not going to run. I just lost my son, I was teaching at Penn, I liked it, until all those guys came, come out of the woods...\par \par \uc2 AP: Charlottesville.\par \par \uc2 BIDEN:... the Charlottesville folks and this other guy said \u8220\'20\'1Cgood people on both sides\u8221\'20\'1D when an innocent woman was killed, etc. And, I made a decision. I\u8217\'20\'19ve been doing this too long to do anything other than to try to do what was right.\par \par \uc2 He went on to defend the America Rescue Plan, his $1.9 trillion spending bill signed last year which is the subject of debate among economists over the degree to which it has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.frbsf.org/economic-research/publications/economic-letter/2021/october/is-american-rescue-plan-taking-us-back-to-1960s/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 contributed to the economy\u8217\'20\'19s current overheating}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Zero evidence of that. Zero evidence of that, number one. Number two, we\u8217\'20\'19ve reduced the deficit by $350 billion last year. We reduced the deficit by a trillion, 700 billion this year. We grow the economy. Today, today, we have more people employed than, in a long, long time and we gained another 8.6 million jobs. And guess what? We still have hundreds of thousands of job openings.\par \par \uc2 Finally, he acknowledged that the fallout from the death, job losses and disruptions to normal life caused by Covid-19 had damaged the national psyche:\par \par \uc2 Think about what it\u8217\'20\'19s like for the graduating classes of the last three years. No proms. No graduation. No, no, none of the things that celebrate who we are. Think about it across the board. How isolated we\u8217\'20\'19ve become. How separated we\u8217\'20\'19ve become. Even practical questions like, you know, can you go out on a date? I mean (inaudible) the normal socialization, how does that take place? There\u8217\'20\'19s overwhelming evidence it\u8217\'20\'19s had a profound impact on the psyche of parents, children, across the board. And we lost a million people.\par \par \uc2 And nine for every, according to a study, of those million people, nine significant family or close friends were left alive after they\u8217\'20\'19re gone.\par \par \uc2 AP: So you\u8217\'20\'19re talking about a country that has undergone profound psychological trauma.\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: Yes.\par \par \uc2 AP: What can you as a president do to address that psychology...\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: Be confident.\par \par \uc2 AP:... to make people feel more optimistic. Be confident?\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: Be confident. Be confident. Because I am confident. We are better positioned than any country in the world to own the second quarter of the 21st century. That\u8217\'20\'19s not hyperbole. That\u8217\'20\'19s a fact.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden hints stopping Russia his priority, despite challenges at home\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. What does \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  want his presidency\u8217\'20\'19s legacy to be? It\u8217\'20\'19s a question worth asking, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/06/joe-biden-entered-faces-daunting-crises"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 given the many challenges facing his White House}}}\uc2 , and a hint into Biden\u8217\'20\'19s thinking was revealed during {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/biden-ap-interview-transcript-fefb405f8383c6fdb4674eef9706fd65"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an interview with the Associated Press on Thursday}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19d say to the American people I\u8217\'20\'19ve done foreign policy my whole career. I\u8217\'20\'19m convinced that if we let Russia roll and Putin roll, he wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t stop,\u8221\'20\'1D the president said. Perhaps seeing Russia defeated in Ukraine is the answer.\par \par \uc2 America\u8217\'20\'19s support for Ukraine isn\u8217\'20\'19t all that\u8217\'20\'19s on the agenda in Washington today:\par \par \uc2 * Negotiations over a bipartisan gun control bill{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://punchbowl.news/archive/6-17-22-punchbowl-news-am/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seem to have hit a stumbling block in the Senate}}}\uc2 . Meanwhile, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/16/alabama-church-shooting-st-stephens"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a shooting at an Alabama church left two people dead}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * Washington is digesting the revelations from yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s hearing of the January 6 committee, in which a top conservative lawyer warned that former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  remains a \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/17/first-thing-trump-a-clear-and-present-danger-to-us-democracy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a clear and present danger to American democracy}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 * Speaking of Trump, the former president is set to speak at 1pm ET at the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ffcoalition.com/about/road-to-majority/#overview"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Faith & Freedom Coalition\u8217\'20\'19s Road to Majority Policy Conference}}}\uc2 . Perhaps he will have something to say about the January 6 committee.\par \par \uc2 * Montana\u8217\'20\'19s largest city{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/16/yellowstone-floods-water-supply-billings-montana"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 may run out of water}}}\uc2  after unprecedented flooding that also Yellowstone national park.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220617ei6h00239\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
