\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18This is not hopeless\u8217\'20\'19: the progressive prosecutors who vow not to enforce  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  bans\b0\par\par\uc2 Poppy Noor \par \uc2 1,652 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 June 2022\par 20:52 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The end of Roe could usher in a complex legal landscape with different enforcement regimes in different states, and even within them\par \par \uc2 Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general, Dana Nessel, never thought she would have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But after finding herself pregnant with triplets in 2002, she faced an unenviable choice: abort one, or miscarry all three. \u8220\'20\'1CI took my doctor\u8217\'20\'19s advice, which I should have been able to do,\u8221\'20\'1D she says in a phone interview.\par \par \uc2 Nessel plans to protect that same right for residents of her state if Roe v Wade is overturned this summer , as a leaked supreme court draft opinion indicates is all but certain.\par \par \uc2 If the draft opinion stands, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/article/2021/10/26-states-are-certain-or-likely-ban-abortion-without-roe-heres-which-ones-and-why"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 26 states are likely or certain to ban \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  . In Michigan, a 1931 law would be triggered, making \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  illegal in almost all cases except to save the life of the pregnant person.\par \par \uc2 Nessel says she won\u8217\'20\'19t enforce the ban in Michigan, along with at least a dozen law enforcement officials across the country \u8211\'20\'13 a bold statement that sets the US up for a complex legal landscape with different enforcement regimes in different states, and even within them.\par \par \uc2 These officials are likely to face swift backlash from the right, including, in some cases, retaliation from state authorities who will demand they enforce the law as written. But they are determined to press ahead.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t want to see politicians removing the rights I had during the course of my pregnancy for other women,\u8221\'20\'1D says Nessel. Her opponent in the race for state attorney general this November, Matt DePerno, has said he would {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/dananessel/status/1521331562230472704?lang=en"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 not support any exceptions to an \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban, even to save the mother\u8217\'20\'19s life.}}}\par \par \uc2 Now, Nessel has a complex set of legal questions on her hands \u8211\'20\'13 even if she is re-elected, and despite having Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s governor on her side.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHow do we make sure that if complaints are filed, physicians won\u8217\'20\'19t lose their licenses to practice medicine? [How do we] ensure insurance carriers don\u8217\'20\'19t drop [them]?\u8221\'20\'1D she asks .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t want to see medical emergencies, where women are literally left to die on an operating table, because of an ectopic pregnancy, or complications in a pregnancy. I don\u8217\'20\'19t want the doctor saying, \u8216\'20\'18I\u8217\'20\'19m out. I\u8217\'20\'19m not going to risk losing my license \u8230\'20\'26 or going to jail,\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D she says.\par \par \uc2 So she is working in conjunction with Governor \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2 , who is bringing a lawsuit asking the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.michigan.gov/whitmer/news/press-releases/2022/05/03/icymi--whitmer-presses-forward-on-lawsuit-to-protect-legal-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Michigan supreme court to protect \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  in the state\u8217\'20\'19s constitution}}}\uc2 , and to get a voter-backed referendum on the books that will protect other reproductive rights, such as the right to contraception.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re not helpless. And this is not hopeless. That\u8217\'20\'19s the message that I want to send,\u8221\'20\'1D Nessel says.\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 Steve Descano was thinking about his 10-year-old daughter when he pledged not to enforce \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans in his home county of Fairfax, Virginia. Virginia is not one of the 26 states that will automatically ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the supreme court overturns Roe, but access could become tenuous.\par \par \uc2 Descano is worried about comments made by Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s governor, Glenn Youngkin, who has described himself as \u8220\'20\'1Cpro-life\u8221\'20\'1D and anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  with exceptions for rape, incest and when the mother\u8217\'20\'19s life is in jeopardy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t want [my daughter] to grow up in a world where she\u8217\'20\'19s a second-class citizen, where she can\u8217\'20\'19t make her own healthcare decisions,\u8221\'20\'1D Descano said.\par \par \uc2 In a post-Roe landscape, Descano says, women could be regularly criminalized \u8211\'20\'13 investigated for miscarriages, with state officials rifling through their trash to learn about their sexual history.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPolice officers can get search warrants, they can go into emails, they can go into text messages,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CIf we take this strong stand it disincentivizes them from doing any of that,\u8221\'20\'1D he adds \u8211\'20\'13 vowing to protect providers in his county as well as people who seek out an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Descano and other progressive district attorneys are basing their pledges on successes they have already had in the fight to decriminalize marijuana possession. In Texas, the district attorneys for Nueces, Travis and Bexar counties all promised not to prosecute possession cases that came to them. They intend do the same with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Descano\u8217\'20\'19s own fight to decriminalize marijuana in Virginia wasn\u8217\'20\'19t easy \u8211\'20\'13 he says judges who opposed him dragged out the battle, arguing Descano could not dismiss such cases \u8211\'20\'13 even though a district attorney\u8217\'20\'19s dismissals are usually granted.\par \par \uc2 That fight does not offer a perfect roadmap. With marijuana, Descano had a nationwide trend toward liberalization on his side. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is moving in the opposite direction. But Descano \u8211\'20\'13 who said he was prepared to go to jail in order to stick to his promise \u8211\'20\'13 says the precedent taught him how to win these fights.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt became very clear we weren\u8217\'20\'19t going to prosecute. [So] police officers stopped spending their time on it,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 You could envisage an uneasy truce, with some pockets retaining limited \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access\par \par \uc2 Rachel Rebouch\u233\'00\'E9, interim dean, Temple law school\par \par \uc2 Council leaders in Austin, Texas, are putting forward a proposal to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/31/texas-austin-resolution-decriminalize-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 restrict city}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/31/texas-austin-resolution-decriminalize-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 funds}}}\uc2  from being spent on investigating \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  crimes if Roe is overturned this summer. They will also make the investigation of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  crimes the lowest priority for the police department.\par \par \uc2 In effect, that would mean officers have to investigate every accusation of littering before they investigate an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Texas is one of the 13 states that has a \u8220\'20\'1Ctrigger law\u8221\'20\'1D in place, which means a clinician could be charged with a first-degree felony punishable by up to life in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://capitol.texas.gov/tlodocs/87R/billtext/pdf/HB01280F.pdf#navpanes=0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 prison and a $100,000}}}\uc2  fine for performing an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  if Roe falls.\par \par \uc2 But non-enforcement obviously isn\u8217\'20\'19t a silver bullet against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans. Laws like {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://capitol.texas.gov/tlodocs/87R/billtext/pdf/SB00008F.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas\u8217\'20\'19s SB 8}}}\uc2 , which bans \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at six weeks, allow individuals to sue \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers. Those aren\u8217\'20\'19t criminal cases, so law enforcement officials have little power over them, making the law difficult to challenge in court.\par \par \uc2 Furthermore, in the event of a total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, many clinics will close \u8211\'20\'13 afraid of legal repercussions and strapped for cash without patients. And even if localities vow to protect individuals, that might not provide sufficient reassurance.\par \par \uc2 There haven\u8217\'20\'19t been many instances \u8211\'20\'13 the civil war would be one of them \u8211\'20\'13 where you will see as much interstate conflict\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe biggest issue here is whether or not any clinic will [exist in] San Antonio,\u8221\'20\'1D said district attorney Joe Gonzales, of Bexar county in Texas, who has also pledged non-enforcement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C[A ban] is not going to make women any safer. What you\u8217\'20\'19re going to see is a lot of backroom procedures being done, jeopardizing the health and possibly the life of the woman,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRegardless of whether your local prosecutor says he won\u8217\'20\'19t prosecute, it is going to have a major chilling effect,\u8221\'20\'1D Descano said. \u8220\'20\'1CWith stances like ours, we\u8217\'20\'19re playing for time, we\u8217\'20\'19re limiting the damage \u8211\'20\'13 but we\u8217\'20\'19re not undoing the worst parts of these \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans,\u8221\'20\'1D he says.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22\u8226\'20\'22\u8226\'20\'22\par \par \uc2 Rachel Rebouch\u233\'00\'E9, the interim dean at the Temple University School of Law, recently co-wrote a paper about some of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://scholarship.law.pitt.edu/fac_articles/517/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 legal quandaries that will arise over the enforcement}}}\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws if Roe v Wade is overturned. She raises a number of potential obstacles to those hoping to ignore future \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans.\par \par \uc2 The state might fight non-enforcement with all its might, punishing localities and overriding their sovereignty, she says. That might mean passing laws to ensure state enforcement trumps local control, neutralizing any local efforts to direct funds or priorities away from \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  cases. Or it could mean forcing counties to collect information on reported \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Ccrimes\u8221\'20\'1D, therefore stymieing any efforts to forego investigations. It could even mean states appointing special prosecutors to enforce \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws if DAs refuse.\par \par \uc2 But Rebouch\u233\'00\'E9 says such measures would be time-consuming and costly and could result in further retaliation and stalemates \u8211\'20\'13 not to mention backlash at the ballot box \u8211\'20\'13 enhancing local prosecutors\u8217\'20\'19 chances of success.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou could envisage an uneasy truce, with [a total ban] being the state\u8217\'20\'19s public policy, but with some pockets retaining limited access, because of the costs of trying to make a ban work,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 This is to say nothing of the conflicts that may arise between states that ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and those that choose to expand access. According to Rebouch\u233\'00\'E9, we are in an unusual moment in American history, where basic principles of inter-state conduct \u8211\'20\'13 such as cooperation between states; the sovereignty of each state within its own borders; and a general willingness of states to comply with criminal extradition requests \u8211\'20\'13 are under threat.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere haven\u8217\'20\'19t been many instances in American history \u8211\'20\'13 the civil war would be one of them \u8211\'20\'13 where you will see as much interstate conflict,\u8221\'20\'1D she says. She points to a recent bill that was weighed and eventually blocked in Missouri , which would have allowed individuals to sue anyone attempting to help a patient travel across state lines to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . These sorts of attempts may become more commonplace, and possibly have more success, if Roe falls.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMissouri, trying to apply its policy across its borders, is like Nebraska saying you can\u8217\'20\'19t gamble in Las Vegas. We just don\u8217\'20\'19t expect that\u8217\'20\'19s how states work,\u8221\'20\'1D Rebouch\u233\'00\'E9 says.\par \par \uc2 But on the local level, officials are hopeful their pledges will make a difference. As Gonzales of Bexar puts it:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor now, the way the present state of law is: I get the final say. I have the ability to make those calls. And until the law changes, that\u8217\'20\'19s how it\u8217\'20\'19s going to be,\u8221\'20\'1D he says.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 This article was amended on 15 June 2022 to correct the spelling of Rachel Rebouch\u233\'00\'E9\u8217\'20\'19s last name.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220614ei6e001e1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
