\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Democrats voice concerns over Biden\u8217\'20\'19s Saudi trip: \u8216\'20\'18Their values are not ours\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein \par \uc2 5,782 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 June 2022\par 20:25 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 President to visit Israel and Saudi Arabia on first Middle East tripJanuary 6 panel postpones hearing over technical issuesAt least 108 Republican candidates back election lie \u8211\'20\'13 analysisGarland watching hearings amid pressure to investigate TrumpSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 Congress was at the center of the action today, where the January 6 committee {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/14/trump-republicans-primary-elections-jan-6-hearings-biden-us-politics-live-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-62a893e58f0824f03c0cc079#block-62a893e58f0824f03c0cc079"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced the surprise postponement of its Wednesday hearing}}}\uc2 . Meanwhile, the top Senate Republican {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/14/trump-republicans-primary-elections-jan-6-hearings-biden-us-politics-live-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-62a8d48a8f0892aa32e163f0#block-62a8d48a8f0892aa32e163f0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said he would support the gun control compromise}}}\uc2  reached with Democrats, while the House {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/14/trump-republicans-primary-elections-jan-6-hearings-biden-us-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-62a8ddaf8f0824f03c0cc459#block-62a8ddaf8f0824f03c0cc459"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voted to approve}}}\uc2  a bill to improve security around the supreme court, sending it to the president\u8217\'20\'19s desk.\par \par \uc2 Other top stories today:\par \par \uc2 * President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  made official{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/14/trump-republicans-primary-elections-jan-6-hearings-biden-us-politics-live-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-62a88ff38f0876830e02b711#block-62a88ff38f0876830e02b711"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 his plans to visit Saudi Arabia}}}\uc2 , which is widely seen as a bid to increase oil supply and lower gas prices at home. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/14/trump-republicans-primary-elections-jan-6-hearings-biden-us-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-62a8af138f0824f03c0cc20b#block-62a8af138f0824f03c0cc20b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Several Democrats have expressed disapproval over the visit}}}\uc2 , citing the kingdom\u8217\'20\'19s human rights record.\par \par \uc2 * The president meanwhile traveled to in Philadelphia to address a convention of the \uc2 AFL-CIO\uc2  trade union federation, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/14/trump-republicans-primary-elections-jan-6-hearings-biden-us-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-62a8b4868f0824f03c0cc26b#block-62a8b4868f0824f03c0cc26b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in which he defended his economic record and attacked Republican policies}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * A top Biden ally in the Senate proposed levying {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/14/trump-republicans-primary-elections-jan-6-hearings-biden-us-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-62a8d0278f0876830e02baa1#block-62a8d0278f0876830e02baa1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a windfall tax on oil companies}}}\uc2  as Democrats try to convince voters corporate greed is fueling record-high gas prices.\par \par \uc2 * An investigation by the \uc2 Capitol Police{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/14/trump-republicans-primary-elections-jan-6-hearings-biden-us-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-62a8e0798f0876830e02bb33#block-62a8e0798f0876830e02bb33"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 determined}}}\uc2  a Republican House representative did not give Trump supporters a tour of the building the day before the January 6 attack.\par \par \uc2 * It\u8217\'20\'19s about to get really hot in America. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/14/extreme-heat-humidity-100m-americans-stay-indoors"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The National Weather Service is advising more than 100 million people to stay indoors due to high humidity and temperatures.}}}\par \par \uc2 The US politics live blog will return on Wednesday, with the supreme court set to announce more decisions at 10am ET.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Republican Party is launching a nine-day \u8220\'20\'1Celection integrity\u8221\'20\'1D tour throughout Wisconsin, less than two months before the battleground state\u8217\'20\'19s primary elections.\par \par \uc2 The tour, which begins Wednesday, will start in La Crosse, Wisconsin and go through Wisconsin\u8217\'20\'19s most liberal cities, including the state\u8217\'20\'19s capital, Madison. Planned events will include an appearance from conservative former state Supreme Court judge Daniel Kelly.\par \par \uc2 The tour has already received pushback from those who say it is meant to spread lies that the 2020 election was fraudulent ahead of the primaries and November\u8217\'20\'19s midterm election.\par \par \uc2 Republicans have argued that the roundtable events are meant to recruit poll workers, voting deputies, and other election day staff as well as connect campaign staff with volunteers.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Capitol Police\uc2  have determined that a Republican House representative did not give a tour to Trump supporters the day before the January 6 attack.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/06/14/politics/barry-loudermilk-reconnaissance-tour-capitol-police/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN reports}}}\uc2  that the investigation into \uc2 Barry Loudermilk\uc2  of Georgia was requested by the chair and vice chair of the House committee investigating the insurrection, over allegations he was seen hosting visitors on 5 January, 2021.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere is no evidence that Representative Loudermilk entered the U.S. Capitol with this group on January 5, 2021,\u8221\'20\'1D Capitol Police Chief Tom Manger wrote to the top Republican on the House Administration Committee. \u8220\'20\'1CWe train our officers on being alert for people conducting surveillance or reconnaissance, and we do not consider any of the activities we observed as suspicious.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Following the attack on the Capitol, several Democrats accused their Republican colleagues of granting tours to people who went on to storm the building as Congress was meeting to certify \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s election win.\par \par \uc2 According to CNN:\par \par \uc2 Manger said the video shows Loudermilk with \u8220\'20\'1Ca group of approximately 12 people which later grew to 15 people\u8221\'20\'1D walking through the Capitol office buildings on January 5. It also states that the group of visitors did not \u8220\'20\'1Cappear in any tunnels that would lead them to the US Capitol.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 House Republicans suggested they may release video they believe exonerates Loudermilk of any insinuation that he led a so-called \u8220\'20\'1Creconnaissance\u8221\'20\'1D tour the night before the January 6 riot.\par \par \uc2 The House select committee declined to comment on Manger\u8217\'20\'19s letter.\par \par \uc2 The letter the committee sent to Loudermilk last month indicated the panel has reviewed evidence that \u8220\'20\'1Cdirectly contradicts\u8221\'20\'1D previous claims by Republican lawmakers who said security footage from the days before January 6 shows there were \u8220\'20\'1Cno tours, no large groups, no one with MAGA hats on\u8221\'20\'1D at the US Capitol complex.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBased on our review of evidence in the Select Committee\u8217\'20\'19s possession, we believe you have information regarding a tour you led through parts of the Capitol complex on January 5, 2021,\u8221\'20\'1D Chairman \uc2 Bennie Thompson\uc2 , a Democrat from Mississippi, and Vice Chairwoman \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 , a Republican from Wyoming, wrote at the time.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 The House has passed a measure to increase security for the supreme court, sending it to the president\u8217\'20\'19s desk for his signature.\par \par \uc2 enltrA vote was requested and postponed on S. 4160 \u8211\'20\'13 Supreme Court Police Parity Act of 2022. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/CcET8jSBAI"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/CcET8jSBAI}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 House Press Gallery (@HouseDailyPress) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/HouseDailyPress/status/1536754355000442885?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 14, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The Senate had unanimously approved the measure back in May, but the House delayed its passage. Republicans in the Senate began attacking Democrats over their failure to pass the measure following last week\u8217\'20\'19s arrest of a man who is charged {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/08/brett-kavanaugh-home-man-arrested-supreme-court-justice"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 with planning to kill justice Brett Kavanaugh}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2022/may/10/us-supreme-court-security-senate-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Senate approves beefed-up security for US supreme court after \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  leak}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is meeting with attorneys and activists ahead of a widely expected supreme court decision that could weaken or overturn nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 enltrVP Harris meeting with legal experts and activist on pending \uc2 SCOTUS\uc2  decision on Roe: \u8220\'20\'1CI do believe that overturning Roe could clear the way for challenges to other fundamental rights\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Named women\u8217\'20\'19s data privacy, IVF, contraception, gay and trans rights {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/qNZnyUEiqo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/qNZnyUEiqo}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jordan Fabian (@Jordanfabian) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Jordanfabian/status/1536781182909702144?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 14, 2022}}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/06/13/politics/kamala-harris-roe-v-wade/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN reports}}}\uc2  that Harris has been encouraged by people outside the Biden administration to lead the charge against any supreme court decision restricting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as a way to better connect with voters. The network quoted an unnamed official as saying Harris\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cgoals really have been around ensuring that people in this country have an understanding of what is at stake here.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The supreme court will issue another batch of decisions on Wednesday beginning at 10 am eastern time, though it\u8217\'20\'19s unknown if that will include the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  case.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republican Senate leader signals support for bipartisan gun compromise\par \par \uc2 The Senate\u8217\'20\'19s top Republican \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  said he will support the compromise measure on gun control reached with Democrats over the weekend.\par \par \uc2 The two parties have seldom found agreement on gun control legislation, and McConnell\u8217\'20\'19s endorsement sends a positive signal that the proposal will win enough votes from his party to pass the evenly divided Senate.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf it leads to a piece of legislation, I intend to support it,\u8221\'20\'1D McConnell said at a press conference. \u8220\'20\'1CI think it\u8217\'20\'19s progress for the country, and I think the bipartisan group has done the best they can to get total support.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 While the bill hasn\u8217\'20\'19t been written yet, it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t go as far as many Democrats would like, such as by raising the age to buy an assault weapon to 21 from 18. Many of its provisions focus on improving mental health, as well as offering states money to implement programs intended to stop mass shootings such as those in Uvalde, Texas and Buffalo, New York.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/12/us-senators-bipartisan-gun-control-deal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US senators reach bipartisan gun control deal after recent mass shootings }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 One of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s Senate allies has an idea for lowering gas prices: levy new taxes on oil companies\u8217\'20\'19 profits.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2022-06-14/biden-ally-floats-21-surtax-on-oil-profits-to-blunt-inflation?sref=fqqmZ8gi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bloomberg reports}}}\uc2  that Democratic senator \uc2 Ron Wyden\uc2  will propose putting a 21 percent tax on petroleum companies with profit margins above 10 percent. The idea comes after the average gas price crossed the $5 a gallon level, which the White House has increasingly looked to blame on forces beyond its control, particularly the disruptions to global markets caused by Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Progressive Democrats have meanwhile sought to convince voters that profit-seeking corporations are to blame for the overall spike in inflation Americans are feeling, and last week, Biden took aim at \uc2 Exxon Mobil\uc2 , saying the oil giant {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=25AKNA28nBY"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cmade more money than God}}}\uc2  this year.\par \par \uc2 Wyden\u8217\'20\'19s proposal, which has yet to be released publicly, would however need the approval of all 50 Democrats to make it through the Senate, and tweaks to the tax code were among the contentious issues the party couldn\u8217\'20\'19t reach an agreement on during last year\u8217\'20\'19s unsuccessful attempt to pass Build Back better.\par \par \uc2 From the article:\par \par \uc2 Taxing excessive oil company profits is one of many policy ideas under consideration in the White House, two administration officials said. Yet internally, aides remain concerned such a tax could hurt ongoing efforts to boost the supply of oil.\par \par \uc2 If combined with a gasoline rebate, a windfall profits tax would both deter supply and encourage fuel demand, said Kevin Book, managing director of research firm ClearView Energy Partners LLC. \u8220\'20\'1CIt is the opposite of balancing the market.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 An idea out of Treasury to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/06/09/politics/white-house-oil-profits/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 place a cap on }}}\uc2  the price of Russian oil, alongside European allies, has gained far more traction inside the administration.\par \par \uc2 Wyden\u8217\'20\'19s plan would also impose a 25% stock buyback tax for oil and gas companies that repurchase their own shares, Wyden spokeswoman Ashley Schapitl confirmed. Both levies apply to oil and gas companies with at least $1 billion in revenue and would expire at the end of 2025, according to the people briefed on the plan.\par \par \uc2 Wyden also proposes to eliminate an accounting benefit, known as last-in first-out, or LIFO, that can deliver tax breaks for oil and gas companies with at least $1 billion in revenue starting in 2023.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s been another sentence handed down over the January 6 attack, this time of a former city councilmember in West Virginia.\par \par \uc2 Eric Barber was sentenced to 45 days in jail for entering the Capitol during the insurrection, as well as a seven-day suspended sentence for stealing a charging station belonging to \uc2 C-SPAN\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://wvmetronews.com/2022/06/14/former-parkersburg-councilman-is-sentenced-to-45-days-after-jan-6-riot/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 West Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s MetroNews reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The former city councilmember in Parkersburg, West Virginia, also received 24 months of federal probation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19re too old and you\u8217\'20\'19re too accomplished and you\u8217\'20\'19re too smart to get involved in nonsense like this,\u8221\'20\'1D federal judge Christopher Cooper said during the Thursday sentencing.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is not about the First Amendment. You are free to express your views. You\u8217\'20\'19re free to support any political candidate or positions or issues that you want. I encourage that. But enough of this nonsense, OK?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 According to MetroNews:\par \par \uc2 Barber, 43, was being sentenced today in U.S. District Court for the District of Columbia after pleading guilty to two misdemeanors.\par \par \uc2 One is a count of parading, demonstrating or picketing in a Capitol Building. The other is theft, an accusation that Barber stole a charging station belonging to a \uc2 C-SPAN\uc2  employee.\par \par \uc2 He has to pay $500 restitution as his share of damage to the Capitol that day, and he has to pay back \uc2 C-SPAN\uc2  a little less than $60 for the charger that he took home.\par \par \uc2 Barber was not accused of violence that day, but prosecutors noted that he wore a Kevlar helmet and went to Washington, D.C. to \u8220\'20\'1Cgo {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://wvmetronews.com/2022/05/13/west-virginia-jan-6-suspect-wanted-to-go-punch-a-antifa-terrorist-in-the-face/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 punch a Antifa terrorist}}}\uc2  in the face,\u8221\'20\'1D referring to the loosely-knit antifascist activists sometimes accused of violence themselves.\par \par \uc2 Prosecutors underscored that Barber entered the Capitol as sirens blared and broken glass was apparent, entering not only the areas that are commonly open to the public but also entering a restricted hallway outside House Speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s office. Prosecutors said Barber wound up in that hallway twice \u8212\'20\'14 the second time after being told to leave. Barber said he was lost.\par \par \uc2 But Barber and his public defense attorney emphasized that he had expressed remorse about what happened that day to local media, to investigators, to Congress\u8217\'20\'19s January 6th Committee and to the judge.\par \par \uc2 Judge Cooper took note of all those factors.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s troubling that you still seem to have a mindset of \u8216\'20\'18There\u8217\'20\'19s a bully out there. I need to prime for the fight.\u8217\'20\'19 You did not go for self-defense, but you went with the helmet, ready to punch somebody or affirmatively engage in violence,\u8221\'20\'1D Cooper said.\par \par \uc2 Barber sentencing memo began with a particularly direct quote.\par \par \uc2 enltrStrongest lede I\u8217\'20\'19ve seen yet in a Jan. 6 defendant\u8217\'20\'19s sentencing memo. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/3Es2hM4Bpl"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/3Es2hM4Bpl}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ryan J. Reilly (@ryanjreilly) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ryanjreilly/status/1534539291199787010?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 8, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 There is still a lot of buzz about the House panel investigating the January 6, 2021 insurrection by extremist supporters of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , as reports spill out about disagreements over whether to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/13/merrick-garland-trump-january-6-capitol-attack"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 refer Trump for criminal prosecution}}}\uc2  or just lay out the evidence and let others deduce, etc, as well as today\u8217\'20\'19s abrupt {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/14/trump-republicans-primary-elections-jan-6-hearings-biden-us-politics-live-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-62a893e58f0824f03c0cc079#block-62a893e58f0824f03c0cc079"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 postponement}}}\uc2  of Hearing No. 3.\par \par \uc2 Most of these tweets speak for themselves.\par \par \uc2 enltrCommittee needs to keep on track. No more referral talk in public. Keep to the schedule. There has been unity and absence of grandstanding so far. They must keep it that way.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jennifer 'I stand with Ukraine' Rubin ???????? (@JRubinBlogger) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JRubinBlogger/status/1536756187076730880?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 14, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Larry Tribe.\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CYou do not get to arm-twist officials or send the mob to the Capitol because you really, really think you won.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/4xtlAfrYf5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/4xtlAfrYf5}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Laurence Tribe (@tribelaw) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/tribelaw/status/1536748424409776128?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 14, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 George Conway, cheeky.\par \par \uc2 enltrA \uc2 Twitter\uc2  contest\u8212\'20\'14let's see who can come up with the best answer for:\par \par \uc2 ??. ?????? ???????? ?????????? ?????????? ???????? ???? ???????? ???? ?????????? ???? ?? ?????????? ?????????\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 George Conway?? (@gtconway3d) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/gtconway3d/status/1536674582236696578?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 14, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Conway on Zimmer\par \par \uc2 enltrExcellent thread. ?? ?? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/scpfcj4SR8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/scpfcj4SR8}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 George Conway?? (@gtconway3d) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/gtconway3d/status/1536761231201259523?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 14, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Scuitto on Trump\par \par \uc2 enltrAs you watch the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/January6thHearings?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #January6thHearings}}}\uc2  remember the principal source of disinformation in the 2016 election was foreign. In 2020, it was the sitting US president. And his lies succeeded in convincing a majority of GOP voters the election was stolen.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jim Sciutto (@jimsciutto) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jimsciutto/status/1536757175313485824?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 14, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 Midday summary\par \par \uc2 Much of today\u8217\'20\'19s action has occurred in Congress, where the January 6 committee {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/14/trump-republicans-primary-elections-jan-6-hearings-biden-us-politics-live-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-62a893e58f0824f03c0cc079#block-62a893e58f0824f03c0cc079"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced the surprise postponement of its Wednesday hearing}}}\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/14/trump-republicans-primary-elections-jan-6-hearings-biden-us-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-62a8aa778f0892aa32e161a5#block-62a8aa778f0892aa32e161a5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Senate still doesn\u8217\'20\'19t have the bill text of its gun control compromise to vote on}}}\uc2 , but the House is moving forward with the vote on a a bill to increase security for the supreme court, which the upper chamber has already approved.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is going on:\par \par \uc2 * President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has made official{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/14/trump-republicans-primary-elections-jan-6-hearings-biden-us-politics-live-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-62a88ff38f0876830e02b711#block-62a88ff38f0876830e02b711"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 his plans to visit Saudi Arabia}}}\uc2 , which is widely seen as a bid to increase oil supply and lower gas prices at home. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/14/trump-republicans-primary-elections-jan-6-hearings-biden-us-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-62a8af138f0824f03c0cc20b#block-62a8af138f0824f03c0cc20b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Several Democrats have expressed disapproval over the visit}}}\uc2 , citing the kingdom\u8217\'20\'19s human rights record.\par \par \uc2 * The president was meanwhile in Philadelphia to address a convention of the \uc2 AFL-CIO\uc2  trade union federation, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/14/trump-republicans-primary-elections-jan-6-hearings-biden-us-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-62a8b4868f0824f03c0cc26b#block-62a8b4868f0824f03c0cc26b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in which he defended his economic record and attacked Republican policies}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * The votes of Republicans in the Senate will be crucial to passing the gun control bill, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/14/trump-republicans-primary-elections-jan-6-hearings-biden-us-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-62a8b6148f0876830e02b962#block-62a8b6148f0876830e02b962"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more of the party\u8217\'20\'19s senators offered their thoughts on the legislation}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * It\u8217\'20\'19s about to get really hot in America. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/14/extreme-heat-humidity-100m-americans-stay-indoors"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The National Weather Service is advising more than 100 million people to stay indoors due to high humidity and temperatures.}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republicans will be crucial in determining whether the bipartisan gun control proposal makes it through the Senate, and more lawmakers are reacting to the deal reached over the weekend.\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CI think the framework is very encouraging,\u8221\'20\'1D GOP Sen. Lisa Murkowski just told me of the guns package. Says she\u8217\'20\'19s eager to see the details but sounds very positive about it. She was not one of the 10 Republicans who signed onto the framework. Bill text still needs to be drafted\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Manu Raju (@mkraju) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1536745269185880064?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 14, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrThune, No. 2 Republican, uncertain whether he would back Senate\u8217\'20\'19s guns package. While he noted there have been some successes, there are \u8220\'20\'1Creal concerns about due process\u8221\'20\'1D with how states adopt red flag laws.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThose are things that are going to have to be addressed,\u8221\'20\'1D he told me\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Manu Raju (@mkraju) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1536725407399129089?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 14, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrBut \uc2 Bill Cassidy\uc2 , R who backs framework, said the bill would mandate due process in red flag laws.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou can argue that some state red flag laws do not have due process. we mandate it. So I think as people become acquainted with that, Republicans will like that,\u8221\'20\'1D he told us\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Manu Raju (@mkraju) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1536725717068795907?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 14, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CFederal government, we don't need to be pushing red flag laws,\u8221\'20\'1D Tommy Tuberville told me when asked about the guns package. \u8220\'20\'1CThe states, if the states want to get involved in it, they need to get involved in it.\u8221\'20\'1D Plan would incentivize states to enact red flag laws.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Manu Raju (@mkraju) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1536727668686835714?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 14, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrAsked him how to take away guns from mentally ill. He said: \u8220\'20\'1CWell let's look at what they've got proposed. I haven't looked at all of it. But let's look\u8230\'20\'26and see if they've got anything in there to prohibit mentally ill patients from having guns, anybody that's having problems\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Manu Raju (@mkraju) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1536728256782688258?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 14, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Democrats are expected to back the proposal even though it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t do all of what they want, such as raising the age to purchase an assault rifle to 21 from 18. To avoid a filibuster, at least 10 Republicans in the Senate will need to vote for the bill, which also must clear the Democrat-controlled House of Representatives.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden has used his speech at the \uc2 AFL-CIO\uc2  convention in Philadelphia to promote his handling of the economy make a pitch for keeping Democrats in office.\par \par \uc2 As CBS News\u8217\'20\'19s Ed O\u8217\'20\'19Keefe reports:\par \par \uc2 enltrTODAY: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @POTUS}}}\uc2  Biden addresses a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AFLCIO?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @AFLCIO}}}\uc2  convention in Philly to tout US economic strength: low unemployment rates, states and cities being buoyed by American Rescue Plan and Bipartisan Infrastructure Law. White House says he\u8217\'20\'19ll reiterate fighting inflation \u8220\'20\'1Cis his top priority.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ed O'Keefe (@edokeefe) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/edokeefe/status/1536672237021024256?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 14, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrAlso expect some election year contrasts: Biden/Dems would \u8220\'20\'1Cask the wealthy to pay their fair share\u8221\'20\'1D while {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenRickScott?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @SenRickScott}}}\uc2  and \u8220\'20\'1CCongressional Republicans\u8221\'20\'1D would \u8220\'20\'1Cput Medicare, Social Security, and Medicaid on the chopping block every five years.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ed O'Keefe (@edokeefe) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/edokeefe/status/1536672524846735363?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 14, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrA new election-year clarion call of sorts from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @POTUS}}}\uc2  Biden in his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AFLCIO?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @AFLCIO}}}\uc2  speech: \u8220\'20\'1CAmerica still has a choice to make. A choice between a government by the few, for the few. Or a government for all of us, democracy for all of us, an economy where all of us have a fair shot.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ed O'Keefe (@edokeefe) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/edokeefe/status/1536741058717044736?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 14, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The president also took special notice of a Republican proposal to make all federal legislation expire after five years, asking, \u8220\'20\'1CHow well are you going to sleep at night knowing that every five years, Ted Cruz and the other ultra-MAGA Republicans are going to vote on whether you have Social Security, Medicare and Medicaid?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democrats in the Senate are raising their eyebrows at Biden\u8217\'20\'19s decision to travel to Saudi Arabia, objecting to the country\u8217\'20\'19s human rights record and worrying the visit won\u8217\'20\'19t meaningfully lower gas prices.\par \par \uc2 As Oregon\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Ron Wyden\uc2  told Manu Raju of CNN:\par \par \uc2 enltrDem pushback this morning on Biden\u8217\'20\'19s decision to meet with MBS. \u8220\'20\'1CI don't see any evidence that the Saudis are going to significantly lower gasoline prices,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Ron Wyden\uc2  said.On the other hand, I see their horrendous human rights record.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Manu Raju (@mkraju) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1536733087186534401?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 14, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s Maryland\u8217\'20\'19s Ben Cardin, who referenced the murder of Jamal Khashoggi:\par \par \uc2 enltrAsked about WH sidestepping queries yesterday on responsibility for Khashoggi murder, Cardin told us: \u8220\'20\'1CI hope they\u8217\'20\'19ll be very clear in the conversation. America's strength is in our values.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Manu Raju (@mkraju) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1536733088528617474?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 14, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Kaitlan Collins, also of CNN, heard this from Illinois\u8217\'20\'19s Dick Durbin:\par \par \uc2 enltr'I have mixed feelings on this and if the President called me, I would say, 'Mr. President, you can't trust these people. Their standards are not our standards, their values are not ours,'" Sen. Dick Durbin says about President Biden's upcoming trip to Saudi Arabia.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kaitlan Collins (@kaitlancollins) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kaitlancollins/status/1536687448415260673?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 14, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senate majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  said the text of the gun control compromise reached by senators this weekend should come in the \u8220\'20\'1Ccoming days.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Before the chamber can vote on the proposal, it needs to see a bill first, following {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/12/us-senators-bipartisan-gun-control-deal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 this weekend\u8217\'20\'19s announcement}}}\uc2  of an agreement that could pass the evenly divided Senate.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.c-span.org/video/?521014-1/senate-session&live&vod"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 In a speech on the floor}}}\uc2 , Schumer said he spoke with Republican senator \uc2 John Cornyn\uc2  and Democratic senator \uc2 Chris Murphy\uc2  and \u8220\'20\'1Cthey are working with the urgency the situation demands and they are hopeful the legislative text can be finalized in the coming days,\u8221\'20\'1D Schumer said, before reiterating his pledge to bring the measure to a vote \u8220\'20\'1Cas soon as possible.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 President Biden is currently addressing the \uc2 AFL-CIO\uc2  trade union federation\u8217\'20\'19s Quadrennial Constitutional Convention, which you can watch {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/live/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 , as he looks to burnish his credentials among a key Democratic voting block. For \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/steven-greenhouse"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Steven Greenhouse}}}\uc2  takes a look at the union drives at \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  and Amazon, which, if successful, would represent major prizes for organized labor.\par \par \uc2 In a historic win in December, baristas in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2021/dec/10/this-victory-of-starbucks-employees-in-buffalo-will-reverberate-across-america"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Buffalo voted}}}\uc2  to make their \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  the first of more than 9,000 corporate-operated \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  in the US to unionize. Since then, 143 other \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  have unionized and workers at 120 other locations have petitioned for union elections.\par \par \uc2 In another historic victory, a vote count on 1 April showed that workers at an 8,300-employee Amazon warehouse in Staten Island, New York, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2022/apr/01/amazon-union-groups-see-hope-workers-vote-alabama-new-york"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 had voted}}}\uc2  to make theirs the first unionized Amazon facility in the country. Since then, however, no other Amazon warehouse has even petitioned for a union election (although workers at a 1,500-employee Amazon facility in Staten Island later {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/02/amazon-union-vote-count-new-york-warehouse"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voted to reject}}}\uc2  unionization).\par \par \uc2 So why has the \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  union drive taken off {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/apr/19/starbucks-manhattan-union-drive-reserve-roastery"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 like a rocket }}}\uc2  while the Amazon campaign is only inching along?\par \par \uc2 Isaiah Thomas, a pro-union worker at the Amazon warehouse in Bessemer, Alabama, sees many reasons for the different pace \u8211\'20\'13 and said the biggest was the different size of the workplace. \u8220\'20\'1CThere might be only 28 workers at a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/starbucks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Starbucks}}}\uc2 , but 6,000 at our Amazon warehouse. In terms of what the organizing committee has to do at \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 , it\u8217\'20\'19s not a lot of people. They can keep a close-knit friendship. They can coordinate things closely.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/14/starbucks-amazon-union-drives"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Why is Starbucks\u8217\'20\'19 union drive speeding ahead while Amazon\u8217\'20\'19s stumbles?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 The White House has confirmed that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will meet Saudia Arabia\u8217\'20\'19s crown prince and de-factor ruler \uc2 Mohammed bin Salman\uc2  on his visit to the country.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C Yes, we can expect the President to see the crown prince as well,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden\u8217\'20\'19s press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  told reporters on Air Force One.\par \par \uc2 The announcement is significant because relations between the two men have often been frosty. As my colleague {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/julianborger"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Julian Borger}}}\uc2  reported, \uc2 Prince Mohammed\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Creportedly declined to take a call from \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  last month, showing his displeasure at the administration\u8217\'20\'19s restrictions on arms sales; what he saw as its insufficient response to attacks on Saudi Arabia by Houthi forces in Yemen; its publication of a report into the Saudi regime\u8217\'20\'19s 2018 murder of the dissident and \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  columnist Jamal Khashoggi; and Biden\u8217\'20\'19s prior refusal to deal in person with the crown prince.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Prince Mohammed\uc2  may also be banking on a return of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to the White House in 2024, whose prior administration was much friendlier with Riyadh.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/24/saudi-arabia-kushner-trump-biden-mohammed-bin-salman"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Saudis\u8217\'20\'19 Biden snub suggests crown prince still banking on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s return}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 The postponed January 6 hearing will likely take place next week, committee member Pete Aguilar said.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.c-span.org/video/?521019-1/house-democratic-caucus-leaders-news-conference"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Speaking at a press conference of the House Democratic Caucus Leaders}}}\uc2 , the California Democrat downplayed the impact of the hearing\u8217\'20\'19s postponement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe schedule has always been fluid. So we\u8217\'20\'19re going to move forward and have a Thursday hearing and then get ready for hearings next week as well,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, predicting the session originally set for Wednesday will \u8220\'20\'1Cmove to likely next week.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He didn\u8217\'20\'19t elaborate on the reasons for the change in schedule, but said, \u8220\'20\'1CWe just want to make sure that you all have the time and space to digest all the information that we\u8217\'20\'19re putting out there.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The committee\u8217\'20\'19s next hearing is scheduled for Thursday, June 16.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Sometime soon, perhaps as soon as tomorrow, the supreme court will hand down a decision that could dismantle or greatly weaken \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights codified by Roe v Wade. If that happens, \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/14/progressive-prosecutors-refuse-abortion-bans-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Poppy Noor}}}\uc2  reports that prosecutors in a number of states are preparing to act to keep \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  accessible.\par \par \uc2 Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general, Dana Nessel, never thought she would have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But after finding herself pregnant with triplets in 2002, she faced an unenviable choice: abort one, or miscarry all three. \u8220\'20\'1CI took my doctor\u8217\'20\'19s advice, which I should have been able to do,\u8221\'20\'1D she says in a phone interview.\par \par \uc2 Nessel plans to protect that same right for residents of her state if {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  is overturned this summer , as a leaked supreme court draft opinion indicates is all but certain.\par \par \uc2 If the draft opinion stands, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/article/2021/10/26-states-are-certain-or-likely-ban-abortion-without-roe-heres-which-ones-and-why"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 26 states are likely or certain to ban \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 . In Michigan, a 1931 law would be triggered, making \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  illegal in almost all cases except to save the life of the pregnant person.\par \par \uc2 Nessel says she won\u8217\'20\'19t enforce the ban in Michigan, along with at least a dozen law enforcement officials across the country \u8211\'20\'13 a bold statement that sets the US up for a complex legal landscape with different enforcement regimes in different states, and even within them.\par \par \uc2 These officials are likely to face swift backlash from the right, including, in some cases, retaliation from state authorities who will demand they enforce the law as written. But they are determined to press ahead.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/14/progressive-prosecutors-refuse-abortion-bans-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18This is not hopeless\u8217\'20\'19: the progressive prosecutors who vow not to enforce \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  bans}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 At its hearing yesterday, the January 6 committee built its case that Trump knew his fraud claims were baseless but pushed them anyway, fueling the attack on the Capitol. My colleague {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/lauren-gambino"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lauren Gambino}}}\uc2  reports on how the hearing\u8217\'20\'19s revelations may not be enough to dislodge belief in the \u8220\'20\'1CBig Lie\u8221\'20\'1D from the Republican party.\par \par \uc2 The House committee investigating the January 6 insurrection charged on Monday that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Clit the fuse\u8221\'20\'1D that fueled the most violent assault on the US Capitol in more than two centuries with his groundless claim that the election was stolen.\par \par \uc2 For those tuned in, the committee meticulously charted the origins and spread of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cbig lie\u8221\'20\'1D, tapping a trove of evidence and interviews to show that the former president was told repeatedly that the election had been free and fair and peddled his myths anyway.\par \par \uc2 But in Republican politics and the conservative media ecosystem, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s myth of a stolen election rages on, uncontrolled in the Republican party as it seeks to surge back into power in November\u8217\'20\'19s midterm elections.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/13/trump-big-lie-january-6-hearing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Despite January 6 panel\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to stamp out Trump\u8217\'20\'19s big lie, the myth rages on }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Wednesday's January 6 hearing postponed\par \par \uc2 The January 6 committee has announced the postponement of its hearing scheduled for Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 enltrJUST IN: Jan. 6 committee says hearing on June 15 at 10a ET \u8212\'20\'14 Wednesday\u8217\'20\'19s hearing \u8212\'20\'14 has been postponed. No explanation at the moment.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Hugo Lowell (@hugolowell) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hugolowell/status/1536699306341720065?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 14, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrThis was supposed to be hearing #3 where the Jan. 6 committee would show how Trump pressured DOJ to investigate election fraud with former acting AG Rosen, his deputy Donoghue, and former assistant AG Engel as witnesses.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Hugo Lowell (@hugolowell) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hugolowell/status/1536702171936444417?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 14, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Committee member \uc2 Zoe Lofgren\uc2  blames technical reasons for the delay.\par \par \uc2 enltrJan 6 committee member {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepZoeLofgren?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @RepZoeLofgren}}}\uc2  says on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Morning_Joe?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @Morning_Joe}}}\uc2  that postponement of tomorrow's hearing on the DOJ done for technical reasons - they have to give the video team time to work, basically\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Garrett Haake (@GarrettHaake) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GarrettHaake/status/1536701889617747975?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 14, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 With gas prices at record highs, Biden to head to Saudi Arabia\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s official: President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will visit Saudi Arabia, a country he once vowed to turn into \u8220\'20\'1Ca pariah\u8221\'20\'1D but which may play a crucial role in lowering US pump prices from their record levels.\par \par \uc2 The visit, which will be coupled with a trip to Israel, comes as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/biden-approval-rating/?ex_cid=rrpromo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s approval rating slumps due to a wave of inflation}}}\uc2  caused in part by energy prices that have risen since Russia invaded Ukraine. Saudi Arabia is a major oil producer, and Biden is looking for ways to increase the global oil supply {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/11/us-gas-price-inflation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to lower pump prices at home}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/02/biden-saudi-arabia-oil-russia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden to visit Saudi Arabia in push to lower oil prices and punish Russia}}}\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s no hint of this dynamic in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2022/06/14/statement-by-press-secretary-karine-jean-pierre-on-president-bidens-travel-to-israel-the-west-bank-and-saudi-arabia/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the White House statement announcing the trip}}}\uc2 , which focuses on Saudia Arabia chairing the \uc2 Gulf Cooperation Council (GCC) \uc2 regional group.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe President will... travel to Jeddah, Saudi Arabia, which is the current chair of the GCC and the venue for this gathering of nine leaders from across the region, at the invitation of King \uc2 Salman bin Abdulaziz al-Saud\uc2 . The President appreciates King Salman\u8217\'20\'19s leadership and his invitation. He looks forward to this important visit to Saudi Arabia, which has been a strategic partner of the United States for nearly eight decades,\u8221\'20\'1D press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  wrote.\par \par \uc2 In Israel, Biden \u8220\'20\'1Cwill meet with Israeli leaders to discuss Israel\u8217\'20\'19s security, prosperity, and its increasing integration into the greater region. The President will also visit the West Bank to consult with the \uc2 Palestinian Authority\uc2  and to reiterate his strong support for a two-state solution, with equal measures of security, freedom, and opportunity for the Palestinian people,\u8221\'20\'1D according to the statement.\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s ire towards Riyadh has centered on the murder of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/apr/07/turkish-court-sends-case-of-26-accused-over-khashoggi-killing-to-saudi-arabia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jamal Khashoggi}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Way back in 2020, a plank of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s successful presidential campaign was restoring bipartisanship in Congress. If all goes well for the president this week, he may soon have the chance to sign the types of compromise legislation he promised Americans.\par \par \uc2 Chief among these would be the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/12/us-senators-bipartisan-gun-control-deal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gun control measure senators negotiated over the weekend}}}\uc2 , which looks like it can get the 10 Republican votes needed to overcome a filibuster by others in the party opposed to the legislation, and which the Senate majority leader has said will be put up for consideration as soon as possible.\par \par \uc2 More immediately, the House could today vote to increase security for the supreme court after a man was arrested on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/08/brett-kavanaugh-home-man-arrested-supreme-court-justice"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 charges of trying to kill justice Brett Kavanaugh, ahead of the court\u8217\'20\'19s expected rulings that could curb \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  and expand gun rights}}}\uc2 . The bill has already passed the Senate unanimously.\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s supporters would also point to the Republican votes for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/nov/06/joe-biden-infrastructure-bill-democrats-monumental-step-forward"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 last year\u8217\'20\'19s infrastructure overhaul}}}\uc2  as a sign of his success in uniting the parties around issues affecting all Americans. But it\u8217\'20\'19s worth pointing out the massive American Rescue Plan spending bill won no Republican support, nor did Build Back Better, the president\u8217\'20\'19s marquee spending plan that ended up floundering because Democrats themselves could not find consensus over it.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 Fraud claims proliferate among Republicans despite January 6 revelations\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US Politics blog readers. Over the past few days, the January 6 committee has used its hearings to make the case that former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  bears responsibility for the attack on the Capitol. But while he\u8217\'20\'19s the most prominent promoter of the baseless claim that the 2020 election was stolen, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2022/06/14/more-than-100-gop-primary-winners-back-trumps-false-fraud-claims/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an analysis published today by the Washington Post}}}\uc2  shows at least 108 Republicans candidates for statewide office or Congress also share that belief.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is going on today:\par \par \uc2 * Senators are considering a bipartisan gun control compromise {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/12/us-senators-bipartisan-gun-control-deal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced over the weekend}}}\uc2  that\u8217\'20\'19s thought to have enough support to pass the evenly divided chamber. The bill has yet to be written, but it would represent Washington\u8217\'20\'19s response to the mass shootings in Uvalde, Texas, and Buffalo, New York.\par \par \uc2 * The House is expected to today approve a bill to increase security for the supreme court following the arrest of a man who was charged with planning {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/08/brett-kavanaugh-home-man-arrested-supreme-court-justice"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to kill Justice Brett Kavanaugh}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * The January 6 committee is taking a break from its hearings today, but will convene again on Wednesday. Expect more reactions today from across Washington to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/13/jan-6-hearing-trump-insurrection-live-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s hearing}}}\uc2 , which focused on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s promotion of fraud claims that his own officials said were baseless.\par \par \uc2 * Maine, Nevada, North Dakota and South Carolina will be holding primary elections ahead of the 8 November midterms, which will be decisive in determining the course of Washington politics over the next two years.\par \par \uc2 * The \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  is beginning its two-day meeting and could decide to make a big interest rate increase to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/jun/10/us-inflation-rate-may-2022-four-decade-high"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fight the runaway inflation}}}\uc2  that\u8217\'20\'19s badly damaged Biden\u8217\'20\'19s standing with voters. The central bankers announce their decision Wednesday at 2pm ET.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220614ei6e0020a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
