\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 First Thing: Trump repeatedly told fraud claims baseless, panel hears\b0\par\par\uc2 Nicola Slawson \par \uc2 1,553 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 June 2022\par 11:19 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 William Barr\uc2  said ex-president\u8217\'20\'19s allegations were \u8216\'20\'18bullshit\u8217\'20\'19, while several advisers told him not to declare victory on election night. Plus, The Bourne Identity at 20Don\u8217\'20\'19t already get First Thing in your inbox? Sign up here\par \par \uc2 Good morning.\par \par \uc2 The House select committee investigating the January 6 insurrection yesterday scrutinized the conspiracy theories that led a group of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s supporters to attack the US Capitol, and produced testimony damning of the former US president.\par \par \uc2 During the two-hour hearing, committee members meticulously documented how several of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s senior advisers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/13/jan-6-house-committee-second-hearing-conspiracy-theories"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 urged him not to declare victory}}}\uc2  on election night, as votes were being counted.\par \par \uc2 When Trump began spreading lies about widespread fraud in the election, some of his top aides, including the ex-attorney general and former Trump loyalist \uc2 William Barr\uc2 , repeatedly told him the claims were baseless.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe will tell the story of how \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  lost an election and knew he lost an election, and as a result of his loss decided to wage an attack on our democracy,\u8221\'20\'1D said the Democratic chair of the committee, the Mississippi congressman \uc2 Bennie Thompson\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What did they find out about Trump claiming victory on election night? Trump rejected several advisers\u8217\'20\'19 guidance to wait for more votes to be counted. Trump instead followed the advice of an \u8220\'20\'1Capparently inebriated\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  to falsely declare victory before a winner was known, \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  said at the hearing.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What has Trump said in response? After yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s hearing, Trump issued a 12-page statement calling the investigation a \u8220\'20\'1Ckangaroo court\u8221\'20\'1D and a distraction, and repeating false claims of voter fraud.\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18This is not hopeless\u8217\'20\'19: the progressive prosecutors who vow not to enforce \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans\par \par \uc2 Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general, Dana Nessel, never thought she would have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But after finding herself pregnant with triplets in 2002, she faced an unenviable choice: abort one, or miscarry all three. \u8220\'20\'1CI took my doctor\u8217\'20\'19s advice, which I should have been able to do,\u8221\'20\'1D she says in a phone interview.\par \par \uc2 Nessel plans to protect that same right for residents of her state if Roe v Wade is overturned this summer , as a leaked supreme court draft opinion indicates is all but certain, Poppy Noor writes.\par \par \uc2 If the draft opinion stands, 26 states are likely or certain to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . In Michigan, a 1931 law would be triggered, making \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  illegal in almost all cases except to save the life of the pregnant person.\par \par \uc2 Nessel says she will not enforce the ban in Michigan, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/14/progressive-prosecutors-refuse-abortion-bans-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 along with at least a dozen law enforcement officials across the country}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 a bold statement that sets the US up for a complex legal landscape with different enforcement regimes in different states, and even within them.\par \par \uc2 Steve Descano was thinking about his 10-year-old daughter when he pledged not to enforce \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans in his home county of Fairfax, Virginia. The district attorney of Bexar county in Texas, Joe Gonzales, has also pledged non-enforcement.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Will there be a backlash? Yes. These officials are likely to face swift backlash from the right, including, in some cases, retaliation from state authorities who will demand they enforce the law as written. But they are determined to press ahead.\par \par \uc2 Ukraine asks the west for huge rise in heavy artillery supply\par \par \uc2 Ukraine has called on the west to supply 300 rocket launchers, 500 tanks and 1,000 howitzers, amid concern in some quarters it is pushing its demands for Nato-standard weapons to the limit.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/13/ukraine-asks-the-west-for-huge-rise-in-heavy-artillery-supply"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 maximalist request was made publicly by Mykhailo Podolyak}}}\uc2 , a key presidential adviser, on \uc2 Twitter\uc2  yesterday where he argued that Ukraine needed \u8220\'20\'1Cheavy weapons parity\u8221\'20\'1D to defeat Russia and end the war.\par \par \uc2 He said that would require 300 multiple launch rocket systems (MLRS) \u8211\'20\'13 vastly more than seven or so committed thus far by the US and UK \u8211\'20\'13 and greater than the 60 or more that other advisers have previously said would meet its needs.\par \par \uc2 A special meeting of defence ministers takes place tomorrow in Brussels, which will be chaired by \uc2 Lloyd Austin\uc2 , the US defense secretary, to discuss future weapons donations, the third such meeting since the war began.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What\u8217\'20\'19s happening in Donbas? The intense battle for Sievierodonetsk will be remembered as one of the most brutal Europe has ever seen and is taking a \u8220\'20\'1Cterrifying\u8221\'20\'1D toll on Ukraine, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/jun/14/russia-ukraine-war-donbas-battles-most-brutal-europe-has-seen-zelenskiy-says-civilians-trapped-in-sievierodonetsk-live?page=with:block-62a813bd8f08f7f9ebefeb2a#block-62a813bd8f08f7f9ebefeb2a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy said last night}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What else is happening? Here\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/14/russia-ukraine-war-what-we-know-on-day-111-of-the-invasion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 what we know on day 111}}}\uc2  of the invasion .\par \par \uc2 In other news \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian president, \uc2 Jair Bolsonaro\uc2 , has said he believes {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/13/dom-phillips-bruno-pereira-bodies-found-brazil"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Csomething wicked\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  was done to the missing British journalist\par \par \uc2 Dom Phillips\par \par \uc2 and the Brazilian Indigenous expert\par \par \uc2 Bruno Pereira, amid unconfirmed claims their bodies had been found in the Amazon.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A growing number of prominent Christian leaders are sounding alarms about threats to democracy posed by ReAwaken America rallies where \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  loyalists \uc2 Michael Flynn\uc2  and \uc2 Roger Stone\uc2  and rightwing pastors have spread misinformation about the 2020 elections and Covid-19 vaccines, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/14/roger-stone-michael-flynn-distorting-christianity-reawaken-america"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 distorted Christian teachings}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Record flooding and rockslides\par \par \uc2 after a burst of heavy rain\par \par \uc2 prompted the rare closure last night of all five entrances to Yellowstone national park at the start of the summer tourist season, the park superintendent said. The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2022/jun/13/yellowstone-national-park-closure-flooding-mudslides"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 entire park will remain closed to visitors}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A self-described \u8220\'20\'1Cincel\u8221\'20\'1D who killed 11 people when he drove a rented van into a busy Toronto sidewalk in 2018 has been sentenced to life in prison. Alek Minassian \u8211\'20\'13 who was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/13/toronto-van-murders-court-victim-2018-attack"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 motivated by a hatred of women}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 was convicted in March of 10 counts of first-degree murder and 16 counts of attempted murder.\par \par \uc2 Stat of the day:\par \par \uc2 Search for clues as bodies of hundreds of little blue penguins wash ashore in New Zealand\par \par \uc2 The penguins lie in orderly, evenly spaced rows, wings splayed, their trademark glossy blue plumage dulled by sand. There are 183 in all, carefully collected by local people, laid out for later investigation. The birds were found at Ninety Mile Beach last week, just the latest in a phenomenon of dead penguins washing up on New Zealand\u8217\'20\'19s beaches in huge numbers. Conservation officials believe {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/14/search-for-clues-as-bodies-of-hundreds-of-little-blue-penguins-wash-ashore-in-new-zealand"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mass die-offs are becoming more frequent as climate crisis disrupts food chains}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t miss this: \u8216\'20\'18I noticed she was transgender, and remember thinking she seemed sweet and shy\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 In 2015, Raya had sworn off relationships, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/2022/jun/13/how-we-met-i-noticed-she-was-transgender-and-remember-thinking-she-seemed-sweet-and-shy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 writes Lizzie Cernik}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CI was in a kind of self-imposed celibacy,\u8221\'20\'1D she says. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m a cisgender lesbian, but I\u8217\'20\'19d made too many mistakes in love because I hadn\u8217\'20\'19t come to terms with my sexuality.\u8221\'20\'1D Towards the end of summer, she was invited to watch a women\u8217\'20\'19s roller derby match. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19d never had any interest in it before, but I\u8217\'20\'19d been told it was a very LGBTQ-inclusive sport, so I thought I\u8217\'20\'19d check it out.\u8221\'20\'1D As she walked in, she spotted a woman on the door. \u8220\'20\'1CI noticed she was transgender,\u8221\'20\'1D says Raya. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd I remember thinking she seemed sweet and shy.\u8221\'20\'1D The couple now live together in Melbourne with Kate\u8217\'20\'19s children.\par \par \uc2 \u8230\'20\'26 or this: The Bourne Identity at 20\par \par \uc2 In the early 2000s, the action movie was in mortal danger. The reliable heroes of the 80s and 90s \u8211\'20\'13 Sly, Schwarzenegger, Bruce Willis and Mel Gibson \u8211\'20\'13 were getting old and out of touch. The director Michael Bay was the new guy on the block, with hits such as The Rock and Armageddon that repurposed the slick style of Tony Scott and Jerry Bruckheimer into high-concept outings. But he seemed content to burn out the genre; once you have saved the world from an asteroid the size of Texas, there\u8217\'20\'19s really nowhere else to go. And {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2022/jun/14/the-bourne-identity-surprise-hit-changed-action-film-making"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 then came The Bourne Identity}}}\uc2 , writes Noah Gittell.\par \par \uc2 Climate check: The 1977 White House climate memo that should have changed the world\par \par \uc2 In 1977 Star Wars hit movie theaters, New York City had a blackout that lasted 25 hours, and the Apple II personal computer went up for sale. It was also the year that a remarkable one-page memo was circulated at the very highest levels of \uc2 US government\uc2 , writes Emma Pattee. Years before climate change was part of national discourse, this memo outlined what was known \u8211\'20\'13 and feared \u8211\'20\'13 about climate change at the time. It was prescient in many ways. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2022/jun/14/1977-us-presidential-memo-predicted-climate-change"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Did anyone listen?}}}\par \par \uc2 Last Thing: The cartoon where it happens. Lin-Manuel Miranda guest stars as horse in new Bluey episode\par \par \uc2 The creator of the smash-hit musicals Hamilton and In the Heights, and winner of multiple Tonys, Grammys and Emmys, has finally fulfilled another of his dreams: to guest star in the Australian animated series Bluey. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/2022/jun/14/the-cartoon-where-it-happens-lin-manuel-miranda-guest-stars-as-horse-in-new-bluey-episode"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lin-Manuel Miranda appears as a friendly horse named Major Tom}}}\uc2  in a new episode. In an interview with Collider last year, he was asked what show he would most like to guest star in. \u8220\'20\'1CThe show we watched the most during the pandemic was Bluey \u8211\'20\'13 because it is the only kids show that the whole family can be hysterically laughing at,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Sign up\par \par \uc2 First Thing is delivered to thousands of inboxes every weekday. If you\u8217\'20\'19re not already signed up, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/info/2018/sep/17/guardian-us-morning-briefing-sign-up-to-stay-informed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 subscribe now}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Get in touch\par \par \uc2 If you have any questions or comments about any of our newsletters please email {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:newsletters@theguardian.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 newsletters@theguardian.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220614ei6e001jr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
