\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 January 6 hearing: hard-hitting evidence puts Trump at heart of assault on democracy \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Maanvi Singh (now) and Chris Stein (earlier) \par \uc2 10,663 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 June 2022\par 02:53 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 January 6 hearing: Trump was at heart of plot that led to \u8216\'20\'18attempted coup\u8217\'20\'19\u8216\'20\'18It was a war scene\u8217\'20\'19: \uc2 Caroline Edwards\uc2  describes Capitol attack violenceIvanka Trump says she does not believe father\u8217\'20\'19s claim 2020 election was stolenHearings aim to be TV spectacular that \u8216\'20\'18blows the roof off\u8217\'20\'19What to know about the public January 6 committee hearingsWho are the key players on the House committee?Sign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.49am BST\par \par \uc2 Key takeaways\par \par \uc2 * The committee made the case that the attack on January 6 was the \u8220\'20\'1Cculmination of an attempted coup.\u8221\'20\'1D Presenting an overview of this hearing and the ones to come, House select committee chair \uc2 Bennie Thompson\uc2  and vice-chair \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  presented their finding that the violent mob that descended on the Capitol was no spontaneous occurrence. Video testimony from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s attorney general, his daughter, and other allies make the case that the former president was working to undermine the election results and foment backlash. \u8220\'20\'1CThe central question is whether the attack on the Capitol was coordinated and plan that you witnessed this what a coordinated and planned effort would look like,\u8221\'20\'1D Thompson said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt was the culmination of months long effort spearheaded by President Trump.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * Even as Trump carried on his lies that victory was stolen from him, his own administration and allies agreed there the election was legitimate. Former attorney general \uc2 William Barr\uc2  testified that he expressed that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s claims of a stolen election were \u8220\'20\'1Cbullshit\u8221\'20\'1D. A Trump campaign lawyer told \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2  in November \u8220\'20\'1Cthere\u8217\'20\'19s no there there\u8221\'20\'1D to support Trump\u8217\'20\'19s claims of widespread fraud. Even \uc2 Ivanka Trump\uc2 , the president\u8217\'20\'19s daughter, said she was convinced by Barr that the election was legitimate.\par \par \uc2 * Graphic footage and harrowing testimony from officer \uc2 Caroline Edwards\uc2 , who on the first line of defense against the attacking mob, reiterated the terror of the insurrection. Edwards compared the scene to a war zone, saying she was slipping on others\u8217\'20\'19 blood as she fought off insurrectionists. \u8220\'20\'1CIt was carnage. It was chaos. I can\u8217\'20\'19t even describe what I saw,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. The officer sustained burns from a chemical spray deployed against her, and a concussion after a bike rack was heaved on top of her. Officers and lawmakers watching the hearings teared up as they relived the violence of that day.\par \par \uc2 * As the attack was being carried out, and the mob was threatening vice president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s life, Trump and his team working to undermine the election carried on their work. After Pence refused to block the election certification, Trump and his supporters turned against him, and Trump fomented resentment in his tweets. As the mob cried \u8220\'20\'1CHang \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 !\u8221\'20\'1D the committee presented evidence that Trump suggested that might not be a bad idea.\u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  deserves it,\u8221\'20\'1D the president then said. As violence ensued, \u8220\'20\'1Cthe Trump legal team in the Willard Hotel war room,\u8221\'20\'1D continuing attempts to subvert the election results, Cheney said.\par \par \uc2 * Footage and testimony from film-maker Nick Quested, one of two witnesses at the hearing, suggested that the Proud Boys had planned to attack. On the morning of January 6, Quested testified that he was confused to see \u8220\'20\'1Ca couple of hundred\u8221\'20\'1D Proud Boys walking away from Trump\u8217\'20\'19s speech and toward the Capitol. The committee implied that this might have allowed them to scope out the defenses and weak spots at the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.53am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.08am BST\par \par \uc2 Following the harrowing video and testimony, Lila, a \uc2 Capitol police\uc2  therapy dog, is there to provide support.\par \par \uc2 enltrLila, the USCP therapy dog, is on the scene providing comfort after the hearing wrapped.\par \par \uc2 Family members of the officers who died after the 1/6 attack are finding comfort in this sweet pup. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Kb6pWRLzbQ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Kb6pWRLzbQ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Julie Tsirkin (@JulieNBCNews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JulieNBCNews/status/1535080127889293313?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 10, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.06am BST\par \par \uc2 Key revelations from the second half of the hearing:\par \par \uc2 * Top members of both the Oath Keepers, a rightwing militia group, and the Proud Boys, another far-right group, have been charged with seditious conspiracy. Video footage of their meeting suggests they may have worked together.\par \par \uc2 * Film-maker Nick Quested, who was with the Proud Boys on January 6, said he was confused to see \u8220\'20\'1Ca couple of hundred\u8221\'20\'1D Proud Boys walking away from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s speech that morning and toward the Capitol. The committee suggested this could be in order to scope out the Capitol before attacking.\par \par \uc2 * Officer \uc2 Caroline Edwards\uc2  compared the scene to a war zone, saying she was slipping on others\u8217\'20\'19 blood as the attack escalated. \u8220\'20\'1CIt was carnage. It was chaos. I can\u8217\'20\'19t even describe what I saw,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.09am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.01am BST\par \par \uc2 The January 6 committee shared never-before-seen footage of the Capitol attack, which showed Trump supporters attacking police officers before storming the building.\par \par \uc2 In one clip, an insurrectionist with a bullhorn read aloud Trump\u8217\'20\'19s tweet crticizing his vice-president, \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , for not attempting to block the certification of the 2020 election results. The next clip showed a mob chanting \u8220\'20\'1CHang \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 !\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The alarming footage was difficult to watch for all of those who were at the Capitol on January 6, including lawmakers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWatching this brings back a lot of memories and emotions I haven\u8217\'20\'19t experienced in a while,\u8221\'20\'1D Democratic congressman \uc2 Brendan Boyle\uc2  said on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.01am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.58am BST\par \par \uc2 Committee adjourns\par \par \uc2 The hearing ended with a video compilation rioters saying they attacked the Capitol because of \uc2 Donald Trump\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTrump asked me to come.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe personally asked us.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.50am BST\par \par \uc2 Officer Edwards: 'I was slipping in people's blood'\par \par \uc2 The committee showed graphic footage \uc2 Caroline Edwards\uc2  getting injured during the riot.\par \par \uc2 She and four other officers were standing guard at the edge of the Capitol lawn, when the crowd began surging toward them. Edwards sustained sustained burns from chemical spray that the rioters deployed, and a concussion after a bike rack was heaved on to her and she fell to the ground.\par \par \uc2 The scene was like a \u8220\'20\'1Cwar zone\u8221\'20\'1D she said, and she was slipping on others\u8217\'20\'19 blood. \u8220\'20\'1CIt was carnage. It was chaos. I can\u8217\'20\'19t even describe what I saw.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not combat trained,\u8221\'20\'1D she added. \u8220\'20\'1CIt was hours of dealing with way beyond what any law enforcement officer is trained for.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.53am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.45am BST\par \par \uc2 On the morning of January 6, film-maker Quested testified that he was confused to see \u8220\'20\'1Ca couple of hundred\u8221\'20\'1D Proud Boys walking away from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s speech and toward the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 The committee implied that this might have allowed them to scope out the defenses and weak spots at the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe central question is whether the attack on the Capitol was coordinated and plan that you witnessed this what a coordinated and planned effort would look like,\u8221\'20\'1D Thompson said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt was the culmination of months long effort spearheaded by President Trump.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.46am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.35am BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s mutual respect there. We\u8217\'20\'19re fighting the same fight,\u8221\'20\'1D said Proud Boys founder \uc2 Enrique Tarrio\uc2 . A videographer filmed a meeting between Tarrio and Oath Keepers founder Stewart Rhodes on 5 January 2021.\par \par \uc2 Top members of both the Oath Keepers, a rightwing militia group, and the Proud Boys, another far-right group, have been charged with seditious conspiracy. But the committee may tonight lay out how the groups may have worked together.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.39am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.24am BST\par \par \uc2 As the committee played never-before-seen footage of the attack on the Capitol, several law enforcement officers who were there that day could be seen in tears.\par \par \uc2 Among those in attendance are Harry Dunn, a US \uc2 Capitol police\uc2  officer, Daniel Hodges, a Washington DC police officer who was beaten with his own baton, Sgt Aquilino Gonell of US \uc2 Capitol police\uc2 , and DC police officer \uc2 Michael Fanone\uc2 , who was nearly killed during the attack. US Capitol Officer \uc2 Caroline Edwards\uc2 , who sustained a brain injury during the attack is also there and currently testifying. Several family members of law enforcement who died as a result of the attack attended, including Gladys Sicknick, the mother of office Brian Sicknick.\par \par \uc2 enltrOfficers Dunn, Hodges, Gonell and Fanone, who responded to the Capitol attack, are in attendance along with the widows of the officers who died in the aftermath of 1/6.\par \par \uc2 Dunn is wearing a shirt that says: \u8220\'20\'1Cinsurrection: a violent apprising against an authority or government\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Bqr2ElFeEX"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Bqr2ElFeEX}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Julie Tsirkin (@JulieNBCNews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JulieNBCNews/status/1535047581646061583?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.31am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.22am BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI was an American, standing face to face with other Americans, asking myself \u8230\'20\'26 how had we gotten here,\u8221\'20\'1D said officer \uc2 Caroline Edwards\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 As was working on January 6 to protect the Capitol, she was called \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s dog\u8221\'20\'1D, \u8220\'20\'1Cincompetent\u8221\'20\'1D, \u8220\'20\'1Cvillain\u8221\'20\'1D, \u8220\'20\'1Ctraitor,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey dared to question my honor. They dared to question my loyalty. And they dared to question my duty,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CI am a proud American and I will gladly sacrifice everything to make sure that the America my grandfather defended is here for many years to come\u8221\'20\'1D.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.25am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.17am BST\par \par \uc2 Witnesses sworn in\par \par \uc2 Nick Quested, a film-maker who was embedded with the Proud Boys, and \uc2 Caroline Edwards\uc2 , a \uc2 Capitol police\uc2  officer vowed to testified truthfully.\par \par \uc2 Both were there as Trump supporters breached the Capitol. Edwards was knocked unconscious as the mob advanced.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.20am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.04am BST\par \par \uc2 Key revelations so far\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re a little under an hour into this hearing and already there have been a number of explosive revelations.\par \par \uc2 Here are some of the most notable:\par \par \uc2 * Trump supported the assasination of \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 . When he learned supporters were chanting \u8220\'20\'1Chang \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said \u8220\'20\'1CMaybe our supporters have the right idea,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  revealed on Thursday. \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  deserves it,\u8221\'20\'1D the president added.\par \par \uc2 * Congressman Scott Perry, a Republican from Pennsylvania, inquired about a pardon after the 6 January riot. Perry played a key role in efforts to overturning the election.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Ivanka Trump\uc2  told the committee she was persuaded by Attorney General \uc2 William Barr\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s statement that there was no widespread fraud in the election. \u8220\'20\'1CI respect attorney general Barr, so I accepted what he was saying.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Jared Kushner\uc2  dismissed the White House counsel\u8217\'20\'19s threats to resign on 6 January, saying it seemed more like whining to him\par \par \uc2 * Attorney General \uc2 William Barr\uc2  told Trump his claims of a stolen election were \u8220\'20\'1Cbullshit\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 * A Trump campaign lawyer told \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2  in November that they weren\u8217\'20\'19t finding widespread fraud. \u8220\'20\'1CSo there\u8217\'20\'19s no there there,\u8221\'20\'1D Meadows told the campaign lawyer.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.28am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.04am BST\par \par \uc2 Congresswoman \uc2 Abigail Spanberger\uc2 , a Democrat of Virginia, is in the room tonight to witness the January 6 committee\u8217\'20\'19s first primetime hearing.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI was in the House Chamber on Jan. 6 as insurrectionists tried to break down doors and law enforcement bravely fought back,\u8221\'20\'1D Spanberger said on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ll be watching the hearing tonight, because we need accountability.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Spanberger is a member of the so-called \u8220\'20\'1CGallery Group,\u8221\'20\'1D the House Democrats who were in the chamber as the insurrection started. The group has become close since the January 6 attack, and several of its members planned to attend tonight\u8217\'20\'19s hearing together, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2022/06/09/democrats-gallery-group-jan-6-hearing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Axios reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.02am BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis was no tourist visit to the Capitol,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Bennie Thompson\uc2  said, introducing graphic video of the violent mob attack on the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 Trump supporters in tactical gear and body armor are seen attacking officers. Footage shows staffers running scared through the office of Kevin McCarthy, the minority leader who has tired to downplay the insurrection.\par \par \uc2 Footage of violence is spliced with Trump saying that these were \u8220\'20\'1Cpeaceful people\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.01am BST\par \par \uc2 What\u8217\'20\'19s happening over at Fox News at the moment? After all, they\u8217\'20\'19re not carrying the January 6 hearings live (leaving them to the smaller Fox Business network).\par \par \uc2 Perhaps unsurprisingly, it\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  downplaying the attack on the Capitol, which has been connected to the deaths of at least seven people.\par \par \uc2 enltrOn Fox News, Tucker Carlson brags about being the only network not to show the Jan. 6 hearing.\par \par \uc2 He says that Jan. 6 was a "a forgettably minor outbreak" of violence and says "it was not even close to an insurrection."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jeremy Barr (@jeremymbarr)\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jeremymbarr/status/1535051414291947522?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 10, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.52am BST\par \par \uc2 Pence's counsel to Trump attorney John Eastman: Attack was 'thanks to your bullshit'\par \par \uc2 Cheney previewed evidence that John Eastman, a lawyer involved in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to overturn the election results, who, she said \u8220\'20\'1Cdid not actually believe the legal position he was taking\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 But it revved up the mob. As the attack on the Capitol was underway, and \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s live was being threatened, Pence\u8217\'20\'19s legal counsel emailed Eastman: \u8220\'20\'1CThanks to your bullshit, we are under siege.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Email records show that Eastman showed no remorse in his response: \u8220\'20\'1CMy \u8220\'20\'1Cbullshit\u8221\'20\'1D - seriously? \u8230\'20\'26 The \u8216\'20\'18siege\u8217\'20\'19 is because you and your boss did not do what was necessary to allow this to be aired in a public way\u8230\'20\'26\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 And yet, Cheney continued, \u8220\'20\'1CWhile Congress was under attack on January 6, and the hours following the violence, the Trump legal team in the Willard Hotel war room,\u8221\'20\'1D continuing attempts to subvert the election results.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.56am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.42am BST\par \par \uc2 Cheney and the committee are making the case from the start that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s own administration, his own allies and aides were aware that he wanted to overturn the election results.\par \par \uc2 She is also making is a focused effort to diffuse accusations that the hearings are a partisan effort. Cheney, a Republican representative of Wyoming, played a clip of testimony from Pence\u8217\'20\'19s chief of staff, explaining why the former vice president ultimately resisted Trump.\par \par \uc2 For four years, Pence \u8220\'20\'1CI was proud to have stood beside the president,\u8221\'20\'1D chief of staff Marc Short said in the clip. \u8220\'20\'1CI think he ultimately knew that his fidelity to the Constitution was his first and foremost.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Cheney said that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s effort to pressure his vice president, \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , to subvert the election results \u8220\'20\'1Cwasn\u8217\'20\'19t just wrong \u8211\'20\'13 it was illegal and it was unconstitutional.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.31am BST\par \par \uc2 More clips presented show testimony from Barr saying that there wasn\u8217\'20\'19t enough to overturn the election, and a preview of an interview with \uc2 Ivanka Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Asked what she made of Barr\u8217\'20\'19s assertion that the election result was legitimate, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s daughter said: \u8220\'20\'1CI respect Attorney General Barr so I accepted what he was saying.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.21am BST\par \par \uc2 Committee Vice-Chair \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  led her speech with Trump\u8217\'20\'19s own words: \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Trump believed his supporters at the Capitol were, and I quote, \u8216\'20\'18doing what they should be doing\u8217\'20\'19,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 She referenced Trump\u8217\'20\'19s reaction to rioters\u8217\'20\'19 chants of \u8220\'20\'1CHang \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D: \u8220\'20\'1CMaybe our supporters have the right idea \u8230\'20\'26 \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  deserves it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COn the morning of January 6, President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s intention was to remain president of the United States, despite the lawful outcome of the 2020 election and in violation of his constitutional obligation to relinquish power,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.31am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.16am BST\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18January 6 was the culmination of an attempted coup,\u8217\'20\'19 Thompson said.\par \par \uc2 The first video clip we are presented is of former Attorney General Bill Barr, who calls the claims of a stolen election \u8220\'20\'1Cbullshit\u8221\'20\'1D. Barr testified that he repeatedly told \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  that he didn\u8217\'20\'19t agree with lies that the 2020 election was stolen. \u8220\'20\'1CHere was the attorney general of the United States, the top law enforcement official in the country, telling the president exactly what he thought about claims of a stolen election,\u8221\'20\'1D Thomson said.\par \par \uc2 But the big lie that the election was stolen didn\u8217\'20\'19t end there, Thompson continued. \u8220\'20\'1CThat was only the beginning of what became a sprawling, multistep conspiracy, aimed at overturning the presidential election, aimed at throwing out the votes of millions of Americans. Your vote. Your voice.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.24am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.08am BST\par \par \uc2 Bennie Thompson\uc2 , chair of House committee investigating the attack, began by invoking the \u8220\'20\'1Cdark history\u8221\'20\'1D of Missouri, and a time when people in power justified \u8220\'20\'1Cthe actions of slavery, the \uc2 Klu Klux Klan\uc2  and lynching.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m reminded of that dark history, as I hear voices today, try and justify the actions of the insurrection on January 6, 2021,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.03am BST\par \par \uc2 January 6 hearing begins\par \par \uc2 Lawmakers who were trapped in the upper gallery of the House as rioters descended are in the audience, as are police officers who defended the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 This is the first of several hearings that are the result of a year of investigation, including interviews with 1,000 witnesses.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.07am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.53am BST\par \par \uc2 Nick Quested is expected to give a short opening statement about how he filmed the far-right Proud Boys group and how the crowd turned from protesters to insurrectionists.\par \par \uc2 According to sources familiar with how things are being scheduled, Quested will deliver very brief remarks before testifying about his recollections embedding with the Proud Boys through January 6.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThank you for the introduction. As stated in the winter of 2020/2021, I was working on a documentary. As part of that documentary, I filmed several rallies in Washington DC on December 11 and December 12, 2020,\u8221\'20\'1D Quested will say in his statement obtained by the Guardian.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI learned there would be a rally on the mall on January 6, 2021, and three colleagues and I came to document the rally. According to the permit for the event there was to be a rally at the Ellipse. I arrived as a group was heading West on the Mall.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI observed a large contingent of Proud Boys marching to the Capitol. I filmed the crowd walking toward Capitol Hill. Almost immediately I was separated from my colleagues. I documented the crowd turn from protesters to insurrectionists.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI was surprised at the size of the group, the anger, and the profanity. I experienced pepper spray, violent surging, and I heard aggressive chanting. I shared this footage with the authorities. I am here today pursuant to a House subpoena.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The opening statement is notably short for a congressional hearing, in large part because the select committee is keen to dive straight into his testimony, and the length of the statement was a subject of extended negotiation with the panel, the sources said.\par \par \uc2 After the hearing, Quested is expected to deliver a longer statement talking about his motivations for filming the Proud Boys as well as his motivations for testifying to the select committee, both in closed-door depositions and at the inaugural hearing.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.58am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.51am BST\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re expecting to hear from who witnesses tonight:\par \par \uc2 Nick Quested, a film-maker who was embedded with the Proud Boys, saw the insurrection escalate and unroll.\par \par \uc2 Caroline Edwards\uc2 , a \uc2 Capitol Police\uc2  officer, was among the first to respond to the attack.\par \par \uc2 Committee Chair \uc2 Bennie Thompson\uc2  and Vice-Chair \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  will question both witnesses, focusing \u8220\'20\'1Cparticularly what they saw and heard from the rioters\u8221\'20\'1D according to the committee.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.52am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.21am BST\par \par \uc2 Setting the stage...\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/edpilkington"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ed Pilkington}}}\uc2  in New York and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/lauren-gambino"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lauren Gambino}}}\uc2  in Washington report:\par \par \uc2 The directors are hoping that the storyline will have all the elements of a TV smash hit: a King Lear figure ranting and raving as his power slips away from him, a glamorous couple struggling to rise above the fray, shady characters scheming sedition in hotel bedrooms, hordes of thugs in paramilitary gear chanting \u8220\'20\'1Chang him\u8221\'20\'1D as they march on the nation\u8217\'20\'19s capitol.\par \par \uc2 When the US House select committee investigating the January 6 insurrection opens its hearings on Thursday evening, it will do so in prime time and with primetime production values. The seven Democrats and two Republicans \u8211\'20\'13 shunned by their own party \u8211\'20\'13 who sit on the panel are pulling out all the stops in an attempt to seize the public\u8217\'20\'19s attention.\par \par \uc2 They have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2022/06/06/jan-6-committee-adviser-james-goldston"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 brought onboard}}}\uc2  a former president of ABC News, James Goldston, a veteran of Good Morning America and other mass-market TV programmes, to tightly choreograph the six public hearings into {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/06/07/us/politics/jan-6-hearings-tv-democrats.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 movie-length episodes}}}\uc2  ranging from 90 minutes to two and a half hours. His task: to fulfill the prediction of one of the Democratic committee members, \uc2 Jamie Raskin\uc2 , that the hearings \u8220\'20\'1Cwill tell a story that will really blow the roof off the House\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 To amplify the event, activists are hosting dozens of public watch parties in living rooms and union halls across the country. A \u8220\'20\'1Cflagship event\u8221\'20\'1D will take place at the Robert Taft Memorial and Carillon in Washington, where attendees can watch the hearing on a jumbotron while enjoying free Ben & Jerry\u8217\'20\'19s ice-cream.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/09/congress-january-6-hearings-tv-production"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Congress\u8217\'20\'19s January hearings aim to be TV spectacular that \u8216\'20\'18blows the roof off\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 Insurrection put 'centuries of constitutional democracy at risk' \u8211\'20\'13 committee chair\par \par \uc2 Mississippi congressman \uc2 Bennie Thompson\uc2 , the chairman of the House January 6 select committee, will open tonight\u8217\'20\'19s hearing by emphasizing that the world is watching to see whether America can continue to be the standard bearer for liberal democracy after the Capitol attack.\par \par \uc2 enltrJust in: Jan. 6 committee chair \uc2 Bennie Thompson\uc2  opening statement excerpt: \u8220\'20\'1CJanuary 6th and the lies that led to insurrection have put two and a half centuries of constitutional democracy at risk.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Hugo Lowell (@hugolowell) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hugolowell/status/1535022350411915265?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe can\u8217\'20\'19t sweep what happened under the rug. The American people deserve answers. So I come before you this evening not as a Democrat, but as an American who swore an oath to defend the Constitution. The Constitution doesn\u8217\'20\'19t protect just Democrats or just Republicans. It protects all of us: \u8216\'20\'18We the People.\u8217\'20\'19 And this scheme was an attempt to undermine the will of the people,\u8221\'20\'1D Thompson will say.\par \par \uc2 He plans to continue: \u8220\'20\'1CSo tonight, and over the next few weeks, we\u8217\'20\'19re going to remind you of the reality of what happened that day. But our work must do much more than just look backwards. Because our democracy remains in danger. The conspiracy to thwart the will of the people is not over. There are those in this country who thirst for power but have no love or respect for what makes America great: devotion to the Constitution, allegiance to the rule of law, our shared journey to build a more perfect Union.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJanuary 6th and the lies that led to insurrection have put two and a half centuries of constitutional democracy at risk. The world is watching what we do here. America has long been expected to be a shining city on a hill. A beacon of hope and freedom. A model for others\u8212\'20\'14when we\u8217\'20\'19re at our best. How can we play that role when our own house is in such disorder?\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe must confront the truth with candor, resolve, and determination. We need to show that we are worthy of the gifts that are the birthright of every American.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrThompson: \u8220\'20\'1CWe must confront the truth with candor, resolve, and determination. We need to show that we are worthy of the gifts that are the birthright of every American.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Hugo Lowell (@hugolowell) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hugolowell/status/1535022386596220929?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.00am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 As the country prepares for the first primetime hearing held by the January 6 committee, some groups are already looking ahead to how those who participated in the Capitol attack can be held accountable.\par \par \uc2 The progressive group Our Revolution has sent letters to 51 state election officials, asking them to \u8220\'20\'1Cenforce the Constitution and bar criminal insurrectionists from the ballot\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe American people cannot stomach any more political theater. The hearings alone won\u8217\'20\'19t help Democrats win the midterms \u8212\'20\'14 unless it results in action,\u8221\'20\'1D said Joseph Geevarghese, executive director of Our Revolution.\par \par \uc2 Our Revolution is staging demonstrations outside elections officials\u8217\'20\'19 offices in battleground states like Pennsylvania, Ohio, and Colorado, and the group has already filed legal complaints against lawmakers who voted against certifying the results of the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe power to enforce the Constitution in this matter lies with state election officials who are obligated to bar insurrectionists from serving in government,\u8221\'20\'1D Geevarghese said. \u8220\'20\'1CThe evidence is clear - former President Trump and some Members of Congress incited and assisted the insurrection.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 Key themes of US Capitol attack investigation\par \par \uc2 How deeply was Trump involved?\par \par \uc2 What Trump knew, and when he knew it, has been a driving focus for the select committee. House investigators have come to the conclusion behind closed doors, say sources familiar with the matter, that Trump was the common thread for all efforts to overturn the election.\par \par \uc2 The panel has evidence about a number of potentially unlawful schemes, including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/feb/04/trump-draft-order-voting-machines-white-house-meeting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the plot to seize voting machines}}}\uc2  or {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.msnbc.com/rachel-maddow/watch/similarities-suggest-coordination-in-fake-elector-letters-from-republicans-in-five-states-130662469836"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the plan to send fake electors}}}\uc2  to Congress to potentially persuade the then vice-president, \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , to refusing to certify states with \u8220\'20\'1Cduelling\u8221\'20\'1D slates.\par \par \uc2 But the central question has long been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/31/capitol-riot-white-house-donald-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 whether Trump had advance knowledge}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 through his network of political operatives \u8211\'20\'13 of the Capitol attack. That remains unanswered, but it appears he did know of the political plan to stop Biden\u8217\'20\'19s election certification.\par \par \uc2 Did Trump violate the law?\par \par \uc2 As the investigation progressed, the select committee appeared to indicate that it had amassed enough evidence of potential criminality on the part of Trump as he sought unsuccessfully to return himself to the White House for a second term.\par \par \uc2 At a business meeting last year, the panel\u8217\'20\'19s vice-chair, \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 , suggested by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pA7scwOVcrw&t=331s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reading from the US criminal code}}}\uc2  that Trump, by failing to stop the Capitol attack through \u8220\'20\'1Cinaction\u8221\'20\'1D, violated a federal law that prohibits obstructing a congressional proceeding.\par \par \uc2 A federal judge earlier this year ruled that Trump and a lawyer, John Eastman, who advised the former president on post-election legal strategies, on a preponderance of evidence, probably also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/mar/02/january-6-commitee-challenge-trump-lawyer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overtly conspired to obstruct Congress and defraudthe United States}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Is the evidence enough for charges?\par \par \uc2 The question to consider at the hearings is whether the select committee appears to have the evidence to prove beyond a reasonable doubt that Trump and his top advisers committed felonies \u8211\'20\'13 either for an obstruction charge, or other related crimes.\par \par \uc2 The final conclusions about the strength of the evidence will probably come after the hearings, when the panel releases its final report, currently slated for September, and whether it shows corrupt intent on the part of the former president \u8211\'20\'13 a key benchmark.\par \par \uc2 The select committee will also decide at that stage whether to make criminal referrals for prosecution. But regardless of the referrals, whether Trump or anyone else is charged with crimes related to January 6 remains a call for the justice department alone.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 The House select committee\u8217\'20\'19s first pimetime hearing on the Jan 6 insurrection will air tonight at 8pm Eastern Time. But one network won\u8217\'20\'19t bee carrying the broadcast: Fox News. \uc2 Rupert Murdoch\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s network will stick with its usual programming of Tucker Carlson Tonight.\par \par \uc2 My colleague David Smith writes:\par \par \uc2 Trump loyalists are expected to flood the airwaves with claims that the January 6 select committee lacks credibility and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats}}}\uc2  are out of touch with more pressing concerns such as inflation, crime, border security and baby formula shortages.\par \par \uc2 Elise Stefanik\uc2 , chair of the House Republican Conference, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zZpGQGyYnJo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told reporters on Capitol Hill on Wednesday}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CThey are scrambling to change the headlines, praying that the nation will focus on their partisan witch-hunt instead of our pocketbooks. It will not work.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In what amounted {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/news/house/3516209-house-gop-mounts-media-battle-in-prebuttal-to-jan-6-hearing/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to an attempt at a prebuttal}}}\uc2 , Stefanik described the January 6 committee as \u8220\'20\'1Cunconstitutional\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cillegitimate\u8221\'20\'1D and designed to \u8220\'20\'1Cpunish\u8221\'20\'1D the House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s opponents. She criticised its decision to hire James Goldston, the former president of ABC News, to help make its presentation compelling.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis further solidifies what we have known from day one: this committee is not about seeking the truth - it\u8217\'20\'19s a smear campaign against President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , against Republican members of Congress, and against Trump voters across this country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The comments set the template for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2022/06/03/trump-january-6-hearings-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican counter-programming}}}\uc2  on conservative media such as Fox News, \uc2 Newsmax\uc2 , the One America News Network, \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1CWar Room\u8221\'20\'1D podcast and other outlets that will seek to portray the hearings as a sinister show trial in which Trump supporters are the victims.\par \par \uc2 Congress\u8217\'20\'19s January hearings aim to be TV spectacular that \u8216\'20\'18blows the roof off\u8217\'20\'19Read more\par \par \uc2 Jim Jordan, the top Republican on the House judiciary committee, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thefederalist.com/2022/06/07/the-arrogant-true-goal-of-the-j6-committee-is-to-slander-and-shame-conservatives-out-of-the-public-sphere/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote on the Federalist website}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CThe committee\u8217\'20\'19s real goal, and what it hopes to achieve with its unprecedented subpoenas and its bright-light hearings, is a repudiation of conservatism and all those who hold conservative values.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/08/house-capitol-attack-hearings-republicans-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican media blitz aims to discredit Capitol attack hearings}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re hours away from the January 6 committee\u8217\'20\'19s first hearing, but already, there\u8217\'20\'19s been a plethora of news, ranging from the negotiations in Congress over gun control legislation to President Biden\u8217\'20\'19s trip to Los Angeles to the ongoing hunt for people involved in the attack on the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a recap of what has happened so far:\par \par \uc2 * President \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/09/jan-6-hearings-capitol-attack-trump-biden-us-politics-latest-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-62a24a778f08f6946a4ee648#block-62a24a778f08f6946a4ee648"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called the attack on the Capitol}}}\uc2  a \u8220\'20\'1Cflagrant violation of the constitution,\u8221\'20\'1D and said tonight\u8217\'20\'19s hearings will show Americans details of the insurrection that they didn\u8217\'20\'19t know about before.\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/09/jan-6-hearings-capitol-attack-trump-biden-us-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-62a241928f08aa6766e50cb9#block-62a241928f08aa6766e50cb9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 No deal was announced}}}\uc2  on gun control legislation demanded in the wake of mass shootings in Buffalo, New York and Uvalde, Texas, but senators are continuing to negotiate. Earlier in the day, the top Senate Democrat {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/09/jan-6-hearings-capitol-attack-trump-biden-us-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-62a205968f08aa6766e509b2#block-62a205968f08aa6766e509b2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sounded optimistic}}}\uc2 , though he acknowledged the measure was unlikely to contain all the provisions his party is demanding.\par \par \uc2 * NBC News reported that a bipartisan Senate deal {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/09/jan-6-hearings-capitol-attack-trump-biden-us-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-62a20b8a8f08f6946a4ee37e#block-62a20b8a8f08f6946a4ee37e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 may be near}}}\uc2  to fix legal loopholes that could exploited by a political candidate to steal an election.\par \par \uc2 * The \uc2 FBI\uc2  arrested a Michigan Republican candidate for the party\u8217\'20\'19s gubernatorial nomination on charges {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/09/ryan-kelley-republican-michigan-governor-arrested-fbi-capitol-riot"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 related to his involvement in the January 6 attack}}}\uc2 . Ryan Kelley was charged with \u8220\'20\'1Cdisorderly and disruptive conduct in a restricted building or grounds\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/09/jan-6-hearings-capitol-attack-trump-biden-us-politics-latest-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-62a2219e8f08aa6766e50b5b#block-62a2219e8f08aa6766e50b5b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The average price of a gallon of gas is nearing $5 a gallon}}}\uc2 , a symbolic threshold it has never before passed. The nationwide spike is likely to only worsen Biden\u8217\'20\'19s approval ratings, which a recent poll found had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://morningconsult.com/2022/06/08/biden-approval-rating-new-low/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hit an all-time low}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The blog is now being handed over to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/maanvi-singh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Maanvi Singh}}}\uc2  on the west coast, who will take you through the start of Congress\u8217\'20\'19s inquiry into the Capitol attack, starting at 8pm eastern.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 With hours to go until the January 6 commission begins meeting, my colleague {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/hugo-lowell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hugo Lowell}}}\uc2  has an explainer that\u8217\'20\'19s worth reading for its details into the hearing\u8217\'20\'19s purpose and what comes after tonight:\par \par \uc2 The House select committee investigating the January 6 Capitol attack is scheduled on Thursday to hold the first of six public hearings where it will {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/23/capitol-attack-panel-public-hearings-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unveil new evidence collected against Donald Trump}}}\uc2  and a range of other operatives over the course of its 10-month inquiry.\par \par \uc2 The congressional investigation into the events of January 6, when a pro-Trump mob stormed the Capitol to stop the certification of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s election win, has said it has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/mar/02/january-6-commitee-challenge-trump-lawyer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 evidence to suggest Trump violated the law}}}\uc2  to overturn the 2020 election results.\par \par \uc2 What are the January 6 committee hearings?\par \par \uc2 Likened to the Watergate hearings, the select committee is holding six public hearings to reveal the mountain of evidence it acquired over the course of the sprawling investigation, which interviewed more than 1,000 people and reviewed more than 125,000 documents.\par \par \uc2 The first and last hearings are due to be shown in prime time in America in a move that may cement them in popular culture as a genuine and high-profile effort to warn of a past and ongoing threat to US democracy.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 Speaking of the Trump administration, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/06/09/business/air-force-one-paint-job/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN is reporting}}}\uc2  that the two new Air Force Ones the former president commissioned are facing production delays because part of its paint scheme would interfere with its operations.\par \par \uc2 The new presidential jets have faced a host of issues since Trump ordered them in 2018, so much so that \uc2 Boeing\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s CEO {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.defenseone.com/business/2022/04/ceo-boeing-should-have-rejected-trumps-air-force-one-deal/366186/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has said taking the contract was a mistake}}}\uc2 . CNN reports that the project is late and over its budget, and has faced issues including a shortages of workers with the right security clearances and a dispute with a subcontractor.\par \par \uc2 Now there\u8217\'20\'19s a problem with its paint job. Here\u8217\'20\'19s how CNN puts it:\par \par \uc2 Trump had criticized the jet\u8217\'20\'19s current color scheme, which has changed little since the Kennedy Administration, particularly the light blue stripe that runs the length of the plane. Trump instead wanted a red, white and dark blue palette that more closely matches the colors of the US flag.\par \par \uc2 But it turns out the darker blue \u8212\'20\'14 which some observers say is similar to the color scheme on one of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s personal jets \u8212\'20\'14 poses challenges to the military planes\u8217\'20\'19 sophisticated electronics system that ensures the president can stay in secure communication with officials on the ground \u8212\'20\'14 even in the case of a nuclear attack.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe paint scheme in question was one of many possible livery colors proposed,\u8221\'20\'1D an Air Force spokesperson told CNN Thursday. \u8220\'20\'1CFurther analysis concluded darker colors, among other factors, on the underside of the VC-25B aircraft might contribute to temperatures exceeding the current qualification limits of a small number of components.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s education secretary \uc2 Betsy DeVos\uc2  contemplated an effort to invoke the 25th amendment and remove him from office following the January 6 insurrection, she said in an interview.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usatoday.com/story/opinion/columnist/2022/06/09/devos-trump-why-i-quit/7529651001/?gnt-cfr=1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Speaking to USA Today columnist Ingrid Jacques}}}\uc2 , DeVos said she opted to resign after concluding her effort would fail:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI spoke with the vice president and just let him know I was there to do whatever he wanted and needed me to do or help with, and he made it very clear that he was not going to go in that direction or that path,\u8221\'20\'1D DeVos says. \u8220\'20\'1CI spoke with colleagues. I wanted to get a better understanding of the law itself and see if it was applicable in this case. There were more than a few people who had those conversations internally.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Once she understood removing the president was pretty much impossible, DeVos resigned later that day.\par \par \uc2 DeVos wasn\u8217\'20\'19t alone in considering using the amendment that provides for the removal of an incapacitated president, potentially on grounds of mental as well as physical fitness, after a majority vote by the cabinet. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s secretary of state and Treasury secretary reportedly pondered doing the same following the attack on the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/nov/16/mnuchin-pompeo-trump-25th-amendment-capitol-attack-betrayal-book-jon-karl"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mnuchin and Pompeo discussed removing Trump after Capitol attack, book claims}}}\par \par \uc2 Neither ultimately acted. Trump was impeached by the Democrat-controlled House in the final days of his term, but the Republican-led Senate acquitted him.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden calls January 6 'flagrant violation of the constitution' US President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  spoke about the January 6 committee during a meeting with Canadian prime minister \uc2 Justin Trudeau\uc2  in Los Angeles. Photograph: Evan Vucci/AP\par \par \uc2 Americans will learn new details of the January 6 insurrection at tonight\u8217\'20\'19s hearings, Biden said, calling the assault on the Capitol, a \u8220\'20\'1Cflagrant violation of the constitution.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think these guys and women broke the law, tried to turn around the result of an election. There\u8217\'20\'19s a lot of questions, who\u8217\'20\'19s responsible, who\u8217\'20\'19s involved. I\u8217\'20\'19m not going to make a judgment on that,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.c-span.org/video/?520915-1/president-biden-january-6-rioters-overturn-election-results"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said during a meeting with Canadian prime minister Justin Trudeau}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA lot of Americans are going to be seeing for the first time some of the detail of what occurred\u8221\'20\'1D at the night\u8217\'20\'19s hearing, the president added.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 Michigan police officer charged with second-degree murder in shooting of Patrick Lyoya\par \par \uc2 A police officer in Grand Rapids, Michigan is facing second-degree murder charges for the shooting death of Patrick Lyoya, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/19/autopsy-confirms-patrick-lyoya-shot-head-police-officer-face-down"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a Black man who was shot in the back of the head while on the ground}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 From {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/06/09/us/patrick-lyoya-grand-rapids-shooting-charging-decision.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The New York Times}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Christopher Becker, the Kent County prosecuting attorney, said the officer, Christopher Schurr, acted unreasonably when he shot Mr. Lyoya, 26, while wrestling with the motorist, who had run away. The officer told Mr. Lyoya he pulled him over for having license plates that did not match his car.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPatrick Lyoya immigrated to the United States from the Democratic Republic of the Congo to pursue the American dream and provide a better and safer life for himself and his family,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Ben Crump\uc2 , a lawyer for the family, said in a statement when the videos were released. \u8220\'20\'1CInstead, what found him was a fatal bullet to the back of the head, delivered by an officer of the Grand Rapids Police Department.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Lyoya\u8217\'20\'19s father described the the killing as an \u8220\'20\'1Cexecution.\u8221\'20\'1D Footage of the altercation was caught on Becker\u8217\'20\'19s body camera.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/15/patrick-lyoya-shooting-family-police-killed-execution"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18That was my beloved son\u8217\'20\'19: family of Patrick Lyoya say police killed their son in an \u8216\'20\'18execution\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 An unintended consequence of the recent congressional push for gun control legislation is that a bill to boost domestic semiconductor production has been put on the back burner, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2022-06-09/biden-s-52-billion-chip-plan-sputters-as-lawmakers-eye-election#xj4y7vzkg?sref=fqqmZ8gi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bloomberg reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The proposed legislation would spend $52 billion to spur domestic manufacturing of the vital computer chips that ran short globally during the pandemic, exacerbating supply chain issues in the United States and driving up inflation. It would also contain provisions to help American businesses compete against China.\par \par \uc2 But with senators so focused on a bipartisan agreement to better regulate guns following recent mass shootings, and with midterms in which Democrats could lose control of one or both chambers of Congress growing nearer, \uc2 Bloomberg\uc2  reports that lawmakers are finding little time or use for the talks:\par \par \uc2 Supporters say that without passage, the US will fall further behind other countries in making the components of everything from fighter jets to vacuum cleaners, putting it at the mercy of overseas supply chains.\par \par \uc2 Frustration with the Biden administration looms large on Capitol Hill and among business lobbyists who have pushed for the measure. Senators and other people close to the negotiations said the White House has not pressed hard enough on House Speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  and Democrats in her chamber to finish the legislation.\par \par \uc2 Arizona Senator Mark Kelly, a Democrat who faces a tough re-election contest, said he\u8217\'20\'19d like the White House to get more involved, especially with the House.\par \par \uc2 Republican supporters of the bill, too, have been puzzled by the White House\u8217\'20\'19s strategy, saying Biden\u8217\'20\'19s team hadn\u8217\'20\'19t pushed House Democrats more forcefully and let months go by without throwing their weight behind what was supposed to be a top priority.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 Despite {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/09/jan-6-hearings-capitol-attack-trump-biden-us-politics-latest-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-62a205968f08aa6766e509b2#block-62a205968f08aa6766e509b2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 earlier optimism}}}\uc2  from the chamber\u8217\'20\'19s top Democrat, it does not look like senators will reach a compromise on gun control today.\par \par \uc2 As CNN\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/profiles/manu-raju"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Manu Raju}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 enltrAfter a meeting in Sen. Simema\u8217\'20\'19s basement hideaway, Sen. \uc2 John Cornyn\uc2  told a group of us there\u8217\'20\'19s no deal yet on guns.\par \par \uc2 \u8221\'20\'1DWe\u8217\'20\'19re meeting again tomorrow and I hope to resolve remaining differences,\u8221\'20\'1D Cornyn said.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Manu Raju (@mkraju) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1534969938896637953?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 That talks are taking so long may mean something, Politico\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/staff/burgess-everett"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Burgess Everett}}}\uc2  notes:\par \par \uc2 enltrNo deal yet. But they are still talking, which at this point is notable {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Z08Xz0Of07"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/Z08Xz0Of07}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Burgess Everett (@burgessev)\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/burgessev/status/1534970424399908865?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden has started his day in Los Angeles with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TtC_oytrxDY"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a speech to business leaders}}}\uc2 , where he encouraged them to focus on sustainability in the face of intensifying climate change. One state away in Arizona, \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/nina-lakhani"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nina Lakhani}}}\uc2  reports officials fear heat deaths as temperatures in the largest city Phoenix are expected to top 110F in the coming days:\par \par \uc2 A dangerous heatwave is due to scorch large swaths of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/arizona"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arizona}}}\uc2  for the rest of the week, triggering the first extreme heat warning of the year as temperatures in Phoenix are forecast to top 113F (45C) on three consecutive days.\par \par \uc2 Day and nighttime temperatures are expected to reach 7F to 10F (4C to 6C) above normal for this time of the year, which could drive a surge in medical emergencies and deaths as people struggle to stay cool amid soaring energy prices and rising homelessness.\par \par \uc2 Extreme heat is America\u8217\'20\'19s leading weather-related killer, and Phoenix, in Maricopa county, is the deadliest city.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/09/arizona-phoenix-triple-digit-heatwave-deaths"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s emergency services brace for temperatures above 110F as deaths mount}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 The January 6 commission will in its hearing tonight try to show that the Proud Boys and Oath Keepers militia groups worked together on attacking the Capitol, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/hugo-lowell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hugo Lowell}}}\uc2  reports.\par \par \uc2 The House select committee investigating the January 6 Capitol attack is expected at its first hearing on Thursday evening to connect the far-right Proud Boys and the Oath Keepers militia groups in the same seditious conspiracy, according to two sources familiar with the matter.\par \par \uc2 The move by the panel and chief investigative counsel Tim Heaphy would likely be one of the major revelations that comes from the hearing, which is expected to focus on the militia groups and how {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/08/capitol-attack-january-6-proud-boys-oath-keepers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 they made plans to storm the Capitol}}}\uc2 , the sources said.\par \par \uc2 Top members of the Proud Boys and the Oath Keepers have been charged separately by the justice department with seditious conspiracy, but the select committee\u8217\'20\'19s intention to show that their efforts were connected would escalate the gravity of the plans to attack the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 Lowell also spoke to MSNBC\u8217\'20\'19s Katie Phang about what his reporting revealed:\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW: \u8220\'20\'1CThe January 6th committee is expected to tie in the Oath Keepers and the Proud Boys militia groups together in the same seditious conspiracy,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hugolowell?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @hugolowell}}}\uc2  tells {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KatiePhang?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @KatiePhang}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 More to come from Katie\u8217\'20\'19s interview with Hugo to preview tonight\u8217\'20\'19s first public 1/6 hearing. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/xSJwcMXEpu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/xSJwcMXEpu}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Katie Phang Show (@katiephangshow) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/katiephangshow/status/1534958432834531328?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/09/proud-boys-oath-keepers-capitol-attack"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Panel to connect Proud Boys and Oath Keepers in Capitol attack conspiracy}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 Thanks for sticking with us through a morning packed with news, as Washington prepares for new revelations from the January 6 committee this evening. Later this afternoon, President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is scheduled to address the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.state.gov/summit-of-the-americas/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Summit of the Americas}}}\uc2  in Los Angeles.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what\u8217\'20\'19s happened in the day so far:\par \par \uc2 * Senators may be nearing a deal on gun control legislation demanded in the wake of mass shootings in Buffalo, New York and Uvalde, Texas, the top Senate Democrat {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/09/jan-6-hearings-capitol-attack-trump-biden-us-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-62a205968f08aa6766e509b2#block-62a205968f08aa6766e509b2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2 , though he acknowledged the legislation was unlikely to contain all the provisions his party is demanding.\par \par \uc2 * NBC News reported that a bipartisan Senate deal {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/09/jan-6-hearings-capitol-attack-trump-biden-us-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-62a20b8a8f08f6946a4ee37e#block-62a20b8a8f08f6946a4ee37e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 may be near}}}\uc2  to fix legal loopholes that could exploited by a political candidate to steal an election.\par \par \uc2 * The \uc2 FBI\uc2  arrested a Michigan Republican candidate for the party\u8217\'20\'19s gubernatorial nomination. While {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/09/jan-6-hearings-capitol-attack-trump-biden-us-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-62a2119d8f08aa6766e50a70#block-62a2119d8f08aa6766e50a70"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 it is unclear}}}\uc2  what the charges are, Ryan Kelley was in Washington on January 6, 2021 and local media reports that there are signs he may have taken part in storming the capitol.\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/09/jan-6-hearings-capitol-attack-trump-biden-us-politics-latest-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-62a2219e8f08aa6766e50b5b#block-62a2219e8f08aa6766e50b5b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The average price of a gallon of gas is nearing $5 a gallon}}}\uc2 , a symbolic threshold it has never before passed. The nationwide spike is likely to only worsen Biden\u8217\'20\'19s approval ratings, which a recent poll found had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://morningconsult.com/2022/06/08/biden-approval-rating-new-low/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hit an all-time low}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 US average gas price nearing $5 a gallon\par \par \uc2 In a sign of the ongoing inflation threat, the average price of a gallon of gasoline is closing to surpassing $5 a gallon in the United States, an all-time high that poses implications for the wider economy and may worsen Biden\u8217\'20\'19s low approval.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://gasprices.aaa.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 According to the American Automobile Association}}}\uc2  (AAA), the average price of a gallon of regular gas is today at $4.97, though GasBuddy\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Patrick De Haan\uc2  say it has already passed the symbolic threshold.\par \par \uc2 enltrBREAKING: According to GasBuddy, the national average has reached $5 per gallon.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Patrick De Haan\uc2  ???? (@GasBuddyGuy) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GasBuddyGuy/status/1534882159671906304?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPeople are still fueling up, despite these high prices,\u8221\'20\'1D AAA spokesman Andrew Gross {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://gasprices.aaa.com/rising-oil-cost-and-high-demand-for-gas-keep-pump-prices-surging/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said earlier this week}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CAt some point, drivers may change their daily driving habits or lifestyle due to these high prices, but we are not there yet.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The gas price spike is attributable to the US economy\u8217\'20\'19s overall recovery from the pandemic downturn in 2020 as people returned to driving and traveling nationwide, but it grew markedly worse earlier this year when Russia invaded Ukraine and western nations imposed sanctions that roiled global oil markets.\par \par \uc2 Rightly or wrongly, many Americans see gas prices as a proxy for the wider economy\u8217\'20\'19s health, and as they hit new heights, Biden is increasingly being blamed for the spike.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/mar/20/joe-biden-cursed-presidency-gas-prices-covid-inflation-russia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18cursed presidency\u8217\'20\'19: gas prices are latest headache as midterms loom}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Tomorrow may be a pretty rough day for the White House. Any damning revelations that come out of the January 6 committee could be overshadowed by the latest inflation numbers from the Labor Department, which will be released at 8:30am eastern time.\par \par \uc2 The May {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bls.gov/cpi/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 consumer price index}}}\uc2  data may very well indicate that the worst bout of inflation the US economy has seen since the 1980s isn\u8217\'20\'19t ending anytime soon, nor will its potently negative effects on the president\u8217\'20\'19s support. In fact, his approval is now at an all-time low, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://morningconsult.com/2022/06/08/biden-approval-rating-new-low/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Morning Consult/Politico data}}}\uc2  released yesterday.\par \par \uc2 The list of factors fueling inflation is lengthy, and ranges from the war in Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s economic ripple effects to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vox.com/23036340/biden-american-rescue-plan-inflation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s own policies}}}\uc2  to the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s decisions to keep rates low throughout last year, which were beyond the White House\u8217\'20\'19s control. One thing\u8217\'20\'19s for certain: the Republican opposition will no doubt seize on tomorrow\u8217\'20\'19s data \u8212\'20\'14 whatever it shows \u8212\'20\'14 to argue Biden is a poor steward of the world\u8217\'20\'19s largest economy.\par \par \uc2 Ahead of its release, the White House has tweeted a video highlighting Biden\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to lower ocean shipping costs, which are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/jun/09/global-supply-chain-crisis-fuels-push-to-local-manufacturing-as-chinas-appeal-dims"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 part of the wider global supply chains snarls}}}\uc2  and indeed a factor in America\u8217\'20\'19s inflation problem.\par \par \uc2 enltrOne of the reasons prices have gone up is because a handful of companies who control the market have raised shipping prices by as much as 1,000%. It\u8217\'20\'19s outrageous \u8212\'20\'14 and I\u8217\'20\'19m calling on Congress to crack down on them. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/eLIdQBmskJ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/eLIdQBmskJ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 President Biden (@POTUS) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS/status/1534919703864528899?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Whether voters will listen is another matter.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 Justice Department to probe Louisiana State Police: AP\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US Department of Justice\uc2  has announced a federal civil rights investigation into the Louisiana State Police following a raft of brutality cases and the fatal beating of a Black motorist, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/feb/05/louisiana-police-ronald-greene-death-mother"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ronald Greene}}}\uc2 , in 2019.\par \par \uc2 Greene, an unarmed 49-year-old, was arrested by six white officers with body camera footage of the incident, obtained years later by the Associated Press, revealing he had been punched, tasered and placed in a chokehold and later dragged face down in handcuffs and left prone for over nine minutes.\par \par \uc2 Police initially claimed Greene had died from injuries sustained after crashing his car into a tree, and a local coroner\u8217\'20\'19s report later determined the death to be accidental. It was not until a federal criminal investigation into the incident began that the finding {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/louisiana-arrests-new-orleans-forensics-death-of-ronald-greene-9b4c44be88fd2778c24c9bc5c05b60da"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was challenged}}}\uc2  by re-examining the autopsy.\par \par \uc2 The incident is currently being investigated in the Louisiana state legislature, which is examining an alleged cover-up instigated by senior members of the state police. Greene\u8217\'20\'19s death is one of a number of recent brutality cases, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2021/09/09/1035446605/louisiana-state-police-bodycam-videos-beatings"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 uncovered by the Associated Press}}}\uc2 , which found at least a dozen cases in the past decade where troopers or their superiors are alleged to have concealed evidence of brutality or blocked investigations.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/09/us-investigatation-louisiana-state-police-brutality-cases-ronald-greene-doj"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US justice department to investigate Louisiana State Police following 2019 death of Ronald Greene}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Back in the Senate, the Republican leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  has renewed his attack on Democrats for creating what he says is an atmosphere that encourages people to threaten supreme court justices, following yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s arrest of an armed man near conservative judge \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s house.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTwo years ago, the Senate Democratic leader stood on the steps of the supreme court and threatened two justices by name. \u8216\'20\'18You will pay the price,\u8217\'20\'19 he shouted. \u8216\'20\'18You won\u8217\'20\'19t know what hit you,\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D McConnell said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.c-span.org/video/?c5018975/user-clip-mcconnell-scotus-threat"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on the Senate floor}}}\uc2 , adding that House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  and \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  also contributed to the tension.\par \par \uc2 McConnell accused the Biden administration of failing to take the threat to justices seriously, particularly after the leak of a draft opinion indicating conservatives were poised to end nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access by overturning Roe v Wade. \u8220\'20\'1CLook, everybody saw where this climate might lead to,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 The meat of his attack concerns {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2022/may/10/us-supreme-court-security-senate-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a bipartisan bill passed by the senate that would beef up security for the justices and their families}}}\uc2 , but which hasn\u8217\'20\'19t passed the House.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI understand Democrats want to stage a big spectacle this week about what they claim is their opposition to political violence,\u8221\'20\'1D McConnell said in a veiled reference to the imminent start of the January 6 hearings. \u8220\'20\'1CBut in reality, they\u8217\'20\'19re going out of their way to block concrete steps to prevent political violence.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/08/brett-kavanaugh-home-man-arrested-supreme-court-justice"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Man arrested near Brett Kavanaugh\u8217\'20\'19s home charged with attempted murder}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 FBI\uc2  arrests Republican Michigan governor candidate who attended January 6 rally\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FBI\uc2  has taken into custody Ryan Kelley, a candidate for the Republican nomination for governor in Michigan who attended the rallies preceding the January 6 attack on the capitol and may have taken part in the assault.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.detroitnews.com/story/news/local/michigan/2022/06/09/ryan-kelley-michigan-republican-gop-governor-candidate-arrested/7566967001/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Detroit News}}}\uc2  reported that Kelley, who is one of five candidates running for the party\u8217\'20\'19s gubernatorial nomination, was arrested at his home in Allendale, near the city of Grand Rapids. Federal agents are also searching his home, but it wasn\u8217\'20\'19t immediately clear what he was being charged with.\par \par \uc2 Kelley was in Washington for the rally with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  that preceded the attack on the capitol, and Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic Party has released footage that appears to show Kelley encouraging people to storm the building.\par \par \uc2 enltrRyan Kelley:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCome on, let's go! This is it! This is, this is war baby!" {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kelleyforgov?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @kelleyforgov}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/IrNc3Rv10M"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/IrNc3Rv10M}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Michigan Tea (@MichiganTea) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MichiganTea/status/1409326266776436736?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 28, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Earlier this year, Kelley in a speech told a crowd to unplug voting machines if \u8220\'20\'1Cyou see something you don\u8217\'20\'19t like happening with the machine,\u8221\'20\'1D according to The Detroit News.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Elections have consequences, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/congress/senate-bipartisan-group-eyes-deal-week-bill-prevent-future-coups-rcna32667"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBC News is reporting}}}\uc2  that one of the effects of the recent victories of Republicans who did not endorse \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cbig lie\u8221\'20\'1D concerning the 2020 election is that senators may be nearing a deal on tweaking existing laws to stop future presidential candidates from trying to steal the vote.\par \par \uc2 Two sources familiar with the group\u8217\'20\'19s work said it is close to a deal, having settled on a series of new provisions and working through options on one major unresolved issue.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve made a lot of major decisions,\u8221\'20\'1D Sen. \uc2 Susan Collins\uc2 , R-Maine, a leader of the group, said in an interview before the meeting. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve resolved a lot of issues, but we have some more work to do, which I hope we\u8217\'20\'19ll finish up this week.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The areas of consensus, Collins said, include amending the Electoral Count Act to restrain the vice president\u8217\'20\'19s role, raising the congressional threshold for objecting to electoral votes, overhauling the transition process and protecting election officials from threats.\par \par \uc2 The group is trying to close loopholes in the electoral system in a flurry of activity among members and staffers in recent weeks to reach consensus on a cause that lawmakers in both parties see as urgent. It was the first face-to-face meeting of members since April. The negotiations were sparked in part by President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s unsuccessful effort to exploit gaps in the law to stay in power even though he lost the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 Why the sudden momentum? Here\u8217\'20\'19s NBC explanation:\par \par \uc2 Some pro-reform Republicans have privately indicated that the cause is helped by the recent primary victories of Republican lawmakers who voted to certify President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s victory, as well as the victories of top state officials in Georgia who defied Trump\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to change the result and defeated his preferred candidates to unseat them.\par \par \uc2 The most notable triumph of a candidate who refused to endorse the \u8220\'20\'1Cbig lie\u8221\'20\'1D took place last month in Georgia, where Republican voters endorsed \uc2 Brad Raffensperger\uc2 , the secretary of state who refused to embrace Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lies about widespread fraud in the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/24/five-key-takeaways-the-us-midterm-elections"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Five key takeaways: the US midterm elections}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 The leaders of more than 220 top American companies are calling on the Senate to pass gun control legislation, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2022/06/09/ceos-senate-gun-legislation-letter?utm_source=newsletter&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=newsletter_axiosam&stream=top"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Axio reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 However, the petition signed by the CEOs of companies like \uc2 Unilever\uc2 , \uc2 Levi Strauss\uc2 , \uc2 Bloomberg\uc2 , \uc2 Dick\u8217\'20\'19s Sporting Goods\uc2  and \uc2 Lululemon\uc2  as well as sports teams like the \uc2 San Francisco Giants\uc2  and \uc2 Philadelphia Eagles\uc2  doesn\u8217\'20\'19t endorse any specific policy, and is a revised version of a letter first released in 2019, though with about 50 percent more signatories this time.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe gun violence epidemic represents a public health crisis that continues to devastate communities \u8212\'20\'14 especially Black and Brown communities \u8212\'20\'14 and harm our national economy. All of this points to a clear need for action: the Senate must take urgent action to pass bold gun safety legislation as soon as possible in order to avoid more death and injury,\u8221\'20\'1D the letter reads.\par \par \uc2 Yesterday, the Democrat-led House of Representatives {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/09/us-house-passes-gun-control-bill-faces-defeat-senate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed their own measure}}}\uc2  yesterday raising the age limit to buy a semi-automatic rifle and banning the sale of magazines that can hold more than 15 rounds, but it\u8217\'20\'19s unlikely to win the Senate\u8217\'20\'19s approval.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 Schumer says 'good progress' being made on bipartisan gun deal\par \par \uc2 Top Senate Democrat \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  sounded optimistic about the prospects of a bipartisan gun deal in a speech Thursday, saying \u8220\'20\'1Cgood progress\u8221\'20\'1D is being made by negotiators from both parties on a bill that can pass the chamber.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYesterday, a bipartisan a group of Democrats and Republicans met again to continue working towards a bipartisan compromise. This morning, my colleague Senator Murphy reported that the group is making good progress and they hope to get something real done very soon,\u8221\'20\'1D Schumer said, referring to Senator \uc2 Chris Murphy\uc2 , the Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 point man in the negotiations.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs soon as the bipartisan group comes to agreement, I want to bring a measure to the floor for a vote as quickly as possible,\u8221\'20\'1D the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.c-span.org/video/?c5018962/user-clip-schumer-guns"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 majority leader said in a speech}}}\uc2  in the chamber.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s unclear what exactly the deal may contain, but the legislation is unlikely to contain all provisions that gun control advocates have called for. Democrats control the Senate by one vote, and the legislation will need at least some support from Republicans, who are far less inclined to limit gun access.\par \par \uc2 In a nod to that reality, Schumer said, \u8220\'20\'1CThe overwhelming consensus of our caucus, of gun safety advocates and of the American people is that getting something real done on gun violence is worth pursuing, even if we cannot get everything that we know we need.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 As {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/edpilkington"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ed Pilkington}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/lauren-gambino"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lauren Gambino}}}\uc2  report, the January 6 committee has gone to great lengths to grab the public\u8217\'20\'19s attention in its hearings beginning tonight, hoping the strength of its evidence and its carefully managed presentation will counteract the enduring allure of Trump among many Americans:\par \par \uc2 The directors are hoping that the storyline will have all the elements of a TV smash hit: a King Lear figure ranting and raving as his power slips away from him, a glamorous couple struggling to rise above the fray, shady characters scheming sedition in hotel bedrooms, hordes of thugs in paramilitary gear chanting \u8220\'20\'1Chang him\u8221\'20\'1D as they march on the nation\u8217\'20\'19s capitol.\par \par \uc2 When the US House select committee investigating the January 6 insurrection opens its hearings on Thursday evening, it will do so in prime time and with primetime production values. The seven Democrats and two Republicans \u8211\'20\'13 shunned by their own party \u8211\'20\'13 who sit on the panel are pulling out all the stops in an attempt to seize the public\u8217\'20\'19s attention.\par \par \uc2 They have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2022/06/06/jan-6-committee-adviser-james-goldston"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 brought onboard}}}\uc2  a former president of ABC News, James Goldston, a veteran of Good Morning America and other mass-market TV programmes, to tightly choreograph the six public hearings into {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/06/07/us/politics/jan-6-hearings-tv-democrats.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 movie-length episodes}}}\uc2  ranging from 90 minutes to two and a half hours. His task: to fulfill the prediction of one of the Democratic committee members, \uc2 Jamie Raskin\uc2 , that the hearings \u8220\'20\'1Cwill tell a story that will really blow the roof off the House\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/09/congress-january-6-hearings-tv-production"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Congress\u8217\'20\'19s January hearings aim to be TV spectacular that \u8216\'20\'18blows the roof off\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 If the supreme court overturns Roe v Wade in the coming weeks, Florida could become a destination for women seeking abortions \u8212\'20\'14 even though a ban on the procedure past 15 weeks comes into effect on July 1. The 19th\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://19thnews.org/author/shefali-luthra/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Shefali Luthra}}}\uc2  looks into the future of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the state, which may not be as bright as it seems:\par \par \uc2 On 1 July, Florida will begin enforcing a law banning abortions for people past 15 weeks of pregnancy. The ban, which has no exceptions for rape or incest, has been framed by its backers as a \u8220\'20\'1Cmoderate\u8221\'20\'1D compromise. The vast majority of abortions take place within the first trimester, which ends at 12 weeks, they note. The law is less stringent than the six-week bans and total prohibitions being passed across the country in anticipation of the supreme court overturning {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2 , which guaranteed the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , later this summer.\par \par \uc2 Still, the 15-week ban, which has no medical rationale as a particular endpoint for access, represents a tremendous shift in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/florida"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida}}}\uc2 . The ripple effects could extend far outside of the state\u8217\'20\'19s borders.\par \par \uc2 Currently, abortions are legal up until 24 weeks in the state, which has more than 60 clinics. If, as expected, Roe is overturned, Florida will become a critical access point. The state, particularly its northeastern region with its cluster of clinics, will offer the most viable option for finding a safe, legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  for places such as South Carolina, Georgia, Mississippi, Alabama and Louisiana \u8211\'20\'13 all of which are poised to ban abortions, either entirely or for patients beyond six weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/09/florida-abortion-ban-ron-desantis-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18I\u8217\'20\'19m scared\u8217\'20\'19: Florida faces uncertain \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  future as 15-week ban set to take effect}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 With much of the conversation dealing with gun control and the perception that his administration is hamstrung by Republicans and rebellious Democrats, my colleague {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/davidsmith"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 David Smith}}}\uc2  reports that Biden\u8217\'20\'19s appearance on \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Jimmy Kimmel\uc2  Live!\u8221\'20\'1D wasn\u8217\'20\'19t that funny at all:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C Our very special guest tonight is to aviator sunglasses what \uc2 Tom Cruise\uc2  is to aviator sunglasses,\u8221\'20\'1D quipped the late-night TV host {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abc.com/shows/jimmy-kimmel-live"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jimmy Kimmel}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m proud to say I voted for him dozens of times. He is the reason we all got a cavity search tonight. \u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 This was how Kimmel introduced {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joebiden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden}}}\uc2  for his first in-person interview with a late-night host since taking office as US president.\par \par \uc2 But any hopes that Biden, whose poll ratings are plunging, might have had that the comedian would invite him to show a lighter side to his personality were soon dashed. It was a night when there were not many laughs.\par \par \uc2 Once the president had sat down, Kimmel asked: \u8220\'20\'1CDo you mind if I ask you some serious questions?\u8221\'20\'1D He then dived straight in to demand why, after a flurry of mass shootings across America, nothing had been done since Biden entered the White House.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/09/no-easy-ride-for-biden-kimmel-tells-him-start-yelling-people-gun-violence"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 No easy ride for Biden as Kimmel tells him to \u8216\'20\'18start yelling at people\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 Nation braces for primetime January 6 hearings\par \par \uc2 Morning, everybody. Much of Washington is sleeping in this morning, ahead of the January 6 committee\u8217\'20\'19s primetime presentation of new evidence into the assault on the Capitol beginning at 8pm Eastern time. The idea is to tell a story that, in the words of one of the committee\u8217\'20\'19s members, \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/09/congress-january-6-hearings-tv-production"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will really blow the roof off the House}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D. We\u8217\'20\'19ll see if they succeed.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is on the agenda for today:\par \par \uc2 * Talks on a bipartisan compromise continue in Congress, though their prospects for success remain unclear. The House of Representatives on Wednesday {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/09/us-house-passes-gun-control-bill-faces-defeat-senate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed its own gun control bill}}}\uc2 , but its chances in the upper chamber appear slim.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will address the Ninth Summit of the Americas in Los Angeles. He arrived in the city yesterday and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/09/no-easy-ride-for-biden-kimmel-tells-him-start-yelling-people-gun-violence"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filmed an interview with TV host Jimmy Kimmel}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * Americans are growing increasingly nervous about inflation, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/business/2022/06/09/inflation-worse-poll-americans/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a survey from the Washington Post and George Mason University found}}}\uc2 , with most expecting the price increases to worsen and changing their spending habits in anticipation. On Friday, the labor department will release updated inflation numbers for May.\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/09/us-natural-gas-plant-explosion-freeport-lng-shortages-europe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 An explosion at a Texas natural gas facility}}}\uc2  has raised fears of shortages in Europe, where markets are already struggling with the cutoff of Russia\u8217\'20\'19s supply.\par \par \uc2 2022-06-09T13:49:12Z 2022-06-10T03:37:33Z {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://media.guim.co.uk/1c7f3bd1d8763eca91112fab9457ba09a2faaddf/0_550_8256_4954/500.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://media.guim.co.uk/1c7f3bd1d8763eca91112fab9457ba09a2faaddf/0_550_8256_4954/500.jpg}}}\uc2  A video showing former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  speaking appears on screen during a House select committee hearing on the January 6 attack on the US Capitol. US President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  spoke about the January 6 committee during a meeting with Canadian prime minister \uc2 Justin Trudeau\uc2  in Los Angeles.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220609ei690025v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
