\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Google\uc2  misdirects one in 10 searches for  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  to \u8216\'20\'18pregnancy crisis centers\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Kari Paul \par \uc2 639 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 June 2022\par 19:21 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 In US \u8216\'20\'18trigger states\u8217\'20\'19 where the procedure may soon be illegal, searchers may be sent to centers that do not actually provide care\par \par \uc2 One in 10 \uc2 Google\uc2  searches for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services in US \u8220\'20\'1Ctrigger states\u8221\'20\'1D, where the procedure is likely to become illegal if the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturns Roe v Wade, are being misdirected to clinics known as \u8220\'20\'1Cpregnancy crisis centers\u8221\'20\'1D that do not actually provide care, according to a new study.\par \par \uc2 After a leak {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2022/may/18/us-supreme-court-abortion-reversal-would-be-global-catastrophe-for-women"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 revealed}}}\uc2  the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  is on the verge of overturning the landmark \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights law Roe v Wade, attention has turned to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/03/what-states-abortion-clinics-access-trigger-laws"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Ctrigger law\u8221\'20\'1D states}}}\uc2  that would ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  immediately if the decades-old decision is undone.\par \par \uc2 In more than a dozen such {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/03/what-states-abortion-clinics-access-trigger-laws"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 trigger-law states}}}\uc2 , researchers found, 11% of \uc2 Google\uc2  search results for \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic near me\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill\u8221\'20\'1D led to \u8220\'20\'1Ccrisis pregnancy centers\u8221\'20\'1D, according to misinformation research non-profit {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://counterhate.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Center for Countering Digital Hate (CCDH)}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 These clinics market themselves as healthcare providers but have a \u8220\'20\'1Cshady, harmful agenda\u8221\'20\'1D, according to the reproductive health non-profit Planned Parenthood, offering no health services and aiming instead to dissuade people from having abortions.\par \par \uc2 Such centers now {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2022/05/12/opinion/crisis-pregnancy-centers-roe.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 outnumber}}}\uc2  real \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics three to one, with approximately 2,600 operating in the US, according to a study by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://alliancestateadvocates.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Alliance,}}}\uc2  a coalition of state advocates for women\u8217\'20\'19s rights and gender equality.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  fake clinics are the conversion \u8216\'20\'18therapy\u8217\'20\'19 wing of an anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement that is hell-bent on sending people to jail for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , miscarriage and pregnancy,\u8221\'20\'1D said Erin Matson, co-founder and executive director of pro-choice organization {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://reproaction.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Reproaction}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Researchers in the study used location-altering tools to study 13 trigger-law states including Wyoming, Utah, Texas, Tennessee and Missouri and found 37% of \uc2 Google\uc2  Maps searches led to fake clinics.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, nearly 28% of \uc2 Google\uc2  ads displayed at the top of such search result pages were for anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  fake clinics. One such ad from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://special.clinecenters.org/clinic?gclid=EAIaIQobChMIsOvR5Znc9wIVgwnnCh0khgoZEAAYASACEgLsC_D_BwE"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Cline Centers}}}\uc2  in Mississippi appeared to offer free \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  consultations, but reviews alleged that the \u8220\'20\'1Cfake clinic\u8221\'20\'1D does not \u8220\'20\'1Cprovide medical care\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cexaggerate[s]\u8221\'20\'1D the risks of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Further investigation showed the clinic neither performs nor provides referrals for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  procedures.\par \par \uc2 While \uc2 Google\uc2  labels the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  advertising with a disclaimer that reads \u8220\'20\'1Cdoes not provide abortions\u8221\'20\'1D, the ads often appeared at the top of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services searches. Studies show these misleading results can confuse users seeking abortions, many of whom overlook these disclaimers and contact the fake clinics.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMisleading online advertising targeting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  seekers is not a new concern, although it becomes more urgent as constitutional protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  disappear,\u8221\'20\'1D Matson said.\par \par \uc2 The study has renewed calls for legislation to rein in the power of Big Tech. \uc2 Google{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.businessinsider.com/how-google-retains-more-than-90-of-market-share-2018-4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 controls}}}\uc2  90% of the online search market, making it difficult for users to find alternatives.\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for \uc2 Google\uc2  said the company has longstanding policies that require any organization seeking to advertise to people seeking \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services to be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://support.google.com/adspolicy/answer/9274988?hl=en"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 certified}}}\uc2  and \u8220\'20\'1Cshow in-ad disclosures that clearly state whether they do or do not offer abortions\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAcross our products, we work to make high-quality information easily accessible, particularly on critical health topics,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re always looking at ways to improve our results to help people find what they\u8217\'20\'19re looking for, or understand if what they\u8217\'20\'19re looking for may not be available.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have a right to expect that safety by design is a key consideration for any tech platform,\u8221\'20\'1D said Imran Ahmed, chief executive of the Center for Countering Digital Hate. \u8220\'20\'1CIf \uc2 Google\uc2  refuses to guarantee users\u8217\'20\'19 right to good information, it will be up to lawmakers to step in to ensure that people aren\u8217\'20\'19t harmed by \uc2 Google\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s negligence and greed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220609ei690038p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
