\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 First Thing: Primetime January 6 congressional hearings to begin\b0\par\par\uc2 Clea Skopeliti \par \uc2 1,207 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 June 2022\par 11:20 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Democrats hope movie-length episodes will \u8216\'20\'18really blow the roof off the House\u8217\'20\'19. Plus, the brutal impact of the Salvadoran government\u8217\'20\'19s crackdown on gangsDon\u8217\'20\'19t already get First Thing in your inbox? Sign up here\par \par \uc2 Good morning.\par \par \uc2 When the US House select committee investigating the January 6 insurrection opens its hearings on Thursday evening, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/09/congress-january-6-hearings-tv-production"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 it will do so in prime time and with primetime production values}}}\uc2 . The seven Democrats and two Republicans \u8211\'20\'13 shunned by their own party \u8211\'20\'13 who sit on the panel are pulling out all the stops in an attempt to seize the public\u8217\'20\'19s attention.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A former president of ABC News, James Goldston, a veteran of Good Morning America, will tightly choreograph the six public hearings into {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/06/07/us/politics/jan-6-hearings-tv-democrats.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 movie-length episodes}}}\uc2 . Democratic committee members have said they want a \u8220\'20\'1Cstory that will really blow the roof off the House\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What about the Republicans? The party\u8217\'20\'19s leadership is counting on the American people being so bored by January 6 and distracted by Ukraine, inflation and other worries that millions will avoid tuning in. But opinion poll research suggests they should not be too confident.\par \par \uc2 Trump to testify in probe into his business practices\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will testify under oath in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/08/donald-trump-testify-investigation-children-new-york-ag"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York attorney general\u8217\'20\'19s investigation into his business practices}}}\uc2  on 15 July, according to a court filing released on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The former president\u8217\'20\'19s daughter \uc2 Ivanka Trump\uc2  and son \uc2 Donald Trump Jr\uc2  will also testify.\par \par \uc2 It is the latest development in attorney general\u8217\'20\'19s Letitia James\u8217\'20\'19s three-year investigation, which has focused on whether the \uc2 Trump Organization\uc2  misrepresented the values of its real estate properties for financial gain. James has said investigators have found \u8220\'20\'1Csignificant evidence\u8221\'20\'1D so far.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Is the date for the testimonies fixed? The Trumps have until 13 June to submit a request for the court of appeals to postpone their testimony.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What has Trump said about the probe? The former president, who is not accused of criminal wrongdoing, has repeatedly denied any wrongdoing and has called it a \u8220\'20\'1Cwitch-hunt\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Sievierodonetsk battle will determine fate of eastern Ukraine, Zelenskiy says\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/08/ukraine-may-pull-back-in-sievierodonetsk-russia-war-donbas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The battle for the eastern city of Sievierodonetsk will decide the fate of Donbas,}}}\uc2  the Ukrainian president, \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2 , has said, as fighting continues after Russia pivoted its forces toward the country\u8217\'20\'19s east.\par \par \uc2 While Zelenskiy claimed on Wednesday night that Ukraine had inflicted \u8220\'20\'1Csignificant losses on the enemy\u8221\'20\'1D, regional leaders earlier said that Ukrainian forces had been forced back to the fringes of the city. The Luhansk governor, \uc2 Serhiy Haidai\uc2 , said that much, though not all, of Sievierodonetsk was now under Russian control and that it was no longer possible to evacuate stranded civilians.\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian military advisers said that while Sievierodonetsk and Lysychansk were not strategic cities, the army aimed to wear down Russian forces by fighting fiercely for them. They are the only parts of the Luhansk oblast not in Russian hands.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 How many civilians remain in the frontline city? About 15,000 people, many of whom are elderly, are still in Sievierodonetsk and neighbouring Lysychansk.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A Ukrainian journalist\par \par \uc2 directly addressed the Russian foreign minister, Sergei Lavrov, about grain exports from Ukraine during a news conference in Ankara.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/09/ukrainian-journalist-confronts-russias-sergei-lavrov-with-grain-theft-claim"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Muslim Umerov asked Lavrov:}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1CApart from cereals, what other goods did you steal from Ukraine and who did you sell them to?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 With Ukraine and Russia producing 30% of the world\u8217\'20\'19s wheat supply,\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/ng-interactive/2022/jun/09/the-black-sea-blockade-mapping-the-impact-of-war-in-ukraine-on-the-worlds-food-supply-interactive"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Guardian has this interactive visual guide}}}\uc2  to the impact of the war on the world\u8217\'20\'19s food levels.\par \par \uc2 Twitter\uc2  prepares to give \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  data on fake accounts\par \par \uc2 Twitter\uc2  is preparing to give {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2022/jun/08/twitter-elon-musk-data-demand-fake-accounts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Elon Musk data he has demanded on fake accounts}}}\uc2  after the world\u8217\'20\'19s richest man threatened to walk away from buying the platform.\par \par \uc2 The social media company will reportedly give the \uc2 Tesla\uc2  chief executive access to data comprising more than 500 million tweets sent daily, as well as its \u8220\'20\'1Cfirehose\u8221\'20\'1D of daily traffic.\par \par \uc2 It comes after Musk warned on Monday that he could pull out of the $44bn deal if he was not provided with the data. The multibillionaire has questioned \uc2 Twitter\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s claim that fake and spam accounts make up less than 5% of its 229 million-strong user base.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What has Musk said about fake accounts? Musk has questioned whether advertisers are getting their money\u8217\'20\'19s worth due to the issue of automated accounts.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What does \uc2 Twitter\uc2  say? It has not wavered from the 5% figure since 2014.\par \par \uc2 In other news \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Salvadoran government claims to have imprisoned more than 38,000 people in its crackdown on gangs, with at least 35 reported to have died in custody.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2022/jun/08/its-a-war-on-the-people-el-salvadora-mass-arrests-send-thousands-into-despair"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Critics say the security crackdown, which began in March, is a war on the country\u8217\'20\'19s young and poor.}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 An 11-year-old survivor of the elementary school massacre {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/07/uvalde-teacher-school-shooting-arnulfo-reyes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in Uvalde, Texas}}}\uc2  has told the House oversight committee she covered herself in a friend\u8217\'20\'19s blood.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/08/us-house-hearing-gun-violence-survivors-testify-miah-cerrillo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Miah Cerrillo said she played dead until she was able to reach her teacher\u8217\'20\'19s phone and call police.}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Dozens of academics have alleged that the \uc2 UN\uc2  human rights chief ignored or contradicted research on abuses in Xinjiang, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/09/fury-at-un-human-rights-chief-over-whitewash-of-uyghur-repression"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 saying they felt \u8220\'20\'1Cdeeply disturbed\u8221\'20\'1D by her statement in Guangzhou.}}}\uc2 Michelle Bachelet\uc2  was criticised for giving limited details or condemnation of China.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Florida\u8217\'20\'19s new \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legislation, which bans the procedure after 15 weeks, will have repercussions beyond state borders when it comes into effect on 1 July. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.co.uk/world/2022/jun/09/florida-abortion-ban-ron-desantis-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 If Roe v Wade is overturned this summer,}}}\uc2  Florida will become a critical access point for neighbouring states.\par \par \uc2 Stat of the day: Reserve, the Louisiana town where the cancer-risk rate is 50 times the national average\par \par \uc2 In the Louisiana community of Reserve, the \uc2 Environmental Protection Agency{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2022/jun/08/cancer-alley-louisiana-denka-pollution-consent-decree"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 estimates the cancer-risk rate to be 50 times the US average.}}}\uc2  Now, a proposed legal settlement between the agency and residents in the so-called \u8220\'20\'1CCancer Alley\u8221\'20\'1D region could slash toxic emissions linked to a synthetic rubber plant that emits the likely human carcinogen chloroprene.\par \par \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t miss this: Paula Rego\u8217\'20\'19s extraordinary \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  series\par \par \uc2 The work of Paula Rego, the internationally celebrated Portuguese-born British artist who died on Wednesday at the age of 87, is believed by many to have been influential in Portugal\u8217\'20\'19s referendums on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/artanddesign/2022/jun/09/women-not-victims-paula-rego-extraordinary-abortion-series"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 While Rego\u8217\'20\'19s \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  series was a \u8220\'20\'1Cdirect gesture of protest\u8221\'20\'1D against anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  laws,}}}\uc2  it succeeded in refocusing the debate on women\u8217\'20\'19s experience: away from primal gore and toward individual feeling.\par \par \uc2 Last Thing: an audience with Thailand\u8217\'20\'19s octogenarian \u8216\'20\'18Condom King\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe came up with a new alphabet. [We used] B for birth, C for condom, I for IUD [intrauterine device], V for vasectomy,\u8221\'20\'1D says Mechai Viravaidya, AKA Thailand\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1CCondom King\u8221\'20\'1D. From putting on vasectomy festivals to condom-blowing competitions, the octogenarian and national treasure has more than earned his title. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/09/sex-laughs-and-the-snip-an-audience-with-thailands-condom-king"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Viravaidya explains how, over almost 50 years, he has used humour}}}\uc2  to confront the serious issue of family planning in the country.\par \par \uc2 Sign up\par \par \uc2 First Thing is delivered to thousands of inboxes every weekday. If you\u8217\'20\'19re not already signed up, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/info/2018/sep/17/guardian-us-morning-briefing-sign-up-to-stay-informed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 subscribe now}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Get in touch\par \par \uc2 If you have any questions or comments about any of our newsletters please email 