\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18To some, guns are more important than children\u8217\'20\'19: families testify at House hearing \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein \par \uc2 6,136 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 June 2022\par 20:16 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 House holds hearing on \u8216\'20\'18urgent need to address gun violence epidemic\u8217\'20\'19Supreme court issues ruling in case of bed and breakfast on US-Canada borderArmed man arrested near \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s home over threats to judgeSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 The US politics blog is ending a very busy day in the capital, which saw new developments in one of the many investigations facing former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , difficult-to-stomach testimony in Congress on gun violence and the arrest of a man who was allegedly plotting to kill a supreme court justice.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a recap:\par \par \uc2 * Trump along with his son \uc2 Donald Trump Jr\uc2  and daughter \uc2 Ivanka Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/08/supreme-court-texas-school-shooting-survivor-testify-congress-biden-politics-latest-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-62a0f66a8f08146afdcd6232#block-62a0f66a8f08146afdcd6232"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will testify under oath}}}\uc2  on 15 July in New York attorney general Letitia James\u8217\'20\'19s long-running inquiry into the former president\u8217\'20\'19s business practices.\par \par \uc2 * The top Senate Republican, \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/08/supreme-court-texas-school-shooting-survivor-testify-congress-biden-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-62a0c9708f08146afdcd603f#block-62a0c9708f08146afdcd603f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 calling}}}\uc2  on Capitol Hill for more security for supreme court justices, after an armed man {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/08/brett-kavanaugh-home-man-arrested-supreme-court-justice"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was arrested}}}\uc2  near justice \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s home on the outskirts of Washington DC. \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/08/supreme-court-texas-school-shooting-survivor-testify-congress-biden-politics-latest-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-62a0ee038f08146afdcd61e8#block-62a0ee038f08146afdcd61e8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 condemned the actions}}}\uc2  of the individual, who the court said told police he wanted to kill the judge.\par \par \uc2 * The House oversight committee held a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/08/supreme-court-texas-school-shooting-survivor-testify-congress-biden-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-62a0aba88f08ff5882a79b97#block-62a0aba88f08ff5882a79b97"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hearing}}}\uc2  dubbed \u8220\'20\'1Cthe urgent Need to address the gun violence epidemic\u8221\'20\'1D. Lawmakers heard gut-wrenching testimony from a survivor of the massacre in Uvalde, Texas, as well as the relatives of people killed and injured there and in Buffalo, New York. But the partisan divide over gun control {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/08/supreme-court-texas-school-shooting-survivor-testify-congress-biden-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-62a0d8868f086e322ae39ac3#block-62a0d8868f086e322ae39ac3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appeared as wide as ever}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * The supreme court ruled in favor of a border agent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/08/supreme-court-texas-school-shooting-survivor-testify-congress-biden-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-62a0acad8f08a492031c1ab2#block-62a0acad8f08a492031c1ab2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in a case}}}\uc2  from the US-Canada frontier involving an inn that allegedly is a stopover when some people cross into Canada unlawfully.\par \par \uc2 The blog returns tomorrow, when lawmakers will continue to negotiate over gun control legislation and the January 6 committee holds its first hearing. See you then.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 9.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 8.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump to testify under oath on 15 July in New York\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will testify under oath on 15 July in New York attorney general Letitia James\u8217\'20\'19s investigation into his business practices, according to a court filing released on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 JUST IN: \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will testify under oath on July 15 alongside Don Jr. and \uc2 Ivanka Trump\uc2 , according to new doc from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NewYorkStateAG?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @NewYorkStateAG}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/BkZGNRcC6D"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/BkZGNRcC6D}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Frank G. Runyeon (@frankrunyeon) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/frankrunyeon/status/1534611205972697088?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 8, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 His daughter \uc2 Ivanka Trump\uc2  and son \uc2 Donald Trump Jr\uc2  will also testify.\par \par \uc2 The testimony is the latest development in the three-year investigation into the former president\u8217\'20\'19s dealings after he failed in an attempt last month to stop her investigation and ended up paying a $110,000 fine.\par \par \uc2 James has said investigators have found \u8220\'20\'1Csignificant evidence\u8221\'20\'1D of wrongdoing in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/27/trump-new-york-attorney-general-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 inquiry}}}\uc2 , which has homed in on whether the \uc2 Trump Organization\uc2  misstated the values of its real estate properties to obtain favorable loans and tax deductions.\par \par \uc2 The attorney general previously said her investigation discovered evidence suggesting that for more than a decade, the company\u8217\'20\'19s financial statements \u8220\'20\'1Crelied on misleading asset valuations and other misrepresentations to secure economic benefits\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Trump has repeatedly denied any wrongdoing and has not been accused of committing a crime. He has called the investigation a \u8220\'20\'1Cwitch-hunt\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/27/trump-new-york-attorney-general-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump loses bid to thwart New York inquiry into his business practices}}}\par \par \uc2 Updated at 9.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 8.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 The gun violence hearing in the House is continuing and the California Democrat Jackie Speier, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/nov/24/jackie-speier-republicans-censure-paul-gosar-retirement"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 who in 1978 was shot during a visit to the Jonestown settlement in an attack that killed the congressman she was accompanying}}}\uc2 , got a turn to question witnesses.\par \par \uc2 Speier asked Joseph Gramaglia, the Buffalo police commissioner, to describe what weapons like an AR-15 can do to a body.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve been to numerous shootings throughout my career that were the result of high-powered rifles, assault rifles, and the cavernous holes that they leave in bodies. Decapitation is a pretty good explanation for it,\u8221\'20\'1D Gramaglia replied. \u8220\'20\'1CSome people couldn\u8217\'20\'19t be buried with an open casket. The damage was absolutely devastating.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Referencing her experience in Jonestown, Speier said, \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m a victim of gun violence. I know what it does to a body. And I cannot believe my colleagues don\u8217\'20\'19t recognize that prohibiting the sale of an assault weapon until the age of 21 isn\u8217\'20\'19t going to save lives.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She rejected the idea put forth by Republicans that fortifying schools was one way to stop the shootings.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe all know what the solution to this problem is. It\u8217\'20\'19s comprehensive gun reform in this country. We know what it is. We are not supposed to be holding our students and our teachers responsible,\u8221\'20\'1D Speier said.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 8.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 7.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden condemns man arrested near Justice Kavanaugh's house\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has condemned a man who said he planned to kill supreme court justice \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2 , amid heightened tensions around the court as it prepares to rule on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and gun rights, among other controversial topics.\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  said the president \u8220\'20\'1Ccondemns the actions [of] this individual in the strongest terms,\u8221\'20\'1D Reuters reported. \u8220\'20\'1CAny threats of violence or attempts to intimidate justices have no place in our society.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A man {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://storage.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.mdd.514015/gov.uscourts.mdd.514015.1.1.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 identified in court documents}}}\uc2  as Nicholas John Roske was arrested early Wednesday morning near the conservative justice\u8217\'20\'19s Maryland home. According to the complaint charging Roske with attempting to kill a supreme court justice, he first got out of a taxicab near Kavanaugh\u8217\'20\'19s house, then walked away and called 911, saying he was having suicidal thoughts and planned to killed a justice of the high court. Police arrested him and found a Glock 17 pistol, pepper spray, zip ties and other items in a backpack and suitcase.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/08/brett-kavanaugh-home-man-arrested-supreme-court-justice"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Armed man arrested near Brett Kavanaugh\u8217\'20\'19s home over threats to judge}}}\par \par \uc2 Updated at 7.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 7.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 US continues to recognize \uc2 Juan Guaido\uc2  as interim president of Venezuela - White House\par \par \uc2 The US regards Venezuelan opposition leader \uc2 Juan Guaid\u243\'00\'F3\uc2  as the true interim president of his country, US national security adviser Jake Sullivan said moments ago aboard Air Force One, more than three years after Guaid\u243\'00\'F3 declared himself {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2019/jan/27/juan-guaido-venezuela-has-chance-to-leave-chaos-behind"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the true victor}}}\uc2  in a disputed election over Nicol\u225\'00\'E1s Maduro and tried to topple the man in control of the troubled South American nation.\par \par \uc2 US president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  plans to speak with Guaido at some point during this week\u8217\'20\'19s Summit of the Americas meeting that the US is hosting in California for leaders from the hemisphere, Sullivan said.\par \par \uc2 Biden, aides, staff and media are on board Air Force One now, en route Washington, DC, to Los Angeles, and Sullivan and White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  are gaggling - with Sullivan on right now, answering accompanying journalists\u8217\'20\'19 questions.\par \par \uc2 Venezuela, Nicaragua and Cuba were not invited to the summit, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/06/06/politics/lopez-obrador-summit-of-the-americas/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 prompting}}}\uc2  a boycott by Mexico, in a debacle for Biden.\par \par \uc2 Brazilian autocratic president \uc2 Jair Bolsonaro\uc2  will attend and Biden is expected to discuss \u8220\'20\'1Copen, transparent and democratic elections\u8221\'20\'1D with him, Sullivan said.\par \par \uc2 And the climate and the health of the Amazon rainforest will be on the agenda, Sullivan said.\par \par \uc2 There is much hope in journalism circles that Bolsonaro can be pressed at the summit to address the topics of illegal logging and drug trafficking in vast, supposedly-protected tracts of the Amazon region and the danger to those who strive against such destructive law-making - including freelance journalist and Guardian regular Dom Phillips and his traveling companion, indigenous culture expert Bruno Ara\u250\'00\'FAjo Pereira, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/07/british-journalist-dom-phillips-missing-amazon-brazil-wife-calls-for-urgency"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 missing in the region}}}\uc2  since Sunday.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/07/british-journalist-dom-phillips-missing-amazon-brazil-wife-calls-for-urgency"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Every second counts\u8217\'20\'19: wife of British journalist missing in Amazon urges action}}}\par \par \uc2 6.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 Interim summary\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s been an extremely busy day in Washington and there is more to come. The House oversight committee hearing on the \u8220\'20\'1Curgent need to address gun violence\u8221\'20\'1D in the US, following very recent mass shootings, is now on lunch recess.\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  is now \u8220\'20\'1Cgaggling\u8221\'20\'1D on Air Force One, as \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  heads to Los Angeles to host the Summit of the Americas. It\u8217\'20\'19s a bumpy ride for those aboard the presidential plane (literally but, presumably, always metaphorically).\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where things stand:\par \par \uc2 * Senate minority leader and Kentucky Republican \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/08/supreme-court-texas-school-shooting-survivor-testify-congress-biden-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-62a0c9708f08146afdcd603f#block-62a0c9708f08146afdcd603f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 calling}}}\uc2  on Capitol Hill for more security for supreme court justices, following the reports this morning that an armed man {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/08/brett-kavanaugh-home-man-arrested-supreme-court-justice"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was arrested}}}\uc2  near supreme court justice \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s home on the outskirts of Washington DC. The court said the man told police he wanted to kill the judge.\par \par \uc2 * The supreme court ruled in favor of a border agent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/08/supreme-court-texas-school-shooting-survivor-testify-congress-biden-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-62a0acad8f08a492031c1ab2#block-62a0acad8f08a492031c1ab2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in a case}}}\uc2  from the US-Canadian border involving an inn that allegedly is a stopover when some people cross into Canada unlawfully.\par \par \uc2 * The House oversight committee opened its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/08/supreme-court-texas-school-shooting-survivor-testify-congress-biden-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-62a0aba88f08ff5882a79b97#block-62a0aba88f08ff5882a79b97"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hearing}}}\uc2  dubbed \u8220\'20\'1Cthe urgent need to address the gun violence epidemic\u8221\'20\'1D, which became a gut-wrenching look into the recent spate of mass shootings nationwide.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 7.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 6.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 Back at the House oversight committee, Democratic and Republican lawmakers are taking turns questioning the witnesses, creating a split-screen view of the two parties\u8217\'20\'19 attitudes on gun control.\par \par \uc2 Louisiana Republican \uc2 Clay Higgins\uc2  recalls a childhood in which \u8220\'20\'1Cwe had guns everywhere\u8221\'20\'1D and wonders why there weren\u8217\'20\'19t mass shootings back then.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI asked you all what happened to that country,\u8221\'20\'1D Higgins said. \u8220\'20\'1CA country where guns were everywhere and virtually not regulated at all, where millions of Americans, 14 million Americans came back... after world war II with incredible skills of war and weapons of war as you call them everywhere, but we didn\u8217\'20\'19t have mass shootings.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2 , a New York Democrat, drew a line between increasing firearm sales and gunmakers\u8217\'20\'19 profits, declaring, \u8220\'20\'1CThis is about blood money.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s also this discussion about anything but, again, but that these are about violent people, but yet we aren\u8217\'20\'19t doing anything about addressing the actual root causes of misogyny, where two-thirds of mass shootings are connected to domestic violence, or the emergence of white supremacy, radicalization, mass incarceration and poverty and the connections between that and mass shootings in our communities,\u8221\'20\'1D Ocasio-Cortez said.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 6.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 6.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ahead of the start of the January 6 hearings tomorrow, the committee\u8217\'20\'19s chair, \uc2 Bennie Thompson\uc2 , told NPR {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2022/06/08/1102909009/jan-6-committee-members-capitol-attack-thompson?utm_campaign=storyshare&utm_source=twitter.com&utm_medium=social"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in an interview}}}\uc2  that democracy came close to ending in the United States that day.\par \par \uc2 Thompson says he\u8217\'20\'19s calling it as he sees it on the investigation into the Jan. 6 attack that was intended to keep Congress from certifying the 2020 presidential election results. And he says he\u8217\'20\'19s gained a new education about the danger the country faced that day, which he aims to share through the hearings.\par \par \uc2 For Thompson, preserving democracy today means telling the full story of the attack on the Capitol and ensuring its moment in history is one that Americans never forget. \u8220\'20\'1C\par \par \uc2 I have learned a lot about how perilously close we came on January 6 to losing this democracy as a lot of us have come to know and love it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 My colleague {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/hugo-lowell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hugo Lowell\u8217\'20\'19s}}}\uc2  story published earlier today outlined how the first hearing will go, which will take place during the prime-time TV hour at 8 pm eastern.\par \par \uc2 At the start of the hearing, the panel\u8217\'20\'19s chairman \uc2 Bennie Thompson\uc2  and vice-chair \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  will make a series of opening arguments before outlining a general roadmap of how each of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/06/capitol-attack-panel-public-hearings"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the six Watergate-style hearings}}}\uc2  are expected to unfold.\par \par \uc2 For the second hour, Thompson and Cheney will hand control of the hearing to Tim Heaphy, the chief investigative counsel for the select committee, who will lead the questioning of two witnesses and walk through the key moments of the Capitol attack.\par \par \uc2 The select committee is expected to start the questioning with testimony from Nick Quested, a British documentary film-maker who was embedded with the far-right Proud Boys group in the days and weeks leading up to January 6 and caught their activities on camera.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/08/inaugural-january-6-hearing-to-track-activities-of-proud-boys-during-capitol-attack"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Inaugural January 6 hearing to track activities of Proud Boys during Capitol attack}}}\par \par \uc2 Updated at 6.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 5.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 The justice department has named a nine-person panel to review the police response to the Uvalde shooting, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/uvalde-school-shooting-texas-shootings-merrick-garland-police-43851792809e619d0ea67d5b7819dd6c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Associated Press reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In a statement, the Justice Department said it was committed to \u8220\'20\'1Cmoving as expeditiously as possible in the development of the report.\u8221\'20\'1D Officials said the team would conduct a complete reconstruction of the shooting; review all relevant documents, including policies, photos and videos; conduct a visit to the school; and interview an array of witnesses and families of the victims, along with police, school and government officials.\par \par \uc2 A \uc2 FBI\uc2  unit chief will take part in the inquiry, as will the former police chief of Sacramento, the sheriff of Orange county, Florida, and a deputy chief whose tenure included \uc2 Virginia Tech\uc2 . Similar investigations followed the 2015 extremist attack in San Bernardino, California and the 2016 Pulse Nightclub shooting in Orlando.\par \par \uc2 The police response to the Uvalde shooting {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/04/uvalde-police-training-school-shooter-response-time"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has been criticized}}}\uc2  after officers waited before confronting the gunman. State officials have acknowledged that hesitating was \u8220\'20\'1Cthe wrong decision,\u8221\'20\'1D and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/01/uvalde-school-police-chief-pete-arredondo-sworn-in"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 scrutiny has focused on Pedro \u8220\'20\'1CPete\u8221\'20\'1D Arredondo, the police chief who was recently sworn onto the city council}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Updated at 5.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 5.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 McConnell decries 'assassination attempt or something close to it' on Kavanaugh\par \par \uc2 Senate minority leader and Kentucky Republican \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  is calling on Capitol Hill for more security for supreme court justices, following the reports this morning that an armed man {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/08/brett-kavanaugh-home-man-arrested-supreme-court-justice"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was arrested}}}\uc2  near supreme court justice \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s home on the outskirts of Washington DC.\par \par \uc2 This morning\u8217\'20\'19s disturbing reports are exactly why the Senate unanimously passed a Supreme Court security bill weeks ago. But House Democrats have inexplicably blocked it. House Democrats need to stop their blockade and pass this uncontroversial bill today. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/wd8UB5RDvm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/wd8UB5RDvm}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Leader McConnell (@LeaderMcConnell) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/LeaderMcConnell/status/1534552571943211009?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 8, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 McConnell said on the floor of the Senate: \u8220\'20\'1CThis is where we are, Mr President, if these reports are correct, an assassination attempt against a sitting justice, or something close to it. This is exactly the kind of event that many feared the terrible breach of the court\u8217\'20\'19s rules and norms would fuel [with the leak last month of the draft opinion that the conservative majority wants to overturn constitutional \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights afforded by the 1973 Roe V Wade ruling].\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is exactly that kind of event that many worried the unhinged, reckless, apocalyptic rhetoric from prominent figures towards the court going back many months and especially in recent weeks could make more likely.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He said that was why the Senate passed legislation shortly after the early May leak, to enhance police protection for sitting justices and their families.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is common sense, non-controversial legislation that passed unanimously in this chamber, but House Democrats have spent weeks blocking. That needs to change right now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Updated at 5.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 5.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 Lawmakers on the House oversight committee are now questioning the witnesses, in a conversation that is overall a little more strident {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/07/joe-biden-us-politics-news-latest-democrats-republicans-primaries-live?page=with:block-629f5c488f08a189de52932b&filterKeyEvents=false"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 than the Senate\u8217\'20\'19s similar hearing yesterday}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Before questioning began, lawmakers heard from Amy Swearer of \uc2 The Heritage Foundation\uc2 , who was invited by the Republican minority and provided the conservative rebuttal to the officials and advocates who spoke before her.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAn unspeakably horrific event, like Uvalde or Buffalo happens. Reflexively, almost compulsively, come calls for Congress to pass a whole host of gun control measures largely targeting peaceable, law abiding citizens,\u8221\'20\'1D Swearer said. \u8220\'20\'1CShould anyone dare question the constitutionality, practicality or even the effectiveness of any of these policies, their opposition is immediately framed as callous obstructionism. And their legitimate concerns are brushed aside as and I quote, bullshit.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She downplayed the effectiveness of legislation against expanded capacity magazines, and called for more armed guards at school, improvements to building security, mental health care and to \u8220\'20\'1Cpromote responsible gun ownership without simultaneously imposing financial burdens on gun owners or hindering their ability to immediately respond to violent threats.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 4.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 Buffalo\u8217\'20\'19s police commissioner, Joseph Gramaglia, took aim at the concept promoted by gun rights advocates that expanding firearms access could stop mass shootings.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is often said that a good guy with a gun will stop a bad guy with a gun,\u8221\'20\'1D Gramaglia told the House. However, retired Buffalo police officer Aaron Salter Jr., who was working as a security guard at the Tops Market and was killed in the shooting, \u8220\'20\'1CWas no match for what he went up against a legal AR-15 with multiple high capacity magazines.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Noting that such mass shootings make up a minority of overall gun crime, the commissioner warned of new gun technologies that could make the problem worse.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe grim reality is that shootings have become a daily occurrence in American cities. Emerging trends like ghost guns and guns modified with switches continue to pose a challenge for law enforcement,\u8221\'20\'1D Gramaglia said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCongress must update our laws to account for these new threats and carnage that has accompanied them. It will be nearly impossible to address the gun violence epidemic without first addressing the underlying violent crime problem.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Updated at 5.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 4.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 Warning that it is \u8220\'20\'1Chigh noon in America,\u8221\'20\'1D New York\u8217\'20\'19s mayor, \uc2 Eric Adams\uc2 , told lawmakers in the House: \u8220\'20\'1CThe clock is ticking, every day, every minute towards another hour of death.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 New York City Police Department\uc2  is overwhelmed by illegal guns, he said, despite confiscating 3,000 this year alone. Adams called for more federal aid for states and cities, the confirmation of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s nominee to lead the federal \uc2 Bureau of Alcohol, Tobacco, Firearms and Explosives\uc2 , and for Congress to expand background check and pass other gun control legislation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI stand with President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in calling on Congress to act now to regulate or ban assault weapons in this country. Even if we only raise the age required to buy one of these weapons, lives will be saved,\u8221\'20\'1D the mayor said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe must build a society where our youth are on a path to fulfillment, not a road to ruin.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Updated at 5.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 4.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Armed man arrested near supreme court justice \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2 's home\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US Supreme Court\uc2  says an armed man has been arrested near associate justice \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s home after making threats against him, the Associated Press writes.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  was first {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/dc-md-va/2022/06/08/kavanaugh-threat-arrest-justice/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 with the story}}}\uc2 , reporting that a California man in his mid-twenties, with at least one weapon in his possession and tools used in burglaries, was apprehended near the judge\u8217\'20\'19s home in Maryland and had told law enforcement that he wanted to kill Kavanaugh, and citing people familiar with the investigation. It happened at about 1.50am ET today.\par \par \uc2 The Post further reports that:\par \par \uc2 Two people familiar with the investigation said the initial evidence indicates the man was angry about the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2022/05/02/roe-v-wade-supreme-court-draft-politico/?itid=lk_inline_manual_2&itid=lk_inline_manual_3&itid=lk_inline_manual_8&itid=lk_inline_manual_5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 leaked draft of an opinion by the Supreme Court }}}\uc2  signaling the court is preparing to overturn Roe. v. Wade, the 49-year-old decision that guaranteed a person\u8217\'20\'19s constitutional right to have an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/abortion/?itid=lk_inline_manual_5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 . He was also angry over a recent spate of mass shootings, those people said.\par \par \uc2 Following the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/02/roe-v-wade-abortion-supreme-court-draft-opinion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 leak last month}}}\uc2  of that draft opinion - with the final opinion awaited with enormous tension across the US this month - {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/13/us-abortion-protests-pro-choice-marches"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 protesters appeared}}}\uc2  near the homes of conservative members of the supreme court bench.\par \par \uc2 These included {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2022/may/06/samuel-alito-profile-abortion-supreme-court-justice"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Samuel Alito}}}\uc2 , who wrote the draft opinion that was leaked and slammed the Roe decision, and two of the justices nominated by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  that represented a strong swing to the right on the nine-member bench - {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/brett-kavanaugh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/06/people-of-praise-accused-child-abuse-amy-coney-barrett"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Amy Coney Barrett}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Those previous protests were entirely peaceful, though technically {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/05/12/politics/supreme-court-justices-abortion-protests-garland/index.html?utm_term=16524378438454b00471ec8f1&utm_source=cnn_Five+Things+for+Friday%2C+May+13%2C+2022&utm_medium=email&bt_ee=sYjt8FIm4dgLCZxraxEOZaYBWsNoQ73DAjfhfVuz9rBebmmwh%2BLzhpgLYP3YX%2B%2Bj&bt_ts=1652437843848"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 probably illegal}}}\uc2 , and there had apparently been no arrests.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what Lauren Burke {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/13/us-abortion-protests-pro-choice-marches"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  for the Guardian at the time:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/13/us-abortion-protests-pro-choice-marches"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Protesters rally outside US supreme court justices\u8217\'20\'19 homes ahead of pro-choice marches}}}\par \par \uc2 4.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 After a brief recess, the House hearing has now moved on to testimony from elected officials, representatives from advocacy groups and other, but it wrapped up its first half with more gut-wrenching testimony from parents affected by gun violence.\par \par \uc2 Kimberly Rubio described how she found out that her daughter Lexi was among those killed in Uvalde, and outlined specific policies she thinks could prevent such attacks. \u8220\'20\'1CWe understand that for some reason, to some people, to people with money, to people who fund political campaigns, the guns are more important than children,\u8221\'20\'1D Rubio said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo at this moment, we ask for progress. We seek to raise the age to purchase these weapons from 18 to 21 years of age, we seek red flag laws, stronger background checks. We also want to repeal gun manufacturers liability, immunity.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Lucretia Hughes of Women for Gun Rights\u8217\'20\'19s DC Project told lawmakers how her 19-year-old son was shot and killed while playing dominoes, but unlike the witnesses before her, she did not call for more restrictions on firearms. Rather, she saw weapons as an important tool for self-defense and linked gun control laws to racism.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSomething has to change. Thoughts and prayers and calls for more gun control isn\u8217\'20\'19t enough. How about letting me defend myself from evil? You don\u8217\'20\'19t think that I\u8217\'20\'19m capable and trustworthy to handle a firearm? You don\u8217\'20\'19t think that the second amendment doesn\u8217\'20\'19t apply to people that look like me?\u8221\'20\'1D said Hughes, who is Black.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWho and you who would call for more gun controls are the same ones that are calling to defund the police? Who is supposed to protect us? We must prepare to be our own first responders to protect ourselves and our loved ones.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 4.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 In recorded testimony, fourth-grader Miah Cerrillo described how the Uvalde killer shot her teacher in the head then opened fire on her classmates, including a friend right next to her.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI thought he was gonna come back into the room, so I grabbed the blood and I put it all over me,\u8221\'20\'1D Cerillo said in a recorded video. Speaking with little emotion, Cerillo, described how she grabbed her teacher\u8217\'20\'19s phone and called 911. An unidentified voice on the video then asked Cerillo if she felt safe at school, to which she responded by shaking her head. When asked if she thinks such a shooting could happen again, she nodded.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 4.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 3.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Roy Guerrero, a pediatrician in Uvalde, is providing a graphic depiction of what he saw on May 24, the day of the mass killing.\par \par \uc2 It began, he said, with a text message from a colleague in nearby San Antonio, asking why pediatric surgeons and anesthesiologists were put on call for a mass shooting in Uvalde. Guerrero raced to the town\u8217\'20\'19s hospital, describing a scene of \u8220\'20\'1Cparents outside yelling children\u8217\'20\'19s names in desperation and sobbing as they beg for any news related to their child. Those mother\u8217\'20\'19s cries I will never get out of my head,\u8221\'20\'1D he told lawmakers.\par \par \uc2 The details of his testimony are harrowing. He describes encountering Mia, a child he\u8217\'20\'19d known since birth, alive but with her white Lilo and Stitch shirt covered in blood from a shrapnel wound on her shoulder. He described finding the bodies of two children \u8220\'20\'1Cwhose bodies had been pulverized by bullets fired at them, decapitate, whose flesh had been ripped apart.\u8221\'20\'1D He talked about realizing that many other children were killed in the same manner.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe thing I can\u8217\'20\'19t figure out is whether our politicians are failing us out of stubbornness, passivity, or both,\u8221\'20\'1D Guerrero said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COnce the blood is rinsed away from the bodies of our loved ones, and scrubbed off the floors of the schools and supermarkets and churches, the carnage from each scene is erased from our collective conscience. And we return again to nostalgia to the rose tinted view of our second amendment as a perfect instrument of American life. No matter how many lives are lost.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 3.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 The committee is now hearing from its first witness, Zeneta Everhart, whose son Zaire Goodman was shot in the racist attack at the Tops Market in a predominantly Black neighborhood in Buffalo.\par \par \uc2 She starts by drawing a link between the shooting and the country\u8217\'20\'19s history of slavery and racism: \u8220\'20\'1CMy ancestors, the first currency of America, were stripped of their heritage and culture, separated from their families bargained for on auction blocks, sold, beaten, lynched. Yet I continuously hear after every mass shooting that this is not who we are as Americans and as a nation. Hear me clearly. This is exactly who we are.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She went on to describe how the bullets from the AR-15 style rifle used in the shooting exploded in her sons body, leaving shrapnel wounds that she has to clean. \u8220\'20\'1CMy son Zaire has a hole in the right side of his neck, on his back, and another on his left leg.caused by an exploding bullet from an AR-15. As I clean his wounds I can feel pieces of that bullet in his back. Shrapnel will be left inside of his body for the rest of his life. Now I want you to picture that exact scenario for one of your children. This should not be your story or mine.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Watch video of Everhart\u8217\'20\'19s testimony:\par \par \uc2 Updated at 5.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 3.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 Supreme court issues ruling in case of bed and breakfast on US-Canada border\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  has just issued its latest, just one opinion today, and it\u8217\'20\'19s none of the biggest cases awaitedthis month.\par \par \uc2 Americans are on the edge of their seats over cases that fundamentally affect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, gun control, government regulation of emissions and the policy of making undocumented migrants who cross the southern border wait in Mexico during their US court cases.\par \par \uc2 However, today\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/opinions/21pdf/21-147_g31h.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 single opinion}}}\uc2 , written by associate justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 , in the case Egbert v Boule, involved the owner of a bed and breakfast \u8211\'20\'13 called the Smugglers Inn and owned by Robert Boule \u8211\'20\'13 on the US-Canadian border and the conduct of immigration agents.\par \par \uc2 The inn has come under suspicion over allegedly unlawful crossings by guests from the US into Canada.\par \par \uc2 Case was brought by Robert Boule, who was allegedly shoved to the ground by a border patrol agent who came onto his property without a warrant to check the immigration status of a guest at the inn Boule owns in Washington.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lydia Wheeler (@WheelerLydia) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/WheelerLydia/status/1534539427409711105?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 8, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The court ruled against Boule.\par \par \uc2 Vox {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vox.com/2022/3/1/22946305/supreme-court-egbert-boule-bivens-law-enforcement-constitution-border"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2  earlier this year:\par \par \uc2 In March of 2014 Boule welcomed a guest who had recently arrived in the United States from Turkey. Although the guest was lawfully present in the United States, federal border patrol agent Erik Egbert decided to confront this guest when he arrived at Boule\u8217\'20\'19s inn.\par \par \uc2 When the guest arrived, Egbert drove onto Boule\u8217\'20\'19s property and approached the car containing the guest. After Boule asked Egbert to leave, and Egbert refused, Boule stepped between the border patrol agent and his guest. Egbert then allegedly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://casetext.com/case/boule-v-egbert-3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shoved Boule against the car, grabbed him, and pushed him to the ground}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Then, after Boule complained to Egbert\u8217\'20\'19s supervisor about this treatment, Egbert allegedly retaliated against him by contacting the \uc2 Internal Revenue Service\uc2  and asking that agency to investigate Boule\u8217\'20\'19s tax statute.\par \par \uc2 Boule, in other words, alleges that Agent Egbert violated his constitutional rights. The Fourth Amendment forbids \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.law.cornell.edu/constitution/fourth_amendment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unreasonable searches and seizures,}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D and if Egbert did, indeed, assault Boule, that could form the basis for a valid Fourth Amendment lawsuit. Boule also claims he had a First Amendment right to complain to Egbert\u8217\'20\'19s supervisor {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://casetext.com/case/boule-v-egbert-3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 without facing retaliation}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The primary issue in Boule is the continued viability of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.law.cornell.edu/supremecourt/text/403/388"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bivens v. Six Unknown Named Agents}}}\uc2  (1971), which permits federal lawsuits against federal officials who allegedly violated the Constitution. Although the Court has not yet overruled Bivens, it has already stripped that case of much of its force.\par \par \uc2 Supreme Court opinion is Egbert v. Boule. Court rules for border patrol agent. Holds Bivens does not extend to create causes of action for a Fourth Amendment excessive-force claim and a First Amendment retaliation claim against a Border Patrol agent.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lydia Wheeler (@WheelerLydia) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/WheelerLydia/status/1534537597690732545?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 8, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The supreme court is expected to rule again tomorrow, it won\u8217\'20\'19t be known on what case(s) until it happens.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 4.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 3.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 In his opening statement the committee\u8217\'20\'19s top Republican, James Comer, offered a concise summary of many of the conservative counterarguments to the push for gun control that has followed these latest mass shootings.\par \par \uc2 Focusing on the recent rise in crime nationwide, Comer said the country must be ready to defend against \u8220\'20\'1Cevil people\u8221\'20\'1D and cast private gun ownership as a way of doing that. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from the Kentucky representative:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe must work together to deliver sensible solutions to secure our schools, protect our most vulnerable among us and bring to justice those responsible for these heinous crimes,\u8221\'20\'1D Comer said.\par \par \uc2 He continued: \u8220\'20\'1CI believe that we must carefully consider the security posture of vulnerable targets sought out by evil people. We must ensure that every American has a safe environment in which to live their lives in peace. And that requires thinking creatively about solutions to harden our infrastructure, enforce our existing laws and work to foster a culture that values conflict resolution and dialogue over violence. I strongly believe that there\u8217\'20\'19s an important place for law abiding gun owners to serve in protecting themselves, their families and their communities from violence.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Updated at 3.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 3.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democratic Congresswoman \uc2 Carolyn B Maloney\uc2  has opened the hearing by acknowledging a hard truth about gun violence in the United States: while mass shootings generate headlines, gun violence is a \u8220\'20\'1Csteady drumbeat\u8221\'20\'1D across the country.\par \par \uc2 The New York representative continued, \u8220\'20\'1CAnd so many of our towns and cities, especially in marginalized communities, Black men make up more than half of all gun victims in the United States. Despite making up less than 6% of the population. Latinos are twice as likely to be killed by gun and four times as likely to be wounded by a gun as white Americans. We need transparency into how guns are reaching the hands of criminals.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Ahead of the testimony, Maloney asked \u8220\'20\'1Cevery member of this committee to listen with an open heart to the brave witnesses who have come forward to tell their stories about how gun violence has impacted their lives. Our witnesses today have endured pain and loss. They displayed incredible courage by coming here to ask us to do our jobs. That let\u8217\'20\'19s hear their voices. Let us honor their courage. Let us find the same courage to pass common sense laws to protect our children.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Democratic-led chamber will today vote for \u8220\'20\'1Ccommon sense gun safety legislation,\u8221\'20\'1D Maloney said, though what the Senate will do with it remains unknown.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 3.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 3.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 House begins hearing on 'urgent need to address gun violence epidemic'\par \par \uc2 The House oversight committee has opened its hearing dubbed \u8220\'20\'1Cthe urgent need to address the gun violence epidemic,\u8221\'20\'1D which is likely to be a gut-wrenching look into the recent spate of mass shootings nationwide.\par \par \uc2 Among those testifying is Miah Cerrillo, a fourth-grade student who survived the shooting at Robb elementary school in Uvalde, Texas, the parents of Lexi Rubio, who was killed in the massacre, local pediatrician Roy Guerrero and Zeneta Everhart, whose son was shot in the massacre at a supermarket in Buffalo, New York. Republican lawmakers, who make up a minority in the chamber, have invited Lucretia Hughes of Women for Gun Rights\u8217\'20\'19s DC Project.\par \par \uc2 You can watch along {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://oversight.house.gov/legislation/hearings/the-urgent-need-to-address-the-gun-violence-epidemic"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Updated at 3.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 2.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today\u8217\'20\'19s gun violence hearing will undoubtedly be harrowing but the tension in Congress won\u8217\'20\'19t end there. The first session of the January 6 committee is set for Thursday evening during the prime-time TV hour, and my colleague {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/hugo-lowell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hugo Lowell}}}\uc2  looks here at what viewers can expect:\par \par \uc2 The House select committee investigating the January 6 Capitol attack is scheduled to hold its inaugural hearing on Thursday and according to the running order obtained by the Guardian, the panel will track the activities of the far-right Proud Boys group before and during the insurrection.\par \par \uc2 At the start of the hearing, the panel\u8217\'20\'19s chairman \uc2 Bennie Thompson\uc2  and vice-chair \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  will make a series of opening arguments before outlining a general roadmap of how each of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/06/capitol-attack-panel-public-hearings"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the six Watergate-style hearings}}}\uc2  are expected to unfold.\par \par \uc2 For the second hour, Thompson and Cheney will hand control of the hearing to Tim Heaphy, the chief investigative counsel for the select committee, who will lead the questioning of two witnesses and walk through the key moments of the Capitol attack.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/08/inaugural-january-6-hearing-to-track-activities-of-proud-boys-during-capitol-attack"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Inaugural January 6 hearing to track activities of Proud Boys during Capitol attack}}}\par \par \uc2 2.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s worth taking a closer look at what happened in San Francisco last night, where voters in a city that\u8217\'20\'19s normally a haven for progressive policies decisively ousted District Attorney \uc2 Chesa Boudin\uc2 , who pledged to reform the criminal justice system. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/sam-levin"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sam Levin}}}\uc2  has unpacked how it happened:\par \par \uc2 San Francisco residents have voted to recall the district attorney, \uc2 Chesa Boudin\uc2 , who was elected on an agenda of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2019/nov/16/son-of-jailed-radicals-reviled-by-the-police-union-now-chesa-boudin-is-san-franciscos-top-cop"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 criminal justice reform}}}\uc2  but faced intensifying backlash from law enforcement, conservatives and residents concerned about crime.\par \par \uc2 Boudin\u8217\'20\'19s removal as the city\u8217\'20\'19s top prosecutor in the middle of his first term is a major blow to a growing movement across the US to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/02/chesa-boudin-san-francisco-da-recall"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 elect progressive DAs}}}\uc2  dedicated to tackling mass incarceration, police brutality and racism in the legal system.\par \par \uc2 The race was called by the Associated Press just over an hour after polls closed, with partial returns showing the recall received about 60% of the vote.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/07/san-francisco-vote-chesa-boudin-recall"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 San Francisco recalls DA Chesa Boudin in blow to criminal justice reform}}}\par \par \uc2 2.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Child massacre survivor to testify before House amid talks on gun compromise\par \par \uc2 Good morning, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-politics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US politics}}}\uc2  blog readers. Americans will today hear congressional testimony from one of the young survivors of last month\u8217\'20\'19s massacre in Uvalde, Texas, as well as the relatives of some of the victims, while the House is also expected to introduce a gun control measure. On top of all that, the supreme court will this morning release rulings on some of the 30 cases still awaiting decisions \u8211\'20\'13 which could lead to major changes in \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, gun access and other hot-button issues.\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s look a little closer at the day\u8217\'20\'19s packed agenda:\par \par \uc2 * The supreme court will release the decisions from 10am ET. There\u8217\'20\'19s no telling which rulings will come, but the most closely watched of the pending decisions are an environmental case out of West Virginia, a gun rights case stemming from New York, an immigration case via Texas involving the US-Mexico border and the pivotal Mississippi \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  case that also includes the state authorities asking justices to overturn Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 * At the same time as the court\u8217\'20\'19s decisions, the House oversight committee will {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://oversight.house.gov/legislation/hearings/the-urgent-need-to-address-the-gun-violence-epidemic"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hold a hearing}}}\uc2  on gun violence featuring testimony from Miah Cerrillo, a fourth grade student at Robb elementary school in Uvalde and others impacted by recent shootings there and in Buffalo, New York.\par \par \uc2 * The House is also expected {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/07/joe-biden-us-politics-news-latest-democrats-republicans-primaries-live?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-629f96fa8f08a189de5295ff#block-629f96fa8f08a189de5295ff"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to release its own gun control bill}}}\uc2  but if any legislation makes it through Congress, it will likely originate in the Senate, where Democratic and Republican lawmakers are holding negotiations on finding a compromise measure.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is going to Los Angeles, where he will speak at the ninth Summit of the Americas and film an interview for Jimmy Kimmel Live that airs at 8pm eastern time.\par \par \uc2 * Voters are digesting the aftermath of yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s primary elections in seven states that saw San Francisco\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/07/san-francisco-vote-chesa-boudin-recall"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 progressive district attorney recalled}}}\uc2  and the Los Angeles mayor\u8217\'20\'19s race {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/07/los-angeles-mayoral-race-karen-bass-rick-caruso-runoff"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 head to a runoff}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Updated at 2.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 2022-06-08T13:21:35Z2022-06-08T20:31:58Z{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://media.guim.co.uk/4580bd56ccfa4032357c5a91ee0e5ee442433d92/0_145_3500_2101/500.jpgBrett"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://media.guim.co.uk/4580bd56ccfa4032357c5a91ee0e5ee442433d92/0_145_3500_2101/500.jpgBrett}}}\uc2  Kavanaugh in 2018.Pro-choice protesters pass in front of Supreme Court Justice \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s house in Chevy Chase, MD, as Montgomery County Police and federal marshals stand guard.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220608ei680020e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
