\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Fire at New York anti- \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  facility investigated as suspected arson\b0\par\par\uc2 Ed Pilkington in New York \par \uc2 439 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 June 2022\par 15:54 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Building in upstate New York New had its windows smashed and premises allegedly firebombed\par \par \uc2 Police are investigating a suspected arson attack at an anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic in upstate New York in which a facility describing itself as a \u8220\'20\'1Cpro-life medical office\u8221\'20\'1D had its windows smashed and premises allegedly firebombed.\par \par \uc2 The fire broke out early on Tuesday morning at the CompassCare \u8220\'20\'1Ccommunity medical facility\u8221\'20\'1D in Amherst, New York. Extensive damage was caused that will take months to repair, the group said.\par \par \uc2 Nobody in the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  group was hurt, though two firefighters incurred minor injuries.\par \par \uc2 Graffiti spray-painted on the side of the CompassCare building said \u8220\'20\'1CJane was here\u8221\'20\'1D. There was speculation that the phrase might be a reference to a pro-choice militant group that goes by the name Jane\u8217\'20\'19s Revenge.\par \par \uc2 Last month Jane\u8217\'20\'19s Revenge {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/10/abortion-arson-attack-wisconsin-pro-choice-janes-revenge"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 claimed responsibility}}}\uc2  for an arson attack at an anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  office in Wisconsin. The group sent a statement to a local paper in which it said it had attacked the headquarters of Wisconsin Family Action in Madison because of its anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  stance, warning that similar institutions in the US faced \u8220\'20\'1Cincreasingly extreme tactics\u8221\'20\'1D if they did not disband.\par \par \uc2 In a video posted on CompassCare\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Facebook\uc2  page, the chief executive, Jim Harden, used hyperbolic language to characterise the attack. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is the pro-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Kristallnacht,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, referring to the violence unleashed by the Nazis against the Jewish population in Germany in November 1938.\par \par \uc2 He added: \u8220\'20\'1CThey broke glass under the cover of darkness to keep us from doing the work of the Lord, from being the light of the world. And we are not going to stop.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 CompassCare claims to offer legitimate medical services to women considering \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Those \u8220\'20\'1Cservices\u8221\'20\'1D include reversal of an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  for women who have taken an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill, and providing information about the health risks of terminating a pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 The American Medical Association\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://journalofethics.ama-assn.org/article/why-crisis-pregnancy-centers-are-legal-unethical/2018-03#:~:text=Often%20using%20neutral%2Dsounding%20language,%2C%20diapers%2C%20and%20parenting%20classes."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Journal of Ethics}}}\uc2  has described pregnancy centers like CompassCare as unethical. They are \u8220\'20\'1Corganisations that seek to intercept women with unintended pregnancies who might be considering \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Their mission is to prevent abortions by persuading women that adoption or parenting is a better option.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The supervisor of Amherst, Brian Kulpa, told the local ABC station WKBW7 that he was \u8220\'20\'1Cdisgusted that lives were put at risk. A violent response is never the answer. There is no place in Amherst for such attacks.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The governor of New York state, \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2 , put out a statement saying that she \u8220\'20\'1Ccondemns violence of any kind\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220608ei68002be\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
