\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Proud Boys leader charged with seditious conspiracy related to Capitol attack \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein (now) and Joanna Walters (earlier) \par \uc2 6,258 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 June 2022\par 20:50 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Full report: \uc2 Enrique Tarrio\uc2  charged with seditious conspiracySenate back in session after series of weekend shootingsSupreme court issues opinions as it enters term\u8217\'20\'19s final monthDeSantis beats Trump in conservative group straw poll for 2024Sign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s it from us today. Here\u8217\'20\'19s how another eventful day in Washington unfolded:\par \par \uc2 * The former leader of the Proud Boys, far-right nationalist group \uc2 Enrique Tarrio\uc2 , and four of his closest associates have been charged with seditious conspiracy related to the January 6 attack, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.justice.gov/usao-dc/press-release/file/1510791/download"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to a Justice Department filing released Monday}}}\uc2 . The rare charge against Tarrio as well as Ethan Nordean, Joseph Biggs, Zachary Rehl, Charles Donohoe and Dominic Pezzola{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/mar/08/enrique-tarrio-proud-boys-leader-arrested-us-capitol-attack-conspiracy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 builds on conspiracy charges filed by the government earlier this year}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * The January 6 committee is preparing to hold its first primetime hearing on Thursday. According to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2022/06/06/jan-6-committee-adviser-james-goldston"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Axios}}}\uc2 , the committee has enlisted James Goldston, a former ABC News president who ran the shows \u8220\'20\'1CNightline\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1CGood Morning America,\u8221\'20\'1D to advise the committee on how to televise the hearing. The panel is expected to share never-before-seen photos taken inside the White House as the Capitol attack unfolded.\par \par \uc2 * A Democratic member of the January 6 committee said the panel\u8217\'20\'19s hearings would demonstrate the extensive planning conducted by those who carried out the attack. \u8220\'20\'1CThe committee has found evidence of concerted planning and premeditated activity,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Jamie Raskin\uc2  said in a virtual discussion with the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  today. \u8220\'20\'1CThe idea that all of this was just a rowdy demonstration that spontaneously got a little out of control is absurd. You don\u8217\'20\'19t almost knock over the \uc2 US government\uc2  by accident.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * The Senate is trying to find a bipartisan compromise on gun-control legislation in the wake of the Uvalde massacre. Democratic senators are trying to find 10 Republicans to join them in supporting tougher gun laws, but that will be a heavy lift in the evenly divided chamber. \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2 , the centrist Democrat who could play a key role in negotiations, said he would support raising the minimum age required to purchase semi-automatic weapons from 18 to 21. Manchin also signaled openness to an assault weapons ban, but that proposal is unlikely to win enough Republican support to be included in the final bill.\par \par \uc2 * The supreme court released more decisions this morning, but the country is still waiting to hear whether justices will move forward with their initial ruling to overturn Roe v Wade. The \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  case is one of dozens of decisions that the court still needs to release in the coming weeks. The court has announced that its next round of rulings will be released on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Thanks for following along with our coverage today. The blog will be back tomorrow morning, with more updates on the January 6 committee and the Senate negotiations over gun-control.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Back in Congress, a group of 10 \u8220\'20\'1Cfrontline\u8221\'20\'1D Democratic House lawmakers, who are considered the most vulnerable to getting ousted in the November midterms, have written a letter to the chamber\u8217\'20\'19s leaders asking for votes on bills that would fight inflation.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://punchbowl.news/frontlinerinflationletter/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 letter reported by Punchbowl News}}}\uc2  comes as the country faces an ongoing wave of price increases for essentials like gasoline, as well as a shortage of baby formula {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/06/joe-biden-entered-faces-daunting-crises"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 that has rattled the Biden administration.}}}\par \par \uc2 Addressed to House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  and majority leader \uc2 Steny Hoyer\uc2 , the letter doesn\u8217\'20\'19t name specific bills, and acknowledges that many proposals the chamber already passed haven\u8217\'20\'19t been brought up in the Senate. The lawmakers nonetheless call for votes:\par \par \uc2 With the time that remains in the 117th Congress after the important upcoming votes on gun violence prevention \u8211\'20\'13 and particularly in the few months that remain before the late summer district work period \u8211\'20\'13 we urge you to prioritize bills that would lower costs for working families, address rising inflation and resolve supply chain challenges. To be clear, we know that many such bills have already received affirmative votes in the House and now await Senate action. However, we believe that more must be done to ensure that this body remains laser focused on addressing the most urgent challenges that continue to impact our constituents.\par \par \uc2 Consumer prices have been rising over the past year at rates not seen since the 1980s, fueling public discontent with the Biden administration. The \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  is hiking interest rates to tame the price increases, but much of the inflation has been caused by factors beyond their control such as global supply chain snarls and the war in Ukraine. Some economists fear the combination of higher rates and global supply shocks will put the economy into a recession \u8212\'20\'14 perhaps next year, just as campaign season for the 2024 presidential election kicks off.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile in the UK, members of parliament have spent the day voting on whether to boot Prime Minister \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2  from office, and the verdict is in: Johnson survives his no-confidence vote, 211 to 148.\par \par \uc2 That means he stays as prime minister, leader of the Conservatives and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s counterpart in one of America\u8217\'20\'19s closest allies. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2022/jun/06/boris-johnson-confidence-vote-graham-brady-tory-mps-live"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Andrew Sparrow has been keeping a meticulous live blog of the historic day.}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Proud Boys leader, members charged with seditious conspiracy\par \par \uc2 Former leader of the Proud Boys far-right nationalist group \uc2 Enrique Tarrio\uc2  and four of his closest associates have been charged with seditious conspiracy related to the January 6 attack, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.justice.gov/usao-dc/press-release/file/1510791/download"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to a Justice Department filing released Monday}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The rare charge against Tarrio as well as Ethan Nordean, Joseph Biggs, Zachary Rehl, Charles Donohoe, and Dominic Pezzola {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/mar/08/enrique-tarrio-proud-boys-leader-arrested-us-capitol-attack-conspiracy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 builds on conspiracy charges filed by the government earlier this year}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In January, the Justice Department leveled seditious conspiracy charges against 11 members of another far-right group, the Oath Keepers militia, over their involvement in the assault on the Capitol as lawmakers were meeting to certify \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 2020 election win.\par \par \uc2 Tarrio, 38, is also facing counts of conspiracy to obstruct an official proceeding and obstruction of an official proceeding, and two counts each of assaulting, resisting, or impeding certain officers and destruction of government property.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 Top Senate Republican eyes gun deal 'this week'\par \par \uc2 Senate Minority Leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  has signaled a deal between Democrat and Republican lawmakers on a new gun control bill could be reached this week.\par \par \uc2 enltrMCCONNELL on whether senate negotiators will strike a gun deal by the end of the week: \u8220\'20\'1Coh I hope so\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jake Sherman (@JakeSherman) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JakeSherman/status/1533888848136110085?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 6, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrMore MCCONNELL on guns. \u8220\'20\'1CWe're trying to get a bipartisan outcome here that makes a difference. And hopefully, sometime this week, we'll come together.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jake Sherman (@JakeSherman) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JakeSherman/status/1533894633268334594?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 6, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Republican Senator \uc2 John Cornyn\uc2  and Democratic Senator \uc2 Chris Murphy\uc2  have been leading negotiations in the evenly divided chamber to introduce some kind of legislation that could restrict gun purchases following a recent wave of mass shootings in Buffalo, New York, Uvalde, Texas and elsewhere.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 The January 6 committee will hold its second hearing on Monday, June 13, at 10am ET, the House panel has just announced.\par \par \uc2 The first hearing is happening on Thursday at 8pm ET, and it is expected to attract worldwide news coverage, but the second hearing is not scheduled for the evening.\par \par \uc2 The select committee has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/06/gun-control-congress-biden-shootings-insurrection-latest-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-629e01488f08c28a9854d92f#block-629e01488f08c28a9854d92f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly}}}\uc2  enlisted the help of James Goldston, a former ABC News president, to assist in the planning of the primetime event.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  earlier today, a Democratic member of the committee, \uc2 Jamie Raskin\uc2 , said investigators had \u8220\'20\'1Cfound evidence of concerted planning and premeditated activity\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe idea that all of this was just a rowdy demonstration that spontaneously got a little out of control is absurd,\u8221\'20\'1D Raskin said. \u8220\'20\'1CYou don\u8217\'20\'19t almost knock over the \uc2 US government\uc2  by accident.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 The supreme court will now issue opinions on Wednesday, June 8, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 its website}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The justice have 30 cases to release decisions on, with the workload possible extending into next month. Several of these may be extremely consequential, including an environmental case out of West Virginia, a gun rights case stemming from New York, an immigration case via Texas involving the US-Mexico border and the pivotal Mississippi \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  case that also includes the state authorities asking \uc2 Scotus\uc2  to overturn Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Nearly half of Republican voters think the US just has to live with mass shootings, according to a poll released in the aftermath of the Texas elementary school murders last month and as politicians in Washington {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jun/06/gun-control-congress-biden-shootings-insurrection-latest-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 negotiate for gun reform}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1mLulXV9rXGLevVOI_XnHJBYsWd_CVqLq/view"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CBS and YouGov poll}}}\uc2  returned familiar results, including 62% support for a nationwide ban on semi-automatic rifles, the kind of gun used in Uvalde, Texas.\par \par \uc2 Nineteen young children and two adults were killed at Robb elementary school on 24 May by an 18-year-old who bought his weapon legally.\par \par \uc2 But clear national support for a ban on such rifles or changes to purchasing ages and background checks is not mirrored in Congress. Most {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2 , supported financially by the powerful gun lobby, remain implacably opposed to most gun reform.\par \par \uc2 Read the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s full report:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/06/us-mass-shootings-republicans-poll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nearly half of Republicans think US has to live with mass shootings, poll finds}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 An end to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights would create yet another crisis for Biden, whose presidency has been increasingly defined by a list problems, annoyances and calamities that seems to only grow longer.\par \par \uc2 From high inflation to the chaotic withdrawal from Afghanistan to nationwide mass shootings, my colleague {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/lauren-gambino"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lauren Gambino}}}\uc2  has an excellent piece on how Biden has become a crisis president \u8212\'20\'14 whether he wants to or not:\par \par \uc2 In his third run for president, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s pitch to Americans was simple: after half a century in elected office, including eight years as vice-president, he understood the demands of what is arguably the hardest job in the world. It was a point Biden stressed on the campaign trail, in his own folksy way: \u8220\'20\'1CEverything landed on the president\u8217\'20\'19s desk but locusts.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Nearly a year and a half into his presidency, Biden now appraises his own fortunes differently. \u8220\'20\'1CI used to say in Barack\u8217\'20\'19s administration: \u8216\'20\'18Everything landed on his desk but locusts,\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/speeches-remarks/2022/04/21/remarks-by-president-biden-at-a-democratic-national-committee-fundraiser-2/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told}}}\uc2  Democratic donors in Oregon. \u8220\'20\'1CWell, they landed on my desk.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Successive mass shootings, including a racist attack at a grocery store in Buffalo, New York, and a massacre at an elementary school in Uvalde, Texas, that left 19 elementary school students and their teachers dead, present just the latest test for a president desperate to act but constrained, once again, by the limits of his own power.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/06/joe-biden-entered-faces-daunting-crises"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden entered office facing daunting crises \u8211\'20\'13 only to be hit with more crises }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 White House condemns Louisiana \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bill\par \par \uc2 The White House has released a statement condemning legislation introduced in Louisiana that would make \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  a crime of murder.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLouisiana\u8217\'20\'19s extreme bill will criminalize \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  with no exceptions for rape or incest and punish reproductive healthcare professionals with up to ten years in prison,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2 , the White House press secretary, in a statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe president is committed to protecting the constitutional rights of Americans afforded by Roe for nearly 50 years, and ensuring that women can make their own choices about their lives, bodies, and families. An overwhelming majority of the American people agree and reject these kinds of radical measures.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/05/louisiana-abortion-bill-murder-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Louisiana Republicans advance bill to make \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  a crime of murder}}}\par \par \uc2 Supporters of the bill admit it\u8217\'20\'19s unconstitutional, but only as long as the Roe v Wade decision that enshrines \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the United States remains law. That decision\u8217\'20\'19s days appear to be numbered, according to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/05/02/supreme-court-abortion-draft-opinion-00029473"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 draft of a supreme court opinion}}}\uc2  that was leaked last month.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 Located just across the street from the Capitol, the supreme court has found itself sucked into the inquiry over January 6 as investigators eye the actions of Ginni Thomas, wife of conservative justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In March, my colleague {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/edpilkington"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ed Pilkington}}}\uc2  reported on the calls for conflict-of-interest rules that erupted after revelations that Ginni Thomas pressed then-president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s chief of staff to overturn the results of the 2020 presidential election:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2022/mar/25/ginni-thomas-texts-clarence-ethics-supreme-court-conflict-of-interest"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ginni Thomas texts spark ethical storm about husband\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court role}}}\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/mar/26/ginni-thomas-house-january-6-committee"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hugo Lowell}}}\uc2  reported later that month that committee members have weighed asking Thomas to cooperate either voluntarily or with a subpoena, but no decision has yet been made.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/mar/26/ginni-thomas-house-january-6-committee"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 House January 6 panel members weigh seeking cooperation from Ginni Thomas}}}\par \par \uc2 More revelations about Thomas\u8217\'20\'19s actions around the time of the insurrection have trickled out since then, including that she pressed Republicans in Arizona to overturn Biden\u8217\'20\'19s victory there, as first reported in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/20/ginni-thomas-2020-election-arizona-emails"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Washington Post last month}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 January 6 committee member \uc2 Jamie Raskin\uc2  hinted to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/washington-post-live/2022/06/06/117th-congress-rep-jamie-raskin-d-md/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Washington Post}}}\uc2  that lawmakers have discovered \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  more than just incited the attack on the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 Raskin did not elaborate on what the House committee found, but the actions of the former president have been at the center of the inquiry from the start.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe select committee has found evidence about a lot more than incitement here, and we\u8217\'20\'19re gonna be laying out the evidence about all of the actors who were pivotal to what took place on Jan 6,\u8221\'20\'1D Raskin said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and the White House were at the center of these events. That\u8217\'20\'19s the only way really of making sense of them all,\u8221\'20\'1D the Democratic House representative added.\par \par \uc2 Trump was impeached by the Democrat-controlled House immediately following the insurrection, but the Republican-led Senate decided not to convict and remove him from office, allowing Trump to remain in the White House for the final weeks of his term.\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepRaskin?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @RepRaskin}}}\uc2  on Jan. 6: \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and the White House were at the center of these events. That\u8217\'20\'19s the only way really of making sense of them all.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/PostLive?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #PostLive}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/gIJJxqPWsx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/gIJJxqPWsx}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Washington Post Live (@PostLive) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PostLive/status/1533828063485632520?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 6, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 January 6 committee 'has found evidence of concerted planning and premeditated activity,' Raskin says\par \par \uc2 A Democratic member of the January 6 committee, \uc2 Jamie Raskin\uc2 , said the panel\u8217\'20\'19s hearings would demonstrate the extensive planning conducted by those who carried out the attack on the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe committee has found evidence of concerted planning and premeditated activity,\u8221\'20\'1D Raskin said in a virtual discussion with the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  today.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe idea that all of this was just a rowdy demonstration that spontaneously got a little out of control is absurd. You don\u8217\'20\'19t almost knock over the \uc2 US government\uc2  by accident.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrRep. \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  talks about the GOP's "cult of personality" around Trump, and what the hearings will reveal about the threat to democracy. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/kFhs30uzzC"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/kFhs30uzzC}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/TrqMfQ0Qjs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/TrqMfQ0Qjs}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CBS Sunday Morning ?? (@CBSSunday) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CBSSunday/status/1533826149565861888?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 6, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Raskin said the committee would use the hearings to outline all the evidence it has collected and provide recommendations on how to avoid future coups that could threaten the security of the \uc2 US government\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Raskin\u8217\'20\'19s comments echo those of \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 , the Republican vice-chair of the committee, who said yesterday that she considers the January 6 attack to be a conspiracy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is extremely broad,\u8221\'20\'1D Cheney told CBS News. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s extremely well-organized. It\u8217\'20\'19s really chilling.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Warning of the danger of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s hold on the Republican party, Cheney added, \u8220\'20\'1CI mean, it is fundamentally antithetical, it is contrary to everything conservatives believe, to embrace a personality cult. And yet, that is what so many in my party are doing today.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Former news executive advises January 6 committee on hearings\par \par \uc2 The January 6 committee has enlisted James Goldston, a former ABC News president who ran the shows \u8220\'20\'1CNightline\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1CGood Morning America,\u8221\'20\'1D to advise the committee on how to televise its hearings beginning Thursday, according to Axios.\par \par \uc2 Axios {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2022/06/06/jan-6-committee-adviser-james-goldston"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m told Goldston is busily producing Thursday\u8217\'20\'19s 8 p.m. ET hearing as if it were a blockbuster investigative special.\par \par \uc2 He plans to make it raw enough so that skeptical journalists will find the material fresh, and chew over the disclosures in future coverage.\par \par \uc2 And he wants it to draw the eyeballs of Americans who haven\u8217\'20\'19t followed the ins and outs of the Capitol riot probe.\par \par \uc2 Goldston will apparently have a lot of material to work with. The committee reportedly plans to show never-before-seen photos from inside the White House on January 6, and new security-camera footage from the Capitol, taken as the insurrection occurred, will also be shared.\par \par \uc2 The committee has already conducted more than 1,000 depositions and interviews as part of its investigation, and clips from those conversations are expected to be played during the hearing.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Republicans are busy planning a counter-messaging program to challenge the committee\u8217\'20\'19s findings. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2022/06/03/trump-january-6-hearings-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 According to Axios}}}\uc2 , House Republican leaders and outside conservative groups will paint the panel as hyperpartisan to try to discredit their conclusions.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2 , the centrist Democrat who could play a key role in reaching a Senate compromise on a gun-control bill, outlined what he would like to see in the legislation.\par \par \uc2 The West Virginia senator told CNN that he would support raising the minimum age required to purchase semi-automatic weapons from 18 to 21. The gunman who carried out the Uvalde shooting was 18.\par \par \uc2 Manchin also indicated he would support some version of a red-flag provision, as long as the policy allowed for due process for those blocked from purchasing guns.\par \par \uc2 enltrManchin told me that a final deal should include two things: Raising the age to 21 for purchasing semi-automatic weapons and standards for state red flag laws. He's also open to an assault weapons ban. On people needing AR-15s? "I never felt I needed something of that magnitude." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/GYUlx1Nhkp"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/GYUlx1Nhkp}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Manu Raju (@mkraju) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1533846629211570176?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 6, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe know we can do something that would have prevented this -- raising the age,\u8221\'20\'1D Manchin said of Uvalde. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd the second thing is that we know that the red-flag laws do work, as long as there\u8217\'20\'19s due process.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On the question of enacting a ban on assault weapons, Manchin said he would be open to the idea, but that proposal faces stiff opposition from Senate Republicans.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI never thought I had a need for that type of high-capacity automatic weapon,\u8221\'20\'1D Manchin said. \u8220\'20\'1CI like to shoot. I like to go out and hunt. I like to go out sports shooting. I do all that. But I\u8217\'20\'19ve never felt I needed something of that magnitude.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 While there were no major decisions made by the supreme court today, the justices did opt not to review legal sanctions against Republican Senate candidate Mark McCloskey and his wife Patricia, who pointed guns at protesters during racial justice protesters in Missouri two years ago.\par \par \uc2 In this June 28, 2020 file photo, Mark and Patricia McCloskey are shown outside their St. Louis mansion with guns after protesters walked onto their private street. Photograph: Laurie Skrivan/AP\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/06/06/politics/supreme-court-mark-patricia-mccloskey/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN reports}}}\uc2  that the McCloskeys, both attorneys, pled guilty to misdemeanors over the incident, which were later pardoned by Missouri\u8217\'20\'19s governor. However the state\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court later sanctioned them, calling their actions \u8220\'20\'1Cmoral turpitude.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The McCloskeys contested the penalties, citing the constitution\u8217\'20\'19s second amendment, but CNN reported the argument didn\u8217\'20\'19t have much chance of success.\par \par \uc2 Mark McCloskey is a candidate in the Republican senate primary in Missouri to succeed \uc2 Roy Blunt\uc2 , who is retiring, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ky3.com/2022/05/17/us-senate-poll-greitens-leads-republican-candidates-ahead-august-primary-mo-kunce-leads-democratic-ticket/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 but a SurveyUSA poll released last month}}}\uc2  did not find him among the race\u8217\'20\'19s frontrunners.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 As the Senate tries to find compromise on gun control, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is using the presidential bully pulpit to urge Congress to take action to prevent more tragedies like Uvalde.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAfter Columbine, after Sandy Hook, after Charleston, after Orlando, after Las Vegas, after Parkland, nothing has been done,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThis time, that can\u8217\'20\'19t be true. This time, we must actually do something.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden offered the same message to the nation last week, when he delivered a primetime address on the need to enact stricter gun laws.\par \par \uc2 He proposed expanding background checks and banning assault weapons. If Congress cannot approve an assault weapons ban, which seems unlikely given Republicans \u8217\'20\'19 opposition to the idea, then the minimum age required to purchase those guns should be raised from 18 to 21, Biden said.\par \par \uc2 enltrAfter Columbine,\par \par \uc2 after Sandy Hook,\par \par \uc2 after Charleston,\par \par \uc2 after Orlando,\par \par \uc2 after Las Vegas,\par \par \uc2 after Parkland,\par \par \uc2 nothing has been done.\par \par \uc2 This time, that can\u8217\'20\'19t be true. This time, we must actually do something.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 President Biden (@POTUS) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS/status/1533837875716009984?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 6, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The House has already passed several gun-control bills, and Biden called on the Senate to act as well in the wake of the Uvalde massacre.\par \par \uc2 However, that will be difficult when the upper chamber is evenly divided between Democrats and Republicans, and the filibuster rules requires 60 votes to advance most legislation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI support the bipartisan efforts that include a small group of Democrats and Republican senators trying to find a way,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said last Thursday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut my God, the fact that the majority of the Senate Republicans don\u8217\'20\'19t want any of these proposals even to be debated or come up for a vote, I find unconscionable. We can\u8217\'20\'19t fail the American people again.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 This week will provide some key clues as to whether any gun-control bill can pass the Senate.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal has published a deep dive into the relationship between \uc2 Chris Murphy\uc2  and \uc2 John Cornyn\uc2 , the two senators tasked with finding a compromise on gun control in Congress, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/past-mass-shootings-prompted-sens-john-cornyn-chris-murphy-to-lead-gun-talks-11654518618?st=5q8ihmrzyhp5sqc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 which focuses on their experiences with mass shootings in their states.}}}\par \par \uc2 The experience of Murphy, a Democrat, stems from the 2012 Sandy Hook shooting which, like last month\u8217\'20\'19s massacre in Uvalde, Texas, left dead scores of children in class. Republican Cornyn\u8217\'20\'19s experience came in 2017 during a shooting at a Sutherland Springs, Texas church that killed 26 people, and again with the killings in Uvalde.\par \par \uc2 As the Journal reports:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBoth of us have gone through things and seen things that are pretty, pretty horrific,\u8221\'20\'1D said Mr. Murphy in an interview, pointing to the shootings in their states. \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think there\u8217\'20\'19s any way that that doesn\u8217\'20\'19t propel you in some way, shape or form to go out, do something, to make sure that all of this stops.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The two men, coming from parties with sharply different positions on the gun debate, are working to overcome decades of distrust and inaction on guns in a deeply polarized Congress, aiming to pull together an agreement as soon as this week. Many Democrats, worn down after repeated failures to advance new laws, have said they are willing to settle for even a small bipartisan deal. Some Republicans also are open to talks, emphasizing school security and mental illness but wary of any steps that could be cast as hurting gun rights.\par \par \uc2 Murphy and Cornyn worked together on legislation enacted in 2017 that improved background checks, though a compromise on tougher gun control measures has eluded Congress for years despite successive mass shootings.\par \par \uc2 A reminder of how perilous the issue can be came on Friday, when Republican New York congressman \uc2 Chris Jacobs\uc2  called off his reelection bid after he drew a fierce backlash for voicing support for gun control legislation.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/04/chris-jacobs-withdraws-reelection-gun-control"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Chris Jacobs withdraws reelection bid amid GOP fire on his gun control stance}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 The secretary of transportation, \uc2 Pete Buttigieg\uc2 , has tested positive for Covid, making him the latest senior official in the Biden administration to contract the virus.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI have tested positive for COVID-19 and am experiencing mild symptoms,\u8221\'20\'1D Buttigieg said on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CI plan to work remotely while isolating according to CDC guidelines, and look forward to when I can safely return to the office and the road.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrI have tested positive for COVID-19 and am experiencing mild symptoms. I plan to work remotely while isolating according to CDC guidelines, and look forward to when I can safely return to the office and the road.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Secretary \uc2 Pete Buttigieg\uc2  (@SecretaryPete) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SecretaryPete/status/1533832183223308293?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 6, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Several of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s cabinet members have tested positive for Covid in recent weeks, as the US confronts {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/01/us-covid-surge-cases-rate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 another surge in cases}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The secretary of the interior, \uc2 Deb Haaland\uc2 , tested positive last week, and Vice-President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  contracted the virus last month, as did secretary of state \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Buttigieg, who ran for president in 2020 before endorsing Biden and later joining his cabinet, has been traveling across the country to tout the benefits of the bipartisan infrastructure law.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 Among the cases the supreme court is expected to release its decision on this month is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2022/may/28/us-supreme-court-gun-rights-second-amendment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York State Rifle & Pistol Association v Bruen, which challenges a New York law limiting concealed handgun carrying in public.}}}\par \par \uc2 Had the justice made their verdict public today, it would have come after a violent weekend across the country, in which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/06/06/politics/senate-gun-control-negotiations/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN counted 10 mass shootings since Friday}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 These include:\par \par \uc2 * Three people killed and 11 wounded in Philadelphia Saturday night when multiple individuals opened fire on South Street, a busy entertainment area.\par \par \uc2 * Two people killed and 14 injured in Chattanooga, Tennessee, while another was killed after being hit by a car.\par \par \uc2 * Two people killed and two wounded by a shooting at a bar in Mesa, Arizona, while in Phoenix, a 14-year-old girl was killed in a shooting downtown.\par \par \uc2 * In Summerton, South Carolina, one person was killed and eight wounded during a shooting that police said targeted a high school graduation party.\par \par \uc2 The New York case could be the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s first major ruling on gun rights in more than a decade. As my colleague Oliver Laughland reported last month, the expectation is for the court\u8217\'20\'19s conservative majority to strike down a New York law limiting who can get a license to carry a concealed weapon, though how much effect it will have on gun rights nationwide will depend on how the decision is phrased:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2022/may/28/us-supreme-court-gun-rights-second-amendment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 After latest mass shooting, is the supreme court poised to expand gun rights?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 Legal claims shed light on founder of faith group tied to Barrett\par \par \uc2 The founder of the People of Praise, a secretive charismatic Christian group that counts supreme court justice {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/amy-coney-barrett"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Amy Coney Barrett}}}\uc2  as a member, was described in a sworn affidavit filed in the 1990s as exerting almost total control over one of the group\u8217\'20\'19s female members, including making all decisions about her finances and dating relationships.\par \par \uc2 The court documents also described alleged instances of a sexualized atmosphere in the home of the founder, Kevin Ranaghan, and his wife, Dorothy Ranaghan.\par \par \uc2 The description of the Ranaghans and accusations involving their intimate behavior were contained in a 1993 proceeding in which a woman, Cynthia Carnick, said that she did not want her five minor children to have visitations with their father, John Roger Carnick, who was then a member of the People of Praise, in the Ranaghan household or in their presence, because she believed it was not in her children\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cbest interest\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Cynthia Carnick also described inappropriate incidents involving the couple and the Ranaghan children. The matter was eventually settled between the parties.\par \par \uc2 Read the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s full report:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/06/people-of-praise-accused-child-abuse-amy-coney-barrett"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Legal claims shed light on founder of faith group tied to Amy Coney Barrett}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 No more opinions are due today from the \uc2 US Supreme Court\uc2 , with all the biggest decisions still awaited.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll be keeping an eye on the court\u8217\'20\'19s calendar and on the indispensable Scotusblog for upcoming dates and the rulings issued on those dates.\par \par \uc2 For anyone curious to know a bit more about how this works, the Scotusblog FAQ page is handy, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.scotusblog.com/faqs-announcements-of-orders-and-opinions/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 . The court doesn\u8217\'20\'19t give lots of notice about which will be opinion days in June and, likely, edging into July with such a big caseload.\par \par \uc2 And the public isn\u8217\'20\'19t told what opinions are coming down until they land. However, of course there was the early May {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/03/biden-democrats-reaction-codifying-roe-v-wade-reform-scotus"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bombshell leak}}}\uc2  of the draft opinion in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/nov/30/explainer-mississippi-abortion-rights-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dobbs v Jackson}}}\uc2  Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization case out of Mississippi, which explicitly includes a request from the state authorities to the court to overturn the pivotal 1973 Roe v Wade decision that afforded the constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the US.\par \par \uc2 The final opinion is awaited...\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/03/biden-democrats-reaction-codifying-roe-v-wade-reform-scotus"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US shaken to its core by supreme court draft that would overturn Roe v Wade}}}\par \par \uc2 This blog is now handing over to the \uc2 Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s new US politics blogger {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/chris-stein"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Chris Stein}}}\uc2  , based in Washington, and our colleague there {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/joan-greve"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joanie Greve}}}\uc2 , who was at the helm of the blog but in recent months took on her new role as one of our senior politics reporters.\par \par \uc2 They\u8217\'20\'19ll take you through the rest of today\u8217\'20\'19s politics news. For all the breaking news on UK politics today involving a no-confidence vote in prime minister \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2 , please follow our London team here as they bring you the events as they happen there, in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2022/jun/06/boris-johnson-confidence-vote-graham-brady-tory-mps-live"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 UK politics live blog}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s Supreme Court justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  again, this time putting his name to a decision in the case of \uc2 Southwest Airlines\uc2  v Saxon.\par \par \uc2 In an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SCOTUSblog/status/1533816587769327616"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 eight to zero opinion}}}\uc2  ( Amy Coney Barrett was recused from this case), Thomas issued the decision that the court essentially said an airline worker is not required to go to arbitration over her pay dispute with Southwest and can fight her case in the courts.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe Supreme Court adopts a broad interpretation of an important exception in the Federal Arbitration Act. The upshot of the 8-0 ruling is that an airport worker (and others similarly situated) can bring a claim for overtime pay in court, rather than being forced into arbitration.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 SCOTUSblog (@SCOTUSblog) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SCOTUSblog/status/1533816390209130496?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 6, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The Bloomberg Law site notes that the case could have a wide impact on worker arbitration rights. It {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.bloomberglaw.com/daily-labor-report/southwests-high-court-case-can-widely-impact-worker-arbitration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 explained}}}\uc2  that Latrice Saxon :\par \par \uc2 Sued the airline in 2019, alleging it failed to pay her and hundreds of current and former ramp supervisors time-and-a-half earned for their overtime work. The Dallas-based carrier countered that its employee was contractually bound to bring the claim in arbitration, rather than in court. While a federal district judge agreed with the airline, the U.S. Court of Appeals for the Seventh Circuit did not. The supreme court took up the case.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  has issued three opinions today, moments ago, although they are not the cases the nation is on the edge of its proverbial seat about \u8211\'20\'13 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and gun rights.\par \par \uc2 The court just ruled that the Florida authorities can recoup $300,000 in medical expenses out of a settlement paid {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://lawandcrime.com/supreme-court/scotus-to-decide-whether-florida-can-take-300000-in-settlement-funds-meant-for-child-in-vegetative-state-and-offset-medicaid-expenses/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in the case}}}\uc2  of Gianinna Gallardo, who suffered appalling injuries at 13, in 2008, when she was hit by a truck after getting off a school bus. A 7-2 majority, with the opinion written by \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  and joined by liberal-leaning Elena Kagan, opined for the state over the Gallardo family.\par \par \uc2 A few minutes prior, the court ruled in a case, Siegel v Fitzgerald, about the constitutionality of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.bloomberglaw.com/bankruptcy-law/justices-question-fixes-for-u-s-trustee-bankruptcy-fee-hike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 increased US Trustee\u8217\'20\'19s fees}}}\uc2  charged to companies in chapter 11 bankruptcy protection.\par \par \uc2 Details on the third ruling in a tick.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe Supreme Court strikes down Congress' decision to increase bankruptcy fees in most states while leaving a different system in place in two states. \uc2 SCOTUS\uc2  unanimously holds that the two different fee systems violates the Constitution's requirement of "uniform" bankruptcy laws.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 SCOTUSblog (@SCOTUSblog) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SCOTUSblog/status/1533812067425210368?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 6, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  is about to issue ruling(s) on cases decided in the current term.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll keep you up to date on what happens, when the opinion(s) are handed down at 10am ET.\par \par \uc2 As Scotusblog notes, there\u8217\'20\'19s a lot for the bench to get to:\par \par \uc2 enltrWe're live now: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/S5A4KeL5nQ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/S5A4KeL5nQ}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ddml8iKgtC"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/ddml8iKgtC}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 SCOTUSblog (@SCOTUSblog) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SCOTUSblog/status/1533803731439034369?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 6, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The four big cases we at the \uc2 Guardian\uc2  are watching most closely are an environmental case out of West Virginia, a gun rights case stemming from New York, an immigration case via Texas involving the US-Mexico border and the pivotal Mississippi \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  case that also includes the state authorities asking \uc2 Scotus\uc2  to overturn Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US Senate\uc2  is back in session today after its latest recess and there will be close attention on a bipartisan group of senators that is exuding increased confidence that a package of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/05/democrat-chris-murphy-gun-control"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gun control measures}}}\uc2  can advance and make it into law.\par \par \uc2 Connecticut Democrat \uc2 Chris Murphy\uc2  is fond of the word significant. Just days ago, less than a week after the mass shooting at Robb elementary {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/texas-school-shooting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 school in Uvalde}}}\uc2 , Texas that killed 19 young children and two teachers, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/29/texas-school-shooting-biden-visits-uvalde"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he talked of}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Can opportunity right now to pass something significant\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Murphy yesterday {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/05/democrat-chris-murphy-gun-control"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 added}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CThe possibility of success is better than ever before. But I think the consequences of failure for our entire democracy are more significant than ever.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Chris Murphy\uc2  in Washington DC. Photograph: J Scott Applewhite/AP\par \par \uc2 Murphy believes {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.wfsu.org/state-news/2019-02-14/how-have-floridas-gun-laws-changed-since-parkland"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 measures passed in Florida}}}\uc2  following the 2018 high school shooting in Parkland could attract Republican support and provide a workable template for action in Congress.\par \par \uc2 Chris Murphy\uc2  of Connecticut, speaking on CNN\u8217\'20\'19s State of the Union, said he was optimistic that recent mass shootings in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/buffalo-shooting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Buffalo, New York}}}\uc2 , and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/texas-school-shooting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Uvalde, Texas}}}\uc2 , could finally prompt enough bipartisan support for legislation that has previously proven elusive.\par \par \uc2 Florida, a Republican-controlled state, acted swiftly after the murders of 17 students and staff at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/florida-school-shooting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Marjory Stoneman Douglas high school}}}\uc2  in February 2018, passing red flag laws and raising the age requirement for buying, but not owning, firearms from 18 to 21, among other steps. The Parkland gunman was 19.\par \par \uc2 In his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/03/biden-speech-gun-control-assault-weapons-ban-reactions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 address to the nation last week}}}\uc2 , \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  called for a federal ban on semi-automatic weapons, and raising the age requirement if that couldn\u8217\'20\'19t be done.\par \par \uc2 Murphy acknowledged the Florida actions and said \u8220\'20\'1Cthere is interest in taking a look at that age range, 18 to 21\u8221\'20\'1D during bipartisan discussions about possible legislation, led on the Republican side by Texas senator \uc2 John Cornyn\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Read {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/05/democrat-chris-murphy-gun-control"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Washington ramps up bipartisan gun safety talks amid crisis of violence\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers, it\u8217\'20\'19s going to be an exceptionally busy, high-stakes week in Washington with Americans\u8217\'20\'19 constitutional rights and democracy itself under the spotlight.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what\u8217\'20\'19s on the agenda.\par \par \uc2 * The \uc2 US Senate\uc2  is back in session on the Hill today after its latest recess and a bipartisan group of senators is exuding confidence that a package of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/05/democrat-chris-murphy-gun-control"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gun control measures}}}\uc2  can make progress, while the leading lawmaker in talks warns of \u8220\'20\'1Csignificant\u8221\'20\'1D consequences of failure.\par \par \uc2 * Talks continue amid another series of deadly shootings at the weekend, following grotesquely on the heels of the school massacre in Uvalde, Texas and the racist killing of Black Americans in a supermarket in Buffalo.\par \par \uc2 * New measures under discussion do not include the demands of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  for a ban on assault weapons, following the recent carnage, but there is more progress being made right now on legislative talks than there has been for years.\par \par \uc2 * The \uc2 US Supreme Court\uc2  is due to issue opinions today and Thursday, June being the crunch month for decisions arising in cases from the current term and with more than 30 decision to be declared. The public (and press) are not party to which cases will be announced until the bench speaks up.\par \par \uc2 * Last but not least for this briefing note: the special House committee investigating events on and around the January 6, 2021 insurrection at the US Capitol by extremist supporters of then-president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is in final preparations for its first public hearing, this Thursday in prime time \u8211\'20\'13 and the right is already revving up its riposte.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220606ei66001rx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
