\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Theocratic\u8217\'20\'19 US  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  bans will violate religious liberty, faith leaders say\b0\par\par\uc2 Melody Schreiber \par \uc2 1,147 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 June 2022\par 12:42 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  side has monopolized arguments based on religion. But some say their faith supports the right to choose\par \par \uc2 Misha Sanders was starting over. She had just left an abusive relationship, and she was in her first semester of seminary, all while caring for her child, a teenager with a pressing health problem.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s when she found out she was pregnant. Sanders took misoprostol and mifepristone, the two drugs known collectively as the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill, to end the pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 The decision, she says, was deeply entwined with her religious beliefs, which include respecting full bodily autonomy and caring for other people \u8211\'20\'13 core beliefs of Unitarian Universalism, which she practices.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe only decision that I could make, as a loving mother, was to focus on mothering this child that I brought into the world and terminating this new pregnancy,\u8221\'20\'1D Sanders said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt was absolutely the right decision.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But Sanders now lives in Georgia, which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/local/atlanta/2022/05/04/georgia-abortion-law-explained"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 could pass}}}\uc2  restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after six weeks of pregnancy if Roe v Wade is overturned in the coming weeks.\par \par \uc2 Reproductive rights are under threat in the US as states implement harsher restrictions and the supreme court weighs a case that is widely expected to reverse the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But while religious arguments around the issue are commonly associated with the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions can violate the right to religious liberty, faith leaders and legal experts say. And some organizations are already gearing up for possible legal challenges to looming \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans.\par \par \uc2 Religious liberty for people of all faiths is protected under the US constitution, state constitutions and federal statutes.\par \par \uc2 In Judaism, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is usually seen as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://caae.phil.cmu.edu/Cavalier/Forum/abortion/background/judaism1.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 permissible}}}\uc2  and even required in cases where the patient\u8217\'20\'19s life is at risk. In Islam, scholars {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC3439741/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 contend}}}\uc2  that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is allowed for the first 120 days, after which it\u8217\'20\'19s seen as a civil \u8211\'20\'13 not a criminal \u8211\'20\'13 issue, and it\u8217\'20\'19s permitted at any time when the health of the mother is in danger. Other believers, including within Christianity, focus on the sacredness of the individual or the family to make such decisions, rather than prosecutors or lawmakers.\par \par \uc2 Personal beliefs can even contravene the dictums of established religions; for instance, \uc2 Catholics for Choice\uc2  believe they have a religious duty to protect reproductive health despite the Catholic church\u8217\'20\'19s stance against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Nearly half of Protestants and 56% of Catholics believe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal in some or all cases, according to a \uc2 Pew Research{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/religion/2022/05/06/americans-views-on-whether-and-in-what-circumstances-abortion-should-be-legal/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 survey}}}\uc2  published in May. More than half of Muslims, 82% of Buddhists and 83% of Jews believe the same, according to a different Pew {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/religion/religious-landscape-study/views-about-abortion/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 study}}}\uc2  from 2014.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou don\u8217\'20\'19t have to be a member of an organized religion,\u8221\'20\'1D said Katherine Franke, a professor of law at \uc2 Columbia University\uc2  and the faculty director of the Law, Rights, and Religion Project. \u8220\'20\'1CYour religious beliefs could be your own idiosyncratic beliefs. They have to just be religious to you.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 With \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans, some clergy object to what they see as a \u8220\'20\'1CChristian theocratic imposition on entire swaths of our country\u8221\'20\'1D, as Rabbi Danya Ruttenberg, scholar-in-residence at the National Council of Jewish Women, put it.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere are very serious religious liberty questions here,\u8221\'20\'1D Ruttenberg said. \u8220\'20\'1CIf you ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , when my religious tradition tells me that I am a) permitted and b) possibly required to access \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care, you are limiting my free exercise of religion.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The same questions arise in other faiths.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn the Muslim tradition, scholars from the medieval time had taken the position that until a fetus is ensouled, it is not a life,\u8221\'20\'1D said Abed Awad, a lawyer and commentator on Islamic law.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA Muslim woman living in Texas, or living in Alabama, who has a sincerely and genuinely held religious belief that in her tradition, she can terminate her pregnancy and it is not a violation of her religious requirements or theology up to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://rcrc.org/muslim/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 120 days}}}\uc2 , is going to be prevented from exercising her religious right to control her reproductive health,\u8221\'20\'1D Awad continued.\par \par \uc2 The first amendment has two components to protecting religious rights: first, the state can\u8217\'20\'19t substantially burden the free exercise of religion, and second, the establishment clause prohibits the government from endorsing some forms of religion and condemning others, or embracing faith-based perspectives on public policy.\par \par \uc2 For example, if states adopt laws on fetal personhood, which would recognize fertilized eggs as people, those laws could violate the establishment clause, because such a view hews closely to Catholicism but not to other religious beliefs on ensoulment and personhood.\par \par \uc2 Legal challenges on the basis of religious liberty could be \u8220\'20\'1Cthe next stage of reproductive rights\u8221\'20\'1D, Awad said, and the National Council of Jewish Women is exploring the possibility of such a challenge, Ruttenberg said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur tradition not only permits us to access \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  but also commands us to pursue justice,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe, as a religious minority with a long and complicated history, know all too well that the separation of church and state is one of the great gifts that our constitution offers. And it is critical that it be taken seriously.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 There is precedent for people with sincerely held religious beliefs fighting against criminal charges for actions that violate the law.\par \par \uc2 Scott Warren, a humanitarian aid worker for No More Deaths, successfully argued that his work helping migrants crossing the US-Mexico border was in line with his religious beliefs about helping others, and he was acquitted of federal charges in 2019.\par \par \uc2 Religious leaders or adherents may feel compelled by their beliefs to provide care, funds, transportation, housing or counseling around \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Franke said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s not a stretch to see the work that they do in this area as part of a ministry.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Sanders, who is now a minister, feels compelled by her beliefs to support access to reproductive healthcare, and she\u8217\'20\'19s now preparing to offer support however she can. \u8220\'20\'1CI have a spare room, and I\u8217\'20\'19m in the middle of sprucing it up right now with exactly that in mind.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Sanders is particularly concerned about the ways restrictions on reproductive rights and trans rights are growing and intersecting. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s so terrifying,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. She believes it is \u8220\'20\'1Can egregious sin\u8221\'20\'1D to cause harm to someone by denying them healthcare or human rights.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe, as Unitarian Universalists, believe fully that all human beings should have bodily autonomy, and anything that happens in or to my body should be my choice,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTo me, the law of the land and [religious] law are two separate and distinct things. It\u8217\'20\'19s great when they overlap. And when they don\u8217\'20\'19t, I\u8217\'20\'19m going to choose morality over the law every time. And for me, that includes helping people in whatever way I can, for whatever reason they are seeking \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220602ei62001ba\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
