\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Austin resolution aims to \u8216\'20\'18decriminalize\u8217\'20\'19  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  if Roe v Wade is overturned\b0\par\par\uc2 Jessica Glenza \par \uc2 650 \uc2 words\par \uc2 31 May 2022\par 14:57 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Group of city council members seeks to protect patients from criminal prosecution if supreme court ends \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights\par \par \uc2 A group of Austin, Texas, city council members is preparing a resolution to \u8220\'20\'1Cdecriminalize\u8221\'20\'1D \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  there in the event the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturns Roe v Wade, a landmark case decided nearly five decades ago that protects the federal right to terminate a pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 An unprecedented leaked supreme court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/03/biden-democrats-reaction-codifying-roe-v-wade-reform-scotus"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 draft decision}}}\uc2  showed a conservative majority of the nine justices are open to reversing Roe v Wade entirely. If that happened, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/05/abortion-deserts-clinics-access-closed-map"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 26 states}}}\uc2  would be certain or likely to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including in Texas. The state has a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://capitol.texas.gov/tlodocs/87R/billtext/pdf/HB01280F.pdf#navpanes=0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Ctrigger\u8221\'20\'1D ban}}}\uc2  that would almost immediately ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A final supreme court decision is expected in June.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe resolution does two things \u8211\'20\'13 one, [it] restricts city funds from being used to essentially investigate any kind of alleged \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  crimes,\u8221\'20\'1D said Jos\u233\'00\'E9 \u8220\'20\'1CChito\u8221\'20\'1D Vela, an Austin councilman. \u8220\'20\'1CThe other thing it does is to make the investigation of any \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related crime the lowest priority for our police department.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The resolution seeks to protect patients and medical professionals from criminal prosecution and would also advise Austin police not to assist other law enforcement, such as state police, in such investigations.\par \par \uc2 Texas has already proven to be a legal pioneer in restricting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The state banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/aug/30/abortion-law-federal-court-decision-texas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 six weeks gestation}}}\uc2 , before most women know they are pregnant, through a novel law that allows citizens to sue anyone, anywhere who \u8220\'20\'1Caids or abets\u8221\'20\'1D a woman in terminating a pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe need them focusing on historically classic criminal activity \u8211\'20\'13 not politically disfavored groups that factions in the government want to harass and punish,\u8221\'20\'1D said Vela. \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s the real core of what we\u8217\'20\'19re trying to do.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Mainstream anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups have long argued they oppose prosecution of women and cast women as victims of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers. Similarly in Texas, the trigger ban would make the performing of an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  a first-degree felony punishable by up to 99 years in prison, an article likely to have a impact on medical providers.\par \par \uc2 However, a vocal minority of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jul/06/anti-abortion-activists-operation-save-america"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  \u8220\'20\'1Cabolitionists\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 , a word appropriated from anti-slavery campaigners, have also recently pushed lawmakers to classify \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as murder.\par \par \uc2 In May, Louisiana lawmakers considered a bill to charge women who have abortions with homicide. \u8220\'20\'1CWe all know that it is actually very simple \u8211\'20\'13 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is murder,\u8221\'20\'1D one of the bill\u8217\'20\'19s supporters, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/louisiana-abortion-bill-murder-charge-vs-women/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 state representative Danny McCormick}}}\uc2  told colleagues, according to CBS News. The bill was pulled after it failed 65-26.\par \par \uc2 Although many anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups say they oppose prosecution of women, anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions and rhetoric have nevertheless resulted in more than 1,600 instances of women since 1973 being, \u8220\'20\'1Carrested, prosecuted, convicted, detained, or forced to undergo medical interventions that would not have occurred but for their status as pregnant persons,\u8221\'20\'1D National Advocates for Pregnant Women said in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/DocketPDF/19/19-1392/193710/20210924170501991_19-1392%20Brief.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recent brief to the supreme court}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 At least one recent, high-profile example from Texas, 26-year-old woman Lizelle Herrera was charged with murder via \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/09/texas-woman-26-charged-murder-self-induced-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 self-induced \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D, a criminal statute that does not appear to exist. Charges were dropped after public outcry. The prosecutor apologized.\par \par \uc2 Austin\u8217\'20\'19s Guarding the Right to \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Care for Everyone or \u8220\'20\'1CGrace\u8221\'20\'1D Act is still in draft form, and text is not expected to be immediately released. Vela said the council would probably consider the act after the supreme court releases its final decision in the highly anticipated \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  case.\par \par \uc2 It is a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/nov/30/explainer-mississippi-abortion-rights-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 case out of Mississippi}}}\uc2 , formally called Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization, in which the southern state has argued that the court should use the case to overturn Roe.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhatever your thoughts on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , criminal prosecution of women who have abortions is absolutely unacceptable and abuse by the criminal justice system,\u8221\'20\'1D said Vela.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220531ei5v0018j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
