\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 First Thing: Biden says pain \u8216\'20\'18palpable\u8217\'20\'19 in Uvalde\b0\par\par\uc2 Nicola Slawson \par \uc2 1,304 \uc2 words\par \uc2 31 May 2022\par 11:08 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 First memorial services for victims begin as president says he will continue to push for gun control. Plus 20 years of Avril Lavigne\par \par \uc2 Good morning.\par \par \uc2 The first memorial services for the 19 children and two teachers killed in a mass shooting at their elementary school in Uvalde began on Monday, a day after \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  visited the small south Texas city and was urged by residents to take action on gun safety laws.\par \par \uc2 Returning to Washington on Monday morning, the US president, wearing a black suit, talked about the \u8220\'20\'1Cpalpable\u8221\'20\'1D pain in Uvalde.\par \par \uc2 Asked by a reporter on the south lawn outside the White House whether he felt more motivated to act on guns now, Biden said: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve been pretty motivated all along. The folks who were victimized, their families \u8230\'20\'26 the pain is palpable. I think a lot of it is unnecessary. I\u8217\'20\'19m going to continue to push.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Republicans in the \uc2 US Senate\uc2  have blocked meaningful federal legislation on gun control for many years. Biden said he had not been negotiating with Republicans in the current round of talks on Capitol Hill but added: \u8220\'20\'1CI think things have gotten so bad that everybody is getting more rational about it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What\u8217\'20\'19s happening in Canada? The mass shooting in Texas has fed concern about gun violence worldwide and \uc2 Canada\u8217\'20\'19s government\uc2  is to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/31/handgun-freeze-in-canada-and-five-round-limit-on-magazines"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 legislate for a national freeze on handgun ownership}}}\uc2  that would prevent people buying and selling them anywhere in the country.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Why has Andy Murray spoken up about gun law in the US? Britain\u8217\'20\'19s two-time Wimbledon champion Andy Murray has said the mass shooting in Uvalde made him \u8220\'20\'1Cangry\u8221\'20\'1D and that a survivor\u8217\'20\'19s account of the incident was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/31/andy-murray-angry-texas-school-shooting-dunblane-massacre"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 similar to his own experience in the 1996 Dunblane massacre}}}\uc2  in Scotland.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What else do we know about what happened?\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/30/texas-uvalde-mass-shooting-timeline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a timeline}}}\uc2  of how the school shooting unfolded.\par \par \uc2 Progressives take aim at Democratic leadership over support for centrist candidates\par \par \uc2 Texas officials have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/30/democrats-progressives-leadership-texas-primary"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 still not declared a winner in the state\u8217\'20\'19s 28th congressional district}}}\uc2 , where the incumbent Democratic congressman \uc2 Henry Cuellar\uc2  currently leads the progressive lawyer Jessica Cisneros by 175 votes out of roughly 45,000 ballots cast.\par \par \uc2 But as progressives wait to see who will win the runoff, they cannot help but think of what might have been if House Democratic leaders had not come to Cuellar\u8217\'20\'19s assistance. Cuellar secured the endorsements of the top three House Democrats, and the congressman\u8217\'20\'19s campaign was also propped up by millions of dollars in Super Pac spending aimed at attacking Cisneros.\par \par \uc2 Progressives complain that House leaders\u8217\'20\'19 intervention in primaries like Cuellar\u8217\'20\'19s is making it harder for their candidates to succeed and they worry about the repercussions of the party embracing centrist candidates with controversial stances on issues like \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and gun control.\par \par \uc2 The potential victory of Cuellar last week, who has previously received {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nrapvf.org/emails/2018/texas/henry-cuellar-tx-28-general-election-email/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an \u8220\'20\'1CA\u8221\'20\'1D rating from the National Rifle Association}}}\uc2 , is all the more painful for progressives given the recent mass shooting at Robb elementary school in Uvalde, Texas.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What has \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2  said? \u8220\'20\'1COn the day of a mass shooting and weeks after news of Roe, Democratic party leadership rallied for a pro-\uc2 NRA\uc2 , anti-choice incumbent under investigation in a close primary. Robocalls, fundraisers, all of it,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CAccountability isn\u8217\'20\'19t partisan. This was an utter failure of leadership.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Austin resolution aims to \u8216\'20\'18decriminalize\u8217\'20\'19 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  if Roe v Wade is overturned\par \par \uc2 A group of Austin, Texas city council members is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/31/texas-austin-resolution-decriminalize-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 preparing a resolution to \u8220\'20\'1Cdecriminalize\u8221\'20\'1D \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  there in the event the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturns Roe v Wade, a landmark case decided nearly five decades ago that protects the federal right to terminate a pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 An unprecedented leaked supreme court draft decision showed a conservative majority of the nine justices are open to reversing Roe v Wade entirely. If that happened, 26 states would be certain or likely to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including Texas. The state has a \u8220\'20\'1Ctrigger\u8221\'20\'1D ban that would almost immediately ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A final supreme court decision is expected in June.\par \par \uc2 The resolution seeks to protect patients and medical professionals from criminal prosecution and would also advise Austin police not to assist other law enforcement, such as state police, in such investigations.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What will the resolution do? \u8220\'20\'1CThe resolution does two things \u8211\'20\'13 one, [it] restricts city funds from being used to essentially investigate any kind of alleged \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  crimes,\u8221\'20\'1D said Jos\u233\'00\'E9 \u8220\'20\'1CChito\u8221\'20\'1D Vela, an Austin councilman. \u8220\'20\'1CThe other thing it does is to make the investigation of any \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related crime the lowest priority for our police department.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In other news \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The new US ambassador to Ukraine {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/30/new-us-ambassador-ukraine-arrives-kyiv-symbolic-move-bridget-brink"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has arrived in Kyiv}}}\uc2 , a symbolic move after the US withdrew all diplomats from the country before the Russian invasion in February. Meanwhile, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has said the US will not supply Ukraine with rockets that can reach into Russia, in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/30/biden-will-not-supply-ukraine-with-long-range-rockets-that-can-hit-russia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an attempt to ease tensions}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 China has made the second\par \par \uc2 -largest incursion into Taiwan\u8217\'20\'19s air defence zone this year with Taipei reporting 30 jets entering the area, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/31/taiwan-scrambles-jets-after-china-makes-largest-incursion-into-air-defence-zone-since-january"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 including more than 20 fighters}}}\uc2 . Taiwan\u8217\'20\'19s defence ministry said yesterday it had scrambled its own aircraft and deployed air defence missile systems to monitor the activity.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Johnny Depp has appeared on stage alongside Jeff Beck in the UK for the second night in a row, amid his ongoing US legal battle. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2022/may/31/johnny-depp-plays-royal-albert-hall-with-jeff-beck"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Depp\u8217\'20\'19s appearance}}}\uc2  in the UK has surprised many as he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2022/may/27/johnny-depp-amber-heard-case-closing-arguments"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 awaits a verdict}}}\uc2  in his multimillion-dollar defamation lawsuit with his ex-wife Amber Heard.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Women in Japan could be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/31/japan-to-approve-abortion-pill-but-partners-consent-will-be-required"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 forced to seek their partner\u8217\'20\'19s consent}}}\uc2  before being prescribed the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill, which will reportedly be approved late this year. Under Japan\u8217\'20\'19s 1948 Maternal Protection Law, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/sep/27/japan-urged-to-abolish-third-party-consent-from-abortion-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 consent is already required}}}\uc2  for surgical abortions \u8211\'20\'13 with very few exceptions\par \par \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t miss this: Avril Lavigne on the 20th anniversary of her debut album that wowed the world\par \par \uc2 In an era when bubblegum pop and \u8220\'20\'1Csexy baby\u8221\'20\'1D personas reigned, 17-year-old Avril Lavigne emerged as its antithesis. Rarely seen without a baggy pair of jeans, heavy kohl eyeliner and a loose tie round her neck, she co-wrote her own songs, with lyrics about skateboarding and getting fired from a chicken shop. Her debut album, Let Go, on 4 June 2002 was not merely a new sound, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/music/2022/may/31/avril-lavigne-let-go-turns-20-interview"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 it was enlightenment}}}\uc2 . Now, as the album hits its 20th anniversary, its pop-punk anthems are finding new life thanks to TikTok.\par \par \uc2 Climate check:\par \par \uc2 did \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2  block climate action to benefit his financial interests?\par \par \uc2 Recent revelations could come back to haunt Democratic West Virginian senator \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2  as he considers a run for re-election. For years, Manchin has justified voting against curbs on the burning of fossil fuels on the grounds that they were bad for West Virginia, but following the news that he has been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/31/joe-manchin-hold-climate-policy-hostage-to-benefit-his-financial-interests"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 quietly making millions of dollars from his coal business}}}\uc2 , people are wondering: has the US climate policy just been held hostage to the senator\u8217\'20\'19s financial interests?\par \par \uc2 Last Thing:\par \par \uc2 man arrested after Mona Lisa smeared with cake\par \par \uc2 A 36-year-old man has been arrested and placed in psychiatric care after he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/30/mona-lisa-smeared-cake-suspected-climate-protester"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 smeared a glass screen encasing the Mona Lisa with cake}}}\uc2  in a purported protest against artists not focusing enough on \u8220\'20\'1Cthe planet\u8221\'20\'1D. Officials at the \uc2 Louvre Museum\uc2  in Paris, where the enigmatic portrait holds pride of place, declined to comment on the bizarre incident on Sunday, which was captured on several phones and circulated widely on social media.\par \par \uc2 Sign up\par \par \uc2 First Thing is delivered to thousands of inboxes every weekday. If you\u8217\'20\'19re not already signed up, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/info/2018/sep/17/guardian-us-morning-briefing-sign-up-to-stay-informed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 subscribe now}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Get in touch\par \par \uc2 If you have any questions or comments about any of our newsletters please email {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:newsletters@theguardian.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 newsletters@theguardian.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220531ei5v001gu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
