\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Pro-choice forces are working to keep  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  legal in Michigan with a ballot initiative\b0\par\par\uc2 Jessica Glenza in Detroit \par \uc2 1,184 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 May 2022\par 06:12 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The year before Roe, Michigan voters defeated a referendum to legalize \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Now activists are compelled to try again\par \par \uc2 Beth Morris is a 63-year-old homemaker whose pink Planned Parenthood shirt and clipboard would hardly betray her as a moderate Republican.\par \par \uc2 But here she is, in the middle of an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights rally on the \uc2 University of Michigan\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s campus in Ann Arbor, collecting signatures to support a constitutional amendment to keep \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legal in one of America\u8217\'20\'19s swingy \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/feb/01/michigan-republican-effort-rig-elections-voting-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 purple}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D states.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Republican party in Michigan has just been hijacked by the extreme right. Somehow, Christian values are things they want,\u8221\'20\'1D said Morris.\par \par \uc2 She feels moderates like herself are \u8220\'20\'1Cendangered\u8221\'20\'1D, and that many of her Republican friends have grown more extreme, and now even oppose birth control.\par \par \uc2 A mother of three adult children, Morris said she has donated to Planned Parenthood every year since college, when the organization helped her get a prescription for the pill. Now, she is part of a high-stakes drive to keep \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legal in Michigan by putting the question to voters, when the right has never appeared more threatened.\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/audio/2022/may/09/the-us-supreme-court-is-ready-to-overturn-the-right-to-an-abortion-what-happens-next"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 leaked supreme court draft opinion}}}\uc2  showed the court is on the precipice of reversing Roe v Wade, a landmark ruling that in 1973 invalidated dozens of state \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans, including in Michigan. Without the protections provided by Roe, a criminal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban dating back to 1846 would reanimate, making \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  punishable by manslaughter in a state that 2.2 million women of reproductive age call home.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf you don\u8217\'20\'19t want to do any of these options, that\u8217\'20\'19s obviously your prerogative. But I don\u8217\'20\'19t feel I should tell someone else what to do,\u8221\'20\'1D said Morris.\par \par \uc2 Michigan would be one of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/05/abortion-deserts-clinics-access-closed-map"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 26 states}}}\uc2  that would be certain or likely to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  if Roe were reversed. It\u8217\'20\'19s also the only one of those states where a coalition of groups has undertaken a ballot initiative to try to establish the right, and indeed expand it, in the state constitution.\par \par \uc2 The coalition, which includes the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.aclumich.org/en/press-releases/reproductive-freedom-all-ballot-initiative-harnesses-unprecedented-momentum-post"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 American Civil Liberties Union}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.miplannedparenthood.org/post/michigan-reproductive-freedom-ballot-committee-launches-statewide-signature-collection"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Planned Parenthood}}}\uc2  and the Black women-led {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.michiganvoices.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Michigan Voices}}}\uc2 , want voters to support a constitutional amendment to protect an expansion of reproductive rights, including but not limited to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s not just about reproductive freedom in the sense most people understand it, around \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access,\u8221\'20\'1D said Chris Melody Fields Figueredo, executive director of the Ballot Initiative Strategy Center, a non-profit that works on progressive state referendums.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s also about how you want to parent, and your pregnancy, including \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , prenatal care, childbirth. That, to me, is really remarkable\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Short of flipping the Republican-controlled Michigan house and senate, which would be a mighty feat as districts were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2021/dec/10/republicans-michigan-voting-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gerrymandered to favor Republicans}}}\uc2 , the ballot initiative is the most direct way to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access. Right now, the focus of 25,000 volunteers is clear: to collect 425,059 signatures, thereby getting the measure on the ballot.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA lot of people want to sign this one,\u8221\'20\'1D said Yvonne Wyborny, 65, a retired accountant wearing a pink polo shirt and sensible black sneakers and thrusting her clipboard at people in Detroit\u8217\'20\'19s Eastern Market. It\u8217\'20\'19s Flower Day, an event that draws tens of thousands of people from all over the state. \u8220\'20\'1CEspecially young women, they tend to grab it out of my hands.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Whether this ballot initiative will become a national model remains an open question. Only 26 states have some form of direct democracy, and just 18 have a provision that allows citizens to initiate a constitutional amendment, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ballotpedia.org/Initiated_constitutional_amendment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ballotpedia}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 However, ballot initiatives often become the forerunners of broad political and legal change, as they did before gay marriage, said Fields Figueredo. The fact that the petition is being signed by a broad, and surprising, assortment of Michigan residents is something the organizers hope may reflect a similarly broad public shift: even people uncomfortable with the procedure don\u8217\'20\'19t want to dictate medical decisions to fellow Americans.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy moral compass leads me to pro-life,\u8221\'20\'1D said Jacqueline Washington, 31, of Warren, who signed the petition in Eastern Market. \u8220\'20\'1CBut I have no reason to decide for other people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 More than {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/1576/abortion.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 two-thirds}}}\uc2  of Americans support access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  under most or all circumstances. Criminal bans are a generally unpopular policy to which Republicans have tied themselves by zealously advocating against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Other {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ballotpedia.org/Abortion_on_the_ballot"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 failed referendums}}}\uc2  to criminalize \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , from South Dakota to Colorado to Mississippi, reveal possible electoral peril for Republicans.\par \par \uc2 Remarkably, this is the second time activists in Michigan have attempted to make \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legal through a ballot initiative. The first came in 1972, the year before Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 At the time, Renee Chelian \u8211\'20\'13 now founder and CEO of Northland Family Planning Centers, three independent \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics outside Detroit \u8211\'20\'13 was an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider in a state where it was still illegal. On the weekends she would travel to Buffalo, New York, to perform legal abortions with a Detroit OBGYN. They met at the airport before dawn on Fridays, and returned home late on Sundays after every patient had been served.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPatients flew, they hitchhiked, they took a bus \u8211\'20\'13 they did whatever they had to do to get there,\u8221\'20\'1D said Chelian. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd they came from, what I can recall, a six-state area and Canada.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In 1972, it appeared as if a reprieve was imminent. A referendum question called {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ballotpedia.org/Michigan_Legislature_Office_Amendment,_Proposal_B_(May_1972)"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CProposition B\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  was on the fall ballot, asking voters whether to legalize \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  up to 20 weeks gestation. The question polled so well that a new \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic was founded in Detroit, anticipating new patients.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI was young, and I was working seven days a week, but I knew there was a referendum \u8211\'20\'13 I knew the polls looked like we were going to win,\u8221\'20\'1D said Chelian.\par \par \uc2 However, a vocal anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  campaign funded by the Catholic church ran wall-to-wall commercials, commented in newspaper articles and sent Catholic high school students out to canvass against the measure \u8211\'20\'13 and it failed, terribly. Voters rejected the measure 61% to 39%, and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained illegal in Michigan.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe lost, and I went right back to work in Buffalo,\u8221\'20\'1D said Chelian. \u8220\'20\'1CThere wasn\u8217\'20\'19t even time to be disappointed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Roe followed just a few months later in January 1973, and seemingly made the history of the first referendum moot. But Chelian, who had an illegal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  herself at 15, is now worried history may repeat. A supreme court decision is expected in June, meaning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be illegal in Michigan for several months before voters get their chance in November to vote on the ballot initiative.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t want to end my career back where I started it, providing abortions in another state,\u8221\'20\'1D Chelian said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy daughters are second-generation providers, and I want them and the women who have worked for me for a long time to be able to run these clinics and take good care of pregnant people long after I\u8217\'20\'19m gone.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220528ei5s000jv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
