\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Oklahoma governor signs strictest  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ban law in US\b0\par\par\uc2 Martin Pengelly and agencies \par \uc2 625 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 May 2022\par 12:34 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Kevin Stitt\uc2  approves legislation in effect outlawing all terminations with exceptions for rape and incest\par \par \uc2 The Republican governor of Oklahoma, \uc2 Kevin Stitt\uc2 , on Wednesday night signed into law {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/19/oklahoma-abortion-ban-strictest"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the strictest \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban in the US}}}\uc2 , making his state the first to in effect end all access to the procedure.\par \par \uc2 The law prohibits abortions with exceptions to save the life of a woman or if the pregnancy is the result of rape or incest reported to law enforcement.\par \par \uc2 The law also authorises doctors to remove a \u8220\'20\'1Cdead unborn child caused by spontaneous \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D or miscarriage, or to remove an ectopic pregnancy, a potentially life-threatening emergency that occurs when a fertilised egg implants outside the uterus, often in a fallopian tube and early in pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 The law does not apply to the use of morning-after pills such as Plan B or any type of contraception.\par \par \uc2 It comes in the wake of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2022/may/23/roe-v-wade-abortion-laurence-tribe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a leaked supreme court ruling}}}\uc2  that indicated the imminent overturning by the conservative majority of Roe v Wade, the 1973 ruling which established the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The leaked ruling prompted outrage and protests across the US. The full ruling is expected in June.\par \par \uc2 Similar to a Texas law passed last year and let stand by the supreme court, the Oklahoma ban will be enforced by civil lawsuits rather than criminal prosecution, allowing private citizens to sue \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers or anyone who helps a woman obtain an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Providers said they would cease operations as soon as the bill was signed.\par \par \uc2 Stitt said: \u8220\'20\'1CI promised Oklahomans that as governor I would sign every piece of pro-life legislation that came across my desk and I am proud to keep that promise today.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFrom the moment life begins at conception is when we have a responsibility as human beings to do everything we can to protect that baby\u8217\'20\'19s life and the life of the mother. That is what I believe and that is what the majority of Oklahomans believe.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 When state politicians passed the law last week, the vice-president, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/VP/status/1527386111323959296"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called it}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cthe latest in a series of blatant attacks on women by extremist legislators\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, Moira Donegan, a Guardian columnist, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MoiraDonegan/status/1529617075462934528"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CAn \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic in Wyoming was set on fire last night. Today, the governor of Oklahoma signed a total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban beginning at fertilisation enforced \u8230\'20\'26 through surveillance and vigilantism by civilians. The attack on women is inventively cruel, and it\u8217\'20\'19s relentless.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Elizabeth Nash\uc2 , state policy analyst for the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights supporting \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ElizNash/status/1529611085464100864"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CThe impact will be disastrous for Oklahomans. It will also have severe ripple effects, especially for Texas patients who had been traveling to Oklahoma in large numbers after the Texas six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban went into effect in September.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The bills are part of an aggressive push in Republican-led states. Nash {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ElizNash/status/1529611090245599232"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 added}}}\uc2  : Oklahoma and Texas are the tip of the iceberg. We estimate that 26 states are certain or likely to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  if \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights are overturned. And the supreme court is poised to overturn Roe v Wade in the next few weeks.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It is unclear what will happen to women who qualify under an exception. The author of the law, state representative Wendi Stearman, says doctors will decide which women qualify for abortions in hospitals. Providers and activists warn that trying to prove qualification could prove difficult and even dangerous.\par \par \uc2 Stitt signed a six-week ban earlier this month. A third Oklahoma bill is to take effect this summer. It would make it a felony to perform an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , punishable by up to 10 years in prison. That bill contains no exceptions for rape or incest.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220526ei5q001xp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
