\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 The network of organisations seeking to influence  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  policy across Europe\b0\par\par\uc2 Angela Giuffrida in Rome and Flora Garamvolgyi \par \uc2 1,325 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 May 2022\par 10:46 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The ultra-Christian, anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and far-right network is allegedly seeking to replicate anti-choice efforts in the US\par \par \uc2 A network of ultra-Christian, anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and far-right organisations is building momentum in its quest to influence \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy in Europe as the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  considers striking down {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2 , the 1973 ruling that legalised the procedure in America.\par \par \uc2 Elements of the network originally came together under the name Agenda Europe, holding yearly summits across the continent between 2013 until at least 2018, by which time it had grown to comprise 300 participants, including politicians and Vatican diplomats.\par \par \uc2 The aim of the group was to \u8220\'20\'1Crestore the natural order\u8221\'20\'1D by devising ways to gradually erode \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, gay rights and policies on combating violence against women, as well as to reduce access to contraceptives.\par \par \uc2 Organisers behind Agenda Europe summits included Terrence McKeegan, a former legal adviser to the Holy See\u8217\'20\'19s mission to the \uc2 UN\uc2  in New York, and Gudrun Kugler, a Catholic theologian, member of the Austrian parliament and human rights spokesperson for the Austrian People\u8217\'20\'19s party.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is a rather loose network that brought together all the different groups \u8211\'20\'13 mostly from around Europe \u8211\'20\'13 that identify themselves as pro-life or pro-family, so anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  or anti-LGBT rights,\u8221\'20\'1D said Neil Datta, secretary of the European Parliamentary Forum for Sexual and Reproductive Rights who conducted an inquiry into the network and shared documents detailing the group\u8217\'20\'19s aims, meeting programmes and participants.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou can see they started out trying to find their relevance, and by the third meeting they were actually coming up with proactive ideas about how to roll back human rights in sexuality and reproduction.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Today, people connected to Agenda Europe are linked to the Political Network of Values (PNfV), a global platform with strikingly similar values that sprung up as the former\u8217\'20\'19s visibility appeared to diminish.\par \par \uc2 PNfV is hosting its fourth {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://politicalnetworkforvalues.org/en/what-we-do/transatlantic-summit/transatlantic-summit-iv-budapest-2021/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 transatlantic summit}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 which includes Kugler and other Agenda Europe personalities among the speakers \u8211\'20\'13 in Budapest on Thursday and Friday.\par \par \uc2 When it comes to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, the network is allegedly seeking to replicate recent anti-choice efforts in the US, where rightwing activists have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2022/feb/22/the-scheme-senators-highlight-rightwing-influence-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gradually manoeuvred people}}}\uc2  who share the same views {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2020/nov/05/trump-lawyers-supreme-court-brett-kavanaugh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 into the judicial and political systems}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19ll be really pumped up by the potential reversal of the Roe v Wade,\u8221\'20\'1D Datta added.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFirstly, because it provides them with a model of one of the most advanced countries taking a position that conforms to their own thinking. But the US court is not responding to changes in society; this is the result of a 20- to 30-year strategy by the US Christian right to influence the whole American judicial system by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2001/mar/26/usa.julianborger"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 training and placing its own people in the system}}}\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The network is believed to have already made headway in Europe, including heavily influencing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2022/mar/28/polish-woman-is-first-to-face-trial-for-violating-strict-abortion-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Poland\u8217\'20\'19s near-total ban on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  as well as the outcome of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2018/oct/05/romanians-to-vote-in-referendum-lgbt-groups-say-is-fuelling-hate-marriage-corruption"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 same-sex marriage referendums}}}\uc2  in countries including Croatia, Romania and Slovenia.\par \par \uc2 Although \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is legal in Hungary, the procedure has become more difficult to access under {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/viktor-orban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Viktor Orb\u225\'00\'E1n}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s rightwing populist government.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, LGBT rights have been gradually eroded in the country over recent years. Last year the Hungarian parliament passed a law banning gay people from featuring in school educational materials or TV shows for under-18s, and in 2020 effectively banned adoption for same-sex couples and ended {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2020/may/19/hungary-votes-to-end-legal-recognition-of-trans-people"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  legal recognition for gender changes}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In Italy, the network is believed to have gained a foothold in 2019 when the country hosted a conference of the controversial World Congress of Families (WCF), a US Christian-right supported global coalition, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2019/mar/29/city-of-love-christian-right-congress-in-verona-divides-italy-league-extremism"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in Verona}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Matteo Salvini\uc2 , leader of the far-right League, a key component of the Italian government, spoke at the event, as did his far-right counterpart, \uc2 Giorgia Meloni\uc2 , who leads {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/aug/03/success-of-far-right-brothers-of-italy-raises-fears-of-fascist-revival"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Brothers of Italy}}}\uc2 , the party currently leading in opinion polls.\par \par \uc2 Since then, measures to restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 such as banning health clinics from providing the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill or allowing anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists to infiltrate hospitals to pressure women not to end their pregnancy \u8211\'20\'13 have been introduced in regions led by a coalition of the two parties and \uc2 Silvio Berlusconi\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Forza Italia, including Marche, Lombardy, Piedmont, Umbria and Veneto.\par \par \uc2 Moreover, even though \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was legalised in Italy via a referendum in 1978, it has become increasingly difficult for women to access a safe procedure due to the high number of gynaecologists \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2016/mar/11/italian-gynaecologists-refuse-abortions-miscarriages"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seven out of 10}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 who are \u8220\'20\'1Cmoral objectors\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe know that the broader network\u8217\'20\'19s strategy in relation to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is to first prevent, then restrict and ban,\u8221\'20\'1D said Datta.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat we\u8217\'20\'19re seeing now in Hungary and in countries such as Italy are attempts to prevent \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  from ever taking place, through conscientious objection and ways of dissuading women.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Silvana Agatone, who until she retired was one of the few gynaecologists in Rome who carried out abortions, said: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s getting worse in Italy. We\u8217\'20\'19ve always had objectors but now the life of a doctor who does do abortions has been made more difficult as you have these anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  people going into hospitals pressuring them, and women, not to abort.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey are also trying to rewrite medicine by paying people to produce material on the dangers of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  that are purported to be scientific.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 An influential politician with the League is Simone Pillon, who until his election as senator in March 2018 was an adviser on the board of Novae Terrae, an anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  organisation headed by his close friend, Luca Volant\u232\'00\'E8, a politician with the now defunct Union of the Centre party and former chairman of the parliamentary group of the European People\u8217\'20\'19s party.\par \par \uc2 Novae Terrae was an integral player in Agenda Europe, at least until Volant\u232\'00\'E8 was investigated for money laundering. Volant\u232\'00\'E8 was recently cleared of the allegations.\par \par \uc2 Pillon said he is aware of Agenda Europe, which he described as akin \u8220\'20\'1Cto a group of friends getting together\u8221\'20\'1D, but never attended any of its meetings.\par \par \uc2 Pillon has a 20-year history of close relationships with Italian anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups and attended a large anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  demonstration in Rome on Saturday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am from the pro-life world and then I entered into politics to bring forward the voice of the pro-life associations,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Pillon said he was \u8220\'20\'1Cenvious\u8221\'20\'1D of the situation regarding Roe v Wade in US, adding that a similar outcome would arrive in Europe \u8220\'20\'1Csooner or later\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt was an ideological current that brought the liberalisation of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the US in the 1970s, which then led to European legislation being adapted to this way of thinking,\u8221\'20\'1D said Pillon. \u8220\'20\'1CI am convinced this new wave will [unfold] in Europe. I don\u8217\'20\'19t know when, but I hope sooner rather than later.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 With the coalition of the League, Brothers of Italy and Forza Italia standing a good chance of winning general elections next spring, he may soon have even more power to influence \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, PNfV will continue to strive to make waves. The speaker lineup at the Budapest summit includes politicians from Hungary, Spain and Slovakia.\par \par \uc2 Hungarian speakers include MEPs from the ruling Fidesz party, such as Balazs Hidveghi and Eniko Gyori. Miklos Sz\u225\'00\'E1nth\u243\'00\'F3, the director of the Center for Fundamental Rights, who hosted CPAC Hungary last week, is also expected to speak, as is Zolt\u225\'00\'E1n Balogh, a commissioner to prime minister Orb\u225\'00\'E1n.\par \par \uc2 Hungary\u8217\'20\'19s newly elected president and former families minister, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/mar/10/orban-loyalist-katalin-novak-elected-hungary-first-female-president"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Katalin Nov\u225\'00\'E1k}}}\uc2 , had been a board member of PNfV since as early as 2015 and became its chairperson in 2019.\par \par \uc2 However, she resigned from the role in March after being elected Hungarian president. In comments to Breitbart in 2019, she said there is no \u8220\'20\'1Cchoice\u8221\'20\'1D when it comes to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CPro-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is pro-killing, it is against choice,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220526ei5q001md\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
