\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Georgia primaries deliver blow to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s grip on Republican party \u8211\'20\'13 live\b0\par\par\uc2 Richard Luscombe \par \uc2 4,347 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 May 2022\par 20:09 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Several candidates who supported the ex-president\u8217\'20\'19s big lie of election fraud were defeated but the Maga wing also had successesResounding setback for Trump as Kemp wins Republican primary in GeorgiaBrad Raffensperger defeats Trump bid to oust him as Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s top election officialBlow to Madison Cawthorn as appeals court reverses \u8216\'20\'18insurrectionist\u8217\'20\'19 rulingSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 Thanks for following the US politics blog today. We\u8217\'20\'19re closing down here, but you can keep up with developments in our {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/may/25/texas-school-shooting-news-victims-uvalde-elementary-school-latest-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 live blog covering the Texas elementary school massacre here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s grip on the Republican party loosened with defeat for his \u8220\'20\'1Cbig lie\u8221\'20\'1D candidates in several key Georgia primary races. But the former president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/meridithmcgraw/status/1529503093674721280"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was more focused}}}\uc2  on his weekend appearance at the national rifle association\u8217\'20\'19s weekend convention in Houston.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Pennsylvania \u8217\'20\'19s Republican Senate primary from last week might not be settled until next month after the state\u8217\'20\'19s elections chief said the deadlocked race between Trump\u8217\'20\'19s pick, celebrity TV doctor Mehmet Oz, and David McCormick, was headed for a recount.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else we followed:\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s hopes of taming inflation before November\u8217\'20\'19s midterm elections were dashed by an economic outlook released by the congressional budget office on Wednesday afternoon that says the crisis will persist into next year.\par \par \uc2 * Senate majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  said Democrats would not immediately bring gun legislation to a vote because of Republican opposition.\par \par \uc2 * Public approval of the supreme court dropped sharply to 44% following the leak of a draft opinion that would overturn the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  decision guaranteeing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights nationwide, according to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://law.marquette.edu/poll/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Marquette Law School poll}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 , the Republican vice chair of the January 6 House panel investigating \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s insurrection, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/may/25/primary-election-results-midterms-georgia-texas-alabama-latest?page=with:block-628e3fa48f08e646defadbc3#block-628e3fa48f08e646defadbc3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has Covid-19}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s hopes of taming inflation before November\u8217\'20\'19s midterm elections look to have been dashed by an economic outlook released by the congressional budget office on Wednesday afternoon that says the crisis will persist into next year.\par \par \uc2 High prices and the soaring cost of gas threaten to derail Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 hopes of retaining control of Congress in the fall, and Biden last week promised tackling them was his \u8220\'20\'1Ctop domestic priority\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Wednesday\u8217\'20\'19s report from the non-partisan agency predicts the consumer price index will rise 6.1% this year and 3.1% in 2023, the Associated Press said. This forecast suggests that inflation will slow from current annual levels of 8.3%, yet would still be dramatically above a long-term baseline of 2.3%.\par \par \uc2 The CBO cautions its numbers \u8220\'20\'1Care subject to considerable uncertainty, in part because of the ongoing pandemic and other world events,\u8221\'20\'1D including Russia\u8217\'20\'19s war in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Maya MacGuineas\uc2 , president of the committee for a responsible federal budget, told the AP ahead of the report\u8217\'20\'19s release that the pandemic, war in Ukraine and other factors point to the importance of reducing the annual deficit.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUnfortunately, the underlying story here is one of fiscally unsustainable positions and on top of that, we have this added challenge of inflation and a reminder that external shocks continue to come at us,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 enltrCBO Director \uc2 Phillip Swagel\uc2  highlights the main findings of "The Budget and Economic Outlook: 2022 to 2032," which was released today. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/AanxPE9ctK"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/AanxPE9ctK}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 U.S. CBO (@USCBO) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/USCBO/status/1529541992136560641?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 25, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden to sign executive order on law enforcement reform\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is about to sign an executive order increasing accountability in law enforcement and creating a national database of police misconduct.\par \par \uc2 In a statement from the White House, the president says the steps are needed following the killing two years ago of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/george-floyd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 George Floyd}}}\uc2  in Minneapolis by a white police officer, who knelt on Floyd\u8217\'20\'19s neck for nine minutes:\par \par \uc2 Two years ago, the murder of \uc2 George Floyd\uc2  exposed for many what Black and Brown communities have long known and experienced - that we must do more to ensure that our nation lives up to its founding promise of fair and impartial justice for all.\par \par \uc2 The incident sparked one of the largest social movements this country has ever seen, with calls from all corners to acknowledge the legacy of systemic racism in our criminal justice system and in our institutions more broadly.\par \par \uc2 As well as creating the database, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2022/05/25/fact-sheet-president-biden-to-sign-historic-executive-order-to-advance-effective-accountable-policing-and-strengthen-public-safety/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s order}}}\uc2  bans the use of chokeholds and carotid restraints unless deadly force is authorized, and restricts the use of no-knock entries, such as the one used by police in Kentucky who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/apr/26/louisville-kentucky-policing-justice-department-investigation-breonna-taylor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 killed an unarmed Black woman, Breonna Taylor}}}\uc2 , at her home in March 2020.\par \par \uc2 It also requires new standards that limit the use of force and require de-escalation for all federal agencies, among other measures.\par \par \uc2 enltrI\u8217\'20\'19ve called on Congress to pass the \uc2 George Floyd\uc2  Justice in Policing Act, but Senate Republicans have stood in the way of progress. That\u8217\'20\'19s why this afternoon, I\u8217\'20\'19m taking action and signing an Executive Order that delivers the most significant police reform in decades.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 President Biden (@POTUS) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS/status/1529528850660610048?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 25, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration blames Republicans in the senate for blocking the \uc2 George Floyd\uc2  justice in policing act, forcing the president to take executive action.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/25/biden-police-reform-executive-order-george-floyd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden to sign police reform executive order on George Floyd anniversary}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Pennsylvania's Republican Senate primary heading for recount\par \par \uc2 Pennsylvania\u8217\'20\'19s top election official said Wednesday that last week\u8217\'20\'19s Republican Senate primary is heading for a recount, with no winner likely until June.\par \par \uc2 Celebrity TV doctor Mehmet Oz is virtually deadlocked with former treasure official David McCormick in the hotly contested race to take on Democratic nominee John Fetterman in November\u8217\'20\'19s election.\par \par \uc2 Leigh Chapman, Pennsylvania\u8217\'20\'19s acting secretary of state, said in a statement that the vote totals for the top two finishers fell well within the 0.5% margin for an automatic recount after the deadline for counties to report unofficial totals.\par \par \uc2 Oz, who is endorsed by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , led McCormick by 902 votes, or 0.07% of 1,343,643 ballots reported by the state by Wednesday, the Associated Press reported.\par \par \uc2 The agency said it would not declare a winner until the recount is complete, possibly as late as 8 June.\par \par \uc2 Counties continued counting hundreds of ballots on Wednesday, including provisional, military and overseas absentee ballots.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 He might have lost the endorsement of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , but Republican Alabama congressman Mo Brooks\u8217\'20\'19s challenge for a \uc2 US Senate\uc2  seat is very much alive, and heading for a June runoff.\par \par \uc2 Some analysts expected {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2022/03/23/1088264503/donald-trump-mo-brooks-withdraws-alabama-endorsement"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the loss of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s backing}}}\uc2 , a revenge act for Brooks\u8217\'20\'19s comments that he believed voters should look forward instead of dwelling on the 2020 election that the former president lost, would be fatal.\par \par \uc2 Mo Brooks. Photograph: Vasha Hunt/AP\par \par \uc2 But Brooks, formerly a staunch Trump ally and mouthpiece, earned enough if the vote on Tuesday to secure a runoff with Katie Britt, former chief of staff to Senator \uc2 Richard Shelby\uc2 , whose retirement opened up the Alabama seat.\par \par \uc2 Trump initially endorsed Brooks, but pulled his backing in March.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMo Brooks of Alabama made a horrible mistake recently when he went \u8216\'20\'18woke\u8217\'20\'19 and stated, referring to the 2020 Presidential Election Scam, \u8216\'20\'18Put that behind you, put that behind you,\u8217\'20\'19 despite the fact that the Election was rife with fraud and irregularities,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 In response, Brooks, a six-term congressman, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/mar/23/mo-brooks-donald-trump-rescind-2020-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 issued an angry statement}}}\uc2  claiming Trump had asked him to \u8220\'20\'1Crescind\u8221\'20\'1D the 2020 election and remove \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  from the White House.\par \par \uc2 Brooks was a prominent figure at the \u8220\'20\'1CSave America\u8221\'20\'1D rally at the Ellipse in Washington DC on 6 January 2021 that preceded the storming of the Capitol building by Trump supporters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday is the day American patriots start taking down names and kicking ass,\u8221\'20\'1D Brooks told the crowd before the riot.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Interim summary\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s been a lively morning so far in US political news and there is more to come, so do stay tuned, Here\u8217\'20\'19s where things stand:\par \par \uc2 * Texas Democratic congressman \uc2 Henry Cuellar\uc2  was still locked in a tight primary runoff race with progressive challenger Jessica Cisneros on Wednesday, but has already {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/may/25/primary-election-results-midterms-georgia-texas-alabama-latest?page=with:block-628e5b918f084f9a73ca61d5#block-628e5b918f084f9a73ca61d5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 faced}}}\uc2  criticism from the party\u8217\'20\'19s progressive wing in Congress due to his anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and pro-gun views.\par \par \uc2 * Senate Democrats{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/may/25/primary-election-results-midterms-georgia-texas-alabama-latest?page=with:block-628e592c8f08e646defadd95#block-628e592c8f08e646defadd95"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 declined}}}\uc2  on Wednesday to bring gun safety legislation to a vote right now, with leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  saying that he knows that the bills will not pass due to Republican opposition.\par \par \uc2 * Public approval of the \uc2 US Supreme Court\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/may/25/primary-election-results-midterms-georgia-texas-alabama-latest?page=with:block-628e4a688f084f9a73ca6098#block-628e4a688f084f9a73ca6098"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dropped}}}\uc2  sharply following the leak of a draft opinion that would overturn Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 , the Republican vice chair of the January 6 House panel investigating \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s insurrection, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/may/25/primary-election-results-midterms-georgia-texas-alabama-latest?page=with:block-628e3fa48f08e646defadbc3#block-628e3fa48f08e646defadbc3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  has Covid-19}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * The former president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/may/25/primary-election-results-midterms-georgia-texas-alabama-latest?page=with:block-628e30c58f08b48a6e743e4c#block-628e30c58f08b48a6e743e4c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 faced}}}\uc2  a resounding setback as Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s governor Brian Kemp won the state\u8217\'20\'19s Republican primary, defeating former senator \uc2 David Perdue\uc2 , a Trump ally who embraced the myth of a stolen election.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  released a statement on his social media platform, Truth Social, saying that he still plans on attending the \uc2 NRA\uc2  convention in Houston this weekend.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAmerica needs real solutions and real leadership in this moment, not politicians and partisanship,\u8221\'20\'1D the former president wrote. \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s why I will keep my longtime commitment to speak in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/texas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas}}}\uc2  at the NRA Convention and deliver an important address to America.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In his statement, Trump made a peculiar stylistic choice and put the word massacre in quotes.\par \par \uc2 enltrTrump is not cancelling his appearance at the \uc2 NRA\uc2  convention this week in Houston, he says on Truth Social {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/BF4WZO6M10"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/BF4WZO6M10}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Meridith McGraw (@meridithmcgraw) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/meridithmcgraw/status/1529503093674721280?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 25, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Anyway, an interesting twist of irony is that people won\u8217\'20\'19t be able to carry firearms when attending Trump\u8217\'20\'19s speech. It seems this rule is one made by the Secret Service, which told {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2022/05/25/1101181842/nra-trump-speech-guns-banned-houston?utm_source=dlvr.it&utm_medium=twitter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NPR}}}\uc2  that it has the \u8220\'20\'1Cauthority to preclude firearms from entering sites visited by our protectees, including those located in open-carry states\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 For all the live news on the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/texas-school-shooting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 school shooting in Texas}}}\uc2 , do head over to our other live blog currently running, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/may/25/texas-school-shooting-news-victims-uvalde-elementary-school-latest-updates?page=with:block-628e62ff8f08b48a6e744142#block-628e62ff8f08b48a6e744142"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Texas Democratic congressman \uc2 Henry Cuellar\uc2  was still locked in a tight primary runoff race with progressive challenger Jessica Cisneros on Wednesday, but \u8220\'20\'1Cthe Squad\u8221\'20\'1D is already angry, regardless of the result.\par \par \uc2 New York congresswoman \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2 , among the most prominent of the party\u8217\'20\'19s progressive wing in Congress, called out its leaders for backing the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , pro-gun Cuellar over Cisneros.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COn the day of a mass shooting and weeks after news of Roe, Democratic Party leadership rallied for a pro-\uc2 NRA\uc2 , anti-choice incumbent under investigation in a close primary,\u8221\'20\'1D the politician known as AOC tweeted.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRobocalls, fundraisers, all of it. Accountability isn\u8217\'20\'19t partisan. This was an utter failure of leadership\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrOn the day of a mass shooting and weeks after news of Roe, Democratic Party leadership rallied for a pro-\uc2 NRA\uc2 , anti-choice incumbent under investigation in a close primary. Robocalls, fundraisers, all of it.\par \par \uc2 Accountability isn\u8217\'20\'19t partisan. This was an utter failure of leadership.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2  (@AOC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AOC/status/1529303844030754816?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 25, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Senior Democrats including \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  campaigned for Cuellar, a nine-term congressman, as he sought to fend off the challenge from Cisneros, a 28-year-old immigration attorney.\par \par \uc2 Cuellar has already declared victory, but according to the Associated Press on Wednesday, the race is still too close to call. Cuellar led Cisneros by 175 votes, or 0.38% of the 45,209 ballots counted by 2am.\par \par \uc2 The winner will face Cassy Garcia, who won the Republican runoff for the seat, in November\u8217\'20\'19s midterm elections.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senate Democrats decline to bring gun safety legislation to a vote right now\par \par \uc2 Senate majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  said on the chamber floor Wednesday morning that he will not be bringing any gun legislation to a vote in the immediate future, saying he knows that the bills will not pass due to Republican opposition.\par \par \uc2 Speaking after Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s massacre of 19 children and two teachers by a gunman at Robb elementary school in Uvalde, Texas, Schumer said:\par \par \uc2 I believe that accountability votes are important, but sadly this isn\u8217\'20\'19t a case of the American people not knowing where their senators stand. Americans can cast their vote in November.\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press reported that Schumer swiftly set in motion a pair of firearms background-check bills in response to the school massacre, but acknowledged the unyielding rejection by Congress of previous legislation to curb the national epidemic of gun violence.\par \par \uc2 If the slaughter of schoolchildren can\u8217\'20\'19t convince Republicans to buck the \uc2 NRA\uc2  [national rifle association], what can we do?\par \par \uc2 But he said he would continue to work on advancing bipartisan legislation.\par \par \uc2 Follow our {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/may/25/texas-school-shooting-news-victims-uvalde-elementary-school-latest-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 live blog on the Texas school shooting here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 From my colleagues Maanvi Singh and Joan E Greve, these are the \uc2 Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s main takeaways from primary night, which was understandably overshadowed by the massacre of elementary school children in Texas:\par \par \uc2 * Blow to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  as a political kingmaker\par \par \uc2 * Key race for Georgia secretary of state signals defeat for \u8216\'20\'18big lie\u8217\'20\'19 candidate\par \par \uc2 * But Trump acolytes performed better in Arkansas and Texas\par \par \uc2 * Elementary school shooting casts pall over the night\par \par \uc2 * Democratic races also hold interest\par \par \uc2 Read the full story here for their observations:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/24/five-key-takeaways-the-us-midterm-elections"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Five key takeaways: the US midterm elections}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 People who take part in insurrections against the \uc2 US government\uc2  can be barred from office, an appeals court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ca4.uscourts.gov/opinions/221251.P.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  on Tuesday, reversing a ruling in favor of Madison Cawthorn, an extremist Republican politician from North Carolina.\par \par \uc2 Hailing a \u8220\'20\'1Cmajor victory\u8221\'20\'1D, Free Speech For People, the group which brought the case, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://freespeechforpeople.org/federal-court-of-appeals-an-1872-amnesty-for-ex-confederates-does-not-apply-to-madison-cawthorn-or-anyone-else-alive/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CThis ruling cements the growing judicial consensus that the 1872 Amnesty Act does not shield the insurrectionists of 6 January 2021 \u8211\'20\'13 including \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 from the consequences of their actions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Madison Cawthorn. Photograph: Octavio Jones/Reuters\par \par \uc2 Cawthorn lost a primary this month and will not return to Congress in November. But Free Speech For People pursued an appeal.\par \par \uc2 It also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://freespeechforpeople.org/key-highlights-of-free-speech-for-peoples-2020-press-coverage/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 brought cases}}}\uc2  against \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  of Georgia, two Arizona Republicans, \uc2 Paul Gosar\uc2  and Andy Biggs, and an Arizona state representative, Mark Finchem. All have been unsuccessful.\par \par \uc2 The challenges cited the the 14th amendment to the US constitution, passed after the civil war.\par \par \uc2 It says: \u8220\'20\'1CNo person shall \u8230\'20\'26 hold any office, civil or military, under the United States, or under any state, who, having previously taken an oath \u8230\'20\'26 to support the constitution of the United States, shall have engaged in insurrection or rebellion against the same, or given aid or comfort to the enemies thereof.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Cawthorn and the other {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2  were closely tied to events around the deadly January 6 attack on the US Capitol by Trump supporters seeking to stop certification of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s election victory. They have denied knowledge of plans for violence.\par \par \uc2 Read the full story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/25/madison-cawthorn-appeals-court-insurrection-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Blow to Madison Cawthorn as appeals court reverses \u8216\'20\'18insurrectionist\u8217\'20\'19 ruling}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Approval of supreme court plummets over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights\par \par \uc2 Public approval of the supreme court has dropped sharply following the leak of a draft opinion that would overturn the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  decision guaranteeing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights nationwide, according to a new poll.\par \par \uc2 Disapproval of the nation\u8217\'20\'19s highest court was especially pronounced among the roughly two-thirds of US adults who oppose overturning Roe, the Associated Press says, while support for the court was high among those in favor, according to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://law.marquette.edu/poll/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Marquette Law School poll}}}\uc2  , which also found increased partisan polarization in approval.\par \par \uc2 Approval fell to 44%, with 55% disapproving of how the court is handling its job, the sample of more than 1,000 adults between 9 and 19 May found.\par \par \uc2 In March, 54% approved and 45% disapproved, itself a massive drop from the 66% approval the panel enjoyed in September 2020, the month that long-serving justice \uc2 Ruth Bader Ginsburg\uc2  died.\par \par \uc2 Approval was fairly steady among Republicans from March to May this year, but fell sharply among Democrats and slightly among independents.\par \par \uc2 enltrNew Marquette Law School national poll finds overall approval of \uc2 US Supreme Court\uc2  has dropped 10 percentage points since March, from 54% to 44%, and disapproval has gone up from 45% to 55%. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/mulawpoll?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #mulawpoll}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 MULawPoll (@MULawPoll) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MULawPoll/status/1529470143117549568?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 25, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s big lie lost bigly in Georgia on Tuesday night. Some might take this as proof that his spell over the Republican party has finally been broken, but that is what the Republican party wants people to believe.\par \par \uc2 The former president had been waging a personal vendetta against Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s governor Brian Kemp and secretary of state \uc2 Brad Raffensperger\uc2  for failing to overturn the 2020 presidential election in his favor.\par \par \uc2 Trump handpicked former senator \uc2 David Perdue\uc2  and congressman \uc2 Jody Hice\uc2  to challenge Kemp and Raffensperger in the Republican primaries. Both parroted the big lie and both were soundly beaten. It was a tangible sign that even many Trump voters are now weary of \u8220\'20\'1Cstop the steal\u8221\'20\'1D and eager to look forward. It was also a blow to Trump in a primary season where his scattergun endorsements have come up with a decidedly mixed win-loss record.\par \par \uc2 But studying Trump\u8217\'20\'19s recent record as kingmaker misses the point. In fact, it actively helps {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2  create the illusion that they have moved on from \u8220\'20\'1CMake America great again\u8221\'20\'1D (Maga) even as they continue to push its radical rightwing agenda.\par \par \uc2 Glenn Youngkin. Photograph: Kendall Warner/AP\par \par \uc2 It all began with Glenn Youngkin, who last year {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/nov/07/virginia-republicans-trump-cheney-christie-scott-youngkin"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 won election as governor of Virginia as a Trump-lite Republican}}}\uc2 . He never campaigned alongside the ex-president but also took pains to avoid criticizing him and alienating his base. \u8220\'20\'1CDon\u8217\'20\'19t insult \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  but do everything to keep him away,\u8221\'20\'1D was how columnist Peggy Noonan put it in the Wall Street Journal.\par \par \uc2 Youngkin projected the image of a safe, sane, old school Republican who could win back suburban and independent voters. But he went Maga by pushing hot button issues such as coronavirus mask mandates, transgender bathrooms and \u8220\'20\'1Ccritical race theory\u8221\'20\'1D and portraying his opponent as a \u8220\'20\'1Cwoke\u8221\'20\'1D liberal. He flirted with, but did not embrace, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s false claims of a stolen election.\par \par \uc2 The formula has been emulated in various ways by candidates facing extreme Trump-backed challengers. It worked for \uc2 Brad Little\uc2 , the governor of Idaho, and now for Kemp in Georgia. Neither should be mistaken for \u8220\'20\'1CNeverTrumpers\u8221\'20\'1D in the mould of Jeb Bush, \uc2 Mitt Romney\uc2 , \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 , \uc2 Adam Kinzinger\uc2  or \uc2 Larry Hogan\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Read the full story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/24/donald-trump-georgia-losses-republicans-maga"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump-backed nominees lost in Georgia, but can Republicans escape the specter of Maga?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 , the Republican vice chair of the 6 January House panel investigating \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s insurrection, has Covid-19.\par \par \uc2 The Wyoming congresswoman and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/nov/15/liz-cheney-wyoming-republican-party-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican party pariah}}}\uc2  made the announcement in a tweet that said she was fully vaccinated and boosted, and following federal guidelines.\par \par \uc2 She said she received a positive test this morning, and was \u8220\'20\'1Cexperiencing mild symptoms\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 undltr {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/lEoQGk3Ru4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/lEoQGk3Ru4}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rep. \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  (@RepLizCheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepLizCheney/status/1529459269241913344?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 25, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 If Brian Kemp\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/24/georgia-primary-elections-kemp-carr-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 obliteration of David Perdue\u8217\'20\'19s challenge}}}\uc2  wasn\u8217\'20\'19t bad enough for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/24/raffensperger-defeats-hice-georgia-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the failure}}}\uc2  of the former president\u8217\'20\'19s pick \uc2 Jody Hice\uc2  to topple Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s secretary of state \uc2 Brad Raffensperger\uc2  might have stung even more.\par \par \uc2 Raffensperger was, of course, the recipient of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/19/georgia-brad-raffensperger-trump-election-secretary-state"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 infamous call}}}\uc2  following the 2020 election asking him to \u8220\'20\'1Cfind\u8221\'20\'1D the votes he needed to overturn \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s victory in the state, which is now the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/may/02/biden-pelosi-poland-president-russia-ukraine-war-biden-33-billion-aid-us-politics-latest"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 subject of a criminal probe}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Brad Raffensperger\uc2 . Photograph: Ben Gray/AP\par \par \uc2 The refusal of Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s Republican officials to bend to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s will resulted in his furious campaign of vengeance, which fell flat on Tuesday when voters soundly rejected the \u8220\'20\'1Cbig lie\u8221\'20\'1D candidates he wanted to install.\par \par \uc2 Raffensperger\u8217\'20\'19s victory wasn\u8217\'20\'19t as sizeable as Kemp\u8217\'20\'19s, but he still achieved more than 50% of the vote, enough to avoid a run-off and win him the Republican nomination outright.\par \par \uc2 enltrBrad Raffensperger found the votes.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Alex Seitz-Wald (@aseitzwald) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/aseitzwald/status/1529316123820310528?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 25, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 My colleague Sam Levine has taken a look at Raffensperger\u8217\'20\'19s victory and how it was, arguably, the biggest blow yet to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to install compliant officials in positions of authority:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/24/raffensperger-defeats-hice-georgia-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Brad Raffensperger defeats Trump bid to oust him as Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s top election official}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kemp victory terminal for former president's 'vendetta tour'\par \par \uc2 It was supposed to be the moment of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s triumphant revenge over Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s governor Brian Kemp and the other RINOs (Republicans in name only) he excoriated for rebuffing his big lie of a stolen presidential election.\par \par \uc2 But as his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/24/big-lie-candidates-election-tracker-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 chosen candidates}}}\uc2  fell one by one in Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s primary elections, a new reality was dawning over the former president: the total control the self-appointed kingmaker believed he still wielded over the Republican party is no longer intact.\par \par \uc2 Reaction to last night\u8217\'20\'19s events was coming in on Wednesday, although, notably, nothing yet from the former president himself, who put his reputation and - for once his money - behind former senator \uc2 David Perdue\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s doomed attempt to unseat Kemp.\par \par \uc2 But others had plenty to say.\par \par \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2 , the former New Jersey governor who was among a number of senior Republicans, including ex-vice president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , to back Kemp, celebrated the demise of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cvendetta tour\u8221\'20\'1D in a tweet.\par \par \uc2 enltrEnormous win tonight for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BrianKempGA?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @BrianKempGA}}}\uc2 . I am so proud of and happy for my friend\u8212\'20\'14and just as importantly for the Georgia GOP and the people of Georgia. They were not going to kick out a great Governor or be willing participants in the DJT Vendetta Tour.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2  (@GovChristie) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GovChristie/status/1529261130455166979?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 25, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Kemp goes on to face Democrat Stacy Abrams - who won her party\u8217\'20\'19s primary Tuesday unopposed in November in a rematch of their 2018 battle, which Kemp won narrowly.\par \par \uc2 Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s secretary of state \uc2 Brad Raffensperger\uc2 , who memorably denied Trump\u8217\'20\'19s request that he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/trump-raffensperger-call-transcript-georgia-vote/2021/01/03/2768e0cc-4ddd-11eb-83e3-322644d82356_story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cfind\u8221\'20\'1D votes}}}\uc2  in 2020, secured the Republican nomination for re-election against the Trump-backed congressman \uc2 Jody Hice\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The state\u8217\'20\'19s Republican party was quick to celebrate:\par \par \uc2 enltrCongratulations \uc2 Brad Raffensperger\uc2 , Republican nominee for Secretary of State {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/LeadRight?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #LeadRight}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/gapol?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #gapol}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/GeorgiaOnTheLine?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #GeorgiaOnTheLine}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/12BrILSlvm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/12BrILSlvm}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 GAGOP (@GaRepublicans) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GaRepublicans/status/1529332094253641729?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 25, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 And Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s Republican attorney general \uc2 Chris Carr\uc2  beat back a challenge from John Gordon, who made Trump\u8217\'20\'19s stolen election myth a central plank of his campaign.\par \par \uc2 Not all Trump-aligned candidates in Georgia fell: his pick for Senate, former \uc2 NFL\uc2  star \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2 , cruised home. And congresswoman Marjory Taylor Greene won her race at a canter.\par \par \uc2 But Republican leaders will worry that Walker, who has a history of domestic violence, is the wrong candidate to be taking on Democratic senator \uc2 Raphael Warnock\uc2  in the fall. And that Greene\u8217\'20\'19s extremism will turn off independent voters.\par \par \uc2 My colleague Lauren Gambino has this look at how Trump\u8217\'20\'19s chosen candidates went down, and how Kemp\u8217\'20\'19s victory marks a \u8220\'20\'1Cresounding setback\u8221\'20\'1D for the former president\u8217\'20\'19s quest to punish those who dared to cross him:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/24/georgia-primary-elections-kemp-carr-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Resounding setback for Trump as Kemp wins Republican primary in Georgia}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Good morning and welcome to the midweek edition of the US politics blog.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is facing a cold new reality this morning: the total power he thought he still held over the Republican party is no longer a thing.\par \par \uc2 Resounding defeats for his \u8220\'20\'1Cbig lie\u8221\'20\'1D candidates \uc2 David Perdue\uc2 , \uc2 Jody Hice\uc2  and John Gordon in Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s primaries in Georgia were a stunning rebuke for what critics have called Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cvendetta tour\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 his plan to take out the state\u8217\'20\'19s top officials who rebuffed his efforts to overturn his defeat by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Former senator Perdue was trounced by incumbent governor Brian Kemp, Hice failed to topple secretary of state \uc2 Brad Raffensperger\uc2 , and Gordon fell to attorney general \uc2 Chris Carr\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 It wasn\u8217\'20\'19t a total blowout for Trump-aligned candidates in Georgia: his pick for Senate, former \uc2 NFL\uc2  star \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2 , cruised home. And congresswoman Marjory Taylor Greene won her race at a canter.\par \par \uc2 But that in itself is alarming Republican leaders, who worry that Walker, who has a history of domestic violence, is the wrong candidate to be taking on Democratic senator \uc2 Raphael Warnock\uc2  in the fall, and that Greene\u8217\'20\'19s extremism will turn off independent voters.\par \par \uc2 * In Alabama, Republican congressman Mo Brooks lost Trump\u8217\'20\'19s endorsement, but won enough votes to reach a run-off to hold on to his seat.\par \par \uc2 * In Texas, attorney general \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2 , who spoke at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s 6 January Washington rally that preceded the Capitol insurrection, saw off a challenge from \uc2 George P Bush\uc2 , grandson of former president \uc2 George HW Bush\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * And the only anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Democrat in the House, \uc2 Henry Cuellar\uc2 , has declared victory over progressive challenger Jessica Cisneros in their Texas district.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll have lots more reaction coming up to the primary elections in Georgia and other states that voted Tuesday, so please stay with us.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220525ei5p001ut\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
