\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 US primary elections live updates: Governor Brian Kemp beats Trump-backed \uc2 David Perdue\uc2  in Georgia primary \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Maanvi Singh (now) and Joan E Greve and Richard Luscombe (earlier) \par \uc2 11,769 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 May 2022\par 05:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2  defeats \uc2 George P Bush\uc2  in Texas AG primaryFormer Trump spokesperson \uc2 Sarah Huckabee Sanders\uc2  wins Arkansas gubernatorial primaryMarjorie Taylor Greene, congresswoman who embraced conspiracy myths, wins her primaryGeorgia Senate race: Democrat \uc2 Raphael Warnock\uc2  and Republican \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  to face off in midtermsStacey Abrams wins uncontested Democratic governor nominationSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.25am BST\par \par \uc2 Primary night summary\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s it from us after an eventful night of primaries across several states. Here\u8217\'20\'19s where the night stands so far:\par \par \uc2 * A shooting at an elementary school in Uvalde, Texas, cast a devastating shadow over today\u8217\'20\'19s primaries. At least 19 children and two adults were killed when a gunman opened fire in Robb elementary school. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  expressed outrage over the tragedy, calling on Congress to pass stricter gun laws. \u8220\'20\'1CWhy are we willing to live with this carnage? Why do we keep letting this happen?\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 * Brian Kemp, the Republican governor of Georgia, defeated former Senator \uc2 David Perdue\uc2 , who had been endorsed by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . \uc2 Perdue\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s loss marked a significant defeat for Trump\u8217\'20\'19s reputation as a kingmaker in the Republican party, as the former president has used the power of his endorsement to wield influence over candidates and lawmakers. \uc2 Perdue\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s defeat raises questions about the impact of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s endorsement, particularly for candidates challenging incumbents. In November, Kemp will face off against voting rights leader \uc2 Stacey Abrams\uc2 , who won the uncontested race for the Democratic nomination.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Brad Raffensperger\uc2 , the Georgia secretary of state who attracted Trump\u8217\'20\'19s ire for refusing to \u8220\'20\'1Cfind\u8221\'20\'1D enough votes to reverse Biden\u8217\'20\'19s 2020 victory in the state, is projected to win the Republican primary for his position. Raffensperger is above 50% in his race against Trump-backed candidate \uc2 Jody Hice\uc2 , who has embraced the former president\u8217\'20\'19s lies about widespread fraud in the 2020 election, and is expected to avoid a runoff and advance to the November general election.\par \par \uc2 * Trump acolytes performed better in Arkansas and Texas. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former press secretary, \uc2 Sarah Huckabee Sanders\uc2 , secured the Republican gubernatorial nomination in Arkansas, meaning she will likely follow in her father\u8217\'20\'19s footsteps to become governor. Texas attorney general \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2 , who filed a lawsuit challenging the results of the 2020 election, also easily defeated land commissioner \uc2 George P Bush\uc2  in his runoff race. Bush\u8217\'20\'19s loss will have long-lasting repercussions for a political dynasty that has produced two presidents and helped shape Texas politics for several decades.\par \par \uc2 * Congresswoman \uc2 Lucy McBath\uc2  defeated fellow House Democrat \uc2 Carolyn Bourdeaux\uc2  to win the nomination in Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s seventh congressional district. McBath currently represents the sixth congressional district, but she chose to run in the neighboring seventh district after Republican redistricting altered the state\u8217\'20\'19s congressional map. McBath\u8217\'20\'19s victory had particular resonance in the wake of the Uvalde shooting. McBath got into politics after her son, Jordan Davis, was shot and killed at the age of 17 in 2012. Since his death, she has staunchly advocated for stricter gun laws in honor of her son\u8217\'20\'19s legacy.\par \par \uc2 * A winner has still not been called in the runoff race between Democratic congressman \uc2 Henry Cuellar\uc2  and Jessica Cisneros in Texas\u8217\'20\'19 28th congressional district, which pitted a longtime centrist incumbent against a progressive challenger. Progressive groups had rallied around Cisneros, attacking Cuellar over his opposition to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights as the country prepares for the likely reversal of Roe v Wade. But organizations backing Cuellar had spent heavily to help the vulnerable incumbent, and he currently leads Cisneros.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.33am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.21am BST\par \par \uc2 Incumbent \uc2 Brad Raffensperger\uc2  is expected to win the Republican secretary of state primary, NBC and CNN project.\par \par \uc2 Raffensperger, who famously defied \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s ask that he \u8220\'20\'1Cfind\u8221\'20\'1D Republican votes in the 2020 election, has nonetheless backed traditional Republican efforts to restrict voting.\par \par \uc2 Trump-backed candidate J ody Hice, who embraced the former president\u8217\'20\'19s election fraud conspiracy theories, was trailing significantly.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.28am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.12am BST\par \par \uc2 Incumbent \uc2 Kay Ivey\uc2  won the Republican nomination for Alabama governor, the AP projects.\par \par \uc2 Ivey declared victory in her Republican primary race as she speaks at her election watch party in Montgomery. Photograph: Mickey Welsh/AP\par \par \uc2 Ivey is poised to avoid a runoff, surpassing 50% of the vote despite attacks from within her party. She ultimately aligned herself with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who did not endorse a candidate in the race. She signed one of the most extreme laws restricting healthcare for trans youth and embraced right-wing conspiracy theories on immigration and the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.03am BST\par \par \uc2 Progressive representative \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2  denounced \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  and Democratic leaders for supporting incumbent Texas Democratic congressman \uc2 Henry Cuellar\uc2 , who is anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , opposes gun restrictions and promotes oil drilling, calling their endorsement an \u8220\'20\'1Cutter failure of leadership\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrOn the day of a mass shooting and weeks after news of Roe, Democratic Party leadership rallied for a pro-\uc2 NRA\uc2 , anti-choice incumbent under investigation in a close primary. Robocalls, fundraisers, all of it.\par \par \uc2 Accountability isn\u8217\'20\'19t partisan. This was an utter failure of leadership.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2  (@AOC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AOC/status/1529303844030754816?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 25, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.52am BST\par \par \uc2 Bee Nguyen appears poised to advance in Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic secretary of state race.\par \par \uc2 Nguyen, a state representative and ally of \uc2 Stacey Abrams\uc2 , has vowed to fight Republican efforts to restrict voting rights. The secretary of state position in Georgia has taken on new importance after \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his allies tried repeatedly to undermine the 2020 election results, and Republicans moved to pass sweeping voting restrictions following Democratic victories in 2020.\par \par \uc2 Brad Raffensperger\uc2 , who is currently leading the Republican secretary of state race, famously refused Trump\u8217\'20\'19s request that he \u8220\'20\'1Cfind\u8221\'20\'1D votes in 2020. But he has \u8220\'20\'1Cwholeheartedly championed traditional Republican efforts to restrict voting access\u8221\'20\'1D, my colleague {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/19/georgia-brad-raffensperger-trump-election-secretary-state"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sam Levine writes}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 He is a staunch defender of a new Georgia law that bans handing out food or water to people standing in line to vote. He believes Georgia should get rid of no-excuse mail-in voting. He also supports getting rid of a federal blackout period that prevents people from being purged from the voter rolls within 90 days of an election. The centerpiece of his campaign is preventing non-citizen voting, which is virtually nonexistent, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ajc.com/politics/no-noncitizen-voters-found-in-georgia-election-review/I5XNSF5YS5HL7LRJCHVUFBLPXE/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according }}}\uc2  to Raffensperger\u8217\'20\'19s own office.\par \par \uc2 Whoever win\u8217\'20\'19s each party\u8217\'20\'19s nomination will preside over voting in the 2024 presidential election.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.02am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.24am BST\par \par \uc2 Lucy McBath\uc2 , who is the projected Democratic winner in Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s seventh congressional district, said she has been forced to deliver a very different victory speech than she had planned.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBecause just hours ago, we paid for the weapons of war on our streets again with the blood of little children sitting in our schools,\u8221\'20\'1D said the representative, who entered politics after her son was shot and killed in 2012. \u8220\'20\'1CWe cannot be the only nation where one party sits on their hands as children are forced to cover their faces in fear. We are exhausted.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrCongresswoman \uc2 Lucy McBath\uc2  takes the stage for her victory speech. She says she wants to thank moms everywhere, as they all champion to keep everyone safe from gun violence. \u8220\'20\'1CI came to give one speech but now I\u8217\'20\'19m forced to make another.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/dLCEDcHWL3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/dLCEDcHWL3}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ciara Cummings (@CiaraCummingsTV) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CiaraCummingsTV/status/1529294608521388032?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 25, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 McBath is a staunch advocate for stricter gun laws. In 2012, a white man shot and killed her teenage son, who was sitting in a friend\u8217\'20\'19s car at a convenience store.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.35am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.58am BST\par \par \uc2 Despite \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s criticism of Georgia governor Brian Kemp and secretary of state \uc2 Brad Raffensperger\uc2 , many Republican voters still went to the polls to support the two Republican incumbents.\par \par \uc2 Kemp easily defeated his Trump-backed challenger, \uc2 David Perdue\uc2 , and Raffensperger is currently leading in his race by 17 points.\par \par \uc2 One primary voter who spoke to the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Sam Levine, 82-year-old Carolee Curti, said she believed the sitting lawmakers had done a good job handling the 2020 election, despite Trump\u8217\'20\'19s baseless claims of widespread fraud.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI know it upset Trump, and I\u8217\'20\'19m a Trump person, but fair is fair,\u8221\'20\'1D Curti said.\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CI felt that under all that pressure, he did a good job,\u8221\'20\'1D said Carolee Curti, an 82-year-old who voted for Kemp and Raffensperger. \u8220\'20\'1CI know it upset Trump, and I\u8217\'20\'19m a Trump person, but fair is fair.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sam Levine (@srl) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/srl/status/1529278363214434306?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 25, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.03am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.45am BST\par \par \uc2 The AP has not yet projected a winner in the Georgia secretary of state Republican primary, where incumbent \uc2 Brad Raffensperger\uc2  has maintained his lead over \uc2 Jody Hice\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 With roughly 74% of votes counted, Raffensperger leads Hice by 17 points, capturing 51.1% of the total vote.\par \par \uc2 The important question is whether Raffensperger can stay above 50% and avoid a runoff against Hice. If Raffensperger\u8217\'20\'19s support dips below 50%, he and Hice will face off in a one-on-one race next month.\par \par \uc2 Hice received \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s endorsement after embracing the former president\u8217\'20\'19s lies about widespread fraud in the 2020 election. One of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s other candidates, \uc2 David Perdue\uc2 , has already lost tonight.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.49am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.32am BST\par \par \uc2 After winning the Republican Senate nomination in Georgia, \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  was asked whether he believes Congress should pass new gun laws in response to the shooting in Uvalde, Texas.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat I like to do is see it and everything and stuff. I like to see it,\u8221\'20\'1D Walker told CNN. He did not expand further.\par \par \uc2 In November, Walker will face off against Democratic incumbent \uc2 Raphael Warnock\uc2  in what is expected to be a very close race, as Republicans try to regain control of the Senate.\par \par \uc2 enltrAsked if he believes there should be new gun laws in the wake of the Texas shooting, Georgia Senate GOP nominee \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  told me in ATL: \u8220\'20\'1CWhat I like to do is see it and everything and stuff.\u8221\'20\'1D He didn\u8217\'20\'19t engage further. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/wpsAZ7yKP5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/wpsAZ7yKP5}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Manu Raju (@mkraju) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1529281988158541825?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 25, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.11am BST\par \par \uc2 McBath defeats Bourdeaux in member v member primary\par \par \uc2 Congresswoman \uc2 Lucy McBath\uc2  has defeated fellow House Democrat \uc2 Carolyn Bourdeaux\uc2  to win the nomination in Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s seventh congressional district, AP projects.\par \par \uc2 When the AP called the race, McBath led Bourdeaux by 32 points, putting her on track to easily avoid a runoff.\par \par \uc2 enltrBREAKING: \uc2 Lucy McBath\uc2  wins Democratic nomination for \uc2 U.S. House\uc2  in Georgia's 7th Congressional District. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/APRaceCall?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #APRaceCall}}}\uc2  at 10:00 p.m. EDT. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/2nlgpji7ac"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/2nlgpji7ac}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 AP Politics (@AP_Politics) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AP_Politics/status/1529281236870565888?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 25, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 McBath currently represents the 6th congressional district, but that district was significantly altered in Republican redistricting. Rather than running in the Republican-leaning district, McBath instead chose to run in the neighboring 7th district, which Bourdeaux currently represents.\par \par \uc2 McBath got into politics after her son, Jordan Davis, was shot and killed at the age of 17 in 2012. Since his death, McBath has been a staunch advocate for stricter gun laws.\par \par \uc2 McBath\u8217\'20\'19s victory came just hours after a shooting occurred at an elementary school in Uvalde, Texas, leaving at least 18 children dead.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.17am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.56am BST\par \par \uc2 George P Bush\uc2  had tried to distance himself from his family members\u8217\'20\'19 criticism of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  by highlighting the former president\u8217\'20\'19s praise of him.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is the only Bush that likes me! This is the only one,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said at a 2019 rally in Texas. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is the Bush that got it right. I like him.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 At one point, Bush\u8217\'20\'19s campaign even distributed koozies highlighting the comments:\par \par \uc2 enltrI missed out on the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/georgepbush?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @georgepbush}}}\uc2  swag yesterday: The koozie says "this is the only Bush that likes me. This is the Bush that got it right. I like him" - \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/txlege?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #txlege}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/pFTzQCmoRG"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/pFTzQCmoRG}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Scott Braddock (@scottbraddock) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/scottbraddock/status/1400431775965396999?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 3, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 But Trump\u8217\'20\'19s past praise was not enough to oust \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2 , a fierce defender of the former president. As attorney general, Paxton filed a lawsuit challenging the results of the 2020 election, despite no evidence of widespread fraud.\par \par \uc2 Now that Paxton has secured the Republican nomination, he will likely face off against Democrat Rochelle Garza, a civil rights lawyer, in November.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.07am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.47am BST\par \par \uc2 Paxton defeats Bush in Texas attorney general primary\par \par \uc2 Texas attorney general \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2  has won his runoff primary race against \uc2 George P Bush\uc2 , son of Jeb Bush and grandson of \uc2 George HW Bush\uc2 , AP projects.\par \par \uc2 Paxton currently leads Bush, who serves as Texas land commissioner, by about 35 points with roughly half of the votes counted.\par \par \uc2 Bush\u8217\'20\'19s loss marks a significant defeat for a political dynasty that has produced two presidents and helped shape Texas politics for several decades.\par \par \uc2 Paxton, a staunch supporter of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , managed to easily beat Bush despite a number of scandals attached to the attorney general. He has been under indictment on securities fraud charges for seven years.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.38am BST\par \par \uc2 Former Trump spokesperson Sanders wins Arkansas gubernatorial primary\par \par \uc2 Sarah Huckabee Sanders\uc2 , who previously served as White House press secretary under \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , has won Arkansas\u8217\'20\'19 Republican gubernatorial primary, AP projects.\par \par \uc2 As of now, Sanders leads the primary race with more than 80% of the vote, after polls indicated she was likely to win the nomination.\par \par \uc2 enltrBREAKING: \uc2 Sarah Huckabee Sanders\uc2  wins Republican nomination for governor in Arkansas primary election. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/APRaceCall?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #APRaceCall}}}\uc2  at 8:30 p.m. CDT. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/2nlgpji7ac"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/2nlgpji7ac}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 AP Politics (@AP_Politics) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AP_Politics/status/1529273810972704768?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 25, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Sanders will also be heavily favored to win the general election in November to replace the current Republican governor, \uc2 Asa Hutchinson\uc2 , who is term-limited.\par \par \uc2 If she wins the general election, Sanders will follow in the footsteps of her father, former Republican presidential candidate \uc2 Mike Huckabee\uc2 , who led the state from 1996 to 2007.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.29am BST\par \par \uc2 In Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s seventh congressional district, Democratic congresswoman \uc2 Lucy McBath\uc2  is leading her House colleague Carolyn Bordeaux by about 32 points, with roughly 40% of votes counted.\par \par \uc2 If McBath can stay above 50%, she will avoid a runoff and advance to the general election, where she will be the favored candidate in the race.\par \par \uc2 McBath currently represents Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s sixth congressional district in the House, but she decided to run in the seventh district after Republican redistricting dramatically altered her chances in November.\par \par \uc2 McBath\u8217\'20\'19s victory would be particularly meaningful tonight, in the wake of the shooting at an elementary school in Uvalde, Texas.\par \par \uc2 McBath\u8217\'20\'19s son, Jordan Davis, was shot and killed at 17, and the congresswoman has been a staunch advocate for gun control legislation in honor of her son\u8217\'20\'19s legacy.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.32am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.17am BST\par \par \uc2 Extremist congresswoman \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  wins primary\par \par \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2 , the extremist Republican congresswoman who has repeatedly sparked outcry by embracing conspiracy theories and attacking her Democratic colleagues, has won her primary.\par \par \uc2 The AP called the race about two hours after polls closed in Georgia, projecting that Greene would defeat the five candidates who challenged her for the Republican nomination.\par \par \uc2 enltrBREAKING: \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  wins Republican nomination for \uc2 U.S. House\uc2  in Georgia's 14th Congressional District. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/APRaceCall?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #APRaceCall}}}\uc2  at 9:04 p.m. EDT. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/2nlgpji7ac"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/2nlgpji7ac}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 AP Politics (@AP_Politics) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AP_Politics/status/1529267504811593729?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 25, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Greene will have a significant advantage in the general election this November, as Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s 14th congressional district skews heavily Republican.\par \par \uc2 Greene\u8217\'20\'19s victory comes after a group of her critics attempted to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/22/marjorie-taylor-greene-court-congress-capitol-attack"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 keep her off the ballot}}}\uc2  by arguing that her role in the January 6 attack at the Capitol made her ineligible, but that effort failed.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.04am BST\par \par \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2 , who was once a close ally of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , celebrated Brian Kemp \u8217\'20\'19s victory in the Georgia gubernatorial primary and mocked the former president\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to unseat Republicans who have not embraced the big lie.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEnormous win tonight for @BrianKempGA,\u8221\'20\'1D Christie, who previously served as governor of New Jersey, said on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am so proud of and happy for my friend \u8211\'20\'13 and just as importantly for the Georgia GOP and the people of Georgia. They were not going to kick out a great Governor or be willing participants in the DJT Vendetta Tour.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrEnormous win tonight for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BrianKempGA?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @BrianKempGA}}}\uc2 . I am so proud of and happy for my friend\u8212\'20\'14and just as importantly for the Georgia GOP and the people of Georgia. They were not going to kick out a great Governor or be willing participants in the DJT Vendetta Tour.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Governor Christie (@GovChristie) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GovChristie/status/1529261130455166979?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 25, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Trump endorsed former Senator \uc2 David Perdue\uc2  in the gubernatorial primary after Kemp did not take steps to block the certification of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s 2020 victory in Georgia.\par \par \uc2 Since leaving office last year, Trump has been focused on ousting Republicans who have criticized his lies about widespread fraud in the 2020 presidential election.\par \par \uc2 In a statement earlier this month, Trump attacked Christie and two sitting Republicans who had endorsed Kemp as \u8220\'20\'1CRINOs,\u8221\'20\'1D meaning Republicans in name only.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.06am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.44am BST\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Republican Governors Association\uc2 , which had backed Brian Kemp in Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s gubernatorial primary, took a victory lap after the incumbent was declared the winner of the race.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTonight, voters proved that Governor Brian Kemp is a results-driven leader who has always put Georgia first,\u8221\'20\'1D said Republican Governors \uc2 Doug Ducey\uc2  and \uc2 Pete Ricketts\uc2 , co-chairs of the \uc2 RGA\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Ducey and Ricketts condemned \uc2 Stacey Abrams\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19 \u8220\'20\'1Cradical agenda\u8221\'20\'1D for Georgia, saying that Kemp would again defeat the voting rights leader in the general election this November.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CVoters rejected her self-promoting antics and out-of-touch agenda four years ago and will do so again,\u8221\'20\'1D Ducey and Rickets said. \u8220\'20\'1CAs we were in the primary, the \uc2 RGA\uc2  is all-in and we will be there to ensure Governor Kemp is re-elected this fall.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.51am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.36am BST\par \par \uc2 Kemp defeats Trump-backed \uc2 Perdue\uc2  in Georgia gubernatorial primary\par \par \uc2 Governor Brian Kemp has defeated former Senator \uc2 David Perdue\uc2  in Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s Republican gubernatorial primary, the AP projects.\par \par \uc2 As of now, Kemp leads Perdue by about 51 points, meaning the incumbent governor is poised to easily avoid a runoff in the race.\par \par \uc2 Kemp will now face off against \uc2 Stacey Abrams\uc2  in November, which will mark a rematch between the two candidates. Kemp narrowly defeated Abrams in 2018.\par \par \uc2 enltrBREAKING: Brian Kemp wins Republican nomination for governor in Georgia primary election. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/APRaceCall?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #APRaceCall}}}\uc2  at 8:30 p.m. EDT. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/2nlgpji7ac"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/2nlgpji7ac}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 AP Politics (@AP_Politics) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AP_Politics/status/1529258931771645956?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 25, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Kemp\u8217\'20\'19s victory marks a significant defeat for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who had endorsed Perdue and criticized the governor for not taking steps to block the certification of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s 2020 victory in Georgia.\par \par \uc2 Perdue\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s loss will likely intensify discussion over the influence and limitations of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s endorsement, particularly in races where the former president is opposing an incumbent.\par \par \uc2 The blog will have more updates and analysis coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.29am BST\par \par \uc2 Georgia secretary of state \uc2 Brad Raffensperger\uc2  has opened a considerable lead over his Republican challenger \uc2 Jody Hice\uc2  in the GOP primary for secretary of state.\par \par \uc2 With around 20% of the vote reported, Raffensperger leads Hice by roughly 40,000 votes. But a more important number will be whether Raffensperger, seeking a second term as Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s top election official, can get more than 50% of the vote to avoid a runoff. He\u8217\'20\'19s been hovering around that number all evening.\par \par \uc2 The race is one of the most important primaries in the country. Raffensperger earned the ire of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  after refusing to overturn the election results in Georgia in 2020. Trump endorsed Hice, who backed efforts to get \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s victory in Georgia thrown out.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.18am BST\par \par \uc2 Incumbent Brian Kemp continues to enjoy a significant lead over \uc2 David Perdue\uc2  in Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s Republican gubernatorial primary.\par \par \uc2 With about 236,000 votes counted, Kemp leads Perdue by 51 points. If he can maintain that advantage, Kemp will easily avoid a runoff against Perdue.\par \par \uc2 Assuming Kemp wins the nomination, he will face off against Democrat \uc2 Stacey Abrams\uc2  in November. That race would mark a rematch for the two candidates, after Kemp narrowly defeated Abrams in the 2018 election.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.01am BST\par \par \uc2 Walker wins Republican Senate nomination, setting up race against Warnock\par \par \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2 , the former professional football player, has won the Republican Senate nomination in Georgia, the AP projects.\par \par \uc2 Walker\u8217\'20\'19s victory means he will face off against Democratic incumbent \uc2 Raphael Warnock\uc2  in November, as Republicans try to regain control of the \uc2 US Senate\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 enltrBREAKING: \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  wins Republican nomination for \uc2 U.S. Senate\uc2  in Georgia primary election. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/APRaceCall?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #APRaceCall}}}\uc2  at 7:56 p.m. EDT. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/2nlgpji7ac"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/2nlgpji7ac}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 AP Politics (@AP_Politics) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AP_Politics/status/1529250318470590464?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 24, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Walker had received the endorsement of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , and he easily avoided a runoff, capturing 70% of the vote when the AP called the race.\par \par \uc2 The Georgia Senate race is sure to attract nationwide interest and donations, with Democrats seeking to retain the seat that they just flipped in 2021.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.51am BST\par \par \uc2 Warnock wins Senate nomination as he looks to secure full term\par \par \uc2 Incumbent \uc2 Raphael Warnock\uc2  has officially won the Democratic senate nomination in Georgia, easily defeating Tamara Johnson-Shealey, the AP projects.\par \par \uc2 enltrBREAKING: \uc2 Raphael Warnock\uc2  wins Democratic nomination for \uc2 U.S. Senate\uc2  in Georgia primary election. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/APRaceCall?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #APRaceCall}}}\uc2  at 7:41 p.m. EDT. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/2nlgpji7ac"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/2nlgpji7ac}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 AP Politics (@AP_Politics) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AP_Politics/status/1529246480271298560?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 24, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Warnock was first elected in January 2021, making him the first Black person to represent Georgia in the \uc2 US Senate\uc2 . He defeated Republican Kelly Loeffler, who had been appointed to serve out the remainder of \uc2 Johnny Isakson\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s term. The 2022 election will give Warnock his first opportunity to secure a full term in the Senate.\par \par \uc2 Warnock is expected to face off against Republican \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  in November, although the AP has not yet officially called that primary.\par \par \uc2 The Georgia Senate race will be closely watched by both parties, as Republicans look to flip the seat in the battleground state and regain control of the upper chamber of Congress.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.55am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.41am BST\par \par \uc2 While Governor Brian Kemp has jumped out to a big lead with the first batch of votes reported in Georgia, \uc2 Brad Raffensperger\uc2  is currently in a much closer race.\par \par \uc2 With roughly 23,000 votes counted, the incumbent secretary of state leads his primary challenger, \uc2 Jody Hice\uc2 , by 14 points.\par \par \uc2 If neither Raffensperger or Hice can get at least 50% of the vote, the two candidates will be forced into a runoff race to determine the Republican nominee for secretary of state.\par \par \uc2 Hice has received \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s endorsement, and he has embraced the former president\u8217\'20\'19s lies about widespread fraud in the 2020 presidential election.\par \par \uc2 This primary race will test how the \u8220\'20\'1Cbig lie\u8221\'20\'1D is influencing Republican voters, as the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Sam Levine reported last week:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/19/georgia-secretary-of-state-primary-will-test-big-lies-hold-on-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Georgia secretary of state primary will test big lie\u8217\'20\'19s hold on Republicans}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.30am BST\par \par \uc2 We are getting the earliest results in the Georgia gubernatorial race, and with roughly 8,000 votes counted so far, Governor Brian Kemp leads \uc2 David Perdue\uc2  by about 57 points.\par \par \uc2 As a reminder, Kemp needs to secure at least 50% of the vote in order to avoid a runoff against Perdue and have a chance to face Democrat \uc2 Stacey Abrams\uc2  in November.\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s still a lot of counting left. Stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.13am BST\par \par \uc2 Abrams wins uncontested Democratic gubernatorial nomination in Georgia\par \par \uc2 No surprise here: \uc2 Stacey Abrams\uc2  has officially won the Democratic gubernatorial nomination in Georgia, after running unopposed in the race, according to the AP.\par \par \uc2 Abrams, a voting rights leader who narrowly lost the 2018 gubernatorial race to Republican Brian Kemp, may have the chance at a rematch against the incumbent governor.\par \par \uc2 But first, Kemp will have to survive a primary challenge from former Senator \uc2 David Perdue\uc2 , who has received \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s endorsement.\par \par \uc2 More results are still coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.16am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.01am BST\par \par \uc2 Polls close in Georgia\par \par \uc2 It is 7pm ET, so the polls are closing in Georgia, which is holding a number of significant primary races tonight.\par \par \uc2 In the gubernatorial race, incumbent Republican Brian Kemp is facing off against former Senator \uc2 David Perdue\uc2 , who has been endorsed by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Trump has also endorsed \uc2 Jody Hice\uc2  in his primary challenge against the incumbent secretary of state, Republican \uc2 Brad Raffensperger\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Those two races will test Trump\u8217\'20\'19s reputation as a kingmaker in the Republican party. Although Trump\u8217\'20\'19s endorsement carries immense sway with Republican primary voters, it\u8217\'20\'19s unclear whether his support will be enough to oust two incumbents.\par \par \uc2 The blog will have updates as results start trickling in, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Polls will close in Georgia in about five minutes. As a reminder, here is when polls close in each state holding races tonight:\par \par \uc2 * Georgia: Polls close at 7pm local time.\par \par \uc2 * Alabama : Polls close at 7pm local time.\par \par \uc2 * Arkansas: Polls close at 7.30pm local time.\par \par \uc2 * Texas: Polls close at 7pm local time.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Progressive groups have rallied around congressional candidate Jessica Cisneros, even as organizations backing incumbent Democratic congressman \uc2 Henry Cuellar\uc2  have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/may/24/primary-elections-texas-georgia-midterms-voting-trump-live?page=with:block-628d55de8f084f9a73ca57ed#block-628d55de8f084f9a73ca57ed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 poured money into the race}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The climate group Sunrise Movement said it has made over 700,000 calls to primary voters in Texas\u8217\'20\'19 28th congressional district since the organization endorsed Cisneros last year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CVoters in this district want someone who will fight for workers rights, reproductive freedoms, a champion on immigration \u8211\'20\'13 and Jessica is that person,\u8221\'20\'1D said Ezra Oliff-Lieberman, Sunrise\u8217\'20\'19s electoral organizer in Texas.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe choice is clear for Democrats \u8211\'20\'13 they can side with an anti-choice, anti-labor \u8216\'20\'18Democrat\u8217\'20\'19, and outcast young and working people in this fight, or they can fight with us for choice, clean air and water, and win elections.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Polls will close in Georgia in less than an hour, as the state\u8217\'20\'19s voters determine which candidates will advance to the general election in November.\par \par \uc2 In Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s seventh congressional district, two incumbent Democratic House members, \uc2 Carolyn Bourdeaux\uc2  and \uc2 Lucy McBath\uc2 , are facing off in a contentious primary race.\par \par \uc2 Bourdeaux currently represents the seventh district, after winning her 2020 general election race by less than three points and flipping the previously Republican-held seat.\par \par \uc2 But after Georgia Republicans were able to redraw the state\u8217\'20\'19s congressional map this year, McBath\u8217\'20\'19s sixth district became safely Republican, so the two-term congresswoman instead decided to run in the neighboring seventh district.\par \par \uc2 Only Bourdeaux or McBath will be able to compete in November, meaning one of them will soon be out of a job. Results will start trickling in soon, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Progressives are bracing for a nail-biter in south Texas tonight in the runoff primary between Jessica Cisneros and congressman \uc2 Henry Cuellar\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/23/texas-democrats-jessica-cisneros-henry-cuellar"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The race}}}\uc2  is, in many ways, a perfect encapsulation of the ideological and generational fight for the soul of the Democratic party. A conservative nine-term incumbent backed by the party\u8217\'20\'19s leadership is in the fight of his political life after being forced into a runoff by a young, progressive immigration lawyer.\par \par \uc2 The runoff is expected to be close, and progressives are eyeing the returns nervously after a stronger-than-expected showing in last week\u8217\'20\'19s primaries. Should she win, it would be an upset and a massive victory for the left.\par \par \uc2 Cisneros was recruited by Justice Democrats, the progressive group that also recruited \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2  to run. Support for Cisneros flooded in after a draft supreme court opinion indicated the justices were poised to overturn Roe v Wade. Cueller is one of the last anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Democrats in Congress.\par \par \uc2 But more has been spent by outside groups to boost Cuellar, one of Congress\u8217\'20\'19 last anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Democrats. Progressives are furious with spending and have demanded House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  condemn it.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn a healthy political party, a human rights attorney and young, charismatic woman of color like Cisneros would be embraced. But the Democratic party establishment has put every barrier in her community\u8217\'20\'19s fight for true representation,\u8221\'20\'1D Waleed Shadid, a spokesperson for Justice Democrats, wrote in a memo on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf Cisneros can mobilize and persuade enough younger and women voters and voters who want a change from the 17-year anti-choice, corporate-backed incumbent opposing reproductive rights and facing an \uc2 FBI\uc2  investigation, she\u8217\'20\'19ll win.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/24/us-progressive-democrats-primaries-wins-congress"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US progressives show strength in primaries and predict more wins ahead}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Kari Paul is anchoring our live blog on the shooting at Robb elementary school in Uvalde, Texas. Governor Greg Abbott has said the gunman shot and killed 14 students and one teacher.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is expected to deliver remarks on the shooting later tonight, when he returns to Washington from Tokyo. Kari will have the latest updates as we learn more. Follow along:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/may/24/texas-elementary-school-shooting-uvalde-latest"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas school shooting: 14 students and one teacher killed }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Fourteen students and one teacher killed in Texas school shooting\par \par \uc2 Fourteen students and one teacher were shot and killed at an elementary school in Uvalde, Texas, according to the state\u8217\'20\'19s governor, Greg Abbott.\par \par \uc2 Abbott said the gunman, identified as 18-year-old Salvador Romas, had \u8220\'20\'1Cshot and killed incomprehensibly 14 students and killed the teacher \u8230\'20\'26 the shooter, he himself is deceased and it is believed responding officers killed him\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The White House press secretary, \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2 , said \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  had been briefed on the shooting and would speak about the tragedy when he returns to the White House tonight. The president was returning from Tokyo when news of the shooting broke.\par \par \uc2 enltrPresident Biden has been briefed on the horrific news of the elementary school shooting in Texas and will continue to be briefed regularly as information becomes available.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  (@PressSec) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PressSec/status/1529209806229106698?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 24, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The shooting comes months before the US is set to mark the 10-year anniversary of the shooting at Sandy Hook Elementary school, which resulted in the deaths of 20 children and six adults.\par \par \uc2 In the decade since the Sandy Hook shooting, no major gun control legislation has passed Congress. Thousands of mass shootings have occurred in the years since, including one {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/15/buffalo-shooting-supermarket-new-york-joe-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 earlier this month}}}\uc2  in Buffalo, New York.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  will have a separate live blog to cover the latest news from Uvalde as we continue to provide updates on today\u8217\'20\'19s primaries.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/24/texas-school-shooting-uvalde-robb-elementary"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fourteen students and one teacher killed in Texas school shooting, governor says}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 Texas is also holding primary runoff races today to determine nominees in a number of key statewide and congressional races.\par \par \uc2 In Texas\u8217\'20\'19 28th congressional district, Democratic incumbent congressman \uc2 Henry Cuellar\uc2  is facing a serious political threat from progressive challenger Jessica Cisneros.\par \par \uc2 Neither of the two candidates finished above 50% in the district\u8217\'20\'19s 1 March primary, forcing them into today\u8217\'20\'19s runoff.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Alexandra Villareal reported on the race this week:\par \par \uc2 Texas-28 is a heavily gerrymandered, predominantly Latino congressional district that rides the US-Mexico border, including the city of Laredo, before sprawling across south-central Texas to reach into San Antonio. During the primary election in March, voters there were so split that barely a thousand votes divided Cuellar from Cisneros, while neither candidate received the majority they needed to win.\par \par \uc2 Now, the runoff on 24 May has come to represent not only a race for the coveted congressional seat, but also a referendum on the future of Democratic politics in Texas and nationally.\par \par \uc2 The House speaker, \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , House majority whip, \uc2 James E Clyburn\uc2 , and House majority leader, \uc2 Steny Hoyer\uc2 , have thrown the full-throated support of the Democratic establishment behind Cuellar, while endorsements from progressive icons such as \uc2 Bernie Sanders\uc2 , Elizabeth Warren and \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2  have elevated Cisneros as a rising star on the national stage.\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18If Cuellar wins, this is a story of how the Democratic machine and the old system is still strong in the district. And if Jessica Cisneros wins, the narrative is this is another successful Latina politician \u8230\'20\'26 carrying the community forward,\u8217\'20\'19 said Katsuo Nishikawa Ch\u225\'00\'E1vez, an associate professor of political science at Trinity University.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/23/texas-democrats-jessica-cisneros-henry-cuellar"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Progressive v anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  Democrat: Texas faces pivotal primary runoff}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Senate Republican leader, \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , pointed to the expected record turnout in Georgia to dispute Democratic criticism of the state\u8217\'20\'19s new voting law.\par \par \uc2 That law, which was signed by Governor Brian Kemp {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/mar/25/georgia-voting-restrictions-law-passed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 last year}}}\uc2 , imposed significant restrictions on absentee voting in Georgia. Voting rights activists argued that the law was an overt attempt to suppress turnout, particularly among Black voters.\par \par \uc2 Speaking at a press conference on Capitol Hill, McConnell said the record turnout disproved Democrats \u8217\'20\'19 claims that Republicans are attempting to limit access to the ballot box across the country.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s no effort in America, in any state in America, to suppress voting,\u8221\'20\'1D McConnell told reporters.\par \par \uc2 According to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.brennancenter.org/our-work/research-reports/voting-laws-roundup-december-2021"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Brennan Center for Justice}}}\uc2 , at least 19 states passed 34 laws restrict\u173\'00\'ADing access to voting last year, as \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  continued to spread the \u8220\'20\'1Cbig lie\u8221\'20\'1D of widespread fraud in the 2020 presidential election.\par \par \uc2 Senate Republicans have also repeatedly blocked Democratic voting rights bills since \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  took office.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 Georgia on track to see record turnout for midterm primary\par \par \uc2 The polls in Georgia are scheduled to close in less than three hours, and the state is on track to set a new record for voter turnout in a midterm primary election.\par \par \uc2 Gabriel Sterling\uc2 , the chief operating officer in the Georgia secretary of state\u8217\'20\'19s office, said on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1CWe are on a solid path to surpass the record for midterm primary turnout. The previous record was 2018 with approximately 1,162,000.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrWe are on a solid path to surpass the record for midterm primary turnout. The previous record was 2018 with approximately 1,162,000.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Gabriel Sterling\uc2  (@GabrielSterling) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GabrielSterling/status/1529163601210122243?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 24, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 This year\u8217\'20\'19s Georgia primaries have attracted nationwide interest because of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s endorsements in the gubernatorial and secretary of state races.\par \par \uc2 Trump has endorsed \uc2 David Perdue\uc2 , who is challenging incumbent Republican Governor Brian Kemp, and \uc2 Jody Hice\uc2 , who is running against current Secretary of State \uc2 Brad Raffensperger\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The two races are being closely watched to determine if the former president\u8217\'20\'19s endorsement has enough sway with Republican primary voters to oust two incumbents.\par \par \uc2 The blog will be closely following the results once polls close in Georgia, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 Thanks for joining me today. I\u8217\'20\'19m handing over the blog now to my colleague Joan E Greve, who will guide you through the next few hours as polls close and results begin to come in from the five states holding their primaries today.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s some of the races we looked at:\par \par \uc2 * In Georgia, it\u8217\'20\'19s a day of reckoning for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , where his big lie-supporting endorsee \uc2 David Perdue\uc2  takes on incumbent Republican governor Brian Kemp. The former president\u8217\'20\'19s power is also being put to the test in the race for secretary of state between incumbent \uc2 Brad Raffensperger\uc2  and his pick congressman \uc2 Jody Hice\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * In Texas, the incumbent Democratic congressman \uc2 Henry Cuellar\uc2  faces a stiff challenge from progressive Jessica Cisneros.\par \par \uc2 * In Alabama, congressman Mo Brooks is looking to show that a Republican can not only survive having the endorsement of Trump taken away in his race, but actually thrive without it.\par \par \uc2 * In Arkansas, former Trump mouthpiece \uc2 Sarah Huckabee Sanders\uc2  is expected to win the Republican nomination for governor easily. The former white House press secretary could follow her father \uc2 Mike Huckabee\uc2  into the governor\u8217\'20\'19s mansion in November.\par \par \uc2 And elsewhere:\par \par \uc2 * The deadlocked Republican senate primary in Pennsylvania could be heading for the supreme court, with party leaders backing TV doctor Mehmet Oz in a legal fight with challenger David McCormick over mail-in ballots.\par \par \uc2 * In her new memoir, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kellyanne-conway"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kellyanne Conway}}}\uc2  lavishes abuse on \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2 , calling the former White House strategist a \u8220\'20\'1Cleaking dirigible\u8221\'20\'1D and an \u8220\'20\'1Cunpaternal, paternalistic bore of a boor\u8221\'20\'1D more concerned with his own image than serving \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * A Maryland man who draped himself in a far right-affiliated flag and sprayed a fire extinguisher at police during the deadly Capitol attack on January 6 has been sentenced to nearly three years in prison, according to federal court records.\par \par \uc2 Please stick with us through the rest of the afternoon and evening for all the developments in the primary election races.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 In the battle for control of the Democratic party, progressives are increasingly confident they are winning. That\u8217\'20\'19s how they explain the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/05/16/democrats-moderate-progressive-super-pacs-00032610"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 record sums}}}\uc2  of Super Pac money targeting their candidates in nominating contests for safely Democratic seats.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s a set of people who are uncomfortable with a new brand of politics,\u8221\'20\'1D said Maurice Mitchell, national director of the progressive \uc2 Working Families party\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re trying to set the clock back. But the genie\u8217\'20\'19s outta the bottle.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 So far this election cycle, progressives have a mixed record. But a stronger-than-expected showing in last week\u8217\'20\'19s primaries has energized the movement and set the stage, they hope, for even more success this summer.\par \par \uc2 In Pennsylvania, state representative Summer Lee {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/congress-pennsylvania-government-and-politics-90db47e132c544cd9838afbb234413bd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overcame}}}\uc2  a deluge of outside spending to win her congressional primary. Lee was declared the winner after three days of counting. She {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SummerForPA/status/1527682077839212547"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tweeted}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1C$4.5 mill\u8221\'20\'1D with a fire and trash can emoji.\par \par \uc2 Oregon progressives cheered the victory of Andrea Salinas, who also went up against a crush of big money in one of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2022/05/11/1097691538/bitter-feuds-and-crypto-ties-inside-one-of-the-most-expensive-democratic-primari"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 most expensive }}}\uc2  House Democratic primaries in the country. Meanwhile, the seven-term Oregon congressman \uc2 Kurt Schrader\uc2 , whose conservative politics drew the left\u8217\'20\'19s ire, appears to be on the verge of losing his seat to progressive challenger Jamie McLeod-Skinner, though results have been delayed by a ballot-printing problem.\par \par \uc2 And in what will be one of the cycle\u8217\'20\'19s most competitive Senate races, John Fetterman, Pennsylvania\u8217\'20\'19s iconoclastic, liberal lieutenant governor, beat Congressman \uc2 Conor Lamb\uc2 , a rising star of the center-left.\par \par \uc2 The next test of progressive political power comes today, in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/texas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas}}}\uc2  runoff election between Congressman Henry Cueller, a conservative Democrat backed by party leadership, and Jessica Cisneros, a progressive immigration lawyer endorsed by \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2  and \uc2 Bernie Sanders\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 And after that, there are competitive intra-party primaries in Illinois, New York and Michigan.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re not doing any victory laps,\u8221\'20\'1D Mitchell said. \u8220\'20\'1CIf anything, those losses and the wins have redoubled our commitment and focus.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read the full story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/24/us-progressive-democrats-primaries-wins-congress"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US progressives show strength in primaries and predict more wins ahead}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Wisconsin Republican party says it has recovered all $2.3m stolen by hackers before the 2020 presidential election.\par \par \uc2 A chunk of the money, $600,000, was recovered by the \uc2 FBI\uc2  and given back to the party last month, the state party chair Mark Jefferson said Tuesday, according to the Associated Press.\par \par \uc2 The party\u8217\'20\'19s bank was able to get back $1.5m through its fraud until, and the rest was reimbursed through insurance payouts and donations, Jefferson said.\par \par \uc2 Officials contacted the \uc2 FBI\uc2  two weeks before election day in 2020 after they noticed money intended for suppliers of campaign materials, including \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  hats, was being siphoned to the hackers.\par \par \uc2 Trump lost Wisconsin to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  by fewer than 21,000 votes.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.22pm BST\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://senatedems.com/mcmorrow/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mallory McMorrow}}}\uc2  remembers the sting of being slandered by a colleague for wanting to \u8220\'20\'1Cgroom\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Csexualize\u8221\'20\'1D young children. \u8220\'20\'1CI felt horrible,\u8221\'20\'1D she says. But instead of shrugging it off or trying to change the subject, as Democrats are often criticised for doing, the state senator from Michigan decided to fight back.\par \par \uc2 In just four minutes and 40 seconds, McMorrow delivered a fierce, impassioned floor speech at the state capitol that went viral on social media and earned a laudatory phone call from the US president.\par \par \uc2 She also offered a blueprint for how Democrats can combat Republicans intent on making education a wedge issue. The New Yorker magazine described her as \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newyorker.com/magazine/2022/05/09/a-role-model-for-the-midterms"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a role model for the midterms}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D. \uc2 The New York Times{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/04/27/us/politics/democrats-mallory-mcmorrow-cultural-issues.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 newspaper added}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CIf Democrats could bottle Mallory McMorrow \u8230\'20\'26 they would do it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Mallory McMorrow. Photograph: Daniel Shular/AP\par \par \uc2 It was quite an ovation for a 35-year-old serving her first term in elected office. McMorrow, who previously worked as a car designer and branding and design consultant, is among a generation galvanised by resistance to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his red meat populism.\par \par \uc2 Soon after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2016/nov/09/how-did-donald-trump-win-analysis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s election as president}}}\uc2  in 2016, she saw a video of middle school students chanting \u8220\'20\'1CBuild the wall!\u8221\'20\'1D at another student ; the school happened to be the polling place where she had voted. She felt motivated to go into politics and was elected in 2018 to the state senate for the 13th district, which covers suburbs just north of Detroit.\par \par \uc2 But the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/michigan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Michigan}}}\uc2  senate has been under Republican control since before McMorrow was born. In a time of acrimony and division, it was never going to be an easy ride.\par \par \uc2 Republican {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.senatorlanatheis.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lana Theis}}}\uc2  opened the latest senate session with an invocation that was part prayer, part Make America Great Again (Maga) battle cry: \u8220\'20\'1CDear Lord, across the country we\u8217\'20\'19re seeing in the news that our children are under attack. That there are forces that desire things for them other than what their parents would have them see and hear and know.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 McMorrow was among three Democrats who walked out in protest at the apparent reference to how schools address sexual orientation, gender identity and critical race theory \u8211\'20\'13 the target of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/mar/26/republicans-midterms-culture-war-lgbtq-abortion-book-bans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican laws across the country}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 She also tweeted criticism of the prayer, prompting Theis to lash out in a fundraising email: \u8220\'20\'1CThese are the people we are up against. Progressive social media trolls like Senator Mallory McMorrow (D-Snowflake) who are outraged they can\u8217\'20\'19t teach can\u8217\'20\'19t groom and sexualize kindergarteners or that 8-year-olds are responsible for slavery.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Grooming, a term used to describe how sex offenders initiate contact with their victims, has recently become a Republican buzzword and nods to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/aug/25/qanon-conspiracy-theory-explained-trump-what-is"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  QAnon conspiracy theories}}}\uc2  that hold Democrats run a pedophile ring. It is no less hurtful for being so preposterous.\par \par \uc2 Read the full story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/24/mallory-mcmorrow-speech-democrats-michigan-midterms"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The \u8216\'20\'18straight, white, Christian, suburban mom\u8217\'20\'19 taking on Republicans at their own game}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Key event\par \par \uc2 An independent commission is recommending new names for nine Army posts that commemorated Confederate officers. If approved, Fort Bragg in North Carolina would become Fort Liberty, and Fort Gordon in Georgia would become Fort Eisenhower.\par \par \uc2 The recommendations are the latest step in a broader effort by the military to confront racial injustice, most recently in the aftermath of the May 2020 police killing of George Floyd in Minneapolis, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 The list recommends naming bases for the first time after women and Black soldiers.\par \par \uc2 Fort Polk, Louisiana, would be renamed Fort Johnson, after Sgt William Henry Johnson, a Black medal of honor recipient who served in the first world war.\par \par \uc2 Fort A.P. Hill in Virginia would be renamed Fort Walker, after Mary Edwards Walker, a doctor who treated soldiers in the Civil War and later received a medal of honor.\par \par \uc2 As recently as 2015 the Army argued that the Confederate names did not honor the rebel cause but were a gesture of reconciliation with the South.\par \par \uc2 But following Floyd\u8217\'20\'19s killing and subsequent racial unrest, the Pentagon and Congress pushed to rename military posts and other federal assets such as roads, buildings, memorials, signs and landmarks that honored rebel leaders.\par \par \uc2 enltrAn independent commission is recommending new names for nine Army posts that commemorated Confederate officers.\par \par \uc2 Among the recommendations, Fort Bragg in North Carolina would become Fort Liberty and Fort Gordon in Georgia would become Fort Eisenhower. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/oghpx3pFSj"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/oghpx3pFSj}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Associated Press (@AP) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AP/status/1529168843305787397?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 24, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 My colleague Sam Levine has this look at one of the most consequential races of today\u8217\'20\'19s primary elections, for Georgia secretary of state.\par \par \uc2 Incumbent \uc2 Brad Raffensperger\uc2 , who famously resisted {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/04/trumps-phone-call-to-brad-raffensperger-five-key-points"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump \u8217\'20\'19s demand}}}\uc2  to \u8220\'20\'1Cfind\u8221\'20\'1D him enough votes to overturn \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s victory in the state is facing a tough battle for reelection. Sam has been talking to Georgia voters:\par \par \uc2 Today Georgia voters are casting ballots in what I believe is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/19/georgia-brad-raffensperger-trump-election-secretary-state"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the most important primary election}}}\uc2  this year: the Republican primary for secretary of state.\par \par \uc2 Last week, we {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/19/georgia-brad-raffensperger-trump-election-secretary-state"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 published a story}}}\uc2  from reporting I did earlier this month about the race between incumbent \uc2 Brad Raffensperger\uc2 , the Republican who became nationally known for refusing to overturn the election results, and his Trump-backed challenger and big lie peddler, Congressman \uc2 Jody Hice\uc2 . There has already been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://georgiarecorder.com/2022/05/23/record-early-voting-ends-setting-up-georgias-high-stakes-2022-election-day/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 record turnout}}}\uc2  during early voting, and polls show {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.11alive.com/article/news/politics/georgia-secretary-of-state-poll-bee-nguyen-brad-raffensperger-jody-hice/85-b46e0b61-4f60-4d66-96be-5de53a97b64e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a close race}}}\uc2  between Hice and Raffensperger.\par \par \uc2 Jay Williams, a Republican strategist in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/state-of-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Georgia}}}\uc2  not affiliated with either campaign, told me Raffensperger had made a strategic error in pushing back on Trump and predicted Hice would win.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s branded. And I think it\u8217\'20\'19s gonna be difficult for Republicans to be able to go out and vote for the guy,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CIf you don\u8217\'20\'19t have a big stick, don\u8217\'20\'19t go after someone who has a bigger stick than you. He\u8217\'20\'19s the president, he\u8217\'20\'19s just not a big enough guy to go after him.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://polsci.umass.edu/toplines-and-crosstabs-december-2021-national-poll-presidential-election-jan-6th-insurrection-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Several polls}}}\uc2  over the last year have shown that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2021/09/15/politics/cnn-poll-most-americans-democracy-under-attack/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the vast majority}}}\uc2  of Republicans believe \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s victory was not legitimate. I was curious to see whether that belief was translating into who they were voting for. Would voters kick Raffensperger out of office for saying the election was legitimate?\par \par \uc2 To my surprise, I didn\u8217\'20\'19t find a huge amount of momentum for Hice, who has said the 2020 election was stolen and tried to overturn it. Instead, I found a lot of voters who said they supported Trump, but were also voting for Raffensperger.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI felt that under all that pressure, he did a good job. I know it upset Trump, and I\u8217\'20\'19m a Trump person, but fair is fair,\u8221\'20\'1D said Carolee Curti, 82, who voted for Raffensperger in Rome, which is in the heart of \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s deeply Republican district in north-west Georgia.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think something happened, but I don\u8217\'20\'19t know anything like everybody else. I don\u8217\'20\'19t know that Raffensperger did anything bad either,\u8221\'20\'1D said Judy C, 80, who declined to give her full name after she cast her vote for Raffensperger in Lawrenceville, an Atlanta suburb. \u8220\'20\'1CTrump, excuse me, he should keep his mouth shut.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Another Republican voter, age 78, who only gave only his first name, Bob, said he had automatically ruled out voting for anyone who said the election was stolen. \u8220\'20\'1CIf you claim the last election was fraudulent, I\u8217\'20\'19m not voting for you,\u8221\'20\'1D he told me.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf you asked people to go illegally to try and overthrow the election, I\u8217\'20\'19m not voting for you.\u8221\'20\'1D He declined to say whom he voted for, but said it was probably safe to say he didn\u8217\'20\'19t cast a ballot for Hice.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/19/georgia-secretary-of-state-primary-will-test-big-lies-hold-on-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Georgia secretary of state primary will test big lie\u8217\'20\'19s hold on Republicans}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/fbi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 FBI}}}\uc2  claims an \uc2 Islamic State\uc2  sympathizer living in Ohio plotted to assassinate \uc2 George W Bush\uc2 , but confidential informants helped federal agents foil the plan, according to court records.\par \par \uc2 Details of the alleged scheme to kill the former president are laid out in a warrant that the \uc2 FBI\uc2  obtained in March to search the accused operative\u8217\'20\'19s cellphone records, a 43-page document that was only unsealed in recent days.\par \par \uc2 NBC News reported that the man named in the warrant \u8211\'20\'13 Shihab Ahmed Shihab \u8211\'20\'13 had been arrested.\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for Bush said in a statement Tuesday that the former president was unworried.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Bush has all the confidence in the world in the \uc2 US Secret Service\uc2  and our law enforcement and intelligence communities,\u8221\'20\'1D said the former president\u8217\'20\'19s chief of staff, Freddy Ford.\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for the \uc2 FBI\uc2  declined comment on the investigation, which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.forbes.com/sites/thomasbrewster/2022/05/24/exclusive-isis-plotting-to-assassinate-george-w-bush-in-dallas/?sh=3e862d01180f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Forbes}}}\uc2  was first to report Tuesday. Shihab could not be reached.\par \par \uc2 Read the full story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/24/george-w-bush-assassination-plot-islamic-state-fbi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 FBI says it foiled Islamic State sympathizer\u8217\'20\'19s plot to kill George W Bush}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republican leaders back Oz in Pennsylvania lawsuit\par \par \uc2 The deadlocked Republican senate primary in Pennsylvania could be heading for the supreme court, with party leaders at state and national level throwing in with celebrity TV doctor Mehmet Oz.\par \par \uc2 Officials are opposing a lawsuit that could help Oz\u8217\'20\'19s opponent, former hedge fund chief executive David McCormick, close the gap in votes. One week after last Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s primary, Oz leads by 997 votes, or 0.07% of 1,341,184 ballots cast.\par \par \uc2 David McCormick. Photograph: Quinn Glabicki/Reuters\par \par \uc2 McCormick filed a lawsuit late Monday, the Associated Press said, less than 24 hours before today\u8217\'20\'19s 5pm deadline for counties to report unofficial results to the state. He wants the state Commonwealth Court to require counties to obey a new federal appeals court decision and promptly count mail-in ballots that lack a required handwritten date on the return envelope.\par \par \uc2 Oz, who is endorsed by former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , has pressed counties not to count the ballots and the \uc2 Republican National Committee\uc2  and state party officials said they would go to court to oppose McCormick.\par \par \uc2 Trump, meanwhile, has urged Oz to declare victory before counting is completed.\par \par \uc2 RNC\uc2  chief counsel Matt Raymer said in a statement: \u8220\'20\'1CElection laws are meant to be followed, and changing the rules when ballots are already being counted harms the integrity of our elections\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 McCormick is doing better than Oz in mail-in ballots and has insisted that \u8220\'20\'1Cevery Republican vote should count\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 A recount is virtually certain, which could push the official result as late as 8 June.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s onetime attorney {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jan/18/us-capitol-attack-committee-subpoenas-rudy-giuliani-and-other-trump-lawyers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rudy Giuliani}}}\uc2  testified to the House select committee investigating the January 6 Capitol attack at length on Friday but declined to discuss the involvement of congressional Republicans in efforts to overturn the 2020 election result, according to sources familiar with the matter.\par \par \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2 . Photograph: Daniel Shular/AP\par \par \uc2 The move by Giuliani to refuse to give insight into Republican involvement could mean his appearance only marginally advanced the inquiry into his ploy to have the then vice-president, \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , unlawfully keep {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump}}}\uc2  in office after he lost to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 However, he did potentially pique the committee\u8217\'20\'19s interest by discussing two notable meetings at the White House involving Trump that took place just weeks before the Capitol insurrection.\par \par \uc2 Giuliani asserted privilege and the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Work-product_doctrine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 work-product doctrine}}}\uc2  to decline to respond when asked to detail the roles played by House and Senate Republicans in the scheme to stop Congress\u8217\'20\'19s certification of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s victory on 6 January 2021, the sources said.\par \par \uc2 The panel was not expecting Giuliani to divulge damning information against Trump, since committee counsel had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/feb/22/giuliani-cooperate-january-6-committee"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 agreed with Giuliani in advance}}}\uc2  that he should not have to violate legitimate claims of privilege he might have as the former president\u8217\'20\'19s attorney.\par \par \uc2 But Giuliani\u8217\'20\'19s refusal to engage with questions about House and Senate Republicans frustrated the select committee, the sources said, not least because Giuliani personally urged them to object to Biden\u8217\'20\'19s victory to delay its certification.\par \par \uc2 Full story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/24/rudy-giuliani-capitol-attack-committee-testimony"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rudy Giuliani stonewalls Capitol attack investigators during lengthy deposition}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kellyanne bashes Bannon \u8230\'20\'26 and Trump\par \par \uc2 In her new memoir, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kellyanne-conway"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kellyanne Conway}}}\uc2  lavishes abuse on \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2 , calling the former White House strategist a \u8220\'20\'1Cleaking dirigible\u8221\'20\'1D and an \u8220\'20\'1Cunpaternal, paternalistic bore of a boor\u8221\'20\'1D more concerned with his own image than serving \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Kellyanne Conway. Photograph: Susan Walsh/AP\par \par \uc2 But in doing so, the former senior counselor to the ex-US president criticises Trump himself, otherwise a notable escapee from her book.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COne of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s biggest selling points,\u8221\'20\'1D Conway writes in one of many takedowns of Bannon, \u8220\'20\'1Cwas his refreshing lack of political experience. But the flip side of that quality was his occasional blind spots when it came to personnel decisions and political endorsements.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s endorsements are the focus of fierce attention. In Georgia primaries on Tuesday his candidate for governor, \uc2 David Perdue\uc2 , seems doomed to defeat while his Senate candidate, \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2 , is widely deemed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/22/herschel-walker-senate-republican-primary-georgia-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unsuitable for the role}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Conway continues: \u8220\'20\'1C[Trump] was often too trusting of others who lacked transparency or talent, and insufficiently skeptical of those who were pushing the wrong people as candidates for office or as colleagues in the administration. I won some of those arguments and lost some.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Full story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/24/kellyanne-conway-book-bannon-trump-kushner"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kellyanne Conway takes aim at Bannon in book but hits Trump in process}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s been almost three years since \uc2 Sarah Huckabee Sanders\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 spell as White House press secretary for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  came to an end.\par \par \uc2 During her two years at the podium, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2019/06/13/media/legacy-of-sarah-sanders/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 at least during the time she actually held briefings}}}\uc2 , her fiery rhetoric, attacks on Democrats and quarrels with reporters always felt more like political speeches anyway.\par \par \uc2 Sarah Huckabee Sanders\uc2 . Photograph: Tork Mason/AP\par \par \uc2 Now Huckabee Sanders is about to become a prominent pro-Trump voice once again, and almost certain to wrap up the Republican nomination today for governor of Arkansas, a post once held by her father \uc2 Mike Huckabee\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 She faces former talk radio host Doc Washburn, and is a heavy favorite, according to the Associated Press.\par \par \uc2 Accompanied by her husband and three children, Huckabee Sanders cast her ballot in Little Rock shortly after polls opened Tuesday, and slammed \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  as she spoke to reporters:\par \par \uc2 Paying attention to the bad policies and the failures of the Biden administration and the impact that they have on our state is critically important.\par \par \uc2 If they continue to fail the way that they have and put states in a difficult position, then absolutely, we\u8217\'20\'19re going to call them out.\par \par \uc2 Trump, unsurprisingly, has given Huckabee Sanders his \u8220\'20\'1Ccomplete and total endorsement\u8221\'20\'1D, calling her a \u8220\'20\'1Cwarrior who will always fight for the people of Arkansas\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 She released a book in 2020 detailing her time as White House press secretary, recalling an episode in which Trump told her North Korean dictator Kim Jong-un was \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/sep/01/donald-trump-sarah-sanders-take-one-for-the-team-kim-jong-un-wink-book"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hitting on her}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D at a summit in Singapore.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 The pulling power of a former Republican president is on the line in a Texas primary run-off today, but for once it\u8217\'20\'19s not \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 George P Bush\uc2 , son of former Florida governor Jeb, nephew of two-term president and former Texas governor George W, and grandson of president George HW, is challenging incumbent \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2  for attorney general in a test of how much weight the Bush family name still carries in the state.\par \par \uc2 George P Bush\uc2  leaves the stage after a 2021 rally in Austin. Photograph: Eric Gay/AP\par \par \uc2 Paxton is a Trump ally and big lie advocate who spoke at the 6 January \u8220\'20\'1Cstop the steal\u8221\'20\'1D rally in Washington DC that preceded the insurrection by Trump supporters.\par \par \uc2 He is also awaiting trial on securities fraud charges after being indicted in 2015, and under \uc2 FBI\uc2  investigation for corruption.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this month he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/06/ken-paxton-texas-attorney-general-state-bar-sue-2020-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 claimed the state bar was threatening to sue him}}}\uc2  over the baseless lawsuit he and fellow Republican attorneys general filed to try to reverse \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s 2020 win over Trump.\par \par \uc2 Yet Bush, the Texas land commissioner who has called his rival \u8220\'20\'1Ca crook\u8221\'20\'1D, continues to trail Paxton, according to the few polls that are available, and finished 20 points behind him in a March primary that resulted in today\u8217\'20\'19s run-off.\par \par \uc2 Bush spoke to reporters after casting his vote in Austin this morning, according to the Associated Press, insisting his candidacy wasn\u8217\'20\'19t about his family name:\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s not about dynasties. It\u8217\'20\'19s not about some sort of myth. It\u8217\'20\'19s about doing the right thing and supporting the right people for the right offices.\par \par \uc2 Anybody can plainly see that we\u8217\'20\'19ve got a crook right now in our top law enforcement position who continually abuses his office.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 One of the biggest Trump-endorsed winners in today\u8217\'20\'19s primaries is likely to be former \uc2 NFL\uc2  star \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2 , who is handily placed to win the Republican nomination for senator in Georgia.\par \par \uc2 Walker is, as journalist Justin Glawe observed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/22/herschel-walker-senate-republican-primary-georgia-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in this profile}}}\uc2  for the Guardian, a relatively rare political being: a Black, Trump-supporting Republican with a base consisting of largely white conservatives.\par \par \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2 . Photograph: Matt Hamilton/AP\par \par \uc2 Already a household name from his years in football, Walker went into today\u8217\'20\'19s election with an almost certainly unassailable lead, ahead in some polls by more than 55 points, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.realclearpolitics.com/epolls/2022/senate/Georgia.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to Real Clear Politics}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Some Republican opponents have questioned the electability of Walker, a close friend of Trump, according to the Associated Press. He has a history of violence against women and has made multiple gaffes on the campaign trail.\par \par \uc2 He also skipped the primary debates. He has been open about his long struggle with mental illness and acknowledged violent urges.\par \par \uc2 Glawe says opinions are mixed, largely depending on a voter\u8217\'20\'19s race:\par \par \uc2 African Americans are hesitant to say anything bad about Walker, but they are certainly not jumping at the chance to praise him. Whites, meanwhile, speak of Walker as the personification of the American Dream: he came from nothing, and now he\u8217\'20\'19s something.\par \par \uc2 Assuming he wins today, Walker faces a far tougher fight in November to unseat Democratic senator \uc2 Raphael Warnock\uc2 , who is also far ahead in his own party\u8217\'20\'19s primary.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/22/herschel-walker-senate-republican-primary-georgia-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Herschel Walker: the ex-football star running for Senate in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s shadow}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 A Maryland man who draped himself in a far right-affiliated flag and sprayed a fire extinguisher at police during the deadly Capitol attack on January 6 has been sentenced to nearly three years in prison, according to federal court records.\par \par \uc2 Matthew Ryan Miller, 23, pleaded guilty in February to felony obstruction of an official proceeding \u8211\'20\'13 that day\u8217\'20\'19s joint congressional session to certify \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s win over \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in the 2020 presidential election \u8211\'20\'13 as well as assaulting, resisting or impeding police officers.\par \par \uc2 At a hearing on Monday, Miller was sentenced to two years and nine months. Judge Randolph Moss also ordered Miller to spend two years on probation after his release and to pay $2,000 in restitution.\par \par \uc2 Federal prosecutors had asked the judge for a sentence of four years and three months. Seeking leniency for his client, Miller\u8217\'20\'19s attorney, A Eduardo Balarezo, argued that the defendant was abusing alcohol and marijuana and therefore was not thinking logically on the day of the Capitol riots.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMatthew is a young man who made a terrible decision,\u8221\'20\'1D Balarezo wrote in a court filing ahead of the sentencing. \u8220\'20\'1CHe recognizes that his personal conduct and participation in the riot were not born of a rational decision but rather were fueled by alcohol and marijuana abuse.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe fully accepts responsibility for what he has done and is not making excuses.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Balarezo also condemned Trump\u8217\'20\'19s claims that the 2020 presidential election was stolen from him by electoral fraudsters as \u8220\'20\'1Clies\u8221\'20\'1D that drove Miller to join other Trump supporters in the nation\u8217\'20\'19s capital on the day the riots occurred because he thought \u8220\'20\'1Cit would be cool to be part of history\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Read the full story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/23/maryland-man-capitol-attack-riots-sentence"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Capitol rioter who sprayed police with fire extinguisher sentenced to three years}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 Confirming what almost everybody in Washington DC circles already knew, MSNBC has announced that the former White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2 , who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/05/white-house-press-secretary-karine-jean-pierre"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 resigned earlier this month}}}\uc2 , is joining the network as a host and political analyst.\par \par \uc2 Reports that Psaki had already {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/01/jen-psaki-press-secretary-msnbc-white-house"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lined up a job with MSNBC}}}\uc2  began circulating weeks before her resignation. It sparked questions during some White House briefings about the integrity of being the public face of the Biden administration while negotiating her own paid role within the media.\par \par \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2 . Photograph: Patrick Semansky/AP\par \par \uc2 But she was widely recognized as a safe pair of hands in the role, and restored stability and daily press briefings to the White House after the turbulence of successive press secretaries during the administration of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 According to MSNBC, she will appear as an analyst during the midterm election season leading up to November, and begin presenting her own streaming show next spring.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, MSNBC president Rashida Jones said:\par \par \uc2 Jen\u8217\'20\'19s sharp wit and relatability combined with the mastery of the subjects she covers have made her a household name across the nation.\par \par \uc2 Her extensive experience in government and on the campaign trail and perspective as a White House and Washington insider is the type of analysis that sets MSNBC apart. She\u8217\'20\'19s a familiar face and trusted authority to MSNBC viewers, and we look forward to her insight during this consequential election season.\par \par \uc2 enltrMSNBC officially announces \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  is joining the network {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/pwUUkrmoAH"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/pwUUkrmoAH}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Max Tani (@maxwelltani) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/maxwelltani/status/1529100106271559681?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 24, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kandiss Taylor has been making waves as the official \u8220\'20\'1Cfire and brimstone\u8221\'20\'1D candidate in Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s race to become Republican candidate for governor.\par \par \uc2 In an extraordinary {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RonFilipkowski/status/1528443821293461505"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 campaign rally speech}}}\uc2  on Sunday, in front of a banner referencing Jesus, guns and babies, the \u8220\'20\'1CChristian wife and mother\u8221\'20\'1D called for the execution by firing squad of sheriffs who \u8220\'20\'1Cdon\u8217\'20\'19t do the will of the people\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KandissTaylor/status/1521132865618071555"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 In a tweet}}}\uc2  earlier this month, she slammed the \u8220\'20\'1Csatanic regime\u8221\'20\'1D currently running Georgia, and vowed to \u8220\'20\'1Cbring it to its knees\u8221\'20\'1D as \u8220\'20\'1Cthe ONLY candidate bold enough to stand up to the Luciferian Cabal\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrI am the ONLY candidate bold enough to stand up to the Luciferian Cabal.\par \par \uc2 Elect me Governor of Georgia, and I will bring the Satanic Regime to its knees\u8212\'20\'14 and DEMOLISH the Georgia Guidestones.\par \par \uc2 Join me in my fight to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/TearThemDown?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #TearThemDown}}}\uc2  !\par \par \uc2 Contribute: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/nvrU2idhNX"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/nvrU2idhNX}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/yoFWeNXUpM"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/yoFWeNXUpM}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kandiss Taylor (@KandissTaylor) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KandissTaylor/status/1521132865618071555?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 2, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The post earned a rebuke from fans of the late, legendary country artist \uc2 Charlie Daniels\uc2 , whose most famous song The Devil Went Down to Georgia tells the tale of of a musician winning Satan\u8217\'20\'19s golden fiddle in a play-off for his soul.\par \par \uc2 enltrMa\u8217\'20\'19am it was my understanding that Georgia had solved its devil problems with a fiddling contest.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sabretooth Nietzsche (@FeralNietzsche) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/FeralNietzsche/status/1521174685781745664?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 2, 2022}}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.realclearpolitics.com/epolls/2022/governor/Georgia.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 According to RealClearPolitics}}}\uc2 , Taylor has the support of 6% of Republican voters.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 While \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  was rallying with Brian Kemp in person on Monday night in Georgia, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  appeared on a virtual link to speak up for \uc2 David Perdue\uc2 , his choice to become Republican candidate for this fall\u8217\'20\'19s election for governor.\par \par \uc2 Perdue, Trump said in an election day statement issued Tuesday morning, complete with trademark random uppercase letters, is \u8220\'20\'1Ca Conservative fighter who isn\u8217\'20\'19t afraid of the Radical Left, and is the only candidate in Georgia who can beat Stacey \u8216\'20\'18The Hoax\u8217\'20\'19 Abrams\u8221\'20\'1D in November.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/stacey-abrams"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Abrams}}}\uc2 , who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ballotpedia.org/Georgia_gubernatorial_election,_2018"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lost to Kemp in 2018}}}\uc2 , is running unopposed for the Democratic nomination.\par \par \uc2 Repeating the lie that Kemp \u8220\'20\'1Callowed massive Election Fraud to take place\u8221\'20\'1D in Georgia in 2020, Trump insisted: \u8220\'20\'1Che can\u8217\'20\'19t win because the MAGA [make America great again] base - which is enormous - will never vote for him\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Trump went on to repeat his endorsement of former \uc2 NFL\uc2  star \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  for the Georgia Republican senate nomination, a primary race he has dominated, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.realclearpolitics.com/epolls/2022/senate/ga/2022-georgia-republican-senate-primary-7384.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to polls}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s reputation as the undisputed Republican kingmaker is on the ballot in today\u8217\'20\'19s Georgia primary, where former vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  showed up last night to twist the knife further in his old boss\u8217\'20\'19s back.\par \par \uc2 As polls opened in the party\u8217\'20\'19s primary for governor this morning, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s preferred candidate and former senator \uc2 David Perdue\uc2  trailed incumbent Brian Kemp by a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.realclearpolitics.com/epolls/2022/governor/Georgia.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 significant margin}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Pence, the once loyal deputy tipped for his own White House run in 2024, amplified his divergence from Trump by rallying for Kemp in Kennesaw on Monday night.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen you say yes to Governor Brian Kemp tomorrow, you will send a deafening message all across America that the Republican party is the party of the future,\u8221\'20\'1D Pence said in another stinging rebuke for Trump\u8217\'20\'19s backwards-looking obsession with his 2020 election defeat.\par \par \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  campaigns for Georgia governor Brian Kemp in Kennesaw on Monday. Photograph: John Amis/\uc2 EPA\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s thirst for revenge over Kemp for refusing to block \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s win in Georgia, or support the big lie that the election was stolen, became calcified in his backing of \uc2 Perdue\uc2 , but if polls prove accurate and his preferred candidate goes down, the value of the once-coveted Trump endorsement will be further eroded.\par \par \uc2 Pence is among a number of senior Republicans who are working to achieve that, however inadvertently. At a conservative conference in Florida in February, Pence said Trump was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/feb/04/mike-pence-rebukes-donald-trump-election-claims-florida"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrong to think the election could be overturned}}}\uc2 , and that to try to do so was \u8220\'20\'1Cun-American\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In Georgia, particularly, and elsewhere, other Republican Trump critics and former and current governors including \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2  of New Jersey and \uc2 Doug Ducey\uc2  of Arizona have worked to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.azcentral.com/story/opinion/op-ed/philboas/2022/05/23/doug-ducey-quietly-schemed-republican-governors-association-break-trump-grip/9892584002/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 weaken Trump\u8217\'20\'19s influence}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 According to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/05/24/us/politics/trump-endorsements-primary-elections.html?smid=url-share"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York analysis}}}\uc2  today, most of the big lie-supporting candidates he endorsed in Republican primaries for this year\u8217\'20\'19s midterms won, but many were running unopposed or against unknown or poorly funded opponents.\par \par \uc2 His record in bigger races is less convincing. Celebrity TV doctor Mehmet Oz failed to deliver a knockout blow in the Pennsylvania senate primary, and is still locked in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/may/18/primary-results-pennsylvania-senate-dr-oz-republican-trump-politics-latest-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a tight race}}}\uc2  with former treasury department official David McCormick, which is heading for a recount.\par \par \uc2 And the extremist, scandal-plagued congressman Madison Cawthorn {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/17/madison-cawthorn-chuck-edwards-congress"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was ousted}}}\uc2  in North Carolina despite Trump\u8217\'20\'19s pleas for voters to give him another chance.\par \par \uc2 My colleagues Sam Levine and Alvin Chang have taken this look at the Trump-backed, big-lie advocates running for office in several states in what many say is an alarming attack on democratic principles in the US:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/24/big-lie-candidates-election-tracker-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 'Big lie' partisans are running for office in swing states across the US}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 Primary day in Georgia and several other states\par \par \uc2 Good morning and welcome to Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s US politics blog. It\u8217\'20\'19s primary day in Georgia and a handful of other states, so buckle in: it\u8217\'20\'19s going to be an absorbing day.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s a day of reckoning, kind of, for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , when his big lie-supporting endorsee \uc2 David Perdue\uc2  takes on incumbent Brian Kemp in the long-awaited Republican primary for governor of Georgia.\par \par \uc2 Kemp became a target of the former president by refusing to block \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s victory in the state, but leads the former Georgia senator Perdue by a handy margin in many polls. And last night \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former vice-president, showed up to rally for Kemp in another rebuke for his old boss.\par \par \uc2 Defeat for Perdue would severely dent Trump\u8217\'20\'19s carefully-crafted reputation as Republican kingmaker.\par \par \uc2 Other intriguing races are taking place in Texas, where the incumbent Democratic congressman \uc2 Henry Cuellar\uc2  faces a stiff challenge from progressive Jessica Cisneros, and in Alabama, where Republican congressman and Trump loyalist Mo Brooks is seeking the party\u8217\'20\'19s Senate nomination having lost Trump\u8217\'20\'19s endorsement.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll look at some of the key races throughout the day, and have all the developments in our \u8220\'20\'1Cafter-hours\u8221\'20\'1D blog later today hosted by my colleague Joan E Greve.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else we\u8217\'20\'19re watching today:\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is heading home from Asia, where he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/23/biden-taiwan-china-strategic-ambiguity-us-foreign-policy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruffled Chinese feathers}}}\uc2  with comments on the defense of Taiwan, and met with Indo-Pacific leaders to bolster US partnerships in the region.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  stonewalled the 6 January House inquiry into \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s efforts to overturn his election defeat during lengthy testimony Friday, the \uc2 Guardian\uc2  has learned. The former president\u8217\'20\'19s personal attorney refused to discuss Republican politicians\u8217\'20\'19 involvement in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s plotting.\par \par \uc2 * New York\u8217\'20\'19s criminal inquiry into Trump\u8217\'20\'19s business dealings, meanwhile, has subpoenaed his longtime executive assistant for a deposition next week. State attorney general Letitia James plans to question \uc2 Rhona Graff\uc2  about allegedly fraudulent financial statements.\par \par \uc2 * Vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will be wearing in Alina Romanowski as ambassador to Iraq, and Deborah Lipstadt as special envoy to monitor and combat antisemitism.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220524ei5o001xi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
