\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t believe those who say ending Roe v Wade will leave society largely intact\b0\par\par\uc2 Laurence H Tribe \par \uc2 1,938 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 May 2022\par 10:44 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 If the high court adopts Alito\u8217\'20\'19s draft opinion, it will be a legal tidal wave that sweeps away a swath of rights unlike anything America has ever seen\par \par \uc2 Now that the dust has begun to settle after the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/05/02/read-justice-alito-initial-abortion-opinion-overturn-roe-v-wade-pdf-00029504"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 initial explosive news}}}\uc2  that the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  is poised to overrule the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and that Justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.documentcloud.org/documents/21835435-scotus-initial-draft"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 draft opinion}}}\uc2  in Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization represents what a majority of the court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bostonglobe.com/2022/05/03/opinion/supreme-court-abortion-opinion-could-strip-other-rights/?s_campaign=8315"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 initially voted to do}}}\uc2 , among the most revealing ways to understand the devastation the court appears ready to wreak on America\u8217\'20\'19s long march toward \u8220\'20\'1Cliberty and justice for all\u8221\'20\'1D is to examine the kinds of arguments being made in the opinion\u8217\'20\'19s defense.\par \par \uc2 The argument that such a ruling would simply {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.yahoo.com/governor-states-state-based-position-110224123.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 return a divisive issue to the people}}}\uc2  had long since been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://scholarship.law.slu.edu/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?article=1851&context=lj"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 widely dismantled}}}\uc2 . It certainly wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be returned to the people most {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usnews.com/news/best-states/alabama/articles/2022-05-04/with-abortion-in-jeopardy-minority-women-have-most-to-lose"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 profoundly affected}}}\uc2  once women were told they may have to remain pregnant despite whatever urgent reasons they might have for seeking a safe and legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It couldn\u8217\'20\'19t be described as returning the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue to the states, now that the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2022/05/09/1097614463/white-house-responds-to-protests-over-leaked-supreme-court-draft-opinion-on-roe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 possibility of a nationwide ban}}}\uc2  that the supreme court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/opinions/06pdf/05-380.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 might uphold}}}\uc2  is on the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bostonglobe.com/2022/05/03/opinion/supreme-court-abortion-opinion-could-strip-other-rights/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 horizon}}}\uc2 . And to the extent the issue is returned to the states, it would be returned to state legislatures so gerrymandered that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/05/13/opinion/overturning-roe-democracy-equality.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 they often represent the views}}}\uc2  of a distinct minority of the people anyway.\par \par \uc2 The argument that \u8220\'20\'1Conly\u8221\'20\'1D \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is involved because {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.documentcloud.org/documents/21835435-scotus-initial-draft"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alito\u8217\'20\'19s draft assures readers}}}\uc2  that the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s opinion won\u8217\'20\'19t be treated as precedent for anything that doesn\u8217\'20\'19t involve killing an unborn human is both profoundly insulting and manifestly misleading. It insults every sentient person by minimizing the significance of commandeering the bodies and lives of half the population \u8211\'20\'13 and re-inserting government power into every family. And it misleads every reader of Alito\u8217\'20\'19s words by suggesting that a court has the power to shape how future lawmakers and judges will build on its decisions and the reasoning underlying them. Alito\u8217\'20\'19s hollow promise brings to mind similar assurances in notorious cases like {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://supreme.justia.com/cases/federal/us/531/98/case.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bush v Gore}}}\uc2 , is inconsistent with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://constitution.org/1-Constitution/cmt/cardozo/jud_proc.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 how the judicial process works}}}\uc2 , and wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t offer any solace to anyone who might become pregnant or whose miscarriage might be treated as a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.motherjones.com/politics/2022/05/roe-abortion-miscarriage-crime-murder-prosecution/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 crime scene for police to investigate}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The foolishness of the argument that there\u8217\'20\'19s nothing to see here other than the future of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law is underscored by some of what is said in its support. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://podcasts.apple.com/us/podcast/the-memes-of-dobbs-leak/id1549624070?i=1000560389305"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re told}}}\uc2  not to worry about the future of decisions like {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tile.loc.gov/storage-services/service/ll/usrep/usrep388/usrep388001/usrep388001.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Loving v Virginia}}}\uc2 , ensuring the right to marry someone of a different race than your own because, after all, Justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  is in an interracial marriage. We\u8217\'20\'19re told not to worry about the right to same-sex marriage because, after all, Justice \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2  would never vote to overturn {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/opinions/14pdf/14-556_3204.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Obergefell v Hodges}}}\uc2 , the most iconic opinion written by his proud mentor, \uc2 Anthony Kennedy\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 the man who left the court only after he had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/story/2018/07/09/brett-kavanaugh-trump-private-meeting-706137"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hand-picked Kavanaugh}}}\uc2  as his successor. We\u8217\'20\'19re told not to worry about contraception (despite the way {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2022/05/19/oklahoma-abortion-ban-fertilization/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 quite a few people view Plan B or IUDs as forms of \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) because even supreme court nominees like Amy Coney Barrett, who were cagey about just how \u8220\'20\'1Csettled\u8221\'20\'1D a precedent they deemed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tile.loc.gov/storage-services/service/ll/usrep/usrep410/usrep410113/usrep410113.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2 , said they {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.judiciary.senate.gov/imo/media/doc/Barrett%20Responses%20to%20QFRs.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 couldn\u8217\'20\'19t imagine}}}\uc2  anybody today challenging {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tile.loc.gov/storage-services/service/ll/usrep/usrep381/usrep381479/usrep381479.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Griswold v Connecticut}}}\uc2 . All that prognostication is cold comfort to the millions of people whose lives are profoundly affected by these shaky predictions.\par \par \uc2 The most substantial argument is one that is equally fallacious but more sophisticated and in some ways more devious and dangerous: it is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://podcasts.apple.com/us/podcast/the-memes-of-dobbs-leak/id1549624070?i=1000560389305"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the argument}}}\uc2  that supreme court reversals of precedent, like the reversal of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.freedomforuminstitute.org/wp-content/uploads/2019/07/Plessy-v.-Ferguson.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Plessy v Ferguson}}}\uc2  by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://landmarkcases.c-span.org/pdf/Brown_Warren_Opinion.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Brown v Board of Education}}}\uc2 , are often to be welcomed as needed course corrections, and that this \u8220\'20\'1Ccourse correction\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/the-end-of-roe-v-wade-11652453609"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be the first time}}}\uc2  the supreme court has rolled back decades-old constitutional rights. The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://msmagazine.com/2022/05/05/alito-opinion-abortion-constitution-womens-rights/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 many}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://today.law.harvard.edu/harvard-law-school-professors-call-potential-abortion-rights-rollback-unprecedented/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 commentators}}}\uc2  who persisted in describing Alito\u8217\'20\'19s draft in those terms \u8211\'20\'13 as an unprecedented retreat in the arc of ever-expanding rights \u8211\'20\'13 have recently been denounced as either inexcusably ignorant or deliberately duplicitous by distinguished scholars like Yale\u8217\'20\'19s Akhil Amar, who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://podcasts.apple.com/us/podcast/the-memes-of-dobbs-leak/id1549624070?i=1000560389305"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 says}}}\uc2  that every first-year law student learns that the very same thing happened during FDR\u8217\'20\'19s second term as president, when the supreme court in 1937 in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tile.loc.gov/storage-services/service/ll/usrep/usrep300/usrep300379/usrep300379.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 West Coast Hotel v Parrish}}}\uc2  overturned a long line of decisions that had blocked minimum wage and maximum hours and other worker-protection laws in the name of employers\u8217\'20\'19 rights of \u8220\'20\'1Cprivate property\u8221\'20\'1D and the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tile.loc.gov/storage-services/service/ll/usrep/usrep198/usrep198045/usrep198045.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cliberty of contract\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 . To be sure, Amar\u8217\'20\'19s argument echoes that of the Alito draft, which cites Parrish and says, in effect, \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.documentcloud.org/documents/21835435-scotus-initial-draft"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nothing to see here}}}\uc2 , we did the same thing before\u8221\'20\'1D when we rolled back the liberty of contract line of decisions in 1937.\par \par \uc2 Justice Alito and Professor Amar are simply wrong: profoundly so. That so-called (and quite misleadingly labeled) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.history.com/news/franklin-roosevelt-tried-packing-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cswitch in time that saved the nine\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  was nothing like the switch that Dobbs would represent. The 1937 \u8220\'20\'1Cswitch\u8221\'20\'1D was no sudden politically driven turnabout but was in fact the culmination of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://scholarship.law.duke.edu/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?article=3093&context=dlj"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 long-simmering movements in legal and economic thought}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 movements that were reflected both in scholarship and in judicial opinions from the earliest days of the 20th century in places like Justice Oliver Wendell Holmes\u8217\'20\'19 dissent in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tile.loc.gov/storage-services/service/ll/usrep/usrep198/usrep198045/usrep198045.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lochner v New York}}}\uc2  insisting that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe 14th amendment does not enact Mr Herbert Spencer\u8217\'20\'19s social statics,\u8221\'20\'1D movements that represented the growing conviction that the \u8220\'20\'1Cfreedom\u8221\'20\'1D to work at low wages and in miserable conditions was an illusion lacking both moral and legal foundations and one that simply helped perpetuate economic inequality and the exploitation of relatively powerless, not-yet-unionized workers by wealthy and powerful {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.amazon.com/American-Constitutional-Law-University-Textbook/dp/0882776010/ref=sr_1_1?crid=1NTOWNXGCXM0O&keywords=9780882776019&qid=1652991986&sprefix=9780882776019%2Caps%2C38&sr=8-1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 corporations}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Indeed, it is noteworthy that West Coast Hotel v Parrish \u8211\'20\'13 the 29 March 1937 decision that is usually marked as the pivot point in the great constitutional upheaval \u8211\'20\'13 was handed down by precisely the same set of ninejustices as the nine who had rendered a decision pointing in the opposite direction less than a year earlier, on 1 June 1936, in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tile.loc.gov/storage-services/service/ll/usrep/usrep298/usrep298587/usrep298587.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Morehead v New York ex rel Tipaldo}}}\uc2 . One justice of the nine, a moderate Republican named Owen J Roberts, who had been rethinking his position on the underlying legal theories, had foreshadowed his shifting views by writing a landmark opinion upholding milk price regulation, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://supreme.justia.com/cases/federal/us/291/502/#tab-opinion-1934246"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nebbia v New York}}}\uc2 , by a 5-4 vote in 1934 \u8211\'20\'13 less than two months after the court had upheld a state mortgage moratorium law by a 5-4 vote in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.law.cornell.edu/supremecourt/text/290/398"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Home Building & Loan Ass\u8217\'20\'19n v Blaisdell}}}\uc2 , a decision clearly foreshadowing the 1937 repudiation of Lochner\u8217\'20\'19s legacy by reconceiving the meaning of the constitution\u8217\'20\'19s clause forbidding all state impairments of the obligation of contracts.\par \par \uc2 Dobbs would represent the crude payoff to a partisan political program to take over the federal judiciary\par \par \uc2 That history is important to keep in mind if one is to understand the depth of the error made by those who seek to compare the 2022 tsunami that Dobbs would represent with the gradual shift in current represented by the 1937 movement away from liberty of contract to protection of workers and consumers. The head-spinning and altogether untimely switch in the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  jurisprudence that Dobbs would represent \u8211\'20\'13 if the decision the court announces late this June or early July is in substance what the leaked Alito draft indicated it would be \u8211\'20\'13 will reflect not the steady maturation of a long-developing jurisprudential movement but the crude payoff to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/20/opinion/trump-judges-federalist-society.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a partisan political program to take over the federal judiciary}}}\uc2 , one beginning with \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s presidency and the rise of the \uc2 Federalist Society\uc2 , and advancing with supreme court appointments made by Republican presidents all of whom lost the popular vote (\uc2 George W Bush\uc2 , appointing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/GPO-CHRG-ALITO/pdf/GPO-CHRG-ALITO.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Justice Alito}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/GPO-CHRG-ROBERTS/pdf/GPO-CHRG-ROBERTS.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Chief Justice John Roberts}}}\uc2  ; Donald J Trump, appointing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CHRG-115shrg28638/pdf/CHRG-115shrg28638.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Neil Gorsuch}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CHRG-115shrg32765/pdf/CHRG-115shrg32765.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh}}}\uc2 , and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.judiciary.senate.gov/meetings/nomination-of-the-honorable-amy-coney-barrett-to-be-an-associate-justice-of-the-supreme-court-of-the-united-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Amy Coney Barrett}}}\uc2  ), and made in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/wp-content/uploads/2021/12/SCOTUS-Report-Final.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 circumstances of dubious legitimacy}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Professor Amar {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://podcasts.apple.com/us/podcast/the-memes-of-dobbs-leak/id1549624070?i=1000560389305"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 treats as laughably na\u239\'00\'EFve}}}\uc2  the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/opinions/2022/05/05/reversals-usually-expand-rights-alitos-ruling-would-deny-them/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 observation}}}\uc2  by \uc2 ACLU\uc2  national legal director and Georgetown law professor David Cole that, although \u8220\'20\'1CParrish took away some rights of business owners \u8230\'20\'26 its real effect was to expand rights protections for millions of Americans subject to exploitation by powerful corporations.\u8221\'20\'1D Amar\u8217\'20\'19s rebuttal? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://podcasts.apple.com/us/podcast/the-memes-of-dobbs-leak/id1549624070?i=1000560389305"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 He says}}}\uc2 , and I\u8217\'20\'19m serious here, that it\u8217\'20\'19d be equally legitimate to say that \u8220\'20\'1CDobbs\u8217\'20\'19 real effect would be to expand rights protection for millions of innocent, unborn Americans \u8230\'20\'26 unborn humans, subject to extermination by society.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s hard to know where to begin in unraveling that alleged parallel. Suffice it to note that the status as rights-bearing persons of embryos and fetuses {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/1104019.Abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 remains a matter of profound sectarian controversy}}}\uc2  in America and throughout the world while no such controversy attends the status as rights-bearing persons of the array of workers whose rights, at least under laws designed to limit economic exploitation if not directly under the constitution itself, were indisputably expanded by virtue of the Parrish decision and the overturning of the Lochner line of cases.\par \par \uc2 The radical change in law and society that Dobbs would represent has no parallel in the history of the supreme court\par \par \uc2 Perhaps no less important is the indisputable fact that, although there remain {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.amazon.com/Rehabilitating-Lochner-Defending-Individual-Progressive/dp/022600404X"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a few commentators}}}\uc2  who continue to think that Lochner was rightly decided and Parrish was wrong, there is a nearly universal consensus, certainly covering the ideological spectrum on the current supreme court, that the \u8220\'20\'1Crights\u8221\'20\'1D protected by Lochner and the other decisions that Parrish tossed into the dustbin of history were not constitutionally sacrosanct, and that inequalities of bargaining power prevented the common-law baseline that Lochner treated as immune to legislative modification from having any special constitutional status. At the same time, the notions of personal autonomy and bodily integrity that provide the constitutional foundation for the substantive \u8220\'20\'1Cliberty\u8221\'20\'1D at stake in cases like Roe and Casey are almost universally accepted as real, although deep disagreements remain about whether, to what degree, and from what point in fetal development the protection of the unborn fetus can properly trump that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.jstor.org/stable/2265091"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 liberty}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The upshot is that the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newyorker.com/magazine/2022/05/16/how-alitos-draft-opinion-on-abortion-rights-would-change-america"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 radical change in law and society}}}\uc2  that Dobbs would represent truly has no parallel in the history of the supreme court or in the history of the United States. As David Cole {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/opinions/2022/05/05/reversals-usually-expand-rights-alitos-ruling-would-deny-them/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 writes}}}\uc2 , the \u8220\'20\'1Cproper analogy is not Brown overruling Plessy, but a decision reviving Plessy, reversing Brown, and relegating Black people to enforced segregation after nearly 70 years of equal protection.\u8221\'20\'1D For, as Jamelle Bouie {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/05/13/opinion/overturning-roe-democracy-equality.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rightly observed}}}\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1Cequal standing is undermined and eroded when the state can effectively seize your person for its own ends \u8211\'20\'13 that is, when it can force you to give birth.\u8221\'20\'1D Whether or not one compares that compulsion and forced labor to literal enslavement, as I did in my {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.jstor.org/stable/1339866"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 1973 article}}}\uc2  on Roe v Wade, attempts to minimize the huge retrogression this would represent must be dismissed as little more than shameful efforts to camouflage the carnage the supreme court of the United States is about to unleash both on its own legitimacy and, even more important, on the people in whose name it wields the power of judicial review.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Laurence H Tribe is the Carl M Loeb University Professor of Constitutional Law Emeritus at \uc2 Harvard University\uc2 , the author of numerous books and articles, a distinguished supreme court advocate, and holder of 11 honorary degrees\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220523ei5n001gt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
