\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Could this tough-on-crime billionaire be LA\u8217\'20\'19s next mayor?\b0\par\par\uc2 Lois Beckett in Los Angeles \par \uc2 1,878 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 May 2022\par 05:01 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Rick Caruso\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s campaign is tapping into fears of rising crime and Angelenos\u8217\'20\'19 frustration with the homelessness emergency\par \par \uc2 A billionaire real estate developer has spent more than $23m on his campaign to become Los Angeles\u8217\'20\'19s next tough-on-crime mayor, and experts say his record-breaking investment is buying him a real chance at victory.\par \par \uc2 Rick Caruso\uc2 , a real estate magnate who is ranked No 261 on Forbes\u8217\'20\'19 list of richest Americans, entered the crowded race to run America\u8217\'20\'19s second largest city in February with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.latimes.com/california/story/2022-02-17/2022-la-mayoral-election-race-karen-bass-takes-lead-poll-finds"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 single-digit support}}}\uc2  and little name recognition.\par \par \uc2 Two months and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.latimes.com/california/story/2022-04-07/caruso-has-now-loaned-his-campaign-10-million"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  nearly $10m in advertising spending}}}\uc2  later, he jumped to first place, polling alongside the previous mayoral frontrunner, congresswoman Karen Bass.\par \par \uc2 Caruso has focused his campaign ahead of the 7 June primary on fears of rising crime and Angelenos\u8217\'20\'19 frustration at an ever-growing homelessness emergency, arguing that the city\u8217\'20\'19s political establishment has been putting residents at risk: \u8220\'20\'1CI see my city being torn apart because of bad decisions by leaders,\u8221\'20\'1D he said in November.\par \par \uc2 He has pledged, if elected, to hire 1,500 more police officers, and has suggested he would arrest unhoused people who refuse to move into city-run homeless shelters. \u8220\'20\'1CYou don\u8217\'20\'19t get a choice to stay on the street any more. The minute we have a bed for you, you move into the bed, or otherwise there\u8217\'20\'19s a consequence,\u8221\'20\'1D he said in an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=n-fjKDxROLY"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 early Fox News interview}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Caruso is \u8220\'20\'1Ccatching the wave\u8221\'20\'1D of some voters\u8217\'20\'19 anxieties about homelessness and crime, but \u8220\'20\'1Cthere\u8217\'20\'19s no way he would be where he was if it wasn\u8217\'20\'19t for the money,\u8221\'20\'1D said Fernando Guerra, a political scientist who has studied Los Angeles\u8217\'20\'19 electoral dynamics for decades.\par \par \uc2 The billionaire has spent more in the first months of the race than the city\u8217\'20\'19s current mayor spent during his entire campaign, Guerra said. Caruso\u8217\'20\'19s millions have translated into a flood of campaign ads, mailers and text messages targeted at different groups across the city.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf you watch TV in Los Angeles, you\u8217\'20\'19ll see [his ads] three times an hour,\u8221\'20\'1D said Adam Conover, a Los Angeles-based comedian who has become a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/adamconover/status/1525287461848420353"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 prominent critic}}}\uc2 . The ads are very effective, Conover added, \u8220\'20\'1Cgorgeously shot\u8221\'20\'1D, \u8220\'20\'1Cglossy\u8221\'20\'1D, and \u8220\'20\'1Ccompletely inescapable\u8221\'20\'1D. In them, a sun-tanned Caruso makes a simple pitch: he loves Los Angeles, and he wants to clean it up.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s pure \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Conover said.\par \par \uc2 A fortune in shopping malls\par \par \uc2 The scion of a wealthy family, Caruso made his fortune in real estate. He owns a luxury beach hotel in Montecito, California, where {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://reservations.rosewoodhotels.com/?adult=1&arrive=2022-05-19&chain=5159&child=0&config=gtm&currency=USD&depart=2022-05-20&hotel=80065&level=hotel&locale=en-US&rooms=1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rooms start at $2,000 a night}}}\uc2 . But he\u8217\'20\'19s perhaps most famous for his outdoor malls, one of which is called the Americana, and which all feature quaint trolleys, giant fountains and speakers playing a rotation of old-fashioned tunes. Caruso\u8217\'20\'19s company likes to tout that the flagship mall in Los Angeles, the Grove, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.forbes.com/sites/katiasavchuk/2016/03/18/los-angeles-developer-of-disneyland-like-open-air-malls-has-amassed-3-5-billion-fortune/?sh=2317eaed5396"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gets more daily visitors than Disneyland}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Caruso has never held public office, but over the years he has served on a series of high-profile public boards, from the department of water and power commission to the Los Angeles police commission and the \uc2 University of Southern California\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s board of trustees, which he chaired in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.latimes.com/california/story/2022-03-20/usc-freefall-la-mayoral-candidate-rick-caruso"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 midst of a sprawling campus sexual abuse scandal}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 He has received glowing, high-profile endorsements \u8211\'20\'13 from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EK1d7TPQgFg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gwyneth Paltrow}}}\uc2 , his neighbour in the posh neighbourhood of Brentwood; \uc2 Bill Bratton\uc2 , the former police chief and champion of \u8220\'20\'1Cbroken windows\u8221\'20\'1D policing; and the rapper Snoop Dogg, who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Elex_Michaelson/status/1526740948461359104"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 endorsed Caruso via a Zoom call}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 His campaign has highlighted photos of smiling Black and Latino youth who benefited from what it says is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://carusocan.com/meet-rick-caruso/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  a total of $130m in charitable giving}}}\uc2 , though his opponents instead like to put the spotlight on what they say is his \u8220\'20\'1C$100m yacht\u8221\'20\'1D, which reportedly has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.foxnews.com/real-estate/inside-super-luxurious-yacht-where-olivia-jade-was-vacationing-with-usc-pals"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nine bedrooms, a gym, a pool and an elevator}}}\uc2 . (Influencer Olivia Jade Giannulli was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tmz.com/2019/03/13/lori-loughlin-daughter-olivia-yacht-usc-board-of-trustees-rick-caruso/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on that same yacht }}}\uc2  when her mother, actor Lori Laughlin, was charged for paying $500,000 in bribes to get her daughters admitted to USC.)\par \par \uc2 Campaign spokesperson Peter Rangone would not confirm the value of the candidate\u8217\'20\'19s yacht, saying in an email: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s too bad that our opponents spend so much time on personal attacks.\u8221\'20\'1D The Caruso campaign declined to make Caruso available for an interview, or share any information about in-person campaign events a reporter could attend.\par \par \uc2 Tough-on-crime Democrat\par \par \uc2 As a real estate billionaire running for office on a law-and-order platform, Caruso has drawn plenty of critical comparisons to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . It doesn\u8217\'20\'19t help that Caruso has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.latimes.com/california/story/2022-04-15/rick-caruso-tax-returns"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 refused to release his tax returns}}}\uc2 , providing instead a summary of his finances \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.latimes.com/business/story/2022-04-18/rick-caruso-tax-disclosure-mayor-los-angeles"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 so sketchy that it\u8217\'20\'19s insulting}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D, as one \uc2 Los Angeles Times\uc2  columnist put it.\par \par \uc2 The comparison has its limits. Caruso is a lifelong Catholic, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://dailytrojan.com/2017/01/26/usc-alumnus-receives-philanthropy-award/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lauded by Pope Francis }}}\uc2  for his service to the church. He is by all accounts a profitable and detail-oriented developer, who continues to operate and fine-tune the properties he builds.\par \par \uc2 You\u8217\'20\'19ll see [his ads] three times an hour... He\u8217\'20\'19s pure \uc2 Ronald Reagan\par \par \uc2 Adam Conover, comedian\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTrump doesn\u8217\'20\'19t remotely know the real estate business like \uc2 Rick Caruso\uc2  knows the real estate business,\u8221\'20\'1D said Don Luis Camacho, a Caruso supporter and the owner of El Paseo Inn restaurant, a longtime family business based in downtown Los Angeles.\par \par \uc2 What is clear, however, is that his policies lean more conservative than those of the other Democrats running in the race. (Caruso announced he had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://spectrumnews1.com/ca/la-west/politics/2022/01/24/rick-caruso-registers-as-democrat"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 registered as a Democrat }}}\uc2  this January, after decades as an independent, and, previously, a Republican.)\par \par \uc2 His campaign says he has \u8220\'20\'1Calways been pro-choice\u8221\'20\'1D and that, with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights under threat nationwide, he plans to spend $1m to support a constitutional amendment guaranteeing the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in California. But Planned Parenthood {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.latimes.com/california/story/2022-05-03/mayor-candidate-rick-caruso-past-abortion-views"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called on him }}}\uc2  this month to apologize for previously donating \u8220\'20\'1Cnearly $1m to policymakers who put forth legislation that criminalized \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D. The Caruso Catholic Center at the \uc2 University of Southern California\uc2 , which the Caruso family {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.usc.edu/19950/New-Design-for-USC-Catholic-Center/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 donated at least $6m to build}}}\uc2 , helped {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.instagram.com/p/CY7a_HfPwzq/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lead the March for Life}}}\uc2  through the streets of Los Angeles earlier this year.\par \par \uc2 At a time when LA\u8217\'20\'19s homelessness emergency has taken on staggering proportions, with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/18/karen-bass-los-angeles-mayor-candidate-homelessness"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 at least 41,000 people unhoused,}}}\uc2  he has pledged to rid the city\u8217\'20\'19s streets of encampments. He has even {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.latimes.com/opinion/story/2022-04-29/editorial-rick-caruso-mayor-los-angeles"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  suggested}}}\uc2  that an army camp for undocumented children at the Texas border that has been the subject of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.buzzfeednews.com/article/adolfoflores/fort-bliss-immigrant-children-shelter-whistleblower"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 multiple}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cbs4local.com/news/local/whistleblower-group-renews-calls-for-safety-investigation-into-migrant-kids-at-fort-bliss"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 whistleblower }}}\uc2  reports alleging \u8220\'20\'1Cgross mismanagement, chaos and substandard conditions\u8221\'20\'1D is a good model for sheltering the unhoused.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFort Bliss is very well done. It has its own medical facilities, recreational facilities, its own cafeteria facilities. It has arts and crafts. It\u8217\'20\'19s really an amazing place,\u8221\'20\'1D Caruso said in late April, noting the camp was built in \u8220\'20\'1Cabout a month and a half\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Caruso has also been a champion of the Los Angeles police department, once working with \uc2 LAPD\uc2  to build {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.lapdonline.org/newsroom/unveiling-of-the-first-fully-staffed-koban-at-the-grove-nr16191ma/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a miniature station for \u8220\'20\'1Ccommunity-based policing\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  at the heart of his flagship mall. (It was set on fire during the \uc2 George Floyd\uc2  protests in 2020.)\par \par \uc2 Police outpost at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/TheGrove?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #TheGrove}}}\uc2  set on fire.... {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/GdN9OZClX8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/GdN9OZClX8}}}\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 Jeff Paul (@Jeff_Paul) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Jeff_Paul/status/1266915595762536448?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 31, 2020}}}\par \par \uc2 And he\u8217\'20\'19s been a critic of some criminal justice reforms designed to reverse mass incarceration. When the \uc2 Nordstrom\uc2  store at the Grove was targeted last November as part of a series of smash-and-grab robberies of high-end stores across LA, Caruso {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/losangeles/news/smash-and-grab-crimes-on-rise-state-leaders-blame-light-punishment-for-robbery/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called the robbery}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Ca manifestation of \u8216\'20\'18We\u8217\'20\'19re going to defund the cops\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D. He has blamed a measure that reduced the criminal penalty for certain thefts under $950 for driving the recent string of California luxury store thefts.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe can all agree that stealing a $900 handbag or watch shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be an offense for which someone is released from custody within hours of being arrested without consequence,\u8221\'20\'1D his campaign website notes.\par \par \uc2 He has also claimed that residents are now experiencing \u8220\'20\'1Csome of the worst crime we\u8217\'20\'19ve had in the history of Los Angeles\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cthe most violent crime\u8221\'20\'1D. Compared with 1992, when Los Angeles saw 1,094 homicides, the city is substantially safer, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://lapdonlinestrgeacc.blob.core.usgovcloudapi.net/lapdonlinemedia/2022/01/2021_crime_initiatives.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  police department data}}}\uc2 . The city\u8217\'20\'19s homicide increase over the past two years, part of a troubling national rise in killings nationwide, pushed the number of homicide victims from under 300 a year to 397. Property crimes ticked up in 2021, but were actually down compared with most of the five previous years.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPeople in LA do not feel safe, that is not fearmongering, it is stating reality,\u8221\'20\'1D Rangone, a campaign spokesperson, wrote in an email.\par \par \uc2 Any increases in crime and violence can have a big impact on people\u8217\'20\'19s sense of safety. Among last year\u8217\'20\'19s homicide victims was a beloved, well-known 81-year-old philanthropist, Jacqueline Avant, who was shot to death during a burglary of her house in Beverly Hills. \uc2 Ted Sarandos\uc2 , the CEO of \uc2 Netflix\uc2  and Avant\u8217\'20\'19s son-in-law, has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/news/politics-news/rick-caruso-los-angeles-mayor-bid-hollywood-supporters-1235098773/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 become a prominent Caruso supporter.}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Unthinkable\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Liberal Democrats have dominated Los Angeles\u8217\'20\'19 politics for so long that it would have been \u8220\'20\'1Cunthinkable\u8221\'20\'1D a year or two ago to have someone like Caruso, \u8220\'20\'1Cwho is not from that progressive coalition, on the brink of winning\u8221\'20\'1D, Guerra said.\par \par \uc2 But Caruso\u8217\'20\'19s arguments have definitely struck a chord with a much broader swath of voters. Polls this year have found that many residents are deeply concerned about homelessness and public safety and feel the city is going in the wrong direction.\par \par \uc2 Twice in the city\u8217\'20\'19s past, after uprisings against police violence towards Black residents in Watts in 1965 and in South Central and across the city in 1992, majorities of Los Angeles voters rejected a liberal Democrat to elect a Republican, pro-police mayoral candidate, Guerra said.\par \par \uc2 In the wake of intense protests in Los Angeles over the police killing of \uc2 George Floyd\uc2  in 2020, Caruso may be the latest conservative police department champion to ride a reactionary wave to the mayor\u8217\'20\'19s office.\par \par \uc2 Some of the traits that Caruso\u8217\'20\'19s more progressive opponents are attacking may actually make him seem more relatable to many Angelenos, Guerra said.\par \par \uc2 The city has the highest total number of Catholics of any US city besides New York, Guerra said, and it\u8217\'20\'19s the center of the largest Catholic diocese in the US, boasting a total of 4.3 million members across the southern California region.\par \par \uc2 For many Catholic voters, watching Caruso struggle with his stance on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , saying he\u8217\'20\'19s pro-choice and does not want Roe v Wade overturned but also funding politicians and a Catholic student center that are actively anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , may feel very familiar, Guerra said.\par \par \uc2 And while the city\u8217\'20\'19s global fame is focused on its film and TV industry, \u8220\'20\'1Cthe number one industry in Los Angeles today, 20 years ago, 50 years, ago, 100 years ago, is land development. Always has been, always will be,\u8221\'20\'1D Guerra said.\par \par \uc2 Caruso \u8220\'20\'1Ccaptures the aspirations of every single Angeleno who bought that second property and thinks they\u8217\'20\'19re going to be the next monopoly tycoon\u8221\'20\'1D, he added.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220521ei5l000e2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
