\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Oklahoma Republican-led legislature passes nation\u8217\'20\'19s strictest  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ban\b0\par\par\uc2 Jessica Glenza and agencies \par \uc2 766 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 May 2022\par 21:51 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bill bans \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at conception and if signed into law it would allow citizens to sue anyone who \u8216\'20\'18aids or abets\u8217\'20\'19 a patient\par \par \uc2 Oklahoma\u8217\'20\'19s Republican-led legislature passed the nation\u8217\'20\'19s strictest \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban on Thursday. The bill, if signed into law, would allows citizens to sue anyone, anywhere who \u8220\'20\'1Caids or abets\u8221\'20\'1D a patient in terminating a pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 The bill bans \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  from conception, even before an egg implants in the uterus, and would go into effect immediately if signed by Republican governor, \uc2 Kevin Stitt\uc2 . \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers expect he will do so before the coming week.\par \par \uc2 Like a six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban in Texas, Oklahoma\u8217\'20\'19s bill would be enforced by citizens. It would allow anyone, anywhere to sue for $10,000 and \u8220\'20\'1Cemotional distress\u8221\'20\'1D, even if they do not have a relationship to the patient in question.\par \par \uc2 Oklahoma\u8217\'20\'19s bill, \u8220\'20\'1Cis not one more ban, it is not another ban \u8211\'20\'13 it is a first,\u8221\'20\'1D said Emily Wales, interim president and CEO of Planned Parenthood Great Plains, which serves patients in Arkansas, Kansas, Missouri and Oklahoma. The law, \u8220\'20\'1Cencourages bounty hunters to sue their neighbors\u8221\'20\'1D, and is a \u8220\'20\'1Creversal of history happening before our eyes\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The bill is part of an aggressive push in Republican-led states across the country to scale back \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s outrageous, and it\u8217\'20\'19s just the latest in a series of extreme laws from around the country,\u8221\'20\'1D Vice-President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  said in reaction to the law. She said the new bans were designed to \u8220\'20\'1Cpunish and control women\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 It comes on the heels of an unprecedented {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/03/biden-democrats-reaction-codifying-roe-v-wade-reform-scotus"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 leaked draft opinion}}}\uc2  from the supreme court, which suggested a majority of conservative justices support a total reversal of Roe v Wade. The landmark decision legalized \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nearly 50 years ago and invalidated dozens of state \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans.\par \par \uc2 A final ruling in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/nov/30/explainer-mississippi-abortion-rights-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a key case}}}\uc2  from Mississippi, called Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization, is expected next month.\par \par \uc2 If the final decision does not change substantially from the leaked draft, the court would in effect return the issue of legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the states. At least {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/05/abortion-deserts-clinics-access-closed-map"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 26 states}}}\uc2  would be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/03/what-states-abortion-clinics-access-trigger-laws"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 certain or likely to ban \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 . The leaked opinion {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/14/abortion-rights-protests-us-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sparked uproar}}}\uc2  from Americans who support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, a roughly two-thirds majority according to polls, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/14/dr-tlaleng-mofokeng-roe-v-wade-reversal-un"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 human rights leaders}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Oklahoma bill promoted by Collinsville Republican representative Wendi Stearman would prohibit all abortions in the state, except to save the life of a pregnant woman or if the pregnancy is the result of rape or incest that has been reported to law enforcement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIs our goal to defend the right to life or isn\u8217\'20\'19t it?\u8221\'20\'1D Stearman asked her colleagues before the bill passed on a 73-16 vote mostly along party lines. At least one lawmaker suggested the bill did not go far enough, and suggested also banning treatment for ectopic pregnancies, a life-threatening medical condition in which an embryo implants inside the fallopian tubes. An ectopic pregnancy is never viable.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese people have no idea what they\u8217\'20\'19re talking about, and they are making laws controlling our medical practice and people\u8217\'20\'19s basic rights,\u8221\'20\'1D said Dr Iman Alsaden, medical director of Planned Parenthood Great Plains.\par \par \uc2 The bill is one of at least three \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans sent to Stitt {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/14/oklahoma-abortion-post-roe-world"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 this year}}}\uc2 . The other laws include a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/01/texas-abortion-law-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 six-week \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban}}}\uc2  and a criminal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, though the way the laws will interact is not yet known. The criminal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, set to take effect this summer if Roe falls, would make it a felony to perform an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  punishable by up to 10 years in prison, with no exceptions for rape or incest.\par \par \uc2 The lead attorney on challenges to Oklahoma\u8217\'20\'19s various \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans, Rabia Muqaddam from the \uc2 Center for Reproductive Rights\uc2 , called the legislature \u8220\'20\'1Cextraordinarily sloppy\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy understanding is the most restrictive law that takes effect latest controls, but it is extraordinarily bizarre,\u8221\'20\'1D said Muqaddam. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re challenging everything as it comes.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The laws passed by Oklahoma also have an outsized effect on women in Texas, the state which pioneered civil enforcement of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans. Oklahoma was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/apr/25/oklahoma-abortion-clinics-texas-new-bans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 briefly a haven state}}}\uc2  for Texan patients, after the supreme court allowed Texas to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at six weeks in 2021 September.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAt this point, we are preparing for the most restrictive environment politicians can create: a complete ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  with likely no exceptions,\u8221\'20\'1D said Wales. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s the worst-case scenario for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care in the state of Oklahoma,\u8221\'20\'1D she added.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220519ei5j00338\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
