\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 Republicans just nominated one of the most radical governor candidates in history\b0\par\par\uc2 Judd Legum \par \uc2 1,148 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 May 2022\par 14:44 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Doug Mastriano\uc2  may be one of the most radical candidates ever to receive a Republican nod and he has been clear that he will use that power\par \par \uc2 Pennsylvania Republicans have nominated state senator \uc2 Doug Mastriano\uc2  to be the next governor. Mastriano is one of the most radical gubernatorial candidates ever to receive a major party nomination.\par \par \uc2 Many Republicans have indulged Trump\u8217\'20\'19s claims that Democrats stole the 2020 presidential election. But few have gone as far as Mastriano has to try to justify Trump\u8217\'20\'19s fever dream.\par \par \uc2 On 25 November, Mastriano \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newyorker.com/news/us-journal/trumps-battle-to-undermine-the-vote-in-pennsylvania"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 staged a faux legal hearing}}}\uc2  in Gettysburg, in which Giuliani played prosecutor before a panel of Republican state senators and representatives\u8221\'20\'1D. Mastriano introduced a number of \u8220\'20\'1Cpoll watchers\u8221\'20\'1D who told unsubstantiated stories of \u8220\'20\'1Cphantom ballots, hacked machines, and dead voters, which they claimed had all led to an election stolen from Trump\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Five days later, after all of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s legal challenges had failed and the Pennsylvania secretary of state had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.inquirer.com/politics/election/pennsylvania-certification-2020-presidential-election-vote-20201124.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 formally certified Biden the winner}}}\uc2 , Mastriano introduced {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.legis.state.pa.us/cfdocs/billinfo/billinfo.cfm?syear=2019&sind=0&body=S&type=R&bn=410"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a resolution}}}\uc2  urging Congress to ignore the official results. His plan was for the Pennsylvania legislature to ignore millions of votes and directly appoint electors pledged to Trump.\par \par \uc2 Ultimately, Mastriano\u8217\'20\'19s resolution didn\u8217\'20\'19t go anywhere in the Republican-controlled state legislature because Pennsylvania\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic governor, \uc2 Tom Wolf\uc2 , did not yield to demands to call a special session. But Mastriano was not deterred. On 10 December 2020, Mastriano {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/DocketPDF/22/22O155/163372/20201210143813616_PA%20Senate%20Amicus%20Brief%20Main%20Document.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signed on to an amicus brief}}}\uc2  supporting Texas\u8217\'20\'19s effort to convince the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  to throw out the results in Pennsylvania and several other states. That effort also failed.\par \par \uc2 In the lead-up to 6 January 2021, Mastriano was reportedly \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://whyy.org/articles/pa-sen-doug-mastriano-subpoenaed-by-jan-6-committee/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in regular communication}}}\uc2  with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D. On the day, Mastriano was at the US Capitol and was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.witf.org/2021/05/28/pa-sen-doug-mastriano-unlikely-to-face-consequences-over-newly-released-jan-6-videos/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 captured on video}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cwalking through police lines with a crowd of people\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://senatormastriano.com/2021/05/25/mastriano-condemns-huffington-post-attack-article/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2 , Mastriano said that \u8220\'20\'1Cpolice lines did shift throughout the course of the day\u8221\'20\'1D and he \u8220\'20\'1Cfollowed those lines as they existed\u8221\'20\'1D. (In February, Mastriano was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://whyy.org/articles/pa-sen-doug-mastriano-subpoenaed-by-jan-6-committee/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 subpoenaed}}}\uc2  by the January 6 committee. It is unclear if he complied.)\par \par \uc2 In July 2021, Mastriano sent a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://senatormastriano.com/2021/07/07/op-ed-why-i-am-initiating-a-forensic-investigation-of-the-2020-general-election-and-2021-primary/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 letter}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cto several counties requesting information and materials needed to conduct a forensic investigation of the 2020 general election and the 2021 primary\u8221\'20\'1D. Mastriano\u8217\'20\'19s conduct, however, was so extreme that he was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.post-gazette.com/news/politics-state/2021/08/20/pennsylvania-2020-election-audit-forensic-investigation-fraud-investigation-pa-senator-doug-mastriano-jake-corman-cris-dush/stories/202108200090"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 removed from the process}}}\uc2  by the Republican leadership of the Pennsylvania senate. The senate president, Jake Corman, said that Mastriano was \u8220\'20\'1Conly ever interested in politics and showmanship and not actually getting things done\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 During his candidacy for governor, Mastriano has been clear that he will use his power \u8211\'20\'13 including his authority to appoint the Pennsylvania secretary of state \u8211\'20\'13 to influence the administration of future elections. He said the following on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://soundcloud.com/kelly-conner-476395918/doug-mastriano-on-the-bombeck-show-03302022/s-N8QNwv36dy6?utm_source=clipboard&utm_medium=text&utm_campaign=social_sharing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 30 March}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m \uc2 Doug Mastriano\uc2 , and I get to appoint the secretary of state who\u8217\'20\'19s delegated from me the power to make the corrections to elections, the voting logs and everything. I could decertify every machine in the state with the stroke of a pen via the secretary of state. I already had the secretary of state picked out. It\u8217\'20\'19s a world-class person that knows voting integrity better than anyone else in the nation, I think, and I already have a team that\u8217\'20\'19s gonna be built around that individual.\par \par \uc2 Yesterday, with Trump\u8217\'20\'19s endorsement, Pennsylvania Republicans put him one step closer to the governor\u8217\'20\'19s mansion.\par \par \uc2 In April, Mastriano {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.inquirer.com/politics/election/doug-mastriano-teddy-daniels-qanon-conference-gop-candidates-20220427.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spoke}}}\uc2  at a far-right Christian conference, Patriots Arise for God and Country, which was organized by \u8220\'20\'1CFrancine and Allen Fodsick, self-described prophets who have long promoted QAnon\u8221\'20\'1D, according to the Philadelphia Inquirer. At the outset of the event, organizers played a video \u8220\'20\'1Cclaiming the world is experiencing a \u8216\'20\'18great awakening\u8217\'20\'19 that will expose \u8216\'20\'18ritual child sacrifice\u8217\'20\'19 and a \u8216\'20\'18global satanic blood cult\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D. The QAnon conspiracy alleges that top Democratic officials and celebrities are Satan-worshipers running a secret child sex-trafficking ring. The video also featured allegations that 9/11 was a false flag, vaccines are \u8220\'20\'1Cgenocide therapy\u8221\'20\'1D, and Hitler faked his death.\par \par \uc2 Last year, the Fodsicks promoted Mastriano on promotional material for the event, but Mastriano said he would not attend. At the time, a spokesman said Mastriano \u8220\'20\'1Cstrongly condemns the \u8216\'20\'18Q anon\u8217\'20\'19 conspiracy theory\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cnever committed to speak at this event but sadly was used to help promote it with his picture on the invite\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Last month, Mastriano attended as a featured speaker, using his remarks to complain about the \u8220\'20\'1Cpersecution and oppression\u8221\'20\'1D he was subjected to for contesting the 2020 presidential election. The Fodsicks auctioned a portrait of Trump for $4,000 during the event, with the proceeds going to Mastriano\u8217\'20\'19s campaign. This year, his campaign did not respond to a request for comment by the Philadelphia Inquirer.\par \par \uc2 In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.paprolifecoalition.org/elections"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 31 March appearance}}}\uc2  at the PA Pro Life Coalition, Mastriano said supporters of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights wanted to \u8220\'20\'1Cwipe out\u8221\'20\'1D Black and Latino communities. He said he believed \u8220\'20\'1Cthat\u8217\'20\'19s a baby from Day 1 \u8211\'20\'13 at conception\u8221\'20\'1D. Mastriano said \u8220\'20\'1Cmy objective, of course, is to save life at conception and not play games\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In a 27 April {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.abc27.com/video/pennsylvania-republican-primary-senate-debate/7632955/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 debate}}}\uc2 , Mastriano said opposition to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is his \u8220\'20\'1CNo 1 issue\u8221\'20\'1D. The first bill he introduced in the Pennsylvania senate was a \u8220\'20\'1Cheartbeat\u8221\'20\'1D bill \u8211\'20\'13 which would ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after six weeks, before many women know they are pregnant. But Mastriano said that, as Pennsylvania\u8217\'20\'19s governor, he would \u8220\'20\'1Cwork our way\u8221\'20\'1D toward a total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban from conception. Mastriano made clear that he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/05/08/us/politics/midterms-abortion-pennsylvania.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 doesn\u8217\'20\'19t support}}}\uc2  any \u8220\'20\'1Cexceptions\u8221\'20\'1D to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans for rape, incest or life of the mother.\par \par \uc2 Mastriano\u8217\'20\'19s position on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  reflect his Christian nationalist worldview. Christian nationalism, the New Yorker {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newyorker.com/news/on-religion/a-pennsylvania-lawmaker-and-the-resurgence-of-christian-nationalism"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2 , is rooted in \u8220\'20\'1Cthe idea that God intended America to be a Christian nation\u8221\'20\'1D. During his time as a military intelligence officer in Iraq and Afghanistan he \u8220\'20\'1Cdeveloped a dim view of Islam\u8221\'20\'1D. He has frequently \u8220\'20\'1Cspread Islamophobic memes online\u8221\'20\'1D, including \u8220\'20\'1Ca conspiracy theory that \uc2 Ilhan Omar\uc2 , the Democratic congresswoman from Minnesota, directed fellow-Muslims to throw a five-year-old over a balcony\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 After retiring from the military and successfully running for office in 2019, Mastriano \u8220\'20\'1Cbegan attending events held by a movement called the New Apostolic Reformation\u8221\'20\'1D. Members of the New Apostolic Reformation believe \u8220\'20\'1Cthat God speaks to them directly, and that they have been tasked with battling real-world demons who control global leaders\u8221\'20\'1D. (Mastriano says he has not \u8220\'20\'1Cworked directly\u8221\'20\'1D with the group.)\par \par \uc2 In the legislature, Mastriano has supported a bill that \u8220\'20\'1Cwould have mandated teaching the Bible in public schools and would have made it legal for adoption agencies to discriminate against same-sex couples\u8221\'20\'1D.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Judd Legum is the founder and author of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://popular.info/subscribe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Popular Information}}}\uc2 , an independent newsletter dedicated to accountability journalism, where this post originally appeared\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220519ei5j001xm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
