\par\par \uc2 Global development\par \b \uc2 US supreme court \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  reversal would be global \u8216\'20\'18catastrophe\u8217\'20\'19 for women\b0\par\par\uc2 Lizzy Davies \par \uc2 899 \uc2 words\par \uc2 18 May 2022\par 06:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 If Roe v Wade is overturned, it will encourage anti-choice groups \u8211\'20\'13 particularly in the developing world, activists warn\par \par \uc2 The probable demise of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a federal right in the US will be a \u8220\'20\'1Ccatastrophe\u8221\'20\'1D for women in low and middle-income countries, with an emboldened anti-choice movement likely to raise renewed pressure on hard-won gains, doctors and activists have warned.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/05/02/supreme-court-abortion-draft-opinion-00029473"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 leak this month}}}\uc2  of the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s draft majority opinion, which argued that the 1973 ruling effectively legalising \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been \u8220\'20\'1Cegregiously wrong from the start\u8221\'20\'1D, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/03/supreme-court-roe-v-wade-draft-abortion-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stunned and enraged}}}\uc2  many in America.\par \par \uc2 But those shock waves did not stop at the borders of the US, as pro-choice figures around the world \u8211\'20\'13 many in countries with restrictive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws and high levels of social stigma around reproductive rights \u8211\'20\'13 warned that Justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s words would \u8220\'20\'1Csend a really clear message\u8221\'20\'1D of inspiration to anti-choice groups.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m sure the pro-life or anti-choice movement in [Uganda] must be hoping and praying that the Roe v Wade legislation be overturned. I\u8217\'20\'19m sure if that succeeds, it will be the biggest achievement the anti-choice movement [has] registered. I\u8217\'20\'19m sure they will use it significantly to counter the work and the gains we thought we had registered,\u8221\'20\'1D said Kenneth Buyinza, a Kampala-based doctor.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Uganda {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/fact-sheet/abortion-and-postabortion-care-uganda"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is legal in certain circumstances}}}\uc2  but highly restricted and dogged by stigma and misinformation. A ministry of health report in 2010 attributed about 8% of the country\u8217\'20\'19s maternal deaths to unsafe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 It is far from the only country in sub-Saharan Africa to see a strong link between stubbornly high levels of maternal mortality and unsafe abortions carried out by unlicensed practitioners, often in unsanitary conditions and without the proper equipment.\par \par \uc2 In such countries, the potential for the US move to encourage anti-choice politicians, judges and activists and further hold back \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights could not be more worrying.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf Roe v Wade is reversed it would be a victory for anti-choice groups who finance the opposition in Africa and a catastrophe for us. It could influence policymakers and mean that in Africa we will keep seeing women dying. Whatever we have gained could be lost,\u8221\'20\'1D said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://et.linkedin.com/in/abebe-shibru-813a33a?original_referer=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.google.com%2F"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Abebe Shibru}}}\uc2 , Ethiopia country director for MSI Reproductive Choices.\par \par \uc2 Another region where {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2022/may/06/samuel-alito-profile-abortion-supreme-court-justice"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alito\u8217\'20\'19s words}}}\uc2  have caused alarm is Central America, where three countries have total bans on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 : El Salvador, Honduras and Nicaragua. In another, Guatemala, lawmakers recently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/mar/09/guatemala-abortion-punishment-bans-same-sex-marriage"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 increased prison sentences}}}\uc2  for women found to have had an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , legal only if the mother\u8217\'20\'19s life is at risk.\par \par \uc2 Eugenia L\u243\'00\'F3pez Uribe, regional director for the \uc2 International Planned Parenthood Federation\uc2 , warned the US move would inspire anti-choice policymakers in countries such as Guatemala.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey can see that if they change the laws and they go against women\u8217\'20\'19s rights, they can do it without any consequence,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CThe sign they are giving now is that women\u8217\'20\'19s rights can be on the table for negotiations. So this is very worrisome.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Sarah Shaw, head of advocacy at MSI, said the potential for legislative backsliding was clear. \u8220\'20\'1CA lot of the countries in which we work that have less restrictive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws are probably a little bit ahead of where the country is socially. So they are very, very fragile. So it\u8217\'20\'19s not going to take much to undermine them, overturn them,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 In recent years US funding has been essential to the anti-choice movement globally, and Shaw said she feared the overturning of Roe would prompt a surge in the flow of money. In countries where corruption is rife and political systems are vulnerable to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.opendemocracy.net/en/5050/us-rightwing-mississippi-abortion/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cdark money\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  lobbying, the impact could be sizeable.\par \par \uc2 The other major concern was that in countries heavily dependent on US aid for public health programmes the move could have a \u8220\'20\'1Cchilling effect\u8221\'20\'1D on African governments\u8217\'20\'19 commitment to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provision and other reproductive rights, making them \u8220\'20\'1Cthink twice about what they spend money on\u8221\'20\'1D, said Shaw.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf there\u8217\'20\'19s a chilling on prioritisation and funding for services that are already massively deprioritised and massively underfunded it\u8217\'20\'19s going to be catastrophic,\u8221\'20\'1D she added.\par \par \uc2 Buyinza, who also works at the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/Uganda-Family-Planning-Consortium-101283301513349/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Uganda family planning consortium}}}\uc2 , said he worried the move could affect \u8220\'20\'1Cfundraising and resource allocations to maternal and child health interventions\u8221\'20\'1D. He added that in Uganda \u8211\'20\'13 perhaps {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/10/divided-america-roe-v-wade-supreme-court-cold-civil-war"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 as in the US}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 anti-choice forces would be unlikely to stop at \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , broadening their attacks on other areas such as LGBT+ rights.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C[By] taking this kind of action, [the US] is actually holding the flag very high now for countries that are still struggling with human rights issues, like, for instance, Uganda, but many other countries. There is no doubt that having this legislation overturned is going to have a significant bearing, [and] most likely it is going to be negative,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/05/02/supreme-court-abortion-draft-opinion-00029473"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 his draft opinion}}}\uc2  laying out why Roe should fall, Alito concluded that the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was \u8220\'20\'1Cnot deeply rooted in the nation\u8217\'20\'19s history and traditions\u8221\'20\'1D. Such reasoning was deeply problematic, warned Buyinza.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSomeone might be looking at \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in isolation, but \u8230\'20\'26 there are so many things that are not \u8230\'20\'26 rooted in Ugandan and African \u8216\'20\'18traditions and history\u8217\'20\'19. And that goes beyond just \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220518ei5i000p6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
