\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18We need to stand up\u8217\'20\'19: Democrats criticized for inaction on  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 Joan E Greve \par \uc2 1,426 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 May 2022\par 08:05 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Even as Democrats have denounced the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s leaked \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opinion, their efforts at the federal level have failed to live up to their rhetoric\par \par \uc2 Shortly after the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/02/roe-v-wade-abortion-supreme-court-draft-opinion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 draft supreme court opinion}}}\uc2  overturning Roe v Wade was leaked to the public, California\u8217\'20\'19s governor, \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 , condemned conservative attacks on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and pledged that his state would be a \u8220\'20\'1Csanctuary\u8221\'20\'1D for those seeking to end a pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 But Newsom also directed some of his most pointed remarks toward fellow Democrats.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhere the hell is my party? Where\u8217\'20\'19s the Democratic party?\u8221\'20\'1D Newsom said. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a concerted, coordinated effort, and yes, they\u8217\'20\'19re winning. They are. They have been. Let\u8217\'20\'19s acknowledge that. We need to stand up. Where\u8217\'20\'19s the counter-offensive?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Even as Democrats have denounced the court\u8217\'20\'19s provisional decision to overturn Roe and vowed to defend \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, their efforts at the federal level have largely failed to live up to their rhetoric. A vote last Wednesday in the Senate to codify Roe and protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights nationwide was once again blocked, as Democrat Joe Manchin joined all 50 Republican senators in opposing the bill.\par \par \uc2 The failure of Democrats in Washington to shore up \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, even as they control the White House and both chambers of Congress, has complicated the party\u8217\'20\'19s messaging to voters about the likely end of Roe. Some frustrated Democrats are instead turning their attention to state and local policies that could protect reproductive rights even if Roe falls.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters\u8217\'20\'19 frustration with Democratic inaction at the federal level has been on display since the draft opinion leaked earlier this month. At a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/05/democrats-voters-senate-midterm-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 protest outside the supreme court}}}\uc2  last week, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights demonstrators chanted: \u8220\'20\'1CDo something, Democrats.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Progressive\uc2  members of Congress have also argued for the urgent need to pass federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights legislation, calling on senators to amend the filibuster to get a bill approved.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPeople elected Democrats precisely so we could lead in perilous moments like these - to codify Roe, hold corruption accountable, [and] have a President who uses his legal authority to break through Congressional gridlock on items from student debt to climate,\u8221\'20\'1D progressive congresswoman \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2  said on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The stakes of Democratic inaction are high, as \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is certain or likely to be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/04/us-supreme-court-abortion-explainer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 outlawed in 26 states}}}\uc2  if the court follows through with overturning Roe. Last weekend, the Senate minority leader, \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , warned that Republicans may go even further if they regain control of the White House and Congress, floating the idea of a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/politics/2022/05/06/gop-avoids-abortion-ahead-potential-scotus-ruling-overturn-roe/9631996002/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 national \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Republicans would probably face widespread public outcry if they advanced a nationwide ban. A poll released by \uc2 Monmouth University\uc2  last week found that just 9% of Americans support the idea of a national ban, while 64% support keeping \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legal. However, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights advocates warn that the threat of a nationwide ban will be real if Republicans take back Congress and the White House.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRepublicans are definitely passing a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban once they have the power to do it,\u8221\'20\'1D said Shaunna Thomas, co-founder and executive director of the reproductive rights group UltraViolet. \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19ve been signaling they were going to pack the supreme court in order to overturn Roe. I don\u8217\'20\'19t think people took them seriously enough. And so people really need to learn the lesson here and take them very, very seriously on this point.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Progressive groups like UltraViolet have called on Democrats to amend the Senate filibuster, which would allow a bill codifying Roe to get through the upper chamber with a simple majority of support. But Manchin and fellow Democrat \uc2 Kyrsten Sinema\uc2  have made it clear they will not support a filibuster carve-out, and the vote last Wednesday failed to even attract the 50 votes that would be necessary if the Senate rules were changed.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has to be more important than their loyalty to arcane Senate procedures that are not even laws,\u8221\'20\'1D Thomas said. \u8220\'20\'1CPeople watched them carve the filibuster out to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/oct/07/debt-ceiling-deal-senate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 raise the debt ceiling}}}\uc2 . If they can do it for that, they should be able to do it for this.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Democratic congressional leaders have encouraged members of their party to direct their criticism toward Republicans rather than each other. In a \u8220\'20\'1CDear colleague\u8221\'20\'1D letter to House Democrats last week, the House speaker, \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , warned of Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 wish for a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban and said their policies could even \u8220\'20\'1Ccriminalize contraceptive care, in vitro fertilization and post-miscarriage care\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMake no mistake: once Republicans have dispensed with precedent and privacy in overturning Roe, they will take aim at additional basic human rights,\u8221\'20\'1D Pelosi said.\par \par \uc2 Christina Reynolds, vice-president of communications at Emily\u8217\'20\'19s List, which promotes pro-choice female candidates for office, insisted that voters who support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights will know to hold Republicans accountable in the midterm elections this November. \u8220\'20\'1CRepublicans have gotten us here in a large number of ways,\u8221\'20\'1D Reynolds said.\par \par \uc2 But Democratic candidates running for office this fall will have to paint a longer-term picture of how the party plans to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, even if they cannot prevent the court from overturning Roe.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Democratic party has to move away from this message about how we can fix everything right away,\u8221\'20\'1D said Kelly Dietrich, CEO of the National Democratic Training Committee. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a lifetime struggle. Government is hard. We will need you to vote this November, next November and every November after that because the people who want to take away your rights aren\u8217\'20\'19t going to stop.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In the meantime, Democrats have an opportunity to turn their attention to the state and local offices that may be able to help protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights if Roe falls, Dietrich argued.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe fight for the next 10-plus years is going to be at the state and local levels,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s going to be in the state legislatures. It\u8217\'20\'19s going to be in the city councils and at all the different local government forums we have around the country that aren\u8217\'20\'19t big and sexy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Some of those efforts are already under way across the country.\par \par \uc2 In Michigan, where a 1931 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban is still on the books and could go back into effect if Roe is overturned, the Democratic governor, \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2 , has filed a lawsuit to block implementation of the law. Several county prosecutors also signed on to a statement saying they would not pursue criminal charges in connection to the 1931 law.\par \par \uc2 One of those prosecutors was Democrat Karen McDonald in Oakland county, the second-largest county in Michigan. She said that, despite her despair over the likely end of Roe, she was committed to finding ways to ensure her neighbors\u8217\'20\'19 rights and healthcare access.\par \par \uc2 This is really turning politics on its head\par \par \uc2 Karen McDonald\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is a sad, tragic moment,\u8221\'20\'1D McDonald said. \u8220\'20\'1CBut I am not going to spend one minute of my energy letting that tear me away from what I think is absolutely critical right now, which is we all need to pay attention and support and fund and help elect [those candidates] who want to protect our right to choose.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Oakland county was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2020/10/30/us/politics/oakland-county-michigan-democrats.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 once a Republican stronghold}}}\uc2 , but it has become increasingly Democratic in recent years. McDonald said she has heard from members of her community who previously supported Republicans and are now rethinking their politics in light of the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s expected decision.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI know a lot of women who voted for Trump and are now saying I will never, ever ever, vote for a pro-life candidate. They just didn\u8217\'20\'19t think it would happen,\u8221\'20\'1D McDonald said. \u8220\'20\'1CSo I think this is really turning politics on its head.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Thomas agreed that many Americans who support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights seem to have been taken aback by the provisional decision to overturn Roe, even after Republicans obtained a 6-3 majority on the court. Conservatives have also been calling for the end of Roe for decades, and Trump promised to nominate anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  justices to the supreme court.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think it\u8217\'20\'19s surprising that people had to see it to believe it, despite having heard this, particularly from Black and brown women who have been bearing the brunt of these attacks at the state level for a long time,\u8221\'20\'1D Thomas said. \u8220\'20\'1CAs an organizer, I will tell you, it\u8217\'20\'19s never too late to join the fight. And the time is really now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220517ei5h000xg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
