\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18We will not go back\u8217\'20\'19: thousands rally for  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights across the US\b0\par\par\uc2 Oliver Milman and Victoria Bekiempis in New York and Dani Anguiano in Los Angeles \par \uc2 1,402 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 May 2022\par 14:47 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 More than 300 pro-choice protests organized around US against expected reversal of 1973 landmark law that made \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legalNationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights protest \u8211\'20\'13 follow live\par \par \uc2 Thousands of people were taking part in protests across the US on Saturday to decry the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s expected reversal of the landmark 1973 law that made \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legal in America.\par \par \uc2 Organizers said there were more than 380 protest events in cities including major demonstrations in Washington DC, New York City, Los Angeles and Chicago to demand that the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not stripped away by the court, which is dominated by rightwing justices.\par \par \uc2 Gathering in large groups and holding signs that included slogans such as \u8220\'20\'1CReproductive justice for all\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1CWe will not go back\u8221\'20\'1D, and chanting \u8220\'20\'1CMy body, my choice\u8221\'20\'1D, the protesters have been spurred by the leak of a supreme court draft opinion on 2 May. The leaked draft showed that the five rightwing justices on the nine-member court had voted to overturn Roe v Wade, the historic case that provided federal protection for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and proved a beacon in international efforts to improve the rights of women.\par \par \uc2 In the US capital, protesters gathered at the Washington Monument before marching to the supreme court, which is surrounded by a security fence. Some held pictures of coat hangers to symbolize the dangerous measures some people resorted to for illegal abortions prior to the Roe v Wade ruling. \u8220\'20\'1CIf it\u8217\'20\'19s a fight they want, it\u8217\'20\'19s a fight they\u8217\'20\'19ll get,\u8221\'20\'1D said Rachel Carmona, executive director of the Women\u8217\'20\'19s March, one of the groups, along with \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2 , UltraViolet and MoveOn that organized Saturday\u8217\'20\'19s demonstrations, which they called \u8220\'20\'1CBans Off Our Bodies\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have to see an end to the attacks on our bodies,\u8221\'20\'1D Carmona added. \u8220\'20\'1CYou can expect for women to be completely ungovernable until this government starts to work for us.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 If the court were to end protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  following the challenge brought by Mississippi, at least {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/03/what-states-abortion-clinics-access-trigger-laws"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 26 US states, mostly in the south and midwest, would be certain or likely to outlaw \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 , forcing women to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/05/abortion-deserts-clinics-access-closed-map"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 travel hundreds of miles to the nearest clinic}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/07/abortion-pill-at-home-activists-future-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 self-manage abortions with medication}}}\uc2  and heighten the risk of prosecution, abuse and violence for women and doctors.\par \par \uc2 Even though a clear majority of Americans support in principle women\u8217\'20\'19s right to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the topic has long been a politically toxic one, with Republicans persistently pushing for the protections to be weakened or scrapped entirely.\par \par \uc2 Oklahoma and Texas, both Republican-led states, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/14/oklahoma-abortion-post-roe-world"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have established bans on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  after six weeks, while lawmakers in Louisiana recently mulled a bill that would charge women with murder should they end their pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Protest organizers stressed that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains legal until the final supreme court decision. \u8220\'20\'1CPlanned Parenthood health centers remain open, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is currently still legal, and we will continue to fight like hell to protect the right to access safe, legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Alexis McGill Johnson\uc2 , chief executive of of \uc2 Planned Parenthood Federation of America\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But people at the protests spoke of their alarm over the prospect of losing a right that women have relied upon for the past 50 years. \u8220\'20\'1CHow can they take away what I feel is a human right from us?\u8221\'20\'1D said Julie Kinsella, a teacher who took part in the New York protest. Kinsella said she felt \u8220\'20\'1Canger\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Coutrage\u8221\'20\'1D when she heard the news of the draft opinion.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt just made me think: what direction is the US moving toward with that decision?\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe have made so much progress up until this point. I would just hate to see us backtrack and fight for what we already have right now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Other women shared their own experiences of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Teisha Kimmons, who traveled 80 miles to attend the Chicago rally, said she feared for women in states that are ready to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . She said she might not be alive today if she had not had a legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  when she was 15.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI was already starting to self-harm and I would have rather died than have a baby,\u8221\'20\'1D said Kimmons, a massage therapist from Rockford, Illinois.\par \par \uc2 At the rally in Los Angeles, Gloria Allred, the women\u8217\'20\'19s rights lawyer, shared the story of how she had an illegal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in California in the 1960s, before Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI was left in a bathtub in a pool of my own blood,\u8221\'20\'1D Allred said. \u8220\'20\'1CA nurse said to me, \u8216\'20\'18I hope this teaches you a lesson.\u8217\'20\'19 It did teach me a lesson, but not the one she wanted. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  must be safe, it must be legal, it must be affordable, it must be available.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Barbara Lee, a Democratic member of Congress, also told the Los Angeles crowd of her own pre-Roe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which happened when she was a teenager. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re here today to tell these radical extremists that if you criminalize people for having an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , if you make \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  illegal, if you take away our rights to make our personal decisions about our bodies, we will see you at the ballot box in November,\u8221\'20\'1D Lee said.\par \par \uc2 Elijah Lopez, 15, stood side by side with his mother, Lidia, at the rally carrying a sign that said: \u8220\'20\'1CMy mom is pissed.\u8221\'20\'1D Lidia\u8217\'20\'19s sign read: \u8220\'20\'1CYeah, I\u8217\'20\'19m pissed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday is an important day in history,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, referring to the rallies taking place across the US. \u8220\'20\'1CI was telling my son even though California is likely to maintain reproductive rights, in many other states that\u8217\'20\'19s not going to be the case.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe can show them that people don\u8217\'20\'19t want this,\u8221\'20\'1D Elijah said.\par \par \uc2 They came from the Inland Empire to advocate for reproductive rights together, part of a shared tradition of activism that began years ago when they started demonstrating against family separation under the Trump administration, which Lidia said was her son\u8217\'20\'19s introduction to peaceful protest.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s easy to just not do anything. We have to take as many opportunities as we can to show up. I want him to be here,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Saturday\u8217\'20\'19s rally brought out many people who had never attended such protests before but were called to action seeing reproductive rights in jeopardy. Reginald Wheeler, a lifelong Los Angeles resident, said the event downtown marked his first protest.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI support women,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CI would hope this is a reality check for those judges.\u8221\'20\'1D He added that he worries about what will happen when people don\u8217\'20\'19t have access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re gonna have a lot of unwanted children, children suffering from homelessness.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Luna Hernandez with Rise Up 4 \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Rights, an organizer of the rally, said the event would get people into the streets to stop the supreme court from taking away reproductive rights.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COnly the people can stop this,\u8221\'20\'1D Hernandez said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe have to refuse to allow this. This has to be a turning point, it\u8217\'20\'19s not a done deal.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is illegal, women die. Forced motherhood is female enslavement,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 The prospect of looming bans on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in dozens of US states has provoked international, as well as domestic alarm. On Saturday, Dr Tlaleng Mofokeng, the United Nations special rapporteur on the right to health, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/14/dr-tlaleng-mofokeng-roe-v-wade-reversal-un"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the Guardian}}}\uc2  that the US should not drop federal protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt sends chills down my spine to think that the court is being brought on to play \u8211\'20\'13 as a very powerful player \u8211\'20\'13 to decide on an issue of human rights that has jurisprudence, and has a basis in legal findings, that will actually lead to restriction of rights,\u8221\'20\'1D said Mofokeng.\par \par \uc2 The primary concern of \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 , however, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2022/may/14/clarence-thomas-supreme-court-leak-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appears to be the leak itself}}}\uc2 . Thomas, a conservative supreme justice, said the release of the draft opinion to Politico was \u8220\'20\'1Ctremendously bad\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The judge, whose wife Virginia repeatedly urged \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s chief of staff to take steps to overturn the 2020 election won by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , told a conference in Dallas: \u8220\'20\'1CI wonder how long we\u8217\'20\'19re going to have these institutions at the rate we\u8217\'20\'19re undermining them. And then I wonder when they\u8217\'20\'19re gone or destabilized, what we\u8217\'20\'19re going to have as a country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220514ei5e001uq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
