\par\par \uc2 Law\par \b \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 : supreme court \u8216\'20\'18dangerous to families and to freedoms\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Richard Luscombe \par \uc2 607 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 May 2022\par 13:53 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 House speaker rails against conservative judges appointed by Trump as justices prepare to finalize draft \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ruling\par \par \uc2 The supreme court is \u8220\'20\'1Cdangerous to families and to freedoms in our country\u8221\'20\'1D, \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  said on Sunday, as justices prepare to finalize a draft ruling {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/03/biden-democrats-reaction-codifying-roe-v-wade-reform-scotus"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stripping almost half a century of \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights}}}\uc2  in the US.\par \par \uc2 The House speaker railed against conservative judges appointed by former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in an interview on CNN\u8217\'20\'19s State of the Union, in which she urged Democrats to keep their \u8220\'20\'1Ceye on the ball\u8221\'20\'1D to protect other freedoms she sees as under threat.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBeware in terms of marriage equality, beware in terms of other aspects,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUnderstand this. This is not just about terminating a pregnancy. This is about contraception, family planning.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a place where freedom and the kitchen table, issues of America\u8217\'20\'19s families, come together. What are the decisions that a family makes? What about contraception for young people? It\u8217\'20\'19s beyond just a particular situation. It\u8217\'20\'19s massive in terms of contraception, in vitro fertilization, a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to decide.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Speaking the day after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/14/abortion-rights-protests-us-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hundreds of protest events}}}\uc2  took place nationwide, Pelosi insisted Democrats had done what they could in terms of protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights through legislation. She pointed out the House had passed a bill before the Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Protection Act {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/11/senate-abortion-rights-bill-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 failed in the Senate on Wednesday}}}\uc2 , and she said she was still optimistic of a resolution with the support of pro-choice Republicans.\par \par \uc2 But she said the 60-vote requirement in the Senate was \u8220\'20\'1Can obstacle to many good things\u8221\'20\'1D, and that Democrats needed to rally ahead of November\u8217\'20\'19s midterm elections to \u8220\'20\'1Cget rid of the damage\u8221\'20\'1D caused by conservative justices, including Trump\u8217\'20\'19s three appointments, \uc2 Neil Gorsuch\uc2 , \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2  and Amy Coney Barrett.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhoever suspected a creature like \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  would become president, waving a list of judges he would appoint, therefore getting the support of the far right and appointing those anti-freedom justices to the court?\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is not about a long game. We played a long game, we won Roe v Wade a long time ago, we voted to protect it over time. Let\u8217\'20\'19s not take our eye off the ball. The ball is this court, which is dangerous to families, to freedoms in our country.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe genius of our founders was to have a constitution that enabled freedom to expand. This is the first time the court has taken back a freedom that was defined by precedent and respect for privacy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The independent Vermont senator Bernie Sanders, on NBC\u8217\'20\'19s Meet the Press, said he remained hopeful that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights legislation could be resurrected before the midterms.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNobody should think this process is dead. We should bring those bills up again, and again and again,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPeople cannot believe you have a supreme court and Republicans who are prepared to overturn 50 years of precedent. What we should do is on this bill end the filibuster, do everything that we can to get 50 votes on the strongest possible bill to protect a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to control her own body.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 An NBC News poll conducted after the leak of a draft opinion and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2022-election/support-abortion-rights-hits-new-high-midterm-outlook-stays-mostly-unc-rcna28869"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported by the network on Sunday}}}\uc2  showed six out of 10 voters were in favor of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, and that 52% of voters were \u8220\'20\'1Cless likely\u8221\'20\'1D to support a candidate who backed the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s draft ruling.\par \par \uc2 But the poll found that inflation and the economy remained the biggest concerns for voters as the midterms approach.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220515ei5f001s1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
