\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  rights: how a governor\u8217\'20\'19s veto can protect women\u8217\'20\'19s freedoms\b0\par\par\uc2 Joan E Greve in Washington \par \uc2 1,356 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 May 2022\par 07:01 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The likely end of Roe has raised the stakes in gubernatorial races with candidates stressing on the urgency of the moment\par \par \uc2 If the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  follows through with its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/02/roe-v-wade-abortion-supreme-court-draft-opinion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 initial decision}}}\uc2  to overturn Roe v Wade next month, 26 states are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/04/us-supreme-court-abortion-explainer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 certain or likely}}}\uc2  to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . For those who want to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, a governor\u8217\'20\'19s veto pen is about to become all the more powerful.\par \par \uc2 The probable end of Roe has raised the stakes in gubernatorial races across the country, particularly in states with Republican-led legislatures that would probably move to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  unless a Democratic governor steps in.\par \par \uc2 Democratic gubernatorial candidates are now stressing the urgency of the moment to voters, portraying themselves as the last line of defense against an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban in their states.\par \par \uc2 Four states with Republican-controlled legislatures and Democratic governors \u8211\'20\'13 Kansas, Michigan, Pennsylvania and Wisconsin \u8211\'20\'13 are holding gubernatorial races in November. Democrats are also paying close attention to gubernatorial elections in battleground states where Republicans currently control both the governor\u8217\'20\'19s mansion and the state legislature, such as Georgia and Arizona.\par \par \uc2 If the supreme court overturns Roe and Republicans have full control of the state government, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans in those states will become all but certain. Some of the toss-up states holding gubernatorial races this year \u8211\'20\'13 including Michigan, Wisconsin and Arizona \u8211\'20\'13 already have \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans on the books that predate Roe, and Republicans have called for their enforcement if the court reverses the landmark case.\par \par \uc2 In Kansas and Pennsylvania, the sitting Democratic governors have both previously vetoed bills restricting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, and those proposals would probably be enacted if a Republican took control.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe leaked draft opinion overturning Roe v Wade makes one thing clear \u8211\'20\'13 the future of reproductive rights will be defined at the state level,\u8221\'20\'1D said Christina Amestoy, senior communications advisor for the \uc2 Democratic Governors Association\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CWho sits in the governor\u8217\'20\'19s office will determine a woman\u8217\'20\'19s ability to access \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Since the court\u8217\'20\'19s draft opinion was made public, Republican gubernatorial candidates\u8217\'20\'19 views on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  have come under renewed scrutiny. In Pennsylvania, all four leading Republican gubernatorial candidates have indicated they would support some form of an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. State senator \uc2 Doug Mastriano\uc2 , who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.realclearpolitics.com/epolls/2022/governor/pa/pennsylvania-governor-republican-primary-7345.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 now leads in polls}}}\uc2  ahead of the Tuesday primary, said at a recent debate that he would oppose any exceptions to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, such as for rape, incest or the safety of the mother.\par \par \uc2 Josh Shapiro, the presumptive Democratic gubernatorial nominee in Pennsylvania, has already cut {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://adm0.page.link/RQN2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an attack ad}}}\uc2  warning that Mastriano \u8220\'20\'1Cwants to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D if elected.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEvery one of our opponents has made it clear: they would sign a bill banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and taking away a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to choose,\u8221\'20\'1D said Shapiro\u8217\'20\'19s spokesperson, Manuel Bonder. \u8220\'20\'1CWith DC failing to protect these rights, Josh Shapiro will stand up and fight to ensure Pennsylvania remains a place where everyone has the freedom to start a family how and when they want to.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A bill to restrict a woman's right to choose will land on the desk of our next Governor, and if one of my GOP opponents wins, they'll sign it into law.\par \par \uc2 I'll veto it.\par \par \uc2 I am the only candidate for Governor who would make that choice. That's a fact.\u8212\'20\'14 Josh Shapiro (@JoshShapiroPA) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JoshShapiroPA/status/1524043003878334467?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 10, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Katie Hobbs\uc2 , a Democrat running for governor in Arizona, has similarly promised that she will use her veto pen to block \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions, while also calling for a repeal of the state\u8217\'20\'19s 1901 law that criminalizes administering the procedure.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI will do everything in my power to protect Arizonans\u8217\'20\'19 fundamental freedoms and access to reproductive healthcare, and use my veto power to strike down anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  measures that come across my desk,\u8221\'20\'1D Hobbs said after the draft opinion leaked.\par \par \uc2 And Democratic gubernatorial candidates are not simply waiting until election day to take action for the potential end of Roe. \uc2 Stacey Abrams\uc2 , the voting rights leader running for governor of Georgia, temporarily paused fundraising for her campaign earlier this month to instead raise money for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights groups.\par \par \uc2 In Michigan, the Democratic governor, \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2 , has filed a lawsuit to block implementation of a 1931 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban that does not allow for exceptions related to rape or incest. Whitmer has also asked the Michigan supreme court to recognize the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access under the state\u8217\'20\'19s constitution.\par \par \uc2 The leaked draft opinion overturning Roe v Wade makes one thing clear \u8211\'20\'13 the future of reproductive rights will be defined at the state level\par \par \uc2 Christina Amestoy\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/05/09/opinion/taking-the-fight-for-safe-legal-abortion-to-the-states.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 her New York Times op-ed}}}\uc2  published last week, Whitmer warned that it would be nearly impossible to repeal the 1931 ban with Republicans controlling the Michigan legislature, and she underscored the need for Democrats to use every tool at their disposal to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe can all sense the hopelessness and despair that tens of millions of American women \u8211\'20\'13 our neighbors, family members and friends \u8211\'20\'13 are feeling,\u8221\'20\'1D Whitmer said. \u8220\'20\'1CBut despair is a choice, and pessimism is a luxury. We must take unprecedented steps to protect the right to choose.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The likely end of Roe has also started to affect some gubernatorial primaries, as candidates use their views on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to distinguish themselves from their opponents. \uc2 David Perdue\uc2 , the Trump-backed gubernatorial candidate in Georgia, has called on the sitting Republican governor, Brian Kemp, to call the state legislature back for an emergency session to pass an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban if Roe is overturned.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGeorgia voters deserve to know where their governor stands on this issue,\u8221\'20\'1D Perdue said after the draft opinion leaked. \u8220\'20\'1CYou are either going to fight for the sanctity of life or you\u8217\'20\'19re not.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But for the most part, Republicans have tried to downplay how much the end of Roe would affect the midterm elections. \u8220\'20\'1CReminder for those wondering about the politics of the leaked \uc2 Scotus\uc2  opinion, \uc2 Terry McAuliffe\uc2  spent all fall trying to make \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  THE central issue in the Virginia gov race,\u8221\'20\'1D Jesse Hunt, communications director for the \uc2 Republican Governors Association\uc2 , said earlier this month. \u8220\'20\'1CHe lost by 2% in a state Biden won by 10%.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Reminder for those wondering about the politics of the leaked \uc2 SCOTUS\uc2  opinion: \uc2 Terry McAuliffe\uc2  spent all fall trying to make \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  THE central issue in the VA Gov race\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 He lost by 2% in a state Biden won by 10% {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/vNEftItbYW"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/vNEftItbYW}}}\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 Jesse Hunt (@JJHunt10) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JJHunt10/status/1521464289630072832?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 3, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Polls show that the probable end of Roe has certainly caught voters\u8217\'20\'19 attention, although many Americans remain more focused on economic issues like {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/may/11/us-inflation-consumer-price-index-figures"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 record-high inflation}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A survey {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.monmouth.edu/polling-institute/reports/monmouthpoll_US_051222/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 released by Monmouth University}}}\uc2  last week showed 26% of Americans named economic policy as their most significant concern for the midterm elections, making it the most common response. But \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was cited almost as often, with 25% of Americans selecting it as their top priority when appraising candidates.\par \par \uc2 Amestoy argued Democratic gubernatorial candidates do not have to choose between campaigning on their plan to combat inflation and their promise to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. Instead, she encouraged candidates to use their opponents\u8217\'20\'19 views on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to paint Republicans as out of touch with the needs of average Americans.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRepublicans are campaigning on extreme, fringe agendas, like banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , rather than on delivering for families,\u8221\'20\'1D Amestoy said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a stark contrast Democratic governors and candidates can draw while they work to address the concerns voters care most about.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Drawing that contrast is even more important for Democratic gubernatorial candidates with federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legislation stalled in Congress. Last Wednesday, Senate Republicans and Democrat Joe Manchin {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vCN2WtQAzlachWt9ijDIopGr7qypMZ2HIazpWS9Xp6I/edit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 again blocked}}}\uc2  a bill that would have codified Roe and secured \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights at the national level. If the supreme court does indeed overturn Roe next month without other federal protections in place, individual states\u8217\'20\'19 policies will soon dictate if and how Americans can access \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe reproductive freedoms of millions of Americans are on the line,\u8221\'20\'1D Amestoy said. \u8220\'20\'1CElecting Democratic governors is our best and perhaps only hope of protecting them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220516ei5g000xh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
