\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Pro-choice demonstrators rally across the US over expected reversal of Roe v Wade \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Justin Madden (now), Mark Oliver and Maya Yang (earlier) \par \uc2 5,054 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 May 2022\par 22:57 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Thousands take to the streets in opposition to supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s draft opinion scrapping constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8216\'20\'18We will not go back\u8217\'20\'19: Thousands rally for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights across the USClarence Thomas calls leak of supreme court \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  draft \u8216\'20\'18tremendously bad\u8217\'20\'19\u8216\'20\'18This is real\u8217\'20\'19: in Oklahoma, a post-Roe world has arrivedSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s live coverage of nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rallies as come to an end. Here\u8217\'20\'19s a look at how the protests unfolded throughout the day.\par \par \uc2 Thousands of people were taking part in protests across the US on Saturday to decry the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s expected reversal of the landmark 1973 law that made \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legal in America.\par \par \uc2 Organizers said there were more than 380 protest events in cities including major ones in Washington DC, New York City, Los Angeles and Chicago to demand that the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not stripped away by the court, which is dominated by rightwing justices.\par \par \uc2 Gathering in large groups and holding signs that included slogans such as \u8220\'20\'1CReproductive justice for all\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1CWe will not go back\u8221\'20\'1D, and chanting \u8220\'20\'1CMy body, my choice\u8221\'20\'1D, the protesters have been spurred by the leak of a supreme court draft opinion on 2 May. The leaked draft showed that the five rightwing justices on the nine-member court had voted to overturn {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2 , the historic case that provided federal protection for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and proved a beacon in international efforts to improve the rights of women.\par \par \uc2 You can read more here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/14/abortion-rights-protests-us-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18We will not go back\u8217\'20\'19: thousands rally for \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights across the US }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 As the Los Angeles rally wrapped up, Elijah Lopez, 15, stood side by side with his mother, Lidia, carrying a sign that said \u8220\'20\'1CMy mom is pissed.\u8221\'20\'1D Lidia\u8217\'20\'19s sign read \u8220\'20\'1CYeah, I\u8217\'20\'19m pissed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday is an important day in history,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, referring to the rallies taking place across the US. \u8220\'20\'1CI was telling my son even though California is likely to maintain reproductive rights, in many other states that\u8217\'20\'19s not going to be the case.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe can show them that people don\u8217\'20\'19t want this,\u8221\'20\'1D Elijah said.\par \par \uc2 They came from the Inland Empire to advocate for reproductive rights together, part of a shared tradition of activism that began years ago when they started demonstrating against family separation under the Trump administration, which Lidia said was her son\u8217\'20\'19s introduction to peaceful protest.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s easy to just not do anything. We have to take as many opportunities as we can to show up. I want him to be here,\u8221\'20\'1D Lidia said.\par \par \uc2 Saturday\u8217\'20\'19s rally brought out many people who had never attended such protests before but were called to action seeing reproductive rights in jeopardy. Reginald Wheeler, a lifelong Los Angeles resident, said the event downtown marked his first protest.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI support women,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, \u8220\'20\'1CI would hope this is a reality check for those judges.\u8221\'20\'1D He added that he worries about what will happen when people don\u8217\'20\'19t have access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re gonna have a lot of unwanted children, children suffering from homelessness.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Luna Hernandez with Rise Up 4 \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Rights, an organizer of the rally, said the event would get people into the streets to stop the supreme court from taking away reproductive rights.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COnly the people can stop this,\u8221\'20\'1D Hernandez said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe have to refuse to allow this. This has to be a turning point, it\u8217\'20\'19s not a done deal.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is illegal, women die. Forced motherhood is female enslavement,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Part of me hopes for change. I really hope that this rally has an impact\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Allison from Baltimore, wearing a long red outfit and a white hat from the Margaret Atwood book A Handmaid\u8217\'20\'19s Tale, was standing at the Washington Monument shortly before the march began.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m just here to let my voice be heard and to be a part of the movement to fight for what should be a really easy right for us to have,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1C I feel that women should be in control of their own bodies and in so many ways we are not already. I don\u8217\'20\'19t want to see this country become \uc2 Gilead\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 hence the outfit \u8211\'20\'13 and I don\u8217\'20\'19t know if Roe v Wade is overturned then a set of complex cells will have more rights than an already living human being and that just doesn\u8217\'20\'19t sit right with me. I\u8217\'20\'19m not necessarily pro like \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but like pro like, that\u8217\'20\'19s not my business to choose that for somebody else.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Handmaid\u8217\'20\'19s Tale chronicles the life and times of the dystopia of \uc2 Gilead\uc2 , a a totalitarian society. It is ruled by a strict religious regime that treats women as property, forcing fertile women, or \u8220\'20\'1Chandmaids\u8221\'20\'1D, to produce children.\par \par \uc2 Allison said she\u8217\'20\'19s hoping for change.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPart of me hopes for change. I really hope that this rally has an impact. I\u8217\'20\'19ve been pretty cynical the last few years. But I hope \u8211\'20\'13 I really hope that you know that this does change,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 enltrFront of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/prochoice?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #prochoice}}}\uc2  March reaches {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/SupremeCourt?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #SupremeCourt}}}\uc2  building across from the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/USCapitol?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #USCapitol}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/guardian?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @guardian}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/u2qOc3BUNo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/u2qOc3BUNo}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lauren Burke (@LVBurke) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/LVBurke/status/1525559211253501952?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 14, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18We\u8217\'20\'19re the generation that\u8217\'20\'19s going to have to deal with this\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 One of the main rallies in New York city is now in the Foley Square area, where the crowd remains energized despite the rain - and the fact that many present gathered early this morning in Brooklyn and walked across the bridge into Manhattan.\par \par \uc2 A group of high-school students stood atop a monument, wearing white pants with red coloring to mimic blood. They held signs with the photographs and names of women who died after being denied safe abortions.\par \par \uc2 enltrA group of high-school students stands at Foley Square to protest for reproductive rights. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/MO6LFhKodY"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/MO6LFhKodY}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Victoria Bekiempis (@vicbekiempis) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/vicbekiempis/status/1525565720880369665?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 14, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Another group of high school students at Foley Square explained that they were protesting, as a Roe reversal would fall on their generation. Eliza and Adriana, both 16, co-founded the feminist student group at their high school. This is their first protest, they said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re the generation that\u8217\'20\'19s going to have to deal with the repercussions of this court decision,\u8221\'20\'1D Eliza said. \u8220\'20\'1CI wish I could say I was surprised, but I don\u8217\'20\'19t think I was. It\u8217\'20\'19s still devastating.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Adriana voiced similar sentiments. \u8220\'20\'1CThe sign I\u8217\'20\'19m carrying today says \u8220\'20\'1CMy uterus does not belong to the state,\u8221\'20\'1D Adriana said. Adriana noted that this was the same slogan advocates used decades ago, to note that the fundamental issues had not changed. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s infuriating.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 At the Los Angeles rally, Megan Triay was at her first reproductive rights protest on Saturday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is crazy. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is healthcare. It\u8217\'20\'19s human rights,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s so hard to put into words how insane it is that you have to explain it\u8217\'20\'19s my body, it\u8217\'20\'19s my choice.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Triay missed work to join thousands of other protesters at the Bans Off Our Bodies rally in LA: \u8220\'20\'1CI might get fired but I had to be here.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve been in this position. I don\u8217\'20\'19t regret my \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , she said, describing how she was terrified and healthcare workers treated her with compassion and care. \u8220\'20\'1CTo think woman after me aren\u8217\'20\'19t going to get that care \u8230\'20\'26 There is no way this can happen.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrMegan Triay was one of thousands of protesters who joined the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/BansOffOurBodies?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #BansOffOurBodies}}}\uc2  rally in LA. \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is healthcare,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve been in this position. I don\u8217\'20\'19t regret my \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . To think women after me won\u8217\'20\'19t have that care \u8230\'20\'26 There is no way this can happen.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/RwLlOTHduL"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/RwLlOTHduL}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Dani Anguiano (@Dani_Anguiano) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Dani_Anguiano/status/1525561834165501952?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 14, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 DC \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights activists marching to Supreme Court\par \par \uc2 enltrLarge {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/prochoice?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #prochoice}}}\uc2  March to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/SupremeCourt?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #SupremeCourt}}}\uc2  building nears {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/USCapitol?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #USCapitol}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/guardian?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @guardian}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/SMAnCXIRz0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/SMAnCXIRz0}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lauren Burke (@LVBurke) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/LVBurke/status/1525554424705318913?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 14, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrFront of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/prochoice?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #prochoice}}}\uc2  March reaches {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/SupremeCourt?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #SupremeCourt}}}\uc2  building across from the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/USCapitol?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #USCapitol}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/guardian?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @guardian}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/u2qOc3BUNo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/u2qOc3BUNo}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lauren Burke (@LVBurke) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/LVBurke/status/1525559211253501952?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 14, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Gloria Allred, women\u8217\'20\'19s right lawyer, has shared the story of an illegal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  she had in California in the 1960s, telling a grim story about the US before Roe V Wade became the law of the land.\par \par \uc2 At a rally in Los Angeles, Allred, who has represented women in cases against Bill Cosby, Donald Trump and Roman Polanski, described how she became pregnant after being raped at gunpoint and then nearly died from the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI was left in a bathtub in a pool of my own blood,\u8221\'20\'1D the renowned feminist said. \u8220\'20\'1CA nurse said to me: I hope this teaches you a lesson. It did reach me a lesson, but not the one she wanted.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  must be safe, it must be legal, it must be affordable, it must be available.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 Congresswoman Maxine Waters just spoke at a reproductive rights rally in Los Angeles, telling the thousands outside city hall: \u8220\'20\'1CWe are not backing down.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are not about to give up control of our body because of the supreme court or anyone else,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 The crowd greeted Waters, a longtime US representative, with thunderous applause, cheering louder under the morning sun as she said \u8220\'20\'1Cwe are going to fight like hell. We are going to fight until our right are restored\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Thousands of people have filled up the blocks between a federal courthouse and city hall, carrying signs reading \u8220\'20\'1CBans off our bodies\u8221\'20\'1D, \u8220\'20\'1CStop the Supreme Court\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is healthcare\u8221\'20\'1D, and dancing in between speeches from lawmakers and actors.\par \par \uc2 Congresswoman Karen Bass, LA mayoral candidate, led the crowd in cheers: \u8220\'20\'1CWe will fight. We will vote.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Anti-choice protesters filled up street corners around the protest, sometimes preaching through loudspeakers. Opponents took to the skies, leaving aerial messages overhead that said \u8220\'20\'1CAlex Jones was right\u8221\'20\'1D and promoted the website for a conservative news outlet.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights protesters participate in rallies in Los Angeles, California, U.S., May 14, 2022. Photograph: Aude Guerrucci/Reuters\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 People who have turned up at the protests spoke of their alarm over the prospect of losing a right that women have relied upon for the past 50 years. \u8220\'20\'1CHow can they take away what I feel is a human right from us?\u8221\'20\'1D said Julie Kinsella, a teacher who took part in the New York protest. Kinsella said she felt \u8220\'20\'1Canger\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Coutrage\u8221\'20\'1D when she heard the news of the draft opinion.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt just made me think: what direction is the US moving toward with that decision?\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe have made so much progress up until this point. I would just hate to see us backtrack and fight for what we already have right now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/14/abortion-rights-protests-us-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18We will not go back\u8217\'20\'19: Thousands rally for \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights across the US }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Pro-choice advocates rally in DC and listen to speakers at the National Mall\par \par \uc2 enltrCrowd grows larger as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/prochoice?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #prochoice}}}\uc2  advocates rally on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/NationalMall?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #NationalMall}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/guardian?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @guardian}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/fUXuYvLiYw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/fUXuYvLiYw}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lauren Burke (@LVBurke) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/LVBurke/status/1525532689046065152?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 14, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 New York city protesters cross the Brooklyn bridge into Manhattan\par \par \uc2 enltrThe {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/BansOffOurBodies?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #BansOffOurBodies}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/BansOffNYC?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #BansOffNYC}}}\uc2  just now crossing onto the Brooklyn Bridge. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/mChrwLvOaI"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/mChrwLvOaI}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Victoria Bekiempis (@vicbekiempis) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/vicbekiempis/status/1525530261319974912?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 14, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrAnother protest group is walking across the Brooklyn Bridge, into BK. Cheers as groups crossed paths. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/mLhIeiRGUX"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/mLhIeiRGUX}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Victoria Bekiempis (@vicbekiempis) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/vicbekiempis/status/1525534399990845444?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 14, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrThe {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/BansOffOurBodies?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #BansOffOurBodies}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/BansOffNYC?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #BansOffNYC}}}\uc2  march is in Manhattan {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ptiWn54oZ5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ptiWn54oZ5}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Victoria Bekiempis (@vicbekiempis) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/vicbekiempis/status/1525539825159479301?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 14, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.15pm BST\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights protesters marching in Chicago\par \par \uc2 At a rally in Chicago, speaker after speaker told the crowd that if \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is banned that the rights of immigrants, minorities and others will also be \u8220\'20\'1Cgutted,\u8221\'20\'1D as Amy Eshleman, wife of Chicago Mayor Lori lightfoot put it. \u8220\'20\'1CThis has never been just about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It\u8217\'20\'19s about control,\u8221\'20\'1D Eshleman told the crowd of thousands. \u8220\'20\'1CMy marriage is on the menu and we cannot and will not let that happen,\u8221\'20\'1D she added.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights demonstrators rally in Chicago\u8217\'20\'19s West Town neighborhood, Saturday morning, May 14, 2022. Photograph: Pat Nabong/AP\par \par \uc2 Kjirsten Nyquist, a nurse toting daughters ages 1 and 3, agreed about the need to vote. \u8220\'20\'1CAs much as federal elections, voting in every small election matters just as much,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 From Pittsburgh to Pasadena, California, and Nashville, Tennessee, to Lubbock, Texas, tens of thousands are participating in the \u8220\'20\'1CBans off our Bodies\u8221\'20\'1D events. Organizers expected that among the hundreds of events, the largest would take place in Chicago, New York, Los Angeles and other big cities. \u8220\'20\'1CIf it\u8217\'20\'19s a fight they want, it\u8217\'20\'19s a fight they\u8217\'20\'19ll get,\u8221\'20\'1D Rachel Carmona, executive director of the Women\u8217\'20\'19s March, said before the march.\par \par \uc2 Protesters sit on the grass while holding a \uc2 Ruth Bader Ginsburg\uc2  during a protest Saturday morning, May 14, 2022 Photograph: Pat Nabong/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 Thousands rally in Washington DC\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights activist rally at the Washington Monument before a march to the \uc2 US Supreme Court\uc2  in Washington, DC Photograph: Jos\u233\'00\'E9 Luis Maga\u241\'00\'F1a/AFP/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 In the nation\u8217\'20\'19s capital, thousands gathered at the Washington Monument before marching to the Supreme Court, which is now surrounded by two layers of security fences.\par \par \uc2 Caitlin Loehr, 34, of Washington, wore a black T-shirt with an image of the late Supreme Court Justice \uc2 Ruth Bader Ginsburg\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cdissent\u8221\'20\'1D collar on it and a necklace that spelled out \u8220\'20\'1Cvote.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think that women should have the right to choose what to do with their bodies and their lives. And I don\u8217\'20\'19t think banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  will stop \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It just makes it unsafe and can cost a woman her life,\u8221\'20\'1D Loehr said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 As one of the New York city protests moved onto the entrance of the Brooklyn bridge, demonstrators chanted \u8220\'20\'1CBans off our bodies now!\u8221\'20\'1D Drummers in the procession provided a powerful rhythm alongside the chants. \u8220\'20\'1CThis bridge represents all of the states in this nation. We will not be divided!\u8221\'20\'1D New York state attorney General Letitia James said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights protesters participate in nationwide demonstrations, in New York City Photograph: Caitlin Ochs/Reuters \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights protesters participate in nationwide demonstrations, in New York City Photograph: Caitlin Ochs/Reuters\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 Striking images have emerged from the Bans Off Our Bodies rally in Washington DC.\par \par \uc2 Here are a few:\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights protester Christa from Atlanta participates in nationwide pro-choice demonstrations in Washington, US, May 14, 2022. Photograph: Leah Millis/Reuters \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights activist rally at the Washington Monument before a march to the \uc2 US Supreme Court\uc2  in Washington, DC, May 14, 2022. Photograph: Jos\u233\'00\'E9 Luis Maga\u241\'00\'F1a/AFP/Getty Images \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights activist rally at the Washington Monument before a march to the \uc2 US Supreme Court\uc2  in Washington, DC, May 14, 2022. Photograph: Jos\u233\'00\'E9 Luis Maga\u241\'00\'F1a/AFP/Getty Images \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights activists participate in a Bans Off Our Bodies rally on May 14, 2022 in Washington, DC. Photograph: Tasos Katopodis/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 People of all ages, races and genders marching for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights\par \par \uc2 Protesters have started to march from Cadman Plaza, in Brooklyn, toward the Brooklyn Bridge, en route to Downtown Manhattan, in a demonstration for reproductive health rights. It is one of hundreds of demonstrations across the US following a leaked draft Supreme Court decision that suggests the justices will vote to overturn Roe v Wade, which legalized \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the US.\par \par \uc2 Protesters rally during an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights demonstration, Saturday, May 14, 2022, in New York Photograph: Jeenah Moon/AP\par \par \uc2 The mood among the two-to-three thousand present is enthusiasm marked by solemnity. People of all ages, races, and genders are participating in this walk across the Brooklyn Bridge. The front line is carrying a green sign that reads \u8220\'20\'1COur bodies, our abortions.\u8221\'20\'1D Others hold signs that read \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is healthcare\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1CMy body, my choice.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI always want my right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be free and accessible,\u8221\'20\'1D protester Nicole Cornell 22, told \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s my own choice to be pregnant. I don\u8217\'20\'19t want the government to infringe on that right.\u8221\'20\'1D Protesters are also expected to gather in New York City\u8217\'20\'19s Union Square at 2 pm.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.52pm BST\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights activists are rallying outside Texas\u8217\'20\'19s State Capitol:\par \par \uc2 enltrHappening now: Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights advocates are hosting the Bans Off Our Bodies rally at the State Capitol. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KVUE?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @KVUE}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/WC67X41SOk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/WC67X41SOk}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Maria E. Aguilera (@maria_aguilera) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/maria_aguilera/status/1525506501766438912?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 14, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrThe \u8216\'20\'18Bans Off Our Bodies\u8217\'20\'19 rally at the state Capitol. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KVUE?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @KVUE}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/0ZjKyQBu0w"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/0ZjKyQBu0w}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Maria E. Aguilera (@maria_aguilera) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/maria_aguilera/status/1525511955921915908?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 14, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrPeople chant \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a human right\u8221\'20\'1D at the Bans Off Our Bodies rally. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KVUE?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @KVUE}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/3C9uCKMxSa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/3C9uCKMxSa}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Maria E. Aguilera (@maria_aguilera) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/maria_aguilera/status/1525513152187727873?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 14, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 As the US braces for the end of a federal right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a new six-week ban in Oklahoma {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/14/oklahoma-abortion-post-roe-world"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 offers}}}\uc2  a preview of what\u8217\'20\'19s to come.\par \par \uc2 The day after the supreme court leak, Andrea Gallegos had already started to cancel patients\u8217\'20\'19 appointments.\par \par \uc2 In the aftermath, Gallegos, the administrator for Tulsa Women\u8217\'20\'19s Clinic, an Oklahoma-based \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider, wasn\u8217\'20\'19t worried about Roe \u8211\'20\'13 at least, it wasn\u8217\'20\'19t the first thing she was worried about.\par \par \uc2 To her, there was a bigger, more immediate threat: a six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban the Republican governor was expected to sign any day now.\par \par \uc2 That same evening, to little fanfare, Governor Kevin Stitt signed into law the six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. The state supreme court declined to block the ban. If the clinic saw their patients on Wednesday, they risked civil lawsuits with a penalty of up to $10,000.\par \par \uc2 Oklahoma Gov. Kevin Stitt speaks after signing into law a bill making it a felony to perform an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , punishable by up to 10 years in prison on April 12, 2022/ Photograph: Sue Ogrocki/AP\par \par \uc2 So Gallegos did what she had dreaded. She began calling back patients who were past six weeks pregnant. The scheduled appointments would have to be canceled. If they wanted to seek an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , she told them, they should look somewhere else \u8211\'20\'13 Kansas, New Mexico or, a bit further away, Colorado.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 More protesters arrive in New York\par \par \uc2 enltrThe crowd is growing in Cadman Plaza for the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/BansOffOurBodies?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #BansOffOurBodies}}}\uc2  March {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/BansOffNYC?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #BansOffNYC}}}\uc2  protest. The demonstration is expected to begin at 1 pm, and will March across Brooklyn Bridge. Here is the plaza thus far. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ehmHTN4XVW"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ehmHTN4XVW}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Victoria Bekiempis (@vicbekiempis) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/vicbekiempis/status/1525505626075537414?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 14, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 State judicial races become increasingly politicized over issues such as \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , partisan gerrymandering and gun rights.\par \par \uc2 Spending and campaigning around the judicial races could intensify if the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturns Roe v Wade, which a leaked draft opinion indicates justices are prepared to do.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CState courts are going to be front-and-center in the fight over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access,\u8221\'20\'1D said Doug Keith, an attorney in the Brennan Center\u8217\'20\'19s Democracy Program. \u8220\'20\'1CThese races in some states are likely going to take a prominence that they\u8217\'20\'19ve never had before.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Michigan is among the states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be a central factor in court races this fall. One Democratic and one Republican justice are up for reelection to a court where Democrats hold a 4-3 majority. The races are technically non-partisan, even though candidates are nominated by political parties.\par \par \uc2 Democratic Governor \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2  is asking the state\u8217\'20\'19s high court to recognize a right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the state Constitution.\par \par \uc2 She also wants it to declare unconstitutional a 1931 near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban that would go into effect if Roe is reversed.\par \par \uc2 Michigan Governor \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2  speaks at the Rouge Electric Vehicle Center in Dearborn, Michigan, U.S. September 16, 2021. Photograph: Rebecca Cook/Reuters\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18I thought it was sickening\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Santiago Bueno and his infant, Adelaide, are among the hundreds who have gathered at Cadman Plaza in New York City today to protest for reproductive rights. Bueno explains why, as a father of a daughter, he felt it important to attend after the leaked Supreme Court opinion that would reverse Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 enltrSantiago Bueno is at Cadman Plaza with his daughter of 1 year 7 mos, Adelaide. He explains why they are at the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/BansOffOurBodies?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #BansOffOurBodies}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/BansOffNYC?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #BansOffNYC}}}\uc2  march today: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/MgC3xTt8zu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/MgC3xTt8zu}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Victoria Bekiempis (@vicbekiempis) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/vicbekiempis/status/1525507096241922049?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 14, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Teisha Kimmons, who traveled 80 miles to attend the Chicago rally, said she fears for women in states that are ready to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . She said she might not be alive today if she had not had a legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  when she was 15.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI was already starting to self harm and I would have rather died than have a baby,\u8221\'20\'1D Kimmons, a massage therapist from Rockford, Illinois, told the Associated Press.\par \par \uc2 The upcoming high court ruling in a case from Mississippi stands to energize voters, potentially shaping the upcoming midterm elections.\par \par \uc2 Kimmons, 46, said she believes the focus needs to be on those races. \u8220\'20\'1CWe have to vote in pro-choice politicians because women\u8217\'20\'19s lives depend on it,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Roe is really the floor... it has not been easy for Asian Americans and Pacific Islanders to get access\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Nimmi Penmatsa and Becca Asaki are at Cadman Plaza this Saturday morning, as organizers with the National Asian Pacific American Women\u8217\'20\'19s Forum. Both said that people within the AAPI community faced challenges accessing reproductive health services. Overturning Roe would only make things worse, they said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are at a really critical time in our country,\u8221\'20\'1D said Penmatsa, 26. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are facing the very real possibility of losing our right to our bodily autonomy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m part of the AAPI community. We face so many barriers when it comes to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 --language barriers, cultural stigma,\u8221\'20\'1D Penmatsa said. \u8220\'20\'1CI fear that what will happen if Roe is overturned... we\u8217\'20\'19re going to create an environment where people will have no place to go.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 And absent access to safe reproductive health services, Penmatsa said, people will seek out potentially life threatening solutions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRoe has really been the floor,\u8221\'20\'1D said Asaki, 35. \u8220\'20\'1CIt has not always been the reality for Asian Americans and Pacific Islanders to access our full \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have been fighting to expand our \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access,\u8221\'20\'1D Asaki said, explaining that a Roe reversal \u8220\'20\'1Cwould be immediately detrimental to our ability to access \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 There are lots of strong images and videos coming out from the protests, here\u8217\'20\'19s a selection from Charlottesville, Virginia:\par \par \uc2 undltr {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/BansOffOurBodies?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #BansOffOurBodies}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/5Er4SaM5D4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/5Er4SaM5D4}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Indivisible Charlottesville (@indivisibleVA05) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/indivisibleVA05/status/1525491222189682688?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 14, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrthe bans off our bodies rally + protest march has gathered on the downtown mall outside charlottesville city hall. there\u8217\'20\'19s a couple hundred people here now with speakers starting soon {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/3FfUZVCL7N"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/3FfUZVCL7N}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 molly conger (@socialistdogmom) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/socialistdogmom/status/1525487127949107200?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 14, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrI\u8217\'20\'19m outside of the Federal Building in Charlottesville covering the \u8220\'20\'1CBans Off Our Bodies\u8221\'20\'1D march and there is a lot of supportive honking. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Uq4GmFxmZ1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Uq4GmFxmZ1}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Allison Wrabel (@craftypanda) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/craftypanda/status/1525480765445775361?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 14, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18I\u8217\'20\'19m here for my friend, and all women\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Women gathering in New York city, where multiple protests are planned, are talking about what is motivating them to be part of Saturday\u8217\'20\'19s actions.\par \par \uc2 enltrBeth and Victoria explain why they are at today's reproductive rights demonstration in Cadman Plaza, which starts at 12. Hundreds of protests are expected across the US today following a draft \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  decision leaked indicating a possible reversal of Roe v Wade {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/dtUJpUWL43"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/dtUJpUWL43}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Victoria Bekiempis (@vicbekiempis) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/vicbekiempis/status/1525487902800719873?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 14, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18What direction is the US moving towards with that decision?\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Julie Kinsella traveled to Brooklyn from Saratoga Springs, New York to participate in Saturday\u8217\'20\'19s demonstration, explaining that she felt \u8220\'20\'1Coutrage\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Canger\u8221\'20\'1D when news broke about the draft opinion.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is to stop things from happening,\u8221\'20\'1D explained Kinsella, 35, of why she decided to protest. \u8220\'20\'1CWe have made so much progress up until this point. I would just hate to see us backtrack and fight for what we already have right now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Kinsella, an educator, described her reaction to the draftthe leaked opinion suggests that the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  is poised to overturn Roe v. Wade. \u8220\'20\'1CHow can they take away what I feel is a human right from us?\u8221\'20\'1D Kinsella said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt just made me think: What direction is the US moving toward with that decision?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Kinsella said this is her first time protesting.\u8221\'20\'1DIn the last five, 10 years, I\u8217\'20\'19ve seen many things that anger me,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CI can\u8217\'20\'19t keep sitting back.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 An \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights protester writes on the sidewalk in New York city Photograph: Eduardo Mu\u241\'00\'F1oz/Reuters\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 Conservative justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2022/may/14/clarence-thomas-supreme-court-leak-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called}}}\uc2  the leak of the supreme court \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  draft \u8220\'20\'1Ctremendously bad.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Supreme Court Justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  speaks at the \uc2 University of Notre Dame\uc2  in South Bend, Indiana. Photograph: Robert Franklin/AP\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat happened at the court was tremendously bad,\u8221\'20\'1D Thomas, 73, said in a dialog at a conference of conservative and libertarian thinkers in Dallas.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI wonder how long we\u8217\'20\'19re going to have these institutions at the rate we\u8217\'20\'19re undermining them...And then I wonder when they\u8217\'20\'19re gone or destabilized, what we\u8217\'20\'19re going to have as a country,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 The comments came one week after the justice said he feared that the judicial system will come under threat if people are unwilling to \u8220\'20\'1Clive with outcomes we don\u8217\'20\'19t agree with\u8221\'20\'1D and that recent events at the apex court might be \u8220\'20\'1Cone symptom of that\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2022/may/14/clarence-thomas-supreme-court-leak-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Clarence Thomas calls leak of supreme court \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  draft \u8216\'20\'18tremendously bad\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Protesters gather in New York: \u8216\'20\'18This has been coming\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 By 10am local time, reproductive rights advocates started arriving at Cadman Plaza, in Brooklyn, New York City, to prepare for a demonstration scheduled for noon.\par \par \uc2 Organizer Jillian White is among them. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m deeply concerned about the erosion of our rights,\u8221\'20\'1D White, 35, told \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CI feel like it\u8217\'20\'19s important to show up and do everything that I can.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrGood morning from Cadman Plaza, in BK NYC. Organizers are here in advance of the reproductive rights demonstration today, following the leaked draft on Roe. Will be following NYC demonstrations for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GuardianUS?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @GuardianUS}}}\uc2 . Organizer Jillian White explains why she is here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/LnPnKaj0ob"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/LnPnKaj0ob}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Victoria Bekiempis (@vicbekiempis) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/vicbekiempis/status/1525478680788619264?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 14, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Demonstrators are gathering at the park as the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  appears poised to overturn Roe v. Wade, the watershed 1973 decision which made \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legal. On 2 May, a draft decision leaked to Politico showed that five conservative justices on the nine-judge panel had voted to overturn the decision.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think I was surprised about the leak, not about its contents,\u8221\'20\'1D White said. \u8220\'20\'1CThis has been coming for a very long time. My heart hurt, but I wasn\u8217\'20\'19t surprised.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Good morning and welcome to the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s coverage of Saturday\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rallies that are set to take place across the nation.\par \par \uc2 We will be covering it all live and have reporters at some of the main protest sites, including Washington DC, New York City and Los Angeles.\par \par \uc2 With the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  apparently poised to overturn the 1973 landmark decision which made \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legal, hundreds of thousands of people across America are planning to take to the streets to protest the looming decision.\par \par \uc2 A coalition of groups such as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.plannedparenthoodaction.org/rightfully-ours/bans-off-our-bodies"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Planned Parenthood}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://weareultraviolet.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 UltraViolet}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://front.moveon.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MoveOn}}}\uc2  and the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.womensmarch.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Women\u8217\'20\'19s March}}}\uc2  are organizing Saturday\u8217\'20\'19s demonstrations, whose rallying cry is \u8220\'20\'1CBans Off Our Bodies\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 More than 380 events are set from Maine to Hawaii, with the largest gatherings expected in Los Angeles, Chicago, New York and other big cities, organizers said.\par \par \uc2 In the nation\u8217\'20\'19s capital, activists planned to gather at the Washington Monument before marching to the Supreme Court, which is now surrounded by a security fence.\par \par \uc2 The demonstrations come after the leak on 2 May of a draft opinion showing five conservatives on the nine-justice supreme court had voted to reverse their predecessors\u8217\'20\'19 ruling in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  nearly 50 years ago.\par \par \uc2 Unless the provisional ruling is changed substantially before becoming final, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be outlawed essentially immediately in more than half of US states.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s no exaggeration to say that for the women of this country, this will be a summer of rage,\u8221\'20\'1D said Rachel Carmona, executive director of the Women\u8217\'20\'19s March.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220514ei5e001p7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
