\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Demonstrators across the US protest expected reversal of Roe v Wade\b0\par\par\uc2 Guardian staff \par \uc2 366 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 May 2022\par 06:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bans Off Our Bodies marches follow the Senate\u8217\'20\'19s failure to pass legislation protecting the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 With the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  apparently poised to overturn the 1973 landmark decision which made \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legal, hundreds of thousands of people across America are planning to take to the streets to protest the looming decision.\par \par \uc2 A coalition of groups such as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.plannedparenthoodaction.org/rightfully-ours/bans-off-our-bodies"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Planned Parenthood}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://weareultraviolet.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 UltraViolet}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://front.moveon.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MoveOn}}}\uc2  and the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.womensmarch.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Women\u8217\'20\'19s March}}}\uc2  are organizing Saturday\u8217\'20\'19s demonstrations, whose rallying cry is \u8220\'20\'1CBans Off Our Bodies\u8221\'20\'1D. More than 370 protests are planned, including in Washington DC, New York, Los Angeles and Chicago.\par \par \uc2 The demonstrations come after the leak on 2 May of a draft opinion showing five conservatives on the nine-justice supreme court had voted to reverse their predecessors\u8217\'20\'19 ruling in Roe v Wade nearly 50 years ago.\par \par \uc2 Unless the provisional ruling is changed substantially before becoming final, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be outlawed essentially immediately in more than half of US states. People in those 26 states hostile to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be forced to either travel hundreds of miles to a clinic in a state where terminating a pregnancy is legal or seek to self-administer an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  through medication from grassroots or illicit groups.\par \par \uc2 While conservatives have celebrated the leak ruling, liberals have objected vociferously, gathering outside the supreme court building in Washington DC as well as the homes of some of the conservative justices to signal their displeasure.\par \par \uc2 Those rallies \u8211\'20\'13 generally peaceful \u8211\'20\'13 have been relatively small, while Saturday\u8217\'20\'19s planned events will almost certainly be compared to the 2017 Women\u8217\'20\'19s March the day after \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was inaugurated as president, which drew an estimated 3 million to 4 million participants across the US.\par \par \uc2 The \u8220\'20\'1CBans Off Our Bodies\u8221\'20\'1D gatherings will take place three days after Democrats in the \uc2 US Senate\uc2  on Wednesday made a largely symbolic effort to advance legislation that would codify the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  into federal law. All 50 Republicans and one conservative-aligned Democrat \u8211\'20\'13 West Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 voted against the measure, leaving it well short of the 60 votes necessary for it to advance.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220514ei5e000ji\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
