\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 US defence chief urges Ukraine ceasefire in call with Russian counterpart \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Martin Pengelly in New York (now) and Adam Gabbatt (earlier) \par \uc2 4,582 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 May 2022\par 20:16 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Lloyd Austin\uc2  urges immediate ceasefire in \uc2 Sergei Shoigu\uc2  callMike Pence likely to draw ire of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in GeorgiaSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll wrap up the blog here, after another busy day in Washington and US politics as a whole.\par \par \uc2 To close on a sobering note, in light of the protests planned across the US tomorrow over the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s apparent desire to overturn the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , here\u8217\'20\'19s Maanvi Singh\u8217\'20\'19s report from Oakland, about the challenges which face those protecting that right even in states which support it:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/13/abortion-access-safe-haven-california"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Even in \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  \u8216\'20\'18safe havens\u8217\'20\'19 finding care can be challenging}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 Widespread marches are planned for Saturday, in protest of the apparent readiness of the supreme court to strike down the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Here\u8217\'20\'19s some preparatory reading from David Sirota and Andrew Perez \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Even as the Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 feeble legislative attempt to codify federal protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/live/2022/05/11/us/abortion-roe-v-wade-senate-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 goes down in flames}}}\uc2 , many Washington elites are directing their attention and anger towards the same target: no, not rightwing judges reaching their ideological hands into millions of people\u8217\'20\'19s bodies, but instead the protesters peacefully demonstrating outside the homes of supreme court justices who are about to overturn Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 Prominent Republican lawmakers, conservative operatives and Beltway pundits are demanding the government arrest demonstrators \u8211\'20\'13 and to do so, they are citing a McCarthy-era statute passed to stop people from protesting against the prosecutions of alleged communists. Ignored in the discourse is a past ruling from the supreme court effectively {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/The_Law_Boy/status/1523725434634276864"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blessing}}}\uc2  conservative protests at the homes of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic workers.\par \par \uc2 The largely manufactured outrage is the latest distraction designed to shift attention away from the issue at hand: the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s conservative supermajority is about to deny basic reproductive rights to tens of millions of people in roughly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2022/05/05/1096738094/roe-v-wade-abortion-overturn-impact-world"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 half the country}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Conservative operatives want Washington reporters focused on inane questions like who leaked the court\u8217\'20\'19s draft opinion, and they want journalists and Democrats to criticize protesters who are outraged by the court\u8217\'20\'19s overriding lack of respect for people\u8217\'20\'19s bodily autonomy. It is part of a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.icnl.org/usprotestlawtracker/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 larger rightwing movement}}}\uc2  in recent years to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/21/us/politics/republican-anti-protest-laws.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cancel}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewtrusts.org/en/research-and-analysis/blogs/stateline/2021/06/21/eight-states-enact-anti-protest-laws"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 criminalize}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2017/08/18/us/legislation-protects-drivers-injure-protesters/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 literally crush}}}\uc2  dissent throughout the country, even as the conservative political noise machine continues to blare Braveheart-esque screams of \u8220\'20\'1Cfreedom!\u8221\'20\'1D against so-called \u8220\'20\'1Ccancel culture\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2022/may/13/abortion-pro-choice-joseph-mccarthy-red-scare"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Prepare for McCarthy-era crackdowns on pro-choice protesters | Andrew Perez and David Sirota}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 The population of the United States is much {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.worlddata.info/average-age.php"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 younger}}}\uc2  than that of most European countries, but its political establishment is much older.\par \par \uc2 The 2020 presidential election was fought between 74-year-old \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and 77-year-old \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 compare that to 53-year-old \uc2 Marine Le Pen\uc2  and 44-year-old \uc2 Emmanuel Macron\uc2  in last month\u8217\'20\'19s French presidential election.\par \par \uc2 The Senate majority leader, \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , is 71, while minority leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  is 80. In the generally younger House of Representatives, the majority leader, \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , is 82, making minority leader Kevin McCarthy look like a spring chicken at a mere 57.\par \par \uc2 This is not just a problem for the functioning of the democratic system; it endangers the survival of it.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2022/may/12/democratic-party-new-younger-leadership-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Democratic party needs new, younger leadership before it\u8217\'20\'19s too late | Cas Mudde}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ariana Grande, Billie Eilish, Megan Thee Stallion, Olivia Rodrigo and Selena Gomez joined a slew of fellow music stars and other celebrities to take out {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PopBase/status/1525114142243311616/photo/1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a full-page advertisement}}}\uc2  in Friday\u8217\'20\'19s New York Times, decrying the looming fall of nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe supreme court is planning to overturn {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D read the ad, referring to the landmark 1973 ruling that in effect legalized \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  across the US.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur power to plan our own futures and control our own bodies depends on our ability to access sexual and reproductive health care, including \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It continued: \u8220\'20\'1CWe are artists. Creators. Storytellers. We are the new generation stepping into our power. Now we are being robbed of our power. We will not go back \u8211\'20\'13 and we will not back down.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 More than 160 musicians, songwriters, actors, models and other celebrities signed the ad, which invited the public to take to the streets on Saturday and participate in planned demonstrations across the US protesting the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s expected reversal of Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 Other notable names include Asa Butterfield, Camila Cabello, Camila Mendes, Demi Lovato, Dove Cameron, Lil Dicky, Dylan O\u8217\'20\'19Brien, Finneas, Hailee Steinfeld, Hailey Bieber, Halsey, Ilana Glazer, Joey King, Kendall Jenner, Miley Cyrus, Paramore, Phoebe Bridgers, Quvenzhan\u233\'00\'E9 Wallis, Shawn Mendes, Tate McRae and Thomas Doherty.\par \par \uc2 Full story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/13/ariana-grande-billie-eilish-roe-v-wade-abortion-nyt-ad"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ariana Grande and other stars support Roe v Wade in New York Times ad}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Chairman Thompson on January 6 GOP subpoenas\par \par \uc2 The House select committee investigating the Capitol attack made a political and legal gambit when it issued unprecedented subpoenas that compel five Republican members of Congress to reveal inside information about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s effort to overturn the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 Bennie Thompson\uc2 . Photograph: Mandel Ngan/AFP/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 The move sets into motion an extraordinary high-stakes showdown of response and counter-response for both the subpoenaed House Republicans \u8211\'20\'13 the House minority leader, Kevin McCarthy, Jim Jordan, Scott Perry, Andy Biggs and Mo Brooks \u8211\'20\'13 and the panel itself.\par \par \uc2 Bennie Thompson\uc2 , the Democrat chair of the committee, authorized the subpoenas on Wednesday after the panel convened for final talks about whether to proceed with subpoenas, with House investigators needing to wrap up work before June public hearings.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe inquired to most of them via letter to come forward, and when they told us they would not come, we issued the subpoena,\u8221\'20\'1D Thompson said of McCarthy and his colleagues. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a process. And the process was clearly one that required debate and discussion.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The decision came after a recognition that their investigation into January 6 would not have been complete if they did not at least attempt to force the cooperation of some of the House Republicans most deeply involved in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s unlawful schemes to return himself to office.\par \par \uc2 But the subpoenas are about deploying a political and legal power play in the crucial final moments of the investigation as much as they are about an effort to gain new information for the inquiry into efforts to stop \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s certification in time for public hearings.\par \par \uc2 Full story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/13/jan-6-panels-subpoenas-trump-republicans-mccarthy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Subpoenas of Trump allies by January 6 panel set up high-stakes showdown}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Psaki finishes final White House briefing\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re on to the Iran nuclear deal and whether Russia is now an obstacle to resurrecting the pact, which \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  dropped. Russia is an obstacle, Psaki says, given its invasion of Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2 . Photograph: Andrew Harnik/AP\par \par \uc2 Why is the US not calling for an independent inquiry into the shooting of Shireen Abu Aqleh, an Al Jazeera journalist, in the West Bank?\par \par \uc2 The US will provide assistance if Israel wants it, Psaki says. That\u8217\'20\'19s that.\par \par \uc2 Asked about immigration reform, which is stalled, Psaki points out simply that Congress won\u8217\'20\'19t move on it. Biden was elected in part on a promise to work with Republicans in Congress, based on his three decades there as a senator, but that\u8217\'20\'19s all part of the fun.\par \par \uc2 Obviously, in a lot of ways a White House briefing should be this frustrating, in that the press secretary should spend the time parrying questions no matter how many times they are rephrased by the press, and should achieve that parrying by verbal sleight of hand or by simply drowning the inconvenient questions in inexorable verbiage.\par \par \uc2 Which is what \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  does here, before nodding, closing her binder and leaving the White House podium for the final time, with a simple: \u8220\'20\'1CThank you, everyone.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 So it goes.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Psaki is asked about Republican attacks over the baby formula situation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe do like facts here,\u8221\'20\'1D Psaki says, flipping her binder, and trying to make the point that perhaps Republican critics of the administration are, let\u8217\'20\'19s say, less keen on facts in such circumstances.\par \par \uc2 Will there soon be a Covid vaccine for the under-fives? Psaki says she as a parent is eager for such a move but \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cmoves at the pace of science\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Psaki is also asked about the absence of meaningful reform on police and policing promised in light of the murder of George Floyd and the national protests that followed.\par \par \uc2 She says the administration is taking such efforts seriously and hopes Republicans will support Biden\u8217\'20\'19s efforts, including $10m for policing announced today, and a police reform executive order \u8220\'20\'1Cwill be a part of that\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Asked about advice for \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2 , her successor as press secretary who is in the room, Psaki says she will have to \u8220\'20\'1Cproject and convey the positions of the president of the United States\u8221\'20\'1D. As a \u8220\'20\'1Cbit of a policy nerd\u8221\'20\'1D, Psaki advises deep engagement on that front too.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou never want to be a meme with one line,\u8221\'20\'1D Psaki also says, advising the provision of context in answers. The camera does not cut to Peter Doocy of Fox News, with Psaki the subject of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Acyn/status/1524101573667745793"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 many such memes}}}\uc2 . Shame.\par \par \uc2 Baby formula is back on the agenda. Psaki notes administration approaches and what it claims are successes.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  continues her final briefing as White House press secretary, fielding questions about Americans held in Iran and about Brittney Griner, the women\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 NBA\uc2  star who is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2022/may/13/brittney-griner-wnba-detention-extended-russia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 being held in Russia}}}\uc2 . Griner has been \u8220\'20\'1Cwrongfully detained\u8221\'20\'1D, Psaki says, without giving much of an answer beyond saying efforts continue to get Griner home.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s our story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2022/may/13/brittney-griner-wnba-detention-extended-russia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 WNBA star Brittney Griner\u8217\'20\'19s detention in Russia extended by month}}}\par \par \uc2 Psaki is also asked about Covid funding from Congress and says, \u8220\'20\'1CThere is no Plan B\u8221\'20\'1D, which seems rather stark as such funding runs out. \u8220\'20\'1CMore Americans will die needlessly,\u8221\'20\'1D she says, if funding is allowed to lapse.\par \par \uc2 Psaki is asked about all the other pressing issues too: the price of living, of gas, the scarcity of baby formula. They all have their roots in the pandemic, she says. And the invasion of Ukraine by Russia. And there are good signs, Psaki insists, including strong economic performance in the US.\par \par \uc2 She rattles through Biden achievements on oil, internet access for the less well off, and so forth, like the pro she is. \u8220\'20\'1CLook at the alternative,\u8221\'20\'1D she says. \u8220\'20\'1CWhat are Republicans presenting as the option?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 A lot of questions are being asked about baby formula. Specifically, when will parents be able to get it.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C[The] \uc2 FDA\uc2  took a step to ensure that babies were taking safe formula,\u8221\'20\'1D Psaki says. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re going to work with manufacturers, we\u8217\'20\'19re going to import more to expedite this as quickly as possible.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Asked whether the government should push to produce more formula, Psaki says:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe production of baby formula is so specialised and so specific that you can\u8217\'20\'19t just use the Defense Production Act to say to a company that makes something else: produce baby formula.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A nationwide {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/12/abbott-baby-formula-shortage-recall"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 baby formula shortage}}}\uc2  has forced parents into online groups to swap and sell to each other to keep their babies fed.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/12/us-baby-formula-shortage"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US infant formula shortage: what you need to know}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Psaki\u8217\'20\'19s final White House briefing continues.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI promised myself I wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t get emotional,\u8221\'20\'1D she says. She succeeds.\par \par \uc2 Psaki thanks the president and first lady, and some staffers, and then the assembled members of the press.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWithout accountability and debate democracy is not as strong and you all play a pivotal role,\u8221\'20\'1D she says.\par \par \uc2 Before asking questions the White House press corps, not known for being the most combative of journalists, are each thanking Psaki for her service.\par \par \uc2 Psaki is asked if the president has a reaction to images from this morning of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/13/israeli-forces-storm-jerusalem-hospital-as-coffin-of-slain-journalist-emerges"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Israeli troops beating}}}\uc2  people carrying the casket of Shireen Abu Aqleh, a Palestinian-American journalist.\par \par \uc2 Abu Aqleh was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/11/al-jazeera-journalist-killed-in-west-bank-unrest"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shot in the head on Wednesday morning}}}\uc2  in the West Bank city of Jenin during what her colleagues at the scene said was a burst of Israeli fire on a small group of journalists covering an expected Israeli military raid.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have all seen those images and they\u8217\'20\'19re obviously deeply disturbing,\u8221\'20\'1D Psaki says. \u8220\'20\'1CWe regret the intrusion into what should have been a peaceful procession,\u8221\'20\'1D she adds. The \uc2 US government\uc2  has been in touch with both Israeli and Palestinian governments, she says.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  is holding her final White House press conference, and she\u8217\'20\'19s arrived with a couple of local officials.\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s a mayor and a chief of police. Psaki says they are sterling examples of how cities can use money from the 2021 $1.9tn Covid-19 relief package \u8211\'20\'13 the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/american-rescue-plan/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 American Rescue Plan}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 to provide \u8220\'20\'1Chistoric levels of support to make our communities safer\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Quinton Lucas\uc2 , the mayor of Kansas City, says money from the rescue plan \u8211\'20\'13 which was introduced to support Americans impacted by the coronavirus pandemic \u8211\'20\'13 has enabled the city to retain and hire more police officers.\par \par \uc2 The Detroit chief of police, \uc2 James White\uc2 , says money from the plan has helped train law enforcement officers, including crisis intervention training.\par \par \uc2 This comes as \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/white-house/biden-urge-cities-spend-covid-relief-money-police-crime-prevention-rcna28656"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 plans to urge}}}\uc2  states and cities to use unspent money from the Covid relief package to fund crime prevention programs and hire police officers.\par \par \uc2 When the plan was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/14/joe-biden-coronavirus-stimulus-package"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 introduced}}}\uc2  in January 2021 \u8211\'20\'13 Biden signed it into law the following March \u8211\'20\'13 Biden said it would help the \u8220\'20\'1Cmillions of Americans, [who] through no fault of their own, have lost the dignity and respect that comes with a job and a paycheck\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 New York attorney general's office "wrapping up" its investigation into Trump business\par \par \uc2 A lawyer for the New York attorney general\u8217\'20\'19s office said Friday that the office is \u8220\'20\'1Cnearing the end\u8221\'20\'1D of its three-year investigation into former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his business practices, The Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 Andrew Amer made the disclosure during a hearing in a federal lawsuit Trump filed against attorney general Letitia James as he seeks to put an end to her investigation.\par \par \uc2 His lawyers argued the probe is a politically motivated fishing expedition.\par \par \uc2 Attorney General Letitia James in announcing a fund to support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights for low-income New Yorkers and people from states that ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Photograph: snapshot/Future Image/J Nacion/REX/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 Trump is seeking a preliminary injunction to stop the investigation, which James has said uncovered evidence that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s company, the \uc2 Trump Organization\uc2 , misstated the value of assets like skyscrapers and golf courses on financial statements for over a decade.\par \par \uc2 James has asked a judge to dismiss Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawsuit.\par \par \uc2 US district judge Brenda Sannes said she would weigh both issues and deliver a decision in writing. She heard arguments for about an hour via video. She did not give a timetable for a ruling.\par \par \uc2 Trump lawyer Alina Habba argued that James, a Democrat, campaigned for office in 2018 as a Trump antagonist and, as attorney general, has used the office to harass the Republican former president and his company with myriad subpoenas and evidence requests. Habba said:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve produced millions and millions and millions of pages\u8221\'20\'1D of evidence...We keep getting subpoenas. They keep looking for things. If they don\u8217\'20\'19t find it, they look again.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  speaks from the podium during a rally, Sunday, May 1, 2022, in Greenwood, Neb. Photograph: Kenneth Ferriera/AP\par \par \uc2 Amer, a special litigation counsel for James, countered that the state judge overseeing legal fights over subpoenas issued by the attorney general\u8217\'20\'19s office has found there is a \u8220\'20\'1Csufficient basis for continuing its investigation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 That finding, combined with evidence uncovered to date, \u8220\'20\'1Creally shuts the door on any argument\u8221\'20\'1D by Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers that the office was proceeding in bad faith, Amer said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 Interim Summary\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s been a lively morning so far in US political news and there is more to come, so do stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where things stand:\par \par \uc2 * US defense secretary \uc2 Lloyd Austin\uc2  held a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/may/13/mike-pence-trump-brian-kemp-georgia-biden-us-politics-live?page=with:block-627e7a6a8f08493b6168c4b3#block-627e7a6a8f08493b6168c4b3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 call}}}\uc2  with Russian defense minister \uc2 Sergei Shoigu\uc2  on Friday in which he called for an immediate ceasefire in Ukraine\par \par \uc2 * In an overt break from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , former US vice president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  will hold a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/may/13/mike-pence-trump-brian-kemp-georgia-biden-us-politics-live?page=with:block-627e49ac8f08493b6168c1d9#block-627e49ac8f08493b6168c1d9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rally}}}\uc2  on May 23 with Georgia governor - and Trump foe - Brian Kemp, a day before Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s midterms Republican primary\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 US defense secretary urges ceasefire in call with Russian counterpart\par \par \uc2 Lloyd Austin\uc2 , the US defense secretary, held a call with Russian Defense Minister \uc2 Sergei Shoigu\uc2  on Friday in which he called for an immediate ceasefire in Ukraine, the Pentagon said.\par \par \uc2 During the call Austin also \u8220\'20\'1Cemphasized the importance of maintaining lines of communication\u8221\'20\'1D, according to Pentagon press secretary John Kirby.\par \par \uc2 The call is the first time Austin had spoken with Shoigu since February 18, six days before Russia invaded Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 The call came after Republican senator \uc2 Rand Paul{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/12/us-ukraine-aid-rand-paul-senate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blocked the passage of a $40bn aid bill}}}\uc2  for Ukraine on Thursday. The bill will be taken up again next week.\par \par \uc2 Russia has shown no signs of halting its aggression. On Friday the UK ministry of defence {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DefenceHQ/status/1524979878654840833"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  Russia was stepping up its attacks near the cities of Izyum and Severodonetsk, in eastern Ukraine, in an attempt to \u8220\'20\'1Cenvelop Ukrainian forces\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 Bernie Sanders has written an interesting op-ed piece today on his new Medicare for All bill, and it has been published in an interesting place: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.foxnews.com/opinion/medicare-for-all-sen-bernie-sanders"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fox News}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The op-ed appears to be an attempt to reach out to Americans who might not normally hear Sanders\u8217\'20\'19 case for universal healthcare.\par \par \uc2 It focuses on the cost and corruption of the medical healthcare system, as Sanders {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sanders.senate.gov/media/press-releases/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 champions his bill}}}\uc2 , which has 15 co-sponsors in the Senate. The legislation be implemented over a four-year period and would guarantee health care in the United States as a fundamental human right to all.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDespite spending more than twice as much on healthcare as the average developed country our health outcomes are worse than most. For example, our life expectancy is about 4.5 years lower than Germany\u8217\'20\'19s and we have the highest infant mortality rate of almost any major country on earth,\u8221\'20\'1D Sanders writes.\par \par \uc2 Sanders continues:\par \par \uc2 Now, if Medicare for All was so great, you might ask, why hasn\u8217\'20\'19t it been enacted by now? Why hasn\u8217\'20\'19t the United States joined every major country on earth in guaranteeing health care for all?\par \par \uc2 Well, the answer is pretty simple. Follow the money. Since 1998, in our corrupt political system, the private health care sector has spent more than $10.6 billion on lobbying and over the last 30 years it has spent more than $1.7 billion on campaign contributions to maintain the status quo. And, by the way, they are \u8220\'20\'1Cbi-partisan.\u8221\'20\'1D In fact, they own many of the politicians in both the Democratic and Republican parties.\par \par \uc2 Here is the bottom line: If every major country on earth can guarantee health care to all and achieve better health outcomes, while spending substantially less per capita than we do, there is no reason, other than greed, that the United States of America cannot do the same.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2 , the White House press secretary, will give her last briefing today, before {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/01/jen-psaki-press-secretary-msnbc-white-house"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly}}}\uc2  taking up a tv host role at MSNBC.\par \par \uc2 Psaki\u8217\'20\'19s departure will mark the end of a 16-month stint as \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s chief spokesperson. \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2 , currently the principal deputy press secretary, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/05/white-house-press-secretary-karine-jean-pierre"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will be taking over}}}\uc2 , becoming the first Black person and first out gay person in the role.\par \par \uc2 In joining MSNBC \u8211\'20\'13 a move that has not been officially announced, but was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2022/04/01/jen-psaki-leaving-white-house-msnbc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 revealed by Axios}}}\uc2  last month \u8211\'20\'13 Psaki is following a well-trodden path of White House communications to television pundit.\par \par \uc2 A slew of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s four former White House press secretaries, \uc2 Kayleigh McEnany\uc2  has gone on to be a Fox News host, while {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thewrap.com/hat-time-sean-spicer-dressed-as-easter-bunny-in-george-w-bushs-white-house/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sean Spicer}}}\uc2  has his own show on the right-wing network \uc2 Newsmax\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  and \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2 . Photograph: Michael Reynolds/\uc2 EPA\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Multiple rallies are set to take place on Saturday across the country as \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights activists take to the streets in opposition to the news that a majority of the Supreme Court favors overturning Roe v Wade, according to a draft {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/02/roe-v-wade-abortion-supreme-court-draft-opinion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruling}}}\uc2  leaked on May 2.\par \par \uc2 The so-called \u8220\'20\'1CBans Off Our Bodies\u8221\'20\'1D marches will take place across small towns and major cities, including Washington, DC, New York, Los Angeles, Boston, Birmingham and Chicago.\par \par \uc2 A coalition of pro-choice advocacy groups, including Planned Parenthood, UltraViolet, Move On and the Women\u8217\'20\'19s March, is helping organize Saturday\u8217\'20\'19s nationwide protests.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis Saturday we are taking to the streets to express our outrage\u8212\'20\'14and our determination,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Planned Parenthood Action Fund\uc2  executive director Kelley Robinson {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonian.com/2022/05/11/a-big-abortion-rights-protest-is-happening-saturday-heres-what-you-need-to-know/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  in a press statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access is in crisis, and Planned Parenthood organizations are proud to stand with partners and hundreds of thousands of people nationwide to come together and show that we reject the rollback our rights and freedoms,\u8221\'20\'1D she added.\par \par \uc2 With tens of thousands expected to turnout across the country, Saturday\u8217\'20\'19s protests could be the biggest women-focussed protest since the first official Women\u8217\'20\'19s March, held in Washington with support marches in other cities on January 21, 2017, the day after \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was inaugurated as president.\par \par \uc2 The brash Republican took the White House despite allegations from dozens of women about sexual harassment and misconduct, which he has always denied, and the emergence on the eve of the 2016 election of a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2016/oct/07/donald-trump-leaked-recording-women"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tape of him boasting}}}\uc2  that he just approaches women he is attracted to and grabs \u8220\'20\'1Cthem by the pussy\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In Washington DC, protestors are expected to march from the Washington Monument to the Supreme Court, which has been heavily {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2022/may/10/us-supreme-court-security-senate-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shielded}}}\uc2  with metal barricades since protests {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/03/us-supreme-court-abortion-protesters-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 immediately erupted}}}\uc2  after the draft decision was leaked that the supreme court is minded, with its conservative super-majority, to overturn the landmark 1973 Roe decision that established a woman\u8217\'20\'19s constitutional right to seek an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in America.\par \par \uc2 Many anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists are also expected to turn out in support of banning the procedure.\par \par \uc2 A pro-choice demonstrator holds a sign with a coat hanger, a symbol of the reproductive rights movement, in front of the \uc2 US Supreme Court\uc2  in Washington, DC. Photograph: Stefani Reynolds/AFP/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 Pence breaks overtly from Trump\par \par \uc2 Former US vice president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  plans to hold a rally for incumbent Georgia governor Brian Kemp on the eve of that state\u8217\'20\'19s midterms Republican primary - in very public defiance of former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  who has chosen to support Kemp\u8217\'20\'19s GOP rival.\par \par \uc2 The Georgia primary is on May 24 and Pence will hold the rally for Kemp on May 23.\par \par \uc2 Trump, who has repeatedly attacked Kemp for refusing to entertain his outlandish and untrue claims of voter fraud, has endorsed former \uc2 David Perdue\uc2  for the governorship, the former US Senator who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/06/jon-ossoff-wins-georgia-runoff-election-democrats-senate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lost his seat}}}\uc2  to Democrat \uc2 Jon Ossoff\uc2  in a sensational sweep by Democrats to turn Georgia blue in 2020.\par \par \uc2 Pence has gently gone against Trump in recent months. In March Pence {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/pence-trump-republicans-putin-apologists/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told Republican donors}}}\uc2  that \u8220\'20\'1Cthere is no room in this party for apologists for Putin\u8221\'20\'1D, comments which came a few days after Trump had called the Russian leader \u8220\'20\'1Csmart\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Csavvy\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Pence has also disputed Trump\u8217\'20\'19s nonsense claim that the former vice-president could have overturned the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 But Pence\u8217\'20\'19s enthusiastic endorsement of Kemp is his most overt pushback against Trump yet. It marks a big change from Pence, who was a famously sycophantic deputy during Trump\u8217\'20\'19s four-year term.\par \par \uc2 enltrFind someone who looks at you the way Pence looks at Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/lRzuEHq3ep"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/lRzuEHq3ep}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Daily Show (@TheDailyShow) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TheDailyShow/status/1228348423117639680?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 14, 2020}}}\par \par \uc2 Beyond the Pence-Trump intrigue, the Georgia governor primary will offer a revealing look at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s influence over Republican voters \u8211\'20\'13 and the future of the Republican party.\par \par \uc2 Trump has had some hits with his endorsed candidates for the Senate and the House so far this year, but appears to wield less influence in governors races. Trump endorsed \uc2 Charles Herbster\uc2  for Nebraska governor, but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2022/05/11/trump-pick-charles-herbster-loses-nebraska-gop-primary-governor-election.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hebster lost this week}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The former president has also endorsed a primary contender to Brad Little, the sitting governor of Nebraska, but Little is expected to win easily next week.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 Pence to hold rally with Georgia governor and Trump foe\par \par \uc2 Good morning and welcome to the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s coverage of daily US political news.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  has made himself a target for the ire of his former boss, by announcing he will holding a rally with Georgia governor \u8211\'20\'13 and Trump foe \u8211\'20\'13 Brian Kemp.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/05/13/pence-georgia-rally-kemp-00032306"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico reported}}}\uc2  that Pence will hold an event with Kemp on May 23, the day before a contentious Georgia primary. Trump, who has repeatedly attacked Kemp for refusing to entertain his outlandish and untrue claims of voter fraud, has endorsed Kemp\u8217\'20\'19s rival, \uc2 David Perdue\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 It sets up what will be revealing clash between Pence and Trump, who apparently remains furious that Pence did not do more to overturn the results of the 2020 presidential election.\par \par \uc2 Trump has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Wk5M7lRmJnw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 campaigned}}}\uc2  for Perdue, and the former president\u8217\'20\'19s political action committee has pumped money into \uc2 Perdue\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s campaign. But polling from April showed Kemp was likely to defeat Trump\u8217\'20\'19s man in the Republican primary.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, Pence called Kemp \u8220\'20\'1Cone of the most successful conservative governors in America\u8221\'20\'1D, per Politico.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBrian Kemp is my friend, a man dedicated to faith, family and the people of Georgia,\u8221\'20\'1D Pence said. \u8220\'20\'1CI am proud to offer my full support for four more years of Brian Kemp as governor of the great state of Georgia.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 In other news, \uc2 Rand Paul\uc2 , the Kentucky senator, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/12/us-ukraine-aid-rand-paul-senate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 single-handedly held up a bill}}}\uc2  on Thursday which would have pledged $40bn aid for Ukraine. Paul\u8217\'20\'19s blockage delayed passage of the measure into next week \u8211\'20\'13 the Senate has scheduled an initial procedural vote on the bill for late Monday afternoon.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will urge states to spend their coronavirus relief money on policing, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wmbfnews.com/2022/05/13/biden-meeting-with-mayors-police-chiefs-friday/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Associated Press}}}\uc2 . Biden will speak from the Rose Garden this afternoon, where he will highlight how some states have already spend their money on policing and public safety, and urge other local officials to do the same.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220513ei5d001ut\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
