\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 Prepare for McCarthy-era crackdowns on pro-choice protesters\b0\par\par\uc2 Andrew Perez and David Sirota \par \uc2 2,105 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 May 2022\par 13:01 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Conservatives and corporate media pundits want to use a Red Scare statute to arrest people demonstrating against the looming anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  victory\par \par \uc2 Even as the Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 feeble legislative attempt to codify federal protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/live/2022/05/11/us/abortion-roe-v-wade-senate-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 goes down in flames}}}\uc2 , many Washington elites are directing their attention and anger towards the same target: no, not rightwing judges reaching their ideological hands into millions of people\u8217\'20\'19s bodies, but instead the protesters peacefully demonstrating outside the homes of supreme court justices who are about to overturn Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 Prominent Republican lawmakers, conservative operatives and Beltway pundits are demanding the government arrest demonstrators \u8211\'20\'13 and to do so, they are citing a McCarthy-era statute passed to stop people from protesting against the prosecutions of alleged communists. Ignored in the discourse is a past ruling from the supreme court effectively {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/The_Law_Boy/status/1523725434634276864"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blessing}}}\uc2  conservative protests at the homes of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic workers.\par \par \uc2 The largely manufactured outrage is the latest distraction designed to shift attention away from the issue at hand: the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s conservative supermajority is about to deny basic reproductive rights to tens of millions of people in roughly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2022/05/05/1096738094/roe-v-wade-abortion-overturn-impact-world"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 half the country}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Conservative operatives want Washington reporters focused on inane questions like who leaked the court\u8217\'20\'19s draft opinion, and they want journalists and Democrats to criticize protesters who are outraged by the court\u8217\'20\'19s overriding lack of respect for people\u8217\'20\'19s bodily autonomy. It is part of a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.icnl.org/usprotestlawtracker/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 larger rightwing movement}}}\uc2  in recent years to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/21/us/politics/republican-anti-protest-laws.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cancel}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewtrusts.org/en/research-and-analysis/blogs/stateline/2021/06/21/eight-states-enact-anti-protest-laws"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 criminalize}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2017/08/18/us/legislation-protects-drivers-injure-protesters/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 literally crush}}}\uc2  dissent throughout the country, even as the conservative political noise machine continues to blare Braveheart-esque screams of \u8220\'20\'1Cfreedom!\u8221\'20\'1D against so-called \u8220\'20\'1Ccancel culture\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Corporate news outlets are taking the bait, fretting about the leak and calling for arrests over peaceful demonstrations. Like usual, they are focused on narrow flashpoints of anger and upheaval that will likely prove temporary, rather than the far more sweeping and ominous impact of the court\u8217\'20\'19s looming ruling to overturn the landmark 1973 Roe v Wade decision and allow states to force people to carry their pregnancies to term.\par \par \uc2 Even as the nation is poised to enact an injustice of historic proportions, those in power and their chosen mouthpieces only appear to care about one thing: upholding the rights and privileges of the ruling class, and ensuring they remain safely ensconced in the Washington bubble.\par \par \uc2 To his credit, the Senate Democratic leader, \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , issued the most rational statement of all: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/news/senate/3483411-schumer-says-he-sees-no-issue-with-protests-at-houses-of-supreme-court-justices/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 saying,}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1CMy house \u8211\'20\'13 there\u8217\'20\'19s protests three, four times a week outside my house. The American way to peacefully protest is OK.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But he has been drowned out by the noise machine demanding a crackdown.\par \par \uc2 The hypocrisy is particularly powerful among liberals like the Senate Democratic whip \uc2 Dick Durbin\uc2  of Illinois. He purports to support the pro-choice movement but he has spent his decades atop the Washington power structure {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.levernews.com/the-roe-disaster-and-what-to-do-about-it-2/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 failing to secure reproductive rights}}}\uc2 , and this week he has spent his time using his platform to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/news/senate/3484312-durbin-calls-protests-outside-supreme-court-justices-homes-reprehensible/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 deride}}}\uc2  the court protesters, calling them \u8220\'20\'1Creprehensible\u8221\'20\'1D. Durbin\u8217\'20\'19s behavior \u8211\'20\'13 emblematic of so many liberals and media elites \u8211\'20\'13 evokes the warning of \uc2 Martin Luther King\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI have been gravely disappointed with the white moderate,\u8221\'20\'1D King wrote in 1963 amid the civil rights struggle of his era. \u8220\'20\'1CThe white moderate who is more devoted to \u8216\'20\'18order\u8217\'20\'19 than to justice; who prefers a negative peace which is the absence of tension to a positive peace which is the presence of justice; who constantly says, \u8216\'20\'18I agree with you in the goal you seek, but I can\u8217\'20\'19t agree with your methods of direct action.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The ghost of McCarthy\par \par \uc2 Justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  authored the draft opinion in Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization that was leaked to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/05/02/supreme-court-abortion-draft-opinion-00029473"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico}}}\uc2  last week. In the opinion, Alito writes the Roe decision \u8220\'20\'1Cwas egregiously wrong from the start\u8221\'20\'1D and finds that the constitution \u8220\'20\'1Cdoes not prohibit the citizens of each state from regulating or prohibiting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The opinion adds that \u8220\'20\'1C??we cannot allow our decisions to be affected by any extraneous influences such as concern about the public\u8217\'20\'19s reaction to our work,\u8221\'20\'1D as if to hammer home the conservatives justices\u8217\'20\'19 contempt for the people whose lives they are seeking to upend.\par \par \uc2 Despite the court\u8217\'20\'19s supposed lack of concern about what the public thinks, tall fences were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/supreme-court/non-scalable-fence-erected-supreme-court-abortion-related-protests-rcna27452"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 quickly erected}}}\uc2  around the supreme court building. In recent days, protesters {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://deadline.com/2022/05/supreme-court-justices-see-protests-outside-homes-pro-choice-activists-1235018793/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/05/09/samuel-alito-home-protest-abortion-rights-00031285"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gathered}}}\uc2  outside the homes of Chief Justice \uc2 John Roberts\uc2 , Justice \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2  and Alito to register their opposition.\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s no evidence that the protests have been violent, and Congress is already fast-tracking legislation to allow the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s police force to provide security for justices\u8217\'20\'19 families. Notably, the bipartisan bill includes no additional security protections for people who go to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  facilities amid {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://revealnews.org/article/abortion-violence-roe-wade-florida/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 credible}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nwlc.org/whats-behind-the-rise-in-anti-abortion-violence/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 threats of violence}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But still, conservatives and elite pundits are calling for a major crackdown against dissent, pitting themselves against a first amendment that explicitly states the government may not pass any law \u8220\'20\'1Cabridging the freedom of speech, or of the press; or the right of the people peaceably to assemble, and to petition the government for a redress of grievances\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The right\u8217\'20\'19s weapon of choice is a law passed during the Red Scare hysteria of the 1950s.\par \par \uc2 Senator \uc2 Josh Hawley{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hawley.senate.gov/sites/default/files/2022-05/2022-05-10%20Letter%20to%20AG%20Garland%20about%20crimes%20related%20to%20abortion_JDHsigned_2.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2  a letter to the attorney general, \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2 , on Tuesday demanding the DoJ \u8220\'20\'1Cvigorously investigate and prosecute\u8221\'20\'1D those protesting at supreme court justices\u8217\'20\'19 homes.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFederal law makes it a crime for a person, \u8216\'20\'18with the intent of influencing any judge, juror, witness, or court officer, in the discharge of his duty\u8217\'20\'19, to \u8216\'20\'18picket[] or parade[] \u8230\'20\'26 in or near a building or residence occupied or used by such judge\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D, Hawley wrote, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CThe First Amendment is no shield to this illegal conduct.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  editorial board agreed with this premise, writing a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/opinions/2022/05/09/stop-protesting-outside-supreme-court-justice-houses/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 column}}}\uc2  on Monday arguing that it is crucial to \u8220\'20\'1Cprotect robust demonstrations of political dissent while preventing them from turning into harassment or intimidation\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 To do so, argued the Post, the nation should look to an old law. \u8220\'20\'1CA federal law \u8211\'20\'13 18 USC section 1507 \u8211\'20\'13 prohibits \u8216\'20\'18pickets or parades\u8217\'20\'19 at any judge\u8217\'20\'19s residence, \u8216\'20\'18with the intent of influencing\u8217\'20\'19 a jurist \u8216\'20\'18in the discharge of his duty\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D, noted the editorial. \u8220\'20\'1CThese are limited and justifiable restraints on where and how people exercise the right to assembly. \uc2 Citizens\uc2  should voluntarily abide by them, in letter and spirit. If not, the relevant governments should take appropriate action.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, Post columnist Marc Thiessen, who worked as the chief speechwriter for President \uc2 George W Bush\uc2  at the time that Roberts and Alito were confirmed to the court, amplified this argument, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/opinions/2022/05/10/abortion-protest-supreme-court-justice-homes-brett-kavanaugh-samuel-alito-john-roberts-illegal/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 writing}}}\uc2  an opinion piece calling on the Biden administration to \u8220\'20\'1Cenforce federal law barring harassment of the justices and their families in their homes\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The supposedly \u8220\'20\'1Climited and justifiable\u8221\'20\'1D anti-picketing statute being cited by all these people \u8211\'20\'13 18 USC \u167\'00\'A7 1507 \u8211\'20\'13 was enacted as part of the Internal Security Act of 1950, a law requiring communist organizations to register with the government. This particular statute was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/GPO-CRECB-1950-pt11/pdf/GPO-CRECB-1950-pt11-4.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 specifically written}}}\uc2  to respond to reports of protests outside federal courts during US prosecutions of alleged communist party leaders.\par \par \uc2 One of the statute\u8217\'20\'19s proponents, the segregationist senator Allen Ellender, a Louisiana Democrat, explained at the time: \u8220\'20\'1CThe practice of picketing courts is of recent origin, and apparently has been employed almost solely in connection with proceedings involving alleged Communist party members and sympathizers \u8230\'20\'26 If we are to keep our national judiciary on the high plane it has enjoyed since the founding of this country, we must restrain these disgraceful practices, adopted by persons and groups who would undermine our country by first undermining our judiciary.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The court has subsequently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mtsu.edu/first-amendment/article/1047/mccarran-internal-security-act-of-1950"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 struck down}}}\uc2  portions of the broader Internal Security Act. Furthermore, in 1983, the court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mtsu.edu/first-amendment/article/626/united-states-v-grace#:~:text=Grace%20(1983)&text=In%201983%2C%20the%20Supreme%20Court,Amendment's%20protection%20of%20free%20speech."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 limited}}}\uc2  the government\u8217\'20\'19s prohibition on protests outside the supreme court, finding that the first amendment protects picketing on sidewalks surrounding the court.\par \par \uc2 While the Post\u8217\'20\'19s Aaron Blake wrote a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2022/05/11/protest-justice-home-illegal/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 story}}}\uc2  on Wednesday headlined, \u8220\'20\'1CYes, experts say protests at \uc2 Scotus\uc2  justices\u8217\'20\'19 homes appear to be illegal,\u8221\'20\'1D one of conservatives\u8217\'20\'19 go-to constitutional law scholars has said that relying on the Internal Security Act statute to quash protests could have troubling constitutional implications.\par \par \uc2 George Washington University\uc2  law professor Jonathan Turley, who has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/opinion/judiciary/3480452-from-court-packing-to-leaking-to-doxing-white-house-yields-to-a-national-rage-addiction/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 criticized}}}\uc2  the protests at justices\u8217\'20\'19 houses, wrote a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/opinion/judiciary/3483105-protesting-at-justices-homes-should-be-a-subject-of-condemnation-not-criminal-charges/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 column}}}\uc2  in the Hill on Tuesday arguing that using the anti-picketing statute \u8220\'20\'1Cto arrest protesters would be a serious blow to free speech and would be difficult to defend in the courts\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He similarly told the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/podcasts/opinion-free-expression/jonathan-turley-and-the-fallout-from-the-supreme-court-leak/363adb0f-8af3-4b91-8516-f04140766c0f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wall Street Journal}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CAs a free speech advocate, I would be very concerned about the use of that statute. I think that what these protesters are doing is reprehensible. I think it\u8217\'20\'19s equally reprehensible for President [Joe] Biden not to denounce this. But when we start to charge protesters with crimes because they\u8217\'20\'19re appearing at the homes of figures, including supreme court justices, you really do raise some first amendment concerns.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Turley added: \u8220\'20\'1CI do think that if you brought a prosecution, it would raise some serious constitutional questions. And I would not bet on that being upheld on appeal.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Beyond the troubling historical legacy of the statute they are referencing, there is another problem with conservatives calling for the detention of these protesters: They only seem to worry about such demonstrations when they\u8217\'20\'19re being done by the left.\par \par \uc2 Hawley, for example, didn\u8217\'20\'19t call for anyone to \u8220\'20\'1Cvigorously investigate and prosecute\u8221\'20\'1D the insurrectionists who violently stormed the US Capitol last year. In fact, he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ksdk.com/article/news/politics/national-politics/senator-josh-hawley-photo-capitol-trump-supporters/63-3b5d7611-9d07-41bd-8113-a9ccf74ebb68"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cheered on}}}\uc2  those protesters shortly before the insurrection and since then, his campaign {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.huffpost.com/entry/josh-hawley-fist-pump-mug_n_6234c2dbe4b009ab92f852ab"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has been selling merchandise}}}\uc2  sporting pictures of him raising a fist to those insurrectionists.\par \par \uc2 Similarly, while the Post\u8217\'20\'19s editorial board noted that it was important to prevent political dissent \u8220\'20\'1Cfrom turning into harassment or intimidation\u8221\'20\'1D, the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement has been known to picket the homes of people who work at \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics \u8211\'20\'13 and worse. Violence against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://prochoice.org/national-abortion-federation-releases-2020-violence-disruption-statistics/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has been on the rise}}}\uc2 , and clinics around the country {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/news/us-news/abortion-clinics-protests-security-rcna27270"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are worried}}}\uc2  that attacks will spike after the supreme court issues its \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  decision.\par \par \uc2 What\u8217\'20\'19s more, the supreme court has in the past approved efforts by protesters to picket private residences \u8211\'20\'13 and specifically did so in a case involving protests by the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement outside the homes of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic workers.\par \par \uc2 In 1994, the supreme court found that a Florida court\u8217\'20\'19s content-neutral injunction creating a 300ft protest-free buffer zone around the residences of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic workers\u8217\'20\'19 homes was unconstitutional and over-broad. The court found \u8220\'20\'1Ca limitation on the time, duration of picketing, and number of pickets outside a smaller zone could have accomplished the desired result\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Finally, by selectively boosting outrage over public protests, corporate media is only making matters worse. After the \uc2 George Floyd\uc2  protests in 2020, major outlets {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=c6E2Nd4vXZk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appeared}}}\uc2  far more concerned about the specter of looters and rioters than they were about the actual grave injustice of a police officer murdering an unarmed Black man for allegedly using a counterfeit $20 bill.\par \par \uc2 News outlets have also been deeply perturbed by activists\u8217\'20\'19 calls to \u8220\'20\'1Cdefund\u8221\'20\'1D the police in the wake of Floyd\u8217\'20\'19s murder. While no cities have actually {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://therealnews.com/nobody-defunded-the-police-a-study"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 slashed}}}\uc2  police budgets, it\u8217\'20\'19s become incredibly common for pundits and conservative Democrats to say that the \u8220\'20\'1Cdefund\u8221\'20\'1D movement is weighing down the party.\par \par \uc2 Thanks to such selective hullabaloo, new legislative attempts to curtail public protests will likely be forthcoming \u8211\'20\'13 and unlike Democratic lawmakers\u8217\'20\'19 doomed attempt to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights on Wednesday, these efforts could be successful.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, the \uc2 US Senate\uc2  unanimously {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.congress.gov/bill/117th-congress/senate-bill/4160/text/is?q=%7B%22search%22%3A%5B%22cornyn%22%2C%22cornyn%22%5D%7D&r=1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed}}}\uc2  a measure offered by the Republican senator \uc2 John Cornyn\uc2  and Democrat Chris Coons to extend supreme court police protection to justices\u8217\'20\'19 families.\par \par \uc2 A previous version of the legislation {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.congress.gov/bill/117th-congress/senate-bill/4146/text?q=%7B%22search%22%3A%5B%22cornyn%22%2C%22cornyn%22%5D%7D&r=3&s=3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 offered}}}\uc2  by Cornyn would have allowed the supreme court police to arrest anyone who \u8220\'20\'1Cknowingly and willfully obstructs, resists, or interferes with a member of the supreme court police\u8221\'20\'1D busy protecting justices or their families.\par \par \uc2 Coons {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.coons.senate.gov/news/press-releases/sens-coons-cornyn-introduce-bill-to-extend-security-and-protection-for-scotus-justices-and-families"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 noted}}}\uc2  in a press release: \u8220\'20\'1CSections from an earlier draft of this bill were removed prior to introduction, citing free speech concerns.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Andrew Perez is a senior editor at the Daily Poster and a co-founder of the Democratic Policy Center\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 David Sirota is a Guardian US columnist and an award-winning investigative journalist. He is an editor-at-large at Jacobin, and the founder of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dailyposter.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Daily Poster}}}\uc2 . He served as Bernie Sanders\u8217\'20\'19 presidential campaign speechwriter\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 This article was originally published in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dailyposter.com/subscribe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Daily Poster}}}\uc2 , a grassroots-funded investigative news outlet\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220513ei5d001bc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
