\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Biden marks imminent \u8216\'20\'18tragic milestone\u8217\'20\'19 of 1m US Covid deaths in address to global summit \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Richard Luscombe \par \uc2 6,993 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 May 2022\par 20:47 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 President under pressure on multiple fronts domesticallySenators are expected to pass a $40bn Ukraine aid packageCapitol attack panel subpoenas five RepublicansSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 Thanks for joining us for a whirlwind day in US politics! We\u8217\'20\'19re closing this blog now, but you can keep on top of developments in the Ukraine-Russia conflict in our {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/may/12/russia-ukraine-war-news-live-updates-latest-putin-zelenskiy-finland-nato-bid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 24-hour live blog here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In a solemn start to the day, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  marked the imminent \u8220\'20\'1Ctragic milestone\u8221\'20\'1D of 1m Covid-19 deaths in the US, and used the second global Covid-19 summit to renew his call for Congress to approve a deal on a relief package.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s still so much left to do. This pandemic isn\u8217\'20\'19t over,\u8221\'20\'1D the president said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe mark a tragic milestone. One million empty chairs around the family dinner table, irreplaceable losses that each leave behind a family or community forever changed because of this pandemic\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Biden ordered flags to fly at half-mast around the country until the end of the weekend.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else we followed today:\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is considering a visit to the Korean demilitarized zone, when he makes the first trip to Asia of his presidency, White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  indicated.\par \par \uc2 * Senate leaders \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  and \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  urged senators from both parties to pass a $40bn Ukraine aid package, although objections in the chamber looked set to delay the vote.\par \par \uc2 * Federal prosecutors opened a grand jury investigation into \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s handling of classified White House material.\par \par \uc2 * The House committee investigating the 6 January Capitol attack incited by Trump subpoenaed the Republican House minority leader Kevin McCarthy and four other congressmen.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  explained why Democrats rejected legislation proposed by Republican senators that would codify \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, claiming states would still have too much power in determining women\u8217\'20\'19s right to choose.\par \par \uc2 * The nine \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  justices met for the first time since last week\u8217\'20\'19s leak of the draft opinion that would overturn almost half a century of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trip by Biden to DMZ between North and South Korea being considered - White House\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is considering a visit to the Korean demilitarized zone, when he makes the first trip to Asia of his presidency, White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  indicated moments ago.\par \par \uc2 The US president plans a trip to South Korea and Japan later this month. It came up at the briefing at the White House today, which is still underway, that Biden may go to the narrow neutral zone between North and South Korea.\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration also believes North Korea could be preparing for a new significant missile test, Psaki indicated.\par \par \uc2 A reporter asked: Does [Biden] intend to visit the DMZ and what\u8217\'20\'19s your current assessment of the threat of a North Korean nuclear test?\par \par \uc2 Psaki responded:\par \par \uc2 Well, on the first question, we\u8217\'20\'19re still finalizing details of the schedule for the trip and what it looks like. Obviously, that is a step that is taken by many who visit the region. But I expect we\u8217\'20\'19ll have our national security adviser here in the briefing room next week with Karine [ {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/05/white-house-press-secretary-karine-jean-pierre"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jean-Pierre}}}\uc2  ] to preview the trip.\par \par \uc2 In terms of whether we expect a test. The United States assesses that [North Korea] could be ready to conduct a test there as early as this month.\par \par \uc2 This would be its seventh such test. We\u8217\'20\'19ve shared this information with allies and partners and are closely coordinating with them.\par \par \uc2 As you noted, the president is traveling to the Republic of Korea and Japan next week, where he will continue strengthening these alliances and make clear our commitment to the security of the Republic of Korea.\par \par \uc2 The trip to Asia is scheduled from May 20 to May 24.\par \par \uc2 In 2019, then-president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  became the first incumbent US president to step into North Korea, after entering the DMZ, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2019/jun/30/trump-and-kims-dmz-meeting-proves-more-than-just-a-photo-op"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he met North Korean leader}}}\uc2  Kim Jong-un.\par \par \uc2 There was no tangible outcome from the meeting, in terms of North Korea pulling back on its nuclear weapons program or other issues.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has spoken with retailers and manufacturers to address a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/09/baby-formula-shortage-abbott"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 chronic shortage of baby formula in stores nationwide}}}\uc2 , the White House has said.\par \par \uc2 In her afternoon briefing, press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  said the president demanded that safe supplies be restored as soon as possible.\par \par \uc2 Earlier today, leading manufacturer \uc2 Abbott Laboratories{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/12/abbott-baby-formula-shortage-recall"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 warned it could take two months}}}\uc2  for its products to reach shelves after a nationwide recall.\par \par \uc2 Psaki said Biden spoke with chief executives of \uc2 Walmart\uc2  and Target to focus on restocking shelves, and said the administration would be looking at improving supplies through more imports, as well as asking the the federal trade commission and state attorneys general to clamp down on price gouging:\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ve already seen an increase in supply over the past couple of weeks. What we are seeing, which is an enormous problem, is hoarding, people hoarding because they\u8217\'20\'19re fearful, and people hoarding because they are trying to profit off fearful parents.\par \par \uc2 We do not want parents, mothers, families out there to be stressed and worried about feeding their babies.\par \par \uc2 Our message to parents is we hear you, we want to do everything we can, and we\u8217\'20\'19re going to cut every element of red tape to help address this and make it better.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ahead of huge protests planned this weekend against the prospect of Roe v Wade being overturned, US attorney general \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  has announced ramped up security for the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/us-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Supreme Court}}}\uc2  justices.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Attorney General directed the U.S. Marshals Service to help ensure the Justices\u8217\'20\'19 safety by providing additional support to the Marshal of the Supreme Court and Supreme Court Police,\u8221\'20\'1D the Department of Justice {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.justice.gov/opa/pr/justice-department-statement-regarding-supreme-court-security"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  in a press statement on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The attorney general\u8217\'20\'19s orders came after more than 100 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/05/09/samuel-alito-home-protest-abortion-rights-00031285"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 protestors marched}}}\uc2  earlier this week to the home of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2022/may/06/samuel-alito-profile-abortion-supreme-court-justice"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Justice Samuel Alito}}}\uc2 . Alito wrote the 98-page draft opinion about Roe v Wade, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/05/02/read-justice-alito-initial-abortion-opinion-overturn-roe-v-wade-pdf-00029504"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 leaked to Politico}}}\uc2  and published on May 2.\par \par \uc2 Pro-\b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights advocates stage a protest outside the house of Supreme Court Associate Justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  in the Fort Hunt neighborhood, in Alexandria, Virgina, USA, 09 May 2022. Photograph: Kent Nishimura/\uc2 EPA\par \par \uc2 The final court decision on whether to remove the constitutional right to seek an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  in the US, afforded by the landmark 1973 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe ruling}}}\uc2 , is expected next month.\par \par \uc2 In addition to Alito, protestors also gathered outside the homes of Chief Justice \uc2 John Roberts\uc2 , even though he was not one of the five conservative justices from the nine-member bench, who signed onto the draft opinion.\par \par \uc2 And there were also demonstrations outside the home of justice {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/brett-kavanaugh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh}}}\uc2  , who did sign on, in the draft opinion, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/03/biden-democrats-reaction-codifying-roe-v-wade-reform-scotus"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to overturn Roe}}}\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GovLarryHogan/status/1524494786031280128?s=20&t=ONJGaBRnZ4a-uWdxfQ0rNw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 According to}}}\uc2  federal statute Title 18, Section 1507 of the US code, it is illegal to picket or parade \u8220\'20\'1Cin or near a building or residence occupied or used by such judge, juror, witness, or court officer\u8221\'20\'1D with the \u8220\'20\'1Cintent of influencing any judge.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On Monday, senators swiftly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2022/may/10/us-supreme-court-security-senate-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed}}}\uc2  the Supreme Court Police Parity Act which seeks to expand protection of the justices and their families. The bill is awaiting to be passed onto the House where if approved, will then be transferred to the president for his signature.\par \par \uc2 White House Press Secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/presssec/status/1523649143951962115?s=21&t=u5D_Vw7kW08TcvsSTfXEWA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  that protests \u8220\'20\'1Cshould never include violence, threats, or vandalism.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 Workers took \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s name off his hotel on Pennsylvania Avenue in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/washington-dc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Washington DC}}}\uc2  on Wednesday, after the completion of the $375m sale of the lease to investors from Florida.\par \par \uc2 House Democrats estimate the former president, under {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/11/trump-fine-contempt-new-york-letitia-james"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 legal and financial pressure}}}\uc2  on multiple fronts, will {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/05/11/us/politics/trump-hotel-sale-washington.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly gain $100m from the sale}}}\uc2 , once a loan for the renovations is paid off.\par \par \uc2 One ethics group {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CREWcrew/status/1524542403889274880"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called}}}\uc2  the hotel \u8220\'20\'1Ca sinkhole of corruption\u8221\'20\'1D. During Trump\u8217\'20\'19s four years in the White House, the hotel became a magnet for aides, supporters and foreign businesses seeking favour.\par \par \uc2 Critics and ethics groups were particularly concerned about the situation as Trump did not formally divest himself from the \uc2 Trump Organization\uc2 . The presidential historian {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BeschlossDC"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Michael Beschloss}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BeschlossDC/status/1524507531984388097"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 predicted}}}\uc2  that even after the sale \u8220\'20\'1Cpolitical ghosts will linger\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The hotel lost more than $70m in the four years of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s presidency, including losses each year before pandemic shutdowns in 2020. Many hotel brokers, owners and consultants did not expect the 263-room hotel, located close to the White House, to fetch such a high price.\par \par \uc2 The price of the lease, equivalent to more than $1.4m a room, has drawn scrutiny from Democrats in Congress. \uc2 The New York Times{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/05/11/us/politics/trump-hotel-sale-washington.html?smtyp=cur&smid=tw-nytimes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  that \uc2 JLL\uc2 , a real estate firm, put the average sales price for hotels in Washington in 2020 at $354,000 per room.\par \par \uc2 CGI Merchant Group, the buyer, reportedly plans to turn the hotel into a branch of the Waldorf Astoria hotel chain. Earlier this month, the House oversight committee {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.govexec.com/oversight/2022/05/lawmakers-want-know-more-about-trump-hotel-sale/366685/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 requested documents}}}\uc2  from CGI, listing all investors, which reportedly include the former \uc2 New York Yankees\uc2  slugger and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2009/feb/10/alex-rodriguez-baseball-drugs-new-york-yankees-texas-rangers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 confessed}}}\uc2  drugs cheat Alex Rodriguez.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/12/sinkhole-corruption-trump-organization-closes-sale-washington-hotel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Sinkhole of corruption\u8217\'20\'19: Trump Organization sells Washington hotel}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 $40bn Ukraine aid package facing Senate delay\par \par \uc2 Senators were urged to pass a $40bn package of military, economic and humanitarian aid for Ukraine by the end of the day, despite last-minute obstacles placed by rogue Republicans.\par \par \uc2 Democratic and Republican leaders tried clearing the way for its passage Thursday afternoon, the Associated Press reports. The measure passed the House 368-57 on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 . Photograph: Samuel Corum/\uc2 EPA\par \par \uc2 Senate minority leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  called on \u8220\'20\'1Cboth sides to help us pass this urgent funding bill today\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The Kentucky Republican\u8217\'20\'19s pointed inclusion of his own colleagues came as the only apparent stumbling block seemed to be a demand from \uc2 Rand Paul\uc2 , the state\u8217\'20\'19s other senator, for an inspector general to scrutinize the new spending.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not allowing a speedy passage of the bill without having something fiscally responsible in the bill,\u8221\'20\'1D Paul told reporters.\par \par \uc2 New York Democrat \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , the senate majority leader, backed McConnell\u8217\'20\'19s call:\par \par \uc2 Republicans shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t block this bill. There is no reason, no reason whatever, not to get Ukraine funding approved fast.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has promised to quickly sign the bill, which he says is crucial to keep military aid, including howitzer artillery and other weaponry, flowing to Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 McConnell said:\par \par \uc2 Helping Ukraine is not an instance of mere philanthropy. It bears directly on America\u8217\'20\'19s national security and vital interests that Russia\u8217\'20\'19s naked aggression not succeed and carries significant costs.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 In probably the least surprising development of an already toxic Republican senate primary race in Pennsylvania, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has weighed in to savage a rival - albeit a far-right one - challenging his favored candidate, the television personality Mehmet Oz.\par \par \uc2 The recipient of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s snark is the self-declared \u8220\'20\'1CAmerica First\u8221\'20\'1D hopeful Kathy Barnette, a political commentator who has surged in popularity in recent weeks to a point where, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2022/05/12/gop-panics-pa-senate-wild-card-kathy-barnette"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to Axios}}}\uc2 , Republicans are \u8220\'20\'1Cpanicking\u8221\'20\'1D she might actually win.\par \par \uc2 Kathy Barnette. Photograph: Michael M Santiago/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 Barnette, who claims she was the product of her mother\u8217\'20\'19s rape at the age of 11, has a long history of controversial and extremist views. She is in the almost certainly unique position of being a Black Republican who has drawn criticism from all wings of the party, from Trump to \uc2 Pat Toomey\uc2 , the moderate senator whose retirement has opened up the Pennsylvania seat.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CKathy Barnette will never be able to win the General Election against the Radical Left Democrats,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump declares in his statement, littered as always with unorthodox grammar and punctuation, and random uppercase letters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShe has many things in her past which have not been properly explained or vetted, but if she is able to do so, she will have a wonderful future in the Republican Party - and I will be behind her all the way.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDr Oz is the only one who will be able to easily defeat the Crazed, Lunatic Democrat in Pennsylvania. A vote for anyone else in the Primary is a vote against Victory in the Fall!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Oz has a narrow advantage in the polls for the 17 May primary over Barnette and David McCormick, an Army veteran and \uc2 George W Bush\uc2  administration official favored by many mainstream Republicans.\par \par \uc2 But Maga voters, as the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/09/dr-oz-trump-pennsylvania-republican-senate-primary"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ed Pilkington found at a Trump rally in Greensburg}}}\uc2  earlier this month, don\u8217\'20\'19t quite know what to make of him.\par \par \uc2 Exactly who is the \u8220\'20\'1Ccrazed lunatic\u8221\'20\'1D Trump refers to is anyone\u8217\'20\'19s guess. There are four candidates for the Democratic nomination, including congressman \uc2 Conor Lamb\uc2  and Pennsylvania\u8217\'20\'19s lieutenant governor John Fetterman.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Interim summary\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s been a lively morning so far in US political news and there is more to come, so do stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where things stand:\par \par \uc2 * Federal prosecutors have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/may/12/biden-us-covid-death-rate-response-inflation-abortion-politics-latest?page=with:block-627d49818f083b856379954f#block-627d49818f083b856379954f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 opened}}}\uc2  a grand jury investigation into Trump\u8217\'20\'19s handling of classified White House material, the NYT reports\par \par \uc2 * The House committee investigating the January 6, 2021 Capitol riots {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/may/12/biden-us-covid-death-rate-response-inflation-abortion-politics-latest?page=with:block-627d44018f08493b6168b8b2#block-627d44018f08493b6168b8b2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 subpoenaed}}}\uc2  Congressman Kevin McCarthy, the top Republican in the House of Representatives, along with other lawmakers on Thursday\par \par \uc2 * House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/may/12/biden-us-covid-death-rate-response-inflation-abortion-politics-latest?page=with:block-627d379b8f08493b6168b80c#block-627d379b8f08493b6168b80c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 explained}}}\uc2  why Democrats rejected legislation proposed by Republican senators that would codify \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CWhat\u8217\'20\'19s in the Republican bill would enable states to do very destructive things when it comes to a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to choose\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * All nine \uc2 US Supreme Court\uc2  justices are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/may/12/biden-us-covid-death-rate-response-inflation-abortion-politics-latest?page=with:block-627d15128f083b8563799209#block-627d15128f083b8563799209"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 meeting}}}\uc2  for the first time on Thursday since last week\u8217\'20\'19s leak of the draft opinion that would overrule Roe v Wade\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has marked the \u8220\'20\'1Ctragic milestone\u8221\'20\'1D of 1m Covid-19 deaths in the US by renewing his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/may/12/biden-us-covid-death-rate-response-inflation-abortion-politics-latest?page=with:block-627d093a8f08e6ce3a77d8f6#block-627d093a8f08e6ce3a77d8f6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 calls }}}\uc2  to Congress to strike a deal on a relief package\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Prosecutors pursue inquiry into Trump\u8217\'20\'19s handling of classified material - NYT\par \par \uc2 Federal prosecutors have opened a grand jury investigation to try to establish whether \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  mishandled classified White House materials that he had access to while he was the president and that have since been found at Mar-a-Lago, the residence he moved to after he lost the election to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , the \uc2 New York Times{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/05/12/us/politics/justice-department-trump-classified.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The outlet speaks of an \u8220\'20\'1Cintensifying inquiry\u8221\'20\'1D indicating that the Department of Justice is looking into how Trump and senior aides handled sensitive documents in the dying days of the Republican\u8217\'20\'19s one-term presidency.\par \par \uc2 It writes:\par \par \uc2 In recent days, the Justice Department has taken a series of steps showing that its investigation has progressed beyond the preliminary stages. Prosecutors issued a subpoena to the \uc2 National Archives and Records Administration\uc2  to obtain the boxes of classified documents, according to the two people familiar with the matter, who spoke on condition of anonymity because of the ongoing investigation.\par \par \uc2 The authorities have also made interview requests to people who worked in the White House in the final days of Mr. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s presidency, according to one of the people.\par \par \uc2 The investigation is focused on the discovery by the National Archives in January that at the end of Mr. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s term he had taken to his home at the Mar-a-Lago resort 15 boxes from the White House that contained government documents, mementos, gifts and letters.\par \par \uc2 After the boxes were returned to the National Archives, its archivists found documents containing \u8220\'20\'1Citems marked as classified national security information,\u8221\'20\'1D the agency told Congress in February. In April, it was reported that federal authorities were in the preliminary stages of investigating the handling of the classified documents.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe intensifying inquiry suggests that the Justice Department is examining the role of Mr. Trump and other officials in his White House in their handling of sensitive materials during the final stages of his administration. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/maggieNYT?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @maggieNYT}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/nytmike?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @nytmike}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/mEmD78IIvN"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/mEmD78IIvN}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Adam Goldman (@adamgoldmanNYT) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/adamgoldmanNYT/status/1524806815971782656?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 12, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 The select committee empowered the panel\u8217\'20\'19s chairman, congressman \uc2 Bennie Thompson\uc2 , to move ahead with subpoenas to House minority leader Kevin McCarthy and other {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2  including Jim Jordan, Scott Perry, and Andy Biggs and Mo Brooks, the sources said.\par \par \uc2 U.S. Rep. \uc2 Bennie Thompson\uc2  (D-MS) exits the office of House Speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  (D-CA) at the U.S. Capitol in Washington, U.S., April 27, 2022. Photograph: Tom Brenner/Reuters\par \par \uc2 Members on the select committee empowered Thompson to take the extraordinary step to subpoena Republican members of Congress after the five flatly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jan/12/kevin-mccarthy-january-6-panel-capitol-riot"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 refused to accept invitations}}}\uc2  to provide voluntary assistance to the investigation, the sources said.\par \par \uc2 The select committee is seeking to compel some of the most sensitive information about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s efforts to overturn the results of the 2020 election in its subpoenas to the Republican members of Congress, the sources said.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/09/capitol-attack-panel-subpoenas-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported earlier this week}}}\uc2  that the panel was moving closer to issuing subpoenas to Republican members of Congress, appalled at their refusal to assist the investigation in any way despite prima facie connections to the events of 6 January.\par \par \uc2 What changed for members of the select committee, according to sources familiar with internal deliberations, was that they could no longer ignore what appeared to be deep involvement in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s unlawful schemes to overturn the 2020 election results.\par \par \uc2 The scope and targets of the subpoenas are not final until the orders are made public, and the sources cautioned that details could still change. But the subpoenas are expected to encompass the contents of the letters seeking voluntary cooperation, they said.\par \par \uc2 That would indicate the select committee {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://january6th.house.gov/sites/democrats.january6th.house.gov/files/2022-1-12.BGT%20Letter%20to%20McCarthy.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 intends to ask McCarthy}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 the top Republican in the House \u8211\'20\'13 about what he knew of the former president\u8217\'20\'19s involvement in, and response to, the Capitol riots, as well as why Trump believed he was at fault for the riot.\par \par \uc2 It also suggests House investigators are interested in seeking more detail about meetings between Trump and Republican members of Congress at the White House before the Capitol attack where they strategized ways to stop \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s certification on 6 January.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 House panel investigating Capitol insurrection subpoenas GOP's McCarthy\par \par \uc2 Congressman Kevin McCarthy, the top Republican in the \uc2 US House of Representatives\uc2 , and other lawmakers on Thursday received subpoenas from the House committee investigating last year\u8217\'20\'19s attack on the US Capitol by supporters of then-president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , an escalation of the panel\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/28/capitol-attack-panel-kevin-mccarthy-republicans-letters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 secure their testimony}}}\uc2 , Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 The January 6 House Select Committee had previously {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/28/capitol-attack-panel-kevin-mccarthy-republicans-letters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sent letters}}}\uc2  to Republican lawmakers, asking for their voluntary cooperation with the panel\u8217\'20\'19s investigation.\par \par \uc2 House Minority Leader Kevin McCarthy, R-Calif., talks to reporters at the Capitol in Washington, April 6, 2022. Photograph: J Scott Applewhite/AP\par \par \uc2 The panel had a renewed interest in McCarthy\u8217\'20\'19s cooperation after new reporting last month showed he had told the Republican leadership days after January 6 that Trump admitted to him at least partial responsibility for the Capitol attack, sources said.\par \par \uc2 The select committee is particularly focused on whether Trump might have indicated to McCarthy why he believed he was culpable for the Capitol attack, the sources said, and whether the former president knew he may have acted unlawfully on January 6.\par \par \uc2 A huge, violent mob invaded the Capitol in an attempt to prevent the official certification by a joint session of Congress - ie the Senate and House - of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s victory over Trump in the November 2020 presidential election.\par \par \uc2 Trump had earlier goaded crowds at a rally near the White House to make their way to Capitol, urging supporters that they needed to \u8220\'20\'1Cfight like hell\u8221\'20\'1D to defend his presidency.\par \par \uc2 The insurrection ultimately failed and Biden\u8217\'20\'19s win was certified in the early hours of the next day, after lawmakers, media and staff had run for their lives from the deadly rioters.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Pelosi rejects Republican bill to codify \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights\par \par \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  has been explaining why Democrats rejected legislation proposed by Republican senators \uc2 Susan Collins\uc2  and Lisa Murkowski that would codify Roe v Wade \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections into federal law.\par \par \uc2 At her weekly briefing, the House speaker spelled out why her party pushed the women\u8217\'20\'19s health protection act, which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/11/senate-abortion-rights-bill-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 failed in the US Senate yesterday}}}\uc2 , instead of backing the more restrictive but still protective reproductive rights act from the pro-choice Republicans, seen as more likely to have attracted bipartisan support.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s not enough just to pass a bill to have a compromise. It\u8217\'20\'19s not a compromise, because what\u8217\'20\'19s in the Republican bill would enable states to do very destructive things when it comes to a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to choose.\par \par \uc2 Pelosi explained that while both bills would have enshrined into law the basics of Roe v Wade, the 1973 ruling guaranteeing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections, which the supreme court looks set to reverse, the Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 act would go further.\par \par \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  addresses reporters on Thursday. Photograph: Mariam Zuhaib/AP\par \par \uc2 It would, she said, have added the protections given by the 1992 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://supreme.justia.com/cases/federal/us/505/833/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Planned Parenthood v Casey}}}\uc2  ruling, which dealt with other issues including the viability of a fetus and restrictions on how far states could go in tinkering with the provisions of Roe:\par \par \uc2 This is not a public policy debate that is isolated from the personal impact that it has on the lives of women, whether it\u8217\'20\'19s contraception, whether it\u8217\'20\'19s invitro fertilization, whether it\u8217\'20\'19s a post-miscarriage care, whether its size and timing of a family.\par \par \uc2 It is personal between a woman, her doctor, her God [and] her family, not the supreme court, or the \uc2 Congress of the United States\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 The US was today confirmed as the host of the 2031 men\u8217\'20\'19s Rugby World Cup and the 2033 women\u8217\'20\'19s event.\par \par \uc2 This is not particularly political news, except \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  formally supported the bid, as we reported {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2022/apr/20/joe-biden-us-rugby-world-cup-bid-letter-bill-beaumont"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 , and has been known to be very enthusiastic about the game, as we reported {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2021/jul/23/joe-biden-rugby-fan-mlr-ireland-all-blacks-syracuse-law-school"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 . And {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/nov/13/biden-ireland-rugby-union-new-zealand"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 We (OK, I) have also reported about how politicians from both sides of the aisle have played and loved the game, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/blog/2018/jun/01/famous-american-rugby-players-wales-v-south-africa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2018/may/28/hr-mcmaster-rugby-warrior-ethos"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/oct/03/hr-mcmaster-donald-trump-national-security-adviser-battlegrounds-book"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 elsewhere}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  is working on a follow-up piece about what the bid announcement might mean for American rugby, and in the course of harvesting statements has spoken both to the Congressional Rugby Caucus (co-chairs \uc2 Eleanor Holmes Norton\uc2 , Democrat of Washington DC and Alex Mooney, Republican of West Virginia).\par \par \uc2 Statements are awaited. In the meantime \uc2 Chris Murphy\uc2 , the Democratic senator from Connecticut, has confirmed he was a college rugby player and said the following:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI was first introduced to rugby at Williams, and although I wasn\u8217\'20\'19t very good, I loved the sport and made lifelong friends. I am excited that the U.S. will host the men\u8217\'20\'19s and women\u8217\'20\'19s Rugby World Cups and look forward to it introducing even more Americans to the game.\par \par \uc2 For further reading, here\u8217\'20\'19s the US Eagles men\u8217\'20\'19s fly-half or full-back Will Hooley on What This All Means For The Game:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/blog/2022/may/12/we-can-build-it-they-will-come-a-usa-rugby-world-cup-will-be-a-gamechanger"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 We can build it, they will come: a USA Rugby World Cup will be a gamechanger | Will Hooley}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 A baseball signed by Ukrainian president \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2  has sold at auction for more than $50,000, the Associated Press reports, with a portion going to Ukrainians displaced in the war with Russia.\par \par \uc2 Boston auctioneer RR Auction said the winning bid for the Rawlings Major League baseball was more than three times its estimate. The company will donate its $15,000 cut of the sale, while seller Randy Kaplan will also donate an undisclosed portion of his proceeds.\par \par \uc2 The ball is signed in black felt tip in Ukrainian Cyrillic and Latin letters. It is accompanied by a transmittal letter signed by Volodymyr Yelchenko, permanent representative of Ukraine to the United Nations.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Local officials have rejected a request from Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor Glenn Youngkin to set up a security perimeter outside the homes of three conservative supreme court justices to thwart pro-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protestors.\par \par \uc2 Officials in Fairfax county say such a move at the residences of \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2 , Amy Coney Barrett and \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  would infringe on the protesters\u8217\'20\'19 first amendment rights.\par \par \uc2 Demonstrators gathered at their homes, and outside that of Justice \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2  in Maryland, after last week\u8217\'20\'19s leaked supreme court draft ruling written by Alito ending almost half a century of constitutional protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 Glenn Youngkin. Photograph: Kendall Warner/AP\par \par \uc2 Youngkin wrote to Fairfax\u8217\'20\'19s county board of supervisors Wednesday, stating: \u8220\'20\'1CI fundamentally believe such demonstrations and picketing should not be allowed at the Justice\u8217\'20\'19s [sic] homes as they are meant to intimidate and influence the Justices\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Fairfax, though, is having none of it.\par \par \uc2 In a forthright written reply, according to the Associated Press, board chair Jeff McKay said the request is \u8220\'20\'1Cunnecessary and improper\u8221\'20\'1D and would amount to creating an unconstitutional neighborhood \u8220\'20\'1Ccheckpoint\u8221\'20\'1D that would infringe on first amendment protest rights.\par \par \uc2 He also noted that protests that have occurred outside Alito\u8217\'20\'19s home in the Fort Hunt neighborhood have been peaceful.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe will enforce laws that serve to protect persons and property,\u8221\'20\'1D McKay wrote.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur officers are equally committed to protecting the first amendment guarantees afforded to those who gather to exercise their freedom of speech.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump officials \u8220\'20\'1Ccollaborated\u8221\'20\'1D with the meatpacking industry to downplay the threat of Covid to plant workers and block public health measures which could have saved lives, a damning new investigation has found.\par \par \uc2 Internal documents reviewed by the congressional select subcommittee on the coronavirus crisis reveal how industry representatives lobbied government officials to stifle \u8220\'20\'1Cpesky\u8221\'20\'1D health departments from imposing evidence-based safety measures to curtail the virus spreading \u8211\'20\'13 and tried to obscure worker deaths from these authorities.\par \par \uc2 At least 59,000 workers at five of the largest meatpacking companies \u8211\'20\'13 \uc2 Tyson Foods\uc2 , \uc2 JBS USA Holdings\uc2 , \uc2 Smithfield Foods\uc2 , Cargill and \uc2 National Beef Packing Company\uc2  which are the subject of the congressional inquiry \u8211\'20\'13 contracted Covid in the first year of the pandemic, of whom at least 269 died.\par \par \uc2 According to internal communications, the companies were warned about workers and their families falling sick within weeks of the virus hitting the US. Despite this, company representatives enlisted industry-friendly Trump appointees at the \uc2 USDA\uc2  to fight their battles against Covid regulations and oversight.\par \par \uc2 In addition, company executives intentionally stoked fears about meat shortages in order to justify continuing to operate the plants under dangerous conditions.\par \par \uc2 The fears were baseless \u8211\'20\'13 there were no meat shortages in the US, while exports to China hit record highs.\par \par \uc2 Yet in April 2020, \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/apr/28/trump-executive-order-meat-processing-plants-coronavirus"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 issued an executive order}}}\uc2  invoking the Defense Production Act to keep meat plants open following a flurry of communication between the White House chief of staff, \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2 , the vice-president\u8217\'20\'19s office, \uc2 USDA\uc2  allies and company executives.\par \par \uc2 Read the full story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2022/may/12/meatpacking-industry-trump-downplay-covid-threat"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump officials and meat industry blocked life-saving Covid controls, investigation finds}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Leaders from the \uc2 Association of South-East Asian Nations\uc2  will meet with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  at the White House later today, with the president making efforts to show he hasn\u8217\'20\'19t forgotten them while the US focuses on Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Ukraine, the Associated Press says.\par \par \uc2 Biden will host dinner for the leaders of eight of the 10 Asean nations attending the two-day summit, before more formal talks at the state department tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 China\u8217\'20\'19s rising influence in the region will be among the topics discussed with leaders from Brunei, Cambodia, Indonesia, Laos, Malaysia, Singapore, Thailand and Vietnam. The two other Asean members, Myanmar and the Philippines, are not expected to attend, the AP says.\par \par \uc2 The Asean leaders were meeting \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , the House speaker, and lawmakers on Capitol Hill this morning.\par \par \uc2 A White House Asia policy adviser told the news agency that the administration remains committed to stepping up relations with Asean nations to address climate, economic and education initiatives.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere has been a sense that in previous administrations that we had set off with a determined pace to focus on East Asia or in the Indo-Pacific and then find ourselves with other pressing challenges that perhaps draws [us] away a little bit,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Kurt Campbell\uc2 , coordinator for Indo-Pacific affairs on the White House national security council, said, acknowledging the conflict in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Campbell took part in a discussion earlier this week previewing the US-Asean summit.\par \par \uc2 enltrThanks for following our preview of this week's U.S.-ASEAN Special Summit with \uc2 Kurt Campbell\uc2 . Watch it again here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/sq4b0EsMp5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/sq4b0EsMp5}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/ASEANUSIP?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #ASEANUSIP}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 U.S. Institute of Peace\uc2  (@USIP) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/USIP/status/1524389314553069568?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 11, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Back to the ongoing second global Covid-19 summit, and we\u8217\'20\'19re learning that the event has attracted $3bn in previously unannounced funds to fight the pandemic.\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2022/05/12/2nd-global-covid-19-summit-commitments/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 White House fact sheet}}}\uc2  just released says $2bn will be available \u8220\'20\'1Cfor immediate Covid-19 response\u8221\'20\'1D and that $962m will be allocated for \u8220\'20\'1Ca new pandemic preparedness and global health security fund at the \uc2 World Bank\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The money is coming from dozens of countries and organizations worldwide who are supporting the summit and, as the White House put it, supporting \u8220\'20\'1Ccollective efforts to get shots into arms, enhance access to tests and treatments, protect the health workforce, and finance and build health security for future pandemics and other health crises\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  issued a joint statement with \uc2 Ursula von der Leyen\uc2 , president of the European commission, which says it is committing $450m to the pandemic preparedness fund.\par \par \uc2 enltrAll regions should have the capacity to prevent pandemic outbreaks & produce their own vaccines & other tools, locally. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/EU_Commission?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @EU_Commission}}}\uc2  plans to make a $450 million contribution to the global pandemic preparedness fund agreed in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/G20?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #G20}}}\uc2 , as soon as its governance is established.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Ursula von der Leyen\uc2  (@vonderleyen) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/vonderleyen/status/1524757284139765760?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 12, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Republican Montana senator Steve Daines continues to reap a whirlwind of mockery for his comments this week comparing pregnant women to sea turtles.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, Daines appeared on the senate floor to rail against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , using an oversize image of six babies in diapers and a number of swimming or hatching turtles as a prop.\par \par \uc2 Steve Daines. Photograph: Reuters\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf you were to take or destroy the eggs of a sea turtle, the criminal penalties are severe,\u8221\'20\'1D Daines asserted.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhy do we have laws in place that protect the eggs of a sea turtle or the eggs of eagles? Because when you destroy an egg, you\u8217\'20\'19re killing a preborn baby sea turtle or a preborn baby eagle.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrDaines on \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 : Why do we have laws in place to protect the eggs of a sea turtle or the eggs of eagles\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/yr0dM7aaAs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/yr0dM7aaAs}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Acyn (@Acyn) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Acyn/status/1524129432213987328?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 10, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The backlash was swift, and not altogether complimentary. \uc2 Twitter\uc2  users in particular were quick to mock the senator, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.huffpost.com/entry/steve-daines-sea-turtles-abortion_n_627c8af6e4b0b74b0e7efbaa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HuffPost compiling a gallery of responses}}}\uc2 , including one with a photo of Daines and a fish he caught, accusing him of \u8220\'20\'1Cmurdering a fish and all the offspring it could produce\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Daines then took umbrage at the barrage of insults, issuing a tweet on Wednesday accusing those who mocked him as throwing a \u8220\'20\'1Cturtle tantrum\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe liberal \uc2 Twitter\uc2  mob throwing a turtle tantrum are the same people who believe men can get pregnant,\u8221\'20\'1D he wrote, without any supporting evidence.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe Liberal \uc2 Twitter\uc2  mob throwing a turtle tantrum are the same people who believe men can get pregnant.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Steve Daines (@SteveDaines) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SteveDaines/status/1524430777710170113?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 11, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Presumably hoping to put the turtle tale behind him, Daines has since reverted to tweeting about more familiar, and arguably safer topics, including attacks on \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  for inflation and gas prices, and wishing the Glacier national park a happy birthday.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Among the rightwing crusaders promoting \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s false claims that the 2020 election was stolen, wealthy pillow entrepreneur Mike Lindell occupies a key niche, spending lavishly on lawsuits to ban voting machines in some states, endorsing big lie advocates for top offices in 2022 and financing an anti-voting machine film, plus related projects.\par \par \uc2 In some respects, Lindell is an unlikely figure to emerge in the hotbed of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-politics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US politics}}}\uc2  and the conservative ecosystem. As the chief executive of MyPillow he was once better known for his TV adverts than his extremist politics. But Lindell has become an ally of a still-powerful Trump who is eying a 2024 bid to return to the White House. Lindell has also become a popular figure on the right himself, making several appearances at recent Trump rallies.\par \par \uc2 Mike Lindell. Photograph: Anadolu Agency/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 But election experts and voting watchdogs say Lindell\u8217\'20\'19s legal blitz to ditch voting machines, and other drives that sustain Trump\u8217\'20\'19s baseless claims about widespread fraud in the 2020 election, are deeply flawed and dangerous and potentially further damage voter confidence in elections.\par \par \uc2 Lindell though sounds undaunted, telling the Guardian that he has spent about $30m to retain about 70 lawyers, cyber consultants, private investigators and other staffers for his projects to prove widespread fraud in the 2020 elections, despite mountains of contrary evidence, and expand his crusade to get rid of voting machines.\par \par \uc2 Last month Lindell pumped about $500,000 dollars into an Arizona lawsuit filed by two Trump and Lindell backed state candidates for Secretary of State and Governor, Mark Finchem and Kari Lake, respectively, to obtain a preliminary injunction against voting machines that Lindell has repeatedly charged are defective.\par \par \uc2 Lindell said that he plans to underwrite similar anti voting machine lawsuits in the next few months in many other states including Colorado, South Dakota, Texas, Wisconsin, Michigan and Alabama. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19d like to file the lawsuits in all 50 states,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CI didn\u8217\'20\'19t come all this way not to succeed. We\u8217\'20\'19ve got to get rid of them all.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 To further spur his conservative agenda, Lindell has publicly endorsed several candidates for top posts in battleground states including Lake and Finchem, who early this month benefitted from a Trump sponsored fundraiser at Mar-a-Lago that Lindell attended.\par \par \uc2 Read the full story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/12/mike-lindell-trump-election-big-lie"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18I\u8217\'20\'19d like to file lawsuits in all 50 states\u8217\'20\'19: Mike Lindell still pushing Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lie}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 Supreme court meets for first time since \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights leak\par \par \uc2 The nine supreme court justices are meeting Thursday for the first time since last week\u8217\'20\'19s leak of a draft opinion that would overrule the 1973 Roe v Wade opinion and sharply curtail \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in roughly half the states.\par \par \uc2 According to the Associated Press, the meeting in the justices\u8217\'20\'19 private, wood-paneled conference room could be a tense affair in a setting noted for its decorum. Nobody other than the justices attends, with the most junior, Amy Coney Barrett, responsible for taking notes.\par \par \uc2 Amy Coney Barrett. Photograph: Sarah Silbiger/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 As the AP recognizes, Thursday\u8217\'20\'19s conference comes at a fraught moment, with the future of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights at stake and an investigation underway to try to find the source of the leak.\par \par \uc2 Chief Justice \uc2 John Roberts\uc2  last week confirmed the authenticity of the opinion, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/05/02/supreme-court-abortion-draft-opinion-00029473"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 revealed by Politico}}}\uc2 , in ordering the court\u8217\'20\'19s marshal to undertake an investigation.\par \par \uc2 Roberts stressed that the draft, written by Justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  and circulated in February, may not be the court\u8217\'20\'19s final word.\par \par \uc2 Supreme court decisions are not final until they are formally issued and the outcomes in some cases changed between the justices\u8217\'20\'19 initial votes shortly after arguments and the official announcement of the decisions.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, a Democrat-led effort to enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights into federal law failed in the UN Senate.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/11/senate-abortion-rights-bill-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats lose Senate vote to codify \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights into federal law}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden: 'We have to prevent Covid-19 complacency'\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  marked the imminent \u8220\'20\'1Ctragic milestone\u8221\'20\'1D of 1m deaths in the US in his address to the second global Covid-19 summit this morning, and renewed his call to Congress to strike a deal on a coronavirus relief package.\par \par \uc2 Biden highlighted the urgency of his $22.5bn request, which he says is crucial to fund vaccines, treatments and testing domestically, as well as boosting global efforts to end the emergency:\par \par \uc2 Today, we\u8217\'20\'19re at a new stage in fighting this pandemic, facing an evolving set of challenges. We have to double down on our efforts to get shots in people\u8217\'20\'19s arms, country by country, community by community, ensure we have reliable and predictable supplies of vaccines and boosters for everyone, everywhere, expand access globally to testing and treatments. And we have to prevent complacency.\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s demand of US lawmakers has stumbled, one of a number of growing headaches for the president amid crises over inflation and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. An on-again, off-again bipartisan Covid deal was scuppered by political wrangling over immigration specifically.\par \par \uc2 Republicans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2022/03/31/senators-reach-deal-on-10-billion-in-covid-relief-funding-romney-says.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  agreed to a $10bn compromise}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cin principle\u8221\'20\'1D, without money for global initiatives, then backed out when the Biden administration insisted on pushing ahead with the termination of the Trump-era {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/03/us-asylum-policy-immigration-border-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Title 42 policy}}}\uc2  that blocked refugees at the southern border because of coronavirus concerns.\par \par \uc2 enltrAs long as COVID-19 is present in one country, it impacts all of us. This morning I join {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/USAmbUN?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @USAmbUN}}}\uc2  at the Second Global COVID Summit to discuss our path forward. Tune in. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/BiSN2peafu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/BiSN2peafu}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  (@VP) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/VP/status/1524738380264841216?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 12, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Officially, the Covid-19 death toll in the US is not yet at 1m, Johns Hopkins reporting on Thursday {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coronavirus.jhu.edu/region/united-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a tally of 999,000}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But the inevitable reaching of that grim figure in the coming few days fired Biden\u8217\'20\'19s new call to action, at home and internationally:\par \par \uc2 I continue to call on Congress to take urgent action to provide emergency Covid-19 funding that is vital to protect Americans, to make sure that we maintain our supplies and Covid-19 tests, treatments and vaccines, including next-generation vaccines that are being developed.\par \par \uc2 The request also includes $5bn to keep up our global partnership in the fight against Covid-19 and sustain our efforts to get shots in people around the world, expand access to treatments and save lives everywhere.\par \par \uc2 We can do this, we can control Covid-19, we can start to build a better, healthier and more secure future today if we all do our part, and if we step up together.\par \par \uc2 He announced new global initiatives including sharing of US Covid-19 technologies, partnerships to expand access to rapid testing and antiviral treatments in harder to reach areas, and $450m seed funding for a pandemic preparedness and global health security fund to be established this summer:\par \par \uc2 The US has provided more than $19bn to help countries fight Covid-19, life saving medicines, oxygen, tests, equipment, supplies, and partnered with countries to improve their capacity to manufacture vaccines.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ve delivered more than 500m vaccines to 115 countries and we\u8217\'20\'19re going to... deliver another 500m doses.\par \par \uc2 But there\u8217\'20\'19s still so much left to do. This pandemic isn\u8217\'20\'19t over. We mark a tragic milestone here in the US, 1m empty chairs around the family dinner table, irreplaceable losses that each leave behind a family or community forever change because of this pandemic.\par \par \uc2 Read the White House {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/presidential-actions/2022/05/12/a-proclamation-on-remembering-the-1000000-americans-lost-to-covid-19/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 proclamation on 1m Covid-19 deaths here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 Good morning blog readers, welcome to Thursday\u8217\'20\'19s edition of US politics live!\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re kicking off with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s appearance later this morning at the second virtual global Covid-19 summit, and his commemoration of 1 million lives lost in the US since the beginning of the pandemic.\par \par \uc2 The president is under pressure on multiple fronts domestically, with soaring prices, raging inflation, and the furore over the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s stripping \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights uppermost on voters\u8217\'20\'19 minds as November\u8217\'20\'19s midterm elections approach.\par \par \uc2 Central to Biden\u8217\'20\'19s woes has been his inability to strike a deal with Congress over his $22.5bn coronavirus relief package request, which got mired in political wrangling over both immigration and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . His speech this morning will include a new demand for lawmakers to get a deal done, aides say.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else we\u8217\'20\'19re watching today:\par \par \uc2 * Leaders from the association of southeast Asian nations (Asean) are in Washington DC, meeting lawmakers and, later, Biden at the White House to discuss the pandemic, climate crisis and economic cooperation.\par \par \uc2 * Yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s defeat in the Senate of Democrat-proposed legislation on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights could come up during \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s weekly briefing.\par \par \uc2 * The House natural resources committee will evaluate a disturbing report on the discovery of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/11/native-american-children-schools-abuse-burial-sites"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dozens of burial sites}}}\uc2  at historic Native American boarding schools.\par \par \uc2 * Outgoing White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  will give what could be her second-to-last briefing set for 2.30pm.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220512ei5c001rx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
