\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Divided States of America: Roe v Wade is \u8216\'20\'18precursor to larger struggles\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 David Smith in Washington \par \uc2 2,098 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 May 2022\par 05:28 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The demise of the 1973 ruling could drive the biggest wedge yet between what appears to be two irreconcilable nations\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou put your babies in the womb, you will be held accountable!\u8221\'20\'1D yelled Steve Corson, tall, bearded and jabbing a finger at women who chanted back: \u8220\'20\'1CMy body, my choice!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Corson took a deep breath and blew into a shofar. Then Nathan Darnell, wearing a \u8220\'20\'1CJesus Christ is king\u8221\'20\'1D cap and holding aloft a cross, grabbed a megaphone.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou guys are demon-possessed!\u8221\'20\'1D declared the 19-year-old from Haymarket, Virginia. \u8220\'20\'1CYou guys are controlled by demons, all of you. Every child has a right to life.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Suddenly Darnell was surrounded by \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights protesters brandishing placards. He kept talking.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou guys are evil. The downfall of America is because of every one of you.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The national day of prayer last Thursday was anything but a solemn occasion outside the supreme court in Washington, where hours earlier an unscalable {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/supreme-court/non-scalable-fence-erected-supreme-court-abortion-related-protests-rcna27452"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  black fence had been erected}}}\uc2 , reminiscent of the one that surrounded the US Capitol after the January 6 insurrection.\par \par \uc2 The fury was unleashed by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/02/roe-v-wade-abortion-supreme-court-draft-opinion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a leaked draft opinion}}}\uc2  that showed the nation\u8217\'20\'19s highest court provisionally voted to overturn Roe v Wade, the 1973 ruling that effectively legalised \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It was a political earthquake that revealed American women are perilously close to losing a fundamental right.\par \par \uc2 It was also a milestone in America\u8217\'20\'19s seemingly inexorable journey from United States to divided states. The likely demise of Roe v Wade could drive the biggest wedge yet between what appear to be two irreconcilable nations coexisting under one flag.\par \par \uc2 Liberal states would become sanctuaries for women seeking abortions and saturated with providers; conservative states would turn into deserts that ban the procedure and criminalise doctors who provide it. Some wonder if the country\u8217\'20\'19s social fabric, frayed by four years of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s presidency, can survive.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe death of Roe is going to tear America apart,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/05/06/opinion/roe-abortion-culture-war.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ran the headline}}}\uc2  of a New York Times column by Michelle Goldberg, which concluded that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe death of Roe will intensify our national animus, turning red states and blue into mutually hostile legal territories. You think we hate each other now? Just wait until the new round of lawsuits start.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Simon Schama, a historian, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/simon_schama/status/1521798915175157761?s=20&t=4YLH8cJRMNRZ-Xpl9B5WPA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tweeted}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CWhen Roe vs Wade is overturned it will be time to find a different name for this country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s draft majority opinion, written by \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  and circulated on 10 February, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/05/02/supreme-court-abortion-draft-opinion-00029473"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was leaked to Politico}}}\uc2  on Monday. It argued in contemptuous tones that Roe v Wade \u8220\'20\'1Cwas egregiously wrong from the start\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cenflamed debate and deepened division\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 For 50 years you can have a right \u8211\'20\'13 and it could be taken away by five people\par \par \uc2 Rochelle Rubin\par \par \uc2 Four other Republican-appointed justices \u8211\'20\'13 \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 , \uc2 Neil Gorsuch\uc2 , \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2  and Amy Coney Barrett \u8211\'20\'13 agreed that Roe \u8220\'20\'1Cmust be overruled\u8221\'20\'1D. If that decision becomes final, possibly next month, it will tear down a national precedent and turn America into a chaotic legal patchwork.\par \par \uc2 The first restrictions would take effect in 13 states with so-called trigger laws to be enacted once Roe is overturned. Some such laws ban abortions almost completely while others would outlaw it after six or 15 weeks. The speed of trigger laws could vary. In Texas, a near-total ban would go into effect 30 days after a supreme court decision.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/abortion-rights-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Guttmacher Institute}}}\uc2 , a research and policy organisation, estimates that 26 of 50 states are certain or likely to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  if Roe is overturned, leaving women in swaths of the south-west and midwest without access. In 11 states there would be no exemptions for rape and incest. Republicans in Louisiana are even considering a bill that would allow prosecutors to charge those having abortions {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2022/05/05/louisiana-republicans-advance-bill-that-would-charge-abortion-homicide/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 with homicide}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Most states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  would still be legal are on the west coast or in the north-east. The California governor, \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 , on Monday {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/03/california-abortion-rights-roe-v-wade-scotus"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 proposed enshrining a right to \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  in the state constitution. In Oregon, Democrats recently passed a bill to create a $15m fund to assist with the costs of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including for women from outside the state.\par \par \uc2 Women might have to travel hundreds of miles to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . This is likely to be especially difficult for women in poverty, often including women of colour, and lead to a sharp climb in unsafe abortions. Republican-led states have already made efforts to restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills, which can be prescribed through online visits.\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18This is personal for me\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 There have been fierce disputes over healthcare, immigration and race in recent years \u8211\'20\'13 the journalist Carl Bernstein has spoken of a \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2018/oct/05/brett-kavanaugh-confirmation-america"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cold civil war}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 but few can match the raw emotional power of reproductive rights. That much was clear outside the fortified supreme court on Thursday, as two vociferous groups faced off.\par \par \uc2 Rev {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/revmahoney"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Patrick Mahoney}}}\uc2 , director of the Christian Defense Coalition, said into a microphone: \u8220\'20\'1CWe look forward to the day when \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ends up on the scrap heap of history like chattel slavery and segregation .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://rochellerubin.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rochelle Rubin}}}\uc2 , about 20 paces away, shouted: \u8220\'20\'1CYou don\u8217\'20\'19t have a uterus! Shut up!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Her voice shaking, Rubin, 50, an estate agent and lawyer, explained later: \u8220\'20\'1CThis is personal for me. I was born the last year that women could not have abortions. My mother had no choice. Had she made the choice she would have had me, but women of her generation did not have choice.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf I didn\u8217\'20\'19t have a choice, my life would be very different today than it would have been. Ten years years ago I exercised my choice and had an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . For 50 years you can have a right \u8211\'20\'13 and it could be taken away by five people .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Even as \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights activists shouted \u8220\'20\'1CKeep your rosaries off my ovaries!\u8221\'20\'1D and held placards such as \u8220\'20\'1CWomen\u8217\'20\'19s bodies are more regulated than guns\u8221\'20\'1D, Mahoney said he was \u8220\'20\'1Coverjoyed\u8221\'20\'1D by the draft opinion but acknowledged the societal shockwaves.\par \par \uc2 He said: \u8220\'20\'1CCan America get any more divided than we are? Tragically, yes it can. We certainly saw that happen on January 6, which was tragic. I would say we have to find a way to address this. Let\u8217\'20\'19s deal locally so if you have California on one end and Alabama on another end, let\u8217\'20\'19s just work on that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Mahoney, 68, added: \u8220\'20\'1CWhat you see on the streets is the cutting edge of the cultural fault lines that we see in our country. We saw that with the tragic murder of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/george-floyd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 George Floyd}}}\uc2 . But our nation went through this upheaval and we\u8217\'20\'19re moving forward so that\u8217\'20\'19s what I hope happens here.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The interview was repeatedly interrupted as Mahoney broke off to restrain fellow anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists from confronting female protesters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s not who we are,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, and it was true that women from the opposing sides engaged in civil conversations while in fundamental disagreement.\par \par \uc2 It is going to get heated up, no doubt about it. It should. It\u8217\'20\'19s a good issue to get heated up about\par \par \uc2 Steve Corson\par \par \uc2 But Corson, 65, from Fredonia, Arizona, gripping his shofar and the Stars and Stripes, was more aggressive. He said: \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t respect their view at all. They didn\u8217\'20\'19t come out with \u8216\'20\'18My body, my choice\u8217\'20\'19 when it came to the [Covid] vaccine.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey have a human body inside them; we speak for that human body; they\u8217\'20\'19re just speaking for themselves. I get sick and tired of these people. They are very corrupt and evil and on the wrong side. It is going to get heated up, no doubt about it. It should. It\u8217\'20\'19s a good issue to get heated up about .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The great divide on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not a 50-50 split. It is asymmetric. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://mailchi.mp/dataforprogress/new-poll-voters-widely-support-the-build-back-better-act-and-its-provisions-8278332?e=3ad84f3d1c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 A poll}}}\uc2  released by the Data for Progress thinktank after this week\u8217\'20\'19s leak showed voters wanted to keep Roe by a two-to-one margin. Democrats, independents and more than a third of Republicans support it.\par \par \uc2 Its imminent fall is due to a quirk of US democracy that skews the electoral college, Senate and supreme court out of kilter with the popular will. Justices Gorsuch, Kavanaugh and Coney Barrett were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/05/trump-abortion-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appointed by Trump}}}\uc2 , who lost the national popular vote by 3m, after Senate Republicans blocked \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s last nominee, \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 This sense of injustice at this {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2018/10/14/opinion/dc-puerto-rico-statehood-senate.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 democratic deficit}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 which gives significantly more representation to white citizens than citizens of colour \u8211\'20\'13 is only likely to incite anger and dissent as blue states go one way and red states go the other.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.brookings.edu/experts/elaine-kamarck/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Elaine Kamarck}}}\uc2 , a senior fellow in governance studies at the \uc2 Brookings Institution in Washington\uc2 , said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe basic structure of politics with all these small rural states being essentially overrepresented is creating the situation where minorities can control the majority. People are going to be furious about it.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAlready friends of mine in New York City talk about not letting their tax dollars go to red states because the irony is that all the blue states send more money to the federal government than they get back and the goddam red states take all the money and then try to run the lives of everybody in the blue states.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo there really is a war going on and it\u8217\'20\'19s a cultural war but it\u8217\'20\'19s one that they [Republicans] are destined to lose.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 If Roe is struck down, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.brookings.edu/blog/fixgov/2022/05/03/america-after-roe-v-wade/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamarck noted}}}\uc2 , it will be the clearest differentiation of rights by state since the era of Jim Crow, when some states racially segregated public places and others did not. This could be a recipe for battles over sovereignty, with red states passing laws to \u8220\'20\'1Cextradite\u8221\'20\'1D anyone who helps their residents get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and blue states passing laws to shield their own doctors.\par \par \uc2 States have been drifting apart for years, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/nov/03/trump-era-division-america"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 across fault lines}}}\uc2  characterised as liberal v conservative, Black v white, urban v rural, college-educated v blue collar, Hollywood v heartland, mask wearers v vaccine sceptics and MSNBC v Fox News. The 2016 presidential election was framed as Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cdeplorables\u8221\'20\'1D against \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Ccoastal elites\u8221\'20\'1D. The supreme court looks ready to toss a grenade into the mix.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jan/09/is-the-us-really-heading-for-a-second-civil-war"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Barbara Walter}}}\uc2 , a political scientist at the \uc2 University of California, San Diego\uc2 , and author of How Civil Wars Start: And How to Stop Them, said: \u8220\'20\'1CWhat I fear will happen is that it will further create this urban-rural divide where the more moderate and liberal voices in red states will move, or their children will move, because they will not want their rights restricted.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf you\u8217\'20\'19re a big corporation that employs a lot of women, are you going to move to states where they and their daughters are not treated equally or they\u8217\'20\'19re under these increasingly restrictive and medieval laws?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Backfire of the century\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 The fight is under way. A liberal group published the addresses of conservative supreme court justices and encouraged protesters to walk by them. A day of action for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2022/05/05/planned-parenthood-nationwide-day-action-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 planned for Saturday}}}\uc2 . The issue could also galvanise Democratic turnout in November\u8217\'20\'19s midterm elections.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://swalwell.house.gov/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Eric Swalwell}}}\uc2 , a Democratic congressman from California, said: \u8220\'20\'1CThere will be an effort to turn out young women and their male allies when that decision comes. I hope it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t have to happen but I think it\u8217\'20\'19s going to be the backfire of the century for Republicans.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Senate will vote on legislation that would codify \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights into federal law but Democrats do not have 60 votes to overcome a Republican filibuster, which means the \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 -backed effort will fail.\par \par \uc2 There have never been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2022/05/05/trailer-four-ways-leaked-draft-abortion-opinion-has-altered-midterms/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 so few Republicans}}}\uc2  who support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, nor have there ever been so few Democrats who call themselves \u8220\'20\'1Cpro-life\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Fareed Zakaria, an author and broadcaster, warned in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/opinions/2022/05/05/america-values-diverge-from-world-abortion-religion/?variant=15bc93f5a1ccbb65"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Washington Post:}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1CYou cannot really understand America anymore by looking at averages. It has become two countries. One is urban, more educated, multiracial, secular and largely left of center. The other is rural, less educated, religious, white and largely right of center.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Blue America would fit comfortably with northern European Protestant countries, Zakaria said, while red America\u8217\'20\'19s cultural values make it closer to Nigeria and Saudi Arabia.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor the country\u8217\'20\'19s political future, the central question is now this: can these two Americas find a way to live, work, cooperate with and tolerate one another? If not, the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  battle may be the precursor to even larger struggles.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220513ei5b002s3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
