\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Democrats lose Senate vote to codify  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights 49-51 \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Richard Luscombe \par \uc2 5,854 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 May 2022\par 21:36 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2  sides with Republicans in voting against measureMcConnell says Senate Republicans couldn\u8217\'20\'19t pass \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  banSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re ending the live US politics blog now, but look out shortly for the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s full coverage of Wednesday\u8217\'20\'19s historic vote in which Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 efforts to enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights into federal law fell well short in the \uc2 US Senate\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The day was dominated by the vote on the women\u8217\'20\'19s health protection act, which Democrats knew was doomed to failure, but which they hope can now be used against Republicans who went on record to defeat the legislation.\par \par \uc2 Here are the day\u8217\'20\'19s highlights:\par \par \uc2 * Senators voted 51-49 to reject the women\u8217\'20\'19s health protection act, West Virginia Democrat \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2  crossing the aisle to vote with Republicans.\par \par \uc2 * Republican senators \uc2 Susan Collins\uc2  of Maine and Lisa Murkowski of Alaska issued a joint statement reaffirming their commitment to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights but promoting instead more restrictive legislation.\par \par \uc2 * Arizona ended an eight-year death penalty hiatus when it executed convicted murderer Clarence Dixon by lethal injection.\par \par \uc2 * A New York district judge said he would lift a civil contempt order against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for failing to cooperate with a criminal investigation into his business activities if the former president paid $110,000 and met other obligations.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  hailed American farmers as the \u8220\'20\'1Cbackbone of freedom\u8221\'20\'1D during a speech in Illinois and announced measures to support the agriculture industry and reduce food prices.\par \par \uc2 * A judge in Florida struck down new congressional districts drawn by the state\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , saying they made it harder for Black voters to elect the candidate of their choice.\par \par \uc2 A reminder you can follow developments in the Ukraine war in our {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/may/11/russia-ukraine-war-zelenskiy-says-ukrainian-forces-gradually-pushing-occupiers-away-from-kharkiv-live"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 live 24-hour news blog here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democrats criticize Republican Senators after doomed vote on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 After leaving the chamber, the vice president, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , told reporters that the Senate is \u8220\'20\'1Cnot where the majority of Americans are on this issue\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CThis vote clearly suggests that the Senate is not where the majority of Americans are on this issue,\u8221\'20\'1D ? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/VP?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @VP}}}\uc2  ? Harris says after presiding over the failed vote on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/BrEmO7yqvt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/BrEmO7yqvt}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lauren Gambino (@laurenegambino) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/laurenegambino/status/1524490043062202372?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 11, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 A number of Senators from the Democrats also quickly reacted after the expected failure to advance their legislation to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Ron Wyden\uc2 , from Oregon, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RonWyden/status/1524490909378826240"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  the vote was a \u8220\'20\'1Cpunch in the gut\u8221\'20\'1D for those who \u8220\'20\'1Cbelieve in liberty, privacy and equal rights. Now Americans know which side every Senator stands on.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Angus King, of Maine, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenAngusKing/status/1524487987375054848"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  women across the country are worried the Supreme Court \u8220\'20\'1Cmay take away their basic right to make decisions about their own body,\u8221\'20\'1D adding \u8220\'20\'1Cwe cannot move backwards\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senate blocks \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights law\par \par \uc2 Senators have voted 51-49 to reject Democrat-sponsored legislation enshrining \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights into federal law.\par \par \uc2 The defeat of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.govinfo.gov/app/details/BILLS-117s4132pcs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Protection Act}}}\uc2 , introduced after a leaked supreme court draft ruling last week {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/02/roe-v-wade-abortion-supreme-court-draft-opinion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jeopardized almost half a century of constitutional \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  protections}}}\uc2 , was expected.\par \par \uc2 The West Virginia Democrat \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2  announced this morning he would join Republicans in voting against the measure, leaving it no chance of achieving a majority. The backing of at least 60 senators would have been needed for it to pass.\par \par \uc2 But Democratic senate majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  insisted on pressing ahead with the doomed vote in order to put Republican senators on record.\par \par \uc2 Polls have shown that an overwhelming majority of voters don\u8217\'20\'19t want to see the supreme court overturn the 1973 Roe v Wade ruling that protected \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, and Democrats see the issue as a vote-winner ahead of November\u8217\'20\'19s crucial midterm elections.\par \par \uc2 In comments before the symbolic vote, Schumer said:\par \par \uc2 Every American will see how they voted. And I believe the Republican party, the Maga Republican party, will suffer the consequences electorally when the American people see that.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senators begin voting on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights legislation\par \par \uc2 Vice-President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has called the vote on the Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Protection Act and senators have begun voting. 60 Senate votes are needed for it to pass.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 Alaska Republican Lisa Murkowski has issued a statement insisting that \u8220\'20\'1CI strongly support women\u8217\'20\'19s reproductive freedoms, including the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 But she says she also \u8220\'20\'1Cbelieves in limited government\u8221\'20\'1D and won\u8217\'20\'19t be voting for the Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Protection Act in the imminent \uc2 US Senate\uc2  vote.\par \par \uc2 Lisa Murkowski. Photograph: Michael Brochstein/SOPA Images/REX/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 Murkowski\u8217\'20\'19s statement follows an earlier joint release with Maine Republican \uc2 Susan Collins\uc2 , in which they promoted their own reproductive rights act as an alternative.\par \par \uc2 In her new statement, Murkowski says:\par \par \uc2 The legislation before the Senate today goes well beyond the precedent established in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2022/05/06/1096885897/roe-established-abortion-rights-20-years-later-casey-paved-the-way-for-restricti"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe and Casey}}}\uc2 . It does not include the Hyde amendment, which prohibits taxpayer dollars from being spent on abortions - and has been the law almost as long as Roe.\par \par \uc2 It does not include conscience protections for healthcare providers that refuse to perform abortions based on religious beliefs. It explicitly overrides the religious freedom restoration act for the first time. It also allows late-term abortions without any notable restrictions.\par \par \uc2 Instead of taking yet another failed vote on a wholly partisan measure, I urge Democrats and Republicans alike to recognize that what Senator Collins and I have offered is in line with the views of a strong majority of Americans who support a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to choose but believe that legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should include reasonable limitations.\par \par \uc2 The Senate is edging ever closer to the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights vote. Members are currently finishing a vote on confirming \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s pick Alvaro Bedoya to the federal trade commission, and will turn their attention to the Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Protection Act next, according to \uc2 C-Span\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden hails farmers as 'backbone of freedom'\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has just wrapped up an address to agricultural workers in Kankakee, Illinois, in which he promised support for farmers and new measures to make food prices more affordable.\par \par \uc2 The president hailed farmers as \u8220\'20\'1Cthe backbone of the country\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cthe backbone of freedom\u8221\'20\'1D as he blamed soaring inflation and high prices on Russian president \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Ukraine:\par \par \uc2 You feed America. You got us through a pandemic and you\u8217\'20\'19re literally the backbone of our country. But you\u8217\'20\'19re also feeding the world. And we\u8217\'20\'19re seeing Putin\u8217\'20\'19s war in Ukraine, you\u8217\'20\'19re like the backbone of freedom.\par \par \uc2 America\u8217\'20\'19s fighting on two fronts. At home, inflation and rising prices. Abroad, it\u8217\'20\'19s helping Ukrainians defend democracy, and feeding those who are left hungry around the world because Russian atrocities exist.\par \par \uc2 American farmers understand Putin\u8217\'20\'19s war has has has cut off critical sources of food.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  speaks Wednesday during a visit to O\u8217\'20\'19Connor Farms in Kankakee, Illinois. Photograph: Andrew Harnik/AP\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, at the White House, Biden insisted that tackling inflation was \u8220\'20\'1Cmy top priority\u8221\'20\'1D. Despite a small lift this morning with news that inflation had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/may/11/us-inflation-consumer-price-index-figures"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 slowed for the first time since August}}}\uc2 , it remains at a near 40-year high and is likely to remain uppermost on voters\u8217\'20\'19 minds as November\u8217\'20\'19s midterm elections approach.\par \par \uc2 Biden laid out measures he was taking to \u8220\'20\'1Clower costs on farmers\u8221\'20\'1D, including doubling an investment in fertilizer production to $500m, and looking at extending crop insurance protection \u8220\'20\'1Cto give financial security to farmers\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 By protecting farmers, Biden said, food prices could stabilize and fall.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEvery little bit matters,\u8221\'20\'1D he said as he went back over previous initiatives to tackle high prices, including issuing a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/apr/12/joe-biden-iowa-us-inflation-soars-january-6-inquiry-ukraine-russia-latest-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 summer waiver for ethanol-rich fuel}}}\uc2  which he said would reduce gas prices.\par \par \uc2 The AAA, however, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://gasprices.aaa.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was reporting}}}\uc2  on Wednesday a new record high national average for a gallon of unleaded gasoline at $4.40.\par \par \uc2 The White House {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2022/05/11/fact-sheet-president-biden-announces-new-actions-to-address-putins-price-hike-make-food-more-affordable-and-lower-costs-for-farmers/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 released a fact sheet}}}\uc2  setting out Biden\u8217\'20\'19s proposals to \u8220\'20\'1Cmake food more affordable, and lower costs for farmers\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Lethal injection ends Arizona's death penalty hiatus\par \par \uc2 Arizona ended an eight-year hiatus on executions Wednesday when it put to death a man convicted of killing a college student in 1978.\par \par \uc2 The state halted the death penalty in 2014 following an execution critics say was botched, and difficulties in finding lethal injection drugs, Reuters reported.\par \par \uc2 Clarence Dixon, 66, died by lethal injection at the state prison in Florence for his murder conviction in the killing of 21-year-old Arizona state university student Deana Bowdoin, making him the sixth person to be executed in the US in 2022.\par \par \uc2 Dixon\u8217\'20\'19s death was announced late Wednesday morning by Frank Strada, a deputy director with Arizona department of corrections.\par \par \uc2 Protestor Charles Keith stands outside the state prison in Florence, Arizona on Wednesday. Photograph: Rick Scuteri/AP\par \par \uc2 Dixon\u8217\'20\'19s death appeared to go smoothly, said Troy Hayden, an anchor for the Fox10 TV news program who witnessed the execution.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COnce the drugs started flowing, he went to sleep almost immediately,\u8221\'20\'1D Hayden said.\par \par \uc2 Dixon\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers asked to postpone his execution, but judges rejected his argument that he wasn\u8217\'20\'19t mentally fit to be executed and didn\u8217\'20\'19t have a rational understanding of why the state wanted to execute him.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  rejected a last-minute delay of Dixon\u8217\'20\'19s execution less than an hour before the execution began.\par \par \uc2 In another Arizona death penalty case, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Ed Pilkington{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/04/arizona-death-row-execution-cyanide-gas-frank-atwood"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported last week}}}\uc2  that Frank Atwood, convicted for murdering an eight-year-old girl, has two weeks to decide whether to be executed with cyanide gas, the poison known as Zyklon B used by the Nazis to murder millions of people in Auschwitz and other extermination camps, or lethal injection.\par \par \uc2 Atwood\u8217\'20\'19s execution is set for 8 June.\par \par \uc2 Last month, the Texas court of criminal appeals {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/25/melissa-lucio-stay-of-execution-texas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 issued a stay of execution}}}\uc2  for Melissa Lucio, a Mexican-American woman set to be judicially killed for the death of her two-year-old daughter Mariah.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 A state judge struck down new congressional districts in north Florida on Wednesday, saying that the state\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , who drew the lines, made it harder for Black voters to elect the candidate of their choice.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am finding the enacted map is unconstitutional because it diminishes African Americans\u8217\'20\'19 ability to elect candidates of their choice,\u8221\'20\'1D circuit judge Lane Smith said on Wednesday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://jaxtrib.org/2022/05/11/judge-strikes-down-part-of-florida-congressional-redistricting-map/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the Tributary}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 . Photograph: \uc2 Paul Hennessy\uc2 /SOPA Images/REX/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 Lawyers for the state of Florida are expected to immediately appeal the ruling, and the Florida supreme court shaped by DeSantis could ultimately decide the case.\par \par \uc2 The decision dealt specifically with DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19 decision to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2022/apr/20/ron-desantis-florida-electoral-map-gerrymandering-republican-advantage"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dismantle Florida\u8217\'20\'19s fifth congressional district}}}\uc2 , which stretched from Jacksonville to Tallahassee, was 46% Black, and is currently represented by Al Lawson, a Black Democrat. DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19 new district chopped the district up into four districts where Republican candidates would be favored to win.\par \par \uc2 A coalition of civic action groups and Florida voters {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.democracydocket.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/2022-04-26-PI-Memorandum-Of-Law.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 immediately challenged the map}}}\uc2 , saying that they {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ballotpedia.org/Florida_Congressional_District_Boundaries,_Amendment_6_(2010)"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 violated a provision}}}\uc2  in Florida\u8217\'20\'19s constitution that says new districts can\u8217\'20\'19t \u8220\'20\'1Cdiminish\u8221\'20\'1D the ability of minority voters to elect the candidate of their choosing.\par \par \uc2 Last month, plaintiffs {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.democracydocket.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/2022-04-26-PI-Memorandum-Of-Law.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  asked the court}}}\uc2  to block the districts in northern Florida specifically from taking effect for the 2022 election. Smith ordered the state to adopt a map that maintained a 5th congressional district stretching from Jacksonville to Tallahasee, according to the Tributary.\par \par \uc2 The Florida map is one of the most aggressively gerrymandered maps in the US. Republicans currently have a 16-11 advantage in the state\u8217\'20\'19s congressional delegation, but DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19 plan would add an additional four GOP-friendly seats, increasing that advantage to 20-8 (Florida is gaining an additional US House seat because of population growth). It\u8217\'20\'19s an effort that\u8217\'20\'19s seen as a critical part of Republican efforts to retake control of the US House in the midterm elections.\par \par \uc2 In a separate court on Tuesday, DeSantis, a possible 2024 presidential candidate, won the opening legal round of his fight with \uc2 Disney\uc2  over the state\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cdon\u8217\'20\'19t say gay\u8221\'20\'1D bill that bans classroom discussions of sexual preference and gender identity issues.\par \par \uc2 Three central Florida taxpayers alleged state laws were broken when DeSantis signed a new law dissolving \uc2 Disney\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s self-governing status, which critics said was in retaliation for the company attacking the \u8220\'20\'1Cdon\u8217\'20\'19t say gay\u8221\'20\'1D law.\par \par \uc2 But district court judge Cecilia Altonaga threw out the lawsuit, partly because the plaintiffs aren\u8217\'20\'19t personally harmed, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.orlandosentinel.com/politics/os-ne-disney-reedy-creek-lawsuit-dismissed-20220510-cuqj5yslbba7jeprckcwzf4cja-story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Orlando Sentinel reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 The supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s upcoming decision to reverse Roe v Wade (an early draft of which was leaked last week) doesn\u8217\'20\'19t ban abortions. It leaves the issue to the states. As a result, it will put another large brick in the growing wall separating blue and red America.\par \par \uc2 The second American civil war is already occurring, but it is less of a war than a kind of benign separation analogous to unhappily married people who don\u8217\'20\'19t want to go through the trauma of a formal divorce.\par \par \uc2 One America is largely urban, racially and ethnically diverse, and young. The other is largely rural or exurban, white and older.\par \par \uc2 The split is accelerating. Red zip codes are getting redder and blue zip codes bluer. Of 3,143 counties, the number of super landslide counties \u8211\'20\'13 where a presidential candidate won at least 80% of the vote \u8211\'20\'13 jumped from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://centerforpolitics.org/crystalball/articles/the-big-sort-continues-with-trump-as-a-driving-force/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 6% in 2004 to 22% in 2020}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Surveys show Americans find it increasingly important to live around {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2022/02/18/1081295373/the-big-sort-americans-move-to-areas-political-alignment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 people who share their political values}}}\uc2 . Animosity toward those in the opposing party is higher than at any time in living memory. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2019/03/13/opinion/hate-politics.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Forty-two per cent}}}\uc2  of registered voters believe Americans in the other party are \u8220\'20\'1Cdownright evil\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Almost {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://today.yougov.com/topics/politics/articles-reports/2020/09/17/republicans-democrats-marriage-poll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 40%}}}\uc2  would be upset at the prospect of their child marrying someone from the opposite party. Even before the 2020 election, when asked if violence would be justified if the other party won the election, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dannyhayes.org/uploads/6/9/8/5/69858539/kalmoe___mason_ncapsa_2019_-_lethal_partisanship_-_final_lmedit.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 18.3%}}}\uc2  of Democrats and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dannyhayes.org/uploads/6/9/8/5/69858539/kalmoe___mason_ncapsa_2019_-_lethal_partisanship_-_final_lmedit.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 13.8%}}}\uc2  of Republicans responded in the affirmative.\par \par \uc2 Increasingly, each America is running under different laws.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2022/may/11/second-american-civil-war-robert-reich"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The second American civil war is already happening | Robert Reich}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump contempt fine halted in New York\par \par \uc2 Good news, of a sort, for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  out of New York, where a judge has said the former president must pay the state attorney general $110,000 and meet other conditions to purge a contempt of court order, but also that the fine will not grow by $10,000 a day, as it had been doing.\par \par \uc2 The New York attorney general, Letitia James, says her civil investigation of the \uc2 Trump Organization\uc2  has found evidence of fraudulent behaviour in tax filings. Trump says the investigation is a politically motivated witch hunt.\par \par \uc2 The judge in the contempt case, \uc2 Arthur Engoron\uc2 , said the daily fine on Trump stopped accruing on Friday, when the former president filed affidavits about his search for requested information \u8211\'20\'13 and his inability to find four phones which investigators would like to look at.\par \par \uc2 Engoron said the contempt order could be restored if certain conditions are not met.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s our report on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s phones, from yesterday:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/10/trump-cellphones-investigation-alleged-fraud-company"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump tells court he lost phones linked to alleged fraud by his company}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ve heard a lot about the \u8220\'20\'1Crival\u8221\'20\'1D \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights bill pushed by Republican senators \uc2 Susan Collins\uc2  and Lisa Murkowski, and they\u8217\'20\'19ve just released a joint statement explaining why they believe their {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.congress.gov/117/bills/s3713/BILLS-117s3713is.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reproductive rights act}}}\uc2  is preferable to the Democratic Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Protection Act they\u8217\'20\'19ll vote against in the Senate this afternoon.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI support codifying the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights established by Roe v Wade. That\u8217\'20\'19s not what the women\u8217\'20\'19s health protection act would do,\u8221\'20\'1D Collins, of Maine, said in the statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUnlike some far-left activists, Senator Murkowski and I want the law today to be the law tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s why we introduced legislation in February that would enshrine the important Roe and Casey protections into law without undercutting statutes that have been in place for decades, and without eliminating basic conscience protections that are relied upon by health care providers who have religious objections to performing abortions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Collins, a pro-choice Republican, says she\u8217\'20\'19s committed to codifying \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, but in a manner that would attract bipartisan support.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAfter today\u8217\'20\'19s vote fails, I plan to continue working with my colleagues on legislation to maintain \u8211\'20\'13 not expand or restrict \u8211\'20\'13 the current legal framework for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in this country,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Manchin to vote with Republicans and block \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights law\par \par \uc2 The Democratic legislation to enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights into federal law looks set to fail in the Senate this afternoon by a vote of 49-51, after the West Virginia senator \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2  said he would cross the aisle and join Republicans to vote no.\par \par \uc2 Manchin, a moderate Democrat, has been speaking with reporters in the Senate hallway, saying he believes the legislation as presented \u8220\'20\'1Cgoes too far\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI would vote for a Roe v Wade codification if it was today. I was hopeful for that, but I found out yesterday in caucus that wasn\u8217\'20\'19t going to be,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 enltrManchin tells reporters he will vote against the Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Protection Act this afternoon {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/sOvTIjxDwl"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/sOvTIjxDwl}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Alan He (@alanhe) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/alanhe/status/1524414354262790144?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 11, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The legislation would codify the 1973 Roe v Wade ruling that gave constitutional protection to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and, crucially, prevent states from acting to remove or alter those protections in the future.\par \par \uc2 Manchin also voted against the women\u8217\'20\'19s health protection act of 2021 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.congress.gov/bill/117th-congress/house-bill/3755"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 earlier this year}}}\uc2 , so his opposition is not entirely surprising.\par \par \uc2 The bill was already expected to fail today because Democrats do not have the 60 votes necessary to overcome a Republican filibuster. With Manchin\u8217\'20\'19s opposition, the final vote to invoke cloture on the bill will likely be 49 to 51, with all Republicans voting against the measure.\par \par \uc2 Republican senators \uc2 Susan Collins\uc2  and Lisa Murkowski have said they would support codifying Roe, but they do not support the women\u8217\'20\'19s health protection act because they consider it too expansive.\par \par \uc2 Tammy Baldwin\uc2 , Democratic senator for Wisconsin and co-sponsor of the legislation, said Manchin was wrong.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think his interpretation of the bill is incorrect when he says it goes a lot further,\u8221\'20\'1D Baldwin told CNN.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CActually, it keeps the states from interfering with Roe v Wade and restricting access.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s the additional provisions of the women\u8217\'20\'19s health protection act, and they need to be there because you look how many states have taken an action like the Texas law that allows vigilantes to go out and and try to find anybody who aided or abetted \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 It wasn\u8217\'20\'19t a good day in Nebraska for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on Tuesday with the defeat of his endorsed candidate, \uc2 Charles Herbster\uc2 , in the Republican primary for governor.\par \par \uc2 Party voters in the state instead picked hog farm owner and veterinarian Jim Pillen as their nominee over a rival accused of groping multiple women.\par \par \uc2 enltrI cannot say it enough: To all of our {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/TeamPillen?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #TeamPillen}}}\uc2  supporters, and to all Nebraskans who entrusted me with your votes yesterday, thank you! You made this victory possible. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/xZTvSTUQXe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/xZTvSTUQXe}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jim Pillen (@jim_pillen) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jim_pillen/status/1524384667281104898?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 11, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Herbster\u8217\'20\'19s loss was a setback for Trump, who has issued hundreds of endorsements and staged rallies in support of candidates in an effort to bend the Republican party to his direction ahead of a possible presidential run in 2024.\par \par \uc2 The loss raises the stakes on other high-profile primaries this month in Pennsylvania and Georgia, where Trump has also intervened.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s influence proved decisive in West Virginia on Tuesday, however.\par \par \uc2 In a US House primary pitting Republican incumbents against each other, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s candidate, Alex Mooney, defeated David McKinley, who angered Trump by voting for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s bipartisan infrastructure package and the creation of the House committee investigating the 6 January attack on the US Capitol.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/11/trump-candidate-loses-republican-jim-pillen-nebraska-governor-primary"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump-endorsed Republican accused of sexual assault loses Nebraska governor primary}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Elizabeth Warren has been on CNN explaining why she\u8217\'20\'19s no supporter of a bipartisan approach to legislation to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 Elizabeth Warren. Photograph: REX/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 The Democratic Massachusetts senator, one of her party\u8217\'20\'19s most outspoken proponents of codifying the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s 1973 Roe v Wade ruling into law, says measures promoted by pro-choice Republicans \uc2 Susan Collins\uc2  of Maine, and Lisa Murkowsk i of Alaska, won\u8217\'20\'19t go far enough.\par \par \uc2 The pair, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thedailybeast.com/senators-collins-murkowski-and-kaine-working-on-a-bipartisan-bill-to-codify-roe-with-some-restrictions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the Daily Beast}}}\uc2 , are working with Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic senator Tim Kaine on more restrictive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights legislation that would codify the basics of Roe v Wade but allow state laws to include items such as a religious conscience exemption.\par \par \uc2 Warren says she\u8217\'20\'19s a hard no:\par \par \uc2 A measure that says \u8216\'20\'18not really\u8217\'20\'19 on Roe, a measure that says, hey, the things that are going on in the states already, even before this latest dust up with Texas, a measure that says it\u8217\'20\'19s OK if in South Dakota there\u8217\'20\'19s only one \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic in the whole state [and] it\u8217\'20\'19s OK to restrict the rights of people across this country? No, that\u8217\'20\'19s not OK.\par \par \uc2 Because keep in mind who this will fall hardest on. It\u8217\'20\'19s going to fall hardest on poor women, it\u8217\'20\'19s going to fall hardest on women of color, it\u8217\'20\'19s going to fall hardest on the 14-year-old who was molested by her uncle, on the mama working three jobs to try to support the children she has.\par \par \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  has [said]... if the Republicans get back into control, we\u8217\'20\'19re willing to open the door to make it fall on everyone, all across this country, to outlaw \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , not just in red states, but in blue states as well.\par \par \uc2 The scope of this is enormous and that\u8217\'20\'19s why the vote today is so important.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 The impending end to legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in half the states will strain capacity and resources in others preserving \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, my colleague Maya Yang has found:\par \par \uc2 After the bombshell leak of a supreme court draft opinion last week revealed that the majority of justices plan to overturn {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2 , a handful of states have been reaffirming and expanding their \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care.\par \par \uc2 In recent days, a flurry of bills and statements have been emerging in largely Democratic-run states as lawmakers and organizations scramble to prepare for the possibility of a post-Roe America.\par \par \uc2 As some states seek to become \u8220\'20\'1Csafe havens\u8221\'20\'1D for out-of-state \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  seekers, other states have been increasing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  funding, expanding provider access and offering legal protections from lawsuits launched by citizen \u8220\'20\'1Cbounty-hunters\u8221\'20\'1D against those involved in abortions.\par \par \uc2 Only 38% of women of reproductive age live in states that have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/article/2019/08/state-abortion-policy-landscape-hostile-supportive"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  shown}}}\uc2  support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, according to the research organization \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 . In contrast, 58% live in states that have demonstrated hostility towards \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. Only 4% of women live in middle-ground states.\par \par \uc2 Liz Krueger\uc2 , with senate majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 . Photograph: Ron Adar/SOPA Images/REX/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 Last month, the New York state senator \uc2 Liz Krueger\uc2  introduced a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nysenate.gov/legislation/bills/2021/S8778"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  bill}}}\uc2  that would shield New York doctors who offer \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services to out-of-state patients by prohibiting law enforcement from cooperating with out-of-state investigations on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provisions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAt this critical moment New York must ensure \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access both to New Yorkers and refugees from other states who are being denied their basic rights,\u8221\'20\'1D Krueger told the Guardian.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe must provide iron-clad protection for New York healthcare providers against abhorrent and regressive laws in other states,\u8221\'20\'1D she added.\par \par \uc2 Similarly, \uc2 Alessandra Biaggi\uc2 , another New York state senator, introduced a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nysenate.gov/newsroom/press-releases/alessandra-biaggi/senator-biaggi-planned-parenthood-brigid-alliance-and"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  bill}}}\uc2  that would create an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access fund and allow taxpayers to contribute to it.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe created this bill to make sure that we were not just saying that people have a right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but also that they have access to it because we know that simply by just saying the right does not mean that people have the means to do it,\u8221\'20\'1D Biaggi told the Guardian.\par \par \uc2 In addition to transportation costs, the fund would cover childcare services, lodging, various medical expenses and other logistical support.\par \par \uc2 Read the full story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/11/abortion-pro-choice-states-safe-havens-funding-legal-protection"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Pro-choice states rush to pledge legal shield for out-of-state abortions}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 White House: 'Imperative' to protect women's reproductive choice\par \par \uc2 The White House has just issued {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/S4132-SAP-Womens-Health-Protection-Act-of-2022.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a statement}}}\uc2  ahead of the \uc2 US Senate\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights vote this afternoon, urging Congress to pass the Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Protection Act:\par \par \uc2 The urgency to protect women\u8217\'20\'19s health, their fundamental right to control their reproductive choices, and the freedom of all people to build their own future has never been greater.\par \par \uc2 The position of the Biden administration has been clear since day one: We will defend women\u8217\'20\'19s constitutional rights recognized in Roe v Wade nearly half a century ago - rights that have been under attack for decades, and are under unprecedented threat now, despite strong support from the American people.\par \par \uc2 It is imperative for Congress to act to adopt statutory protections for women\u8217\'20\'19s access to essential health care services and reproductive choice, regardless of where they live.\par \par \uc2 Congress must further act to protect health care providers\u8217\'20\'19 ability to provide such critical services free from unwarranted and inappropriate restrictions, and to eliminate unjustified burdens on commerce that prevent women and their families from participating fully and equally in the economic and social life of the United States.\par \par \uc2 The protections that the Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Protection Act would ensure are essential to the health, safety, and progress of our nation. Congress should advance this important bill with the utmost urgency this moment demands.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/S4132-SAP-Womens-Health-Protection-Act-of-2022.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Read the full statement from the executive office of the president here.}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a few tweets from some key Democratic players in the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights debate, ahead of this afternoon\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 US Senate\uc2  vote. From \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , the Senate majority leader:\par \par \uc2 enltrToday, this Senate will vote on the Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Protection Act to codify the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  into federal law.\par \par \uc2 The American people will see where every single U.S. Senator stands.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  (@SenSchumer) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenSchumer/status/1524372050546200577?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 11, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Bob Casey, senator for Pennsylvania, staunch Catholic and self-confessed anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Democrat:\par \par \uc2 enltrMy statement on the Senate\u8217\'20\'19s upcoming vote on the Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Protection Act: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ABap00RiOV"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ABap00RiOV}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Senator Bob Casey (@SenBobCasey) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenBobCasey/status/1524050097021009920?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 10, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Elizabeth Warren, senator for Massachusetts and vocal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights campaigner:\par \par \uc2 enltrA far-right, extremist Supreme Court wants to force its unpopular views on Americans. We can't let this happen. Watch my speech on why the Senate needs to pass the Women's Health Protection Act to enshrine the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in federal law: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/jZIxnQaLtZ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/jZIxnQaLtZ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Elizabeth Warren (@SenWarren) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenWarren/status/1524116791412281347?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 10, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Dick Durbin\uc2  of Illinois, Senate majority whip:\par \par \uc2 enltrWith the future of Roe v. Wade in question, it has never been more important for Congress to pass the Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Protection Act.\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m live on the Senate floor, discussing the need to pass this bill and protect reproductive rights. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/1iVhxvunIH"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/1iVhxvunIH}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Senator \uc2 Dick Durbin\uc2  (@SenatorDurbin) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenatorDurbin/status/1524046723911401473?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 10, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Richard Blumenthal of Connecticut, lead sponsor of the Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Protection Act:\par \par \uc2 enltrWe cannot rely on the courts to defend \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights & access. The Senate needs to take action to enshrine the promise & vision of Roe v. Wade in federal law. We must pass the Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Protection Act. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/WHPA?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #WHPA}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Richard Blumenthal (@SenBlumenthal) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenBlumenthal/status/1524385029899620357?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 11, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 A day before {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats}}}\uc2  staged a vote in the Senate to codify into law the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a right under threat from the supreme court, the Republican leader in the chamber said his party would not be able to pass an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban should it take control in midterm elections in November.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHistorically, there have been \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  votes on the floor of the Senate. None of them have achieved 60 votes,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Mitch McConnell{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/news/senate/3483391-mcconnell-tamps-down-chance-abortion-bill-could-pass-gop-senate/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told reporters}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think it\u8217\'20\'19s safe to say there aren\u8217\'20\'19t 60 votes there at the federal level, no matter who happens to be in the majority, no matter who happens to be in the White House.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 . Photograph: REX/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 The chamber is split 50-50 and therefore controlled by the tie-breaking vote of the vice-president, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . Democrats and progressives have urged the party to seek to scrap the filibuster, the Senate rule that requires 60 votes for most legislation.\par \par \uc2 Such reform seems unlikely. With key Democrats opposed, Punchbowl News, a Washington outlet, reported on Wednesday that the issue was not even discussed at a party Senate lunch the day before.\par \par \uc2 When \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was in power McConnell, too, came under pressure to scrap the filibuster to advance the Republican agenda.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, the Kentucky senator {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/news/senate/3483391-mcconnell-tamps-down-chance-abortion-bill-could-pass-gop-senate/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told reporters}}}\uc2  there were \u8220\'20\'1Cno issues that Republicans believe should be exempt from the 60-vote threshold\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The measure before the Senate on Wednesday \u8211\'20\'13 for which the Democrats do not even have 50 votes, with opposition from some in their own party as well as pro-choice {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 is the Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Protection Act. It would codify Roe v Wade, the 1973 supreme court decision that protects the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Read the full story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/11/mitch-mcconnell-senate-republicans-could-not-pass-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mitch McConnell says Senate Republicans couldn\u8217\'20\'19t pass \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democrats will start taking names on Wednesday afternoon as their attempt to enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights into federal law faces inevitable defeat in the \uc2 US Senate\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 What senate majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  has called \u8220\'20\'1Camong the most important votes of the century\u8221\'20\'1D will not reach the required 60-vote threshold, with Maine\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Susan Collins\uc2  and Alaska\u8217\'20\'19s Lisa Murkowski, two Republicans who support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, having declared their intention to vote against.\par \par \uc2 Susan Collins\uc2 . Photograph: J Scott Applewhite/AP\par \par \uc2 But with the symbolic vote, Schumer will achieve his goal of putting Republican senators on record, just months before November\u8217\'20\'19s midterm elections, over an issue that has proved hugely unpopular with voters:\par \par \uc2 Every senator will have to vote and every American will see how they voted. And I believe the Republican party, the Maga Republican party, will suffer the consequences electorally when the American people see that.\par \par \uc2 Opinion polls appear to back Schumer, at least as far as the unpopularity of last week\u8217\'20\'19s leaked draft ruling from the supreme court that would end constitutional protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A new {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://morningconsult.com/2022/05/11/supreme-court-roe-v-wade-abortion-survey/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico/Morning Consult poll}}}\uc2  on Wednesday shows increasing numbers opposed to the supreme court overturning the 1973 Roe v Wade opinion, including, for the first time, fewer than 50% of Republican supporters.\par \par \uc2 The survey shows 48% of Republicans would want the draft ruling to become final, down 3% from a week ago. Among Democrats, 75% want Roe upheld, up 7%, and among independents the figure is 52%.\par \par \uc2 enltrSince a survey conducted before the leaked draft opinion revealing that the court\u8217\'20\'19s conservative majority had voted to overturn Roe, the share of Democrats who were \u8220\'20\'1Cextremely\u8221\'20\'1D or \u8220\'20\'1Cvery\u8221\'20\'1D enthusiastic to vote in the midterms increased from 48% to 54%. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/rYbP5DXwax"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/rYbP5DXwax}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/VDeRMbygIF"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/VDeRMbygIF}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Morning Consult (@MorningConsult) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MorningConsult/status/1524373858081517569?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 11, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s why, despite Democrats lacking the numbers to pass legislation to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, and predicted to lose control of one, or both, chambers of Congress in November, they think they can still turn the issue to their advantage.\par \par \uc2 Morning Consult says since the supreme court draft ruling was leaked, Democratic voters who say they are \u8220\'20\'1Cextremely\u8221\'20\'1D or \u8220\'20\'1Cvery\u8221\'20\'1D enthusiastic to vote in the midterms rose six points to 54%.\par \par \uc2 In the words of Democratic Nevada senator Jackie Rosen :\par \par \uc2 We have to take that fear, we have to take that anger that we\u8217\'20\'19re feeling, channel it into action to defend our majority. You have to elect more pro-choice senators. We\u8217\'20\'19re not living in a hypothetical.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Good morning and welcome to the midweek edition of the US politics blog.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s voting day in the US Senate on Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 legislation to codify constitutional \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections in the wake of the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s draft ruling overturning them.\par \par \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , the Senate majority leader, says it\u8217\'20\'19s among the most important votes of the century, and when it fails, because he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t have the 60 votes he needs, the party can start pointing to the Republicans who blocked it.\par \par \uc2 A new Politico/Morning Consult poll on Wednesday shows fewer than 50% of Republican voters want Roe v Wade overturned.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s a hugely busy day elsewhere in US politics:\par \par \uc2 * Senators will pick up the $40m Ukraine aid bill passed in the House last night after \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  dropped his demand for it to be tied to his $20bn+ Covid-19 relief request.\par \par \uc2 * Biden heads for Illinois to talk about food prices and the economy, as new data Wednesday reflected a slowing in inflation for the first time since August. With gas prices at record highs, Biden says tackling inflation is \u8220\'20\'1Cmy top domestic priority\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 * There\u8217\'20\'19s fallout from Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s Republican primaries in Nebraska and West Virginia, where candidates endorsed by former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  experienced mixed fortunes.\par \par \uc2 * White House chief medical adviser Dr \uc2 Anthony Fauci\uc2  is among a number of Biden administration officials testifying to Congress, as an alarming new wave of Covid-19 spreads across the US, and cases and hospitalizations rise.\par \par \uc2 * Commerce secretary \uc2 Gina Raimondo\uc2 , international development administrator Samantha Power, defense secretary Lloyd Austin and joint chiefs chair \uc2 Mark Milley\uc2  also have appointments on Capitol Hill.\par \par \uc2 * Incoming White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  will host a \u8220\'20\'1Cgaggle\u8221\'20\'1D with journalists abort Air Force One en route to Chicago.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220511ei5b0025x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
