\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  says Senate Republicans couldn\u8217\'20\'19t pass  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ban\b0\par\par\uc2 Martin Pengelly in New York \par \uc2 593 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 May 2022\par 12:42 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Republican leader says \u8216\'20\'18I think it\u8217\'20\'19s safe to say there aren\u8217\'20\'19t 60 votes\u8217\'20\'19 to pass ban should Republicans take control in midterm elections\par \par \uc2 A day before Democrats staged a vote in the Senate to codify into law the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a right under threat from the supreme court, the Republican leader in the chamber said his party would not be able to pass an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban should it take control in midterm elections in November.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHistorically, there have been \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  votes on the floor of the Senate. None of them have achieved 60 votes,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Mitch McConnell{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/news/senate/3483391-mcconnell-tamps-down-chance-abortion-bill-could-pass-gop-senate/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told reporters}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think it\u8217\'20\'19s safe to say there aren\u8217\'20\'19t 60 votes there at the federal level, no matter who happens to be in the majority, no matter who happens to be in the White House.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The chamber is split 50-50 and therefore controlled by the tie-breaking vote of the vice-president, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . Democrats and progressives have urged the party to seek to scrap the filibuster, the Senate rule that requires 60 votes for most legislation.\par \par \uc2 Such reform seems unlikely. With key Democrats opposed, Punchbowl News, a Washington outlet, reported on Wednesday that the issue was not even discussed at a party Senate lunch the day before.\par \par \uc2 When \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was in power McConnell, too, came under pressure to scrap the filibuster to advance the Republican agenda.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, the Kentucky senator {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/news/senate/3483391-mcconnell-tamps-down-chance-abortion-bill-could-pass-gop-senate/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told reporters}}}\uc2  there were \u8220\'20\'1Cno issues that Republicans believe should be exempt from the 60-vote threshold\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The measure before the Senate on Wednesday \u8211\'20\'13 for which the Democrats do not even have 50 votes, with opposition from some in their own party as well as pro-choice Republicans \u8211\'20\'13 is the Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Protection Act. It would codify Roe v Wade, the 1973 supreme court decision that protects the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Roe has been under imminent threat since last week, when a draft supreme court ruling overturning it, reportedly supported by five conservative justices, was leaked.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, Politico, which published the leak, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/05/11/alito-abortion-draft-opinion-roe-00031648"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  the draft ruling by \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  was still the only one in circulation, with publication expected in June.\par \par \uc2 The Democratic Senate vote is a response to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/10/divided-america-roe-v-wade-supreme-court-cold-civil-war"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 protests that have spread}}}\uc2  since the draft ruling was published. Many Republican-run states have trigger laws ready to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at various stages should Roe fall.\par \par \uc2 McConnell said: \u8220\'20\'1CIf the leaked opinion became the final opinion, legislative bodies \u8211\'20\'13 not only at the state level but at the federal level \u8211\'20\'13 certainly could legislate in that area.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans would be possible, he said.\par \par \uc2 Polling shows {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.forbes.com/sites/alisondurkee/2022/05/09/even-most-republicans-dont-want-congress-to-ban-abortion-nationwide-poll-finds/?sh=7bf679e93979"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 consistent majority support}}}\uc2  for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights but Republicans say they doubt the issue will damage them at the midterms in November.\par \par \uc2 McConnell\u8217\'20\'19s deputy, \uc2 John Thune\uc2  of South Dakota, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/news/senate/3483876-republicans-see-little-political-danger-in-abortion-showdown/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the Hill}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1COur members are going to continue to hammer away on inflation, the economy, the border, crime.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Democrats hope the vote on Wednesday will prove politically useful.\par \par \uc2 The Senate majority leader, \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  of New York, told reporters: \u8220\'20\'1CEvery senator will have to vote, and every, every American will see how they voted. And I believe the Republican party \u8230\'20\'26 will suffer the consequences electorally when the American people see that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Jackie Rosen, of Nevada, said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe have to take that fear, we have to take that anger that we\u8217\'20\'19re feeling, channel it into action to defend our majority. You have to elect more pro-choice senators. We\u8217\'20\'19re not living in a hypothetical.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220511ei5b001xl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
