\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 First Thing: Ukraine forces pushing back Russian troops in Kharkiv\b0\par\par\uc2 Nicola Slawson \par \uc2 1,354 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 May 2022\par 10:38 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 President says military gradually pushing Russian troops away from key city. Plus, robot recruiters might be to blame if you are struggling to get a new job\par \par \uc2 Good morning.\par \par \uc2 Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s government has suggested Kyiv could {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/11/zelenskiy-says-ukraine-forces-pushing-back-russia-troops-in-kharkiv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expand its own war aims}}}\uc2  with an intensifying counteroffensive against Russia\u8217\'20\'19s forces, and said it would suspend the flow of Russian gas through its country to Europe.\par \par \uc2 With the war now in its 11th week and Russia pounding the vital port of Odesa with missile strikes in an apparent effort to disrupt supply lines, the Ukrainian president, \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2 , said late last night that the military was gradually pushing Russian troops away from the key city of Kharkiv and back towards the border with Russia.\par \par \uc2 The Ukrainian military\u8217\'20\'19s general staff said its forces drove the Russians out of four villages to the north-east of Kharkiv, a key city that has been under attack from the Russians since the beginning of the conflict.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, trapped and wounded Azovstal soldiers are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/may/11/russia-ukraine-war-zelenskiy-says-ukrainian-forces-gradually-pushing-occupiers-away-from-kharkiv-live"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  pleading for rescue}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In what way might they expand? Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s foreign minister, \uc2 Dmytro Kuleba\uc2 , seemed to indicate that the country could go beyond merely pushing Russia back to areas it or its allies held on the day of the 24 February invasion and mean \u8220\'20\'1Cthe liberation of the rest of our territories\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What else is happening? Here\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/11/russia-ukraine-war-what-we-know-on-day-77-of-russias-invasion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 what we know on day 77}}}\uc2  of the invasion.\par \par \uc2 Pro-choice states rush to pledge legal shield for out-of-state abortions\par \par \uc2 After the bombshell leak of a supreme court draft opinion last week revealed that the majority of justices plan to overturn Roe v Wade, a handful of states have been reaffirming and expanding their \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care.\par \par \uc2 In recent days, a flurry of bills and statements have been emerging in largely Democratic-run states as lawmakers and organizations scramble to prepare for the possibility of a post-Roe America.\par \par \uc2 As some states seek to become \u8220\'20\'1Csafe havens\u8221\'20\'1D for out-of-state \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  seekers, other states have been increasing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  funding, expanding provider access and offering legal protections from lawsuits launched by citizen \u8220\'20\'1Cbounty-hunters\u8221\'20\'1D against those involved in abortions.\par \par \uc2 Only 38% of women of reproductive age live in states that have shown support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, according to the research organization \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 . In contrast, 58% live in states that have demonstrated hostility towards \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. Only 4% of women live in middle-ground states.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Last month, the\par \par \uc2 New York state senator \uc2 Liz Krueger\par \par \uc2 introduced a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nysenate.gov/legislation/bills/2021/S8778"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  bill}}}\uc2  that would shield New York doctors who offer \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services to out-of-state patients.\par \par \uc2 Al Jazeera accuses Israeli forces of killing journalist in West Bank\par \par \uc2 Al Jazeera has accused Israel of deliberately killing one of its reporters during a firefight between Israeli security forces and Palestinian gunmen in the occupied West Bank town of Jenin.\par \par \uc2 Shireen Abu Akleh, 51, a Palestinian American and one of the Arab world\u8217\'20\'19s most well-known reporters who had covered the conflict for decades, was shot in the head this morning and taken to hospital in critical condition. She had been covering a military raid in a northern town and nearby refugee camp, a historical flashpoint in the Israeli-Palestinian conflict.\par \par \uc2 Abu Akleh was wearing a helmet and body armour clearly marked as \u8220\'20\'1Cpress\u8221\'20\'1D. The Qatar-based television network said her colleagues at the scene said the veteran reporter was shot by Israeli forces.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, Al Jazeera called on the international community to hold Israeli forces accountable for their {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/11/al-jazeera-journalist-killed-in-west-bank-unrest"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cintentional targeting and killing\u8221\'20\'1D of Abu Akleh}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CIn a blatant murder, violating international laws and norms, the Israeli occupation forces assassinated in cold blood Al Jazeera\u8217\'20\'19s correspondent in Palestine,\u8221\'20\'1D it said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What has the Israeli military said? A statement said its troops had shot back after coming under \u8220\'20\'1Cmassive fire\u8221\'20\'1D in Jenin and that \u8220\'20\'1Cthere is a possibility, now being looked into, that reporters were hit \u8211\'20\'13 possibly by shots fired by Palestinian gunmen\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In other news \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 As president, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  repeatedly asked aides if China could be manufacturing hurricanes and sending them to damage the U\par \par \uc2 S, three unnamed former senior officials told Rolling Stone. Trump also reportedly wanted to know {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/10/donald-trump-china-hurricanes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 if using such a \u8220\'20\'1Churricane gun\u8221\'20\'1D would constitute an act of war}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Survivors of the brutal regime of the late Philippines dictator Ferdinand Marcos have described his son\u8217\'20\'19s apparent landslide presidential election victory as the product of trickery, warning that it is unlikely the billions stolen by his family will be recovered, and that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/10/philippines-election-torture-survivors-from-marcos-sr-era-in-shock-after-sons-win"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 human rights in the country will be weakened}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The lifting of zero-Covid policies in China would see a \u8220\'20\'1Ctsunami\u8221\'20\'1D of infections and almost 1.6 million deaths, a study claims, citing in part {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/11/lifting-zero-covid-policies-in-china-could-risk-16m-deaths-says-study"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 China\u8217\'20\'19s low vaccination rate of elderly people.}}}\uc2  China\u8217\'20\'19s government remains committed to a zero-Covid policy, enforcing lockdowns, strict quarantine and isolation.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Vicky White spent 16 years developing a reputation as a model deputy in the sheriff\u8217\'20\'19s office that operates the jail in Lauderdale county, Alabama, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/10/alabama-prison-officer-vicky-white-inmate-escape"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to her boss}}}\uc2 . Authorities now say that makes it harder to come to grips with how she became the lover of a murder suspect incarcerated at her lockup.\par \par \uc2 Stat of the day: California water use leaps 19% in March,\par \par \uc2 one of the driest months on record\par \par \uc2 California\u8217\'20\'19s drought is worsening yet new figures show that in March, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/10/california-water-use-leaps-19-in-march-amid-one-of-the-driest-months-on-record"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 water usage jumped nearly 19% compared with 2020}}}\uc2 , one of the driest months on record. The startling figures come despite pleas from the authorities who have urged residents to curb their water usage. They also come the same day that the Los Angeles mayor ordered residents and businesses to restrict outdoor watering to just two days a week in an effort to conserve.\par \par \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t miss this: Finding it hard to get a new job? Robot recruiters might be to blame\par \par \uc2 There is a phenomenon in recruiting that is baffling experts: while there are record-level job openings in both the UK and in the US, why do many people still have to apply to sometimes hundreds of jobs, while many companies complain they can\u8217\'20\'19t find the right talent? Some experts argue that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/11/artitifical-intelligence-job-applications-screen-robot-recruiters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 algorithms and artificial intelligence now used extensively}}}\uc2  in hiring are playing a role.\par \par \uc2 \u8230\'20\'26 Or this:\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Republican and more Republican\u8217\'20\'19: Idaho shifts ever rightward\par \par \uc2 Idaho has long been one of the most conservative states in America with its fair share of extremism. Now, critics warn, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/11/iowa-right-wing-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 extremists are being normalised}}}\uc2 . Once dismissed as backwoods fanatics, the far right has entered the political arena and identified a path to power. That path leads through a state Republican party that has long exploited tensions between independent-spirited Idahoans and the federal government and more recently embraced \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s culture of grievance.\par \par \uc2 Climate check: Vanuatu\u8217\'20\'19s push for legal protection from climate change wins crucial support\par \par \uc2 Vanuatu\u8217\'20\'19s push for the international court of justice (ICJ) to protect vulnerable nations from climate change has received the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/11/vanuatus-push-for-legal-protection-from-climate-change-wins-crucial-support"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 backing of 1,500 civil society organisations from more than 130 countries}}}\uc2 , as it heads toward a crucial vote at the \uc2 UN\uc2  general assembly later this year. If it succeeds, the ICJ\u8217\'20\'19s advisory opinion \u8211\'20\'13 although non-binding \u8211\'20\'13 carries legal weight and moral authority which experts say could help shape international law.\par \par \uc2 Last Thing: Ordure! Ordure! Canadian MP sorry for logging on to session from toilet stall\par \par \uc2 A Canadian lawmaker has apologized after he was caught logging on to a parliamentary session from a toilet stall. The Liberal party member Shafqat Ali participated in the hybrid session of parliament, joining a Zoom-like feed. But {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/10/canadian-mp-toilet-stall-virtual-session"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 members grew suspicious}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThe member of parliament was literally using the washroom while participating in a sitting of the House of Commons, the cathedral of Canadian democracy,\u8221\'20\'1D the Conservative House leader, John Brassard, said.\par \par \uc2 Sign up\par \par \uc2 First Thing is delivered to thousands of inboxes every weekday. If you\u8217\'20\'19re not already signed up, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/info/2018/sep/17/guardian-us-morning-briefing-sign-up-to-stay-informed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 subscribe now}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Get in touch\par \par \uc2 If you have any questions or comments about any of our newsletters please email {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:newsletters@theguardian.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 newsletters@theguardian.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220511ei5b001mn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
