\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s not just the US, Britain needs no-protest buffer zones around its  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  clinics too\b0\par\par\uc2 Frances Ryan \par \uc2 973 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 May 2022\par 09:12 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Women seeking legal healthcare in the UK also suffer harassment. A decent, caring state would protect them\par \par \uc2 Thousands of miles from the United States supreme court, protesters have been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/backoffscotland/status/1521834681867591688?s=20&t=Qw0MhTOIruNVrcusKI3P_g"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 targeting women}}}\uc2  outside the Glasgow Royal Infirmary.\par \par \uc2 Recent weeks have seen reports of rising levels of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protests outside {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2022/may/04/calls-for-buffer-zones-around-abortion-clinics-in-scotland-after-protests?CMP=Share_iOSApp_Other"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Scottish hospitals}}}\uc2 , as well as ongoing anti-choice activism outside clinics {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.elle.com/uk/life-and-culture/a38036746/battle-outside-uk-abortion-clinics/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 across the UK}}}\uc2 . The methods are as varied as they are cruel. Calling women \u8220\'20\'1CMummy!\u8221\'20\'1D as they walk by. Leaflets warning falsely that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  causes cancer. Waving medically incorrect foetus dolls. Those who would force a woman through childbirth do not flinch from causing a woman distress.\par \par \uc2 Since 2018 there has been an anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  presence at 42 clinics across England and Wales, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.opendemocracy.net/en/5050/how-we-won-the-uks-first-ever-buffer-zone-around-an-abortion-clinic/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to}}}\uc2  the \uc2 British Pregnancy Advisory Service\uc2  (\uc2 BPAS\uc2 ). In Scotland, 70% of reproductive-age women live in a health board area that has been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thetimes.co.uk/article/doctors-call-for-protest-free-buffer-zones-at-abortion-clinics-k2ckh3ptb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 targeted by anti-choice protesters}}}\uc2  in the past five years. The scale of this is vast: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.opendemocracy.net/en/5050/how-we-won-the-uks-first-ever-buffer-zone-around-an-abortion-clinic/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than 100,000 women}}}\uc2  were subjected to anti-choice harassment while attending an appointment in 2019 (the last available data due to Covid).\par \par \uc2 After a lull during the pandemic lockdowns, \uc2 BPAS\uc2  tells me anti-choice activity outside clinics has now escalated. Women have reported severe intimidation to the charity. Men waiting for them and being followed from their car. Boyfriends having to \u8220\'20\'1Cshield\u8221\'20\'1D them to be able to get by. Having panic attacks as they walk in. Centuries ago, \u8220\'20\'1Cfallen\u8221\'20\'1D women were sometimes strapped to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.lancastercastle.com/history-heritage/further-articles/the-scolds-bridle/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ducking stool}}}\uc2  at the local river. Nowadays, they are accosted at health clinics.\par \par \uc2 Campaigners in the UK have long argued for buffer zones around women\u8217\'20\'19s health centres to address this \u8211\'20\'13 in essence creating a safe space that would offer those seeking \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legal protection from protesters. The SNP\u8217\'20\'19s manifesto pledged to support local authorities to establish protest-free zones around clinics. In England, similar zones exist in a handful of areas following a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.opendemocracy.net/en/5050/how-we-won-the-uks-first-ever-buffer-zone-around-an-abortion-clinic/?__cf_chl_tk=HOPhMJ5YxdnaLXN90GJSHcIfgAUWUWY6EiGjikf8svI-1652188009-0-gaNycGzNCJE"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 landmark case in Ealing}}}\uc2 , London, thanks to years of work by feminist activists. In March, Northern Ireland (where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services are severely limited, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://amp.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/04/abortion-services-in-northern-ireland-almost-nonexistent-despite-legalisation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 despite recent legalisation}}}\uc2  ) passed its own law to bring in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://humanists.uk/2022/03/25/northern-ireland-assembly-passes-buffer-zone-law-to-protect-women-accessing-abortion-services/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 protective buffers}}}\uc2 . And yet there is still no action from the Scottish government, nor are there plans for a buffer-zone policy across England and Wales after then home secretary \uc2 Sajid Javid{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/uk-45509202.amp"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rejected calls}}}\uc2  for one in 2018. Without a national solution, clinics have to rely on their local councils to apply for a public spaces protection order, pushing the burden on to already cash-strapped local authorities and leaving women facing a postcode lottery of dignity.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s hard not to feel that the inaction on buffer zones reflects that deep down, there is an acceptance of the prejudice that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  isn\u8217\'20\'19t quite \u8220\'20\'1Cnormal\u8221\'20\'1D healthcare. That the women going through the clinic doors may have the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  but it shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be made \u8220\'20\'1Ceasy\u8221\'20\'1D. No patient undertaking any other medical procedure would be expected to walk through an intimidating crowd to get treatment. If an extremist group coordinated nationwide opposition to heart transplants as being \u8220\'20\'1Cunnatural\u8221\'20\'1D, ministers would soon put measures in place to protect cardiac patients.\par \par \uc2 Even calling the issue protests is misleading, as if what is happening is people harmlessly exercising their democratic right. Anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists outside clinics are not protesting \u8211\'20\'13 they are harassing. Their ultimate aim is not simply to protest against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  but to obstruct women seeking what is essential, legal medical treatment. In some cases, these are calculated delaying tactics \u8211\'20\'13 women report missing appointments because they felt unable to face the harassment (\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a time-sensitive procedure). As well as patients, clinic staff are being subjected to daily intimidation at work. Some report being called \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.google.com/amp/s/www.mylondon.news/news/west-london-news/ealings-abortion-clinic-staff-being-16116053.amp"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 murderers\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cbaby killers}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D, and have even been followed by activists.\par \par \uc2 The growth of anti-choice intimidation in Britain will naturally be seen in the shadow of the leaked plan for the US to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/04/first-thing-us-shaken-by-supreme-court-draft-overturning-roe-v-wade-abortion?CMP=Share_iOSApp_Other"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturn Roe v Wade}}}\uc2 . It would be simplistic to conflate the two countries \u8211\'20\'13 the US and UK are different beasts politically and culturally \u8211\'20\'13 but it\u8217\'20\'19s naive to ignore the links. Long before any law change, US anti-choice activists began by spreading {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.opendemocracy.net/en/5050/trump-linked-religious-extremists-global-disinformation-pregnant-women/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 disinformation}}}\uc2  through clinics, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2015/11/29/us/30abortion-clinic-violence.html?mtrref=undefined&gwh=23474DBB6088EF8AB24443C62DF09DDE&gwt=pay&assetType=PAYWALL"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attacking doctors}}}\uc2  and getting buffer zones {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://adfmedia.org/case/mccullen-v-coakley"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 banned}}}\uc2 . There are coordinated efforts by wealthy American anti-choice organisations to extend their work to the UK. The US-based religious group 40 Days for Life recruited the organiser of the recent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dailyrecord.co.uk/news/scottish-news/scots-anti-abortion-protester-recruited-26484563.amp"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Scottish protest}}}\uc2 . Some even host {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2022/may/05/us-far-right-abortion-laws-europe-roe-v-wade?CMP=Share_iOSApp_Other"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Conservative MPs}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The UK\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law may be on firmer ground than our neighbours\u8217\'20\'19 across the Atlantic, but that does not mean we should be complacent. A woman\u8217\'20\'19s human rights are never permanently won. This is the time for the government to reaffirm its commitment to reproductive rights: making access to medical \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills at home {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.scotsman.com/news/politics/scotland-must-act-quickly-on-abortion-services-as-new-study-shows-women-overwhelmingly-support-telemedicine-provisions-3684745"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 permanent in Scotland}}}\uc2  to follow gains in England and Wales; decriminalising \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ending a pregnancy is still a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/health-40418986"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 criminal act}}}\uc2  in England and Wales unless two doctors give permission and agree it\u8217\'20\'19s detrimental to the woman\u8217\'20\'19s wellbeing or health); and finally introducing national buffer zone legislation.\par \par \uc2 Whether it is a judge with a pen or an activist with a placard, all strategies to impinge female bodily autonomy must be resisted. The state\u8217\'20\'19s refusal to offer women protection outside health clinics is not a small matter but goes to the very heart of what it means to live in a country with reproductive control. It is not enough for women to have the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 they should have the right to one without fear, harassment or shame. Otherwise, it is barely a real right at all.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Frances Ryan is a Guardian columnist\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220511ei5b001gv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
