\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  calls inflation his \u8216\'20\'18top domestic priority\u8217\'20\'19 but blames Covid and Putin \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Lauren Gambino in Washington \par \uc2 6,053 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 May 2022\par 21:05 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 President says he understands American\u8217\'20\'19s frustration with Democrats, who control all three branches of government: \u8216\'20\'18I don\u8217\'20\'19t blame them\u8217\'20\'19US immigration agency operates vast surveillance dragnet, study findsDivided States of America: Roe v Wade is \u8216\'20\'18precursor to larger struggles\u8217\'20\'19Sign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Evening summary\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said inflation was his \u8220\'20\'1Ctop domestic priority\u8221\'20\'1D as he attempted to draw a contrast between his party and the \u8220\'20\'1Cultra Maga\u8221\'20\'1D Republicans who he warned would enact an extremist agenda that doesn\u8217\'20\'19t address the economic challenges facing the nation. He also said he understood that voters were frustrated with the party in power, but insisted his economic agenda had \u8220\'20\'1Chelped, not hurt\u8221\'20\'1D the economic recovery.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  said he would lift \uc2 Twitter\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s ban on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , allowing the former president to use the platform more than a year after he was removed after the January 6 riot.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Avril Haines\uc2 , the national director of intelligence, testified that \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  was prepared for a \u8220\'20\'1Cprolonged conflict\u8221\'20\'1D in Ukraine, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Julian Borger reports.\par \par \uc2 * A New York appeals court has dismissed a lawsuit by state attorney general Letitia James against {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/amazon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Amazon}}}\uc2  over its coronavirus safety protocols, and against a former employee who led the successful union organizing effort on Staten Island.\par \par \uc2 * Florida\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , a possible 2024 presidential hopeful, has signed a law mandating the state\u8217\'20\'19s students receive instruction about \u8220\'20\'1Cthe victims of communism\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 * Pennsylvania\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic senator Bob Casey, one of the last self-described \u8220\'20\'1Cpro life\u8221\'20\'1D Democrats, announced he would support legislation to codify {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections. The measure still does not have enough support to overcome Republican opposition.\par \par \uc2 * Treasury secretary \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2  said ending the constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  would have \u8220\'20\'1Cvery damaging\u8221\'20\'1D effects on the economy and women\u8217\'20\'19s earning potential, during testimony to the Senate banking committee.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 Still to come today\par \par \uc2 At present, Biden is still meeting with House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  and other members of a congressional delegation that visited Ukraine earlier this month to discuss their experience in the war-torn country. Later this evening, the House is expected to vote tonight on a nearly $40bn military and humanitarian aid package.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, voters in Nebraska and West Virginia are still casting ballots in a series of primary elections that will test \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s enduring influence over his party.\par \par \uc2 In West Virginia, Trump waded into a contentious Republican primary between two sitting members of Congress, endorsing congressman Alex Mooney over congressman \uc2 David McKinley\uc2 , who infuriated the former president when he voted for the creation of a House committee to investigate the January 6 attack on the US Capitol. And in Nebraska, Trump endorsed \uc2 Charles Herbster\uc2  to be the Republican nominee for governor in a bitter, nine-way primary race to replace the sitting Republican governor, who is limited. Herbster is accused of groping multiple women, allegations he has denied.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 During an Oval Office visit, Italian Premier \uc2 Mario Draghi\uc2  urged Biden and world leaders to work toward \u8220\'20\'1Cthe possibility of bringing a ceasefire\u8221\'20\'1D between Ukraine and Russia in the hope of restarting negotiations.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn Italy and Europe now, people want to put an end to these massacres and this violence, this butchery,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/russia-ukraine-biden-europe-italy-avril-haines-437b738cd782a7d657e6b9dfed79b295"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fuller analysis of the meeting }}}\uc2  from the Associated Press, which stated that the visit \u8220\'20\'1Cprovided a window into divergent approaches\u8221\'20\'1D to the Russian invasion of Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Biden did not echo Draghi\u8217\'20\'19s comments, and U.S. officials appear openly skeptical that there\u8217\'20\'19s a way to restart talks at this point.\par \par \uc2 Avril Haines\uc2 , Biden\u8217\'20\'19s director of national intelligence, testified earlier Tuesday that both Ukraine and Russia believe they can make progress on the battlefield at this point, so \u8220\'20\'1Cwe do not see a viable negotiating path forward, at least in the short term.\u8221\'20\'1D...\par \par \uc2 The different tones over Ukraine reflect Italy\u8217\'20\'19s geographic proximity to the war and deeper economic ties to Russia, which provides 40% of the country\u8217\'20\'19s natural gas. There\u8217\'20\'19s also growing skepticism in Italy about sending weapons to Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 In a floor speech on Tuesday, New York congressman \uc2 Tom Reed\uc2  announced that he was resigning with more than seven months left of his term.\par \par \uc2 Last year, Reed announced he would not seek re-election after he was accused of sexual misconduct.\par \par \uc2 In his speech, Reed denounced the \u8220\'20\'1Cthe focus on extremism\u8221\'20\'1D, according to Politico.\par \par \uc2 enltrRep. \uc2 Tom Reed\uc2  (R-NY) denounces "the focus on extremism" on the House floor right before he submitted his resignation, making it his last day serving in the House.\par \par \uc2 "It is time for petty political posturing to end," he says in a 1 minute speech. "Leadership must emerge..." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/QVQqjPaTJ2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/QVQqjPaTJ2}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Olivia Beavers (@Olivia_Beavers)\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Olivia_Beavers/status/1524093840046665728?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 10, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am leaving to continue that work and hope to have a greater impact on our country,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 Reed was among the lawmakers in his state who called for the resignation of former New York governor \uc2 Andrew Cuomo\uc2  over {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/new-york-andrew-cuomo-6e3c286c9ccfde352fc7b15ae7be9f70"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sexual harassment allegations}}}\uc2 . And late last year, Reed said he was considering running for governor to challenge Cuomo, who later resigned amid the cascading scandal.\par \par \uc2 After the accusations against the congressman, Reed said in a statement apologizing for his behavior that he would not run for any office in 2022.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s David Smith looks at what the fight over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights tells us about the divisions in America today.\par \par \uc2 This opening scenes encapsulates the current political climate well.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou put your babies in the womb, you will be held accountable!\u8221\'20\'1D yelled Steve Corson, tall, bearded and jabbing a finger at women who chanted back: \u8220\'20\'1CMy body, my choice!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Corson took a deep breath and blew into a shofar. Then Nathan Darnell, wearing a \u8220\'20\'1CJesus Christ is king\u8221\'20\'1D cap and holding aloft a cross, grabbed a megaphone.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou guys are demon-possessed!\u8221\'20\'1D declared the 19-year-old from Haymarket, Virginia. \u8220\'20\'1CYou guys are controlled by demons, all of you. Every child has a right to life.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Suddenly Darnell was surrounded by \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights protesters brandishing placards. He kept talking.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou guys are evil. The downfall of America is because of every one of you.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The national day of prayer last Thursday was anything but a solemn occasion outside the supreme court in Washington, where hours earlier an unscalable {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/supreme-court/non-scalable-fence-erected-supreme-court-abortion-related-protests-rcna27452"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  black fence had been erected}}}\uc2 , reminiscent of the one that surrounded the US Capitol after the January 6 insurrection.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/10/divided-america-roe-v-wade-supreme-court-cold-civil-war"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Divided States of America: Roe v Wade is \u8216\'20\'18precursor to larger struggles\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 Whether Democrats support the pro-choice protests outside the homes of Supreme Court justices has become a hot topic in Washington as passions intensify ahead of a ruling poised to strip millions of Americans of access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 During a press conference today, Schumer was asked whether he was comfortable with the protests. He said he was as long as they remained peaceful.\par \par \uc2 enltrQ: "Are you comfortable with the protests that we saw outside the homes of Supreme Court justices over the weekend?" {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenSchumer?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @SenSchumer}}}\uc2  : "If protests are peaceful; yes. My house, there's protests 3-4 times a week outside my house." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Mlu5dbHDbr"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Mlu5dbHDbr}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CSPAN (@cspan)\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cspan/status/1524098988827418628?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 10, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 The president blessed a plan to unhitch Ukraine assistance and coronavirus funding. But now there\u8217\'20\'19s no clear path forward on passing pandemic funding for tests, vaccines and therapeutics.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShould Americans start preparing for shortages?\u8221\'20\'1D a reporter asked.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe don\u8217\'20\'19t want to sugarcoat it: we need more money,\u8221\'20\'1D Psaki said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe don\u8217\'20\'19t have a plan B here.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She was asked if the president would be OK with holding a vote on Title 42, a pandemic-era public health order that is being used to control immigration at the border. The administration has said it plans to lift the order, but Republicans and some Democrats oppose the decision, which is tied up in court proceedings. Now Republicans want Democrats to allow a vote on keeping Title 42 in place before they will support Biden\u8217\'20\'19s request for pandemic funding.\par \par \uc2 Psaki said it was a hypothetical and she wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t speculate on what the legislative path forward would be.\par \par \uc2 In response to a question on whether Biden would support businesses leaving states that impose \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans should Roe fall, Psaki said she hadn\u8217\'20\'19t spoken to the president about this yet. Biden previously supported efforts by companies and sports teams to leverage their clout to pressure conservative states to back off restrictive voting legislation.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 The first question is about inflation, specifically, whether Biden thinks the size of his coronavirus relief bill contributed to rising costs. Earlier today, the president said he believed his policies had \u8220\'20\'1Chelped, not hurt\u8221\'20\'1D the economy.\par \par \uc2 Psaki said many economists agree that the pandemic is a major cause of inflation, and that his domestic agenda has helped combat the virus, which is necessary for bringing down costs. She also pointed to the war in Ukraine as another factor, which Biden will continue to highlight on his travels outside of Washington.\par \par \uc2 A reporter also asked who came up with the term \u8220\'20\'1Cultra-MAGA\u8221\'20\'1D, which the president unveiled as a new epithet for Trump-friendly Republicans.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s the president\u8217\'20\'19s phrase,\u8221\'20\'1D Psaki said, explaining that Biden has been \u8220\'20\'1Cstruck\u8221\'20\'1D by how \u8220\'20\'1Cextreme some of the policies and proposals\u8221\'20\'1D that certain Republicans support are. \u8220\'20\'1CAdding a little ultra to it gives it a little extra pop.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Another reporter pressed her on why Biden said a \u8220\'20\'1Cmajority\u8221\'20\'1D of Republicans supported Scott\u8217\'20\'19s 11-point plan when many have sought to distance themselves from it, Psaki rattled off a list of quotes from Republicans who had praised the agenda.\par \par \uc2 She has been asked multiple questions about the protests outside the justices\u8217\'20\'19 homes after the leaked supreme court draft that showed the court was poised to overturn Roe. Psaki said she understood passions were high and that the president and the White House strongly supported the right to peaceful protest, and stressed that the protests have so far remained peaceful at the justices\u8217\'20\'19 homes. She also said there was \u8220\'20\'1Chypocrisy\u8221\'20\'1D on the part of Republicans who are upset over these protests and yet remained silent when their supporters intimidated school board members and election officials.\par \par \uc2 The decision to let Trump back on \uc2 Twitter\uc2  was one for the private sector to make, she said, responding to an interview in which Musk said he would reverse the ban against the former president. But Psaki said the White House\u8217\'20\'19s goal was to protect freedom of speech while ensuring social media platforms don\u8217\'20\'19t become a \u8220\'20\'1Cforum for disinformation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2 , the outgoing White House press secretary, is now briefing reporters on Biden\u8217\'20\'19s Wednesday trip to Illinois, where he will visit a family farm to highlight \u8220\'20\'1CPutin\u8217\'20\'19s price hike\u8221\'20\'1D and the impact on food prices.\par \par \uc2 She also announced that he will host Pelosi and other congressional members this afternoon in the Situation Room to hear more about their trip to Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 A New York appeals court has dismissed a lawsuit by state attorney general Letitia James against {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/amazon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Amazon}}}\uc2  over its coronavirus safety protocols, and against a former employee who led the successful union organizing effort on Staten Island, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 The suit had claimed that \uc2 Amazon\uc2  potentially exposed workers to Covid-19 at two facilities in New York city, and that the company illegally retaliated against workers who spoke up about poor safety conditions in its warehouses.\par \par \uc2 They included {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/10/chris-smalls-amazon-union-staten-island"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Chris Smalls}}}\uc2  , the fired \uc2 Amazon\uc2  worker who heads the \uc2 Amazon\uc2  labor union, and Derrick Palmer, the group\u8217\'20\'19s vice president of organizing.\par \par \uc2 The appellate court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling Tuesday said federal labor law preempted state labor law, and the national labor relations board \u8220\'20\'1Cshould serve as the forum\u8221\'20\'1D for disputes, not the states.\par \par \uc2 Palmer, who was given a final written warning in the early days of the pandemic, is still employed at \uc2 Amazon\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling is a win for \uc2 Amazon\uc2 , which had sought to have the case thrown out. Neither \uc2 Amazon\uc2 , nor James\u8217\'20\'19 office immediately responded to the AP\u8217\'20\'19s request for comment.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 Musk says he would reverse \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's \uc2 Twitter\uc2  ban\par \par \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 , the \uc2 Tesla\uc2  chief executive and world\u8217\'20\'19s richest person who recently agreed a deal to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2022/apr/25/twitter-elon-musk-buy-takeover-deal-tesla"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 buy Twitter for $44bn}}}\uc2 , says he will reverse the social media platform\u8217\'20\'19s permanent ban on former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 . Photograph: Joe Skipper/Reuters\par \par \uc2 The decision to ban Trump from \uc2 Twitter\uc2  did not silence his voice, but rather amplified his views among people on the political right, Musk said, during remarks on Tuesday at the \uc2 Financial Times\uc2  future of the car conference.\par \par \uc2 Calling the ban \u8220\'20\'1Cmorally wrong and flat-out stupid\u8221\'20\'1D, Musk said:\par \par \uc2 Permanent bans should be extremely rare and really reserved for accounts that are bots, or scam, spam accounts.\par \par \uc2 I do think it was not correct to ban \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . I think that was a mistake, because it alienated a large part of the country and did not ultimately result in \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  not having a voice.\par \par \uc2 Trump was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/08/donald-trump-twitter-ban-suspended"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 banned permanently}}}\uc2  two days after inciting the deadly 6 January Capitol attack for breaching \uc2 Twitter\uc2  rules. The platform\u8217\'20\'19s owners cited \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://blog.twitter.com/en_us/topics/company/2020/suspension"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the risk of further incitement of violence}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D for its decision.\par \par \uc2 Musk, who has called himself a \u8220\'20\'1Cfree speech absolutist,\u8221\'20\'1D said he would reverse the ban, but noted:\par \par \uc2 I don\u8217\'20\'19t own \uc2 Twitter\uc2  yet. So this is not like a thing that will definitely happen, because what if I don\u8217\'20\'19t own \uc2 Twitter\uc2 ?\par \par \uc2 Trump, meanwhile, says {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/technology/trump-says-he-wont-return-twitter-if-account-reinstated-after-musk-takeover-2022-04-25/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he wants no further part}}}\uc2  of a platform where he once enjoyed a following of more than 85m. He told Fox News last month he was going to stay instead on Truth Social, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2022/mar/16/truth-social-donald-trump-failing-anti-twitter-platform"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 failing anti-Twitter rival}}}\uc2  he rarely uses.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2022/may/10/elon-musk-pledges-overturn-twitter-ban-donald-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Elon Musk pledges to overturn Twitter\u8217\'20\'19s ban on Donald Trump}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Interim summary\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where we are halfway through a busy Tuesday:\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  insisted that soaring inflation was his \u8216\'20\'18top domestic priority\u8217\'20\'19 as he delivered remarks on the economy at the White House. The president said his policies had \u8220\'20\'1Chelped not hurt\u8221\'20\'1D the nation\u8217\'20\'19s economic outlook but acknowledged voters were \u8220\'20\'1Cfrustrated\u8221\'20\'1D as November\u8217\'20\'19s midterms loom.\par \par \uc2 * Florida\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , a possible 2024 presidential hopeful, has signed a law mandating the state\u8217\'20\'19s students receive instruction about \u8220\'20\'1Cthe victims of communism\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 * Pennsylvania\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic senator Bob Casey, one of the last self-described \u8220\'20\'1Cpro life\u8221\'20\'1D Democrats, announced he would support legislation to codify {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections.\par \par \uc2 * Treasury Secretary \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2  said ending the constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  would have \u8220\'20\'1Cvery damaging\u8221\'20\'1D effects on the economy and women\u8217\'20\'19s earning potential, during testimony to the Senate banking committee.\par \par \uc2 * Lawmakers were set to begin debating a nearly $40bn aid package for Ukraine, a sum that exceeds the $33bn Biden requested of Congress. An agreement was reached among Congressional leaders to swiftly send the aid to Biden\u8217\'20\'19s desk, after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats}}}\uc2  untangled the package from a separate request for coronavirus funding.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 Avril Haines\uc2 , the national director of intelligence, testified that Putin was preparing for \u8220\'20\'1Cprolonged conflict\u8221\'20\'1D in Ukraine, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Julian Borger reports.\par \par \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  could view the prospect of defeat in Ukraine as an existential threat to his regime, potentially triggering his resort to using a nuclear weapon, the top US intelligence official has warned.\par \par \uc2 The warning on Tuesday came in an assessment from intelligence chiefs briefing the Senate on worldwide threats. The prediction for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukraine}}}\uc2  was a long, gruelling war of attrition, which could lead to increasingly volatile acts of escalation from Putin, including full mobilisation, the imposition of martial law, and \u8211\'20\'13 if the Russian leader felt the war was going against him, endangering his position in Moscow \u8211\'20\'13 even the use of a nuclear warhead.\par \par \uc2 ... Haines told the Senate armed services committee that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/mar/26/russia-reasserts-right-to-use-nuclear-weapons-in-ukraine-putin"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Putin would continue to brandish Russia\u8217\'20\'19s nuclear arsenal}}}\uc2  in an attempt to deter the US and its allies from further support for Ukraine. The shift of focus to the east and the south are most likely a temporary tactic rather than a permanent scaling back of war aims, she said.\par \par \uc2 The Russian leader would not use a nuclear weapon until he saw an existential threat to Russia or his regime, Haines argued. But she added that he could view the prospect of defeat in Ukraine as constituting such a threat.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/10/putin-nuclear-weapons-us-intelligence-avril-haines"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US intelligence chief warns of nuclear risk if Putin perceives \u8216\'20\'18existential threat\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s resident Miami correspondent and part-time politics blogger sends this dispatch on an effort by a Florida school to hide activism by its students against the state\u8217\'20\'19s controversial \u8220\'20\'1Cdon\u8217\'20\'19t say gay\u8221\'20\'1D law.\par \par \uc2 A Florida high school is covering up yearbook photographs of students who took part in protest against the state\u8217\'20\'19s so-called {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/mar/08/dont-say-gay-bill-florida-senate-lgbtq"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 don\u8217\'20\'19t say gay law}}}\uc2 , in a move its editors are calling blatant censorship, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.orlandosentinel.com/news/education/os-ne-seminole-yearbook-censorship-20220509-bme2ndwu2fagjh5gk6lim2j7si-story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the Orlando Sentinel}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Administrators at Lyman high school in Seminole county delayed distribution of the book on Monday, the newspaper says, until they can black out photographs of students holding rainbow flags and a \u8220\'20\'1Clove is love\u8221\'20\'1D sign, taken during a walkout protest in March against the law that prohibits discussion in certain Florida classrooms of gender identity and sexual orientation.\par \par \uc2 The Sentinel quotes student Skye Tiedemann, one of the yearbook\u8217\'20\'19s editors-in-chief: \u8220\'20\'1CThis really shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be happening because all we did as journalists was document what was happening at our school on our campus.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTo have that covered up isn\u8217\'20\'19t right. This is censorship.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The school\u8217\'20\'19s principal, Michael Hunter, told parents in a recorded message that the photographs \u8220\'20\'1Cdid not meet school board policy\u8221\'20\'1D, but gave no further details.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRather than reprinting the yearbook at substantial cost and delay, we have elected to cover the material that is out of compliance... so that yearbooks can be distributed as soon as possible,\u8221\'20\'1D he added, according to the Sentinel.\par \par \uc2 Florida\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  received massive blowback for the controversial \u8220\'20\'1Cdon\u8217\'20\'19t say gay\u8221\'20\'1D law, which prompted a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/09/ron-desantis-disney-republican-culture-war"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 squabble with Disney}}}\uc2 , the state\u8217\'20\'19s largest private employer, and drew a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2022/04/01/1090211332/dont-say-gay-law-florida-lawsuit-desantis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lawsuit from LBGTQ+ groups}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Students at several Florida high schools walked out of classes in protest as the bill passed through the state\u8217\'20\'19s Republican-dominated legislature in March.\par \par \uc2 For more on Florida schools, here\u8217\'20\'19s Richard\u8217\'20\'19s story from earlier today on a new law that would require students in the state to receive \u8220\'20\'1Cat least 45 minutes\u8217\'20\'19 instruction every November about the \u8216\'20\'18victims of communism.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/10/florida-ron-desantis-communism-bill-students"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DeSantis signs bill for Florida students to learn about \u8216\'20\'18victims of communism\u8217\'20\'19 }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 After his remarks, Biden lingered at the podium to take a few questions on the topic of inflation. (He dismissed off-topic questions, including one about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.)\par \par \uc2 Asked whether he believed his agenda was to blame or had contributed to rising costs, he said his policies have \u8220\'20\'1Chelped not hurt\u8221\'20\'1D the economy.\par \par \uc2 Yet he said he understood why Americans were frustrated as they struggled to pay bills and afford basic necessities like gas and food.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re in power\u8230\'20\'26we control all three branches of government,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, before lamenting that Democrats did not have 60 votes in the Senate to advance his agenda.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re frustrated,\u8221\'20\'1D he said of voters. \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t blame them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Asked why he hasn\u8217\'20\'19t urged Americans to travel less and shift to more environmentally-friendly modes of transportation, Biden said Americans are already reducing their travel to save on costs. He added that right now many Americans don\u8217\'20\'19t have any other option than to drive and said the infrastructure bill would help change that.\par \par \uc2 A reporter asked for Biden\u8217\'20\'19s response to the statement from senator Scott, which referred to Biden as \u8220\'20\'1Cincoherent\u8221\'20\'1D and said the president should resign, a reporter asked for his response. Laughing, Biden said: \u8220\'20\'1CI think the man has a problem.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He also said he was surprised that the \u8220\'20\'1Cultra-MAGA\u8221\'20\'1D Republicans maintained such a strong grip on the party.\par \par \uc2 He declined to say when he thought inflation would ebb: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not going to predict that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On the topic of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s tariffs on China, Biden said he was deliberating over whether to lift them but no decision had been made.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here is the quote in full that effectively, though not succinctly, sums up the White House\u8217\'20\'19s message on inflation heading into the midterm elections.\par \par \uc2 Americans have a choice right now between two paths, reflecting two very different sets of values. My plan attacks inflation and grows the economy by lowering the costs for working families, giving workers well-deserved raises, reducing the deficits by historic levels, and making big corporations and the very wealthiest Americans pay their fair share. The other path is the \u8216\'20\'18ultra-MAGA\u8217\'20\'19 plan put forward by Congressional republicans to raise taxes on American families , lower the income of American workers, threaten sacred programs Americans count on like social security, medicare and medicaid, and give break after break to big corporations and billionaires just like they did the last time in power when their top priority was the reckless $2tn tax cut the majority of that going to the wealthiest Americans which ballooned the deficit and not a penny of it was paid for,\u8221\'20\'1D the president said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden: inflation is 'my top domestic priority'\par \par \uc2 Speaking from the White House, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  laid the blame for rising costs on two key factors: a \u8220\'20\'1Conce-in-a-century pandemic\u8221\'20\'1D that shut down the global economy and snarled supply chains and Russian leader \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 , who invaded Ukraine and sent the cost of gas and food soaring.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI want every American to know that I\u8217\'20\'19m taking inflation very seriously and it\u8217\'20\'19s my top domestic priority,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 Republicans and some economists have accused the White House of being slow to recognize the urgency of inflation, which Biden once suggested would be temporary. But as costs continue to climb, Biden has re-oriented his agenda to address inflation, which he said was the nation\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Ctop economic challenge right now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden is now assailing Republicans for their economic agenda, which he said is making inflation worse. He blamed them for being \u8220\'20\'1Cextreme\u8221\'20\'1D and more interested in protecting large corporations than working families.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn this moment of peril, with the war overseas and inflation surging around the world, the last thing we should be thinking about is rewarding companies for exploiting the situation,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 The president is now pulling from Scott\u8217\'20\'19s aforementioned 11-point plan, warning that Republicans are a threat to beloved social-safety net programs like social security and Medicare.\par \par \uc2 Even if Republicans don\u8217\'20\'19t ultimately want to end those programs, Biden said they would use the threat as a \u8220\'20\'1Chostage\u8221\'20\'1D to get their way on other issues.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senator Bob Casey, a Catholic and one of the last self-described \u8220\'20\'1Cpro life\u8221\'20\'1D Democrats, announced on Tuesday that he would support legislation to codify Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, the Pennsylvania Democrat said the \u8220\'20\'1Ccircumstances on the entire debate of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  have changed\u8221\'20\'1D after a leaked draft opinion revealed the nation\u8217\'20\'19s highest court was prepared to end a woman\u8217\'20\'19s constitutional right to terminate a pregnancy. The question before the Senate now, he argues, is \u8220\'20\'1Cdo you support a categorical ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDuring my time in public office, I have never voted for \u8211\'20\'13 nor do I support \u8211\'20\'13 such a ban,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 enltrMy statement on the Senate\u8217\'20\'19s upcoming vote on the Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Protection Act: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ABap00RiOV"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ABap00RiOV}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Senator Bob Casey (@SenBobCasey) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenBobCasey/status/1524050097021009920?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 10, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Casey voted previously to open debate on the measure, but said would support the bill if it ever came to a final vote. His decision underscores how deeply partisan the issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has become.\par \par \uc2 Yet his support for the measure does little to change its political fate in Congress \u8211\'20\'13 the bill does not have the support of a single Republican, including the two pro-choice Republican senators who have introduced separate legislation to codify Roe. It remains unclear if Joe Manchin, the other Democrat who has opposed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, will vote to advance the measure when it comes up for a preliminary vote on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The announcement came as activists said they were staging a sit in at Casey\u8217\'20\'19s office in the state\u8217\'20\'19s capital, Harrisburg, demanding he back efforts to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 The president is due to speak shortly about the administration\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to reduce inflation. But a significant chunk of the remarks are expected to highlight a plan by Senator \uc2 Rick Scott\uc2 , a Republican of Florida, that would increase the federal income taxes for many Americans.\par \par \uc2 A White House statement on Tuesday {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2022/05/10/the-biden-harris-inflation-plan-lowering-costs-and-lowering-the-deficit/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  : Congressional Republicans, led by Senator \uc2 Rick Scott\uc2 , have called for a new minimum tax on the middle class \u8211\'20\'13 firefighters and teachers \u8211\'20\'13 that would mean an average of almost $1,500 less in families\u8217\'20\'19 pockets each year. And, while part of President Biden\u8217\'20\'19s plan to lower costs is to strengthen Medicare by giving it the power to negotiate prescription drug prices, the Congressional Republican plan would put Medicare \u8211\'20\'13 in addition to Social Security, Medicaid, the Affordable Care Act and other critical programs for American families \u8211\'20\'13 on the chopping block every five years.\par \par \uc2 However, few Republicans have embraced the plan and many have denounced it.\par \par \uc2 Inflation is a top concern for many voters, and Republicans are confident that blaming Democrats for rising costs is a winning message ahead of the 2022 midterms. In response, the White House and Democrats have seized on Scott\u8217\'20\'19s 11-point plan to make the case that Republicans, not Democrats, want to raise taxes on Americans.\par \par \uc2 Ahead of the president\u8217\'20\'19s remarks, Scott, who is chairman of the National Republican Senatorial Committee, has issued a blistering statement calling Biden \u8220\'20\'1Cunwell\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cunfit for office\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrAs Biden highlights \uc2 Rick Scott\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s plan to make all Americans pay some federal income tax, Scott issues this statement: \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is unwell. He\u8217\'20\'19s unfit for office. He\u8217\'20\'19s incoherent, incapacitated and confused. He doesn\u8217\'20\'19t know where he is half the time. He\u8217\'20\'19s incapable of leading\u8230\'20\'26\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sahil Kapur (@sahilkapur) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/sahilkapur/status/1524035479687020546?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 10, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 Yellen: Overturning Roe would 'set women back decades' economically\par \par \uc2 Treasury Secretary \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2  said ending the constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  would have \u8220\'20\'1Cvery damaging\u8221\'20\'1D effect on the economy and women\u8217\'20\'19s earning potential.\par \par \uc2 Testifying before the Senate banking committee this morning, Yellen was asked by Senator \uc2 Bob Menendez\uc2 , a Democrat of New Jersey, what the loss of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access would mean for women economically.\par \par \uc2 I believe that eliminating the right of women to make decisions about when and whether to have children would have very damaging effects on the economy and would set women back decades,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 enltrSec. Yellen in a Senate hearing weighs in on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  debate: "I believe that eliminating the right of women to make decisions about when and whether to have children would have very damaging effects on the economy and would set women back decades."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Amara Omeokwe (@TheAmaraReport) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TheAmaraReport/status/1524029116927905794?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 10, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrSecretary Yellen: \u8220\'20\'1CRoe v. Wade and access to reproductive healthcare, including \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , helped lead to increased labor force participation. It enabled many women to finish school. That increased their earning potential. It allowed women to plan and balance\u8221\'20\'1D families and careers\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Manu Raju (@mkraju) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1524034842530394113?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 10, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Senator Tim Scott, a Republican from South Carolina, pushed back on Yellen\u8217\'20\'19s assertion that the loss of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access will hurt women economically, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.brookings.edu/research/what-can-economic-research-tell-us-about-the-effect-of-abortion-access-on-womens-lives/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bolstered by years of research}}}\uc2 , calling it \u8220\'20\'1Ccallous\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Charsh.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt means children will grow up in poverty,\u8221\'20\'1D she replied.\par \par \uc2 enltrGOP {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenatorTimScott?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @SenatorTimScott}}}\uc2  tells Yellen it's "callous" to connect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to labor statistics, "harsh" to refer to this as a risk to economic stability\par \par \uc2 Yellen: "It means children will grow up in poverty'' {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/mCyLkX5vhF"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/mCyLkX5vhF}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Saleha Mohsin (@SalehaMohsin) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SalehaMohsin/status/1524035606472687616?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 10, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 As the White House prepares to convene a Covid-19 summit this week, former heads of state, dignitaries and Nobel laureates are urging Biden to do more to lead the world\u8217\'20\'19s response to the virus and improve preparedness for a future pandemic.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/live/2022/05/10/world/covid-19-mandates-vaccine-cases?partner=slack&smid=sl-share#biden-covd-aid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 According to the New York Times,}}}\uc2  the group are calling on the US to commit $5bn to combat the virus globally.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI want America to recognize that the disease is not over anywhere until it\u8217\'20\'19s over everywhere,\u8221\'20\'1D former British prime minister Gordon Brown {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/live/2022/05/10/world/covid-19-mandates-vaccine-cases?partner=slack&smid=sl-share#biden-covd-aid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told}}}\uc2  the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  in an interview.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe must not sleepwalk into the next variant,\u8221\'20\'1D said Brown, now the now the \uc2 World Health Organization\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s ambassador for global health financing>\par \par \uc2 But as we explained earlier, the White House\u8217\'20\'19s request for additional resources to buy more tests, vaccines and therapeutics is being held up in Congress over Republican opposition to a decision by the administration to lift a pandemic-era immigration rule.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, Biden said it a statement that he supported the decision to decouple coronavirus funding from an aid package for Ukraine, leaving the fate of the former uncertain.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLet me be clear,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said in the statement, \u8220\'20\'1Cas vital as it is to help Ukraine combat Russian aggression, it is equally vital to help Americans combat Covid. Biden told lawmakers that a failure to approve additional funding would hurt both domestic and international efforts to beat back the pandemic.\par \par \uc2 Biden has requested $22.5bn in emergency coronavirus aid, including $5bn for the global response to the pandemic. The virtual summit on Thursday will be hosted jointly by Belize, Germany, Indonesia and Senegal.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 Lawmakers on Tuesday are set to begin debating a nearly $40bn aid package, an extraordinary sum that exceeds the $33bn Biden requested of Congress.\par \par \uc2 An agreement was reached among Congressional leaders to swiftly send the aid to Biden\u8217\'20\'19s desk, after Democrats untangled the package from a separate request for coronavirus funding.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe cannot afford delay in this vital war effort,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said in a statement on Monday. \u8220\'20\'1C. Hence, I am prepared to accept that these two measures move separately, so that the Ukrainian aid bill can get to my desk right away.\u8221\'20\'1D He urged Congress to send the package to him \u8220\'20\'1Cin the next few days.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As lawmakers discuss the aid, Ukraine Ambassador \uc2 Oksana Markarova\uc2  will be on the Hill to speak at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/news/senate/3482753-ukrainian-ambassador-to-attend-senate-gop-lunch/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the caucus lunches}}}\uc2 , according to The Hill. It comes after Biden on Monday signed a bill into law that will expedite the shipment of military aid and equipment to Ukraine and other allies in Eastern Europe.\par \par \uc2 While the agreement paves the way for additional aid to Ukraine, the fate of billions of dollars in funding for coronavirus vaccines, testing and therapeutics remains uncertain.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 With the supreme court poised to end the constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Democrats are under increasing pressure to fulfill their promises to protect reproductive choice.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, they will hold a vote in the Senate on legislation that would codify the landmark supreme court decision Roe v Wade into federal law. But the bill is doomed to fail amid Republican opposition.\par \par \uc2 And when it does, Democrats are not planning to hold a vote to modify or end the Senate filibuster, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2022/05/10/democrats-arent-planning-vote-scrap-filibuster-abortion-bill/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the Washington Post.}}}\par \par \uc2 That is not particularly surprising or new.\par \par \uc2 For months, activists have been demanding Democrats amend or eliminate the filibuster, the parliamentary procedure requiring 60 votes to move forward with most legislation, to pass measures they believe are critical on voting rights, immigration and, now, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. But Democrats lack the votes to do so in the evenly divided Senate and the revelation that the supreme court intends to strike down Roe hasn\u8217\'20\'19t changed the calculus.\par \par \uc2 But that hasn\u8217\'20\'19t stopped some progressive Democrats from trying. According to the Post, a group of 114 House Democrats, led by Illinois congressman Sean Casten, California congresswomen Judy Chu and Barbara Lee, Missouri congresswoman \uc2 Cori Bush\uc2  and Colorado congresswoman \uc2 Diana DeGette\uc2 , sent a letter to Senate Majority Leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  demanding he hold a vote to scrap the filibuster.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen voters gave Democrats control of the House, Senate, and the White House, they did so with the expectation that we would legislate boldly and do what is necessary to advance our fight for justice and economic prosperity. Now more than ever it is the time to deliver on our promises,\u8221\'20\'1D the letter states. \u8220\'20\'1CThe Senate must meet the moment, end the filibuster, and pass the Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Protection Act (WHPA) immediately.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Schumer almost certainly won\u8217\'20\'19t hold such a vote. Two Democratic senators \u8211\'20\'13 \uc2 Kyrsten Sinema\uc2  of Arizona and Joe Manchin of West Virginia \u8211\'20\'13 publicly oppose such a move, leaving the party at least two votes shy of enacting the change.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 Good morning. It\u8217\'20\'19s another busy day in Washington DC, as the president and lawmakers on Capitol Hill scramble to respond to some of the most urgent issues of the day \u8211\'20\'13 rising inflation, the anticipated demise of Roe v Wade, the war in Ukraine and the pandemic.\par \par \uc2 From the White House, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will deliver remarks on the administration\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to combat inflation at 11.30am. He will attempt to draw a sharp contrast with what the White House is calling \u8220\'20\'1CCongressional Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 ultra-Maga plan to raise taxes on 75 million American families and threaten to sunset programs like Social Security, Medicare, and Medicaid\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Later in the day, the US president will hold a bilateral meeting with the Italian prime minister, \uc2 Mario Draghi\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2 , in her last week as press secretary, will brief reporters at 2.30pm ET.\par \par \uc2 Expect lots of wheeling and dealing on Capitol Hill, where Democrats and Republicans in both chambers are hoping to push through a massive aid bill for Ukraine. The swift action comes after Biden gave his blessing for decoupling the Ukraine aid from a Covid preparedness funding bill that Republicans oppose. This makes the road to passing any sort of Covid funding much more precarious.\par \par \uc2 At the same time, Democrats are preparing to hold a doomed vote on legislation that would codify the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  into federal law. A vote is expected tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 And it\u8217\'20\'19s another primary day. This Tuesday, it\u8217\'20\'19s West Virginia and Nebraska holding elections that offer another test of former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s influence within the Republican party.\par \par \uc2 Thanks for following along.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 2022-05-10T13:15:40Z 2022-05-10T22:14:49Z {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://media.guim.co.uk/92d33b18244fcfb7f348d99c3f1afd17f160ff88/0_130_7240_4347/500.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://media.guim.co.uk/92d33b18244fcfb7f348d99c3f1afd17f160ff88/0_130_7240_4347/500.jpg}}}\uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220510ei5a001us\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
