\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Pro-choice group claims arson attack on Wisconsin anti- \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  office\b0\par\par\uc2 Richard Luscombe \par \uc2 719 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 May 2022\par 20:31 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Madison police investigate attack on Wisconsin Family Action after claim by group calling itself Jane\u8217\'20\'19s revenge\par \par \uc2 Federal agents and detectives from the Madison police department are investigating a claim by a pro-choice group that it was behind a weekend arson attack on an anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  office in Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 The headquarters of Wisconsin Family Action in Madison was attacked in the early hours of Sunday, with a molotov cocktail thrown through a window, starting a small fire, and graffiti spray-painted on an exterior wall. Nobody was hurt.\par \par \uc2 In a statement reported on Tuesday {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://journalstar.com/news/national/group-claims-responsibility-for-attack-on-wisconsin-anti-abortion-organization-promises-more-violence/article_90f1677b-fa62-52e6-8a79-3b0c480dfdd7.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 by the Lincoln Journal Star}}}\uc2 , which said it was unable to verify the group\u8217\'20\'19s authenticity, Jane\u8217\'20\'19s Revenge said it launched the attack because of the organization\u8217\'20\'19s anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  stance, and demanded that similar institutions across the US disband or face \u8220\'20\'1Cincreasingly extreme tactics\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWisconsin is the first flashpoint, but we are all over the US, and we will issue no further warnings,\u8221\'20\'1D the statement said, citing the violence of anti-choice groups who \u8220\'20\'1Cbomb [\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ] clinics and assassinate doctors with impunity\u8221\'20\'1D as justification.\par \par \uc2 The Madison attack came days after the leaking of a supreme court draft ruling that would overturn its 1973 Roe v Wade decision and end almost half a century of constitutional \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, a spokesperson for the federal \uc2 Bureau of Alcohol, Tobacco, Firearms and Explosives\uc2  (ATF) told the Guardian that its agents were aware of the group\u8217\'20\'19s claims of responsibility, but cited the ongoing investigation for being unable to give more details.\par \par \uc2 The Madison police department said it was \u8220\'20\'1Caware of a group claiming responsibility for the arson at Wisconsin Family Action and are working with our federal partners to determine the veracity of that claim\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 It urged anyone with relevant information to make contact, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CWe take all information and tips related to this case seriously and are working to vet each and every one.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 At a press conference on Monday afternoon, the Madison PD and ATF agents announced a joint investigation into what it called an \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  extremism case involving an arson and graffiti attack of a pro-life advocacy office in Madison\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The Madison police chief, Shon Barnes, said no suspects had so far been identified. Authorities were expected to give a further update on Tuesday afternoon.\par \par \uc2 In a values statement on its website, Wisconsin Family Action (WFA) describes itself as a Judeo-Christian group dedicated to \u8220\'20\'1Cstrengthening, preserving, and promoting marriage, family, life and liberty.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe support the sanctity of human life from the moment of conception through natural death. This includes opposing legislation that promotes the destruction of human life \u8211\'20\'13 which starts at conception \u8211\'20\'13 through \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and other means,\u8221\'20\'1D it says.\par \par \uc2 Jack Hoogendyk, the WFA board chairman, attacked the response to the attack in a tweet posted on Tuesday morning, singling out Wisconsin\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic governor, \uc2 Tony Evers\uc2 , and Madison PD detectives.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe need to see a much stronger message of condemnation of this activity from our Governor [and] from local law enforcement,\u8221\'20\'1D he wrote.\par \par \uc2 At a press conference on Monday, Evers called the attack \u8220\'20\'1Ca horrible incident\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Calling for a full investigation and arrests, he added: \u8220\'20\'1CAs the state of Wisconsin, we don\u8217\'20\'19t accept that type of violence here.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 An attack on an anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  office is a relative rarity compared with attacks on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics and providers. In 2019, the Guardian reported on an \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2019/may/24/abortion-providers-disruption-intimidation-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 alarming escalation}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D in picketing, vandalism and trespassing by anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists at medical facilities.\par \par \uc2 Arson, bombings, murders and acid attacks were among more than 300 acts of extreme violence {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://users.nber.org/~jacobson/JacobsonRoyer6.2.10.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recorded by the Rand Corporation}}}\uc2  between 1973 and 2003, and in one of the most heinous incidents, in 2009, Dr George Tiller, a Kansas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global/2009/jul/29/george-tiller-abortion-doctor-shot"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was shot dead}}}\uc2  in a church in Wichita.\par \par \uc2 In March, MS magazine reported that the number of brick-and-mortar \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics nationwide had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://msmagazine.com/2022/03/09/independent-abortion-provider-clinic-roe/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dropped precipitously}}}\uc2 , partly because of the constant threat of violence against personnel. Six states, MS said, had only one \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider, mostly small, independent operators who were considered most at risk.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics have been closing at an alarming rate,\u8221\'20\'1D the article said. \u8220\'20\'1CIndependent providers are the most vulnerable to anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  attacks and violence directed at their staff.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220510ei5a0035y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
