\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Susan Collins\uc2  calls the cops over polite  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  message chalked outside home\b0\par\par\uc2 Gloria Oladipo \par \uc2 483 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 May 2022\par 18:21 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Intricately drawn\u8217\'20\'19 message urging Republican senator to back reproductive rights bill was not a crime, police in Maine say\par \par \uc2 A Republican US senator called local police to investigate a pro-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights \u8211\'20\'13 but otherwise harmless \u8211\'20\'13 message written in chalk in front of her home, according to authorities.\par \par \uc2 The Maine senator \uc2 Susan Collins\uc2  called officers last Saturday evening to complain about an anonymous message written in chalk on a sidewalk just outside her residence in Bangor that asked her to support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights legislation, according to a police report that was obtained by the Guardian.\par \par \uc2 The chalk art, described in the police report as \u8220\'20\'1Cintricately drawn\u8221\'20\'1D and non-threatening, read: \u8220\'20\'1CSusie, please, Mainers want WHPA \u8212\'20\'14\u8211\'20\'13> vote yes, clean up your mess.\u8221\'20\'1D WHPA refers to the Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Protection Act, which would codify \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 In the report, police wrote that they did not notice anything suspicious around Collins\u8217\'20\'19s residence. They also said that the chalk message did not constitute a crime.\par \par \uc2 A Bangor public works department employee later went to Collins\u8217\'20\'19s home to wash off the chalk message.\par \par \uc2 The senator provided a statement to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://bangordailynews.com/2022/05/09/news/bangor/pro-abortion-chalk-message-appears-on-susan-collins-bangor-sidewalk/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bangor Daily News}}}\uc2 , which first reported on the chalk message, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CWe are grateful to the Bangor police officers and the city public works employee who responded to the defacement of public property in front of our home.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 With last week\u8217\'20\'19s leak of a draft opinion showing that the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  is poised to overturn Roe v Wade, the 1973 landmark decision which legalized \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Collins has faced {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/mar/01/republicans-joe-manchin-us-senate-block-bill-abortion-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 criticism from voters for helping block the advancement of the WHPA to the Senate floor for debate in February}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Senate plans to again vote on potentially advancing the WHPA this Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Collins has signaled she plans to again oppose the WHPA, which would need 60 votes to advance, a threshold that most doubt the bill will clear. She, along with Senator Lisa Murkowski of Alaska, a fellow Republican, has introduced a different bill that would codify \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights while still allowing individual states to roll back protections.\par \par \uc2 Collins has also been criticized for backing the confirmation of the supreme court justices \uc2 Neil Gorsuch\uc2  and \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2 , who form part of the court\u8217\'20\'19s conservative majority that supports overturning Roe v Wade, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/02/roe-v-wade-abortion-supreme-court-draft-opinion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the leaked draft opinion}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 After the leak, Collins sought to distance herself from Gorsuch and Kavanaugh, issuing a statement decrying the two justices as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/congress/sen-collins-completely-inconsistent-gorsuch-kavanaugh-support-overturn-rcna27099"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 being \u8220\'20\'1Ccompletely inconsistent\u8221\'20\'1D }}}\uc2  with what they said during their confirmation hearings or in conversations with her.\par \par \uc2 Collins suggested both had indicated they would not support overturning Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf this leaked draft opinion is the final decision \u8230\'20\'26 it would be completely inconsistent with what Justice Gorsuch and Justice Kavanaugh said in their hearings and in our meetings in my office,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/congress/sen-collins-completely-inconsistent-gorsuch-kavanaugh-support-overturn-rcna27099"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Collins\u8217\'20\'19 statement said.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220510ei5a002s6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
