\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Senate Democrats aim to reveal which Republicans oppose  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ahead of midterms \u8211\'20\'13 live\b0\par\par\uc2 Richard Luscombe \par \uc2 6,005 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 May 2022\par 20:46 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 How GOP lawmakers are prepping to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as soon as possibleNew York expands \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, including for non-residentsBiden signs lend-lease law speeding up Ukraine aidGroups perpetuating Trump\u8217\'20\'19s 2020 election lie face scrutiny and lawsuitsSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s a wrap for our first US politics blog of the week.\par \par \uc2 The White House is slamming comments by Republican Senate minority leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  hinting at a nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, and attacking other Republicans pondering extreme legislation affecting women.\par \par \uc2 And \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has just signed a law speeding up US military aid to Ukraine, updating a second world war era act that allowed western allies to better stand up to Nazi Germany.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where else the day went:\par \par \uc2 * The \uc2 US Senate\uc2  is poised to advance a vote on enshrining into law \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. The move would set up a floor vote Wednesday that Democrats would lose, but use to win voters for November\u8217\'20\'19s midterm elections.\par \par \uc2 * Biden joined vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  in the White House Rose Garden to unveil a program that would make high-speed internet access free for millions of low-income Americans.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  says Republicans will take aim at basic human rights and \u8220\'20\'1Cdrag our nation back to a dark time\u8221\'20\'1D if the supreme court overturns \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections this summer.\par \par \uc2 * New York state\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general Letitia James announced a plan to significantly expand \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, including for non-residents, if the supreme court overturns the Roe v Wade ruling.\par \par \uc2 * The Biden administration said it would erase the Trump-era 25% tariff on Ukrainian steel imports, for an initial period of one year.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 White House 'exploring options' to protect women's rights\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration is exploring \u8220\'20\'1Ca range of considerations\u8221\'20\'1D to counter extreme Republican laws that might follow the overturning of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, the White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  has said.\par \par \uc2 In her afternoon media briefing, she also slammed comments by \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , the Republican Senate minority leader, that his party might consider a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.motherjones.com/politics/2022/05/congress-certainly-could-ban-abortion-nationwide-mcconnell-says/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nationwide \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban}}}\uc2 , and attacked Republicans in several states looking to introduce measures that she said would further restrict women\u8217\'20\'19s fundamental rights.\par \par \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  addresses reporters on Monday. Photograph: Nicholas Kamm/AFP/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 Psaki said she believed the US was \u8220\'20\'1Cat serious risk\u8221\'20\'1D of a Republican \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban:\par \par \uc2 Dozens of Republicans in Congress signed on to the Mississippi court case advocating for severe restrictions on a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to choose, and a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to make choices about her own body.\par \par \uc2 Just yesterday, the governor of Mississippi {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/09/mississippi-governor-contraception-abortion-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t say directly if they would go after the right to use contraception}}}\uc2 ... Louisiana legislators advanced a bill to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/05/louisiana-abortion-bill-murder-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 classify \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  as homicide}}}\uc2 , which would allow women who terminate their pregnancies to be charged with murder, and potentially criminalize in-vitro fertilization and forms of birth control.\par \par \uc2 So yes, you\u8217\'20\'19re seeing an outcry by the nearly two thirds of the public, many of them peacefully protesting, who are concerned about what this [supreme court] opinion will say.\par \par \uc2 But you\u8217\'20\'19re also seeing a number of Republicans in states, and some in Congress, double down on this potential to overturn a law that has been the law of the land for 50 years.\par \par \uc2 Asked what the Biden administration could do if some of the proposals came to fruition, Psaki said:\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s a range of considerations that are under way by our counsel\u8217\'20\'19s office [and] by the Department of Justice led by the gender policy council, to take every step we can to protect women\u8217\'20\'19s fundamental rights and protect rights beyond that.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden signs lend-lease law speeding up Ukraine aid\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has just appeared at a ceremony in the White House to sign the so-called {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/russia-ukraine-putin-immigration-zelenskyy-biden-311d1ef91f320ff262cd99a3e5454f8a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lend-lease act}}}\uc2  speeding up aid to Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 The bipartisan bill, passed 417-10 in the House last month, updates a 1941 law that allowed the US, before its own entrance into the second world war, to hasten military support for allies fighting the forces of Nazi Germany.\par \par \uc2 Biden said it would allow Ukraine to better defend itself against the Russian invasion ordered by its president \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Support for Ukraine is pivotal at this moment. Every day Ukrainians pay with their lives... the atrocities that the Russians are engaging in are just beyond the pale and the cost of the fight is not cheap.\par \par \uc2 But caving to aggression is even more costly. That\u8217\'20\'19s why we\u8217\'20\'19re staying in this.\par \par \uc2 Biden referenced yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s Victory in Europe (VE) Day, that marked the end of the war in Europe in 1945.\par \par \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2 , the White House press secretary, expanded on the theme in her afternoon press briefing:\par \par \uc2 This day is supposed to be about celebrating peace and unity in Europe and the defeat of Nazis in world war two. That is what is celebrated every year in Russia as well.\par \par \uc2 Instead, Putin is perverting history, attempting to change it I should say, to justify his unprovoked and unjustified war, which has brought catastrophic loss of life and immense human suffering.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re continuing to do what we can to provide support for Ukraine at this pivotal moment on security, economic and humanitarian assistance.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Discussion of gender identity or sexual preference is now banned in many of Florida\u8217\'20\'19s classrooms because of governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/11/republican-states-mimic-florida-dont-say-gay-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 don\u8217\'20\'19t say gay}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D bill.\par \par \uc2 But with one more stroke of the Republican governor\u8217\'20\'19s pen on Monday, another subject became compulsory: students must receive at least 45 minutes\u8217\'20\'19 instruction learning about the \u8220\'20\'1Cvictims of communism\u8221\'20\'1D every November.\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 . Photograph: Marta Lavandier/AP\par \par \uc2 In a ceremony at Miami\u8217\'20\'19s Freedom Tower, where scores of Cuban immigrants were admitted into the US, DeSantis signed House Bill 395, designating 7 November as Victims of Communism Day, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.miamiherald.com/news/politics-government/article261246872.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the Miami Herald}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The newspaper says the law makes Florida one of a handful of states to adopt the designation, but it is the first state to mandate school instruction on that day.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat body count of Mao is something that everybody needs to understand because it is a direct result of this communist ideology,\u8221\'20\'1D DeSantis said, according to the Herald, noting that tens of millions of people died in China under his rule.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI know we don\u8217\'20\'19t need legislation here to do this, but I think it\u8217\'20\'19s our responsibility to make sure people know about the atrocities committed by people like [former Cuban dictator] \uc2 Fidel Castro\uc2  and even more recently people like Nicolas Maduro [president of Venezuela].\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The instruction will begin in the 2023-2024 school year, DeSantis said, and require teaching of \uc2 Joseph Stalin\uc2 , \uc2 Mao Zedong\uc2  and \uc2 Fidel Castro\uc2 , as well as \u8220\'20\'1Cpoverty, starvation, migration, systemic lethal violence, and suppression of speech\u8221\'20\'1D endured under those regimes.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 Say what you like about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s supporters, you cannot fault them for commitment. When the former president arrived for his latest rally in a deeply rural corner of western Pennsylvania, many had already been standing in solid rain for 10 hours.\par \par \uc2 The field in which they were to greet their revered leader was a mud bath. By the time Trump finally arrived, 20 minutes late, the scene had taken on the qualities of the apocalypse \u8211\'20\'13 like the closing sequences of the Fyre festival.\par \par \uc2 On this occasion, the seemingly boundless patience of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s devoted followers was being put to the test for an additional reason. He had come to the Westmoreland Fairgrounds outside Greensburg to sprinkle Trump stardust on his preferred choice for the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-senate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US Senate}}}\uc2  seat vacated by retiring Republican senator \uc2 Pat Toomey\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A rain-soaked Mehmet Oz addresses the crowd in Greensburg, Pennsylvania. Photograph: Anadolu Agency/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 Whether Pennsylvanian conservatives go along with the endorsement when the primary is held on 17 May will have big consequences, not merely on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s record of advancing his chosen people \u8211\'20\'13 and with it his grip on the Republican party. It will also have ramifications for the November election which, in tune with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.270towin.com/states/Pennsylvania"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recent contests in the state}}}\uc2 , is almost certain to be nail-bitingly close and could be critical in determining whether the Republicans retake the Senate.\par \par \uc2 The trouble is, many Trump supporters don\u8217\'20\'19t know what to make of Mehmet Oz, the celebrity TV surgeon better known as Dr Oz.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe love Trump, but we\u8217\'20\'19ll be booing Oz,\u8221\'20\'1D said Pam, 46, a local educator who asked to give only her first name. She admitted one of the reasons she had turned up in the first place was to see how hostile her fellow Trump supporters would be towards the candidate.\par \par \uc2 In the end, after all that sodden waiting, Pam was disappointed. Occasional booing could be heard earlier in the evening whenever Oz was mentioned, but when the man himself took to the stage, whether by design or accident, the music was cranked up so loud that it was impossible to tell jeering from cheering.\par \par \uc2 Read the full story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/09/dr-oz-trump-pennsylvania-republican-senate-primary"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dr Oz embraced Trump\u8217\'20\'19s big lie \u8211\'20\'13 will Maga voters reward him in Senate race?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden reveals fast internet program for low-income Americans\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has been speaking at the White House to announce plans for free high-speed internet for millions of low-income Americans.\par \par \uc2 The US president is using the partnership with 20 tech companies to promote the success of his $1tn bipartisan infrastructure, more than $14bn has been used to provide $30 monthly subsidies to families for internet service.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  speaks at the White House, watched by vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . Photograph: Nicholas Kamm/AFP/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  was also present at the Rose Garden event at which Biden revealed details of the affordable connectivity program (\u8220\'20\'1CI refuse to call it the ACP. I am so tired of acronyms in Washington, I can\u8217\'20\'19t stand \u8216\'20\'18em,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said).\par \par \uc2 Under the new program, the providers have agreed to drop their monthly charge to $30 a month, effectively making high-speed internet free for 48m Americans, Biden said.\par \par \uc2 In the past, 30 bucks a month meant you had to settle for a slow internet service, unless you wanted to pay a heck of a lot more out of pocket.\par \par \uc2 We secured a commitment from 20 providers to lower prices for high speed for tens of millions of households. Families who are eligible can select a plan from a participating provider and receive high speed internet at no cost in most cases.\par \par \uc2 Biden said he understood the feelings of isolation that being disconnected from the outside world could bring, particularly during the Covid-19 pandemic:\par \par \uc2 Mental health problems are becoming a serious problem, feeling left out, feeling you can\u8217\'20\'19t participate, and not knowing what to do.\par \par \uc2 I know Vivek Murthy, the surgeon general, is going to talk about this in other contexts, but you know, I really think that just knowing that you belong, knowing and feeling that you can get access to what other people get on a regular basis, will make a big difference for people.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Interim summary\par \par \uc2 Where things stand halfway through our day:\par \par \uc2 * The \uc2 US Senate\uc2  is set to advance a vote on enshrining into law \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. The move would set up a floor vote Wednesday that Democrats would lose, but use to win voters for November\u8217\'20\'19s midterm elections.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is speaking at the White House about a program that would make high-speed internet access free for millions of low-income Americans.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  says Republicans will take aim at basic human rights and \u8220\'20\'1Cdrag our nation back to a dark time\u8221\'20\'1D if the supreme court overturns \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections this summer.\par \par \uc2 * New York state\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general Letitia James has announced a plan to significantly expand \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, including for non-residents, if the supreme court overturns the Roe v Wade ruling.\par \par \uc2 * The Biden administration says it will erase the Trump-era 25% tariff on Ukrainian steel imports, for an initial period of one year.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Brad Raffensperger\uc2 , Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s secretary of state best known for being asked by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/04/trumps-phone-call-to-brad-raffensperger-five-key-points"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cfind\u8221\'20\'1D enough votes}}}\uc2  to overturn the former president\u8217\'20\'19s 2020 defeat, has announced plans to solve a problem that doesn\u8217\'20\'19t exist: non-US citizens voting in elections.\par \par \uc2 Brad Raffensperger\uc2 . Photograph: Erik S Lesser/\uc2 EPA\par \par \uc2 Raffensperger has conducted a citizenship audit of the state\u8217\'20\'19s voter rolls, and will integrate citizenship checks into the voter registration process, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 He admits noncitizen voting is not a problem and that state law already bars those who aren\u8217\'20\'19t US citizens from voting. And while his audit flagged more than 1,600 potential noncitizens who tried to register over the last 25 years, none was successful.\par \par \uc2 But Raffensperger, who doubles as the state\u8217\'20\'19s chief elections officer, is making the issue a centerpiece of his effort to win over diehard conservatives ahead of what could be a difficult bid to clinch the Republican nomination for another four year term in office, the AP says.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI want to make sure that we follow the law, that we follow the constitution, and I want to make sure that only Americans can vote in our elections,\u8221\'20\'1D Raffensperger said.\par \par \uc2 His Trump-endorsed rival, Republican congressman \uc2 Jody Hice\uc2 , who objected to Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s electoral votes being counted for Biden, wasted no time in attacking Raffensperger.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNon-citizens voting in Georgia elections is already illegal,\u8221\'20\'1D he said in an emailed statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf Brad worked as hard at executing the responsibilities of secretary of state as he does at political posturing, I wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be challenging him.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Conservative groups perpetuating \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s false charges that the 2020 election was rigged have sparked a lawsuit against one in Colorado, and a congressional panel investigation of another in New Mexico, over aggressive tactics allegedly used to seek out possible voter fraud.\par \par \uc2 The scrutiny and criticism facing these conservative groups underscore how Trump loyalists in several US states are working to sustain falsehoods about Trump\u8217\'20\'19s loss, while launching new drives that voting rights advocates say smack of voter intimidation, often targeting communities of color.\par \par \uc2 A lawsuit was filed by the \uc2 NAACP\uc2  and two other groups in March charging that Colorado-based US Election Integrity Plan (USEIP), which has echoed Trump\u8217\'20\'19s baseless claims about 2020 election fraud, has gone door to door in some counties aggressively questioning residents about their voting status and sometimes bearing arms.\par \par \uc2 Moreover, the House Committee on Oversight and Reform has been investigating EchoMail, a firm that helped push false claims of election fraud in Arizona and has reportedly been paid $50,000 by a New Mexico county to oversee a local \u8220\'20\'1Caudit force\u8221\'20\'1D doing intrusive door-to-door voter canvassing.\par \par \uc2 enltr {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/NM?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #NM}}}\uc2  elections are some of the most secure in the U.S. with multi levels of canvassing & auditing & taxpayer $$ should never be spent selling the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/BigLie?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #BigLie}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Controversial Otero County Election Audit Canceled, Finds No Fraud" {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/vvxmTl9Ezz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/vvxmTl9Ezz}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/nmpol?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #nmpol}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/nmleg?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #nmleg}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 New Mexico Secretary of State (@NMSecOfState) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NMSecOfState/status/1522996168854175746?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 7, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Other states including Michigan and Utah boast conservative groups that, under the guise of protecting voting integrity by ferreting out fraud, have been criticized for the methods they employed in seeking out potential voter fraud.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs Americans, we expect and demand an open and participatory democracy that welcomes all voters equally,\u8221\'20\'1D said Danielle Lang, senior director of voting rights at the nonpartisan Campaign Legal Center. \u8220\'20\'1CThose engaging in these pressure tactics should know that voter intimidation is a crime with serious consequences.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit against USEIP filed by the \uc2 NAACP\uc2  in Colorado, the \uc2 League of Women Voters\uc2  in Colorado and Mi Familia Vota charges that USEIP has engaged in \u8220\'20\'1Cdoor-to-door voter intimidation\u8221\'20\'1D, including taking pictures of some houses, in neighborhoods with a large number of minority residents.\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit alleges, without providing specific cases, that USEIP representatives have at times worn badges or carried firearms when visiting voters\u8217\'20\'19 residences, although they are not government officials.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/09/conservative-groups-trump-election-lie-lawsuits-scrutiny"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Groups perpetuating Trump\u8217\'20\'19s 2020 election lie face scrutiny and lawsuits}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Following last Monday night\u8217\'20\'19s leak of a supreme court draft opinion that would overrule {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2 , the 1973 case that guaranteed the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Republican state lawmakers are working to make sure they are ready to limit access as soon as is legally permissible.\par \par \uc2 The language of the court\u8217\'20\'19s decision will probably change at least somewhat when it is ultimately issued by the end of June. But its central, top-line declaration \u8211\'20\'13 a 5-4 majority issuing a clear, unequivocal overturning of Roe \u8211\'20\'13 is widely expected to remain.\par \par \uc2 Here is what Republican state lawmakers across the country are doing in the lead-up to the decision to assure that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions will swiftly go into effect:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/09/republican-lawmakers-abortion-ban-roe-v-wade-trigger-laws"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 How GOP lawmakers are prepping to ban \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  as soon as legally possible}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 John Oliver delivered an impassioned episode of his HBO show after the \u8220\'20\'1Ccatastrophic\u8221\'20\'1D news that the supreme court is poised overturn the basic right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 On the latest episode of Last Week Tonight, the host said that \u8220\'20\'1Cwhile the fate of Roe might not have been a surprise, the draft itself was still a horror show\u8221\'20\'1D, referring to \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s leaked draft calling for the 1973 decision to be reversed.\par \par \uc2 Oliver said that \u8220\'20\'1Cwe need to be able to talk about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  like adults\u8221\'20\'1D, which means focusing on the \u8220\'20\'1Cimmediate and devastating consequences\u8221\'20\'1D this will have.\par \par \uc2 He referred to it as \u8220\'20\'1Ccatastrophic\u8221\'20\'1D as it will quickly trigger bans on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 22 states. He noted that approximately 25% of women have had an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and said this reversal is ultimately about \u8220\'20\'1Cbodily autonomy\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He played a clip from Fox News where a host said that people can just move to a different state if they want an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s not about merely having the right to go somewhere else, it\u8217\'20\'19s also about whether you have the resources and ability to do that and many may not,\u8221\'20\'1D Oliver said.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/2022/may/09/john-oliver-abortion-supreme-court-last-week-tonight-recap"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 John Oliver: \u8216\'20\'18Your basic rights could become crimes tomorrow\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Pelosi: 'Republicans will take aim at basic human rights'\par \par \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  has assailed Republicans in her weekly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.speaker.gov/newsroom/5922"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDear Colleague\u8221\'20\'1D letter}}}\uc2  to fellow Democrats, saying once Roe v Wade \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections are overturned, basic human rights will be next.\par \par \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 . Photograph: Ukrainian Presidential Press Service/Reuters\par \par \uc2 In the missive, the House speaker says it is \u8220\'20\'1Curgent and essential\u8221\'20\'1D that Democrats share with the American public the \u8220\'20\'1Cdangers of the Republican agenda\u8221\'20\'1D in the wake of the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s draft ruling ending almost half a century of constitutional \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections:\par \par \uc2 Republican state legislators across the country are already advancing extreme new laws, seeking to arrest doctors for offering reproductive care, ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  entirely with no exceptions, and even {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/05/louisiana-abortion-bill-murder-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 charge women with murder}}}\uc2  who exercise their right to choose.\par \par \uc2 These draconian measures could even criminalize contraceptive care, in vitro fertilization and post-miscarriage care, dragging our nation back to a dark time decades into the past.\par \par \uc2 Make no mistake: once Republicans have dispensed with precedent and privacy in overturning Roe, they will take aim at additional basic human rights. At this pivotal moment, the stakes for women - and every American \u8211\'20\'13 could not be higher.\par \par \uc2 enltrPelosi in Dear Colleague letter to House Dems says Republicans "want to punish & control women for exercising their constitutional rights".\par \par \uc2 "It is urgent and essential we remain disciplined and focused in sharing... the dangers of the Republican agenda." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/zQ0v2dNQtj"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/zQ0v2dNQtj}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Joan Greve (@joanegreve) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/joanegreve/status/1523698864254971904?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 Authorities in Wisconsin are investigating an arson attack on an anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  group\u8217\'20\'19s office in the early hours of Sunday, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 According to police in Madison, a Molotov cocktail thrown into the building at about 6am yesterday, starting a small fire at the Wisconsin Family Action office. Nobody was present and damage was minimal.\par \par \uc2 The words \u8220\'20\'1Cif abortions aren\u8217\'20\'19t safe then you aren\u8217\'20\'19t either\u8221\'20\'1D were spray-painted on the building\u8217\'20\'19s exterior, according to a statement from police chief, Shon Barnes.\par \par \uc2 Tony Evers\uc2 , the Democratic Wisconsin governor, condemned the attack in a meeting with reporters on Monday, calling it \u8220\'20\'1Chorrible\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is unacceptable. Violence does not solve the issues we\u8217\'20\'19re facing as a country,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 enltr"Our department has and continues to support people being able to speak freely and openly about their beliefs.\par \par \uc2 But we feel that any acts of violence, including the destruction of property, do not aid in any cause."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Madison Police (@madisonpolice) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/madisonpolice/status/1523407362425376768?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 8, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Republican governor of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/mississippi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mississippi}}}\uc2  has refused to rule out attempting to ban some forms of contraception if the supreme court ruling which guarantees the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should fall.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat is not what we\u8217\'20\'19re focused on at this time,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Tate Reeves\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 The ruling, Roe v Wade, seems likely to fall this summer, after the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/02/roe-v-wade-abortion-supreme-court-draft-opinion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 leak of a draft supreme court decision}}}\uc2  supported by five conservatives on the nine-member court.\par \par \uc2 The leak set off celebrations among conservatives and protests among liberals, as a near 50-year battle over a key privacy right approached a decisive moment.\par \par \uc2 Like {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/09/republican-lawmakers-abortion-ban-roe-v-wade-trigger-laws"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 other states}}}\uc2 , Mississippi has a \u8220\'20\'1Ctrigger law\u8221\'20\'1D which if Roe falls will outlaw almost all abortions, with exceptions in cases of rape or threat to the life of the mother. The case at issue in the draft ruling, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.oyez.org/cases/2021/19-1392"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organisation}}}\uc2 , originated in Mississippi.\par \par \uc2 Speaking on CNN on Sunday, Reeves confirmed that his state\u8217\'20\'19s trigger law would go into effect if Roe fell.\par \par \uc2 Reeves\u8217\'20\'19 host on CNN, Jake Tapper, then referred to neighbouring Louisiana, where Republicans have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/05/louisiana-abortion-bill-murder-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 advanced}}}\uc2  a bill to make \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  a crime of murder.\par \par \uc2 Tapper said: \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re talking about not only criminally charging girls and women who get abortions as committing homicide, but they\u8217\'20\'19re also talking about defining the moment of conception as fertilisation, which would theoretically \u8230\'20\'26 mean if you use an IUD [intrauterine device], you are committing murder.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\u8230\'20\'26 I\u8217\'20\'19m not making this up. These are the conversations going on in legislatures in your area. So, just to be clear, you have no intention of seeking to ban IUDs or Plan B [morning-after pills]?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Reeves said: \u8220\'20\'1CThat is not what we\u8217\'20\'19re focused on at this time.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re focused on looking at \u8211\'20\'13 see[ing] what the court allows for. The bill that is before the court is a 15-week [\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ] ban. We believe that the overturning of Roe is the correct decision by the court. And so, in Mississippi, we don\u8217\'20\'19t have laws on the books that would lead to arresting individuals or anything along those lines.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Asked if that meant he would arrest doctors who performed abortions, Reeves said: \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think that you\u8217\'20\'19re going to see doctors performing abortions if we have a state statute which says that they\u8217\'20\'19re not allowable, except for those exceptions that we have mentioned earlier.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/09/mississippi-governor-contraception-abortion-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mississippi governor refuses to rule out banning contraception}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden to lift Ukraine steel tariffs: report\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration is reversing Trump-era tariffs on Ukrainian steel for an initial period of one year, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/live/2022/05/09/world/ukraine-russia-war-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York Times is reporting}}}\uc2 , citing a document it says is a copy of an announcement coming from the White House later in the day.\par \par \uc2 Trump imposed a 25% tariff on foreign steel in 2018, the former president claiming at the time that cheap overseas metal was harming the US steel industry and posing a threat to national security.\par \par \uc2 The newspaper says that although Ukraine is only a minor provider, its 218,000 metric tons of steel to the US in 2019 ranking it 12th in overseas suppliers, the administration sees it as an important additional way to assist the country as it fights the Russian invasion.\par \par \uc2 The Ukraine prime minister Denys Shmyhal, in a visit to Washington DC last month, told administration officials that some Ukrainian steel mills were starting to produce again after initially shutting down because of the invasion.\par \par \uc2 The Times said Shmyhal asked the Biden administration to suspend the tariffs, citing a senior commerce department official, who was not authorized to speak publicly before the official announcement.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 New York expands \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, including for non-residents\par \par \uc2 New York\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general Letitia James has just given a press briefing at which she announced a program to expand \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access to residents, and those from states where the procedure will become illegal if Roe v Wade is overturned:\par \par \uc2 We know what happens when women are unable to control their own bodies and make their own choices and we will not go back to those dark times.\par \par \uc2 New York must lead the fight to keep \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  safe and accessible for all who seek it.\par \par \uc2 According to an accompanying {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ag.ny.gov/press-release/2022/attorney-general-james-takes-action-expand-abortion-access"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement released by James\u8217\'20\'19s office}}}\uc2 , clinics in New York already perform at least 7,000 abortions a year for women from out of state, 9% of its annual total.\par \par \uc2 enltrNew York must lead the fight to protect the fundamental right to choose.\par \par \uc2 Today, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenatorCCleare?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @SenatorCCleare}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/votejgr?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @votejgr}}}\uc2 , and I are announcing legislation to create a new program that will expand \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access for New Yorkers and people living in other states that ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/0jAmr8iS1p"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/0jAmr8iS1p}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 NY AG James (@NewYorkStateAG) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NewYorkStateAG/status/1523668904769634305?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 If the supreme court ends almost half a century of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections, as last week\u8217\'20\'19s leaking of its draft ruling suggested it was about to do, New York expects a massive surge from states with \u8220\'20\'1Ctrigger laws\u8221\'20\'1D that would immediately make the procedure illegal.\par \par \uc2 From Ohio and Pennsylvania alone, the statement predicts, an additional 32,000 women will come to New York each year seeking an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The measure announced by James includes a reproductive freedom and equity program within the New York state department of health \u8220\'20\'1Cthat would provide funding to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers and non-profit organizations to grow the capacity of providers and meet present and future care needs\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 The White House is previewing \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s lunchtime appearance in the Rose Garden, at which he will announce that 20 internet companies have agreed to provide discounted service to people with low incomes.\par \par \uc2 More than $14bn from the $1tn bipartisan infrastructure package passed last year went towards $30 a month subsidies for lower income families to pay for internet service.\par \par \uc2 The internet providers have agreed to drop their prices to match the subsidy, Biden will announce today, the Associated Press reports, making about 48m households will be eligible for fully paid for $30 monthly plans for 100 megabits per second, or higher speed.\par \par \uc2 According to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2022/05/09/fact-sheet-president-biden-and-vice-president-harris-reduce-high-speed-internet-costs-for-millions-of-americans/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 White House fact sheet}}}\uc2  posted Monday, Biden will say:\par \par \uc2 High-speed internet service is no longer a luxury - it\u8217\'20\'19s a necessity. But too many families go without high-speed internet because of the cost or have to cut back on other essentials to make their monthly internet service payments.\par \par \uc2 The 20 companies that have agreed to lower rates provide service in areas where 80% of the US population, including 50% of the rural population, live, according to the White House.\par \par \uc2 Participating companies that offer service on tribal lands are providing $75 rates in those areas, the equivalent of the federal government subsidy in those areas.\par \par \uc2 Biden and vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will meet telecoms executives and members of Congress before the Rose Garden announcement, according to the AP.\par \par \uc2 enltrStarting today, the cost of internet is fully covered for millions of eligible American families under a new Biden-Harris Administration initiative. Learn if you are eligible and how you can apply at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/rYeK5u6Ho7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/rYeK5u6Ho7}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The White House (@WhiteHouse) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/WhiteHouse/status/1523636760336637952?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Members on the House select committee investigating the Capitol attack on 6 January are moving closer to issuing subpoenas to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican members of Congress}}}\uc2  to compel their cooperation in the inquiry \u8211\'20\'13 though it has started to dawn on them that they may be out of time.\par \par \uc2 The panel is expected to make a final decision on the subpoena question over the next couple of weeks, according to sources directly familiar with internal deliberations, with House investigators needing to start wrapping up their work ahead of public hearings in June.\par \par \uc2 While the members on the select committee remain undecided about whether to subpoena Republican members of Congress, their refusal to assist the investigation in any form has caused the sentiment to turn towards taking that near-unprecedented action, the sources said.\par \par \uc2 The shifting view has come as a result of the dismay among the members in January, when House minority leader Kevin McCarthy and others turned down requests for voluntary cooperation, turning to anger after three more of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s allies {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/02/capitol-attack-republicans-mo-brooks-andy-biggs-ronny-jackson"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 last week refused to cooperate}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 What has changed in recent weeks in the select committee\u8217\'20\'19s assessment is that they cannot ignore the deep involvement between some Republican members of Congress and the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 former president\u8217\'20\'19s}}}\uc2  unlawful schemes to overturn the results of the 2020 election, the sources said.\par \par \uc2 The recent letters to House {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2  Mo Brooks, Andy Biggs and \uc2 Ronny Jackson\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former White House doctor \u8211\'20\'13 provided just a snapshot of the entanglement, the sources said, with the Trump White House, and potentially the militia groups that attacked the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 House investigators are particularly interested in any potential connections between Republican members of Congress and the Oath Keepers and Proud Boys militia groups, the sources said, since those groups were actually involved in the riot element of January 6.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/09/capitol-attack-panel-subpoenas-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Capitol attack panel moves closer to issuing subpoenas to Republicans }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 New York Democratic Senator Kirsten Gillibrand has emerged as one of her party\u8217\'20\'19s leading voices for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. She tore into the supreme court at a press conference at the Capitol last week, her fury evident during a three-minute tirade in which she framed the issue as a \u8220\'20\'1Clife or death\u8221\'20\'1D battle.\par \par \uc2 Kirsten Gillibrand. Photograph: Jacquelyn Martin/AP\par \par \uc2 On Sunday, she followed up with an appearance on CNN\u8217\'20\'19s State of the Union in which she called it the \u8220\'20\'1Cbiggest fight of a generation\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Gillibrand urged her party to stand up to Republicans seeking to abolish the constitutional right, and called the draft \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  opinion {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/03/biden-democrats-reaction-codifying-roe-v-wade-reform-scotus"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 leaked last week}}}\uc2 , revealing a conservative-leaning super-majority supports overturning the landmark 1973 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/dec/05/abortion-opposition-focus-white-evangelical-anger"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade decision}}}\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1Cbone-chilling\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 She told CNN:\par \par \uc2 This is the biggest fight of a generation \u8230\'20\'26 and if America\u8217\'20\'19s women and the men who love them do not fight right now, we will lose the basic right to make decisions, to have bodily autonomy and to decide what our futures look like.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Maya Yang on Gillibrand\u8217\'20\'19s call to action:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/08/kirsten-gillibrand-democrat-abortion-rights-fight-of-generation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gillibrand calls \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights \u8216\'20\'18fight of generation\u8217\'20\'19 after \u8216\'20\'18bone-chilling\u8217\'20\'19 court draft opinion}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrI\u8217\'20\'19ve been saying it, and I\u8217\'20\'19ll keep saying it. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Qz49t2Dl8i"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/Qz49t2Dl8i}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sen. Kirsten Gillibrand (@gillibrandny) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/gillibrandny/status/1522299038430900225?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 5, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Schumer seeks to capitalize on voters' fury over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US Senate\uc2  will today channel a week of anger, acrimony and fractious debate over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights into the formal step of setting up a vote to enshrine a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to the procedure into law.\par \par \uc2 By filing for cloture (the official term for cutting off debate), senators will move towards a floor vote Wednesday on legislation proposed by the Connecticut Democrat Richard Blumenthal. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights defenders have been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/05/democrats-voters-senate-midterm-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 demanding action}}}\uc2  ever since the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s draft ruling overturning the 1973 Roe v Wade opinion {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/03/biden-democrats-reaction-codifying-roe-v-wade-reform-scotus"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was leaked last week}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Democrats know the legislation is doomed to fall, because it won\u8217\'20\'19t reach the 60 votes it needs in the bitterly divided chamber.\par \par \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights activists in New York on Sunday. Photograph: Ron Adar/SOPA Images/REX/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 But Senate majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  will not consider it an outright failure. He\u8217\'20\'19s playing a longer game, in which he sees Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 refusal to support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights working in Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 favor in November\u8217\'20\'19s midterms. After all, polls show overwhelming support nationally among voters for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEvery American will see how every senator stands,\u8221\'20\'1D Schumer said at a press conference Sunday in which he called the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s draft ruling \u8220\'20\'1Can abomination\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 With Democrats predicted to lose control of one or both chambers of Congress in November, some see the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  debate coming at a fortuitous time. Comments by \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , the Republican senate minority leader, as reported by The Hill, that a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/news/senate/3480725-mcconnell-says-national-abortion-ban-possible/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 national \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban \u8220\'20\'1Cis possible\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 , will only serve to strengthen pro-choice activists\u8217\'20\'19 outrage.\par \par \uc2 This \uc2 Bloomberg\uc2  article examines how the Democratic party is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2022-05-08/biden-taps-democrats-abortion-fury-with-midterm-wipeout-looming?srnd=premium"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tapping into voters\u8217\'20\'19 fury over \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  to avoid a midterms blowout.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll keep you abreast of today\u8217\'20\'19s developments as they happen.\par \par \uc2 While we wait, here\u8217\'20\'19s a look at how Republicans in numerous states are moving in the opposite direction, and towards even more restrictive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legislation.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/09/republican-lawmakers-abortion-ban-roe-v-wade-trigger-laws"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 How GOP lawmakers are prepping to ban \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  as soon as legally possible}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Good morning, happy Monday, and welcome to the blog! It\u8217\'20\'19s a brand new week in US politics, but some familiar themes are playing out.\par \par \uc2 The Senate will invoke cloture (that\u8217\'20\'19s the official term for cutting off debate) today to set up a vote Wednesday on legislation to codify a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , following last week\u8217\'20\'19s bombshell supreme court draft ruling ending almost half a century of constitutional protections for the procedure.\par \par \uc2 The vote will fail, because it won\u8217\'20\'19t reach the required 60 votes. But that\u8217\'20\'19s not the point. The Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 strategy is to force Republicans to vote to defeat it, thus showing where every senator stands on the issue and providing a stick to beat them with for the midterm elections later this year. Polls show overwhelming support nationally among voters for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 What else we\u8217\'20\'19re watching today:\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and the vice-president, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , will speak from the White House at lunchtime about expanding high speed internet access. We\u8217\'20\'19ll see if they take questions about the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  debate.\par \par \uc2 * The House panel investigating the 6 January insurrection is closer to issuing subpoenas for senior Republicans, but beginning to realize it\u8217\'20\'19s running short on time.\par \par \uc2 * The House itself is not in session, but the Biden administration is keeping up pressure on lawmakers to pass requests for Covid-19 funding and $33bn in aid for Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 * White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  delivers her first briefing of the week at 3pm.\par \par \uc2 And a reminder that we\u8217\'20\'19re covering all the developments in the Ukraine conflict in our {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/may/09/russia-ukraine-war-latest-russia-to-mark-victory-day-uk-defence-secretary-to-accuse-putin-of-mirroring-fascism-live"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 live 24-hour blog here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220509ei59001s4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
