\par\par \uc2 Global development\par \b \uc2 Erosion of  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights gathers pace around the world as US signals new era\b0\par\par\uc2 Weronika Strzyzynska \par \uc2 828 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 May 2022\par 10:20 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 A leaked supreme court draft ruling shows the US is set to end 50 years of a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to choose. Elsewhere, the battle still rages\par \par \uc2 In 2022, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains one of the most controversial and bitterly contested ethical and political battlegrounds. It is illegal for women to terminate their pregnancies in any circumstance in 24 countries, with a further 37 restricting access in any case except when the mother\u8217\'20\'19s life is in danger.\par \par \uc2 As a leaked document signals that the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  is poised to strike down the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/02/roe-v-wade-abortion-supreme-court-draft-opinion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 landmark 1973 ruling in Roe v Wade}}}\uc2 , millions of American women face losing their access to legal abortions, joining millions more living in those countries rejecting a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to choose.\par \par \uc2 According to data from the \uc2 World Health Organization (WHO)\uc2 , unsafe abortions kill more than 47,000 people every year, with five million hospitalised for complications such as bleeding or infection.\par \par \uc2 WHO data also shows that banning abortions has little or no effect on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://worldpopulationreview.com/country-rankings/abortion-rates-by-country"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rates}}}\uc2  throughout the world.\par \par \uc2 Latin America\par \par \uc2 Latin America has some of the world\u8217\'20\'19s most extreme anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is illegal under any circumstances in El Salvador, Nicaragua and Honduras. Since 1998, at least 140 women in El Salvador, where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is punishable with up to 35 years imprisonment, have been charged under anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws. Many of them had suffered a miscarriage.\par \par \uc2 In Brazil, under the far-right president Jair Bolsonaro, access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 only legal in the country on the grounds of rape, severe foetal defects and women\u8217\'20\'19s health \u8211\'20\'13 has been curtailed. In 2020, the country {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hrw.org/world-report/2021/country-chapters/brazil"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 introduced new legislation}}}\uc2  that requires medical staff to inform the police of rape survivors seeking the procedure.\par \par \uc2 However, other countries on the continent have broadened access to legal abortions. In February, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2022/feb/22/colombia-legalises-abortion-in-move-celebrated-as-historic-victory-by-campaigners"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Colombia decriminalised \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 , while Chile signalled that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/world/americas/chile-abortion-debate-gets-key-place-constitution-redraft-2022-03-16/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wider access to abortions}}}\uc2  may be enshrined in its new constitution.\par \par \uc2 In 2020, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2020/dec/30/argentina-legalises-abortion-in-landmark-moment-for-womens-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Argentina legalised \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  on request in the first 14 weeks of pregnancy. Uruguay passed similar legislation, allowing abortions up to the 12th week of pregnancy, in 2012.\par \par \uc2 Africa\par \par \uc2 Africa has the highest death rate related to unsafe abortions, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/report/from-unsafe-to-safe-abortion-in-subsaharan-africa-executive-summary"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the Guttmacher Institute}}}\uc2 , with 92% of women of reproductive age in the region having restricted access to legal terminations. The Center for Reproductive Rights estimates that the deaths of up to 15,000 women a year could be prevented by improving access to safe abortions across the continent.\par \par \uc2 In several countries, including Egypt, Democratic Republic of Congo and Senegal, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is completely illegal. According to the Association of Senegalese Women Lawyers, 19% of female prisoners in Senegal in 2015 were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.safeabortionwomensright.org/news/senegal-access-to-safe-abortion-in-cases-of-rape-and-incest-has-become-an-urgent-and-absolute-necessity-a-statement-on-behalf-of-the-task-force-for-legal-access-to-safe-abortion-in-senegal-associa/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 incarcerated on the grounds of \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  or infanticide.}}}\par \par \uc2 However, the number of African countries that allow \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  on request is growing. In 2021, Benin became the seventh country in the continent to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/world/africa/benin-parliament-votes-legalise-abortion-2021-10-21/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 legalise the procedure in the first trimester}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Europe\par \par \uc2 Nearly all European countries offer legal abortions, yet it remains completely illegal in three microstates: Andorra, Malta and Vatican City. However, convictions in these countries remain rare.\par \par \uc2 Poland is the only country where access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is highly restricted. After {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/jan/27/poland-to-implement-near-total-ban-on-abortion-imminently"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  a legislative ban was introduced in 2021,}}}\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  can only be carried out when the pregnancy was caused by an illegal act, such as rape or incest, or when it threatens a woman\u8217\'20\'19s health. In reality, though, it is difficult to secure a legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the grounds of rape, with fewer than five legal abortions a year carried out for this reason. Even when a woman\u8217\'20\'19s health is at risk, doctors have become reluctant to carry out an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , leading to several deaths.\par \par \uc2 In December, Poland also announced it is planning to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2021/dec/03/poland-plans-to-set-up-register-of-pregnancies-to-report-miscarriages"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 introduce a centralised register of pregnancies }}}\uc2  that would oblige doctors to report all pregnancies and miscarriages to the government.\par \par \uc2 In Romania, women are finding it increasingly difficult to access their legal right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with doctors refusing to provide the service. A 2019 survey found that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://centrulfilia.ro/avortul-un-drept-legiferat-dar-greu-de-accesat-in-romania-anului-2019/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 only 25% of hospitals}}}\uc2  offered to carry out the procedure on request.\par \par \uc2 Asia\par \par \uc2 According to the WHO, more than half of all {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.who.int/news-room/fact-sheets/detail/abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unsafe abortions occur in Asia}}}\uc2 , most of them in south and central Asia. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains completely illegal in Laos and the Philippines.\par \par \uc2 The Philippines\u8217\'20\'19 ban is still based on colonial-era laws introduced by the Spanish in 1870. An additional law passed in 1987 obliges the government to place equal weight on protecting the \u8220\'20\'1Clife of the unborn from conception\u8221\'20\'1D as on the life of the mother. Reproductive services are also severely curtailed, with emergency contraception, also known as the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/womens-blog/2016/nov/30/the-morning-after-pill-is-safe-so-why-is-it-so-difficult-to-access"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 morning-after pill}}}\uc2 , banned across the country.\par \par \uc2 A woman who has an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the Philippines risks up to six years in prison. While there is no collected data on how many are convicted on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related offences, reports of such cases in local media are not rare.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220509ei59002mo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
