\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Canada and Mexico prepare to accept Americans seeking abortions\b0\par\par\uc2 Hilary Beaumont \par \uc2 871 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 May 2022\par 15:17 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 30\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 If the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  does vote to overthrow Roe v Wade, many Americans in need of surgical abortions could be forced to travel to Canada or Mexico\par \par \uc2 Carolyn Egan has seen people cross the Canada-US border for abortions \u8211\'20\'13 going north to south.\par \par \uc2 In the years before Canada\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court legalised \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 1988, it was common for Canadians who needed abortions to travel to the US. \u8220\'20\'1CWe had a network of people who could make referrals and help them get there [to the US]. If it\u8217\'20\'19s necessary, that probably would happen again \u8211\'20\'13 but the other way,\u8221\'20\'1D said Egan, spokesperson for the \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Rights Coalition of Canada.\par \par \uc2 If, as a leaked draft decision indicates, the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  votes to overturn Roe v Wade, many Americans in need of surgical \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be forced to travel not just across state lines but, once again, across international borders \u8211\'20\'13 both along the northern border to Canada and the southern one to Mexico.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, Canada\u8217\'20\'19s minister of families, \uc2 Karina Gould\uc2 , reaffirmed that Americans can access \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services in Canada. \u8220\'20\'1CIf they, people, come here and need access, certainly, you know, that\u8217\'20\'19s a service that would be provided,\u8221\'20\'1D she told {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbc.ca/news/politics/canada-provide-abortion-access-american-women-1.6440238"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CBC News}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 An estimated {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/news-release/2021/if-roe-v-wade-overturned-new-interactive-map-shows-how-far-people-seeking-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 26 states}}}\uc2  are likely to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  if Roe v Wade is overturned, according to the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 , an American sexual and reproductive health rights research organization. That includes Michigan, which sits across the water from southern Ontario, where there are plenty of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics. \u8220\'20\'1CIf a state like Michigan banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , certainly there would be interest in coming across the border,\u8221\'20\'1D Egan said.\par \par \uc2 Michigan has a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.freep.com/story/news/politics/2022/05/03/roe-v-wade-overturned-decision-supreme-court-abortion-michigan/9626072002/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 1931 ban}}}\uc2  that could automatically kick in when Roe v Wade ends. Michigan residents could also travel to Illinois or Pennsylvania, as those states are unlikely to outlaw the procedure, according to Guttmacher data, and many Americans would be expected to travel internally between states.\par \par \uc2 Those travelling internationally won\u8217\'20\'19t find it free \u8211\'20\'13 people without immigration status in Canada are charged about C$500 (US$388) for a surgical \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Egan said \u8211\'20\'13 but Americans do not need a health card to access clinics in Canada. Wait times vary, from one to two weeks in Ontario to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theglobeandmail.com/opinion/article-i-wanted-an-abortion-in-nova-scotia-but-all-around-barriers-still/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 several weeks or months}}}\uc2  in the Atlantic provinces.\par \par \uc2 Crossing the border will probably only be possible for those who can afford to do. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  advocates in the US have underscored that after Roe v Wade falls it will be wealthier white women who have the means \u8211\'20\'13 including travelling \u8211\'20\'13 to access \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while people on lower incomes and those who face socioeconomic barriers including African American, Latino and Indigenous women and transgender people may struggle more.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou have to have the financial resources\u8221\'20\'1D to travel between states or internationally, Meghan Doherty, director of global policy and advocacy at Action Canada for Sexual Health and Rights, said. \u8220\'20\'1CThere will be a limited number of people who will be able to do that.\u8221\'20\'1D She added that not everyone has dependable childcare, the ability to take time off work or a valid passport.\par \par \uc2 The cheapest option early in pregnancy will probably continue to be \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills, obtainable either through the mail or via telehealth services.\par \par \uc2 But after working for more than 10 years at clinics in Ireland while \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was illegal, Doherty says she has no doubt that people will cross borders. \u8220\'20\'1COver 5,000 women a year travelled to the UK, so we know that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions don\u8217\'20\'19t stop women from accessing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 it just places more burden on them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 South of the US border, Mexican advocates are preparing for an increase in Americans visiting to access \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services. In 2021, Mexico\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court ruled it was unconstitutional to criminalise \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , although access still varies by state.\par \par \uc2 The advocacy group Las Libres is part of a network that helps people on both sides of the border access \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills. Vero Cruz, advocacy coordinator with Las Libres, said Americans can technically obtain surgical abortions in public clinics in certain Mexican states for free, though she doesn\u8217\'20\'19t know of anyone who has done so yet. Cruz said surgical abortions were available in Sinaloa, Coahuila and Baja California, but only up to 12 weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe women who are crossing into Mexico are coming to Monterrey, Tijuana and other cities to have abortions using medication,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. The \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills are free, too. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s completely free, it costs nothing.\u8221\'20\'1D She said both private and public clinics in border cities in Mexico were planning for an American influx; both Tijuana and Coahuila recently set up services, she said.\par \par \uc2 Egan said Americans in Canada will be warmly received, too. \u8220\'20\'1CFor a cabinet minister to say that Americans would be welcome here, gives the sense that the government is considering the possibility, and making it clear they would not be interfering in that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Many Canadians are upset about the looming end of Roe v Wade, she said. \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s tremendous upset, distress and anger that Americans would be in the situation of having to face this kind of thing. So my sense is people will do everything they can to make access easier.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220509ei59000ur\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
