\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Gillibrand calls  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights \u8216\'20\'18fight of generation\u8217\'20\'19 after \u8216\'20\'18bone-chilling\u8217\'20\'19 court draft opinion\b0\par\par\uc2 Maya Yang \par \uc2 1,061 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 May 2022\par 14:59 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 New York Democrat urges her party to stand up to concerted efforts from Republicans seeking to abolish constitutional right\par \par \uc2 Senator Kirsten Gillibrand on Sunday called the battle over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the US the \u8220\'20\'1Cbiggest fight of a generation\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The New York Democrat urged her party to stand up to Republicans seeking to abolish the constitutional right, and called the draft \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  opinion {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/03/biden-democrats-reaction-codifying-roe-v-wade-reform-scotus"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 leaked last week}}}\uc2 , revealing a conservative-leaning super-majority supports overturning the landmark 1973 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/dec/05/abortion-opposition-focus-white-evangelical-anger"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade decision}}}\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1Cbone-chilling\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 She told CNN\u8217\'20\'19s State of the Union Sunday politics talkshow: \u8220\'20\'1CThis is the biggest fight of a generation \u8230\'20\'26 and if America\u8217\'20\'19s women and the men who love them do not fight right now, we will lose the basic right to make decisions, to have bodily autonomy and to decide what our futures look like.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Mississippi\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor, \uc2 Tate Reeves\uc2 , praised the draft ruling, which emerged last Monday evening and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/03/us-supreme-court-abortion-protesters-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 immediately sparked}}}\uc2  protests outside the supreme court in Washington DC, with more {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/03/roe-v-wade-protests-outside-us-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the next day}}}\uc2  and huge demonstrations planned across the US.\par \par \uc2 His state {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/nov/30/explainer-mississippi-abortion-rights-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has the pivotal case}}}\uc2  currently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/dec/01/oral-arguments-mississippi-abortion-case-begin-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 before the court}}}\uc2  that includes the option not just to severely restrict the procedure further but specifically to overturn the Roe v Wade opinion that made \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  a federal right, which was reaffirmed by the supreme court in 1992.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhile this is a great victory for the pro-life movement, it is not the end. In fact, it\u8217\'20\'19s just the beginning,\u8221\'20\'1D Reeves said of the draft opinion. Mississippi {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/nov/30/explainer-mississippi-abortion-rights-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hopes to ban}}}\uc2  almost all \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a state that normally carries out around 3,500 such procedures a year.\par \par \uc2 He talked of providing more education for women, to help them get better jobs to support children.\par \par \uc2 Gillibrand called Reeves \u8220\'20\'1Cpaternalistic\u8221\'20\'1D and his and the court\u8217\'20\'19s stance outrageous.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s taking away women\u8217\'20\'19s right for life, liberty and the pursuit of happiness, our right to be a full citizen,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, adding that women are \u8220\'20\'1Chalf-citizens under this ruling and if this is put into law, it changes the foundation of America\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Reeves said Mississippi plans to improve adoption processes and foster care systems and provide more resources for those expecting. However the state has a poor {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2021/dec/16/mississippi-miserly-healthcare-system"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 record on healthcare}}}\uc2  for low-income women, particularly women of color, in a nation frequently called out for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2019/nov/25/african-american-doula-collective-mothers-toxic-stress-racism-cleveland-infant-mortality-childbirth"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 high infant mortality}}}\uc2  rates and poor antenatal health.\par \par \uc2 CNN host Jake Tapper {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/justinbaragona/status/1523291020821159937"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 noted that Mississippi}}}\uc2  has the highest rate of child mortality in the US, the highest rate of child poverty, no guaranteed paid {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/jan/27/maternity-leave-us-policy-worst-worlds-richest-countries"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 maternity leave}}}\uc2  and that the legislature in Mississippi \u8220\'20\'1Cjust rejected extending postpartum Medicaid coverage\u8221\'20\'1D, referring to government health insurance for low-income populations. Tapper also pointed out that Mississippi\u8217\'20\'19s foster care system is the subject of a long-running federal lawsuit over its failure to protect children from abuse.\par \par \uc2 Reeves said: \u8220\'20\'1CI was elected not to try to hide our problems but to try to fix our problems.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Jake Tapper to Mississippi Gov. \uc2 Tate Reeves\uc2 : You say you want to do more to support mothers and children, but you\u8217\'20\'19ve been in state government since 2004... Based on the track record of the state of Mississippi, why should any of these girls or moms believe you?" {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/VLuA6gcS1F"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/VLuA6gcS1F}}}\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 Justin Baragona (@justinbaragona) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/justinbaragona/status/1523291020821159937?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 8, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Gillibrand said she was offended by Reeves\u8217\'20\'19s remarks, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CI thought he was quite paternalistic towards women. He doesn\u8217\'20\'19t look at women as full citizens.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Senate majority leader, \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , a fellow New York Democrat, said on Sunday that a piece of legislation that has been stalled in Congress would be put to the vote by the Senate again, on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Protection Act, which enshrines the rights afforded by Roe into federal legislation, rather than relying on court decisions, has passed the House of Representatives but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/mar/01/republicans-joe-manchin-us-senate-block-bill-abortion-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was struck down}}}\uc2  in the Senate in March, with one Democrat joining Republicans in opposing it.\par \par \uc2 The final supreme court decision on Roe is due in June.\par \par \uc2 Overturning Roe and instead letting each state set its own law on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  would leave entire regions of the country without an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic within a day\u8217\'20\'19s drive, reshaping the geography of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in America in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/05/abortion-deserts-clinics-access-closed-map"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 single seismic shift}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Minnesota Democratic senator Amy Klobuchar told ABC\u8217\'20\'19s This Week host Martha Raddatz that there were Democrats in Congress and Democratic candidates who do not support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 But she said: \u8220\'20\'1CYou have people who are personally pro-life but believe that that decision should be a woman\u8217\'20\'19s personal choice, even if they might not agree with them. We have people in our party who vote to uphold Roe v Wade who might have different personal opinions, that\u8217\'20\'19s a really important distinction.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn the wake of the leaked draft, activists on both sides of the debate immediately began mobilizing for a drastic shift in America\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MarthaRaddatz?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @MarthaRaddatz}}}\uc2  sits down with the leaders of two advocacy groups: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ECy1oebCRT"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/ECy1oebCRT}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/fU8IVPgdlf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/fU8IVPgdlf}}}\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 This Week (@ThisWeekABC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ThisWeekABC/status/1523300247304548353?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 8, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 She accused the supreme court, which achieved a right-leaning {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/oct/26/amy-coney-barrett-confirmed-supreme-court-justice-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 controlling majority}}}\uc2  after Donald {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2018/oct/06/brett-kavanaugh-confirmed-us-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump nominated}}}\uc2  three justices \u8211\'20\'13 now having six conservatives and only three liberal-leaning judges on the nine-member bench, of wanting to take America back into ancient history.\par \par \uc2 The draft opinion was written by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2022/may/06/samuel-alito-profile-abortion-supreme-court-justice"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 conservative justice Samuel Alito}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe court is looking at reversing 50 years of women\u8217\'20\'19s rights, and the fall will be swift. Over 20 states have laws [to ban] in place already. Who should make this decision, should it be a woman and her doctor, or a politician? Should it be [conservative Republican Senator] Ted Cruz \u8230\'20\'26 or a woman and her family? Justice Alito is literally not just taking us back to the 1950s, he\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2022/may/06/samuel-alito-profile-abortion-supreme-court-justice"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 taking us back}}}\uc2  to the 1850s,\u8221\'20\'1D Klobuchar said.\par \par \uc2 Pro-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights groups Naral Pro-Choice America, Planned Parenthood and Emily\u8217\'20\'19s List plan between the three of them to put more than $150m into campaigns to support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights advocates as political candidates in elections this year.\par \par \uc2 Mini Timmaraju, president of NARAL, told ABC: \u8220\'20\'1CAs a movement, this has been probably the most devastating year since pre-1973.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220508ei5800209\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
