\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 The activists championing DIY abortions for a post-Roe v Wade world\b0\par\par\uc2 Poppy Noor \par \uc2 2,491 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 May 2022\par 16:25 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Forget back alleys and coat hangers. Self-managed abortions can be \u8216\'20\'18safer than aspirin\u8217\'20\'19, research says\par \par \uc2 Maggie Mayhem knows when she decided to become a reproductive rights activist. At around 13 she discovered two conditions in her southern California Catholic girls school\u8217\'20\'19s manual:\par \par \uc2 If a student was found to have had an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , they would be expelled, because \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was against the teaching of the Catholic church.\par \par \uc2 At the same time, the school would not accommodate a student who became pregnant.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt taught me my reproductive system was something I should be afraid of, that it could have negative consequences for my life,\u8221\'20\'1D Mayhem says. \u8220\'20\'1CI saw: \u8216\'20\'18there will be no sympathy for you. And anyone that you talk to about this poses a risk.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She also saw beautiful things: friends helping friends to the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic. Teenagers taking care of teenagers, keeping grownups at bay. That solidarity led her to her current line of work.\par \par \uc2 Mayhem \u8211\'20\'13 a pseudonym \u8211\'20\'13 is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theatlantic.com/magazine/archive/2022/05/roe-v-wade-overturn-abortion-rights/629366/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 just one of many US activists}}}\uc2  vouching for self-managed abortions outside the gaze of the medical establishment. With a growing slate of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://viewer.gutools.co.uk/us-news/live/2022/may/03/roe-v-wade-us-supreme-court-preliminary-vote-overturns-abortion-ruling-leaked-draft-livev-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the recent leak}}}\uc2  of a supreme court draft opinion indicating justices have already voted to overturn the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , activists like Mayhem say such measures aren\u8217\'20\'19t just necessary, they are also better than what\u8217\'20\'19s currently on offer. They are saying: \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is your right \u8211\'20\'13 and you don\u8217\'20\'19t need to depend on doctors or the state for it.\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 When most people think of self-managed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , they think of back alleys, coat hangers or throwing oneself down the stairs; of last resorts, despair, shame. But that is no longer the reality. Today, self-managed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  often means taking pills that are available over the counter {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.medab.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in many countries}}}\uc2 , with little risk of death or serious complications. Other times, it means using herbs, or vacuum aspirators, like {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theatlantic.com/magazine/archive/2022/05/roe-v-wade-overturn-abortion-rights/629366/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Del-Em}}}\uc2  (a homemade suction device created by activists in the 70s), under the watchful eye of somebody experienced \u8211\'20\'13 like a midwife or a doula \u8211\'20\'13 who can advise if things go wrong.\par \par \uc2 Self-managed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not a silver bullet. It carries with it the risk of prosecution, even though it is not illegal in most states. In April, a Texas woman was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/09/texas-woman-26-charged-murder-self-induced-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 charged with murder}}}\uc2  for a self-induced \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , even though there was no legal basis for the charges \u8211\'20\'13 as the district attorney {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/10/texas-woman-murder-charges-dropped-self-induced-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 admitted}}}\uc2  when he dropped the case. And not everybody wants to turn to a clandestine market for their \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care. Some people feel more comfortable with a licensed practitioner. People want options. But for many, options are fast receding.\par \par \uc2 Those who look outside the medical establishment will find, often through word of mouth, an underground movement of doctors, midwives, doulas and activists \u8211\'20\'13 some trained by formal institutions, others by practitioners in the network. They will find those who mostly undertake legal work \u8211\'20\'13 sharing information from the \uc2 World Health Organization\uc2  about how to use medication to induce an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , for example. They\u8217\'20\'19ll also find some who do not \u8211\'20\'13 assisting with abortions later down the line, or giving medical advice when things go wrong.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is not a practitioner\u8217\'20\'19s or a government\u8217\'20\'19s job to give people power,\u8221\'20\'1D says Samantha Zipporah, an educator who refers to herself as a traditional midwife \u8211\'20\'13 Zipporah is not credentialed. Zipporah says she rejects state regulation of pregnancy care. To her, home-centered \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care is far from a last resort or a reaction to a changing policy landscape. It\u8217\'20\'19s simply not something that should be dependent on an outside authority.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThroughout history, we have a much greater tradition of our fertility and reproductive capacities being social, spiritual and ecological rather than medical or political,\u8221\'20\'1D she explains.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe medical-industrial paradigm, the church, the state \u8211\'20\'13 these institutions are set up in a way that requires obedience and submission,\u8221\'20\'1D she says. \u8220\'20\'1COur power was never theirs. Our bodies have power.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The advent of medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has made the work of these activists easier \u8211\'20\'13 because it is easily available. Medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ansirh.org/sites/default/files/publications/files/mifepristone_safety_4-23-2019.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 safer than Tylenol}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kff.org/womens-health-policy/fact-sheet/the-availability-and-use-of-medication-abortion/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 resulting in a successful termination 99.6%}}}\uc2  of the time when used appropriately, with less than a 1% risk of complications, according to the \uc2 Kaiser Family Foundation\uc2 . The safety of other means used outside a clinical setting hasn\u8217\'20\'19t been sufficiently studied, but broadly speaking, existing data from recent years does not show elevated fatality rates from self-managed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FDA\uc2  recently allowed people to receive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills by mail, without needing to first visit a medical facility. But states seeking to restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://viewer.gutools.co.uk/us-news/2022/apr/07/us-mail-order-abortions-oklahoma"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have required}}}\uc2  in-person visits or have banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  telehealth services outright.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s just one reason activists want to cut out the middle man.\par \par \uc2 Although the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://viewer.gutools.co.uk/world/2022/feb/24/medication-abortion-majority-2020-analysis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 majority of abortions}}}\uc2  are completed with medication, only 21% of the US public {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kff.org/womens-health-policy/poll-finding/abortion-knowledge-and-attitudes-kff-polling-and-policy-insights/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 know these pills exist}}}\uc2 . People can order them {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://viewer.gutools.co.uk/world/2021/dec/12/rebecca-gomperts-doctor-defying-laws-abortions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 online}}}\uc2  but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.womenonwaves.org/en/page/974/warning--fake-abortion-pills-for-sale-online"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 scam sites are common}}}\uc2 . So activists use in-person and virtual grassroots networks to share where to buy the pills, how to safely ingest them, what a normal response to them looks like and when to seek help. Crucially, they can explain the legal landscape \u8211\'20\'13 after all, if you turn up at the emergency room admitting you tried to cause your own \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , you could face legal risk. But because medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and complications from it look exactly the same, medically, as a miscarriage \u8211\'20\'13 people need not disclose they tried to induce their own \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 Self-managed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  can eradicate barriers, even in a world where in-clinic abortions aren\u8217\'20\'19t under attack. It offers privacy: the ability to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at home, away from protesters, or your community. It may offer cover from an abusive partner. And it means that people who live far away from a clinic, or can\u8217\'20\'19t afford to make the trip, can still access the procedure.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt all comes down to someone assessing their own situation, and being able to make a decision about how to manage their reproductive care. There\u8217\'20\'19s simply no medical reason that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be over the counter,\u8221\'20\'1D says a spokesperson for Mountain Access Brigade, a group that runs an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  hotline in Appalachia and the south-east. \u8220\'20\'1CTo make people jump through these hoops: to go to appointments, to have a mandatory ultrasound \u8211\'20\'13 these things are designed to humiliate, shame and coerce them into changing their mind,\u8221\'20\'1D she adds.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese pills are safer than aspirin. They\u8217\'20\'19re safer than Viagra. We let people manage very complex conditions at home \u8211\'20\'13 such as diabetes. And yet these pills are so restricted,\u8221\'20\'1D says reproductive rights activist Susan Yanow. \u8220\'20\'1CPeople are afraid of them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s simply no reason that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be over the counter \u8230\'20\'26 these pills are safer than aspirin\par \par \uc2 Susan Yanow\par \par \uc2 Of course, some doctors worry about self-managed abortions. The \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kff.org/womens-health-policy/fact-sheet/the-availability-and-use-of-medication-abortion/#:~:text=Medication%20abortion%2C%20also%20known%20as,(10%20weeks)%20of%20pregnancy."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 considered safe only until 10 weeks}}}\uc2 . People can still use it effectively up to 14 weeks, but the risk of complications goes up.\par \par \uc2 Doctors worry about people estimating the wrong date of conception; that they may still be pregnant after taking the medication without realizing; or they will experience complications and end up in need of urgent help.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI absolutely worry about people self-managing their abortions,\u8221\'20\'1D says Dr Mark Rosing, an obstetrician gynecologist who works in the Bronx, New York. \u8220\'20\'1CA patient could hemorrhage, develop a severe infection and even die,\u8221\'20\'1D he adds.\par \par \uc2 Rosing was in training in New York in the early 2000s, when he noticed patients in the emergency room talking about taking a \u8220\'20\'1Cstar pill\u8221\'20\'1D before miscarriage. They were referring to misoprostol, one of the drugs used to induce a medical \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which was not widely available for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  uses then. He presumes many people used the medication successfully and didn\u8217\'20\'19t end up in the emergency room. But those who did were panicked, scared of how much they were bleeding and sometimes hadn\u8217\'20\'19t successfully evacuated the pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 He understands that in a landscape that looks {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://viewer.gutools.co.uk/us-news/2022/may/02/roe-v-wade-abortion-supreme-court-draft-opinion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 increasingly likely}}}\uc2  to overturn the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , leading to bans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/article/2021/10/26-states-are-certain-or-likely-ban-abortion-without-roe-heres-which-ones-and-why"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  in 26 states}}}\uc2 , people might not have a choice. \u8220\'20\'1CI wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t blame them. People aren\u8217\'20\'19t going to stop trying to get what they need,\u8221\'20\'1D he says.\par \par \uc2 Rosing was trained by many doctors who practiced before Roe v Wade, the seminal supreme court decision which established the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . His mentors and teachers told him about cases involving self-managed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and the gruesome complications which haunted them.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPeople came in with perforated uteruses, hemorrhage and severe infections. People lost their uterus and all kinds of things,\u8221\'20\'1D he says. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m really afraid we\u8217\'20\'19re going back there.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The reality is that self-managed abortions don\u8217\'20\'19t look the same now as pre-Roe. There were 19 deaths related to \u8220\'20\'1C illegal \u8221\'20\'1D abortions \u8211\'20\'13 those not performed by a licensed clinician \u8211\'20\'13 in 1973, the year Roe v Wade was decided, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/volumes/69/ss/ss6907a1.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CDC data}}}\uc2 . In the last two decades, two people have died from an illegal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/volumes/69/ss/ss6907a1.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 while 103 have died from a legal \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 . The comparison is not like-for-like \u8211\'20\'13 hundreds of thousands of legal abortions take place every year in the US, whereas the full scale of self-managed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unknown \u8211\'20\'13 but the dangers of self-managed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be overstated.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are more capable of being able to understand our reproductive selves \u8211\'20\'13 and to manage that effectively and safely \u8211\'20\'13 than we\u8217\'20\'19ve been led to believe,\u8221\'20\'1D says Vienna Farlow, a holistic healthcare practitioner. \u8220\'20\'1CBut the system is set up to say, you\u8217\'20\'19re too dumb to do any of this. And not only are you too dumb, your body doesn\u8217\'20\'19t matter enough for us to even care to tell you how to do it,\u8221\'20\'1D she expands.\par \par \uc2 Activists believe much of the stigma around self-managed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was caused, in part, by a campaigning technique by the pro-choice movement \u8211\'20\'13 when \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists would hand out small coat hangers, defending the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  by evoking images of dangerous procedures that are no longer the norm.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat may have been very necessary or appropriate for the time, but it increased the fear of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and added a lot more abstract ideas of danger rather than demystifying what \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is,\u8221\'20\'1D Mayhem says.\par \par \uc2 Between 2017 and 2020, researchers from the \uc2 University of California, San Francisco\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://jamanetwork.com/journals/jamanetworkopen/fullarticle/2774320"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tried to understand the prevalence}}}\uc2 , effectiveness and dangers of self-managed abortions \u8211\'20\'13 the first ever such study to do so. They asked a random sample of 7,022 women if they had self-managed an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in their lifetime and 1.4% responded that they had, leading researchers to predict that something like 7% of all women in the US will self-manage an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in their lifetime.\par \par \uc2 The researchers were surprised by the methods women use to induce their own abortions \u8211\'20\'13 booze, herbs, pills, even asking a partner to hit them in the abdomen. They thought medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be more prevalent. These methods were largely ineffective, but also largely not life-threatening. Of 92 participants who said they had tried to manage their own abortions, 27 were effective. Twelve said they experienced complications (defined as something requiring \u8220\'20\'1Ctreatment by a doctor or nurse\u8221\'20\'1D). Nobody experienced severe complications.\par \par \uc2 For one in five participants, not being able to locate an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic, or having to travel too far to get to one, was the reason the person attempted self-management.\par \par \uc2 Forebodingly, the researchers pointed out: \u8220\'20\'1CUnprecedented levels of new state-level \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions \u8230\'20\'26 and the potential for a Supreme Court decision that could reshape federal Constitutional protections on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , suggest an urgent need to pay close attention to trends in [self-managed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ] \u8230\'20\'26 in the coming years.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 While fears over medical difficulties abound when discussing self-managed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , incarceration is the bigger threat in the US. At least {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.law.berkeley.edu/wp-content/uploads/2016/01/SIA-Legal-Team-Brochure.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 17 people}}}\uc2  have been arrested in the US for charges connected to self-induced \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . They include Jennifer Whalen, who served jail time for buying pills online for her 16-year-old daughter to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , after they couldn\u8217\'20\'19t access an appointment at a clinic. Some, like {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://viewer.gutools.co.uk/us-news/2016/jul/22/purvi-patel-abortion-sentence-reduced"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Purvi Patel}}}\uc2  in Indiana and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://viewer.gutools.co.uk/society/2006/sep/04/health.medicineandhealth1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Regina McKnight}}}\uc2  in South Carolina, were given decades-long sentences. Both were overturned, but not before each spent years in jail.\par \par \uc2 But what are the risks of not getting an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ? First, a lot more people will die during childbirth \u8211\'20\'13 which is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/article/us-abortion/abortion-safer-than-giving-birth-study-idUSTRE80M2BS20120123"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 14 times more deadly}}}\uc2  than \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a very safe procedure. And in the United States, staying pregnant is relatively deadly, because we have such an abysmal rate of pregnancy-related mortality and morbidity,\u8221\'20\'1D explains Dr Amanda Stevenson, who conducted research predicting how many more people will die if Roe v Wade is overturned {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://read.dukeupress.edu/demography/article/58/6/2019/265968/The-Pregnancy-Related-Mortality-Impact-of-a-Total"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 solely because of the greater mortality risk }}}\uc2  of continuing a pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Her study found that, in the event of a nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, pregnancy-related deaths would increase by 21% within two years. The numbers would be worst for racial minorities. Black people would experience the greatest rate of increase in deaths (33%), followed by Hispanic people (18%).\par \par \uc2 Denying women access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  also increases their chances of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ansirh.org/sites/default/files/publications/files/the_harms_of_denying_a_woman_a_wanted_abortion_4-16-2020.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 life-threatening complications,}}}\uc2  financial hardship and prolonged domestic violence. But if more people know how to manage their own abortions, risks would be reduced, surmises Dr Stevenson. \u8220\'20\'1CIf the alternative is self-managed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and that\u8217\'20\'19s because clinic-based care isn\u8217\'20\'19t accessible, then that\u8217\'20\'19s a whole lot safer than staying pregnant,\u8221\'20\'1D she says.\par \par \uc2 Another midwife, who supports abortions outside a clinical context, points out the dangers associated with in-clinic abortions. She says she has supported people who have gone for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in-clinic, and then found themselves with complications \u8211\'20\'13 like hemorrhage, or incomplete removal \u8211\'20\'13 who did not want to go back to the doctor. \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s so many people that are sent home with pills, without any education about what [their experience should look like],\u8221\'20\'1D says the midwife, who did not want to be identified for legal reasons.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI have supported people who have had incomplete abortions, and needed to go back to the clinic for a repeat suction a number of times, or have had infections and retained tissues, who did not go back to the clinic because the clinic was abusive \u8230\'20\'26 because the clinical care was so impersonal,\u8221\'20\'1D she says.\par \par \uc2 As Zipporah puts it, it\u8217\'20\'19s not about placing one treatment over the other, it\u8217\'20\'19s about giving people a choice.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am not demonizing medical care providers or medical care. I don\u8217\'20\'19t think that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be only always in the clinic with a doctor or only always at home with a midwife. I believe that people need to have the education and support to do whatever the fuck they want. And to realize that they have options,\u8221\'20\'1D says Zipporah.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220507ei570018k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
