\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 To Reasonable Rational People counseling calm about  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2 : Aaaarrggh!\b0\par\par\uc2 Arwa Mahdawi \par \uc2 1,023 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 May 2022\par 13:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Worried the Republicans will follow up their attack on reproductive rights by taking our other rights? You should be\par \par \uc2 Aaaaaaaaaaarrrrrrrrrgggggh\par \par \uc2 I tried to think of a pithy introduction to this week\u8217\'20\'19s newsletter. Something witty, something drily poking fun at the dystopic week we\u8217\'20\'19ve had. Something that was not yet another reference to \uc2 Gilead\uc2  and the Handmaid\u8217\'20\'19s Tale. But, unfortunately, all jokes were drowned out with internal existential screaming: aaaarggh.\par \par \uc2 First, there was the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/03/first-edition-abortion-rights-leak-roe-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bombshell leak}}}\uc2  on Monday night of a draft supreme court opinion that appeared to show the court is ready to overturn Roe v Wade and the federal right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . While this was a shock it wasn\u8217\'20\'19t exactly a surprise. When Donald Trump was elected plenty of people were worried about the future of reproductive rights in the US. Calm down, dear, we were told by Reasonable Rational People\u8482\'21\'22. You\u8217\'20\'19re being alarmist!\par \par \uc2 Like clockwork, the Reasonable Rational People\u8482\'21\'22 emerged right after the supreme court leak to chide anyone worried that Republicans are not going to stop at overturning Roe but want to take away even more of our rights. \u8220\'20\'1CI think the people catastrophizing about contraception or interracial marriage being next after Roe sincerely believe it,\u8221\'20\'1D a (female) \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  columnist {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MollyJongFast/status/1522195299376275456?s=20&t=g8WcnJDRPAcXqd8OqcjslA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 snarked}}}\uc2  on \uc2 Twitter\uc2  on Wednesday. \u8220\'20\'1CBut I\u8217\'20\'19m sorry, I cannot take this seriously.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m sorry, we should all be taking this very seriously indeed. On the same day that prominent columnists were telling people to calm down \u8211\'20\'13 and less than 48 hours after the leaked supreme court opinion \u8211\'20\'13 Republicans in Louisiana advanced a bill that would redefine personhood to begin at the moment of fertilization and make {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/05/louisiana-abortion-bill-murder-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  a crime of murder}}}\uc2 . Yes, you read that right: the moment of fertilization. I\u8217\'20\'19m sure the people involved in drafting this law have no idea about how reproduction actually works (they like controlling female bodies, not learning about them), but between one-third and one-half of all fertilized eggs {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/gpr/2005/05/implications-defining-when-woman-pregnant#:~:text=Implantation%20can%20be%20completed%20as,only%20after%20implantation%20is%20complete."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 never fully implant}}}\uc2 . Which means someone in Louisiana needs to arrest God \u8211\'20\'13 he\u8217\'20\'19s responsible for a hell of a lot of abortions! This incredibly broad definition of personhood also means that anyone experiencing an ectopic pregnancy (which are not viable and very dangerous) in Louisiana has only two choices: go to prison or die. And that\u8217\'20\'19s not all: experts are worried that the law would criminalize in vitro fertilization as well as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/world/us/louisiana-legislators-advance-bill-classifying-abortion-homicide-2022-05-05/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 some forms of birth control}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s a reason I brought God up just now. There\u8217\'20\'19s supposed to be a division between church and state in the US but the people who drafted the Louisiana law seemingly forgot about that. The proposal contains a line about \u8220\'20\'1Cthe sanctity of innocent human life, created in the image of God\u8221\'20\'1D. This is clearly unconstitutional\u8211\'20\'13 \u8211\'20\'13 but that doesn\u8217\'20\'19t bother the bill\u8217\'20\'19s creators who have made it very clear that they don\u8217\'20\'19t care about democratic norms. Indeed, the bill\u8217\'20\'19s text states that the state should enforce the law \u8220\'20\'1Cwithout regard to the opinions and judgments of the \uc2 Supreme Court of the United States\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s unclear whether the Louisiana bill will become law anytime soon. But what is clear is that we are going to see more and more extreme proposals like this. As I discussed in a previous {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2021/dec/11/radicalized-christian-nationalism-growing-threat-american-democracy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Week in Patriarchy}}}\uc2 , radicalized Christian nationalism is a growing threat in the US; a small but very organised group of people are intent on turning the country into a modern theocracy. A few years ago a researcher called {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://religiondispatches.org/project-blitz-seeks-to-do-for-christian-nationalism-what-alec-does-for-big-business/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Frederick Clarkson}}}\uc2  exposed a Christian supremacist initiative called {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2018/jun/04/project-blitz-the-legislative-assault-by-christian-nationalists-to-reshape-america"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Project Blitz}}}\uc2 , whose mission is undermining the separation of church and state. You know what one major component of their strategy is? Flooding state legislatures with so many bills that trying to fight them becomes a game of \u8220\'20\'1CWhac-A-Mole\u8221\'20\'1D. And as liberals are busy playing Whac-A-Mole with proposals like this Louisiana bill, extremists and evangelicals are busy consolidating power. So don\u8217\'20\'19t let anyone tell you that you\u8217\'20\'19re \u8220\'20\'1Ccatastrophizing\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Data broker sells locations of people who visit \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vice.com/en/article/m7vzjb/location-data-abortion-clinics-safegraph-planned-parenthood?mc_cid=be8f374baa&mc_eid=8ce16ced76"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 According to Motherboard}}}\uc2 , a company called SafeGraph obtains location data from ordinary apps on people\u8217\'20\'19s phones and sells it on. Planned Parenthood is classified by SafeGraph as a \u8220\'20\'1Cbrand\u8221\'20\'1D that can be tracked; Motherboard was able to get a week\u8217\'20\'19s worth of data on where people who visited Planned Parenthood came from, and where they went afterwards for just $160.\par \par \uc2 Fox host says he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t know why people would hire pregnant women for important jobs\par \par \uc2 Brian Kilmeade was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.today.com/parents/dads/fox-why-hire-pregnant-women-rcna27550"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 referencing Nina Jankowicz}}}\uc2 , who was recently appointed to lead a newly created advisory board on misinformation {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/05/02/technology/partisan-dhs-disinformation-board.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 at the Department of Homeland Security}}}\uc2 . She is eight months pregnant. Kilmeade, by the way, is a father of three. For some reason he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t seem to think that becoming a father had any impact on his ability to do his job. (Then again, a racist potato could do his job, so that\u8217\'20\'19s not saying much.)\par \par \uc2 Missing and murdered Indigenous women remembered\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2022/5/5/us-canada-commemorate-missing-and-murdered-indigenous-women"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Thursday}}}\uc2  marked Missing and Murdered Indigenous Persons Awareness Day in the US {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbc.ca/news/canada/british-columbia/red-dress-day-2022-bc-1.6443456"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 and Red Dress Day in Canada}}}\uc2 . As {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/05/05/us/missing-murdered-indigenous-persons-awareness-day/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN reports}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CNationally, there were 764 unresolved cases of missing Native American people as of March 2022, according to data from the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://namus.nij.ojp.gov/sites/g/files/xyckuh336/files/media/document/namus-stats-ai-an-march-2022.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 National Missing and Unidentified Persons System}}}\uc2 . But advocates and experts have said those figures do not reflect the full extent of the issue due to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.gao.gov/products/gao-22-104045"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lack of comprehensive data.}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Menopausal women lack basic support, UK study finds\par \par \uc2 About {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2022/may/05/menopausal-women-lack-basic-support-landmark-survey-finds"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 80% of women surveyed}}}\uc2  said their workplaces have no policies or help in place; 41% said menopause symptoms were treated as a joke by colleagues; 45% said they avoid speaking to their doctor due to stigma.\par \par \uc2 The week in pac-triarchy\par \par \uc2 The World Video Game Hall of Fame announced its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.museumofplay.org/press-release/world-video-game-hall-of-fame-inductees-for-2022-announced/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 latest inductees}}}\uc2  on Thursday; among the four \u8220\'20\'1Ciconic\u8221\'20\'1D games are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/technology-arts-and-entertainment-rochester-games-video-800be4bbfbbae2940ebe2229586ce2f8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ms Pac-Man}}}\uc2 . The 41-year-old arcade game is munching its way into the Hall of Fame seven years after Pac-Man.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220507ei57001md\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
