\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Texas attorney general says state bar suing him over bid to overturn 2020 election \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Gloria Oladipo \par \uc2 6,292 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 May 2022\par 20:23 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Full story: \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2  says state bar plans to sue him over election liesNo-exception \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws gain traction across USRussia-Ukraine war \u8211\'20\'13 latest updatesSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll close the blog here, on the Friday of the week the leak of a draft supreme court ruling heralded the end of the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and sent the nation into uproar.\par \par \uc2 Joan E Greve and Gloria Oladipo have been looking at what it all might mean for the midterm elections:\par \par \uc2 Speaking to reporters on a Thursday press call, \uc2 Jaime Harrison\uc2 , chair of the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2 , argued that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights will become a critical issue in the November midterms if the 1973 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/04/us-supreme-court-abortion-explainer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 landmark decision}}}\uc2  in the Roe v Wade case is overturned.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Republican attacks on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, their attacks on birth control and women\u8217\'20\'19s healthcare \u8211\'20\'13 these things have dramatically escalated the stakes of the 2022 election,\u8221\'20\'1D Harrison said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn November, we must elect Democrats who will serve as the last lines of defense against the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s assault on our established and fundamental freedoms.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But Republicans have insisted that issues such as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/feb/10/us-inflation-reached-highest-level-40-years-january"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 record-high inflation}}}\uc2  and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/01/republicans-politics-us-immigration-midterm-strategy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 handling of the US-Mexican border}}}\uc2  will weigh far more heavily on voters\u8217\'20\'19 minds in November.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCould be wrong, but I\u8217\'20\'19d predict that all those issues that have 60% of Americans [feeling] we are on the wrong track (high inflation, rising crime, the border, etc.) will play a bigger role in the elections [than] a supreme court decision on Roe,\u8221\'20\'1D Republican strategist Doug Heye {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DougHeye"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said on Twitter}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the full read:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/06/abortion-midterms-elections-roe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 How overturning Roe v Wade could supercharge the 2022 midterm campaigns}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Shortly before the 2020 election, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s national security adviser, \uc2 Robert O\u8217\'20\'19Brien\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1Cstunned\u8221\'20\'1D the chairman of the joint chiefs of staff by saying the president wanted to kill a senior Iranian military officer operating outside the Islamic Republic.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis was a really bad idea with very big consequences,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Mark Esper\uc2 , Trump\u8217\'20\'19s second and last secretary of defense, writes in his new memoir, adding that \uc2 Gen Mark Milley\uc2  suspected O\u8217\'20\'19Brien saw the strike purely in terms of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s political interests.\par \par \uc2 A Sacred Oath: Memoirs of a Defense Secretary in Extraordinary Times will be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.amazon.com/Sacred-Oath-Memoirs-Secretary-Extraordinary/dp/006314431X"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 published next week}}}\uc2 . \uc2 The Guardian{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2022/may/06/trump-defense-secretary-mark-esper-book"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 obtained}}}\uc2  a copy.\par \par \uc2 Throughout the memoir, Esper presents himself as one of a group of aides who resisted bad or illegal ideas proposed by Trump or subordinates \u8211\'20\'13 such as the proposed strike on the Iranian officer.\par \par \uc2 Among other such ideas that were discussed, Esper {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/05/trump-aides-pence-losers-2020-protests-book-mark-esper"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 says}}}\uc2 , were sending \u8220\'20\'1Cmissiles into Mexico to destroy the drug labs\u8221\'20\'1D; sending 250,000 troops to the southern border; and dipping the decapitated head of a terrorist leader in pig\u8217\'20\'19s blood as a warning to other Islamist militants.\par \par \uc2 More:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2022/may/06/trump-proposal-iranian-military-figure-book-mark-esper"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump sought strike on top Iran military figure for political reasons \u8211\'20\'13 Esper book}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  just wrapped up speaking in Ohio where he announced a new program where large manufacturers will be partnering with small and medium firms on 3D printing.\par \par \uc2 Biden also used the opportunity to promote a new competition and innovation bill that he is hoping Congress will pass, legislation he says is critical to addressing production delays across the country.\par \par \uc2 Here are some clips from today\u8217\'20\'19s speech.\par \par \uc2 From the Recount via \uc2 Twitter\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve never been more optimistic about America than I am today.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 President Biden at a speech in Ohio today {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/2eisfsBjlq"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/2eisfsBjlq}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1522666487743455232?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 6, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 From Now This via \uc2 Twitter\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8216\'20\'18You\u8217\'20\'19ve never seen a time when Europe and \uc2 NATO\uc2  were more closely aligned. No breathing room between us\u8217\'20\'19 \u8212\'20\'14 While discussing the Bipartisan Innovation Act, Pres. Biden emphasized America\u8217\'20\'19s role in world politics {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/1GixtyU5Yh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/1GixtyU5Yh}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 NowThis (@nowthisnews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/nowthisnews/status/1522666396252966912?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 6, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 Tennessee governor Bill Lee also signed legislation today banning trans women from participating in collegiate athletics, reports the Associated Press.\par \par \uc2 After the legislation passed through the GOP statehouse, Lee signed the bill today, not providing comment on why he signed the law. However, previously, Lee has stated that allowing trans women to participate would \u8220\'20\'1Cdestroy women\u8217\'20\'19s sports,\u8221\'20\'1D reports AP.\par \par \uc2 The bill will go into effect on 1 July. Tennessee is one of eight states that have passed anti-transgender sports bills. Other states include Arizona, Georgia, Iowa, Kentucky, Oklahoma, South Dakota and Utah.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Tennessee will strictly regulate the dispensing of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills, including imposing harsh penalties on doctors who violate them, under legislation recently signed into law by Republican Governor Bill Lee, reports the Associated Press.\par \par \uc2 The measure, which Lee signed on Thursday, will go into effect Jan. 1, 2023. Once enacted, a medical clinician will be required to be physically present when \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills are administered to a patient even though federal regulations now allow mail delivery nationwide.\par \par \uc2 The issue has become even more important as the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  seems poised to overturn the landmark 1973 Roe v. Wade decision as suggested through a recently leaked draft opinion. Notably, Tennessee is among the 13 states with a so-called trigger law that would make \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  illegal should Roe be overturned.\par \par \uc2 To date, 19 states have placed strict restrictions on accessing medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Under the Tennessee version, delivery of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills by mail would be outlawed and anyone who wanted to use \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills would be required to visit a doctor in advance and then return to pick up the pills.\par \par \uc2 The drugs may be dispensed only by qualified physicians which would include barring pharmacists from doing so. Violators would face a Class E felony and up to a $50,000 fine.\par \par \uc2 However, according to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law experts, it\u8217\'20\'19s an unsettled question whether states can restrict access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills in the wake of the \uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s decision.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe general rule is that federal law preempts conflicting state law,\u8221\'20\'1D Laura Hermer, a professor at the Mitchell Hamline School of Law in St. Paul, Minnesota, recently told The Associated Press.\par \par \uc2 No lawsuit has been filed challenging Tennessee\u8217\'20\'19s newly enacted restrictions.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the in-person requirement had long been opposed by medical societies, including the \uc2 American Medical Association\uc2 , which said the restriction offers no clear benefit to patients\par \par \uc2 Use of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills has been rising in the U.S. since 2000 when the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2  approved mifepristone the main drug used in medication abortions. More than half of U.S. abortions are now done with pills, rather than surgery, according to the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 , a research group that supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 Two drugs are required. The first, mifepristone, blocks a hormone needed to maintain a pregnancy. A second drug, misoprostol, taken one to two days later, empties the uterus. Both drugs are available as generics and are also used to treat other conditions.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a piece from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/martin-pengelly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Martin Pengelly}}}\uc2  about \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  allegedly lying to Congress during testimony on her involvement in the 6 January insurrection.\par \par \uc2 Greene was accused of lying by the lawyers of the same group who petitioned to have her excluded from the midterm ballot.\par \par \uc2 Lawyers for voters seeking to bar the far-right Republican \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  from Congress over her support for the January 6 insurrection have accused her of lying in a hearing in the case.\par \par \uc2 In a filing Friday, lawyers for groups challenging Greene said a text from the Georgia congresswoman to then White House chief of staff \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/26/marjorie-taylor-greene-texts-mark-meadows-martial-law-2020-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 released}}}\uc2  by the House committee investigating January 6, shows she lied in testimony.\par \par \uc2 At the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/22/marjorie-taylor-greene-court-congress-capitol-attack"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hearing in Atlanta}}}\uc2  earlier this month, a fractious affair in front of an administrative judge, Greene said she could not recall advocating for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to impose martial law after the Capitol attack, as the then president sought to remain in power despite losing the 2020 election to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In the text message released this week, Greene told Meadows on 17 January 2021, 11 days after the riot and three days before Biden\u8217\'20\'19s inauguration: \u8220\'20\'1CIn our private chat with only Members several are saying the only way to save our Republic is for Trump to call Marshall [sic] law.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI just wanted you to tell him. They stole this election. We all know. They will destroy our country next.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2022-04-29/greene-s-accusers-in-insurrection-case-say-she-lied-under-oath?fbclid=IwAR0mGEZy5ujm3SYVp0F5AOZLpu0C1lEzsU9w5XWWrkKe9AKbpx2TVHgAmZg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported by Bloomberg News}}}\uc2 , attorneys for Greene\u8217\'20\'19s challengers said: \u8220\'20\'1CGreene\u8217\'20\'19s testimony at the hearing that she could not remember discussing martial law with anyone was already dubious.\par \par \uc2 Read the full article {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/30/marjorie-taylor-greene-accused-lying-capitol-attack-case"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 In other GOP news, a judge in Georgia found that US representative \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  is eligible to run for re-election, despite challenges from a group of voters over allegations that Greene played a significant role in the 6 January insurrection, reports the Associated Press.\par \par \uc2 Judge Charles Beaudrot announced his decision after a daylong hearing in April that included extensive questioning of Greene.\par \par \uc2 Whether or not Greene is on the ballot will ultimately be decided by Republican Secretary of State \uc2 Brad Raffensperger\uc2 , who Beaudrot has to submit his findings to according to Georgia state law.\par \par \uc2 enltrA judge in Georgia has found that U.S. Rep. \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  can run for reelection, rejecting arguments from a group of voters who had challenged her eligibility over allegations that she engaged in insurrection. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/PCLQTGXBsR"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/PCLQTGXBsR}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Associated Press (@AP) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AP/status/1522645740929048577?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 6, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Texas State Bar has published a statement in response to \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s claim that the bar is conducing a \u8220\'20\'1Cwitch-hunt\u8221\'20\'1D over him contesting 2020 election results in Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 Texas\u8217\'20\'19s state bar said, in part:\par \par \uc2 The system is designed to ensure fairness to all parties. Partisan political considerations play no role in determining whether to pursue a grievance or how that grievance proceeds through the system. Any claims to the contrary are untrue.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe state bar responds to AG \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2 , after he said the bar is conducting a \u8220\'20\'1Cwitch-hunt\u8221\'20\'1D over his lawsuit contesting 2020 election results in Pennsylvania. Bar says partisan politics plays no role in determining whether to pursue a grievance. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/txlege?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #txlege}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/GcgDV2kNfR"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/GcgDV2kNfR}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Monica Madden (@themonicamadden) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/themonicamadden/status/1522607193614434304?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 6, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s also a statement from Paxton who said he will be investigating the Texas Bar Foundation \u8220\'20\'1Cfor facilitating mass influx of illegal aliens,\u8221\'20\'1D shortly after the state bar announced their investigation.\par \par \uc2 enltrAG {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KenPaxtonTX?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @KenPaxtonTX}}}\uc2  announces he\u8217\'20\'19s investigating Texas Bar Foundation \u8220\'20\'1Cfor facilitating mass influx of illegal aliens\u8221\'20\'1D \u8212\'20\'14 right after denouncing the state bar for a "witch hunt" related to his lawsuit contesting the 2020 election results in Pennslyvania. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/jnwWk6ZWgt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/jnwWk6ZWgt}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/et0ECH75sQ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/et0ECH75sQ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Monica Madden (@themonicamadden) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/themonicamadden/status/1522598472561664004?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 6, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2  is a two-term incumbent and drew an unusual number of primary challenges after eight of his top deputies told the \uc2 FBI\uc2  in 2020 that the attorney general had been using his office to benefit a wealth donor, The Associated Press writes.\par \par \uc2 They accused him of bribery, abuse of office and other crimes prompting an ongoing federal investigation.\par \par \uc2 Paxton has denied wrongdoing and separately pleaded not guilty in a state securities fraud case that has languished since 2015. His defense lawyer, Philip Hilder, declined to comment.\par \par \uc2 Shortly after saying the bar plans to sue him, Paxton\u8217\'20\'19s office announced that it will be investigating the Texas Bar Foundation for \u8220\'20\'1Cits possibly aiding and abetting the mass influx of illegal aliens.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The charitable group\u8217\'20\'19s broad is partially appointed by the bar president.\par \par \uc2 Gary Ratner, a Maryland attorney with Lawyers Defending American Democracy, which brought one of the complaints against Paxton, declined to comment.\par \par \uc2 Kevin Moran, a Democratic Party activist in Galveston, who brought another, did not immediately respond to a phone message seeking comment.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 More on the news that Texas attorney general \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2  is apparently being sued by the bar in his own state for his efforts in the failed attempt to overturn \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s election defeat in 2020.\par \par \uc2 In December 2020, the \uc2 US supreme court{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/dec/11/supreme-court-rejects-trump-backed-texas-lawsuit-aiming-to-overturn-election-results"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unanimously rejected}}}\uc2  a baseless lawsuit filed by Paxton on behalf of Texas, seeking to overturn the 2020 presidential election result.\par \par \uc2 The suit had been yet another move by the right in the increasingly desperate and ludicrous efforts to reverse {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2020/nov/24/us-election-results-2020-joe-biden-defeats-donald-trump-to-win-presidency"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s loss}}}\uc2  and all nine justices (bearing in mind the six-to-three, ultra-conservative supermajority on the nine-member bench).\par \par \uc2 Paxton wasn\u8217\'20\'19t even suing on behalf of Texas, of course, which Trump legitimately won, but to try to get the result overturned in four decisive states where Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2020/nov/24/us-election-results-2020-joe-biden-defeats-donald-trump-to-win-presidency"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lost to Joe Biden}}}\uc2  - Georgia, Michigan, Pennsylvania and Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press adds that, in bringing a court action against an attorney, the bar can seek punishment ranging from a written admonition to suspension or disbarment.\par \par \uc2 The discipline process resembles a trial and could include both sides taking testimony and obtaining records through discovery.\par \par \uc2 The bar complaints against Paxton alleged that his petitioning the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  to overturn the 2020 election was frivolous and unethical.\par \par \uc2 Paxton forecast the legal action against him during the final weeks of his Republican primary runoff against state land commissioner \uc2 George P. Bush\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Texas attorney general says state bar plans to sue him over his efforts to overturn Trump 2020 defeat\par \par \uc2 The Texas attorney general, \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2 , has announced that the state bar plans to sue him over his failed efforts to overturn the 2020 presidential election based on bogus claims of fraud, raising yet another legal danger as the embattled Republican is locked in a primary runoff, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 Since last summer, the state bar of Texas has been investigating complaints over Paxton\u8217\'20\'19s petitioning of the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  to block {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/nov/13/us-election-most-secure-history-voter-fraud-false-claim"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden\u8217\'20\'19s victory}}}\uc2  over \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  arrives at Cincinnati/Northern Kentucky international airport in Hebron, Kentucky. Photograph: Olivier Douliery/AFP/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 The professional group has not publicly filed a suit but Paxton, saying it plans to bring one against him and his top deputy, suggests the agency may believe their actions amounted to professional misconduct.\par \par \uc2 The attorney general said he stood behind his challenge to the \u8220\'20\'1Cunconstitutional 2020 presidential election,\u8221\'20\'1D even as he blasted the bar and announced an investigation into a charitable group associated with it.\par \par \uc2 I am certain that the bar will not only lose but be fully exposed for what they are: a liberal activist group masquerading as a neutral professional association,\u8221\'20\'1D Paxton said on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The bar, which is a branch of the Texas supreme court, said in a statement that \u8220\'20\'1Cpartisan political considerations play no role\u8221\'20\'1D in its actions.\par \par \uc2 State law prohibits it from discussing investigations unless a public complaint is filed and a spokesman declined to comment.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  at a rally in Greenwood, Nebraska. Photograph: Kenneth Ferriera/AP\par \par \uc2 Stay tuned for more on this....\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 A New York state judge\u8217\'20\'19s son who dressed like a caveman and helped a pro-\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  mob storm the US Capitol has received a prison sentence for his role in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/04/trump-oath-keepers-capitol-attack"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the 6 January 2021 attack}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Aaron Mostofsky, 35, must spend eight months in prison \u8211\'20\'13 and after his release, he must spend a year under federal supervision while also performing 200 hours of community service, a US district court judge in Washington, DC, ruled Friday.\par \par \uc2 This is not a cop. Supporters of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , including Aaron Mostofsky, right, who is identified in his arrest warrant, walk down the stairs outside the Senate Chamber in the US Capitol, in Washington, Jan. 6, 2021. Mostofsky, the son of a New York judge, referred to himself as a \u8220\'20\'1Ccaveman\u8221\'20\'1D eager to protest \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s presidential election loss, is to go to prison. Photograph: Manuel Balce Ceneta/AP\par \par \uc2 The judge, \uc2 James Boasberg\uc2 , also ordered Mostofsky to pay $2,000 in restitution to the federal government, court documents show.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.justice.gov/usao-dc/pr/new-york-man-pleads-guilty-felony-charges-offenses-committed-during-jan-6-capitol-breach"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 According to prosecutors}}}\uc2 , Mostofsky donned a caveman costume and wielded a walking stick while forming part of a crowd of Trump supporters who broke past a line of police officers trying to protect the Capitol, in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-capitol-breach"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 deadly insurrection}}}\uc2  that occurred on the day that Congress had convened {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/06/congress-certify-election-biden-republicans-object"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to certify Joe Biden\u8217\'20\'19s win}}}\uc2  in the 2020 presidential election.\par \par \uc2 He broke into the Capitol through a door that was forced open, stole body armor and a riot shield from the police, and even gave an on-camera interview to a media reporter, prosecutors alleged in a summary of the case that Mostofsky endorsed.\par \par \uc2 Mostofsky, in the video interview, repeated Trump supporters\u8217\'20\'19 lies that Biden had won thanks to election fraud. \u8220\'20\'1CThe election was stolen. \u8230\'20\'26 We were cheated. \u8230\'20\'26 I don\u8217\'20\'19t think 75 million people voted for Trump. I think it was close to 85 million,\u8221\'20\'1D Mostofsky said during the interview, according to court documents.\par \par \uc2 Prosecutors have charged about 800 people in the attack. More than 250 have already pleaded guilty, mostly to misdemeanors, and about 160 have been sentenced.\par \par \uc2 Mostofsky in February pleaded guilty to felony civil disorder as well as two misdemeanors: theft of government property and entering and remaining in a restricted building or grounds. He technically faced up to seven years in prison when he appeared for his sentencing Friday in front of Boasberg, though defendants who plead guilty without going to trial generally don\u8217\'20\'19t receive the harshest punishments available.\par \par \uc2 Mostofsky\u8217\'20\'19s father, Steven Mostofsky, is a judge in the Brooklyn-based New York supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s second district.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s fuller comments made by White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  today about claims that US intel helped sink the Russian ship Moskva.\par \par \uc2 From Bloomberg News\u8217\'20\'19 Jennifer Jacobs:\par \par \uc2 enltr"We did not provide Ukraine with specific targeting information for the Moskva...We had no prior knowledge of Ukraine's intend to target the ship," {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PressSec?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @PressSec}}}\uc2  says. They "have a greater level of intelligence and access to intelligence than we do" to track Russian naval vessels.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jennifer Jacobs (@JenniferJJacobs) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JenniferJJacobs/status/1522624280672051201?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 6, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 The White House disputed a claim that US intel helped Ukraines sink the Russian ship Moskva last month.\par \par \uc2 During a gaggle on AF1, White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  responded to a question on whether US intel helped sink the Russian ship.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTo speak to the reports, they\u8217\'20\'19re inaccurate,\u8221\'20\'1D said Psaki.\par \par \uc2 Psaki said that the US was not involved in the decision to strike Moskva and had no prior knowledge of Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s intent to strike the ship, adding that any intel reports of US involvement are an \u8220\'20\'1Coverclaiming\u8221\'20\'1D of the US\u8217\'20\'19 role and an \u8220\'20\'1Cunderclaiming\u8221\'20\'1D of the role of Ukraine and their intelligence capabilities.\par \par \uc2 enltrUS not involved in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Ukraine?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Ukraine}}}\uc2  decision or operation to strike {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Russia?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Russia}}}\uc2  Moskva ship, had no prior knowledge of Kyiv's intent to target the ship, did not supply the intel - {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PressSec?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @PressSec}}}\uc2  refuting reports.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Patsy Widakuswara (@pwidakuswara) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/pwidakuswara/status/1522619261344264192?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 6, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  began her last gaggle as White House press secretary, with her last day on 13 May.\par \par \uc2 While aboard AF1, Psaki joked:\par \par \uc2 This is my last gaggle on Air Force One. So I have a lot of things to get off my chest.\par \par \uc2 enltr"This is my last gaggle on Air Force One. So I have a lot of things to get off my chest," {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PressSec?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @PressSec}}}\uc2  joked to press otw to Cincinatti.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Patsy Widakuswara (@pwidakuswara) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/pwidakuswara/status/1522615602749321217?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 6, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Stay tuned for more from today\u8217\'20\'19s gaggle, happening now.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is currently en-route to Ohio, where he is set to announce that five US manufacturers have made commitments to boost their dependence on small and medium American firms for 3D printing, reports the Associated Press.\par \par \uc2 enltrBIDEN VISITS CINCINNATI: President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  departs the White House on Air Force One, heading to Cincinnati.\par \par \uc2 Here's everything we know on the president's visit: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/qBiEmx65z1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/qBiEmx65z1}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/wDNmQQNXq5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/wDNmQQNXq5}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 WLWT (@WLWT) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/WLWT/status/1522609240476692480?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 6, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s visit to the Midwest and announcement of the 3D printing program coincides with his ask to Congress to approve a stalled competition and innovation bill.\par \par \uc2 Biden says the bill is critical to boosting domestic manufacturing and addressing production delays throughout the country, reports AP.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m determined to make sure the United States holds the technological high ground in competition with other nations, especially China, as we move forward,\u8221\'20\'1D said Biden this week ahead of his visit.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Massachusetts senator Elizabeth Warren said today that a roll back of Roe v Wade would \u8220\'20\'1Cfall on the most vulnerable women in our country,\u8221\'20\'1D while appearing on a talkshow.\par \par \uc2 During her appearance on the View, host Joy Behar asked the senator: \u8220\'20\'1CWhat do you say to the American women who are just as angry as you are, about the fact that they are about to lose the autonomy over their own bodies?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Warren replied: \u8220\'20\'1CSo, I start with getting centered on what this is about. Understand, well-to-do women, they\u8217\'20\'19re gonna do fine,\u8221\'20\'1D adding that more privileged women can travel to get abortions if they are in a restrictive state.\par \par \uc2 Warren continued: \u8220\'20\'1CWho is this going to fall on? This is going to fall on the most vulnerable women in our country,\u8221\'20\'1D adding that poor women, women of color, and victims of sexual violence will be disproportionately impacted.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat is what makes me furious and gets me into this fight,\u8221\'20\'1D added Warren.\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenWarren?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @SenWarren}}}\uc2  tells {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/TheView?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #TheView}}}\uc2  that overturning Roe v. Wade would "fall on the most vulnerable women in our country."\par \par \uc2 "That is what makes me furious and gets me into this fight." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/cVclFZQmjA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/cVclFZQmjA}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/G2s81FJQQK"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/G2s81FJQQK}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The View (@TheView) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TheView/status/1522600512503308296?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 6, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 US congresswoman \uc2 Cori Bush\uc2  stopped by an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic in St. Louis, following news that the Supreme Court is prepared to roll back \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 In a Tik Tok posted by staff at a Planned Parenthood clinic in the St. Louis region, Bush is seen dancing and laughing with staff as the group attempts to replicate a dance on the app.\par \par \uc2 Bush wrote via \uc2 Twitter\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 Joy is an act of resistance. I stopped by the our local \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic, and we made a TikTok together.\par \par \uc2 Colleagues looking to support our community during this tough time: reach out to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics in your district. They deserve our love, especially right now.\par \par \uc2 enltrJoy is an act of resistance. I stopped by the our local \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic, and we made a TikTok together ??\par \par \uc2 Colleagues looking to support our community during this tough time: reach out to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics in your district. They deserve our love, especially right now. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/3qpTuDICQg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/3qpTuDICQg}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Cori Bush\uc2  (@CoriBush) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CoriBush/status/1522345492457394176?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 5, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Umi, a staff member who was retweeted by Bush, wrote:\par \par \uc2 My Congresswoman is the absolute BEST! She is not only talking that talk but walking the walk for all Missourians and making sure that we have access to affordable healthcare. Thank you to all the staff at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PPSLR"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @PPSLR}}}\uc2  for truly doing the work you do. Our Congresswoman loves us.\par \par \uc2 enltrMy Congresswoman is the absolute BEST! She is not only talking that talk but walking the walk for all Missourians and making sure that we have access to affordable healthcare. Thank you to all the staff at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PPSLR?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @PPSLR}}}\uc2  for truly doing the work you do. Our Congresswoman loves us ?? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/tyca83W7ek"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/tyca83W7ek}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Umi (@Umik90) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Umik90/status/1522270605202149377?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 5, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Bush has publicly shared the story behind her own \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , joining two other Democratic congresswoman last September who shared their personal stories during a House oversight committee meeting on reproductive rights.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/sep/30/congresswomen-personal-abortion-stories-cori-bush-barbara-lee-pramila-jayapal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cori Bush and other congresswomen share personal \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  stories}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here are more pictures from Jill Biden\u8217\'20\'19s trip to Romania and Slovakia, where she will visit with Ukraine refugees over Mother\u8217\'20\'19s Day weekend.\par \par \uc2 enltr {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/FLOTUS?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @FLOTUS}}}\uc2  is in europe this weekend supporting \uc2 NATO\uc2  countries on the front lines of the war in Ukraine. Today, she's in Romania at a military base. On Sunday, she'll be in Slovakia meeting Ukrainian refugees. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/I2DuZIn63e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/I2DuZIn63e}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Chris Sheridan (@ChrisSheridan34) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ChrisSheridan34/status/1522599567312760837?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 6, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrJill Biden cuts into an American flag cake at the MK Air Force base in Romania. The cake was made to commemorate her visit here. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/P1hLu6bdfX"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/P1hLu6bdfX}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Tyler Pager (@tylerpager) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/tylerpager/status/1522600835699470337?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 6, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 In addition to serving food, Biden also brought ketchup for personnel stationed overseas, as many have run out of different comforts from home like the condiment.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe air base the First Lady is visiting in Romania has tripled in size, to 2,700 US/\uc2 NATO\uc2  personnel, since the beginning of the Russian invasion. The soldiers here have run out of small comforts, like ketchup. The First Lady brought five gallons of Heinz over on her plane. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/2Ty1yixs0J"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/2Ty1yixs0J}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Katie Rogers (@katierogers) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/katierogers/status/1522595582296174592?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 6, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and other \uc2 G7\uc2  leaders will hold talks with Ukraine president \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2  on Sunday, reports Reuters.\par \par \uc2 The world leaders will meet in a virtual meeting on Sunday, confirmed a spokesperson for the \uc2 White House\u8217\'20\'19s National Security Council\uc2  today.\par \par \uc2 Follow the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s live blog coverage of the Russia-Ukraine war {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/may/06/russia-ukraine-war-rescue-operations-to-resume-in-mariupol-hellscape-un-says-amid-rumours-russia-wants-to-claim-city-for-victory-day-live"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/may/06/russia-ukraine-war-rescue-operations-to-resume-in-mariupol-hellscape-un-says-amid-rumours-russia-wants-to-claim-city-for-victory-day-live"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Russia-Ukraine war: Mariupol is being \u8216\'20\'18tortured to death\u8217\'20\'19, says Zelenskiy; new evacuation of steelworks under way \u8211\'20\'13 live}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jill Biden is currently in Romania, using her second solo trip overseas to visit those impacted by Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Departing Washington DC on Thursday night, Biden said:\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s so important to the president and to me that the Ukrainian people know that we stand with them.\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/FLOTUS?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @FLOTUS}}}\uc2  at Andrews Air Force Base Thursday night before departing for Romania and Slovakia where she\u8217\'20\'19ll meet with Ukrainian refugees and others over Mother\u8217\'20\'19s Day weekend:\par \par \uc2 "It\u8217\'20\'19s so important to the president and to me that the Ukrainian people know that we stand with them." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/8xRVP1fk34"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/8xRVP1fk34}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Hunter Schwarz (@hunterschwarz) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hunterschwarz/status/1522584470880198658?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 6, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 After flying overnight, Biden is at the Mihail Kogalniceanu Air Base in Romania, where she is serving dinner to US service members stationed there, reports the Associated Press.\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/FLOTUS?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @FLOTUS}}}\uc2  serves food to U.S. service members at MK Air Base in Romania. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/3R4Vs3Z7o1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/3R4Vs3Z7o1}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Tyler Pager (@tylerpager) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/tylerpager/status/1522586024274059265?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 6, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltr.? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/FLOTUS?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @FLOTUS}}}\uc2  ? serving scoops of macaroni and cheese, and potatoes to US soldiers picking up dinner at Mihail Kogalniceanu Air Base in Romania. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/byYd3lbP70"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/byYd3lbP70}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 darlene superville (@dsupervilleap) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/dsupervilleap/status/1522586725658370053?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 6, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 In addition to visiting Romania, Biden will also travel to Slovakia. The two countries, both \uc2 NATO\uc2  allies, border Ukraine and have taken in millions of refugees since Russia invaded Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Biden will specifically be in Slovakia on Sunday Mother\u8217\'20\'19s day to meet with displaced Ukraine refugees, reports AP. Biden\u8217\'20\'19s daughter, Ashley Biden, had planned to join her mother on the trip, but backed out after learning she had been in close contact with someone who tested positive for Covid-19.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 428,000 jobs added in April- US Department of labor report\par \par \uc2 US employers added 428,000 jobs in April, extending a streak of hires despite inflation, Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Ukraine, chronic supply chain issues, and other economic woes , reports the Associated Press.\par \par \uc2 The latest report today from the US department of labor showed that last month\u8217\'20\'19s hiring kept the unemployment rate at 3.6%, among the lowest rates in almost 50 years.\par \par \uc2 Hiring gains have also been steady despite ongoing inflation, some of the worst in four decades. Despite that, employers have consistently added 400,000 jobs for 12 straight months, reports AP.\par \par \uc2 However, the most recent employment figures did include some warnings about the job market. The government revised down its estimate of job gains for February and March by a total of 39,000.\par \par \uc2 The number of people in the labor force also decreased in April by 363,000, the first drop since September 2021. The drop reduced the amount of Americans who are either working or looking for work from 62.4% to 62.2%.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 A coalition of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights groups announced today that they will be holding a nationwide day of action, \u8220\'20\'1CBans off Our Bodies\u8221\'20\'1D day, on 14 May.\par \par \uc2 In light of the potential rollback of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, several groups, including Planned Parenthood, UltraViolet, Women\u8217\'20\'19s March and MoveOn, will hold marches across the country, with four \u8220\'20\'1Canchor marches\u8221\'20\'1D to be held in New York City, Chicago, Los Angeles, and Washington DC, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2022/05/05/planned-parenthood-nationwide-day-action-abortion?utm_source=twitter&utm_medium=social&utm_campaign=editorial&utm_content=politics-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports Axios}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re expecting hundreds of thousands of folks in these anchor cities and still hundreds of events all across the country. So no matter where you are, there\u8217\'20\'19s somewhere for you to go,\u8221\'20\'1D said Kelley Robinson, \uc2 Planned Parenthood Action Fund\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s executive director.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  would immediately become illegal in at least 13 states if Roe v Wade was overturned, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2021/10/31/roe-v-wade-repeal-supreme-court-texas-mississippi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports Axios}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a piece from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/davidsmith"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s David Smith}}}\uc2  on Trump being a hero for the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement after placing several conservative justices on the Supreme Court:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m very pro-choice.\u8221\'20\'1D So said \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/meet-the-press/video/trump-in-1999-i-am-very-pro-choice-480297539914"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in an interview}}}\uc2  on NBC\u8217\'20\'19s Meet the Press in 1999, attributing his views on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \u8220\'20\'1Ca little bit of a New York background\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Two decades later, the businessman and reality TV star is the unlikeliest of heroes for social conservatives and Christian evangelicals because he delivered the ultimate prize: the end of America\u8217\'20\'19s constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/02/roe-v-wade-abortion-supreme-court-draft-opinion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 leak this week}}}\uc2  of a draft supreme court opinion showing that the court\u8217\'20\'19s conservative majority is poised to overturn Roe v Wade, the landmark 1973 decision legalising \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , represented a vivid aftershock of the Trump presidency.\par \par \uc2 He had reversed his position on the issue by the time he reached the White House and, with uncharacteristic discipline, spent his four years in office bending {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2021/may/23/us-supreme-court-trump-judicial-appointments"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the federal judiciary to the right}}}\uc2 , including with three supreme court appointments.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe supreme court will be his most important and long-lasting political legacy,\u8221\'20\'1D said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pomona.edu/directory/people/amanda-l-hollis-brusky"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Amanda Hollis-Brusky}}}\uc2 , an associate professor of politics at Pomona College in Claremont, California.\par \par \uc2 Read the full article {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/05/trump-abortion-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has remained uncharacteristically quiet on the news that the Supreme Court is ready to roll back \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, despite adding several conservative justices during his administration.\par \par \uc2 Former US President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  speaks at the Conservative Political Action Conference 2022 (CPAC) in Orlando, Florida. Photograph: Chandan Khanna/AFP/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 Trump, who appointed three of justices who are prepared to overturn Roe v Wade, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://go.politicoemail.com/?qs=7013dc33566f22aef59d8262d503967ca65fef84ec3967890ff4807b02ca0367be24d76643a09e5750fb7c69aed34164"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told Politico\u8217\'20\'19s Meridith McGraw }}}\uc2  that he is waiting to see the \u8220\'20\'1Cfinality\u8221\'20\'1D of the case and, for now, is only speaking on the decision in interviews.\par \par \uc2 According to Politico, four of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s current and former advisors believe he will take credit for the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights roll back once the decision is finalized.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Trump is holding a rally in Pennsylvania today to support celebrity doctor Mehmet Oz, who is a GOP senate candidate, and could give remarks on the leaked decision there.\par \par \uc2 enltrFormer President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is coming to Pennsylvania today to try to push Mehmet Oz over the finish line in his contentious primary campaign for \uc2 U.S. Senate\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/4dv4rsMUvD"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/4dv4rsMUvD}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Philadelphia Inquirer (@PhillyInquirer) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PhillyInquirer/status/1522557904066330624?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 6, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Politicians are being called out online for using the potential roll back of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights to fundraise for elections.\par \par \uc2 In one email that is being criticized, House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  urges recipients to send in $3 to help elect a \u8220\'20\'1Cslew of pro-choice House Democrats\u8221\'20\'1D to \u8220\'20\'1Cmake Republicans regret EVER coming after our reproductive rights.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrThis email does not contain a single word indicating that if we elect Democrats they will protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. Instead it's all about making Republicans "regret" and rue" their actions. It's just "elect us -- that'll show 'em!" {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/sFqKE7sImP"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/sFqKE7sImP}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jamison Foser (@jamisonfoser) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jamisonfoser/status/1521997083263127553?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 4, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Stacy Abrams, Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic gubernatorial candidate, pivoted her fundraising efforts on Wednesday and asked people to donate to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights groups active in her state.\par \par \uc2 From NPR\u8217\'20\'19s Rachel Treisman:\par \par \uc2 Abrams \u8212\'20\'14 who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2021/03/02/973067859/stacey-abrams-on-why-securing-voting-rights-is-as-necessary-now-as-in-the-past"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 helped turn Georgia blue}}}\uc2  in the 2020 presidential election after narrowly losing her last governor\u8217\'20\'19s race in 2018 \u8212\'20\'14 is continuing to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://secure.actblue.com/donate/afg22-email-scotus?ak_proof=1&akid=.846084.dkAktj&amount=10&amounts=10%2C20%2C30%2C40%2C50&rd=1&refcode=sa_em_220504_B1_ReproOrgs_S1_T1_SYA_30click&refcode2=_846084_dkAktj&t=1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 solicit donations}}}\uc2  for the Feminist Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Center, SisterSong, Planned Parenthood Southeast, Access Reproductive Care Southeast and NARAL Pro-Choice Georgia.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe know that no one individual, campaign or organization can guarantee reproductive choice on their own,\u8221\'20\'1D Abrams\u8217\'20\'19 campaign wrote in a fundraising email. \u8220\'20\'1CWe can only win this fight by uniting and doing the work together.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/staceyabrams/status/1522009382355193857?s=20&t=CJLPGlDMBXcPhAW_BmVZjg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tweet later that night}}}\uc2 , Abrams thanked the more than 187,000 supporters who have invested in her campaign so far and urged them to consider donating to the reproductive freedom organizations as well.\par \par \uc2 Abrams, who is running unopposed in the May 24 Democratic primary, has raised large sums of money for causes as well as her own candidacy.\par \par \uc2 Read the full article {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2022/05/05/1096872994/stacey-abrams-abortion-funds-georgia-governor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Lawmakers across the political aisle are using this week\u8217\'20\'19s seismic news that the supreme court is ready to overturn Roe v Wade and ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to electrify the midterms elections, following the shocking news that US justices are prepared to roll back \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 Vulnerable democrats, specifically in swing districts, are hoping the issue will rally voters. Specifically in Nevada, a state that largely voted in 1999 to codify Roe v Wade, senator \uc2 Catherine Cortez Masto\uc2  has used \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights to turn voters against her opponent, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://go.politicoemail.com/?qs=7013dc33566f22aecec54a57662982fca3c4e4afc0645e7c07547b9f2e39b9f2cc3b38c185e2fc8c581ee052c213ad6b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports Politico}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In an interview this week, Cortez said:\par \par \uc2 I have a record in support of a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to choose. And my opponent, Adam Laxalt, opposes it, and will take it away.\par \par \uc2 From Cortez via \uc2 Twitter\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 enltrMy opponent says that overturning Roe v. Wade and ending protections for a woman's right to choose is a "historic victory."\par \par \uc2 I trust women and their doctors to make the health care decisions that are best for them \u8212\'20\'14 not politicians. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/4SxpKdKEBC"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/4SxpKdKEBC}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Catherine Cortez Masto\uc2  (@CortezMasto) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CortezMasto/status/1521637261934166017?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 3, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Republicans have also used the opportunity to challenge their opponents\u8217\'20\'19 commitment to conservative ideals.\par \par \uc2 In Georgia, candidate \uc2 David Perdue\uc2  challenged incumbent governor Brian Kemp to \u8220\'20\'1Cpromise to call a special session of the legislature to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  outright if the court eliminates federal protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and leaves it to states to set their own laws\u8221\'20\'1D, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://go.politicoemail.com/?qs=7013dc33566f22aed2b0238e1cd4a51d214b5770723271fae20d8f63ad9de83b7ca6d7009b664a5ba9625bd4e8ac41cd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported the New York Times}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 From Perdue via \uc2 Twitter\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 enltrI\u8217\'20\'19m calling on Brian Kemp to join me in calling for an immediate special session of the legislature to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Georgia after Roe v. Wade is overturned.\par \par \uc2 You are either going to fight for the sanctity of life or you\u8217\'20\'19re not. (2/2)\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 David Perdue\uc2  (@DavidPerdueGA) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DavidPerdueGA/status/1522208072739049474?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 5, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 Leaked \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights decision electrifies midterms\par \par \uc2 Good morning US live blog readers! This is Gloria Oladipo from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s New York office.\par \par \uc2 Shock from the news that US justices appear ready to roll back \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights has electrified midterms, with Democrats hoping to use the issue to motivate voters, reports Politico. Meanwhile, Republicans locked in primaries are using the leak as an opportunity to challenge their opponents to pledge complete bans on abortions.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has been fairly quiet on the Roe v Wade news, despite bringing several conservatives justices to the Supreme Court during his tenure. According to Politico, while the former president never shies away from taking credit for a political accomplishment, he has only addressed the leaked decision in interviews and is waiting on a final ruling to be issued before speaking more widely.\par \par \uc2 In other news:\par \par \uc2 * Cities across the nation are bracing for possible civil arrest ahead of large \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights gatherings happening throughout the weekend. On Wednesday, 150 officials nationwide joined a call to discuss security concerns in connections to the leaked decision, including possible threats to Supreme Court justices, reported Politico.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is will be visiting Ohio today to meet with manufacturing leaders at \uc2 United Performance Metals\uc2  in Hamilton, Ohio. He is set to deliver remarks at 3.45pm Eastern time.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220506ei56001xn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
