\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 How overturning Roe v Wade could supercharge the 2022 midterm campaigns\b0\par\par\uc2 Joan E Greve in Washington and Gloria Oladipo in New York \par \uc2 1,012 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 May 2022\par 18:56 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Swing state Democrats are calling for a defense of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and Republicans doubling down on ending them\par \par \uc2 As the US waits to see whether the supreme court will follow through on its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/03/biden-democrats-reaction-codifying-roe-v-wade-reform-scotus"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 provisional decision}}}\uc2  to end the federal right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Democrats and Republicans are already preparing for how a reversal of Roe v Wade would affect the 2022 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/03/abortion-midterms-election-scotus-draft-opinion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 midterm elections}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Republicans have been heavily favored to retake control of the House and probably the Senate as well, but the court\u8217\'20\'19s forthcoming final opinion in the crucial Mississippi case now before it, Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization, could alter those predictions.\par \par \uc2 Since the court\u8217\'20\'19s draft opinion leaked on Monday night, vulnerable Democrats have made a point to portray themselves as champions of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy opponent says that overturning {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  and ending protections for a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to choose is a \u8216\'20\'18historic victory\u8217\'20\'19,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Catherine Cortez Masto\uc2 , a Democratic senator who is up for re-election in the swing state of Nevada, said on Tuesday. \u8220\'20\'1CI trust women and their doctors to make the healthcare decisions that are best for them \u8211\'20\'13 not politicians.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 My opponent says that overturning Roe v. Wade and ending protections for a woman's right to choose is a "historic victory."\par \par \uc2 I trust women and their doctors to make the health care decisions that are best for them \u8212\'20\'14 not politicians. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/4SxpKdKEBC"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/4SxpKdKEBC}}}\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Catherine Cortez Masto\uc2  (@CortezMasto) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CortezMasto/status/1521637261934166017?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 3, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Speaking to reporters on a Thursday press call, \uc2 Jaime Harrison\uc2 , chair of the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2 , argued that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights will become a critical issue in the November midterms if the 1973 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/04/us-supreme-court-abortion-explainer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 landmark decision}}}\uc2  in the Roe case is overturned.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Republican attacks on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, their attacks on birth control and women\u8217\'20\'19s healthcare \u8211\'20\'13 these things have dramatically escalated the stakes of the 2022 election,\u8221\'20\'1D Harrison said. \u8220\'20\'1CIn November, we must elect Democrats who will serve as the last lines of defense against the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s assault on our established and fundamental freedoms.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But Republicans have insisted that issues such as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/feb/10/us-inflation-reached-highest-level-40-years-january"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 record-high inflation}}}\uc2  and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/01/republicans-politics-us-immigration-midterm-strategy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 handling of the US-Mexican border}}}\uc2  will weigh far more heavily on voters\u8217\'20\'19 minds in November.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCould be wrong, but I\u8217\'20\'19d predict that all those issues that have 60% of Americans [feeling] we are on the wrong track (high inflation, rising crime, the border, etc.) will play a bigger role in the elections [than] a Supreme Court decision on Roe,\u8221\'20\'1D Republican strategist Doug Heye {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DougHeye"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said on Twitter}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Rather than celebrating the news of Roe\u8217\'20\'19s likely demise, Republican leaders have mostly tried to focus {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/03/chief-justice-roberts-abortion-leak-investigation-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on the leak itself}}}\uc2 , saying it represents a break in court decorum and blaming the incident on Democrats. (It is not known who leaked the draft opinion.)\par \par \uc2 Asked about the court\u8217\'20\'19s provisional decision on Tuesday, the Senate minority leader, \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , told reporters: \u8220\'20\'1CYou need, it seems to me, a lecture to concentrate on what the news is today. Not a leaked draft, but the fact that the draft was leaked.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Even the de facto leader of the Republican party, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , has been hesitant to address the content of the court\u8217\'20\'19s decision. The normally verbose former president has not yet released a statement about the draft opinion, although he has commented on the leak when asked by reporters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNobody knows what exactly it represents, if that\u8217\'20\'19s going to be it,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/05/05/trump-set-the-stage-for-roes-demise-for-now-he-doesnt-wanna-talk-about-it-00030543"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told Politico}}}\uc2  on Wednesday. \u8220\'20\'1CI think the one thing that really is so horrible is the leaking \u8230\'20\'26 for the court and for the country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s reluctance to address the draft opinion is even more notable considering his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2022/may/04/how-supreme-court-justices-voted-abortion-alito-roberts-thomas-kavanaugh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 three supreme court nominees}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 \uc2 Neil Gorsuch\uc2 , \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2  and Amy Coney Barrett \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/03/biden-democrats-reaction-codifying-roe-v-wade-reform-scotus"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 all initially voted}}}\uc2  to overturn Roe, according to the leaked provisional opinion published on Monday night.\par \par \uc2 The former president also promised during his 2016 campaign to select supreme court nominees who would help reverse the landmark 1973 case.\par \par \uc2 Now Republicans stand on the precipice of achieving their {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/video/2022/may/03/i-am-angry-elizabeth-warren-lambasts-supreme-court-after-draft-abortion-opinion-leak-video"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decades-long goal}}}\uc2 , and many of them seem hesitant to declare victory. However, some Republican primary candidates are using the draft opinion to draw a contrast between themselves and their opponents.\par \par \uc2 David Perdue\uc2 , the Trump-endorsed gubernatorial candidate in Georgia, condemned Governor Brian Kemp\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cbureaucratic response\u8221\'20\'1D to the news of Roe\u8217\'20\'19s likely reversal.\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m calling on Brian Kemp to join me in calling for an immediate special session of the legislature to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Georgia after Roe v. Wade is overturned.\par \par \uc2 You are either going to fight for the sanctity of life or you\u8217\'20\'19re not. (2/2)\u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 David Perdue\uc2  (@DavidPerdueGA) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DavidPerdueGA/status/1522208072739049474?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 5, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m calling on Brian Kemp to join me in calling for an immediate special session of the legislature to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Georgia after Roe v Wade is overturned,\u8221\'20\'1D Perdue {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DavidPerdueGA/status/1522208072739049474"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said on Thursday}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CYou are either going to fight for the sanctity of life or you\u8217\'20\'19re not.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Perdue and Kemp will face off in the Georgia gubernatorial primary later this month, providing an early test of how Republican voters feel about the looming end of Roe. But other Americans\u8217\'20\'19 thoughts about the matter will not be fully known until November.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, new metal barriers went up in front of the marble steps and columns of the majestic supreme court building in Washington DC, close to the US Capitol, this week, a stark symbol of the sudden politicization of the court that has always preferred to keep itself above the partisan fray.\par \par \uc2 This came after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/03/roe-v-wade-protests-outside-us-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fierce protests}}}\uc2  erupted there within minutes of the leak on Monday, with police separating protesters in rival camps the following day.\par \par \uc2 Now law enforcement officials in many places across the US {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/05/05/law-enforcement-violence-scotus-draft-roe-opinion-00030509?nname=playbook&nid=0000014f-1646-d88f-a1cf-5f46b7bd0000&nrid=00000168-5c87-d6fb-a77d-fdb72f6a0000&nlid=630318"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are braced}}}\uc2  for potential civil unrest and women\u8217\'20\'19s rights groups are planning massive protests in several cities for next weekend to demand the protection of the right to choose in reproductive healthcare.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220506ei5600335\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
