\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Schumer announces Senate  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights vote: \u8216\'20\'18America will be watching\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Richard Luscombe \par \uc2 5,214 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 May 2022\par 13:07 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Measure has next to no chance of passing in divided chamberBiden names \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  new White House press secretarySupreme court justice Alito bails on senior judges\u8217\'20\'19 conference\u8216\'20\'18Do something\u8217\'20\'19: Democrats struggle to rise to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  challengeSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re closing the US politics blog now after another day dominated by the fallout from the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s draft ruling upending almost half a century of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the US.\par \par \uc2 Senate majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  set a vote for next Wednesday to codify \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights into federal law. Democrats don\u8217\'20\'19t have the numbers for it to pass, but Schumer says the symbolic vote will show the country where every senator stands on the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAmerica will be watching,\u8221\'20\'1D he says.\par \par \uc2 Here are the day\u8217\'20\'19s other key developments:\par \par \uc2 * Democrats tore into Republican former vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  over an anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  speech he was set to deliver at a South Carolina Christian \u8220\'20\'1Cclinic\u8221\'20\'1D that serves to dissuade women from terminating their pregnancies.\par \par \uc2 * Republican senate leaders indicated a bipartisan deal was close on \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s request to Congress for $33bn in aid for Ukraine. Minority whip \uc2 John Thune\uc2  suggested the $20bn the president wants for military support could rise.\par \par \uc2 * Louisiana Republicans advanced an extreme bill that could see women who have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  charged with murder.\par \par \uc2 * Another audio clip released by the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  captured House minority leader Kevin McCarthy discussing the 25th amendment as an option to remove then-president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  from office two days after the 6 January Capitol attack.\par \par \uc2 * Supreme court justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  canceled an appearance at a conference of senior judges in New Orleans in the wake of the leak of his draft ruling ending \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights for women.\par \par \uc2 Thanks for joining us today. A reminder you can follow live developments in the Ukraine conflict in our {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/may/05/russia-ukraine-war-bloody-battles-inside-mariupol-steelworks-ukraine-claims-it-has-retaken-areas-near-kherson-live"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 24-hour blog here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * This post was amended on 6 May 2022. \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  is a former vice-president, not former president as an earlier version said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.57am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden names \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  new White House press secretary\par \par \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  has been named the new White Press secretary, replacing \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  who will depart on 13 May, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2022/05/05/president-biden-announces-karine-jean-pierre-as-white-house-press-secretary/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 it has just been announced}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2 . Photograph: Patrick Semansky/AP\par \par \uc2 Today\u8217\'20\'19s White House briefing, which was scheduled to have begun at 3pm with Psaki at the podium, is not yet under way.\par \par \uc2 Jean-Pierre, currently the principal deputy press secretary, has filled in for Psaki on several occasions, most recently while her predecessor was quarantining with Covid-19. She is a former political analyst with NBC and MSNBC.\par \par \uc2 Biden said in his statement:\par \par \uc2 Karine not only brings the experience, talent and integrity needed for this difficult job, but she will continue to lead the way in communicating about the work of the Biden-Harris administration on behalf of the American people.\par \par \uc2 Jill and I have known and respected Karine a long time and she will be a strong voice speaking for me and this Administration.\par \par \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  has set the standard for returning decency, respect and decorum to the White House briefing room. I want to say thank you to Jen for raising the bar, communicating directly and truthfully to the American people, and keeping her sense of humor while doing so.\par \par \uc2 I thank Jen her service to the country, and wish her the very best as she moves forward.\par \par \uc2 enltrLots to say about how grateful I am to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @POTUS}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/FLOTUS?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @FLOTUS}}}\uc2  and the Biden family for trusting me to serve as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PressSec?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @PressSec}}}\uc2  and plenty of time before my last day to share, but today is about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KJP46?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @KJP46}}}\uc2  so a few thoughts on this remarkable woman who will soon be behind the podium every day.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  (@PressSec) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PressSec/status/1522300494391226369?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 5, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Jean-Pierre will become the first Black woman and the first openly LGBTQ+ to serve as press secretary, Psaki {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PressSec/status/1522300494391226369"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said on Twitter}}}\uc2  after the president issued his statement.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  reported last month that Psaki, Biden\u8217\'20\'19s press secretary since he took office in January 2021, was lined up for a new job {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/01/jen-psaki-press-secretary-msnbc-white-house"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 as a host at MSNBC}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The White House also announced the return of Anita Dunn as a senior advisor and assistant to the president.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/01/jen-psaki-press-secretary-msnbc-white-house"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden press secretary Jen Psaki to become TV host at MSNBC, reports say}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 Bipartisan deal 'close' on Biden's $33bn Ukraine aid request\par \par \uc2 A compromise vote on \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s $33bn request to Congress for Ukraine aid could come as early as next week, the Associated Press is reporting.\par \par \uc2 Senior members of both parties told the news agency that bipartisan talks among House and Senate appropriations committee leaders are under way in hopes of producing legislation Congress could vote on as soon as next week.\par \par \uc2 Changes in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/28/joe-biden-ukraine-military-aid-us-congress"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s proposal}}}\uc2  are likely. The amount the president is seeking for military aid, currently $20bn, could rise.\par \par \uc2 Senator \uc2 John Thune\uc2 . Photograph: Kent Nishimura/\uc2 Los Angeles Times\uc2 /REX/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 South Dakota Republican \uc2 John Thune\uc2 , the minority whip, told the agency:\par \par \uc2 [Republican budget writers] are probably knocking some things out and adding some things. But I think by and large, everybody agrees we\u8217\'20\'19ve got to do all we can to help.\par \par \uc2 This package may not be robust enough, but I think it probably strikes close to the right balance.\par \par \uc2 Republican Senate minority leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  indicated broad backing for the measure but aides said he objected to proposed funding to some international organizations Republicans have criticized for spending money on alternative energy.\par \par \uc2 McConnell said:\par \par \uc2 This isn\u8217\'20\'19t about battling climate change. If the Senate is serious about helping Ukraine win, we need to show it by passing supplemental assistance. Clean, no strings attached, and soon.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/nashville"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nashville}}}\uc2  public library has debuted new library cards celebrating banned books amid attempts to censor literature throughout the state.\par \par \uc2 Patrons of the Nashville public library system can now get limited-edition bright yellow library cards that say: \u8220\'20\'1CI read banned books.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newschannel5.com/news/nashville-public-library-debuts-limited-edition-i-read-banned-books-library-cards"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 With only 5,000 limited-edition cards available}}}\uc2 , the Nashville public library hopes to distribute all of them in May to a variety of library users, with existing patrons and first-time visitors eligible for the special cards.\par \par \uc2 The newly released cards are a part of the library\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1CFreedom to Read\u8221\'20\'1D campaign, a rebuttal to escalating attempts in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/tennessee"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tennessee}}}\uc2  to censor books.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis campaign is our way of bringing our community together in our shared Freedom to Read, which is essential to sustaining our democracy,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/nation/2022/05/05/nashville-library-card-banned-books/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said Kent Oliver}}}\uc2 , the Nashville public library\u8217\'20\'19s director, in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://library.nashville.org/sites/default/files/2022-04/NPL-PRESS-RELEASE-NPL-LAUNCHES-FREEDOM-TO-READ-CAMPAIGN.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 news release}}}\uc2  announcing the campaign.\par \par \uc2 In Tennessee, conservative lawmakers have forwarded new proposals that drastically censor material within classrooms.\par \par \uc2 In January, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jan/27/tennessee-school-board-bans-pulitzer-prize-winning-holocaust-novel-maus"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a Tennessee school board unanimously voted to ban}}}\uc2  the Pulitzer prize-winning graphic novel Maus from all its classrooms. Maus, which tells the story of Holocaust survivors, was reportedly banned for eight curse words used in the book and a drawing of a naked mouse.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/nation/2022/05/05/nashville-library-card-banned-books/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 A month later}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tennessean.com/story/news/local/williamson/2022/01/25/williamson-county-schools-committee-removes-book-elementary-curriculum/9217318002/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a separate school board upheld a ban}}}\uc2  on the 1994 novel Walk Two Moons, which focuses on a 13-year-old Native American girl, after the ban was suggested by a chapter of the conservative group Moms for \uc2 Liberty\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Last month, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/nation/2022/05/05/nashville-library-card-banned-books/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lawmakers in Tennessee\u8217\'20\'19s house and senate passed legislation}}}\uc2  that would give a state-run commission the power to ban books in public schools and veto curriculum decisions made by school boards. The Tennessee governor, \uc2 Bill Lee\uc2 , has not confirmed if he will sign the bill.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/05/nashville-public-library-banned-books-cards"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nashville library debuts \u8216\'20\'18I read banned books\u8217\'20\'19 cards amid censorship efforts}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democrats slam Pence over anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  speech\par \par \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  has been slammed by Democrats ahead of the Republican former vice-president\u8217\'20\'19s appearance in South Carolina today at a fundraising event for the Carolina Pregnancy Center, a Christian organization that provides services to pregnant people.\par \par \uc2 According to a press release, Pence\u8217\'20\'19s remarks would focus on \u8220\'20\'1Cprotecting the right to life [and] restoring the sanctity of life,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.postandcourier.com/politics/mike-pence-to-condemn-abortion-in-sc-as-supreme-court-suggests-roe-v-wade-overturn/article_01cbfbca-cae0-11ec-9e16-232b41a3ac88.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 per the Charleston Post and Courier}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Pence\u8217\'20\'19s speech comes days after the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s draft opinion in Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization leaked to the public. The draft decision indicated the court plans to overturn Roe v Wade, which established the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights activists {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2019/aug/16/georgia-abortion-crisis-pregnancy-centers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have criticized}}}\uc2  centers such as the one in South Carolina as \u8220\'20\'1Cfake clinics\u8221\'20\'1D over their efforts to dissuade clients from terminating their pregnancies.\par \par \uc2 Democrats attacked Pence for touting his anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  views just as the supreme court appears ready to override nearly 50 years of precedent and jeopardize reproductive rights across the country.\par \par \uc2 Jaime Harrison\uc2 , chair of the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2 , said on a press call:\par \par \uc2 Make no mistake, this draft opinion is the direct result of the Republican party\u8217\'20\'19s extreme, decades-long campaign against reproductive rights and Americans\u8217\'20\'19 fundamental freedom to make their own decisions about their health care.\par \par \uc2 Looking ahead to the midterm elections in November, Harrison added:\par \par \uc2 We must elect Democrats who will serve as the last lines of defense against [Republicans\u8217\'20\'19] assault on our established and fundamental freedoms.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 Schumer sets \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights vote: 'America will be watching'\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US Senate\uc2  will vote next week on legislation that would codify \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights into federal law, although the measure has next to no chance of passing the divided chamber and will be mostly symbolic, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 . Photograph: Michael Brochstein/SOPA Images/REX/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , the Democratic majority leader, said senators will vote on Wednesday on the pregnant workers fairness act. A similar measure failed in February, following the House passing an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights bill in September.\par \par \uc2 Although he does not have the necessary 60 votes to overcome a Republican filibuster and move ahead with the bill, Schumer said it was important members of both parties go on record about where they stand:\par \par \uc2 Next week\u8217\'20\'19s vote will be one of the most important we ever take because it deals with one of the most personal and difficult decisions a woman ever has to make in her life.\par \par \uc2 Come next week, senate Republicans will have to answer for everything they\u8217\'20\'19ve done over the years to embolden the hard right\u8217\'20\'19s hostility against a woman\u8217\'20\'19s choice.\par \par \uc2 The vote will tell next week. America will be watching.\par \par \uc2 Democratic leaders, lacking the support needed to change senate rules and pass an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bill on a majority vote, have signaled they intend to take the fight to voters during the campaign leading to the November election.\par \par \uc2 The inability of Congressional Democrats to take concrete action, in terms of legislation or \u8220\'20\'1Cpacking\u8221\'20\'1D the supreme court to counter the conservative majority, has upset supporters, who have urged the party to \u8220\'20\'1Cdo something\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/05/democrats-voters-senate-midterm-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Do something, Democrats\u8217\'20\'19: party struggles to rise to \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  challenge}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Louisiana Republicans push \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  'murder' law\par \par \uc2 Republicans in Louisiana have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/nation/2022/05/05/louisiana-abortion-bill-would-make-crime-murder/9656102002/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 advanced}}}\uc2  a bill to make \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  a crime of murder, as draft decision that would end \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights continues to spark nationwide protests and police in Washington raised \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/supreme-court/non-scalable-fence-erected-supreme-court-abortion-related-protests-rcna27452"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 non-scalable}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D fences around the supreme court.\par \par \uc2 Supporters admitted the bill, under which a woman terminating a pregnancy or anyone assisting her could be charged, was unconstitutional \u8211\'20\'13 as long as Roe v Wade was law.\par \par \uc2 The supreme court is expected to formally overturn {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.oyez.org/cases/1971/70-18"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2 , the 1973 case which established the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in June.\par \par \uc2 Danny McCormick, the state representative behind the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/louisiana"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Louisiana}}}\uc2  bill, said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe can\u8217\'20\'19t wait on the supreme court.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Since the draft ruling that seems set to overturn {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.oyez.org/cases/1971/70-18"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe}}}\uc2  was published by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/05/02/read-justice-alito-initial-abortion-opinion-overturn-roe-v-wade-pdf-00029504"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico}}}\uc2  on Monday night, Democrats have warned of a likely torrent of challenges to established rights.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has sounded the alarm about threats to privacy-based rights including the rights to contraception ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.oyez.org/cases/1964/496"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Griswold v Connecticut, 1965}}}\uc2  ) and to same-sex marriage ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.oyez.org/cases/2014/14-556"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Obergefell v Hodges, 2015}}}\uc2  ). The president also raised the prospect of attacks on the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/04/biden-lgbtq-children-next-target-maga-crowd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 teaching}}}\uc2  of LGTBQ+ children.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, Biden said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2  pushing such cases constituted \u8220\'20\'1Cthe most extreme political organisation \u8230\'20\'26 in recent American history\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Read the full story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/05/louisiana-abortion-bill-murder-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Louisiana Republicans advance bill to make \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  a crime of murder}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Numbers are growing and tempers are fraying outside the supreme court. My colleague David Smith has just sent this video of protestors on both sides of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights debate facing off:\par \par \uc2 enltrOutside Supreme Court. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/6ntroQk7n1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/6ntroQk7n1}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 David Smith (@SmithInAmerica) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SmithInAmerica/status/1522255908847472640?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 5, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Celebrities are sharing their \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  stories as the backlash to the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s draft ruling removing women\u8217\'20\'19s rights to the procedure grows. My colleague Lizzy Davies has this report:\par \par \uc2 Television presenter Cathy Newman has become the latest high-profile woman to go public with her experience of having an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as the possibility of the \uc2 US supreme court{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/02/roe-v-wade-abortion-supreme-court-draft-opinion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturning Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  sparks a defiant outpouring of testimony.\par \par \uc2 Cathy Newman, a presenter for Channel 4 News in the UK. Photograph: Steve Meddle/REX/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/IndyVoices/status/1522139630132420610?s=20&t=cOp7cDbNHPNs1f6vcOQnPw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Posting on Twitter}}}\uc2  on Thursday, the (UK) Channel 4 News presenter wrote that she was sad to have had an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  but had \u8220\'20\'1Cnever for one second regretted it\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEvery woman \u8211\'20\'13 here, in America and the world over \u8211\'20\'13 needs to have that choice,\u8221\'20\'1D Newman said.\par \par \uc2 Since Justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s draft opinion {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/05/02/supreme-court-abortion-draft-opinion-00029473"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was leaked to Politico}}}\uc2  on 2 May, setting out his belief that the landmark 1973 decision guaranteeing the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been \u8220\'20\'1Cegregiously wrong from the start\u8221\'20\'1D, women have been speaking out about their own terminations.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, the American singer-songwriter Phoebe Bridgers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/phoebe_bridgers/status/1521582506801254400?s=20&t=cOp7cDbNHPNs1f6vcOQnPw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tweeted}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CI had an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in October of last year while I was on tour. I went to Planned Parenthood, where they gave me the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill. It was easy. Everyone deserves that kind of access.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In Manhattan, New York attorney general Letitia James told a crowd of protesters that for her \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , she had \u8220\'20\'1Cwalked proudly into Planned Parenthood \u8211\'20\'13 and I make no apologies to anyone. To no one.\u8221\'20\'1D Describing herself as a woman of faith, James {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/es_indivisible/status/1521616407775035393?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw%7Ctwcamp%5Etweetembed%7Ctwterm%5E1521616407775035393%7Ctwgr%5E%7Ctwcon%5Es1_c10&ref_url=https%3A%2F%2Fvinnews.com%2F2022%2F05%2F04%2Fwatch-ny-ag-letitia-james-was-proud-to-get-abortion-makes-no-aplogies-to-anyone%2F"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the rally}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CMy God says that you\u8217\'20\'19ve got to make the best decision for you and your life.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2022/may/05/i-had-an-abortion-on-tour-celebrities-share-abortion-stories-in-backlash-to-roe-v-wade-leak"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18I had an \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  on tour\u8217\'20\'19: celebrities share their stories in backlash to Roe v Wade leak}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 McCarthy discussed 25th amendment for removing Trump from office: report\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s step away from \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights for a minute and take a look at the latest audiotape scandal engulfing Kevin McCarthy, the Republican House minority leader and see-sawing \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  ally.\par \par \uc2 Kevin McCarthy. Photograph: Kent Nishimura/\uc2 Los Angeles Times\uc2 /REX/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 The California Republican might have hoped recent revelations {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/04/22/us/politics/mccarthy-trump-republicans.html?action=click&module=RelatedLinks&pgtype=Article"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 that he lied}}}\uc2  about telling colleagues he would ask for Trump\u8217\'20\'19s resignation following the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-capitol-breach"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 6 January Capitol attack}}}\uc2  were behind him.\par \par \uc2 No such luck.\par \par \uc2 New York Times\uc2  journalists Jonathan Martin and Alexander Burns, authors of the book {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thiswillnotpass.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 This Will Not Pass}}}\uc2 , have published another potentially damaging audio recording, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/05/04/politics/mccarthy-audio-25th-amendment-biden/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported by CNN}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 McCarthy, the would-be House speaker if Republicans seize control of the chamber in November\u8217\'20\'19s midterm elections, is heard in the leaked recording discussing the setbacks of using the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/shortcuts/2017/jul/03/trump-us-constitution-25th-amendment-pass-notes-twitter?CMP=gu_com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 25th amendment}}}\uc2  to remove the then-president from office.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat takes too long too. It could go back to the House, right?\u8221\'20\'1D McCarthy is heard asking an aide who had already suggested the 25th amendment \u8220\'20\'1Cis not exactly an elegant solution here\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The recording was made on 8 January 2021, two days after the Trump-incited Capitol riot, for which McCarthy said at the time the president bore responsibility for:\par \par \uc2 What the president did is atrocious and totally wrong.\par \par \uc2 I do think the impeachment divides the nation further and continues the fight even greater. That\u8217\'20\'19s why I want to reach out to [Joe] Biden. I wanted the president to meet with Biden, but that\u8217\'20\'19s not going to happen.\par \par \uc2 I want to see about us meeting with Biden, sitting down, make a smooth transition...\par \par \uc2 In public, McCarthy has transformed from a vocal critic following the insurrection into a loyal defender as Trump mulls another run at the White House in 2024.\par \par \uc2 Previous audio clips have caught McCarthy telling Republican leadership colleagues that he would seek Trump\u8217\'20\'19s resignation, which he initially denied, and one in which he accused rightwing Republicans in the House of \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/27/kevin-mccarthy-capitol-attack-accusations-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 putting people in jeopardy}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D with their responses to the Capitol attack.\par \par \uc2 It remains to be seen if the recordings will damage McCarthy\u8217\'20\'19s pursuit of the speaker\u8217\'20\'19s gavel. House colleagues gave him {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/apr/27/mccarthy-house-republican-caucus-capitol-attack-trump-leaked-audio-biden-covid-us-politics-latest"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a standing ovation}}}\uc2  at a caucus meeting last month, and Trump himself has indicated he is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/mccarthy-said-he-would-advise-trump-to-resign-after-jan-6-riot-tape-shows-11650637401?AID=11557093&PID=6415797&SID=undefined%7C16517675583471shse4p4&subid=Business+Insider&cjevent=1d8d3b8ecc8f11ec821720f00a82b82c&tier_1=affiliate&tier_2=moa&tier_3=Business+Insider&tier_4=3861930&tier_5=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.wsj.com%2Farticles%2Fmccarthy-said-he-would-advise-trump-to-resign-after-jan-6-riot-tape-shows-11650637401"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 not concerned by the furore}}}\uc2 , the Wall Street Journal reported.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 Medical professionals are speaking out over the impending reversal of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. In this special for \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 , first published in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://19thnews.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The 19th}}}\uc2 , health reporter Shefali Luthra finds doctors warning of \u8220\'20\'1Cunnecessary suffering and unnecessary deaths\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 Dr Herman Miller didn\u8217\'20\'19t learn the news until he turned on MSNBC on Tuesday morning.\par \par \uc2 According to a draft opinion authored by Justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2 , the supreme court was ready to overturn Roe v Wade, the 1973 ruling that guarantees the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  up until a fetus can live outside the womb \u8211\'20\'13 typically around 22 to 25 weeks. Someone had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/05/02/supreme-court-abortion-draft-opinion-00029473"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 leaked the draft to Politico}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Miller was not surprised. He has provided abortions since he was a medical resident in 1978, and has watched for years as Republicans chipped away at \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections.\par \par \uc2 The 75-year-old doctor is semi-retired, but still works three days a week providing abortions as the medical director of A Woman\u8217\'20\'19s Choice, a clinic on the south side of Jacksonville, Florida.\par \par \uc2 He\u8217\'20\'19s the only doctor in the clinic who provides abortions up to 20 weeks of pregnancy. Many of his patients are teenagers; some are incest survivors.\par \par \uc2 So that morning he drove to the clinic. He saw maybe 16 patients for abortions. He counseled another 16 who were scheduled for Thursday appointments, and he told each of them the same thing: abortions were still legal right now. But their rights \u8211\'20\'13 enshrined for almost 50 years \u8211\'20\'13 were in grave danger.\par \par \uc2 Florida just recently passed a ban on abortions after 15 weeks, which will take effect if Roe is overturned. But Miller worries that\u8217\'20\'19s just the first step. He\u8217\'20\'19s waiting for when, not if, lawmakers move to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  entirely.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI tell my patients that that\u8217\'20\'19s why they need to get out to vote,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Read the full story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/05/abortion-providers-reactions-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Unnecessary suffering and death\u8217\'20\'19: doctors fear for patients\u8217\'20\'19 lives in a post-Roe world}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s not just Democrats wrestling with the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s draft ruling on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights... Republicans must find a way to sell the overwhelmingly unpopular justices\u8217\'20\'19 decision to voters as November\u8217\'20\'19s midterm elections loom.\par \par \uc2 So far, at least, the strategy of senior party officials appears to be to concentrate on the leak of the draft document instead of what the ruling actually says.\par \par \uc2 And with good reason: voters want the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections of Roe v Wade preserved by a ration of two to one, according to separate polls this week by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/05/04/poll-roe-v-wade-00029889"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico/Morning Consult}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2022/05/03/most-americans-say-supreme-court-should-uphold-roe-post-abc-poll-finds/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ABC/Washington Post}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 . Photograph: J Scott Applewhite/AP\par \par \uc2 Unsurprisingly, one of the most vocal in condemning the leak is \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , the senate minority leader who maneuvred conservatives \uc2 Neil Gorsuch\uc2 , \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2  and Amy Coney Barrett onto the supreme court bench during \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s single term in office.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://slate.com/news-and-politics/2022/05/mcconnell-schumer-roe-overturn-congress-supreme-court.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in-depth look at McConnell\u8217\'20\'19s strategy}}}\uc2  from Slate.\par \par \uc2 In the chamber on Tuesday, the Kentucky Republican {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/news/senate/3475407-mcconnell-supreme-court-leak-should-be-investigated-punished/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was outraged}}}\uc2 , the Hill reported:\par \par \uc2 This lawless action should be investigated and punished to the fullest extent possible. If a crime was committed, the department of justice must pursue it completely.\par \par \uc2 Notably, McConnell was silent about the implications of the imminent ending of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. And, by prominent contrast, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2022/04/07/mcconnell-axios-jonathan-swan-clarence-thomas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he has defended}}}\uc2  supreme court justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  after his rightwing wife Virginia Thomas was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2022/mar/25/ginni-thomas-texts-clarence-ethics-supreme-court-conflict-of-interest"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 implicated in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s 6 January insurrection}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 It didn\u8217\'20\'19t escape the notice of White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  during her Wednesday briefing:\par \par \uc2 Our focus is on not losing sight from what the content is in the draft and what is at risk here.\par \par \uc2 Republicans have wanted to talk about [the leak] and not about whether they support the protection of a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to choose, a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to make decisions with her doctor about her health care.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s maybe not a surprise given by more than a two to one margin Americans want the supreme court to support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 If leadership Republicans are attempting to downplay the ruling, fearing it could hurt their midterm prospects, extremist party members have no such qualms.\par \par \uc2 The bellicose Florida congressman \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2 , himself under a justice department {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/22/matt-gaetz-republican-sex-trafficking-investigation-marries-california"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sex-trafficking inquiry}}}\uc2 , is receiving a social media backlash, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/news/house/3477193-gaetz-faces-backlash-for-over-educated-women-remark/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to The Hill}}}\uc2 , for tweeting that protestors are \u8220\'20\'1Cover-educated, under-loved millennials\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrHow many of the women rallying against overturning Roe are over-educated, under-loved millennials who sadly return from protests to a lonely microwave dinner with their cats, and no bumble matches?\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2  (@mattgaetz) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mattgaetz/status/1521797001175834625?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 4, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 And there were curious tweets from \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2 , Republican Florida senator:\par \par \uc2 enltrIf we have \u8220\'20\'1Cpregnant people\u8221\'20\'1D then how can Roe be about \u8220\'20\'1Ca woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to choose\u8221\'20\'1D?\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2  (@marcorubio) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/marcorubio/status/1522188957890535424?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 5, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 From Colorado congresswoman \uc2 Lauren Boebert\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 enltrWhere\u8217\'20\'19s the outrage from all the pregnant men?\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Lauren Boebert\uc2  (@laurenboebert) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/laurenboebert/status/1521558980362969088?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 3, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 And from \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2 , rightwing congresswoman for Georgia:\par \par \uc2 enltrOur God is bigger. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ljNIeglFKS"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ljNIeglFKS}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rep. \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  (@RepMTG) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepMTG/status/1521342129481601025?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 3, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 Supreme court analyst and Ashe family chair of Georgia state university\u8217\'20\'19s college of law {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://law.gsu.edu/profile/eric-j-segall/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Eric Segall}}}\uc2  posts this picture this morning from the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 , the respected and symbolic home of American freedoms and justice:\par \par \uc2 enltrGood morning. Live shot which says it all. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Xj3kphKyIr"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Xj3kphKyIr}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Eric Segall (@espinsegall) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/espinsegall/status/1522181804404482048?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 5, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 Alito bails on senior judges' conference\par \par \uc2 Vocal in his leaked draft ruling about the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/03/abortion-midterms-election-scotus-draft-opinion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cegregious\u8221\'20\'1D right of American women}}}\uc2  to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it appears supreme court justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  has nothing to say to his colleagues in the judiciary.\par \par \uc2 Associate Justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2 . Photograph: Reuters\par \par \uc2 The conservative has bailed on a conference of senior judges Thursday in New Orleans, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/legal/government/us-supreme-courts-alito-cancels-conference-appearance-after-abortion-ruling-leak-2022-05-04/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Reuters reports}}}\uc2 , just three days after his opinion indicating the high court would overturn its landmark 1973 Roe v Wade decision that guaranteed the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide was leaked.\par \par \uc2 According to the news agency, Alito had been set to appear at the 5th US circuit court of appeals\u8217\'20\'19 judicial conference, a gathering of judges from the New Orleans-based federal appeals court and the district courts of Louisiana, Mississippi and Texas, a person familiar with the matter said.\par \par \uc2 But he has since canceled, the person said, and Patricia McCabe, a spokesperson for the supreme court, said he was not attending. No reason was given for why Alito, who is the justice assigned to hear emergency appeals from the 5th Circuit, was not going.\par \par \uc2 Reuters further reports that the 5th circuit\u8217\'20\'19s office of the circuit executive declined to confirm its conference was occurring this week, citing security, but in a press release last week the the legal society American Inns of Court detailed the date and location.\par \par \uc2 Chief Justice \uc2 John Roberts\uc2  and Associate Justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  were slated to speak separately on Thursday and Friday at the 11th circuit\u8217\'20\'19s judicial conference in Atlanta, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tmsnrt.rs/37URakl"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to an event program.}}}\uc2  It is unclear if they will still attend.\par \par \uc2 The in-person circuit conferences are among the first to be held since the beginning of the Covid-19 pandemic Similar events are planned this year in at least five other circuits, Reuters says.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ve plenty more coverage of the aftermath of the leaked supreme court draft ruling overturning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. My colleague Joan E Greve analyzes the justices\u8217\'20\'19 previous comments on Roe v Wade, and whether this week\u8217\'20\'19s developments constitute \u8220\'20\'1Ca betrayal\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 Chief Justice \uc2 John Roberts{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/03/chief-justice-roberts-abortion-leak-investigation-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has condemned}}}\uc2  the leak of a draft supreme court opinion overturning Roe v Wade as a \u8220\'20\'1Cbetrayal\u8221\'20\'1D. But for the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/Politics/supreme-court-poised-reverse-roe-americans-support-abortion/story?id=84468131"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 majority of Americans}}}\uc2  who support the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, the true betrayal was committed by the five justices who have initially voted to overturn the landmark case.\par \par \uc2 Neil Gorsuch\uc2 . Photograph: Erin Schaff/AP\par \par \uc2 That is especially true of the three conservative supreme court justices who were nominated by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 : \uc2 Neil Gorsuch\uc2 , \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2  and Amy Coney Barrett. During their Senate confirmation hearings, each of those three justices was asked about Roe and Planned Parenthood v Casey, the 1992 case that upheld the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access and could now be overturned as well.\par \par \uc2 The comments that the three justices made during those hearings are now coming under renewed scrutiny, as they face accusations of having misled politicians and the public about their willingness to overturn Roe.\par \par \uc2 During his 2017 confirmation hearings, Gorsuch said: \u8220\'20\'1CCasey is settled law in the sense that it is a decision of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/us-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court}}}\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D When Kavanaugh appeared before the Senate judiciary committee in 2018, he similarly described Roe as \u8220\'20\'1Cimportant precedent of the supreme court that has been reaffirmed many times\u8221\'20\'1D, and he defined Casey as \u8220\'20\'1Cprecedent on precedent\u8221\'20\'1D because it upheld Roe.\par \par \uc2 But legal excerpts say Gorsuch and Kavanaugh\u8217\'20\'19s comments about Roe and Casey did not clearly indicate how they might vote in a case like Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization, raising the prospect that some people may have read into their statements only what they wished to hear.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen people are nominated to the supreme court and they testify in Senate confirmation hearings, they are very careful about their language,\u8221\'20\'1D said Professor Katherine Franke of Columbia Law School. \u8220\'20\'1CSomething like \u8216\'20\'18settled law\u8217\'20\'19 actually has no concrete legal meaning. What it means is that that\u8217\'20\'19s a decision from the supreme court, and I acknowledge that it exists. But it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t carry any kind of significance beyond that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read the full story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2022/may/05/trump-justices-abortion-roe-v-wade-gorsuch-kavanaugh-coney-barrett"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump justices accused of going back on their word on Roe \u8211\'20\'13 but did they?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democrats are facing increasing pressure to do something about protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights before their predicted loss of control in one, or both chambers of Congress in November\u8217\'20\'19s midterm elections.\par \par \uc2 But options are limited, and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s administration sees no easy path forward as the supreme court prepares to finalize its reversal, in the coming weeks, of the 1973 Roe v Wade ruling that guaranteed women\u8217\'20\'19s constitutional rights to the procedure.\par \par \uc2 Legislation to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, which has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.congress.gov/bill/117th-congress/house-bill/3755"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 already passed the House}}}\uc2 , looks certain to stall again in the senate, despite Democratic majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2022/05/05/1096636861/democrats-votes-abortion-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 promise to bring it up for another vote}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The women\u8217\'20\'19s health protection act {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/mar/01/republicans-joe-manchin-us-senate-block-bill-abortion-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 failed in the chamber in March}}}\uc2 , sunk by Republicans and the West Virginia Democrat \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2 , and stands no chance of securing the support of the 60 senators it would need.\par \par \uc2 Progressive\uc2  voices such as the Democratic Massachusetts senator Elizabeth Warren, meanwhile, are calling for the \u8220\'20\'1Cpacking\u8221\'20\'1D of the supreme court with liberal judges to nullify the conservative majority, another likely non-starter given the reluctance of Manchin and other moderates to play along.\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s frustration became apparent during Wednesday\u8217\'20\'19s media briefing by White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 I can\u8217\'20\'19t speak for what actions could be possible.\par \par \uc2 What I can tell you will happen, and this is what we are preparing for, if Roe were to fall, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  would probably be illegal and about half the states in the country, up to 26 states, particularly in the south and midwest and west.\par \par \uc2 What we\u8217\'20\'19re really focused on is the impact. Tens of millions of women may lack access to reproductive health care services as soon as the summer.\par \par \uc2 Women, the majority of whom are below poverty level, and are Black, Hispanic, or API [Asian Pacific islanders], are going to be forced to figure out how to travel, how to take time off work, how to get childcare. It is a prohibitive cost, it will not be safe.\par \par \uc2 That is what we\u8217\'20\'19re focused on, working to address, as we\u8217\'20\'19re making policy decisions.\par \par \uc2 But anger is growing. As my colleagues Lauren Gambino and Lauren Burke report, furious protestors at the supreme court and in cities around the country, are demanding action. \u8220\'20\'1CDo something, Democrats!\u8221\'20\'1D is the rallying call.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/05/democrats-voters-senate-midterm-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Do something, Democrats\u8217\'20\'19: party struggles to rise to \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  challenge}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Good morning, and welcome to the blog. We\u8217\'20\'19re edging towards the end of an already drama-filled week in US politics that, incredibly, still has two full days to run.\par \par \uc2 Washington DC, and the nation, is still reeling from Monday\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/03/biden-democrats-reaction-codifying-roe-v-wade-reform-scotus"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bombshell news}}}\uc2  that the supreme court stands ready to strike down almost half a century of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 Democrats are under increasing pressure to do something about it before their predicted loss of control in one, or both chambers of Congress in November\u8217\'20\'19s midterms.\par \par \uc2 But legislation to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, or \u8220\'20\'1Cpacking\u8221\'20\'1D the supreme court with liberal judges to nullify the conservative majority, would face significant obstacles.\par \par \uc2 Republicans, meanwhile, must find a way to sell to voters the overwhelmingly unpopular supreme court move.\par \par \uc2 Russia\u8217\'20\'19s assault in Ukraine continues, and you can follow developments in our {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/may/05/russia-ukraine-war-bloody-battles-inside-mariupol-steelworks-ukraine-claims-it-has-retaken-areas-near-kherson-live"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 24-hour live blog here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In the US today:\par \par \uc2 * Immigration comes under scrutiny on Capitol Hill with officials from the state, homeland, and health and human services departments testifying this morning to lawmakers about security at the southern border.\par \par \uc2 * The White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  will brief at 2pm. Expect more questions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, immigration, the economy and Covid-19.\par \par \uc2 * We\u8217\'20\'19re waiting to see if other high-profile attendees at last weekend\u8217\'20\'19s White House correspondents\u8217\'20\'19 dinner come down with Covid-19. Secretary of state \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  declared he tested positive yesterday.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will greet Mexico\u8217\'20\'19s first lady Beatriz Guti\u233\'00\'E9rrez Mueller de L\u243\'00\'F3pez Obrador at a White House reception this afternoon to commemorate Cinco de Mayo.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220506ei56000dy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
