\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 Ending Roe v Wade could badly backfire on Republicans during elections this year\b0\par\par\uc2 Lloyd Green \par \uc2 939 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 May 2022\par 10:12 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The Democrats now have a fighting chance to maintain control of the Senate. Their odds of retaining and flipping seats have improved overnight\par \par \uc2 On Monday night, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/05/02/supreme-court-abortion-draft-opinion-00029473"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico reported}}}\uc2  that a majority of the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  is poised to overturn Roe v Wade, eviscerate a half-century of precedent, and leave the issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the states. Five of the court\u8217\'20\'19s nine justices are prepared to give the Republican base exactly what it demanded. The remaining question for the Republican party is whether answered prayers are the most dangerous.\par \par \uc2 If the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/05/02/read-justice-alito-initial-abortion-opinion-overturn-roe-v-wade-pdf-00029504"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 leaked draft of the majority opinion}}}\uc2  in Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization is close to the final cut, the court stands to energize otherwise dejected Democrats and put Republican members of Congress in Democratic-leaning states at risk. Expect the anticipated Republican House majority in the midterms to be smaller than currently projected.\par \par \uc2 Indeed, the Democrats also now have a real shot to maintain their control of the Senate. Overnight, their odds of retaining seats in Arizona, Nevada, Georgia and New Hampshire, while flipping Pennsylvania and Wisconsin, improved.\par \par \uc2 Beyond federal offices, fights will now be waged this fall over governorships and legislatures in Michigan and Pennsylvania, where \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  narrowly won in 2020, but where the incumbent governor is a Democrat, and the legislature is in the hands of the Republican party. In a post-Dobbs world, look to the states to emerge as roiling battlegrounds.\par \par \uc2 Make no mistake, the draft opinion is sweeping. \u8220\'20\'1CWe hold that Roe and Casey must be overruled,\u8221\'20\'1D Justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  writes for himself and four of his colleagues. \u8220\'20\'1CIt is time to heed the constitution and return the issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the people\u8217\'20\'19s elected representatives.\u8221\'20\'1D Along the way, the ruling also offers implicit criticism of the court\u8217\'20\'19s prior decisions on personal autonomy.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/elliotcwilliams/status/1521315457613107201"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Prior precedents}}}\uc2  on contraception, interracial marriage, consensual sex and gay marriage are now at risk. At a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.freep.com/story/news/politics/2022/02/21/michigan-gop-ag-hopefuls-criticize-case-nixed-contraception-ban/6877934001/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February debate}}}\uc2  among Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s prospective Republican candidates for attorney general, all three men, including Matthew DePerno, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mlive.com/public-interest/2022/04/matt-deperno-trumps-pick-wins-republican-endorsement-for-michigan-attorney-general.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s choice}}}\uc2 , criticized Griswold v Connecticut. In that case, the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  struck down a state law that barred the sale of contraceptives to married couples.\par \par \uc2 In a post-Dobbs world, look to the states to emerge as roiling battlegrounds\par \par \uc2 DePerno, an advocate of election conspiracy theories, framed his understanding of this this way: \u8220\'20\'1CThe supreme court \u8230\'20\'26 has to decide, mark my words, that the privacy issue currently is unworkable. It\u8217\'20\'19s going to be a states\u8217\'20\'19 rights issue on all these things, as it should be.\u8221\'20\'1D DePerno is also the state Republican party\u8217\'20\'19s officially preferred candidate.\par \par \uc2 Elissa Slotkin\uc2 , a moderate Michigan Democrat, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ElissaSlotkin/status/1521311942534705155"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tweeted on Monday night}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CIf tonight\u8217\'20\'19s news is true, Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s 1931 state law banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  would snap back into effect, making any \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  illegal in our state \u8211\'20\'13 even if the mom will die, or if she was raped by a family member. No exceptions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A former member of the US intelligence community and the wife of a retired army helicopter pilot, Slotkin {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ElissaSlotkin/status/1521311943788797953"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 added}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CMy poor mother is turning over in her grave. The House has already voted to codify Roe \u8211\'20\'13 let all Senators be on record on this one in an up or down vote.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In the same neo-Confederate spirit as Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s DePerno, the Indiana senator \uc2 Mike Braun\uc2  offered up his benighted take on interracial marriage. Braun argued that like \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , interracial marriage should be left to the states to decide \u8211\'20\'13 not the federal judiciary. Said differently, he was arguing that the supreme court got it wrong in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.indystar.com/story/news/politics/2022/03/22/mike-braun-indiana-us-senate-interracial-marriage-law-loving-virginia/7131891001/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Loving v Virginia}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen you want that diversity to shine within our federal system, there are going to be rules and proceedings, they\u8217\'20\'19re going to be out of sync with maybe what other states would do,\u8221\'20\'1D Braun announced.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s the beauty of the system, and that\u8217\'20\'19s where the differences among points of view in our 50 states ought to express themselves.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 After the ensuing uproar, Braun walked his words back. But in light of Politico\u8217\'20\'19s reporting, the Democrats now have names, faces and an issue. Think ready-made campaign ad.\par \par \uc2 To be sure, clearer Republican heads viewed the wholesale gutting of Roe as a threat to the Republican party\u8217\'20\'19s elected officials. In the summer of 2021, they attempted to guide the court\u8217\'20\'19s hand; they failed.\par \par \uc2 Last July, 228 Republican members of Congress, 44 senators and 184 House members, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wicker.senate.gov/services/files/91b4f962-785b-4a88-b298-908ae76dd297"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filed an amicus brief}}}\uc2  in support of the Mississippi \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law in question. Nowhere did the Republican submission refer to contraception, interracial marriage, or individual autonomy. Likewise, the word \u8220\'20\'1Cprivacy\u8221\'20\'1D only appeared as a part of a title of a footnoted law review article. \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , Kevin McCarthy, \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  and \uc2 Lauren Boebert\uc2  couched their arguments in pastels. Words like \u8220\'20\'1Cpreviability\u8221\'20\'1D filled the page, as did polling data.\par \par \uc2 Justices Alito, \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 , \uc2 Neil Gorsuch\uc2 , \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2  and Amy Coney Barrett, however, were having none of that. For them, it is time to return to what they consider the original constitution.\par \par \uc2 More {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wpr.org/poll-most-americans-oppose-overturning-roe-v-wade-split-new-abortion-restrictions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 than seven in 10}}}\uc2  Americans oppose overturning Roe even as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/support-for-15-week-abortion-ban-outweighs-opposition-wsj-poll-finds-11648821601"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the public is split}}}\uc2  over where to draw a line. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://poll.qu.edu/poll-release?releaseid=3822"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 In Texas}}}\uc2 , 77% support legal abortions in case of rape and incest. Not all restrictions are the same. America\u8217\'20\'19s cold civil war just got really hot.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Lloyd Green is an attorney in New York. He was opposition research counsel to \uc2 George HW Bush\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 1988 campaign and served in the Department of Justice from 1990 to 1992\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220506ei56001gu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
