\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 First Thing: \uc2 UN\uc2  plans third evacuation from Azovstal steelworks in Ukraine\b0\par\par\uc2 Nicola Slawson \par \uc2 1,410 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 May 2022\par 10:19 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 As a large-scale Russian propaganda campaign gets under way, fighting continues in the steel plant in Mariupol. Plus, \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  named new US press secretary\par \par \uc2 Good morning.\par \par \uc2 A third United Nations operation was under way this morning to evacuate Ukrainian civilians from the Russian-besieged Azovstal steel plant in Mariupol, which the \uc2 UN\uc2  secretary general has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/06/un-plans-third-evacuation-from-azovstal-steelworks-as-battle-continues-to-rage"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 described as a series of \u8220\'20\'1Chellscapes\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 An estimated 200 civilians, along with Ukrainian resistance fighters, remain trapped in underground refuges at the huge industrial complex. The \uc2 UN\uc2  humanitarian chief, \uc2 Martin Griffiths\uc2 , said a convoy was headed to Azovstal \u8220\'20\'1Cto receive those civilians remaining in that bleak hell \u8230\'20\'26 and take them back to safety\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The Ukrainian deputy prime minister \uc2 Iryna Vereshchuk\uc2  said people would be evacuated from Mariupol at midday local time on Friday. The \uc2 UN\uc2  and the Red Cross said they had so far helped nearly 500 civilians flee the steelworks area in the southern port city during two operations in the past week.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, US officials have reportedly confirmed they are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/05/us-intelligence-helping-ukraine-kill-russian-generals-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 providing intelligence that has helped Ukrainian forces}}}\uc2  target and kill many of the Russian generals who have died in the Ukraine war.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Why is Putin so determined to capture Mariupol over the next few days? As {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/05/putin-hopes-to-claim-mariupol-as-key-prop-in-victory-day-celebrations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Victory Day, 9 May, approaches in Russia}}}\uc2 , \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  has yet to win any prize in two months of war in Ukraine that can be shown off to the Russian people. But Mariupol could be close. Here\u8217\'20\'19s how Victory Day became {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/06/how-victory-day-became-central-to-putin-idea-of-russian-identity"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 central to Putin\u8217\'20\'19s idea of Russian identity}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What else is happening?\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/06/russia-ukraine-war-what-we-know-on-day-72-of-the-invasion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what we know}}}\uc2  on day 72 of the invasion.\par \par \uc2 Biden names \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\par \par \uc2 as press secretary\par \par \uc2 to replace \uc2 Jen Psaki\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has named his new press secretary, after it was announced that \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  will leave the administration and is expected to become a TV host at MSNBC.\par \par \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2 , currently the principal deputy press secretary, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/05/white-house-press-secretary-karine-jean-pierre"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will take over the role after Psaki }}}\uc2  leaves in mid-May. Jean-Pierre, a political analyst, was Kamala Harris\u8217\'20\'19s chief of staff during the vice-president\u8217\'20\'19s presidential campaign in 2020 and served on \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s campaigns in 2008 and 2012. She was also an adviser and spokesperson for \uc2 MoveOn.org\uc2 , a progressive Pac.\par \par \uc2 Jean-Pierre will be the first Black person and first out gay person in the role. She has filled in for Psaki on several occasions, most recently while her predecessor was quarantining with Covid-19.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShe is passionate. She is smart and she has a moral core that makes her not just a great colleague, but an amazing mom and human,\u8221\'20\'1D Psaki {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PressSec/status/1522300498925297666?s=20&t=X14-HCqOzZL8O8suYnspVw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tweeted}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CPlus, she has a great sense of humor.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What has Biden said about her appointment? Biden lauded Jean-Pierre\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cexperience, talent and integrity\u8221\'20\'1D. He said: \u8220\'20\'1CJill and I have known and respected Karine a long time and she will be a strong voice speaking for me and this administration.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 When will Psaki leave? Her last day will be 13 May.\par \par \uc2 Louisiana Republicans advance bill to make \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  a crime of murder\par \par \uc2 Republicans in Louisiana have advanced a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/05/louisiana-abortion-bill-murder-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bill to make \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  a crime of murder}}}\uc2 , as a draft decision that would end \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights continues to spark nationwide protests and police in Washington raised \u8220\'20\'1Cnon-scalable\u8221\'20\'1D fences around the supreme court.\par \par \uc2 Supporters admitted the bill, under which a woman terminating a pregnancy or anyone assisting her could be charged, was unconstitutional \u8211\'20\'13 as long as Roe v Wade was law.\par \par \uc2 The supreme court is expected to formally overturn Roe v Wade, the 1973 case that established the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in June. Danny McCormick, the state representative behind the Louisiana bill, said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe can\u8217\'20\'19t wait on the supreme court.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Since the draft ruling that seems set to overturn Roe was published by Politico on Monday night, Democrats have warned of a likely torrent of challenges to established rights.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What else is happening? Extreme anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups are now emboldened to fight for laws that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/06/no-exception-rape-incest-anti-abortion-laws-republicans-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ban ending pregnancies conceived in rape or incest}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 How have the medical community reacted? \u8220\'20\'1CIf this decision ends up being similar to what [was leaked], this is going to substantially affect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care, obstetrics care and healthcare more generally,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/06/abortion-bans-patient-doctor-medical-advice"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said Dr Nisha Verma}}}\uc2 , a Darney-Landy fellow with the \uc2 American College of Obstetricians and Gynecologists\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In other news \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Local Conservative leaders in the UK have urged\par \par \uc2 the prime minister, \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2 , to consider his position after losing flagship London councils to Labour and council seats across the south of England to the Lib Dems, with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2022/may/06/local-elections-2022-tory-council-leaders-point-finger-at-johnson-after-losses-blamed-on-partygate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 several blaming Partygate and the cost of living crisis}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A week before election day 2020, the US secretary of defense was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2022/may/06/trump-defense-secretary-mark-esper-book"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 so worried that Donald Trump would seek to involve the military}}}\uc2  in the election in an attempt to hold on to power, he told the general commanding the US national guard to notify him of any communication from anyone at the White House.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 China\u8217\'20\'19s president, \uc2 Xi Jinping\uc2 , has confirmed there is no intention to turn away from China\u8217\'20\'19s zero-Covid commitment, in a major speech\par \par \uc2 that also warned against any criticism of the policy. He {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/06/xi-jinping-attacks-doubters-as-he-doubles-down-on-chinas-zero-covid-policy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 defended the \u8220\'20\'1Cscientific and effective\u8221\'20\'1D mass lockdowns}}}\uc2  despite protests, shortages and damage to economic growth.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s former attorney \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  is not expected to appear at an interview scheduled for today with the House select committee investigating the January 6 Capitol attack, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/05/rudy-giuliani-house-january-6-committee-interview-donald-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 throwing into jeopardy the prospect of his cooperation}}}\uc2 , say sources familiar with the matter.\par \par \uc2 Stat of the day: US stocks\par \par \uc2 experience worst day this year as Dow falls 3.1%\par \par \uc2 US stock markets suffered their {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/may/05/us-stock-market-inflation-federal-reserve"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 worst day of the year}}}\uc2  on Thursday as investors worried about the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s plans to raise interest rates to tackle soaring inflation. The Dow Jones industrial average lost more than 1,000 points (3.1%). The S&P 500 and Nasdaq Composite fell 3.5% and 4.9% respectively. Tech stocks were particularly hard-hit, with \uc2 Amazon\uc2  dropping 7.6% and \uc2 Tesla\uc2  falling 8.3%. The steep fall came one day after the Fed chair, \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2 , announced the sharpest rise in interest rates in more than 20 years.\par \par \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t miss this: \u8216\'20\'18Name names? Never, never, never!\u8217\'20\'19 Lee Grant on her decades of defiance\par \par \uc2 Lee Grant, child of the Depression, survivor of the anti-communist blacklist, director, Oscar winner and \u8211\'20\'13 incredibly \u8211\'20\'13 95 and looking nothing of the sort, is standing in her Manhattan kitchen. Having survived waves of oppression in her youth, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2022/may/06/name-names-never-never-never-lee-grant-on-her-decades-of-defiance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 she is not done yet}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CI feel there\u8217\'20\'19s some way that I can still somehow do something. I don\u8217\'20\'19t know what.\u8221\'20\'1D Experience makes her confident: something always turns up. \u8220\'20\'1CLife is like that. You slip to another place, go into another world, and you\u8217\'20\'19re curious, and you take sides. And it\u8217\'20\'19s a kind of miracle.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Climate check:\par \par \uc2 firefighters slow advance of New Mexico blaze as experts blame climate\par \par \uc2 crisis\par \par \uc2 Firefighters in New Mexico have slowed the advance of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/05/new-mexico-wildfire-us-biden-declares-disaster"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the largest wildfire burning in the US}}}\uc2 , as \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  declared the situation a disaster. The extent of the fire is not a surprise to experts. Wildfires have become a year-round threat in the drought-stricken west \u8211\'20\'13 moving faster and burning hotter than ever due to the climate crisis, scientists and fire specialists have said. \u8220\'20\'1CClimate change is taking a situation that would be bad for us normally,\u8221\'20\'1D says Gregg Garfin, a climatologist at the \uc2 University of Arizona\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1Cand turning the dial up\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Last Thing:\par \par \uc2 does Liam Neeson not understand the rules of the game? Or is he having us on?\par \par \uc2 Liam Neeson is making a bid to become the greatest interviewee in the world. Every other celebrity understands and adheres to the rules of the game. Their job is to promote a project, to better increase its revenue. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2022/may/06/does-liam-neeson-not-understand-the-rules-of-the-game-or-is-he-having-us-on"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Everyone, that is, except Neeson}}}\uc2 . Because his interview tactic is different. Neeson likes to sit back, answer questions about his newest film and then, just as everyone is getting ready to pack up for the day, blurt out the single maddest thing that comes into his head, writes Stuart Heritage.\par \par \uc2 Sign up\par \par \uc2 First Thing is delivered to thousands of inboxes every weekday. If you\u8217\'20\'19re not already signed up, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/info/2018/sep/17/guardian-us-morning-briefing-sign-up-to-stay-informed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 subscribe now}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Get in touch\par \par \uc2 If you have any questions or comments about any of our newsletters please email {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:newsletters@theguardian.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 newsletters@theguardian.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220506ei56001gt\par }\par \b \uc2 Search Summary\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\c